msgid "Asynchronous support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht asincrónach"

msgid ""
"Django has support for writing asynchronous (\"async\") views, along with an "
"entirely async-enabled request stack if you are running under :doc:`ASGI </"
"howto/deployment/asgi/index>`. Async views will still work under WSGI, but "
"with performance penalties, and without the ability to have efficient long-"
"running requests."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht ag Django chun tuairimí asincrónacha (“async”) a scríobh, mar "
"aon le cruach iarratais atá cumasaithe go hiomlán asinc-chumasaithe má tá tú "
"ag rith fao:doc: `ASGI` </howto/deployment/asgi/index>. Oibreoidh tuairimí "
"async fós faoi WSGI, ach le pionóis feidhmíochta, agus gan an cumas "
"iarratais éifeachtacha fadtéarmach a bheith acu."

msgid ""
"We're still working on async support for the ORM and other parts of Django. "
"You can expect to see this in future releases. For now, you can use "
"the :func:`sync_to_async` adapter to interact with the sync parts of Django. "
"There is also a whole range of async-native Python libraries that you can "
"integrate with."
msgstr ""
"Táimid fós ag obair ar thacaíocht async don ORM agus do chodanna eile de "
"Django. Is féidir leat a bheith ag súil leis seo a fheiceáil in eisiúintí "
"amach anseo. Go dtí seo, is féidir leat an cuibheoir: func: `sync_to_async` "
"a úsáid chun idirghníomhú le codanna sioncrónaithe de Django. Tá raon iomlán "
"leabharlanna Python asinc-dúchasacha ann freisin ar féidir leat comhtháthú "
"leo."

msgid "Async views"
msgstr "Tuairimí async"

msgid ""
"Any view can be declared async by making the callable part of it return a "
"coroutine - commonly, this is done using ``async def``. For a function-based "
"view, this means declaring the whole view using ``async def``. For a class-"
"based view, this means declaring the HTTP method handlers, such as ``get()`` "
"and ``post()`` as ``async def`` (not its ``__init__()``, or ``as_view()``)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir aon radharc a dhearbhú async tríd an gcuid inghlaonta de coroutine "
"a thabhairt ar ais - go coitianta, déantar é seo ag baint úsáide as ``async "
"def``. Maidir le dearcadh bunaithe ar fheidhm, ciallaíonn sé seo an dearcadh "
"iomlán a dhearbhú ag baint úsáide as ``async def``. Maidir le dearcadh rang-"
"bhunaithe, ciallaíonn sé seo láimhseálaithe modh HTTP a dhearbhú, mar "
"shampla ``get () ``agus ``post ()`` mar `async def`` (ní a ``__init__ () ``, "
"nó ``as_view ()``)."

msgid ""
"Django uses ``asgiref.sync.iscoroutinefunction`` to test if your view is "
"asynchronous or not. If you implement your own method of returning a "
"coroutine, ensure you use ``asgiref.sync.markcoroutinefunction`` so this "
"function returns ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django ``asgiref.sync.iscoroutinefunction`` chun tástáil a "
"dhéanamh an bhfuil do thuairim asincrónach nó nach bhfuil. Má chuireann tú "
"do mhodh féin chun coroutine a thabhairt ar ais, déan cinnte go n-úsáideann "
"tú ``asgiref.sync.markcoroutinefunction` ionas go bhfillfidh an fheidhm seo "
"``True``."

msgid ""
"Under a WSGI server, async views will run in their own, one-off event loop. "
"This means you can use async features, like concurrent async HTTP requests, "
"without any issues, but you will not get the benefits of an async stack."
msgstr ""
"Faoi fhreastalaí WSGI, reáchtálfaidh tuairimí async ina lúb imeachta "
"aonuaire féin. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat gnéithe async a úsáid, "
"cosúil le hiarratais HTTP async comhthráthacha, gan aon cheisteanna, ach ní "
"gheobhaidh tú na buntáistí a bhaineann le cruach async."

msgid ""
"The main benefits are the ability to service hundreds of connections without "
"using Python threads. This allows you to use slow streaming, long-polling, "
"and other exciting response types."
msgstr ""
"Is iad na príomhbhuntáistí an cumas na céadta naisc a sheirbheáil gan "
"snáitheanna Python a úsáid. Ligeann sé seo duit sruthú mall, vótaíocht "
"fhada, agus cineálacha freagartha spreagúla eile a úsáid."

msgid ""
"If you want to use these, you will need to deploy Django using :doc:`ASGI </"
"howto/deployment/asgi/index>` instead."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat iad seo a úsáid, beidh ort Django a úsáid ag baint "
"úsáidea:doc: `ASGI` ina ionad </howto/deployment/asgi/index>."

msgid ""
"You will only get the benefits of a fully-asynchronous request stack if you "
"have *no synchronous middleware* loaded into your site. If there is a piece "
"of synchronous middleware, then Django must use a thread per request to "
"safely emulate a synchronous environment for it."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhfaighidh tú na buntáistí a bhaineann le cruach iarratais lán-"
"asincrónach mura bhfuil * aon mheánghearraí sioncrónach agat* luchtaithe "
"isteach i do shuíomh. Má tá píosa de mheán-earraí sioncrónach ann, ansin "
"caithfidh Django snáithe in aghaidh an iarratais a úsáid chun aithris a "
"dhéanamh ar thimpeallacht sioncrónach dó go sábháilte."

msgid ""
"Middleware can be built to support :ref:`both sync and async <async-"
"middleware>` contexts. Some of Django's middleware is built like this, but "
"not all. To see what middleware Django has to adapt for, you can turn on "
"debug logging for the ``django.request`` logger and look for log messages "
"about *\"Asynchronous handler adapted for middleware ...\"*."
msgstr ""
"<async-middleware>Is féidir Middleware a thógáil chun tacú le "
"comhthéacsanna: ref: `sync agus async` araon. Tógtar cuid de mheán-earraí "
"Django mar seo, ach ní gach ceann. Chun a fheiceáil cad iad na middleware "
"caithfidh Django oiriúnú dó, is féidir leat logáil dífhabhtaithe a chasadh "
"air don logálaí ``django.request`` agus teachtaireachtaí logála a lorg "
"fao*\"Láimhseálaí asincrónach oiriúnaithe le haghaidh middleware... “*."

msgid ""
"In both ASGI and WSGI mode, you can still safely use asynchronous support to "
"run code concurrently rather than serially. This is especially handy when "
"dealing with external APIs or data stores."
msgstr ""
"I mód ASGI agus WSGI araon, is féidir leat tacaíocht asincrónach a úsáid go "
"sábháilte fós chun cód a reáchtáil ag an am céanna seachas go sraitheach. Tá "
"sé seo áisiúil go háirithe agus tú ag déileáil le APIs seachtracha nó "
"stórais sonraí."

msgid ""
"If you want to call a part of Django that is still synchronous, you will "
"need to wrap it in a :func:`sync_to_async` call. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat glaoch ar chuid de Django atá fós sioncrónach, beidh ort é a "
"fhilleadh i nglao a:func: `sync_to_async`. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"If you accidentally try to call a part of Django that is synchronous-only "
"from an async view, you will trigger Django's :ref:`asynchronous safety "
"protection <async-safety>` to protect your data from corruption."
msgstr ""
"<async-safety>Má dhéanann tú iarracht de thaisme glaoch ar chuid de Django "
"atá sioncrónach amháin ó radharc async, spreagfaidh tú Django's:ref: "
"`cosaint sábháilteachta asincrónach `chun do chuid sonraí a chosaint ar "
"éilliú."

