"Then, to register this custom user model with Django's admin, the following "
"code would be required in the app's ``admin.py`` file::"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, chun an tsamhail úsáideora saincheaptha seo a chlárú le riarachán "
"Django, bheadh an cód seo a leanas ag teastáil i gcomhad `admin.py` an aip:"

msgid ""
"Finally, specify the custom model as the default user model for your project "
"using the :setting:`AUTH_USER_MODEL` setting in your ``settings.py``::"
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, sonraigh an tsamhail saincheaptha mar an tsamhail úsáideora "
"réamhshocraithe do do thionscadal ag baint úsáide as an socrú: setting: "
"`AUTH_USER_MODEL` i do `settings.py``:"

msgid "Adding an async interface"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To optimize performance when called from an async context authentication, "
"backends can implement async versions of each function - "
"``aget_user(user_id)`` and ``aauthenticate(request, **credentials)``. When "
"an authentication backend extends ``BaseBackend`` and async versions of "
"these functions are not provided, they will be automatically synthesized "
"with ``sync_to_async``. This has :ref:`performance penalties "
"<async_performance>`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While an async interface is optional, a synchronous interface is always "
"required. There is no automatic synthesis for a synchronous interface if an "
"async interface is implemented."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Django's out-of-the-box authentication backends have native async support. "
"If these native backends are extended take special care to make sure the "
"async versions of modified functions are modified as well."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using the Django authentication system"
msgstr "Córas fíordheimhnithe Django a úsáid"

msgid ""
"This document explains the usage of Django's authentication system in its "
"default configuration. This configuration has evolved to serve the most "
"common project needs, handling a reasonably wide range of tasks, and has a "
"careful implementation of passwords and permissions. For projects where "
"authentication needs differ from the default, Django supports "
"extensive :doc:`extension and customization </topics/auth/customizing>` of "
"authentication."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo úsáid chóras fíordheimhnithe Django ina chumraíocht "
"réamhshocraithe. Tá an chumraíocht seo tagtha chun cinn chun freastal ar na "
"riachtanais tionscadail is coitianta, ag láimhseáil raon réasúnta leathan "
"tascanna, agus tá pasfhocail agus ceadanna curtha i bhfeidhm Maidir le "
"tionscadail ina bhfuil riachtanais fíordheimhnithe difriúil ó na "
"réamhshocraithe, tacaíonn Django le fairsing:doc: `síneadh agus "
"saincheapach' fíordheimhnithe </topics/auth/customizing>."

msgid ""
"Django authentication provides both authentication and authorization "
"together and is generally referred to as the authentication system, as these "
"features are somewhat coupled."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn fíordheimhniú Django fíordheimhniú agus údarú le chéile agus go "
"ginearálta tugtar an córas fíordheimhnithe air, toisc go bhfuil na gnéithe "
"seo cúpláilte"

msgid "``User`` objects"
msgstr "``Úsáideoir ``rudaí"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` objects are the core of the "
"authentication system. They typically represent the people interacting with "
"your site and are used to enable things like restricting access, registering "
"user profiles, associating content with creators etc. Only one class of user "
"exists in Django's authentication framework, i.e., :attr:`'superusers' "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_superuser>` or admin :attr:`'staff' "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_staff>` users are just user objects with "
"special attributes set, not different classes of user objects."
msgstr ""
":class: Is iad rudaí `~django.contrib.auth.models.user` croílár an chórais "
"fíordheimhnithe. <django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_staff>Is iondúil go "
"léiríonn siad na daoine atá ag idirghníomhú le do shuíomh agus úsáidtear iad "
"chun rudaí cosúil le rochtain a shrianadh, próifílí úsáideora a chlárú, "
"ábhar a cheangal le cruthaitheoirí srl. Níl ach aicme fíordheimhnithe "
"Django, ie: <django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_superuser>attr: `superusers' "
"nó admin:attr: `'staff'."

msgid "The primary attributes of the default user are:"
msgstr "Is iad príomhthréithe an úsáideora réamhshocraithe:"

msgid ":attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.username`"
msgstr ":attr: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.ainm úsáideora `"

msgid ":attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.password`"
msgstr ":attr: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.password`"

msgid ":attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.email`"
msgstr ":attr: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.email`"

msgid ":attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.first_name`"
msgstr ":attr: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.First_ainm`"

msgid ":attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.last_name`"
msgstr ":attr: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.last_ainm`"

msgid ""
"See the :class:`full API documentation <django.contrib.auth.models.User>` "
"for full reference, the documentation that follows is more task oriented."
msgstr ""
"Féach an:class: `doiciméadú iomlán API <django.contrib.auth.models.User>`le "
"haghaidh tagartha iomlán, tá an doiciméadú a leanas níos dírithe ar thasc."

msgid "Creating users"
msgstr "úsáideoirí a chruthú"

msgid ""
"The most direct way to create users is to use the "
"included :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.UserManager.create_user` helper "
"function:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach is díreach chun úsáideoirí a chruthú ná an fheidhm chúntóra "
"san áireamh: meth: `~django.contrib.auth.models.userManager.create_user` a "
"úsáid:"

msgid ""
"If you have the Django admin installed, you can also :ref:`create users "
"interactively <auth-admin>`."
msgstr ""
"<auth-admin>Má tá riarachán Django suiteáilte agat, is féidir leat "
"freis:ref: `úsáideoirí a chruthú go idirghníomhach`."

msgid "Creating superusers"
msgstr "Superusers a chruthú"

msgid "Create superusers using the :djadmin:`createsuperuser` command:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh sárúsáideoirí ag baint úsáide as an ordú:djadmin: "
"`createsuperuser`:"

msgid ""
"You will be prompted for a password. After you enter one, the user will be "
"created immediately. If you leave off the :option:`--username "
"<createsuperuser --username>` or :option:`--email <createsuperuser --email>` "
"options, it will prompt you for those values."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear pasfhocal ort. Tar éis duit ceann a iontráil, cruthófar an t-"
"úsáideoir láithreach. Má fhágann tú na roghanna: rogha: `--ainm úsáideora "
"<createsuperuser --username>`nó: rogha: `--ríomhphost`, spreagfaidh sé tú do "
"na <createsuperuser --email>luachanna sin."

msgid "Changing passwords"
msgstr "Athrú pasfhocail"

msgid ""
"Django does not store raw (clear text) passwords on the user model, but only "
"a hash (see :doc:`documentation of how passwords are managed </topics/auth/"
"passwords>` for full details). Because of this, do not attempt to manipulate "
"the password attribute of the user directly. This is why a helper function "
"is used when creating a user."
msgstr ""
"Ní stóráilíonn Django pasfhocail amh (téacs soiléir) ar an tsamhail "
"úsáideora, ach ach hash amháin (féach: doc: `doiciméadú ar an gcaoi a "
"mbainistítear pasfhocail `le haghaidh sonraí iomlána). </topics/auth/"
"passwords> Mar gheall air seo, ná déan iarracht tréith pasfhocal an "
"úsáideora a ionramháil go díreach. Sin é an fáth go n-úsáidtear feidhm "
"chúntóra agus úsáideoir á chruthú."

msgid "To change a user's password, you have several options:"
msgstr "Chun pasfhocal úsáideora a athrú, tá roinnt roghanna agat:"

msgid ""
":djadmin:`manage.py changepassword *username* <changepassword>` offers a "
"method of changing a user's password from the command line. It prompts you "
"to change the password of a given user which you must enter twice. If they "
"both match, the new password will be changed immediately. If you do not "
"supply a user, the command will attempt to change the password whose "
"username matches the current system user."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Cuireann `manage.py changepassword *ainm úsáideora* "
"<changepassword>`modh chun pasfhocal úsáideora a athrú ón líne ordaithe. "
"Spreagann sé duit pasfhocal úsáideora ar leith a athrú a chaithfidh tú a "
"iontráil faoi dhó. Má mheaitseálann an bheirt acu, athrófar an pasfhocal nua "
"láithreach. Mura soláthraíonn tú úsáideoir, déanfaidh an t-ordú iarracht an "
"pasfhocal a mheaitseálann a n-ainm úsáideora leis an úsáideoir reatha córais "
"a athrú."

msgid ""
"You can also change a password programmatically, "
"using :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_password()`:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat pasfhocal a athrú go cláraitheach freisin, ag baint "
"úsáid:meth: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.set_password () `:"

msgid ""
"If you have the Django admin installed, you can also change user's passwords "
"on the :ref:`authentication system's admin pages <auth-admin>`."
msgstr ""
"<auth-admin>Má tá riarachán Django suiteáilte agat, is féidir leat "
"pasfhocail an úsáideora a athrú ar leathanaigh riaracháin an chórais "
"fíordheimhniúcháin: ref: `."

msgid ""
"Django also provides :ref:`views <built-in-auth-views>` and :ref:`forms "
"<built-in-auth-forms>` that may be used to allow users to change their own "
"passwords."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django freis:ref: `views <built-in-auth-views>`agus:ref: "
"`foirmeacha` is féidir a úsáid chun ligean d'úsáideoirí a <built-in-auth-"
"forms>gcuid pasfhocail féin a athrú."

msgid ""
"Changing a user's password will log out all their sessions. "
"See :ref:`session-invalidation-on-password-change` for details."
msgstr ""
"Athrú pasfhocal úsáideora logálfar amach a seisiúin go léir. Féach: Ref: "
"`seision-invalidation-on-pasfho-athraithe' le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Authenticating users"
msgstr "Úsáideoirí fíordheimhnithe"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aauthenticate()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``aheimhniú () ``"

msgid ""
"Use :func:`~django.contrib.auth.authenticate()` to verify a set of "
"credentials. It takes credentials as keyword arguments, ``username`` and "
"``password`` for the default case, checks them against "
"each :ref:`authentication backend <authentication-backends>`, and returns "
"a :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` object if the credentials are "
"valid for a backend. If the credentials aren't valid for any backend or if a "
"backend raises :class:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied`, it returns "
"``None``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: func: `~django.contrib.auth.autenticate () `chun tacar dintiúir a "
"fhíorú. Glacann sé dintiúir mar argóintí eochairfhocal, ``ainm úsáideora "
"``agus `pasfhocal`` don chás réamhshocraithe, seiceálann sé iad i gcoinne "
"gach ceann:ref: ``backend fíordheimhniúcháin `, agus filleann sé a:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user<authentication-backends>` réad má tá na "
"dintiúir bailí le haghaidh cúltaca. Mura bhfuil na dintiúir bailí d'aon "
"chúltaca nó má ardaíonn cúltaca: class: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.permissionDenied`, filleann sé ``None``. Mar "
"shampla::"

msgid ""
"``request`` is an optional :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` which is passed "
"on the ``authenticate()`` method of the authentication backends."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``request`` roghnaí:class: `~django.http.httpRequest` a chuirtear ar an "
"modh ``fíordheimhniú () ``de na cúltaca fíordheimhnithe."

msgid ""
"This is a low level way to authenticate a set of credentials; for example, "
"it's used by "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.RemoteUserMiddleware`. Unless "
"you are writing your own authentication system, you probably won't use this. "
"Rather if you're looking for a way to login a user, use "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.views.LoginView`."
msgstr ""
"Is bealach ar leibhéal íseal é seo chun tacar dintiúir a fhíordheimhniú; mar "
"shampla, úsáideann an: class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.remoteUserMiddleware` é. Mura bhfuil do "
"chóras fíordheimhnithe féin á scríobh agat, is dócha nach n-úsáidfidh tú é "
"seo. Ina ionad sin má tá tú ag lorg bealach chun úsáideoir a logáil isteach, "
"bain úsáid as an:class: `~django.contrib.auth.views.loginView`."

msgid "Permissions and Authorization"
msgstr "Ceadanna agus Údarú"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a built-in permissions system. It provides a way to assign "
"permissions to specific users and groups of users."
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le córas ceadanna ionsuite. Soláthraíonn sé bealach chun "
"ceadanna a shannadh d'úsáideoirí agus do ghrúpaí úsáideoirí ar leith."

msgid ""
"It's used by the Django admin site, but you're welcome to use it in your own "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann suíomh riaracháin Django é, ach tá fáilte romhat é a úsáid i do "
"chód féin."

msgid "The Django admin site uses permissions as follows:"
msgstr "Úsáideann suíomh riaracháin Django ceadanna mar seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Access to view objects is limited to users with the \"view\" or \"change\" "
"permission for that type of object."
msgstr ""
"Tá rochtain ar rudaí féachana teoranta d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil an cead "
"“amharc” nó “athraigh” acu don chineál réada sin."

msgid ""
"Access to view the \"add\" form and add an object is limited to users with "
"the \"add\" permission for that type of object."
msgstr ""
"Tá rochtain chun an fhoirm “cuir leis” a fheiceáil agus réad a chur leis "
"teoranta d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil cead “cuir leis” don chineál réada sin."

msgid ""
"Access to view the change list, view the \"change\" form and change an "
"object is limited to users with the \"change\" permission for that type of "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Tá rochtain chun an liosta athraithe a fheiceáil, féachaint ar an bhfoirm "
"“athraigh” agus réad a athrú teoranta d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil cead “athraithe” "
"acu don chineál réada sin."

msgid ""
"Access to delete an object is limited to users with the \"delete\" "
"permission for that type of object."
msgstr ""
"Tá rochtain chun réad a scriosadh teoranta d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil cead "
"“scrios” acu don chineál réada sin."

msgid ""
"Permissions can be set not only per type of object, but also per specific "
"object instance. By using "
"the :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.has_view_permission`, :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.has_add_permission`, :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.has_change_permission` "
"and :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.has_delete_permission` methods "
"provided by the :class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` class, it is "
"possible to customize permissions for different object instances of the same "
"type."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ceadanna a shocrú ní amháin in aghaidh an chineál réada, ach "
"freisin de réir shampla réad ar leith. Trí úsáid a:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.has_view_permission`, :meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.has_add_permission`, :meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.has_change_permission` agus:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.Modhanna admin.modeladmin.has_delete_permission` a "
"sholáthraíonn an rang:class: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin`, is féidir "
"ceadanna a shaincheapadh do chásanna réad éagsúla den chineál céanna."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` objects have two many-to-many "
"fields: ``groups`` and "
"``user_permissions``. :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` objects can "
"access their related objects in the same way as any other :doc:`Django model "
"</topics/db/models>`::"
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.auth.models.User` tá dhá réimse go leor réimse ag "
"rudaí: ``groups`` agus ``user_permissions``. :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user` Is féidir le rudaí rochtain a fháil ar a "
"gcuid rudaí gaolmhara ar an mbealach céanna le haon ear:doc: `Django model "
"`</topics/db/models>:"

msgid "Default permissions"
msgstr "Ceadanna réamhshocrai"

msgid ""
"When ``django.contrib.auth`` is listed in your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` "
"setting, it will ensure that four default permissions -- add, change, "
"delete, and view -- are created for each Django model defined in one of your "
"installed applications."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a liostaítear ``django.contrib.auth`` i do shuíomh: `INSTALLED_APPS`, "
"cinnteoidh sé go gcruthaítear ceithre chead réamhshocraithe -- cuir, athrú, "
"scrios agus amharc - do gach samhail Django atá sainmhínithe i gceann de "
"d'fheidhmchláir suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"These permissions will be created when you run :djadmin:`manage.py migrate "
"<migrate>`; the first time you run ``migrate`` after adding "
"``django.contrib.auth`` to :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, the default "
"permissions will be created for all previously-installed models, as well as "
"for any new models being installed at that time. Afterward, it will create "
"default permissions for new models each time you run :djadmin:`manage.py "
"migrate <migrate>` (the function that creates permissions is connected to "
"the :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` signal)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthófar na ceadanna seo nuair a rith t:djadmin: `manage.py migration "
"<migrate>`; an chéad uair a reáchtáil tú ```migrate`` tar éis "
"``django.contrib.auth`` a chur chuig:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, cruthófar na "
"ceadanna réamhshocraithe do gach samhail atá suiteáilte roimhe seo, chomh "
"maith le haghaidh aon mhúnlaí nua atá suiteáilte ag an am sin. Ina dhiaidh "
"sin, cruthóidh sé ceadanna réamhshocraithe do mhúnlaí nua gach uair a rith "
"tú: djadmin: `manage.py migration <migrate>`(tá an fheidhm a chruthaíonn "
"ceadanna ceangailte leis an gcomhartha: data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate`)."

msgid ""
"Assuming you have an application with "
"an :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.app_label` ``foo`` and a model named "
"``Bar``, to test for basic permissions you should use:"
msgstr ""
"Ag glacadh leis go bhfuil feidhmchlár agat le an:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.app_label` ``foo`` agus samhail darb ainm "
"``Bar``, chun tástáil a dhéanamh ar cheadanna bunúsacha ba chóir duit a "
"úsáid:"

msgid "add: ``user.has_perm('foo.add_bar')``"
msgstr "cuir leis: ``user.has_perm ('foo.add_bar') ``"

msgid "change: ``user.has_perm('foo.change_bar')``"
msgstr "athrú: ``user.has_perm ('foo.change_bar') ``"

msgid "delete: ``user.has_perm('foo.delete_bar')``"
msgstr "scrios: ``user.has_perm ('foo.delete_bar') ``"

msgid "view: ``user.has_perm('foo.view_bar')``"
msgstr "amharc: ``user.has_perm ('foo.view_bar') ``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.Permission` model is rarely accessed "
"directly."
msgstr ""
"Is annamh a bhíonn rochtain dhíreach ar an msamhail:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.permission`."

msgid "Groups"
msgstr "Grúpaí"

msgid ""
":class:`django.contrib.auth.models.Group` models are a generic way of "
"categorizing users so you can apply permissions, or some other label, to "
"those users. A user can belong to any number of groups."
msgstr ""
":class: Is bealach cineálach iad samhlacha "
"`django.contrib.auth.models.group` chun úsáideoirí a chatagóiriú ionas gur "
"féidir leat ceadanna, nó lipéad éigin eile, a chur i bhfeidhm ar na "
"húsáideoirí sin. Is féidir le húsáideoir baineann le líon ar bith grúpaí."

msgid ""
"A user in a group automatically has the permissions granted to that group. "
"For example, if the group ``Site editors`` has the permission "
"``can_edit_home_page``, any user in that group will have that permission."
msgstr ""
"Tá na ceadanna deonaithe don ghrúpa sin go huathoibríoch ag úsáideoir i "
"ngrúpa. Mar shampla, má tá an cead `can_edit_home_page`` ag an ngrúpa "
"``eagarthóirí láithreáin``, beidh an cead sin ag aon úsáideoir sa ghrúpa sin."

msgid ""
"Beyond permissions, groups are a convenient way to categorize users to give "
"them some label, or extended functionality. For example, you could create a "
"group ``'Special users'``, and you could write code that could, say, give "
"them access to a members-only portion of your site, or send them members-"
"only email messages."
msgstr ""
"Seachas ceadanna, is bealach áisiúil iad grúpaí chun úsáideoirí a "
"chatagóiriú chun roinnt lipéad, nó feidhmiúlacht leathnaithe a thabhairt Mar "
"shampla, d'fhéadfá grúpa ````Úsáideoirí speisialta' a chruthú, agus "
"d'fhéadfá cód a scríobh a d'fhéadfadh, abair, rochtain a thabhairt dóibh ar "
"chuid de do shuíomh do bhaill amháin, nó teachtaireachtaí ríomhphoist do "
"bhaill amháin a sheoladh chucu."

msgid "Programmatically creating permissions"
msgstr "Ceadanna a chruthú go cláraitheach"

msgid ""
"While :ref:`custom permissions <custom-permissions>` can be defined within a "
"model's ``Meta`` class, you can also create permissions directly. For "
"example, you can create the ``can_publish`` permission for a ``BlogPost`` "
"model in ``myapp``::"
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir ceadanna saincheaptha a shainiú laisti <custom-permissions>gh "
"de rang ``Meta` samhail, is féidir leat ceadanna a chruthú go díreach "
"freisin. Mar shampla, is féidir leat an cead ``can_publish ``a chruthú do "
"mhúnla ``blogpost`` i `myapp``:"

msgid ""
"The permission can then be assigned to "
"a :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` via its ``user_permissions`` "
"attribute or to a :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.Group` via its "
"``permissions`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an cead a shannadh ansin do a:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user` tríd a thréith ``user_permissions`` nó "
"chuig a:class: `~django.contrib.auth.models.group` trína tréith "
"``permissions``."

msgid "Proxy models need their own content type"
msgstr "Teastaíonn a gcineál ábhair féin ó mhúnlaí"

msgid ""
"If you want to create :ref:`permissions for a proxy model <proxy-models-"
"permissions-topic>`, pass ``for_concrete_model=False`` "
"to :meth:`.ContentTypeManager.get_for_model` to get the appropriate "
"``ContentType``::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat: ref: `ceadanna do mhúnla seachfhreastala` a chruthú<proxy-"
"models-permissions-topic>, pas ``for_concrete_model=false`` chuig:meth: "
"`.contentTypeManager.get_for_model` chun an `ContentType`` cuí a fháil:"

msgid "Permission caching"
msgstr "Cacháil ceadanna"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend` caches permissions "
"on the user object after the first time they need to be fetched for a "
"permissions check. This is typically fine for the request-response cycle "
"since permissions aren't typically checked immediately after they are added "
"(in the admin, for example). If you are adding permissions and checking them "
"immediately afterward, in a test or view for example, the easiest solution "
"is to re-fetch the user from the database. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an: Class: `~django.contrib.auth.backends.modelBackend` ceadanna ar "
"an réad úsáideora tar éis an chéad uair is gá iad a fháil le haghaidh "
"seiceáil ceadanna. De ghnáth bíonn sé seo go breá don timthriall iarrata-"
"freagartha ós rud é nach ndéantar ceadanna a sheiceáil de ghnáth díreach tar "
"éis iad a chur leis (sa riarachán, mar shampla). Má tá ceadanna á chur leis "
"agus iad a sheiceáil díreach ina dhiaidh sin, i dtástáil nó i radharc mar "
"shampla, is é an réiteach is éasca an t-úsáideoir a fháil ón mbunachar "
"sonraí a ath-fháil. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Proxy models"
msgstr "Múnlaí proxy"

msgid ""
"Proxy models work exactly the same way as concrete models. Permissions are "
"created using the own content type of the proxy model. Proxy models don't "
"inherit the permissions of the concrete model they subclass::"
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn samhlacha seachfhreastalaí go díreach ar an mbealach céanna "
"Cruthaítear ceadanna ag baint úsáide as cineál ábhair féin an tsamhail "
"seachfhreastalaí Ní fhaigheann samhlacha seachfhreastalaí ceadanna an "
"tsamhail choincréite a fho-aicmigh siad:"

msgid "Authentication in web requests"
msgstr "Fíordheimhniú in iarratais gréasáin"

msgid ""
"Django uses :doc:`sessions </topics/http/sessions>` and middleware to hook "
"the authentication system into :class:`request objects "
"<django.http.HttpRequest>`."
msgstr ""
"</topics/http/sessions> <django.http.HttpRequest>Úsáideann Django: doc: "
"`seisiúin` agus middleware chun an córas fíordheimhnithe a cheangal "
"la:class: `iarr rudaí `."

msgid ""
"These provide a :attr:`request.user <django.http.HttpRequest.user>`  "
"attribute and a :meth:`request.auser <django.http.HttpRequest.auser>` async "
"method on every request which represents the current user. If the current "
"user has not logged in, this attribute will be set to an instance "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AnonymousUser`, otherwise it will be "
"an instance of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User`."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.auser>Soláthraíonn siad seo a: attr: `request.user "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.user>`tréith agus a:meth: `request.auser` modh "
"async ar gach iarratas a léiríonn an t-úsáideoir reatha. Mura bhfuil an t-"
"úsáideoir reatha logáil isteach, socraítear an tréith seo go sampla "
"de:class: `~django.contrib.auth.models.anonymousUser`, ar shlí eile beidh sé "
"ina shampla de:class: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user`."

msgid ""
"You can tell them apart "
"with :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_authenticated`, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat iad a insint óna chéile la:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.is_Authenticated`, mar sin:"

msgid "Or in an asynchronous view::"
msgstr "Nó i radharc asincrónach::"

msgid "How to log a user in"
msgstr "Conas úsáideoir a logáil isteach"

msgid ""
"If you have an authenticated user you want to attach to the current session "
"- this is done with a :func:`~django.contrib.auth.login` function."
msgstr ""
"Má tá úsáideoir fíordheimhnithe agat gur mhaith leat a cheangal leis an "
"seisiún reatha - déantar é seo le feidhm a:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.login`."

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``alogin()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``alogin () ``"

msgid ""
"To log a user in, from a view, use :func:`~django.contrib.auth.login()`. It "
"takes an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object and "
"a :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` "
"object. :func:`~django.contrib.auth.login()` saves the user's ID in the "
"session, using Django's session framework."
msgstr ""
"Chun úsáideoir a logáil isteach, ó radharc, bain úsáid as: func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.login () `. Tógann sé: aicme: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest` réad agus a:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user` réad. :func: Sábhálann "
"`~django.contrib.auth.login () `ID an úsáideora sa seisiún, ag baint úsáide "
"as creat seisiúin Django."

msgid ""
"Note that any data set during the anonymous session is retained in the "
"session after a user logs in."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcoinnítear aon tacar sonraí le linn an tseisiúin gan "
"ainm sa seisiún tar éis úsáideoir logáil isteach."

msgid ""
"This example shows how you might use "
"both :func:`~django.contrib.auth.authenticate()` "
"and :func:`~django.contrib.auth.login()`::"
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an sampla seo conas a d'fhéadfá an dá cheann a úsáid:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.auth.autenticate () `agus:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.login ()`:"

msgid "Selecting the authentication backend"
msgstr "An cúltaca fíordheimhnithe a roghnú"

msgid ""
"When a user logs in, the user's ID and the backend that was used for "
"authentication are saved in the user's session. This allows the "
"same :ref:`authentication backend <authentication-backends>` to fetch the "
"user's details on a future request. The authentication backend to save in "
"the session is selected as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a logálann úsáideoir isteach, sábhálfar aitheantas an úsáideora agus "
"an cúltaca a úsáideadh le haghaidh fíordheimhnithe i seisiún an úsáideora. "
"Ligeann sé seo an chéanna: ref: `backend fíordheimhniúcháin <authentication-"
"backends>`sonraí an úsáideora a fháil ar iarratas amach anseo. Roghnaítear "
"an cúltaca fíordheimhnithe le sábháil sa seisiún mar seo a leanas:"

msgid "Use the value of the optional ``backend`` argument, if provided."
msgstr "Úsáid luach an argóint roghnach ``backend`, má chuirtear ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Use the value of the ``user.backend`` attribute, if present. This allows "
"pairing :func:`~django.contrib.auth.authenticate()` "
"and :func:`~django.contrib.auth.login()`: :func:`~django.contrib.auth.authenticate()` "
"sets the ``user.backend`` attribute on the user object it returns."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid luach an tréith ``user.backend``, má tá sé ann. Ceadaíonn sé seo "
"péireáil: func: `~django.contrib.auth.autenticate () `agus:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.login ()`: :func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.auth.autenticate () `socraíonn an tréith "
"``user.backend`` ar an réad úsáideora a fhilleann sé."

msgid ""
"Use the ``backend`` in :setting:`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS`, if there is only "
"one."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an ``backend`` in:setting: `AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS`, mura bhfuil ach "
"ceann amháin ann."

msgid "Otherwise, raise an exception."
msgstr "Seachas sin, ardaigh eisceacht."

msgid ""
"In cases 1 and 2, the value of the ``backend`` argument or the "
"``user.backend`` attribute should be a dotted import path string (like that "
"found in :setting:`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS`), not the actual backend class."
msgstr ""
"I gcásanna 1 agus 2, ba chóir go mbeadh luach an argóint ``backend`` nó an "
"tréith ``user.backend`` ina shreang cosán allmhairiúcháin poncaí (cosúil "
"leis sin a fhaightear in:setting: `AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS`), ní an aicme "
"cúltaca iarbhír."

msgid "How to log a user out"
msgstr "Conas úsáideoir a logáil amach"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``alogout()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``alogout () ``"

msgid ""
"To log out a user who has been logged in "
"via :func:`django.contrib.auth.login()`, "
"use :func:`django.contrib.auth.logout()` within your view. It takes "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object and has no return value. "
"Example::"
msgstr ""
"Chun logáil amach úsáideoir atá logáilte isteach trí:func: "
"`django.contrib.auth.login () `, bain úsáid as: func: "
"`django.contrib.auth.logout ()` laistigh de d'amharc. Tógann sé réad: class: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest` agus níl aon luach tuairisceáin aige. Sampla::"

msgid ""
"Note that :func:`~django.contrib.auth.logout()` doesn't throw any errors if "
"the user wasn't logged in."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach gcaitheann :func: `~django.contrib.auth.logout () "
"`aon earráidí mura raibh an t-úsáideoir logáilte isteach."

msgid ""
"When you call :func:`~django.contrib.auth.logout()`, the session data for "
"the current request is completely cleaned out. All existing data is removed. "
"This is to prevent another person from using the same web browser to log in "
"and have access to the previous user's session data. If you want to put "
"anything into the session that will be available to the user immediately "
"after logging out, do that *after* "
"calling :func:`django.contrib.auth.logout()`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a ghlaonn tú: func: `~django.contrib.auth.logout () `, glantar sonraí "
"na seisiúin don iarraidh reatha go hiomlán amach. Baintear na sonraí go léir "
"atá ann cheana. Is é seo chun cosc a chur ar dhuine eile an brabhsálaí "
"gréasáin céanna a úsáid chun logáil isteach agus rochtain a fháil ar shonraí "
"seisiún an úsáideora roimhe seo. Más mian leat rud ar bith a chur isteach sa "
"seisiún a bheidh ar fáil don úsáideoir díreach tar éis logáil amach, déan "
"sean*tar éis dó* glaoi:func: `django.contrib.auth.logout () `."

msgid "Limiting access to logged-in users"
msgstr "Rochtain a theorannú ar úsáideoirí logáilte isteach"

msgid "The raw way"
msgstr "An bealach amh"

msgid ""
"The raw way to limit access to pages is to "
"check :attr:`request.user.is_authenticated "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_authenticated>` and either redirect to a "
"login page::"
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_authenticated>Is é an bealach amh chun "
"rochtain ar leathanaigh a theorannú ná seiceál:attr: "
"`request.user.is_authorated `agus ceachtar acu a atreorú chuig leathanach "
"logála isteach::"

msgid "...or display an error message::"
msgstr "... nó teachtaireacht earráide a thaispeáint::"

msgid "The ``login_required`` decorator"
msgstr "An maisitheoir ``login_required``"

msgid ""
"As a shortcut, you can use the "
"convenient :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Mar aicearra, is féidir leat an maisitheoir áisiúil: func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` a úsáid:"

msgid ""
":func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` does the following:"
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` déanann an méid seo "
"a leanas:"

msgid ""
"If the user isn't logged in, redirect to :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL "
"<LOGIN_URL>`, passing the current absolute path in the query string. "
"Example: ``/accounts/login/?next=/polls/3/``."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an t-úsáideoir logáilte isteach, atreoraigh chuig:setting: "
"`settings.login_url <LOGIN_URL>`, ag dul ar an gcosán iomlán reatha sa "
"sreangán fiosrúcháin. Sampla: ``/cuntais/logáil isteach/? next =/polls/3/``."

msgid ""
"If the user is logged in, execute the view normally. The view code is free "
"to assume the user is logged in."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an t-úsáideoir logáilte isteach, déan an radharc a dhéanamh de ghnáth. "
"Tá an cód amharc saor in aisce glacadh leis go bhfuil an t-úsáideoir "
"logáilte isteach."

msgid ""
"By default, the path that the user should be redirected to upon successful "
"authentication is stored in a query string parameter called ``\"next\"``. If "
"you would prefer to use a different name for this "
"parameter, :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` takes an "
"optional ``redirect_field_name`` parameter::"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, stóráiltear an cosán ar chóir an t-úsáideoir a "
"atreorú chuig nuair a fhíordheimhniú rathúil i bparaiméadar teaghrán "
"ceisteanna ar a dtugtar ``\"next” `. Más fearr leat ainm difriúil a úsáid "
"don pharaiméadar seo, glacann: :func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` paraiméadar roghnach "
"``redirect_field_name``:"

msgid ""
"Note that if you provide a value to ``redirect_field_name``, you will most "
"likely need to customize your login template as well, since the template "
"context variable which stores the redirect path will use the value of "
"``redirect_field_name`` as its key rather than ``\"next\"`` (the default)."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara má sholáthraíonn tú luach do `redirect_field_name``, is "
"dócha go mbeidh ort do theimpléad logála isteach a shaincheapadh freisin, ós "
"rud é go n-úsáidfidh an athróg comhthéacs teimpléid a stóráilíonn an cosán "
"atreoraithe luach ``redirect_field_name`` mar eochair seachas ``\"next” `(an "
"réamhshocraithe)."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` also takes an "
"optional ``login_url`` parameter. Example::"
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` tógann paraiméadar "
"roghnach ``login_url ``freisin. Sampla::"

msgid ""
"Note that if you don't specify the ``login_url`` parameter, you'll need to "
"ensure that the :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL <LOGIN_URL>` and your login "
"view are properly associated. For example, using the defaults, add the "
"following lines to your URLconf::"
msgstr ""
"<LOGIN_URL>Tabhair faoi deara mura sonraíonn tú an paraiméadar ``login_url "
"``, beidh ort a chinntiú go bhfuil baint i gceart la:setting: "
"`settings.login_URL `agus d'amharc logála isteach. Mar shampla, ag baint "
"úsáide as na réamhshocruithe, cuir na línte seo a leanas le do URLConf:"

msgid ""
"The :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL <LOGIN_URL>` also accepts view function "
"names and :ref:`named URL patterns <naming-url-patterns>`. This allows you "
"to freely remap your login view within your URLconf without having to update "
"the setting."
msgstr ""
"<naming-url-patterns>Glacann an: setting: `settings.login_URL <LOGIN_URL>`le "
"hainmneacha feidhm amharc agus:ref: `patrúin URL ainmnithe`. Ligeann sé seo "
"duit do radharc logála isteach a athmhapáil go saor laistigh de do URLConf "
"gan an socrú a nuashonrú."

msgid ""
"The ``login_required`` decorator does NOT check the ``is_active`` flag on a "
"user, but the default :setting:`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` reject inactive "
"users."
msgstr ""
"NÍ sheiceálann an maisitheoir ``login_required`` an bhratach ``is_active`` "
"ar úsáideoir, ach diúltaíonn an réamhshocraithe:setting: "
"`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` úsáideoirí neamhghníomhacha."

msgid ""
"If you are writing custom views for Django's admin (or need the same "
"authorization check that the built-in views use), you may find "
"the :func:`django.contrib.admin.views.decorators.staff_member_required` "
"decorator a useful alternative to ``login_required()``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tuairimí saincheaptha á scríobh agat do riarachán Django (nó má "
"theastaíonn an seiceáil údaraithe céanna uait a úsáideann na tuairimí "
"ionsuite), b'fhéidir go bhfaighidh tú an:func: "
"`django.contrib.admin.views.decorators.staff_member_required` rogha "
"úsáideach seachas `login_required () `."

msgid "Support for wrapping asynchronous view functions was added."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht le haghaidh feidhmeanna amharc asincrónacha a fhilleadh."

msgid "The ``LoginRequiredMixin`` mixin"
msgstr "An meascán ``LoginRequiredMixin``"

msgid ""
"When using :doc:`class-based views </topics/class-based-views/index>`, you "
"can achieve the same behavior as with ``login_required`` by using the "
"``LoginRequiredMixin``. This mixin should be at the leftmost position in the "
"inheritance list."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáideann tú: doc: `tuairimí rang-bhunaithe ', is féidir leat an t-"
"iompar céanna a bhaint amach agus le ``login_required`` </topics/class-based-"
"views/index> tríd an `LoginRequiredMixin`` a úsáid. Ba chóir go mbeadh an "
"meascán seo ag an suíomh is clé sa liosta oidhreachta."

msgid ""
"If a view is using this mixin, all requests by non-authenticated users will "
"be redirected to the login page or shown an HTTP 403 Forbidden error, "
"depending on "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin.raise_exception` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an mixin seo á úsáid ag amharc, atreorófar gach iarratas ó úsáideoirí "
"neamh-fhíordheimhnithe chuig an leathanach logála isteach nó taispeánfar "
"earráid toirmiscthe HTTP 403, ag brath ar an bparaiméadar: attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessmixin.raise_exception`."

msgid ""
"You can set any of the parameters "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin` to customize the "
"handling of unauthorized users::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat aon cheann de na paraiméadair de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessMixin` a shocrú chun láimhseáil "
"úsáideoirí neamhúdaraithe a shaincheapadh::"

msgid ""
"Just as the ``login_required`` decorator, this mixin does NOT check the "
"``is_active`` flag on a user, but the "
"default :setting:`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` reject inactive users."
msgstr ""
"Díreach mar an maisitheoir ``login_required``, NÍ sheiceálann an meascán seo "
"an bhratach ``is_active`` ar úsáideoir, ach diúltaíonn an "
"réamhshocraithe:setting: `AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` úsáideoirí "
"neamhghníomhacha."

msgid "The ``login_not_required`` decorator"
msgstr "An maisitheoir ``login_not_required``"

msgid ""
"When :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.LoginRequiredMiddleware` is "
"installed, all views require authentication by default. Some views, such as "
"the login view, may need to disable this behavior."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn: Class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.loginrequiredMiddleware` suiteáilte, "
"teastaíonn fíordheimhniú de réir réamhshocraithe ó gach radharc. B'fhéidir "
"go mbeidh ar roinnt tuairimí, mar shampla an radharc logála isteach, an t-"
"iompar seo a dhíchumas"

msgid ""
"Allows unauthenticated requests to this view "
"when :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.LoginRequiredMiddleware` is "
"installed."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn sé iarratais neamhfhíordheimhnithe chuig an radharc seo "
"nuai:class: `~django.contrib.auth.middleware.loginrequiredMiddleware` "
"suiteáilte."

msgid "Limiting access to logged-in users that pass a test"
msgstr "Rochtain a theorannú ar úsáideoirí logáilte isteach a rachaidh tástáil"

msgid ""
"To limit access based on certain permissions or some other test, you'd do "
"essentially the same thing as described in the previous section."
msgstr ""
"Chun rochtain a theorannú bunaithe ar cheadanna áirithe nó ar thástáil éigin "
"eile, déanfá an rud céanna go bunúsach mar a thuairiscítear sa chuid roimhe "
"seo."

msgid ""
"You can run your test on :attr:`request.user <django.http.HttpRequest.user>` "
"in the view directly. For example, this view checks to make sure the user "
"has an email in the desired domain and if not, redirects to the login page::"
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.user>Is féidir leat do thástáil a reáchtáil "
"ar:attr: `request.user `sa radharc go díreach. Mar shampla, seiceálann an "
"radharc seo chun a chinntiú go bhfuil ríomhphost ag an úsáideoir sa réimse "
"atá ag teastáil agus mura bhfuil, atreoraíonn sé chuig an leathanach logála "
"isteach::"

msgid ""
"As a shortcut, you can use the convenient ``user_passes_test`` decorator "
"which performs a redirect when the callable returns ``False``::"
msgstr ""
"Mar aicearra, is féidir leat an maisitheoir áisiúil ``user_passes_test`` a "
"úsáid a dhéanann atreorú nuair a fhilleann an t-inghlaoch ``False``:"

msgid ""
":func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.user_passes_test` takes a required "
"argument: a callable that takes a :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` "
"object and returns ``True`` if the user is allowed to view the page. Note "
"that :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.user_passes_test` does not "
"automatically check that the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` is "
"not anonymous."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.contrib.auth.decorators.user_passes_test` glacann argóint "
"riachtanach: glaoch a thógann a:class: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user` "
"réad agus filleann ``True`` má cheadaítear don úsáideoir an leathanach a "
"fheiceáil. Tabhair faoi deara nach seiceálann :func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.user_passes_test` go huathoibríoch nach "
"bhfuil an:class: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user` gan ainm."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.user_passes_test` takes two optional "
"arguments:"
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.contrib.auth.decorators.user_passes_test` glacann dhá "
"argóint roghnach:"

msgid "``login_url``"
msgstr "``log_url``"

msgid ""
"Lets you specify the URL that users who don't pass the test will be "
"redirected to. It may be a login page and defaults "
"to :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL <LOGIN_URL>` if you don't specify one."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann duit an URL a shonrú a atreorófar úsáideoirí nach rachaidh an "
"tástáil chuig. <LOGIN_URL>D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh sé ina leathanach logála "
"isteach agus réamhshocraithe to:setting: `settings.login_url `mura sonraíonn "
"tú ceann amháin."

msgid "``redirect_field_name``"
msgstr "``ainm_redirect_field``"

msgid ""
"Same as for :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required`. Setting "
"it to ``None`` removes it from the URL, which you may want to do if you are "
"redirecting users that don't pass the test to a non-login page where there's "
"no \"next page\"."
msgstr ""
"Mar an gcéanna le haghaidh: func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required`. Ag socrú é go ``None "
"``baintear é as an URL, rud a d'fhéadfá a dhéanamh má tá tú ag atreorú "
"úsáideoirí nach dtéann an tástáil chuig leathanach neamh-logála isteach nach "
"bhfuil “an chéad leathanach eile” ann."

msgid ""
"Support for wrapping asynchronous view functions and using asynchronous test "
"callables was added."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht le haghaidh feidhmeanna amharc asincrónacha a fhilleadh "
"agus glaonna tástála asincrónacha a úsáid."

msgid ""
"When using :doc:`class-based views </topics/class-based-views/index>`, you "
"can use the ``UserPassesTestMixin`` to do this."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáideann tú: doc: `tuairimí rang-bhunaithe ', is féidir leat an "
"``UserPassestestMixin`` a úsáid chun </topics/class-based-views/index> é seo "
"a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"You have to override the ``test_func()`` method of the class to provide the "
"test that is performed. Furthermore, you can set any of the parameters "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin` to customize the "
"handling of unauthorized users::"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh tú an modh `test_func () ``den rang a shárú chun an tástáil a "
"dhéantar a sholáthar. Ina theannta sin, is féidir leat aon cheann de na "
"paraiméadair de:class: `~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessMixin` a shocrú "
"chun láimhseáil úsáideoirí neamhúdaraithe a shaincheapadh::"

msgid ""
"You can also override the ``get_test_func()`` method to have the mixin use a "
"differently named function for its checks (instead of :meth:`test_func`)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an modh ``get_test_func () ``a shárú freisin chun feidhm "
"ainmnithe difriúil a úsáideann an mixin dá sheiceálacha (in ionad:meth: "
"`test_func`)."

msgid "Stacking ``UserPassesTestMixin``"
msgstr "Cruachadh ``UserPassestestMixin``"

msgid ""
"Due to the way ``UserPassesTestMixin`` is implemented, you cannot stack them "
"in your inheritance list. The following does NOT work::"
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an mbealach a chuirtear ``UserPassestestMixin`` i bhfeidhm, ní "
"féidir leat iad a chruachadh i do liosta oidhreachta. NÍ oibríonn an méid "
"seo a leanas::"

msgid ""
"If ``TestMixin1`` would call ``super()`` and take that result into account, "
"``TestMixin1`` wouldn't work standalone anymore."
msgstr ""
"Dá ndéanfadh ``TestMixin1`` glaoch ar ``super () ``agus go gcuirfeadh an "
"toradh sin san áireamh, ní oibreodh ``TestMixin1`` neamhspleách níos mó."

msgid "The ``permission_required`` decorator"
msgstr "An maisitheoir ``ceadú_riachtana``"

msgid ""
"It's a relatively common task to check whether a user has a particular "
"permission. For that reason, Django provides a shortcut for that case: "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required()` decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Is tasc réasúnta coitianta é a sheiceáil an bhfuil cead áirithe ag "
"úsáideoir. Ar an gcúis sin, soláthraíonn Django aicearra don chás sin: "
"the:func: `~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required () "
"`decorator::"

msgid ""
"Just like the :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_perm` method, "
"permission names take the form ``\"<app label>.<permission codename>\"`` "
"(i.e. ``polls.add_choice`` for a permission on a model in the ``polls`` "
"application)."
msgstr ""
"<app label>Díreach cosúil leis an modh:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.has_perm`, glacann ainmneacha ceada an "
"fhoirm ``”. <permission codename>“``(ie ``polls.add_choice`` le haghaidh "
"cead ar mhúnla san iarratas ``polls``)."

msgid ""
"The decorator may also take an iterable of permissions, in which case the "
"user must have all of the permissions in order to access the view."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh an maisitheoir ceadanna in-athraithe a ghlacadh freisin, agus sa "
"chás sin caithfidh na ceadanna go léir a bheith ag an úsáideoir chun "
"rochtain a fháil ar an radharc."

msgid ""
"Note that :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required()` also "
"takes an optional ``login_url`` parameter::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go dtógann: func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required () `paraiméadar "
"roghnach ``login_url ``freisin:"

msgid ""
"As in the :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` decorator, "
"``login_url`` defaults to :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL <LOGIN_URL>`."
msgstr ""
"<LOGIN_URL>Mar atá sa maisitheoir: func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required`, réamhshocraithe "
"``login_url ``: socrú: `Settings.login_url `."

msgid ""
"If the ``raise_exception`` parameter is given, the decorator will "
"raise :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied`, prompting :ref:`the "
"403 (HTTP Forbidden) view<http_forbidden_view>` instead of redirecting to "
"the login page."
msgstr ""
"<http_forbidden_view>Má thugtar an paraiméadar ``raise_exception``, ardóidh "
"an maisitheoir:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.permissiondenied`, ag "
"iarraidh:ref: `an amharc 403 (HTTP Forbidden) `in ionad atreorú chuig an "
"leathanach logála isteach."

msgid ""
"If you want to use ``raise_exception`` but also give your users a chance to "
"login first, you can add "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat ``raise_exception`` a úsáid ach deis a thabhairt d'úsáideoirí "
"logáil isteach ar dtús, is féidir leat an maisitheoir: func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` a chur leis:"

msgid ""
"This also avoids a redirect loop when :class:`.LoginView`'s "
"``redirect_authenticated_user=True`` and the logged-in user doesn't have all "
"of the required permissions."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíonn sé seo lúb atreoraithe freisin nuai:class: `.loginView` "
"``Redirect_Authenticated_user=True`` agus níl na ceadanna riachtanacha go "
"léir ag an úsáideoir logáilte isteach."

msgid "The ``PermissionRequiredMixin`` mixin"
msgstr "An meascán ``Ceadúnas RequiredMixin``"

msgid ""
"To apply permission checks to :doc:`class-based views </ref/class-based-"
"views/index>`, you can use the ``PermissionRequiredMixin``:"
msgstr ""
"Chun seiceálacha ceada a chur i bhfeidhm chuig:doc: `tuairimí rang-bhunaithe "
"', is féidir leat an ``PermissionRequiredMixin`` </ref/class-based-views/"
"index> a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"This mixin, just like the ``permission_required`` decorator, checks whether "
"the user accessing a view has all given permissions. You should specify the "
"permission (or an iterable of permissions) using the ``permission_required`` "
"parameter::"
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann an meascán seo, díreach cosúil leis an maisitheoir "
"``permission_required``, an bhfuil gach cead tugtha ag an úsáideoir a "
"rochtain ar radharc. Ba chóir duit an cead a shonrú (nó ceadanna "
"inathraithe) ag baint úsáide as an paraiméadar ``permission_required``:"

msgid ""
"You can set any of the parameters "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin` to customize the "
"handling of unauthorized users."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat aon cheann de na paraiméadair de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessMixin` a shocrú chun láimhseáil "
"úsáideoirí neamhúdaraithe a shaincheapadh."

msgid "You may also override these methods:"
msgstr "Féadfaidh tú na modhanna seo a shárú freisin:"

msgid ""
"Returns an iterable of permission names used by the mixin. Defaults to the "
"``permission_required`` attribute, converted to a tuple if necessary."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ainmneacha ceada a úsáideann an mixin ar ais. Réamhshocraithe go "
"dtí an tréith ``permission_required``, a thiontú go tuple más gá."

msgid ""
"Returns a boolean denoting whether the current user has permission to "
"execute the decorated view. By default, this returns the result of "
"calling :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_perms()` with the list "
"of permissions returned by :meth:`get_permission_required()`."
msgstr ""
"Filleann boolean a thugann le fios an bhfuil cead ag an úsáideoir reatha an "
"radharc maisithe a fhorghníomhú. De réir réamhshocraithe, filleann sé seo "
"toradh glaoi:meth: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.has_perms () `leis an "
"liosta ceadanna ar ais ar:meth: `get_permission_required ()`."

msgid "Redirecting unauthorized requests in class-based views"
msgstr "Iarrataí neamhúdaraithe a atreorú i dtuairimí bunaithe"

msgid ""
"To ease the handling of access restrictions in :doc:`class-based views </ref/"
"class-based-views/index>`, the ``AccessMixin`` can be used to configure the "
"behavior of a view when access is denied. Authenticated users are denied "
"access with an HTTP 403 Forbidden response. Anonymous users are redirected "
"to the login page or shown an HTTP 403 Forbidden response, depending on "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin.raise_exception` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""
"Chun láimhseáil srianta rochtana in:doc: `tuairimí rang-bhunaithe 'a mhaolú, "
"is féidir an ``AccessMixin`` a úsáid chun iompar radharc a chumrú nuair a "
"dhiúlta</ref/class-based-views/index> ítear rochtain. Diúltaítear rochtain "
"d'úsáideoirí fíordheimhnithe le freagra toirmiscthe HTTP 403. Atreoraítear "
"úsáideoirí gan ainm chuig an leathanach logála isteach nó taispeántar "
"freagra toirmiscthe HTTP 403, ag brath ar thréith: attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessmixin.raise_exception`."

msgid ""
"Default return value for :meth:`get_login_url`.  Defaults to ``None`` in "
"which case :meth:`get_login_url` falls back to :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL "
"<LOGIN_URL>`."
msgstr ""
"Luach tuairisceáin réamhshocraithe le haghaidh: meth: `get_login_url`. "
"<LOGIN_URL>Réamhshocraithe go ``None`` ina dtagann cás: meth: "
"`get_login_url` ar ais chuig: socrú: `settings.login_url `."

msgid ""
"Default return value for :meth:`get_permission_denied_message`. Defaults to "
"an empty string."
msgstr ""
"Luach tuairisceáin réamhshocraithe le haghaidh: meth: "
"`get_permission_denied_message`. Réamhshocraithe chuig teaghrán folamh."

msgid ""
"Default return value for :meth:`get_redirect_field_name`. Defaults to "
"``\"next\"``."
msgstr ""
"Luach tuairisceáin réamhshocraithe le haghaidh: meth: "
"`get_redirect_field_name`. Réamhshocraithe go ``\"eile” ``."

msgid ""
"If this attribute is set to ``True``, "
"a :class:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied` exception is raised when "
"the conditions are not met.  When ``False`` (the default), anonymous users "
"are redirected to the login page."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an tréith seo socraithe go ``True``, ardaítear eisceacht: a:class: "
"`~django.core.Exceptions.PermissionDenied` nuair nach gcomhlíontar na "
"coinníollacha. Nuair a dhéantar `False`` (an réamhshocrú), atreoraítear "
"úsáideoirí gan ainm chuig an leathanach logála isteach."

msgid ""
"Returns the URL that users who don't pass the test will be redirected to. "
"Returns :attr:`login_url` if set, or :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL "
"<LOGIN_URL>` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an URL ar ais a atreorófar úsáideoirí nach rachaidh an tástáil "
"chuig. <LOGIN_URL>Tuairisceáin: attr: `login_url` má tá sé socraithe, nó: "
"setting: `settings.login_url `ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"When :attr:`raise_exception` is ``True``, this method can be used to control "
"the error message passed to the error handler for display to the user. "
"Returns the :attr:`permission_denied_message` attribute by default."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: attr: `raise_exception` ``True``, is féidir an modh seo a úsáid chun "
"an teachtaireacht earráide a chuirtear chuig an láimhseálaí earráide a rialú "
"lena thaispeáint don úsáideoir. Tugann an tréith: attr: "
"`permission_denied_message` ar ais de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Returns the name of the query parameter that will contain the URL the user "
"should be redirected to after a successful login. If you set this to "
"``None``, a query parameter won't be added. Returns "
"the :attr:`redirect_field_name` attribute by default."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ainm an pharaiméadair fiosrúcháin ina mbeidh an URL ba chóir an t-"
"úsáideoir a atreorú chuig tar éis logáil isteach rathúil. Má shocraíonn tú é "
"seo go ``None ``, ní chuirfear paraiméadar ceisteanna leis. Tugann an "
"tréith: attr: `redirect_field_name` ar ais de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Depending on the value of ``raise_exception``, the method either raises "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied` exception or redirects the "
"user to the ``login_url``, optionally including the ``redirect_field_name`` "
"if it is set."
msgstr ""
"Ag brath ar luach ``raise_exception``, ardaíonn an modh eisceacht a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.permissionDenied` nó atreoraíonn an t-úsáideoir "
"chuig an `login_url ``, roghnach lena n-áirítear an ``redirect_field_name`` "
"má tá sé socraithe."

msgid "Session invalidation on password change"
msgstr "Neamhbhailí seisiúin ar athrú pasfhocal"

msgid ""
"If your :setting:`AUTH_USER_MODEL` inherits "
"from :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser` or implements its "
"own :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash()` "
"method, authenticated sessions will include the hash returned by this "
"function. In the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser` case, "
"this is an HMAC of the password field. Django verifies that the hash in the "
"session for each request matches the one that's computed during the request. "
"This allows a user to log out all of their sessions by changing their "
"password."
msgstr ""
"Má tá do: setting: `AUTH_USER_MODEL` oidhreacht ó:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.abstractBaseUser` nó má chuireann sé a modh "
"féin: meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.abstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash () `san "
"áireamh seisiúin fhíordheimhnithe an hash ar ais ag an bhfeidhm seo. Sa "
"chás: class: `~django.contrib.auth.Models.AbstractBaseUser`, is HMAC é seo "
"den réimse pasfhocal. Fíoraíonn Django go n-oireann an hash sa seisiún do "
"gach iarratas leis an gceann a ríomhtar le linn na hiarratais. Ligeann sé "
"seo d'úsáideoir a gcuid seisiúin go léir a logáil amach trína bhfocal faire "
"a athrú."

msgid ""
"The default password change views included with "
"Django, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.views.PasswordChangeView` and the "
"``user_change_password`` view in the :mod:`django.contrib.auth` admin, "
"update the session with the new password hash so that a user changing their "
"own password won't log themselves out. If you have a custom password change "
"view and wish to have similar behavior, use "
"the :func:`update_session_auth_hash` function."
msgstr ""
"Na tuairimí athraithe pasfhocal réamhshocraithe san áireamh le "
"Django, :class: `~django.contrib.auth.views.passwordChangeView` agus an "
"radharc ``user_change_password`` in:mod: `django.contrib.auth` admin, "
"nuashonraigh an seisiún leis an hash pasfhocal nua ionas nach logálfaidh "
"úsáideoir a phasfhocal féin. Má tá amharc saincheaptha athraithe pasfhocal "
"agat agus má theastaíonn uait iompar den chineál céanna a bheith agat, bain "
"úsáid as an bhfeidhm:func: `update_session_auth_hash`."

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aupdate_session_auth_hash()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aupdate_session_auth_hash () ``"

msgid ""
"This function takes the current request and the updated user object from "
"which the new session hash will be derived and updates the session hash "
"appropriately. It also rotates the session key so that a stolen session "
"cookie will be invalidated."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an fheidhm seo an t-iarratas reatha agus an réad úsáideora "
"nuashonraithe as a ndíorthófar an hash seisiúin nua agus nuashonraíonn sé an "
"hash seisiúin go cuí. Rothlaíonn sé an eochair seisiúin freisin ionas go "
"ndéanfar fianán seisiúin goidte a chur ar bhailí."

msgid "Example usage::"
msgstr "Úsáid sampla::"

msgid ""
"Since :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash()` "
"is based on :setting:`SECRET_KEY`, secret key values must be rotated to "
"avoid invalidating existing sessions when updating your site to use a new "
"secret. See :setting:`SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS` for details."
msgstr ""
"Ó shin: Meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.abstractbaseUser.get_session_auth_hash () "
"`bunaithe ar:setting: `SECRET_KEY`, caithfear príomhluachanna rúnda a rothlú "
"chun seisiúin atá ann cheana a sheachaint agus do shuíomh á nuashonrú chun "
"rún nua a úsáid. Féach: SETTING: `SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Authentication Views"
msgstr "Radhairc Fíordheimhni"

msgid ""
"Django provides several views that you can use for handling login, logout, "
"and password management. These make use of the :ref:`stock auth forms <built-"
"in-auth-forms>` but you can pass in your own forms as well."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django roinnt tuairimí is féidir leat a úsáid chun logáil "
"isteach, logáil amach agus bainistíocht pasfhocal a láimhseáil. Úsáideann "
"siad seo na foirmeacha: ref: `stoc auth <built-in-auth-forms>`ach is féidir "
"leat dul i do fhoirmeacha féin freisin."

msgid ""
"Django provides no default template for the authentication views. You should "
"create your own templates for the views you want to use. The template "
"context is documented in each view, see :ref:`all-authentication-views`."
msgstr ""
"Ní sholáthraíonn Django aon teimpléad réamhshocraithe do na tuairimí fí Ba "
"chóir duit do theimpléid féin a chruthú do na tuairimí is mian leat a úsáid. "
"Tá comhthéacs an teimpléid doiciméadaithe i ngach amharc, féach:ref: `all-"
"autentiúcháin-views`."

msgid "Using the views"
msgstr "Úsáid na tuairimí"

msgid ""
"There are different methods to implement these views in your project. The "
"easiest way is to include the provided URLconf in "
"``django.contrib.auth.urls`` in your own URLconf, for example::"
msgstr ""
"Tá modhanna difriúla ann chun na tuairimí seo a chur i bhfeidhm i do "
"thionscadal Is é an bealach is éasca ná an URLConf a chuirtear ar fáil a "
"áireamh in ``django.contrib.auth.urls`` i do URLConf féin, mar shampla:"

msgid "This will include the following URL patterns:"
msgstr "Áireofar seo na patrúin URL seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The views provide a URL name for easier reference. See :doc:`the URL "
"documentation </topics/http/urls>` for details on using named URL patterns."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn na tuairimí ainm URL le haghaidh tagartha níos éasca. Féach: "
"doc: `an doiciméadú URL` le haghaidh sonraí maidir le patrúin URL </topics/"
"http/urls> ainmnithe a úsáid."

msgid ""
"If you want more control over your URLs, you can reference a specific view "
"in your URLconf::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat níos mó smachta ar do URLanna, is féidir leat tagairt a "
"dhéanamh do radharc ar leith i do URLConf:"

msgid ""
"The views have optional arguments you can use to alter the behavior of the "
"view. For example, if you want to change the template name a view uses, you "
"can provide the ``template_name`` argument. A way to do this is to provide "
"keyword arguments in the URLconf, these will be passed on to the view. For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Tá argóintí roghnacha ag na tuairimí is féidir leat a úsáid chun iompar an "
"radharc a athrú. Mar shampla, más mian leat an t-ainm teimpléid a úsáideann "
"amharc a athrú, is féidir leat an argóint ``template_name`` a sholáthar. "
"Bealach chun é seo a dhéanamh ná argóintí eochairfhocal a sholáthar sa "
"URLConf, cuirfear iad seo ar aghaidh chuig an dearcadh. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"All views are :doc:`class-based </topics/class-based-views/index>`, which "
"allows you to easily customize them by subclassing."
msgstr ""
"Is iad na tuairimí go léir:doc: `class-based` </topics/class-based-views/"
"index>, rud a ligeann duit iad a shaincheapadh go héasca trí fho-aicmiú."

msgid "All authentication views"
msgstr "Gach tuairim fíordheimhni"

msgid ""
"This is a list with all the views ``django.contrib.auth`` provides. For "
"implementation details see :ref:`using-the-views`."
msgstr ""
"Seo liosta leis na tuairimí go léir a sholáthraíonn ``django.contrib.auth``. "
"Le haghaidh sonraí cur chun feidhme féach:ref: `using-the-views`."

msgid "**URL name:** ``login``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ``logáil isteach ``"

msgid ""
"See :doc:`the URL documentation </topics/http/urls>` for details on using "
"named URL patterns."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `an doiciméadú URL` le haghaidh sonraí maidir le patrúin URL </"
"topics/http/urls> ainmnithe a úsáid."

msgid "**Methods and Attributes**"
msgstr "**Modhanna agus Gnéithe **"

msgid ""
"The name of a template to display for the view used to log the user in. "
"Defaults to :file:`registration/login.html`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm teimpléad le taispeáint don amharc a úsáidtear chun an t-úsáideoir a "
"logáil isteach. Réamhshocraithe chuig: file: `clárúcháin/logain.html`."

msgid ""
"The URL to redirect to after login. Defaults "
"to :setting:`LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL`."
msgstr ""
"An URL le atreorú chuig tar éis logáil isteach. Réamhshocraithe chuig: "
"socrú: `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL`."

msgid ""
"The name of a ``GET`` field containing the URL to redirect to after login. "
"Defaults to ``next``. Overrides the :meth:`get_default_redirect_url` URL if "
"the given ``GET`` parameter is passed."
msgstr ""
"Ainm réimse ``GET`` ina bhfuil an URL le atreorú chuig tar éis logáil "
"isteach. Réamhshocraithe go ```next ``. Sáraíonn an URL:meth: "
"`get_default_redirect_url` má chuirtear an paraiméadar ``GET`` a thugtar."

msgid ""
"A callable (typically a form class) to use for authentication. Defaults "
"to :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir glaoch (rang foirme de ghnáth) le húsáid le haghaidh "
"fíordheimhnithe. Réamhshocraithe chuig: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm`."

msgid ""
"A dictionary of context data that will be added to the default context data "
"passed to the template."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir sonraí comhthéacs a chuirfear leis na sonraí comhthéacs "
"réamhshocraithe a chuirtear chuig an teimpléad."

msgid ""
"A boolean that controls whether or not authenticated users accessing the "
"login page will be redirected as if they had just successfully logged in. "
"Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Déanfar boolean a rialaíonn cibé acu úsáideoirí fíordheimhnithe a rochtann "
"rochtain ar an leathanach logála isteach a atreorú amhail is dá ndearna siad "
"logáil isteach go rathúil. Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid ""
"If you enable ``redirect_authenticated_user``, other websites will be able "
"to determine if their visitors are authenticated on your site by requesting "
"redirect URLs to image files on your website. To avoid this \"`social media "
"fingerprinting <https://robinlinus.github.io/socialmedia-leak/>`_\" "
"information leakage, host all images and your favicon on a separate domain."
msgstr ""
"Má chumasaíonn tú ``redirect_autenticated_user``, beidh láithreáin ghréasáin "
"eile in ann a chinneadh an bhfuil a gcuairteoirí fíordheimhnithe ar do "
"shuíomh trí URLanna atreoraithe a iarraidh chuig comhaid íomhá ar do shuíomh "
"Gréasáin. Chun an sceitheadh faisnéise seo “`méarloirg na meán sóisiala`_ < "
"https://robinlinus.github.io/socialmedia-leak/>” a sheachaint, óstach na "
"híomhánna go léir agus do favicon ar fearann ar leithligh."

msgid ""
"Enabling ``redirect_authenticated_user`` can also result in a redirect loop "
"when using the :func:`.permission_required` decorator unless the "
"``raise_exception`` parameter is used."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir lúb atreoraithe a bheith mar thoradh ar "
"``redirect_autenticated_user`` a chumasú nuair a úsáidtear an maisitheoir: "
"func: `.permission_required` mura n-úsáidtear an paraiméadar "
"``raise_exception``."

msgid ""
"A :class:`set` of hosts, in addition to :meth:`request.get_host() "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>`, that are safe for redirecting after "
"login. Defaults to an empty :class:`set`."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>A: aicme: `tac` óstach, i dteann:meth: "
"`request.get_host () `, atá sábháilte le hathreorú tar éis logáil isteach. "
"Réamhshocraithe go folamh: class: `set`."

msgid ""
"Returns the URL to redirect to after login. The default implementation "
"resolves and returns :attr:`next_page` if set, "
"or :setting:`LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an URL le atreorú chuig tar éis logáil isteach. Réiteann agus "
"filleann an cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe: attr: `next_page` má tá sé "
"socraithe, nó:setting: `LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` ar shlí eile."

msgid "Here's what ``LoginView`` does:"
msgstr "Seo cad a dhéanann ``LoginView ``:"

msgid ""
"If called via ``GET``, it displays a login form that POSTs to the same URL. "
"More on this in a bit."
msgstr ""
"Má thugtar air trí `GET``, taispeánann sé foirm logála isteach a Postálann "
"chuig an URL céanna. Níos mó faoi seo i mbeagán."

msgid ""
"If called via ``POST`` with user submitted credentials, it tries to log the "
"user in. If login is successful, the view redirects to the URL specified in "
"``next``. If ``next`` isn't provided, it redirects "
"to :setting:`settings.LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL <LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL>` (which "
"defaults to ``/accounts/profile/``). If login isn't successful, it "
"redisplays the login form."
msgstr ""
"Má ghlaonn sé trí `POST ``le dintiúir a chuirtear isteach ag an úsáideoir, "
"déanann sé iarracht an t-úsáideoir a logáil isteach. Má éiríonn logáil "
"isteach, atreoraíonn an radharc chuig an URL a shonraítear in ``next ``. "
"<LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL>Mura gcuirtear ``next ``ar fáil, atreoraíonn sé "
"chuig:setting: `settings.login_redirect_url `(a dhéanann réamhshocraithe go "
"``/cuntas/próifíl/``). Mura n-éiríonn le logáil isteach, athaispeánann sé an "
"fhoirm logála isteach."

msgid ""
"It's your responsibility to provide the html for the login template , called "
"``registration/login.html`` by default. This template gets passed four "
"template context variables:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé de fhreagracht ort an html a sholáthar don teimpléad logála isteach, "
"ar a dtugtar ``registration/login.html`` de réir réamhshocraithe. Rinne an "
"teimpléad seo ceithre athróg comhthéacs teimplé"

msgid ""
"``form``: A :class:`~django.forms.Form` object representing "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm`."
msgstr ""
"``foirm ``: A:Class: `~Django.Forms.Form` réad a léiríonn an: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm`."

msgid ""
"``next``: The URL to redirect to after successful login. This may contain a "
"query string, too."
msgstr ""
"``next``: An URL le atreorú chuig tar éis logáil isteach rathúil. "
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh teaghrán ceisteanna ann freisin."

msgid ""
"``site``: The current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site`, according "
"to the :setting:`SITE_ID` setting. If you don't have the site framework "
"installed, this will be set to an instance "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite`, which derives the "
"site name and domain from the current :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest`."
msgstr ""
"``site``: An reatha: aicme: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site`, de réir an "
"socrú: socrú: `SITE_ID`. Mura bhfuil creat an láithreáin suiteáilte agat, "
"socraítear é seo go sampla de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.requests.requestsite`, a fhaigheann ainm an "
"láithreáin agus an fearainn ón reatha:class: `~django.http.httpRequest`."

msgid ""
"``site_name``: An alias for ``site.name``. If you don't have the site "
"framework installed, this will be set to the value "
"of :attr:`request.META['SERVER_NAME'] <django.http.HttpRequest.META>`. For "
"more on sites, see :doc:`/ref/contrib/sites`."
msgstr ""
"``site_name``: Ailias le haghaidh ``site.name``. "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.META>Mura bhfuil creat an láithreáin suiteáilte "
"agat, socraítear é seo go luach de:attr: `request.meta ['SERVER_NAME'] `. Le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh eolais ar shuíomhanna, féach:doc: `/ref/contrib/sites`."

msgid ""
"If you'd prefer not to call the template :file:`registration/login.html`, "
"you can pass the ``template_name`` parameter via the extra arguments to the "
"``as_view`` method in your URLconf. For example, this URLconf line would "
"use :file:`myapp/login.html` instead::"
msgstr ""
"Más fearr leat gan glaoch ar an teimpléad:file: `registration/login.html`, "
"is féidir leat an paraiméadar ``template_name`` a chur ar aghaidh trí na "
"hargóintí breise chuig an modh `as_view`` i do URLConf. Mar shampla, "
"úsáidfeadh an líne URLConf seo:file: `myapp/login.html` ina ionad:"

msgid ""
"You can also specify the name of the ``GET`` field which contains the URL to "
"redirect to after login using ``redirect_field_name``. By default, the field "
"is called ``next``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ainm an réimse ``GET`` a shonrú ina bhfuil an URL le atreorú "
"chuig tar éis logáil isteach ag baint úsáide as ``redirect_field_name``. De "
"réir réamhshocraithe, tugtar “next” ar an réimse."

msgid ""
"Here's a sample :file:`registration/login.html` template you can use as a "
"starting point. It assumes you have a :file:`base.html` template that "
"defines a ``content`` block:"
msgstr ""
"Seo teimpléad sampla:file: `registration/login.html` is féidir leat a úsáid "
"mar phointe tosaigh. Glacann sé leis go bhfuil teimpléad a:file: `base.html` "
"agat a shainmhíníonn bloc ``content``:"

msgid ""
"If you have customized authentication (see :doc:`Customizing Authentication "
"</topics/auth/customizing>`) you can use a custom authentication form by "
"setting the ``authentication_form`` attribute. This form must accept a "
"``request`` keyword argument in its ``__init__()`` method and provide a "
"``get_user()`` method which returns the authenticated user object (this "
"method is only ever called after successful form validation)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá fíordheimhniú saincheaptha agat (féach: doc: `Fíordheimhniú "
"Saincheapach') is féidir leat foirm fíordheimhnithe saincheaptha a úsáid "
"tríd an tréith ``foirm autentication_form`` </topics/auth/customizing> a "
"shocrú. Ní mór don fhoirm seo glacadh le hargóint eochairfhocal ``iarraidh` "
"ina modh ``__init__ () ``agus modh ``get_user ()`` a sholáthar a thugann an "
"réad úsáideora fíordheimhnithe ar ais (ní ghlaofar an modh seo ach amháin "
"tar éis bailíochtú foirme rathúil)."

msgid "Logs a user out on ``POST`` requests."
msgstr "Logáil úsáideoir amach ar iarratais ``POST ``."

msgid "**URL name:** ``logout``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ``logáil isteach ``"

msgid "**Attributes:**"
msgstr "**Tréithe: **"

msgid ""
"The URL to redirect to after logout. Defaults "
"to :setting:`LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URL`."
msgstr ""
"An URL le atreorú chuig tar éis logáil amach. Réamhshocraithe chuig: socrú: "
"`LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URL`."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to display after logging the user out. Defaults "
"to :file:`registration/logged_out.html`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléid le taispeáint tar éis an t-úsáideoir a logáil amach. "
"Réamhshocraithe chuig: file: `clárúcháin/logged_out.html`."

msgid ""
"The name of a ``GET`` field containing the URL to redirect to after log out. "
"Defaults to ``'next'``. Overrides the :attr:`next_page` URL if the given "
"``GET`` parameter is passed."
msgstr ""
"Ainm réimse ``GET`` ina bhfuil an URL le atreorú chuig tar éis logáil amach. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``'next t'``. Sáraíonn an URL:attr: `next_page` má "
"chuirtear an paraiméadar ``GET`` a thugtar."

msgid ""
"A :class:`set` of hosts, in addition to :meth:`request.get_host() "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>`, that are safe for redirecting after "
"logout. Defaults to an empty :class:`set`."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>A: aicme: `tac` óstach, i dteann:meth: "
"`request.get_host () `, atá sábháilte le hathreorú tar éis logáil amach. "
"Réamhshocraithe go folamh: class: `set`."

msgid "**Template context:**"
msgstr "** Comhthéacs teimpléad: **"

msgid "``title``: The string \"Logged out\", localized."
msgstr "``title``: An teaghrán “Logáilte amach”, logánaithe."

msgid "Logs a user out on ``POST`` requests, then redirects to the login page."
msgstr ""
"Logáil úsáideoir amach ar iarratais ``POST ``, ansin atreoraíonn sé chuig an "
"leathanach logála isteach."

msgid "**URL name:** No default URL provided"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** Níl URL réamhshocraithe ar fáil"

msgid "**Optional arguments:**"
msgstr "** Argóintí roghnacha: **"

msgid ""
"``login_url``: The URL of the login page to redirect to. Defaults "
"to :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL <LOGIN_URL>` if not supplied."
msgstr ""
"``login_url``: URL an leathanaigh logála isteach le atreorú chuig. "
"<LOGIN_URL>Réamhshocraithe to:setting: `settings.login_url `mura gcuirtear "
"ar fáil."

msgid "**URL name:** ``password_change``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ``password_change``"

msgid "Allows a user to change their password."
msgstr "Ligeann sé d'úsáideoir a phasfhocal a athrú."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to use for displaying the password change form. "
"Defaults to :file:`registration/password_change_form.html` if not supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléid le húsáid chun an fhoirm athraithe pasfhocal a "
"thaispeáint. Réamhshocraithe to:file: `clárúcháin/password_change_form.html` "
"mura gcuirtear ar fáil."

msgid ""
"The URL to redirect to after a successful password change. Defaults to "
"``'password_change_done'``."
msgstr ""
"An URL le atreorú chuig tar éis athrú pasfhocal rathúil. Réamhshocraithe go "
"```'password_change_done'``."

msgid ""
"A custom \"change password\" form which must accept a ``user`` keyword "
"argument. The form is responsible for actually changing the user's password. "
"Defaults to :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordChangeForm`."
msgstr ""
"Foirm saincheaptha “athraigh pasfhocal” a chaithfidh glacadh le hargóint "
"eochairfhocal ``úsáideoir ``. Tá an fhoirm freagrach as pasfhocal an "
"úsáideora a athrú i ndáiríre. Réamhshocraithe chuig: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordChangeForm`."

msgid "``form``: The password change form (see ``form_class`` above)."
msgstr "``foirm``: An fhoirm athraithe pasfhocal (féach ``form_class`` thuas)."

msgid "**URL name:** ``password_change_done``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ```password_change_done``"

msgid "The page shown after a user has changed their password."
msgstr "An leathanach a thaispeántar tar éis d'úsáideoir a phasfhocal a athrú."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to use. Defaults to :file:`registration/"
"password_change_done.html` if not supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléad le húsáid. Réamhshocraithe to:file: `clárúcháin/"
"password_change_done.html` mura gcuirtear ar fáil."

msgid "**URL name:** ``password_reset``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ```password_reset``"

msgid ""
"Allows a user to reset their password by generating a one-time use link that "
"can be used to reset the password, and sending that link to the user's "
"registered email address."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé d'úsáideoir a bhfocal faire a athshocrú trí nasc úsáide aonuaire "
"a ghiniúint is féidir a úsáid chun an pasfhocal a athshocrú, agus an nasc "
"sin a sheoladh chuig seoladh ríomhphoist cláraithe an úsáideora."

msgid "This view will send an email if the following conditions are met:"
msgstr ""
"Seolfaidh an dearcadh seo ríomhphost má chomhlíontar na coinníollacha seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid "The email address provided exists in the system."
msgstr "Tá an seoladh ríomhphoist a chuirtear ar fáil sa chóras."

msgid "The requested user is active (``User.is_active`` is ``True``)."
msgstr "Tá an t-úsáideoir iarrtha gníomhach (``User.is_Active`` is ``True``)."

msgid ""
"The requested user has a usable password. Users flagged with an unusable "
"password "
"(see :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_unusable_password`) aren't "
"allowed to request a password reset to prevent misuse when using an external "
"authentication source like LDAP."
msgstr ""
"Tá pasfhocal inúsáidte ag an úsáideoir iarrtha. Ní cheadaítear d'úsáideoirí "
"a bhfuil pasfhocal neamhúsáidte orthu (féach: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.set_unusable_password`) athshocrú "
"pasfhocal a iarraidh chun mí-úsáid a chosc agus foinse fíordheimhnithe "
"seachtrach cosúil le LDAP á úsáid acu."

msgid ""
"If any of these conditions are *not* met, no email will be sent, but the "
"user won't receive any error message either. This prevents information "
"leaking to potential attackers. If you want to provide an error message in "
"this case, you can "
"subclass :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordResetForm` and use the "
"``form_class`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Mura gcomhlíontar aon cheann de na coinníollacha seo *níl*, ní sheolfar aon "
"ríomhphost, ach ní gheobhaidh an t-úsáideoir aon teachtaireacht earráide ach "
"an oiread. Coscann sé seo faisnéis a sceitheadh chuig ionsaitheoirí "
"ionchasacha Más mian leat teachtaireacht earráide a sholáthar sa chás seo, "
"is féidir leat subclass:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.passwordResetForm` agus an tréith ``form_class "
"``a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Be aware that sending an email costs extra time, hence you may be vulnerable "
"to an email address enumeration timing attack due to a difference between "
"the duration of a reset request for an existing email address and the "
"duration of a reset request for a nonexistent email address. To reduce the "
"overhead, you can use a 3rd party package that allows to send emails "
"asynchronously, e.g. :pypi:`django-mailer`."
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas go gcosnaíonn ríomhphost a sheoladh ama breise, dá bhrí sin "
"b'fhéidir go mbeadh tú leochaileach d'ionsaí uainiúcháin áireamh seoltaí "
"ríomhphoist mar gheall ar difríocht idir fad iarratais athshocraithe ar "
"sheoladh ríomhphoist atá ann cheana agus fad iarratais athshocraithe ar "
"sheoladh ríomhphoist nach bhfuil ann. Chun an lasbhreas a laghdú, is féidir "
"leat pacáiste 3ú páirtí a úsáid a cheadaíonn ríomhphoist a sheoladh go "
"hincrónach, m.sh.: pypi: `django-mailer`."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to use for displaying the password reset form. "
"Defaults to :file:`registration/password_reset_form.html` if not supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléid le húsáid chun an fhoirm athshocraithe pasfhocal a "
"thaispeáint. Réamhshocraithe to:file: `clárúcháin/password_reset_form.html` "
"mura gcuirtear ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Form that will be used to get the email of the user to reset the password "
"for. Defaults to :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordResetForm`."
msgstr ""
"Foirm a úsáidfear chun ríomhphost an úsáideora a fháil chun an pasfhocal a "
"athshocrú dó. Réamhshocraithe chuig: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordResetForm`."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to use for generating the email with the reset "
"password link. Defaults to :file:`registration/password_reset_email.html` if "
"not supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléid le húsáid chun an ríomhphost a ghiniúint leis an nasc "
"pasfhocal athshocraithe. Réamhshocraithe to:file: `registration/"
"password_reset_email.html` mura gcuirtear ar fáil."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to use for the subject of the email with the "
"reset password link. Defaults to :file:`registration/"
"password_reset_subject.txt` if not supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléid le húsáid le haghaidh ábhar an ríomhphoist leis an "
"nasc pasfhocal athshocraithe. Réamhshocraithe to:file: `clárúcháin/"
"password_reset_subject.txt` mura gcuirtear ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Instance of the class to check the one time link. This will default to "
"``default_token_generator``, it's an instance of "
"``django.contrib.auth.tokens.PasswordResetTokenGenerator``."
msgstr ""
"Sampla den rang chun an nasc aonuaire a sheiceáil. Beidh sé seo "
"réamhshocraithe go ``default_token_generator``, is sampla é de "
"``django.contrib.auth.tokens.passwordResetTokenGenerator``."

msgid ""
"The URL to redirect to after a successful password reset request. Defaults "
"to ``'password_reset_done'``."
msgstr ""
"An URL le atreorú chuig tar éis iarratas rathúil athshocraithe pasfhocal. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ```'password_reset_done'``."

msgid ""
"A valid email address. By default Django uses "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL`."
msgstr ""
"Seoladh ríomhphoist bailí. De réir réamhshocraithe úsáideann Django "
"an:setting: `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL`."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to use for generating a :mimetype:`text/html` "
"multipart email with the password reset link. By default, HTML email is not "
"sent."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléid le húsáid chun ríomhphost ilpháirteach a: mimetype: "
"`text/html` a ghiniúint leis an nasc athshocraithe pasfhocal. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, ní sheoltar ríomhphost HTML."

msgid ""
"A dictionary of context data that will be available in the email template. "
"It can be used to override default template context values listed below e.g. "
"``domain``."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir sonraí comhthéacs a bheidh ar fáil sa teimpléad ríomhphoist. Is "
"féidir é a úsáid chun luachanna comhthéacs teimpléad réamhshocraithe atá "
"liostaithe thíos a shárú m.sh. ``réimse``."

msgid ""
"``form``: The form (see ``form_class`` above) for resetting the user's "
"password."
msgstr ""
"``foirm ``: An fhoirm (féach ``form_class`` thuas) chun pasfhocal an "
"úsáideora a athshocrú."

msgid "**Email template context:**"
msgstr "** comhthéacs teimpléad ríomhphoist: **"

msgid "``email``: An alias for ``user.email``"
msgstr "``email``: Ainm le haghaidh ``user.email``"

msgid ""
"``user``: The current :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User`, according "
"to the ``email`` form field. Only active users are able to reset their "
"passwords (``User.is_active is True``)."
msgstr ""
"``user``: An reatha: aicme: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user`, de réir "
"réimse foirme ``ríomhphost``. Níl ach úsáideoirí gníomhacha in ann a gcuid "
"pasfhocail a athshocrú (``User.is_Active is True``)."

msgid ""
"``domain``: An alias for ``site.domain``. If you don't have the site "
"framework installed, this will be set to the value of ``request.get_host()``."
msgstr ""
"``domain``: Ainm le haghaidh ``site.domain``. Mura bhfuil creat an "
"láithreáin suiteáilte agat, socraítear é seo go luach ``request.get_host () "
"``."

msgid "``protocol``: http or https"
msgstr "“prótacal”: http nó https"

msgid "``uid``: The user's primary key encoded in base 64."
msgstr "``uid``: Príomh-eochair an úsáideora ionchódaithe i mbonn 64."

msgid "``token``: Token to check that the reset link is valid."
msgstr ""
"``token``: Comhartha chun a sheiceáil go bhfuil an nasc athshocraithe bailí."

msgid ""
"Sample ``registration/password_reset_email.html`` (email body template):"
msgstr ""
"Sampla ``clárúcháin/password_reset_email.html`` (teimpléad comhlacht "
"ríomhphoist):"

msgid ""
"The same template context is used for subject template. Subject must be "
"single line plain text string."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an comhthéacs teimpléid céanna do theimpléad ábhair. Caithfidh an "
"t-ábhar a bheith ina sreang téacs simplí líne aonair."

msgid "**URL name:** ``password_reset_done``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ```password_reset_done``"

msgid ""
"The page shown after a user has been emailed a link to reset their password. "
"This view is called by default if the :class:`PasswordResetView` doesn't "
"have an explicit ``success_url`` URL set."
msgstr ""
"An leathanach a thaispeántar tar éis nasc a sheoladh chuig úsáideoir chun a "
"bhfocal faire a athshocrú. Tugtar an radharc seo de réir réamhshocraithe "
"mura bhfuil socrú URL sainráite ``success_url`` ag an:class: "
"`PasswordResetView`."

msgid ""
"If the email address provided does not exist in the system, the user is "
"inactive, or has an unusable password, the user will still be redirected to "
"this view but no email will be sent."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an seoladh ríomhphoist a chuirtear ar fáil sa chóras ann, tá an "
"t-úsáideoir neamhghníomhach, nó má tá pasfhocal neamhúsáidte aige, "
"atreorófar an t-úsáideoir chuig an radharc seo fós ach ní sheolfar aon "
"ríomhphost."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to use. Defaults to :file:`registration/"
"password_reset_done.html` if not supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléad le húsáid. Réamhshocraithe to:file: `clárúcháin/"
"password_reset_done.html` mura gcuirtear ar fáil."

msgid "**URL name:** ``password_reset_confirm``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ```password_reset_confirm``"

msgid "Presents a form for entering a new password."
msgstr "Cuireann sé foirm i láthair chun pasfhocal nua a iontráil."

msgid "**Keyword arguments from the URL:**"
msgstr "**Argóintí eochairfhocal ón URL: **"

msgid "``uidb64``: The user's id encoded in base 64."
msgstr "``uidb64``: Aitheantas an úsáideora ionchódaithe i mbonn 64."

msgid "``token``: Token to check that the password is valid."
msgstr "``token``: Comhartha chun a sheiceáil go bhfuil an pasfhocal bailí."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to display the confirm password view. Default "
"value is :file:`registration/password_reset_confirm.html`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléad chun an dearcadh pasfhocal deimhnithe a thaispeáint. "
"Is é an luach réamhshocraithe:file: `clárúcháin/password_reset_confirm.html`."

msgid ""
"Instance of the class to check the password. This will default to "
"``default_token_generator``, it's an instance of "
"``django.contrib.auth.tokens.PasswordResetTokenGenerator``."
msgstr ""
"Sampla den rang chun an pasfhocal a sheiceáil. Beidh sé seo réamhshocraithe "
"go ``default_token_generator``, is sampla é de "
"``django.contrib.auth.tokens.passwordResetTokenGenerator``."

msgid ""
"A boolean indicating if the user should be automatically authenticated after "
"a successful password reset. Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a léiríonn an chóir an t-úsáideoir a fhíordheimhniú go huathoibríoch "
"tar éis athshocrú pasfhocal rathúil. Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid ""
"A dotted path to the authentication backend to use when authenticating a "
"user if ``post_reset_login`` is ``True``. Required only if you have "
"multiple :setting:`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` configured. Defaults to ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Conair poncaí chuig an gcúltaca fíordheimhnithe le húsáid agus úsáideoir á "
"fhíordheimhniú má tá ``post_reset_login`` ``True``. Ní gá ach amháin má tá "
"iolr:setting: `AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` cumraithe agat. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``None``."

msgid ""
"Form that will be used to set the password. Defaults "
"to :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.SetPasswordForm`."
msgstr ""
"Foirm a úsáidfear chun an pasfhocal a shocrú. Réamhshocraithe chuig: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.setPasswordForm`."

msgid ""
"URL to redirect after the password reset done. Defaults to "
"``'password_reset_complete'``."
msgstr ""
"URL chun a atreorú tar éis an athshocrú pasfhocal a dhéanamh. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``'password_reset_complete'``."

msgid ""
"Token parameter displayed as a component of password reset URLs. Defaults to "
"``'set-password'``."
msgstr ""
"Paraiméadar comhartha a thaispeántar mar chomhpháirt d'URLanna athshocraithe "
"pas Réamhshocraithe go ```'pasfhocal a shocraí'."

msgid ""
"``form``: The form (see ``form_class`` above) for setting the new user's "
"password."
msgstr ""
"``foirm ``: An fhoirm (féach ``form_class`` thuas) chun pasfhocal an "
"úsáideora nua a shocrú."

msgid ""
"``validlink``: Boolean, True if the link (combination of ``uidb64`` and "
"``token``) is valid or unused yet."
msgstr ""
"``validlink``: Boolean, Fíor má tá an nasc (teaglaim de ``uidb64`` agus "
"`token``) bailí nó neamhúsáidte fós."

msgid "**URL name:** ``password_reset_complete``"
msgstr "**Ainm URL: ** ```password_reset_complete``"

msgid ""
"Presents a view which informs the user that the password has been "
"successfully changed."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé dearcadh i láthair a chuireann in iúl don úsáideoir go bhfuil an "
"pasfhocal athraithe go rathúil."

msgid ""
"The full name of a template to display the view. Defaults "
"to :file:`registration/password_reset_complete.html`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm iomlán teimpléad chun an radharc a thaispeáint. Réamhshocraithe chuig: "
"file: `clárúcháin/password_reset_complete.html`."

msgid "Helper functions"
msgstr "Feidhmeanna cúnta"

msgid ""
"Redirects to the login page, and then back to another URL after a successful "
"login."
msgstr ""
"Atreoraíonn sé chuig an leathanach logála isteach, agus ansin ar ais chuig "
"URL eile tar éis logáil isteach rathúil."

msgid "**Required arguments:**"
msgstr "** Argóintí riachtanacha: **"

msgid "``next``: The URL to redirect to after a successful login."
msgstr "``next``: An URL le atreorú chuig tar éis logáil isteach rathúil."

msgid ""
"``redirect_field_name``: The name of a ``GET`` field containing the URL to "
"redirect to after login. Overrides ``next`` if the given ``GET`` parameter "
"is passed."
msgstr ""
"``redirect_field_name``: Ainm réimse ``GET`` ina bhfuil an URL le atreorú "
"chuig tar éis logáil isteach. Sáraigh ```next ``má chuirtear an paraiméadar "
"``GET`` a thugtar ar rith."

msgid "Built-in forms"
msgstr "Foirmeacha tógtha"

msgid ""
"If you don't want to use the built-in views, but want the convenience of not "
"having to write forms for this functionality, the authentication system "
"provides several built-in forms located in :mod:`django.contrib.auth.forms`:"
msgstr ""
"Mura dteastaíonn uait na tuairimí ionsuite a úsáid, ach mura dteastaíonn "
"uait an áisiúlacht gan foirmeacha a scríobh don fheidhmiúlacht seo, "
"soláthraíonn an córas fíordheimhnithe roinnt foirmeacha ionsuite in:mod: "
"`django.contrib.auth.forms`:"

msgid ""
"The built-in authentication forms make certain assumptions about the user "
"model that they are working with. If you're using a :ref:`custom user model "
"<auth-custom-user>`, it may be necessary to define your own forms for the "
"authentication system. For more information, refer to the documentation "
"about :ref:`using the built-in authentication forms with custom user models "
"<custom-users-and-the-built-in-auth-forms>`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann na foirmeacha fíordheimhnithe ionsuite toimhde áirithe faoin "
"tsamhail úsáideora a bhfuil siad ag obair leis. Má tá a: ref: `samhail "
"úsáideora saincheaptha <auth-custom-user>`á úsáid agat, b'fhéidir go mbeadh "
"sé riachtanach d'fhoirmeacha féin a shainiú don chóras fíordheimhnithe. "
"<custom-users-and-the-built-in-auth-forms>Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, "
"féach ar an doiciméadú fao:ref: `úsáid na bhfoirmeacha fíordheimhnithe "
"ionsuite le samhlacha úsáideora saincheaptha `."

msgid ""
"A form used in the admin interface to change a user's password, including "
"the ability to set an :meth:`unusable password "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_unusable_password>`, which blocks the "
"user from logging in with password-based authentication."
msgstr ""
"Foirm a úsáidtear sa chomhéadan riaracháin chun pasfhocal úsáideora a athrú, "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_unusable_password>lena n-áirítear an "
"cumas an:meth: `pasfhocal neamhúsáidte `a shocrú, a chuireann bac ar an "
"úsáideoir logáil isteach le fíordheimhniú bunaithe ar phasfhocal."

msgid "Takes the ``user`` as the first positional argument."
msgstr "Glacann sé an ``úsáideoir ``mar an chéad argóint seasaimh."

msgid ""
"Option to disable (or reenable) password-based authentication was added."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh rogha chun fíordheimhniú bunaithe ar phasfhocal a dhíchumasú (nó a "
"athchumasú) leis."

msgid ""
"A form used in the admin interface to create a new user. Inherits "
"from :class:`UserCreationForm`."
msgstr ""
"Foirm a úsáidtear sa chomhéadan riaracháin chun úsáideoir nua a chruthú. "
"Oidhreacht ó:class: `UserCreationForm`."

msgid ""
"It includes an additional ``usable_password`` field, enabled by default. If "
"``usable_password`` is enabled, it verifies that ``password1`` and "
"``password2`` are non empty and match, validates the password "
"using :func:`~django.contrib.auth.password_validation.validate_password`, "
"and sets the user's password "
"using :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_password()`. If "
"``usable_password`` is disabled, no password validation is done, and "
"password-based authentication is disabled for the user by "
"calling :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_unusable_password()`."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn sé réimse breise ```usable_password``, cumasaithe de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Má tá ``usable_password`` cumasaithe, fíoraíonn sé nach "
"bhfuil `password1`` agus `password2`` folamh agus comhoiriúnach, "
"bailíochnaíonn sé an pasfhocal ag baint úsáid:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.password_validation.validate_password`, agus socraíonn "
"sé pasfhocal an úsáideora ag baint úsáidea:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.contrib.Models.user.set_password () `. Má "
"dhíchumasaítear ``usable_password``, ní dhéantar aon bhailíochtú pasfhocal, "
"agus díchumasaítear fíordheimhniú pasfhocal don úsáideoir trí ghlaoch:: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.set_unusable_password () `."

msgid "A form for logging a user in."
msgstr "Foirm chun úsáideoir a logáil isteach."

msgid ""
"Takes ``request`` as its first positional argument, which is stored on the "
"form instance for use by sub-classes."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé “iarratas” mar a chéad argóint seasaimh, a stóráiltear ar an "
"sampla foirme le húsáid ag fo-aicmí."

msgid ""
"By default, ``AuthenticationForm`` rejects users whose ``is_active`` flag is "
"set to ``False``. You may override this behavior with a custom policy to "
"determine which users can log in. Do this with a custom form that subclasses "
"``AuthenticationForm`` and overrides the ``confirm_login_allowed()`` method. "
"This method should raise a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if "
"the given user may not log in."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, diúltaíonn ``AuthenticationForm ``úsáideoirí a "
"bhfuil a bhratach ``is_active`` socraithe go ``False``. Féadfaidh tú an t-"
"iompar seo a shárú le beartas saincheaptha chun a chinneadh cé na "
"húsáideoirí is féidir leo logáil isteach. Déan é seo le foirm saincheaptha a "
"dhéanann fo-aicme ``AuthenticationForm ``agus a sháraíonn an modh "
"``confirm_login_allow ()``. Ba chóir go n-ardódh an modh seo a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` mura bhféadfadh an t-úsáideoir "
"tugtha logáil isteach."

msgid ""
"For example, to allow all users to log in regardless of \"active\" status::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun ligean do gach úsáideoir logáil isteach beag beann ar "
"stádas “gníomhach”:"

msgid ""
"(In this case, you'll also need to use an authentication backend that allows "
"inactive users, such "
"as :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.AllowAllUsersModelBackend`.)"
msgstr ""
"(Sa chás seo, beidh ort cúltaca fíordheimhnithe a úsáid freisin a cheadaíonn "
"úsáideoirí neamhghníomhacha, mar shampla:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.allowAllUsersModelBackend`.)"

msgid "Or to allow only some active users to log in::"
msgstr "Nó chun ligean ach roinnt úsáideoirí gníomhacha logáil isteach:"

msgid ""
"A :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` for creating a new user. This is the "
"recommended base class if you need to customize the user creation form."
msgstr ""
"A: Class: `~Django.Forms.ModelForm` chun úsáideoir nua a chruthú. Is é seo "
"an bunaicme molta más gá duit an fhoirm chruthaithe úsáideora a "
"shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"It has three fields: ``username`` (from the user model), ``password1``, and "
"``password2``. It verifies that ``password1`` and ``password2`` match, "
"validates the password "
"using :func:`~django.contrib.auth.password_validation.validate_password`, "
"and sets the user's password "
"using :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_password()`."
msgstr ""
"Tá trí réimse aige: ``ainm úsáideora ``(ón tsamhail úsáideora), "
"``pasfhocal1``, agus ``pasfhocal 2``. Fíoraíonn sé go n-oireann "
"``password1`` agus `password2``, bailíochtú an pasfhocal ag baint "
"úsáidea:func: `~django.contrib.auth.password_validation.validate_password`, "
"agus socraíonn sé pasfhocal an úsáideora ag baint úsáidea:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.set_password () `."

msgid "A form for allowing a user to change their password."
msgstr "Foirm chun ligean d'úsáideoir a phasfhocal a athrú."

msgid ""
"A form for generating and emailing a one-time use link to reset a user's "
"password."
msgstr ""
"Foirm chun nasc úsáide aon-uaire a ghiniúint agus a sheoladh ríomhphoist "
"chun pasfhocal úsáideora a athshocrú."

msgid ""
"Uses the arguments to send an ``EmailMultiAlternatives``. Can be overridden "
"to customize how the email is sent to the user. If you choose to override "
"this method, be mindful of handling potential exceptions raised due to email "
"sending failures."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé na hargóintí chun ``EmailMultiAlternatives`` a sheoladh. Is "
"féidir é a athsheoladh chun an chaoi a sheoltar an ríomhphost chuig an "
"úsáideoir a shaincheapadh. Má roghnaíonn tú an modh seo a shárú, bí ar an "
"gcuimhne ar eisceachtaí féideartha a ardaíodh mar gheall ar theipeanna "
"seolta ríomhphoist"

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "Paraiméadair"

msgid "the template for the subject."
msgstr "an teimpléad don ábhar."

msgid "the template for the email body."
msgstr "an teimpléad don chomhlacht ríomhphoist."

msgid ""
"context passed to the ``subject_template``, ``email_template``, and "
"``html_email_template`` (if it is not ``None``)."
msgstr ""
"comhthéacs a chuirtear chuig an ``subject_template``, ``email_teimple``, "
"agus ``html_email_teimple`` (mura bhfuil sé ``None``)."

msgid "the sender's email."
msgstr "ríomhphost an tseoltóra."

msgid "the email of the requester."
msgstr "ríomhphost an iarratóra."

msgid ""
"the template for the HTML body; defaults to ``None``, in which case a plain "
"text email is sent."
msgstr ""
"an teimpléad don chomhlacht HTML; réamhshocraithe go ``None``, sa chás sin "
"seoltar ríomhphost gnáth-théacs."

msgid ""
"By default, ``save()`` populates the ``context`` with the same variables "
"that :class:`~django.contrib.auth.views.PasswordResetView` passes to its "
"email context."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, líonann ``save () ``an `context`` leis na hathróga "
"céanna a théann: class: `~django.contrib.auth.views.passwordResetView` chuig "
"a chomhthéacs ríomhphoist."

msgid ""
"A form that lets a user change their password without entering the old "
"password."
msgstr ""
"Foirm a ligeann d'úsáideoir a phasfhocal a athrú gan an sean-phasfhocal a "
"iontráil."

msgid ""
"A form used in the admin interface to change a user's information and "
"permissions."
msgstr ""
"Foirm a úsáidtear sa chomhéadan riaracháin chun faisnéis agus ceadanna "
"úsáideora a athrú."

msgid ""
"Inherits from :class:`BaseUserCreationForm`. To help prevent confusion with "
"similar usernames, the form doesn't allow usernames that differ only in case."
msgstr ""
"Oidhreacht ó:class: `BaseUserCreationForm`. Chun cabhrú le mearbhall le "
"hainmneacha úsáideora comhchosúla a chosc, ní cheadaíonn an fhoirm "
"ainmneacha úsáideora atá difriúil"

msgid "Authentication data in templates"
msgstr "Sonraí fíordheimhnithe i dteimpl"

msgid ""
"The currently logged-in user and their permissions are made available in "
"the :doc:`template context </ref/templates/api>` when you "
"use :class:`~django.template.RequestContext`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an t-úsáideoir logáilte isteach faoi láthair agus a gceadanna ar "
"fáil in:doc: `template context` nuair a úsáideann tú :class: "
"`~django.template.requestContext` </ref/templates/api>."

msgid "Technicality"
msgstr "Teicniúlacht"

msgid ""
"Technically, these variables are only made available in the template context "
"if you use :class:`~django.template.RequestContext` and the "
"``'django.contrib.auth.context_processors.auth'`` context processor is "
"enabled. It is in the default generated settings file. For more, see "
"the :ref:`RequestContext docs <subclassing-context-requestcontext>`."
msgstr ""
"Go teicniúil, ní chuirtear na hathróga seo ar fáil ach amháin i gcomhthéacs "
"an teimpléid má úsáideann tú: class: `~django.template.requestContext` agus "
"cumasaítear an próiseálaí comhthéacs "
"``'django.contrib.auth.context_processors.auth'`. Tá sé sa chomhad socruithe "
"réamhshocraithe a ghintear. <subclassing-context-requestcontext>Le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh, féach an:ref: `RequestContext docs `."

msgid "Users"
msgstr "Úsáideoirí"

msgid ""
"When rendering a template :class:`~django.template.RequestContext`, the "
"currently logged-in user, either "
"a  :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` instance or "
"an :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AnonymousUser` instance, is stored in "
"the template variable ``{{ user }}``:"
msgstr ""
"Agus teimpléad:class: `~django.template.requestContext` á rindreáil, "
"stóráiltear an t-úsáideoir logáilte isteach faoi láthair, a:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user` nó sampla: :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.anonymousUser`, san athróg teimpléad ``{{user}}"
"``:"

msgid ""
"This template context variable is not available if a ``RequestContext`` is "
"not being used."
msgstr ""
"Níl an athróg comhthéacs teimpléad seo ar fáil mura bhfuil "
"``RequestContext`` á úsáid."

msgid "Permissions"
msgstr "Ceada"

msgid ""
"The currently logged-in user's permissions are stored in the template "
"variable ``{{ perms }}``. This is an instance of "
"``django.contrib.auth.context_processors.PermWrapper``, which is a template-"
"friendly proxy of permissions."
msgstr ""
"Stóráiltear ceadanna an úsáideora logáilte isteach faoi láthair san athróg "
"teimpléad ``{{perms}}``. Seo sampla de "
"``django.contrib.auth.context_processors.permWrapper``, seachfhreastalaí "
"ceadanna atá cairdiúil don teimpléad é."

msgid ""
"Evaluating a single-attribute lookup of ``{{ perms }}`` as a boolean is a "
"proxy to :meth:`User.has_module_perms() "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_module_perms>`. For example, to check "
"if the logged-in user has any permissions in the ``foo`` app:"
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_module_perms>Is seachfhreastalaí é "
"cuardach aontréithe de ``{{perms}}`` a mheas mar boolean "
"seachfhreastalaí:meth: `User.has_module_perms () `. Mar shampla, chun "
"seiceáil an bhfuil aon cheadanna ag an úsáideoir logáilte isteach san aip "
"`foo':"

msgid ""
"Evaluating a two-level-attribute lookup as a boolean is a proxy "
"to :meth:`User.has_perm() <django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_perm>`. For "
"example, to check if the logged-in user has the permission ``foo.add_vote``:"
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_perm>Is seachfhreastalaí é cuardach "
"tréithe dhá leibhéal a mheas mar boolean chun: meth: `User.has_perm () `. "
"Mar shampla, chun seiceáil an bhfuil an cead ``foo.add_vote`` ag an "
"úsáideoir logáilte isteach:"

msgid "Here's a more complete example of checking permissions in a template:"
msgstr "Seo sampla níos iomláine de cheadanna a sheiceáil i dteimpléad:"

msgid ""
"It is possible to also look permissions up by ``{% if in %}`` statements. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ceadanna a lorg suas freisin le ráitis ``{% má tá i%}``. Mar "
"shampla:"

msgid "Managing users in the admin"
msgstr "Úsáideoirí a bhainistiú sa riarachán"

msgid ""
"When you have both ``django.contrib.admin`` and ``django.contrib.auth`` "
"installed, the admin provides a convenient way to view and manage users, "
"groups, and permissions. Users can be created and deleted like any Django "
"model. Groups can be created, and permissions can be assigned to users or "
"groups. A log of user edits to models made within the admin is also stored "
"and displayed."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn `django.contrib.admin ``agus ``django.contrib.auth`` "
"suiteáilte agat, soláthraíonn an riarachán bealach áisiúil chun úsáideoirí, "
"grúpaí agus ceadanna a fheiceáil agus a bhainistiú. Is féidir úsáideoirí a "
"chruthú agus a scriosadh cosúil le haon samhail Django. Is féidir grúpaí a "
"chruthú, agus is féidir ceadanna a shannadh d'úsáideoirí nó do ghrúpaí. "
"Stóráiltear agus taispeántar log d'eagarthóirí úsáideora ar mhúnlaí a "
"dhéantar laistigh den riarachán freisin."

msgid ""
"You should see a link to \"Users\" in the \"Auth\" section of the main admin "
"index page. The \"Add user\" admin page is different than standard admin "
"pages in that it requires you to choose a username and password before "
"allowing you to edit the rest of the user's fields. Alternatively, on this "
"page, you can choose a username and disable password-based authentication "
"for the user."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit nasc le “Úsáideoirí” a fheiceáil sa chuid “Auth” den "
"phríomhleathanach innéacs riaracháin. Tá an leathanach riaracháin “Cuir "
"úsáideoir leis” difriúil ná leathanaigh riaracháin caighdeánacha sa mhéid go "
"n-éilíonn sé ort ainm úsáideora agus pasfhocal a roghnú sula ligfidh sé duit "
"an chuid eile de réimsí an úsáideora a chur in eagar. Nó, ar an leathanach "
"seo, is féidir leat ainm úsáideora a roghnú agus fíordheimhniú bunaithe ar "
"phasfhocal a dhíchumasú don úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"Also note: if you want a user account to be able to create users using the "
"Django admin site, you'll need to give them permission to add users *and* "
"change users (i.e., the \"Add user\" and \"Change user\" permissions). If an "
"account has permission to add users but not to change them, that account "
"won't be able to add users. Why? Because if you have permission to add "
"users, you have the power to create superusers, which can then, in turn, "
"change other users. So Django requires add *and* change permissions as a "
"slight security measure."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin: más mian leat go mbeadh cuntas úsáideora in ann "
"úsáideoirí a chruthú ag baint úsáide as suíomh riaracháin Django, beidh ort "
"cead a thabhairt dóibh úsáideoirí a chur leis *agus* úsáideoirí a athrú (ie, "
"na ceadanna “Cuir úsáideoir leis” agus “Athraigh úsáideoir”). Má tá cead ag "
"cuntas úsáideoirí a chur leis ach gan iad a athrú, ní bheidh an cuntas sin "
"in ann úsáideoirí a chur leis. Cén fáth? Toisc má tá cead agat úsáideoirí a "
"chur leis, tá an chumhacht agat sárúsáideoirí a chruthú, ar féidir leo "
"úsáideoirí eile a athrú ansin. Mar sin éilíonn Django ceadúna* agus* "
"athraithe a chur leis mar bheart slándála beag."

msgid ""
"Be thoughtful about how you allow users to manage permissions. If you give a "
"non-superuser the ability to edit users, this is ultimately the same as "
"giving them superuser status because they will be able to elevate "
"permissions of users including themselves!"
msgstr ""
"Bí tuisceanach faoi conas a ligeann tú d'úsáideoirí ceadanna a bhainistiú Má "
"thugann tú an cumas do neamh-sárúsáideoir úsáideoirí a chur in eagar, tá sé "
"seo mar an gcéanna sa deireadh le stádas sárúsáideora a thabhairt dóibh "
"toisc go mbeidh siad in ann ceadanna úsáideoirí lena n-áirítear iad féin a "
"ardú!"

msgid ""
"User passwords are not displayed in the admin (nor stored in the database), "
"but the :doc:`password storage details </topics/auth/passwords>` are "
"displayed. Included in the display of this information is a link to a "
"password change form that allows admins to change or unset user passwords."
msgstr ""
"Ní thaispeántar pasfhocail úsáideora sa riarachán (ná ní stóráiltear sa "
"bhunachar sonraí), ach taispeántar na:doc: `sonraí stórála pasfhocal </"
"topics/auth/passwords>. San áireamh i dtaispeáint na faisnéise seo tá nasc "
"le foirm athraithe pasfhocal a ligeann do riarthóirí pasfhocail úsáideora a "
"athrú nó a dhíshocrú."

msgid "User authentication in Django"
msgstr "Fíordheimhniú úsáideora i Django"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a user authentication system. It handles user accounts, "
"groups, permissions and cookie-based user sessions. This section of the "
"documentation explains how the default implementation works out of the box, "
"as well as how to :doc:`extend and customize </topics/auth/customizing>` it "
"to suit your project's needs."
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le córas fíordheimhnithe úsáideora. Láimhseálann sé cuntais "
"úsáideora, grúpaí, ceadanna agus seisiúin úsáideora bhunaithe ar Míníonn an "
"chuid seo den doiciméadú conas a oibríonn an cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe "
"as an mbosca, chomh maith le cona:doc: é a leathnú agus a shaincheapadh chun "
"freastal ar riachtanais do thion</topics/auth/customizing> scadail."

msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Forbhreathnú"

msgid ""
"The Django authentication system handles both authentication and "
"authorization. Briefly, authentication verifies a user is who they claim to "
"be, and authorization determines what an authenticated user is allowed to "
"do. Here the term authentication is used to refer to both tasks."
msgstr ""
"Láimhseálann córas fíordheimhnithe Django fíordheimhniú agus údarú Go "
"hachomair, fíoraíonn fíordheimhniú gurb é an t-úsáideoir cé a mhaíonn sé, "
"agus cinneann údarú cad is ceadaítear d'úsáideoir fíordheimhnithe a "
"dhéanamh. Anseo úsáidtear an téarma fíordheimhniú chun tagairt a dhéanamh "
"don dá thasc."

msgid "The auth system consists of:"
msgstr "Is éard atá sa chóras auth ná:"

msgid ""
"Permissions: Binary (yes/no) flags designating whether a user may perform a "
"certain task."
msgstr ""
"Ceadanna: Bratacha dénártha (tua/níl) a ainmníonn an bhféadfaidh úsáideoir "
"tasc áirithe a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"Groups: A generic way of applying labels and permissions to more than one "
"user."
msgstr ""
"Grúpaí: Bealach cineálach chun lipéid agus ceadanna a chur i bhfeidhm ar "
"níos mó ná úsáideoir amháin."

msgid "A configurable password hashing system"
msgstr "Córas hashing pasfhocal cumraithe"

msgid "Forms and view tools for logging in users, or restricting content"
msgstr ""
"Foirmeacha agus uirlisí féachana chun úsáideoirí a logáil isteach, nó ábhar "
"a shrianadh"

msgid "A pluggable backend system"
msgstr "Córas cúltaca plugáilte"

msgid ""
"The authentication system in Django aims to be very generic and doesn't "
"provide some features commonly found in web authentication systems. "
"Solutions for some of these common problems have been implemented in third-"
"party packages:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé mar aidhm ag an gcóras fíordheimhnithe i Django a bheith an-chineálach "
"agus ní sholáthraíonn sé roinnt gnéithe a fhaightear go coitianta i gcór "
"Cuireadh réitigh ar chuid de na fadhbanna coitianta seo i bhfeidhm i "
"bpacáistí tríú"

msgid "Password strength checking"
msgstr "Seiceáil neart pasfhocal"

msgid "Throttling of login attempts"
msgstr "Scaoileadh iarrachtaí logála isteach"

msgid "Authentication against third-parties (OAuth, for example)"
msgstr "Fíordheimhniú i gcoinne tríú páirtithe (OAuth, mar shampla)"

msgid "Object-level permissions"
msgstr "Ceadanna ar leibhéal réada"

msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Suiteáil"

msgid ""
"Authentication support is bundled as a Django contrib module in "
"``django.contrib.auth``. By default, the required configuration is already "
"included in the :file:`settings.py` generated by :djadmin:`django-admin "
"startproject <startproject>`, these consist of two items listed in "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting:"
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht fíordheimhnithe curtha i mbun mar mhodúl contrib Django i "
"``django.contrib.auth``. <startproject>De réir réamhshocraithe, tá an "
"chumraíocht riachtanach san áireamh cheana féin in:file: `settings.py` arna "
"ghineadh ar:djadmin: `django-admin startproject `, tá dhá mhír atá "
"liostaithe i do shuíomh: `INSTALLED_APPS`:"

msgid ""
"``'django.contrib.auth'`` contains the core of the authentication framework, "
"and its default models."
msgstr ""
"Tá croílár an chreat fíordheimhnithe, agus a mhúnlaí réamhshocraithe sa "
"``django.contrib.auth'`."

msgid ""
"``'django.contrib.contenttypes'`` is the Django :doc:`content type system </"
"ref/contrib/contenttypes>`, which allows permissions to be associated with "
"models you create."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``'django.contrib.contenttypes'`` an córas django:doc: `cineál ábhar`, "
"a cheadaíonn ceadanna a bheith bainteach le samhlacha a chruthaíonn tú </ref/"
"contrib/contenttypes>."

msgid "and these items in your :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting:"
msgstr "agus na míreanna seo i do shuíomh: `MIDDLEWARE`:"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware` "
"manages :doc:`sessions </topics/http/sessions>` across requests."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.sessionMiddleware` "
"bainistí:doc: `</topics/http/sessions> seisiúin` trasna iarratais."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware` associates "
"users with requests using sessions."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware` "
"comhcheanglaíonn úsáideoirí le hiarratais ag baint úsáide as seisiúin."

msgid ""
"With these settings in place, running the command ``manage.py migrate`` "
"creates the necessary database tables for auth related models and "
"permissions for any models defined in your installed apps."
msgstr ""
"Agus na socruithe seo i bhfeidhm, cruthaíonn an t-ordú `manage.py migrate`` "
"na táblaí bunachar sonraí riachtanacha do mhúnlaí agus ceadanna a bhaineann "
"le auth d'aon mhúnlaí a shainmhínítear i d'aipeanna suiteáilte."

msgid "Usage"
msgstr "Úsáid"

msgid ":doc:`Using Django's default implementation <default>`"
msgstr "<default>:doc: `Úsáid cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe Django `"

msgid ":ref:`Working with User objects <user-objects>`"
msgstr "<user-objects>:ref: `Ag obair le rudaí Úsáideora `"

msgid ":ref:`Permissions and authorization <topic-authorization>`"
msgstr "<topic-authorization>:ref: `Ceadanna agus údarú `"

msgid ":ref:`Authentication in web requests <auth-web-requests>`"
msgstr "<auth-web-requests>:ref: `Fíordheimhniú in iarratais gréasáin `"

msgid ":ref:`Managing users in the admin <auth-admin>`"
msgstr "<auth-admin>:ref: `Úsáideoirí a bhainistiú sa riarachán `"

msgid ":doc:`API reference for the default implementation </ref/contrib/auth>`"
msgstr ""
":doc: `Tagairt API don chur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe</ref/contrib/auth> '"

msgid ":doc:`Customizing Users and authentication <customizing>`"
msgstr "<customizing>:doc: `Úsáideoirí a shaincheapadh agus fíordheimhniú `"

msgid ":doc:`Password management in Django <passwords>`"
msgstr "<passwords>:doc: `Bainistíocht pasfhocal i Django `"

msgid "Password management in Django"
msgstr "Bainistíocht pasfhocal i Django"

msgid ""
"Password management is something that should generally not be reinvented "
"unnecessarily, and Django endeavors to provide a secure and flexible set of "
"tools for managing user passwords. This document describes how Django stores "
"passwords, how the storage hashing can be configured, and some utilities to "
"work with hashed passwords."
msgstr ""
"Is rud é bainistíocht pasfhocal nár cheart é a athchruthú go ginearálta gan "
"ghá, agus déanann Django iarracht sraith uirlisí slán solúbtha a sholáthar "
"chun pasfhocail úsáideora a bhainistiú. Déanann an doiciméad seo cur síos ar "
"an gcaoi a stórálann Django pasfhocail, conas is féidir an hashing stórála a "
"chumrú, agus roinnt fóntais chun oibriú le pasfhocail"

msgid ""
"Even though users may use strong passwords, attackers might be able to "
"eavesdrop on their connections. Use :ref:`HTTPS <security-recommendation-"
"ssl>` to avoid sending passwords (or any other sensitive data) over plain "
"HTTP connections because they will be vulnerable to password sniffing."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhféadfadh úsáideoirí pasfhocail láidre a úsáid, b'fhéidir go mbeadh "
"ionsaitheoirí in ann cluaise a gcuid naisc. Úsáid: tagairt: `HTTPS <security-"
"recommendation-ssl>`chun pasfhocail a sheachaint (nó aon sonraí íogaire "
"eile) a sheachaint thar naisc simplí HTTP toisc go mbeidh siad leochaileach "
"do shnifeadh pasfhocal."

msgid "How Django stores passwords"
msgstr "Conas a stórálann Django pasfhocail"

msgid ""
"Django provides a flexible password storage system and uses PBKDF2 by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django córas stórála pasfhocal solúbtha agus úsáideann sé "
"PBKDF2 de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.password` attribute of "
"a :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` object is a string in this "
"format:"
msgstr ""
"Is teaghrán sa fhormáid seo é an tréith: Attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.password` tréith a:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user` réad:"

msgid ""
"Those are the components used for storing a User's password, separated by "
"the dollar-sign character and consist of: the hashing algorithm, the number "
"of algorithm iterations (work factor), the random salt, and the resulting "
"password hash.  The algorithm is one of a number of one-way hashing or "
"password storage algorithms Django can use; see below. Iterations describe "
"the number of times the algorithm is run over the hash. Salt is the random "
"seed used and the hash is the result of the one-way function."
msgstr ""
"Is iad sin na comhpháirteanna a úsáidtear chun pasfhocal Úsáideora a "
"stóráil, scartha ag an gcarachtar comhartha dollar agus tá: an algartam "
"hashing, líon na n-athrú algartam (fachtóir oibre), an salann randamach, "
"agus an hash pasfhocal mar thoradh air. Tá an algartam ar cheann de roinnt "
"halgartaim hashing aon-bhealach nó stórála pasfhocal is féidir le Django a "
"úsáid; féach thíos. Déanann athrá cur síos ar an líon uaireanta a "
"reáchtáiltear an algartam thar an hash. Is é salann an síol randamach a "
"úsáidtear agus is é an hash toradh ar an fheidhm aon-bhealach."

msgid ""
"By default, Django uses the PBKDF2_ algorithm with a SHA256 hash, a password "
"stretching mechanism recommended by NIST_. This should be sufficient for "
"most users: it's quite secure, requiring massive amounts of computing time "
"to break."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáideann Django algartam PBKDF2_ le hash SHA256, "
"meicníocht síneadh pasfhocal a mhol NIST_. Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo "
"leordhóthanach don chuid is mó d'úsáideoirí: tá sé slán go leor, ag teastáil "
"go leor ama ríomhaireachta chun briseadh."

msgid ""
"However, depending on your requirements, you may choose a different "
"algorithm, or even use a custom algorithm to match your specific security "
"situation. Again, most users shouldn't need to do this -- if you're not "
"sure, you probably don't.  If you do, please read on:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, ag brath ar do riachtanais, féadfaidh tú algartam difriúil a "
"roghnú, nó fiú algartam saincheaptha a úsáid chun do staid slándála ar leith "
"a mheaitseáil. Arís, níor chóir go gcaithfeadh mórchuid na n-úsáideoirí é "
"seo a dhéanamh - mura bhfuil tú cinnte, is dócha nach ndéanann tú. Má "
"dhéanann tú, léigh ar aghaidh le do thoil:"

msgid ""
"Django chooses the algorithm to use by consulting "
"the :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` setting. This is a list of hashing algorithm "
"classes that this Django installation supports."
msgstr ""
"Roghnaíonn Django an algartam le húsáid trí chomhairle leis an socrú: "
"setting: `PASSWORD_HASHERS`. Seo liosta de ranganna algartam hashing a "
"thacaíonn an suiteáil Django seo."

msgid ""
"For storing passwords, Django will use the first hasher "
"in :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS`. To store new passwords with a different "
"algorithm, put your preferred algorithm first in :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS`."
msgstr ""
"Chun pasfhocail a stóráil, úsáidfidh Django an chéad hasher in:setting: "
"`PASSWORD_HASHERS`. Chun pasfhocail nua a stóráil le halgartam difriúil, "
"cuir an algartam is fearr leat ar dtús in:setting: `PASSWORD_HASHERS`."

msgid ""
"For verifying passwords, Django will find the hasher in the list that "
"matches the algorithm name in the stored password. If a stored password "
"names an algorithm not found in :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS`, trying to "
"verify it will raise ``ValueError``."
msgstr ""
"Chun pasfhocail a fhíorú, gheobhaidh Django an hasher sa liosta a "
"mheaitseálann ainm an algartam sa phasfhocal stóráilte. Má ainmníonn "
"pasfhocal stóráilte algartam nach bhfaightear in:setting: "
"`PASSWORD_HASHERS`, ardóidh sé ``ValueError`` ag iarraidh a fhíorú."

msgid "The default for :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` is::"
msgstr "Is é an réamhshocrú le haghaidh: socrú: `PASSWORD_HASHERS`:"

msgid ""
"This means that Django will use PBKDF2_ to store all passwords but will "
"support checking passwords stored with PBKDF2SHA1, argon2_, and bcrypt_."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé seo go n-úsáidfidh Django PBKDF2_ chun gach pasfhocal a "
"stóráil ach tacóidh sé le pasfhocail a stóráiltear le PBKDF2SHA1, argon2_, "
"agus bcrypt_ a sheiceáil."

msgid ""
"The next few sections describe a couple of common ways advanced users may "
"want to modify this setting."
msgstr ""
"Déanann na cúpla chuid eile cur síos ar chúpla bealach coitianta a "
"d'fhéadfadh ardúsáideoirí a bheith ag iarraidh an socrú seo a"

msgid "Using Argon2 with Django"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as Argon2 le Django"

msgid ""
"Argon2_ is the winner of the 2015 `Password Hashing Competition`_, a "
"community organized open competition to select a next generation hashing "
"algorithm. It's designed not to be easier to compute on custom hardware than "
"it is to compute on an ordinary CPU. The default variant for the Argon2 "
"password hasher is Argon2id."
msgstr ""
"Is é Argon2_ buaiteoir an “Comórtas Hashing Pasfhocal” 2015, comórtas "
"oscailte eagraithe ag an bpobal chun algartam hashing den chéad ghlúin eile "
"a roghnú. Tá sé deartha chun nach mbeadh sé níos éasca a ríomh ar chrua-"
"earraí saincheaptha ná mar atá sé a ríomh ar ghnáth LAP. Is é Argon2id an "
"leagan réamhshocraithe don hasher pasfhocal Argon2."

msgid ""
"Argon2_ is not the default for Django because it requires a third-party "
"library. The Password Hashing Competition panel, however, recommends "
"immediate use of Argon2 rather than the other algorithms supported by Django."
msgstr ""
"Ní hé Argon2_ an réamhshocrú do Django toisc go dteastaíonn leabharlann tríú "
"páirtí uaidh. Molann an painéal Comórtais Hashing Pasfhocal, áfach, Argon2 a "
"úsáid láithreach seachas na halgartaim eile a thacaíonn Django."

msgid "To use Argon2id as your default storage algorithm, do the following:"
msgstr ""
"Chun Argon2id a úsáid mar do algartam stórála réamhshocraithe, déan an méid "
"seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Install the :pypi:`argon2-cffi` package. This can be done by running "
"``python -m pip install django[argon2]``, which is equivalent to ``python -m "
"pip install argon2-cffi`` (along with any version requirement from Django's "
"``pyproject.toml``)."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil an pacáiste: pypi: `argon2-cffi`. Is féidir é seo a dhéanamh trí "
"``python -m pip install django [argon2] ``a reáchtáil, atá comhionann le "
"``python -m pip install argon2-cffi`` (in éineacht le haon riachtanas leagan "
"ó ``pyproject.toml`` Django)."

msgid ""
"Modify :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` to list ``Argon2PasswordHasher`` first. "
"That is, in your settings file, you'd put::"
msgstr ""
"Athraigh: Socrú: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` chun `Argon2PasswordHasher`` a liostáil "
"ar dtús. Is é sin, i do chomhad socruithe, chuirfeá:"

msgid ""
"Keep and/or add any entries in this list if you need Django to :ref:`upgrade "
"passwords <password-upgrades>`."
msgstr ""
"<password-upgrades>Coinnigh agus/nó cuir aon iontrálacha sa liosta seo má "
"theastaíonn Django uait to:ref: `pasfhocail a uasghrádú `."

msgid "Using ``bcrypt`` with Django"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as ``bcrypt`` le Django"

msgid ""
"Bcrypt_ is a popular password storage algorithm that's specifically designed "
"for long-term password storage. It's not the default used by Django since it "
"requires the use of third-party libraries, but since many people may want to "
"use it Django supports bcrypt with minimal effort."
msgstr ""
"Is algartam stórála pasfhocal móréilimh é Bcrypt_ atá deartha go sonrach le "
"haghaidh stórála pasfhocal fadtéarmach. Ní hé an réamhshocrú a úsáideann "
"Django é ós rud é go n-éilíonn sé leabharlanna tríú páirtí a úsáid, ach ós "
"rud é go bhféadfadh go leor daoine é a úsáid tacaíonn Django le bcrypt gan "
"iarracht íosta."

msgid "To use Bcrypt as your default storage algorithm, do the following:"
msgstr ""
"Chun Bcrypt a úsáid mar do algartam stórála réamhshocraithe, déan an méid "
"seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Install the :pypi:`bcrypt` package. This can be done by running ``python -m "
"pip install django[bcrypt]``, which is equivalent to ``python -m pip install "
"bcrypt`` (along with any version requirement from Django's "
"``pyproject.toml``)."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil an pacáiste: pypi: `bcrypt`. Is féidir é seo a dhéanamh trí "
"``python -m pip install django [bcrypt] ``a reáchtáil, atá comhionann le "
"``python -m pip install bcrypt`` (in éineacht le haon riachtanas leagan ó "
"``pyproject.toml`` Django)."

msgid ""
"Modify :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` to list ``BCryptSHA256PasswordHasher`` "
"first. That is, in your settings file, you'd put::"
msgstr ""
"Athraigh: Socrú: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` chun `bCryptSha256PasswordHasher`` a "
"liostáil ar dtús. Is é sin, i do chomhad socruithe, chuirfeá:"

msgid ""
"That's it -- now your Django install will use Bcrypt as the default storage "
"algorithm."
msgstr ""
"Sin é - anois úsáidfidh do shuiteáil Django Bcrypt mar an algartam stórála "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid "Using ``scrypt`` with Django"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as ``scrypt`` le Django"

msgid ""
"scrypt_ is similar to PBKDF2 and bcrypt in utilizing a set number of "
"iterations to slow down brute-force attacks. However, because PBKDF2 and "
"bcrypt do not require a lot of memory, attackers with sufficient resources "
"can launch large-scale parallel attacks in order to speed up the attacking "
"process. scrypt_ is specifically designed to use more memory compared to "
"other password-based key derivation functions in order to limit the amount "
"of parallelism an attacker can use, see :rfc:`7914` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Tá scrypt_ cosúil le PBKDF2 agus bcrypt agus líon socraithe athraitheanna a "
"úsáid chun ionsaithe brute-force a mhoilliú. Mar sin féin, toisc nach "
"dteastaíonn go leor cuimhne ó PBKDF2 agus bcrypt, is féidir le "
"hionsaitheoirí a bhfuil dóthain acmhainní acu ionsaithe a sheoladh chun an "
"próiseas ionsaitheora a bhrostú. Tá scrypt_ deartha go sonrach chun níos mó "
"feidhmeanna díorthaithe bunaithe ar phasfhocal eile d'fhonn teorainn a chur "
"ar an méid comhthreomhaíochta is féidir le hionsaitheoir a úsáid, féach: "
"rfc: `7914` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "To use scrypt_ as your default storage algorithm, do the following:"
msgstr ""
"Chun scrypt_ a úsáid mar do algartam stórála réamhshocraithe, déan an méid "
"seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Modify :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` to list ``ScryptPasswordHasher`` first. "
"That is, in your settings file::"
msgstr ""
"Athraigh: Socrú: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` chun `ScryptPasswordHasher`` a liostáil "
"ar dtús. Is é sin, i do chomhad socruithe::"

msgid "``scrypt`` requires OpenSSL 1.1+."
msgstr "Éilíonn ``scrypt`` OpenSSL 1.1+."

msgid "Increasing the salt entropy"
msgstr "An t-entróp salainn a mhéadú"

msgid ""
"Most password hashes include a salt along with their password hash in order "
"to protect against rainbow table attacks. The salt itself is a random value "
"which increases the size and thus the cost of the rainbow table and is "
"currently set at 128 bits with the ``salt_entropy`` value in the "
"``BasePasswordHasher``. As computing and storage costs decrease this value "
"should be raised. When implementing your own password hasher you are free to "
"override this value in order to use a desired entropy level for your "
"password hashes. ``salt_entropy`` is measured in bits."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an chuid is mó de na hashes pasfhocal salann in éineacht lena hash "
"pasfhocal d'fhonn cosaint a dhéanamh ar ionsaithe tábla tuar ceatha. Is "
"luach randamach é an salann féin a mhéadaíonn méid agus dá bhrí sin costas "
"an tábla ceatha agus tá sé socraithe faoi láthair ag 128 giotán leis an "
"luach `salt_entropy`` sa `BasePasswordHasher``. Mar a laghdaíonn costais "
"ríomhaireachta agus stórála ba chóir an luach seo a ardú Agus do phasfhocal "
"féin á chur i bhfeidhm tá saor agat an luach seo a shárú d'fhonn an leibhéal "
"entróp atá ag teastáil a úsáid le haghaidh do hashes pasfhocal. Tomhaistear "
"`salt_entropy`` i ngiotáin."

msgid "Implementation detail"
msgstr "Sonraí cur chun feidhme"

msgid ""
"Due to the method in which salt values are stored the ``salt_entropy`` value "
"is effectively a minimum value. For instance a value of 128 would provide a "
"salt which would actually contain 131 bits of entropy."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an modh ina stóráiltear luachanna salainn is íosluach é an "
"luach `salt_entropy`` go héifeachtach. Mar shampla, chuirfeadh luach 128 "
"salann ar fáil ina mbeadh 131 giotán d'entróp i ndáiríre."

msgid "Increasing the work factor"
msgstr "An fachtóir oibre a mhéadú"

msgid "PBKDF2 and bcrypt"
msgstr "PBKDF2 agus bcrypt"

msgid ""
"The PBKDF2 and bcrypt algorithms use a number of iterations or rounds of "
"hashing. This deliberately slows down attackers, making attacks against "
"hashed passwords harder. However, as computing power increases, the number "
"of iterations needs to be increased. We've chosen a reasonable default (and "
"will increase it with each release of Django), but you may wish to tune it "
"up or down, depending on your security needs and available processing power. "
"To do so, you'll subclass the appropriate algorithm and override the "
"``iterations`` parameter (use the ``rounds`` parameter when subclassing a "
"bcrypt hasher). For example, to increase the number of iterations used by "
"the default PBKDF2 algorithm:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann halgartaim PBKDF2 agus bcrypt roinnt athrá nó babhtaí hashing. "
"Moillíonn sé seo ionsaitheoirí d'aon ghnó, rud a fhágann go bhfuil ionsaithe "
"i gcoinne pasfhoc Mar sin féin, de réir mar a mhéadaíonn cumhacht "
"ríomhaireachta, is gá líon na n-athrá a mhéadú. Tá réamhshocrú réasúnta "
"roghnaithe againn (agus méadóimid sé le gach scaoileadh de Django), ach "
"b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat é a thiúnadh suas nó síos, ag brath ar do "
"riachtanais slándála agus ar an chumhacht próiseála atá ar fáil. Chun é sin "
"a dhéanamh, déanfaidh tú an algartam cuí a fho-aicmiú agus an paraiméadar "
"``iterations` a shárú (bain úsáid as an paraiméadar ``rounds` agus tú ag fo-"
"aicmiú hasher bcrypt). Mar shampla, chun líon na n-athrú a úsáideann an "
"algartam PBKDF2 réamhshocraithe a mhéadú:"

msgid ""
"Create a subclass of ``django.contrib.auth.hashers.PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` ::"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh fo-aicme de `django.contrib.auth.hashers.pbkdf2PasswordHasher``:"

msgid ""
"Save this somewhere in your project. For example, you might put this in a "
"file like ``myproject/hashers.py``."
msgstr ""
"Sábháil seo áit éigin i do thionscadal. Mar shampla, b'fhéidir go gcuirfeá é "
"seo i gcomhad mar ``myproject/hashers.py``."

msgid "Add your new hasher as the first entry in :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS`::"
msgstr ""
"Cuir do hasher nua leis mar an gcéad iontráil in:setting: "
"`PASSWORD_HASHERS`::"

msgid ""
"That's it -- now your Django install will use more iterations when it stores "
"passwords using PBKDF2."
msgstr ""
"Sin é - anois úsáidfidh do shuiteáil Django níos mó athraithe nuair a "
"stóráil sé pasfhocail ag baint úsáide as PBKDF2."

msgid ""
"bcrypt ``rounds`` is a logarithmic work factor, e.g. 12 rounds means ``2 ** "
"12`` iterations."
msgstr ""
"Is fachtóir oibre logartamach é bcrypt ``babhtaí ``, m.sh. ciallaíonn 12 "
"babhta ``2 ** 12`` athraitheanna."

msgid "Argon2"
msgstr "Argon2"

msgid "Argon2 has the following attributes that can be customized:"
msgstr "Tá na tréithe seo a leanas ag Argon2 is féidir a shaincheapadh:"

msgid "``time_cost`` controls the number of iterations within the hash."
msgstr "Rialaíonn ``time_cost`` líon na n-athrá laistigh den hash."

msgid ""
"``memory_cost`` controls the size of memory that must be used during the "
"computation of the hash."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn ``memory_cost`` méid na cuimhne nach mór a úsáid le linn ríomh an "
"hash."

msgid ""
"``parallelism`` controls how many CPUs the computation of the hash can be "
"parallelized on."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn ``parallelism`` cé mhéad CPU is féidir ríomh an hash a dhéanamh "
"comhthreomhar orthu."

msgid ""
"The default values of these attributes are probably fine for you. If you "
"determine that the password hash is too fast or too slow, you can tweak it "
"as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Is dócha go bhfuil luachanna réamhshocraithe na dtréithe seo go breá duit. "
"Má chinneann tú go bhfuil an hash pasfhocal ró-tapa nó ró-mhall, is féidir "
"leat é a tweak mar seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Choose ``parallelism`` to be the number of threads you can spare computing "
"the hash."
msgstr ""
"Roghnaigh `paralelism`` mar líon na snáitheanna is féidir leat a spáráil a "
"ríomh an hash."

msgid "Choose ``memory_cost`` to be the KiB of memory you can spare."
msgstr ""
"Roghnaigh `memory_cost`` chun a bheith mar an KiB de chuimhne is féidir leat "
"a spáráil."

msgid ""
"Adjust ``time_cost`` and measure the time hashing a password takes. Pick a "
"``time_cost`` that takes an acceptable time for you. If ``time_cost`` set to "
"1 is unacceptably slow, lower ``memory_cost``."
msgstr ""
"Coigeartaigh ``time_cost`` agus tomhas an t-am a thógann hashú pasfhocal. "
"Roghnaigh ``time_cost`` a thógann am inghlactha duit. Má tá ``time_cost`` "
"socraithe go 1 go neamhghlactha go mall, ísligh ``memory_cost``."

msgid "``memory_cost`` interpretation"
msgstr "Léirmhíniú ``memory_cost``"

msgid ""
"The argon2 command-line utility and some other libraries interpret the "
"``memory_cost`` parameter differently from the value that Django uses. The "
"conversion is given by ``memory_cost == 2 ** memory_cost_commandline``."
msgstr ""
"Léirmhíníonn fóntais líne ordaithe argon2 agus roinnt leabharlanna eile an "
"paraiméadar `memory_cost` difriúil ón luach a úsáideann Django. Tugann an "
"tiontú le ``memory_cost == 2 ** memory_cost_commandline``."

msgid "``scrypt``"
msgstr "``scrípt``"

msgid "scrypt_ has the following attributes that can be customized:"
msgstr "Tá na tréithe seo a leanas ag scrypt_ is féidir a shaincheapadh:"

msgid "``work_factor`` controls the number of iterations within the hash."
msgstr "Rialaíonn ``work_factor ``líon na n-athrá laistigh den hash."

msgid "``block_size``"
msgstr "``Bloc_size``"

msgid "``parallelism`` controls how many threads will run in parallel."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn ``parallelism`` cé mhéad snáitheanna a bheidh ag rith go "
"comhthreomhar."

msgid ""
"``maxmem`` limits the maximum size of memory that can be used during the "
"computation of the hash. Defaults to ``0``, which means the default "
"limitation from the OpenSSL library."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann `maxmem`` teorainn leis an méid uasta na cuimhne is féidir a úsáid "
"le linn ríomh an hash. Réamhshocraithe go ``0``, rud a chiallaíonn an "
"teorannú réamhshocraithe ón leabharlann OpenSSL."

msgid ""
"We've chosen reasonable defaults, but you may wish to tune it up or down, "
"depending on your security needs and available processing power."
msgstr ""
"Tá réamhshocruithe réasúnta roghnaithe againn, ach b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat "
"é a thiúnú suas nó síos, ag brath ar do riachtanais slándála agus ar an "
"chumhacht próiseála atá ar fáil."

msgid "Estimating memory usage"
msgstr "Úsáid cuimhne a mheas"

msgid "The minimum memory requirement of scrypt_ is::"
msgstr "Is é an riachtanas cuimhne íosta scrypt_:"

msgid ""
"so you may need to tweak ``maxmem`` when changing the ``work_factor`` or "
"``block_size`` values."
msgstr ""
"mar sin b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort ``maxmem`` a tweak agus na luachanna "
"``work_factor`` nó `block_size`` á athrú."

msgid "Password upgrading"
msgstr "Uasghrádú Pasfho"

msgid ""
"When users log in, if their passwords are stored with anything other than "
"the preferred algorithm, Django will automatically upgrade the algorithm to "
"the preferred one. This means that old installs of Django will get "
"automatically more secure as users log in, and it also means that you can "
"switch to new (and better) storage algorithms as they get invented."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a logálann úsáideoirí isteach, má stóráiltear a gcuid pasfhocail le "
"rud ar bith seachas an algartam is fearr leat, déanfaidh Django an algartam "
"a uasghrádú go huathoibríoch go dt Ciallaíonn sé seo go n-éireoidh sean-"
"shuiteálacha de Django níos sábháilte go huathoibríoch de réir mar a "
"logálann úsáideoirí isteach, agus ciallaíonn sé freisin gur féidir leat "
"aistriú chuig halgartaim stórála nua (agus níos fearr) de réir mar a "
"chruthaítear iad."

msgid ""
"However, Django can only upgrade passwords that use algorithms mentioned "
"in :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS`, so as you upgrade to new systems you should "
"make sure never to *remove* entries from this list. If you do, users using "
"unmentioned algorithms won't be able to upgrade. Hashed passwords will be "
"updated when increasing (or decreasing) the number of PBKDF2 iterations, "
"bcrypt rounds, or argon2 attributes."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, ní féidir le Django ach pasfhocail a úsáideann halgartaim a "
"luaitear in:setting: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` a uasghrádú, mar sin agus tú ag "
"uasghrádú chuig córais nua ba chóir duit a chinntiú nach ndéanfaidh tú "
"iontrálacha a bhaint riamh ón liosta seo. Má dhéanann tú, ní bheidh "
"úsáideoirí a úsáideann halgartaim neamhluaite in ann uasghrádú a dhéanamh. "
"Déanfar pasfhocail hashaithe a nuashonrú nuair a mhéadaítear (nó ag laghdú) "
"líon na n-athrú PBKDF2, babhtaí bcrypt, nó tréithe argon2."

msgid ""
"Be aware that if all the passwords in your database aren't encoded in the "
"default hasher's algorithm, you may be vulnerable to a user enumeration "
"timing attack due to a difference between the duration of a login request "
"for a user with a password encoded in a non-default algorithm and the "
"duration of a login request for a nonexistent user (which runs the default "
"hasher). You may be able to mitigate this by :ref:`upgrading older password "
"hashes <wrapping-password-hashers>`."
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas mura bhfuil na pasfhocail go léir i do bhunachar sonraí "
"ionchódaithe in algartam réamhshocraithe, d'fhéadfá a bheith leochaileach "
"d'ionsaí uainiúcháin úsáideora mar gheall ar difríocht idir fad iarratais "
"logála isteach d'úsáideoir le haghaidh pasfhocal ionchódaithe in algartam "
"neamhréamhshocraithe agus fad iarratais logála isteach d'úsáideoir nach "
"bhfuil ann (a ritheann an hasher réamhshocraithe). <wrapping-password-"
"hashers>B'fhéidir go mbeidh tú in ann é seo a mhaolú trí:ref: `hashes "
"pasfhocal níos sine a uasghrádú `."

msgid "Password upgrading without requiring a login"
msgstr "Uasghrádú pasfhocal gan logáil isteach a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"If you have an existing database with an older, weak hash such as MD5, you "
"might want to upgrade those hashes yourself instead of waiting for the "
"upgrade to happen when a user logs in (which may never happen if a user "
"doesn't return to your site). In this case, you can use a \"wrapped\" "
"password hasher."
msgstr ""
"Má tá bunachar sonraí agat le hash níos sine, lag mar MD5, b'fhéidir gur "
"mhaith leat na hashes sin a uasghrádú féin in ionad fanacht go dtarlóidh an "
"t-uasghrádú nuair a logálann úsáideoir isteach (nach bhféadfadh tarlú riamh "
"mura bhfillfidh úsáideoir ar do shuíomh). Sa chás seo, is féidir leat hasher "
"pasfhocal “fillte” a úsáid."

msgid ""
"For this example, we'll migrate a collection of MD5 hashes to use "
"PBKDF2(MD5(password)) and add the corresponding password hasher for checking "
"if a user entered the correct password on login. We assume we're using the "
"built-in ``User`` model and that our project has an ``accounts`` app. You "
"can modify the pattern to work with any algorithm or with a custom user "
"model."
msgstr ""
"Don sampla seo, aistróimid bailiúchán de hashes MD5 chun PBKDF2 (MD5 "
"(pasfhocal) a úsáid agus cuirfimid an hasher pasfhocal comhfhreagrach le "
"seiceáil an chuir úsáideoir an bhféadfadh úsáideoir an focal faire ceart "
"isteach ar logáil isteach. Glacaimid leis go bhfuilimid ag úsáid an tsamhail "
"``Úsáideoir ``ionsuite agus go bhfuil aip ``cuntas`` ag ár dtionscadal. Is "
"féidir leat an patrún a mhodhnú chun oibriú le haon algartam nó le samhail "
"úsáideora saincheaptha."

msgid "First, we'll add the custom hasher:"
msgstr "Ar dtús, cuirfimid an hasher saincheaptha leis:"

msgid "``accounts/hashers.py``"
msgstr "``accounts/hashers.py``"

msgid "The data migration might look something like:"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cuma ar an imirce sonraí mar:"

msgid "``accounts/migrations/0002_migrate_md5_passwords.py``"
msgstr "``cuntas/imirceach/0002_migrate_md5_passwords.py``"

msgid ""
"Be aware that this migration will take on the order of several minutes for "
"several thousand users, depending on the speed of your hardware."
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas go dtógfaidh an imirce seo ar ord cúpla nóiméad do roinnt "
"mílte úsáideoir, ag brath ar luas do chrua-earraí."

msgid "Finally, we'll add a :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` setting:"
msgstr "Faoi dheireadh, cuirfimid suíomh a:setting: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` leis:"

msgid "``mysite/settings.py``"
msgstr "``mysite/settings.py``"

msgid "Include any other hashers that your site uses in this list."
msgstr ""
"Cuir aon hashers eile a úsáideann do shuíomh sa liosta seo san áireamh."

msgid "Included hashers"
msgstr "Hashers san áireamh"

msgid "The full list of hashers included in Django is::"
msgstr "Is é an liosta iomlán de hashers atá san áireamh i Django:"

msgid "The corresponding algorithm names are:"
msgstr "Is iad na hainmneacha algartam comhfhreagrach"

msgid "``pbkdf2_sha256``"
msgstr "``pbkdf2_sha256``"

msgid "``pbkdf2_sha1``"
msgstr "``pbkdf2_sha1``"

msgid "``argon2``"
msgstr "``Argon2``"

msgid "``bcrypt_sha256``"
msgstr "``bcrypt_sha256``"

msgid "``bcrypt``"
msgstr "``bcrypt``"

msgid "``md5``"
msgstr "``md5``"

msgid "Writing your own hasher"
msgstr "Do hasher féin a scríobh"

msgid ""
"If you write your own password hasher that contains a work factor such as a "
"number of iterations, you should implement a ``harden_runtime(self, "
"password, encoded)`` method to bridge the runtime gap between the work "
"factor supplied in the ``encoded`` password and the default work factor of "
"the hasher. This prevents a user enumeration timing attack due to  "
"difference between a login request for a user with a password encoded in an "
"older number of iterations and a nonexistent user (which runs the default "
"hasher's default number of iterations)."
msgstr ""
"Má scríobhann tú do phasfhocal féin ina bhfuil fachtóir oibre cosúil le "
"roinnt athraithe, ba cheart duit modh `harden_runtime (self, password, "
"ionchódaithe) `a chur i bhfeidhm chun an bearna réamhshocraithe idir an "
"fachtóir oibre a sholáthraítear sa phasfhocal ``encoded ``agus fachtóir "
"oibre réamhshocraithe an hasher. Cuireann sé seo cosc ar ionsaí uainiúcháin "
"áireamh úsáideora mar gheall ar difríocht idir iarratas logála isteach "
"d'úsáideoir le pasfhocal atá ionchódaithe i líon níos sine athrá agus "
"úsáideoir nach bhfuil ann (a ritheann líon réamhshocraithe athraithe an "
"hasher réamhshocraithe)."

msgid ""
"Taking PBKDF2 as example, if ``encoded`` contains 20,000 iterations and the "
"hasher's default ``iterations`` is 30,000, the method should run "
"``password`` through another 10,000 iterations of PBKDF2."
msgstr ""
"Ag glacadh le PBKDF2 mar shampla, má tá 20,000 athraitheach sa ``encoded "
"``agus is é 30,000 réamhshocraithe an hasher, ba chóir don modh "
"``pasfhocal`` a reáchtáil trí 10,000 athrú eile de PBKDF2."

msgid ""
"If your hasher doesn't have a work factor, implement the method as a no-op "
"(``pass``)."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil fachtóir oibre ag do hasher, cuir an modh i bhfeidhm mar no-op "
"(``pass ``)."

msgid "Manually managing a user's password"
msgstr "Pasfhocal úsáideora a bhainistiú de láimh"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`django.contrib.auth.hashers` module provides a set of functions to "
"create and validate hashed passwords. You can use them independently from "
"the ``User`` model."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an modúl:MOD: `django.contrib.auth.hashers` sraith feidhmeanna "
"chun pasfhocail hashaithe a chruthú agus a bhailíochtú. Is féidir leat iad a "
"úsáid go neamhspleách ón tsamhail ``Úsáideoir ``."

msgid ""
"If you'd like to manually authenticate a user by comparing a plain-text "
"password to the hashed password in the database, use the convenience "
"function :func:`check_password`. It takes two mandatory arguments: the plain-"
"text password to check, and the full value of a user's ``password`` field in "
"the database to check against. It returns ``True`` if they match, ``False`` "
"otherwise. Optionally, you can pass a callable ``setter`` that takes the "
"password and will be called when you need to regenerate it. You can also "
"pass ``preferred`` to change a hashing algorithm if you don't want to use "
"the default (first entry of ``PASSWORD_HASHERS`` setting). See :ref:`auth-"
"included-hashers` for the algorithm name of each hasher."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat úsáideoir a fhíordheimhniú de láimh trí phasfhocal téacs "
"simplí a chur i gcomparáid leis an bhfocal faire hasháite sa bhunachar "
"sonraí, bain úsáid as an bhfeidhm áisiúlachta: func: `check_password`. "
"Tógann sé dhá argóint éigeantach: an pasfhocal gnáthtéacs le seiceáil, agus "
"luach iomlán réimse `pasfhocal ``úsáideora sa bhunachar sonraí le seiceáil "
"ina choinne. Filleann sé ``True`` má mheaitseálann siad, ``False`` ar shlí "
"eile. Go roghnach, is féidir leat ``setter`` inghlaonta a rith a thógann an "
"pasfhocal agus a ghlaofar air nuair is gá duit é a athghiniúint. Is féidir "
"leat ``preferred`` a rith freisin chun algartam hashing a athrú mura "
"dteastaíonn uait an réamhshocrú a úsáid (an chéad iontráil de shuíomh "
"``PASSWORD_HASHERS``). Féach:ref: `auth-included-hashers` le haghaidh ainm "
"algartam gach hasher."

msgid ""
"Creates a hashed password in the format used by this application. It takes "
"one mandatory argument: the password in plain-text (string or bytes). "
"Optionally, you can provide a salt and a hashing algorithm to use, if you "
"don't want to use the defaults (first entry of ``PASSWORD_HASHERS`` "
"setting). See :ref:`auth-included-hashers` for the algorithm name of each "
"hasher. If the password argument is ``None``, an unusable password is "
"returned (one that will never be accepted by :func:`check_password`)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé pasfhocal hashed san fhormáid a úsáideann an feidhmchlár seo. "
"Tógann sé argóint éigeantach amháin: an pasfhocal i dtéacs simplí (teaghrán "
"nó béite). Go roghnach, is féidir leat salann agus algartam hashing a "
"sholáthar le húsáid, mura dteastaíonn uait na réamhshocruithe a úsáid (an "
"chéad iontráil de shuíomh ``PASSWORD_HASHERS``). Féach:ref: `auth-included-"
"hashers` le haghaidh ainm algartam gach hasher. Más é ``None`` an argóint "
"pasfhocal, cuirtear pasfhocal neamhúsáidte ar ais (ceann nach nglacfaidh: "
"func: `check_password` riamh)."

msgid ""
"Returns ``False`` if the password is a result "
"of :meth:`.User.set_unusable_password`."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``False`` má tá an pasfhocal mar thoradh ar:meth: "
"`.user.set_unusable_password`."

msgid "Password validation"
msgstr "Bailíochtú pasfhocal"

msgid ""
"Users often choose poor passwords. To help mitigate this problem, Django "
"offers pluggable password validation. You can configure multiple password "
"validators at the same time. A few validators are included in Django, but "
"you can write your own as well."
msgstr ""
"Is minic a roghnaíonn úsáideoirí pasfhocail Chun cabhrú leis an bhfadhb seo "
"a mhaolú, cuireann Django bailíochtú pasfhocal plugáilte ar fáil Is féidir "
"leat bailíochtóirí pasfhocal iolracha a chumrú ag an am céanna. Tá cúpla "
"bailíochtóir san áireamh i Django, ach is féidir leat do chuid féin a "
"scríobh freisin."

msgid ""
"Each password validator must provide a help text to explain the requirements "
"to the user, validate a given password and return an error message if it "
"does not meet the requirements, and optionally define a callback to be "
"notified when the password for a user has been changed. Validators can also "
"have optional settings to fine tune their behavior."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh gach bailíochtóir pasfhocal téacs cabhrach a sholáthar chun na "
"riachtanais a mhíniú don úsáideoir, pasfhocal ar leith a bhailíochtú agus "
"teachtaireacht earráide a thabhairt ar ais mura gcomhlíonann sé na "
"riachtanais, agus glaoch ar ais a shainiú go roghnach a chuirfear in iúl "
"nuair a athraítear an focal faire d'úsáideoir. Is féidir le bailíochtóirí "
"socruithe roghnacha a bheith acu freisin chun a n-iompar a mhíniú."

msgid ""
"Validation is controlled by the :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` setting. "
"The default for the setting is an empty list, which means no validators are "
"applied. In new projects created with the default :djadmin:`startproject` "
"template, a set of validators is enabled by default."
msgstr ""
"Tá bailíochtú á rialú ag an socrú: setting: `AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`. Is é "
"liosta folamh an réamhshocraithe don socrú, rud a chiallaíonn nach gcuirtear "
"aon bhailíochtóirí i bhfeidhm. I dtionscadail nua a cruthaíodh leis an "
"teimpléad réamhshocraithe: djadmin: `startproject`, cumasaítear tacar "
"bailíochtóirí de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"By default, validators are used in the forms to reset or change passwords "
"and in the :djadmin:`createsuperuser` and :djadmin:`changepassword` "
"management commands. Validators aren't applied at the model level, for "
"example in ``User.objects.create_user()`` and ``create_superuser()``, "
"because we assume that developers, not users, interact with Django at that "
"level and also because model validation doesn't automatically run as part of "
"creating models."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáidtear bailíochtóirí sna foirmeacha chun "
"pasfhocail a athshocrú nó a athrú agus sna horduithe bainistíochta: djadmin: "
"`createsuperuser` agus:djadmin: `changepassword`. Ní chuirtear bailíochtóirí "
"i bhfeidhm ag an leibhéal samhail, mar shampla in ``User.objects.create_user "
"() ``agus ``create_superuser () `, toisc go nglacaimid leis go n-"
"idirghníomhaíonn forbróirí, ní úsáideoirí, le Django ag an leibhéal sin agus "
"freisin toisc nach ritheann bailíochtú samhail go huathoibríoch mar chuid de "
"mhúnlaí a chruthú."

msgid ""
"Password validation can prevent the use of many types of weak passwords. "
"However, the fact that a password passes all the validators doesn't "
"guarantee that it is a strong password. There are many factors that can "
"weaken a password that are not detectable by even the most advanced password "
"validators."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le bailíochtú pasfhocal cosc a chur ar úsáid go leor cineálacha "
"pasfhocail laga. Mar sin féin, ní ráthaíonn an fíric go dtéann pasfhocal ar "
"na bailíochtóirí go léir gur pasfhocal láidir é. Tá go leor fachtóirí ann a "
"d'fhéadfadh pasfhocal a lagú nach féidir fiú na bailíochtóirí pasfhocal is "
"úire a bhrath."

msgid "Enabling password validation"
msgstr "Cumasú bailíochtú pasfhocal"

msgid ""
"Password validation is configured in the :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` "
"setting::"
msgstr ""
"Tá bailíochtú pasfhocal cumraithe sa socrú:: `AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`:"

msgid "This example enables all four included validators:"
msgstr "Cumasaíonn an sampla seo na ceithre bhailíochtóirí san áireamh"

msgid ""
"``UserAttributeSimilarityValidator``, which checks the similarity between "
"the password and a set of attributes of the user."
msgstr ""
"``UserAttributeSimilarityValidator``, a sheiceálann an chosúlacht idir an "
"pasfhocal agus sraith tréithe an úsáideora."

msgid ""
"``MinimumLengthValidator``, which checks whether the password meets a "
"minimum length. This validator is configured with a custom option: it now "
"requires the minimum length to be nine characters, instead of the default "
"eight."
msgstr ""
"``MinimumLengthValidator``, a sheiceálann an gcomhlíonann an pasfhocal fad "
"íosta. Tá an bailíochtóir seo cumraithe le rogha saincheaptha: éilíonn sé "
"anois go mbeadh an fad íosta ná naoi charachtar, in ionad na hocht "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"``CommonPasswordValidator``, which checks whether the password occurs in a "
"list of common passwords. By default, it compares to an included list of "
"20,000 common passwords."
msgstr ""
"``CommonPasswordValidator``, a sheiceálann an dtarlaíonn an pasfhocal i "
"liosta de phasfhocail choitianta. De réir réamhshocraithe, déanann sé "
"comparáid le liosta san áireamh de 20,000 pasfhocal coitianta."

msgid ""
"``NumericPasswordValidator``, which checks whether the password isn't "
"entirely numeric."
msgstr ""
"``NumericPasswordValidator``, a sheiceálann an bhfuil an pasfhocal uimhriúil "
"go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"For ``UserAttributeSimilarityValidator`` and ``CommonPasswordValidator``, "
"we're using the default settings in this example. "
"``NumericPasswordValidator`` has no settings."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le ``UserAttributeSimilarityValidator`` agus "
"``CommonPasswordValidator``, táimid ag úsáid na socruithe réamhshocraithe sa "
"sampla seo. Níl aon socruithe ag ``NumericPasswordValidator``."

msgid ""
"The help texts and any errors from password validators are always returned "
"in the order they are listed in :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear na téacsanna cabhrach agus aon earráidí ó bhailíochtóirí pasfhocal "
"ar ais i gcónaí san ord a liostaítear ion:setting: "
"`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`."

msgid "Included validators"
msgstr "Bailíochtóirí san áireamh"

msgid "Django includes four validators:"
msgstr "Cuimsíonn Django ceithre bhailíochtóir:"

msgid ""
"Validates that the password is of a minimum length. The minimum length can "
"be customized with the ``min_length`` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn sé go bhfuil an pasfhocal ar fad íosta. Is féidir an fad íosta a "
"shaincheapadh leis an bparaiméadar ``min_length ``."

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the ``ValidationError`` error message. Defaults to "
"``\"This password is too short. It must contain at least <min_length> "
"characters.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the validator's help text. Defaults to ``\"Your "
"password must contain at least <min_length> characters.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Validates that the password is sufficiently different from certain "
"attributes of the user."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn sé go bhfuil an pasfhocal difriúil go leor ó thréithe áirithe an "
"úsáideora."

msgid ""
"The ``user_attributes`` parameter should be an iterable of names of user "
"attributes to compare to. If this argument is not provided, the default is "
"used: ``'username', 'first_name', 'last_name', 'email'``. Attributes that "
"don't exist are ignored."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an paraiméadar ``user_attributes`` ina athraitheach "
"d'ainmneacha tréithe úsáideora le comparáid a dhéanamh leo. Mura gcuirtear "
"an argóint seo ar fáil, úsáidtear an réamhshocrú: ````ainm úsáideora', "
"'first_name', 'last _name', 'r-phost'``. Déantar neamhaird ar thréithe nach "
"bhfuil ann."

msgid ""
"The maximum allowed similarity of passwords can be set on a scale of 0.1 to "
"1.0 with the ``max_similarity`` parameter. This is compared to the result "
"of :meth:`difflib.SequenceMatcher.quick_ratio`. A value of 0.1 rejects "
"passwords unless they are substantially different from the "
"``user_attributes``, whereas a value of 1.0 rejects only passwords that are "
"identical to an attribute's value."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an cosúlacht uasta ceadaithe de phasfhocail a shocrú ar scála 0.1 "
"go 1.0 leis an bparaiméadar ``max_similarity``. Déantar é seo i gcomparáid "
"leis an toradh ar:meth: `Difflib.sequencematcher.quick_ratio`. Diúltaíonn "
"luach 0.1 do phasfhocail mura bhfuil siad difriúil go suntasach ón "
"``user_attributes``, ach ní dhiúltaíonn luach 1.0 ach pasfhocail atá "
"comhionann le luach tréithe."

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the ``ValidationError`` error message. Defaults to "
"``\"The password is too similar to the <user_attribute>.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the validator's help text. Defaults to ``\"Your "
"password can’t be too similar to your other personal information.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Validates that the password is not a common password. This converts the "
"password to lowercase (to do a case-insensitive comparison) and checks it "
"against a list of 20,000 common password created by `Royce Williams <https://"
"gist.github.com/roycewilliams/226886fd01572964e1431ac8afc999ce>`_."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn sé nach pasfhocal coitianta é an pasfhocal. < https://"
"gist.github.com/roycewilliams/226886fd01572964e1431ac8afc999ce>Athraíonn sé "
"seo an pasfhocal go litreacha beaga (chun comparáid cás-neamh-íogair a "
"dhéanamh) agus seiceálann sé é i gcoinne liosta de 20,000 pasfhocal "
"coitianta a chruthaigh `Royce Williams`_."

msgid ""
"The ``password_list_path`` can be set to the path of a custom file of common "
"passwords. This file should contain one lowercase password per line and may "
"be plain text or gzipped."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an `password_list_path`` a shocrú go cosán comhad saincheaptha de "
"phasfhocail choitianta. Ba chóir go mbeadh pasfhocal beaga amháin in aghaidh "
"an líne sa chomhad seo agus d'fhéadfadh sé go mbeadh sé téacs simplí nó "
"gzipped."

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the ``ValidationError`` error message. Defaults to "
"``\"This password is too common.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the validator's help text. Defaults to ``\"Your "
"password can’t be a commonly used password.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Validate that the password is not entirely numeric."
msgstr "Bailíochtaigh nach bhfuil an pasfhocal uimhriúil go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the ``ValidationError`` error message. Defaults to "
"``\"This password is entirely numeric.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A hook for customizing the validator's help text. Defaults to ``\"Your "
"password can’t be entirely numeric.\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Integrating validation"
msgstr "Bailíochtú a chomhth"

msgid ""
"There are a few functions in ``django.contrib.auth.password_validation`` "
"that you can call from your own forms or other code to integrate password "
"validation. This can be useful if you use custom forms for password setting, "
"or if you have API calls that allow passwords to be set, for example."
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla feidhm i ``django.contrib.auth.password_validation`` ar féidir leat "
"glaoch a ghlaoch ó d'fhoirmeacha féin nó ó chód eile chun bailíochtú "
"pasfhocal a chomhtháthú. Is féidir leis seo a bheith úsáideach má úsáideann "
"tú foirmeacha saincheaptha le haghaidh socrú pasfhocal, nó má tá glaonna API "
"agat a cheadaíonn pasfhocail a shocrú, mar shampla."

msgid ""
"Validates a password. If all validators find the password valid, returns "
"``None``. If one or more validators reject the password, raises "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with all the error messages "
"from the validators."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn sé pasfhocal. Má aimsíonn gach bailíochtóir an pasfhocal bailí, "
"filleann sé ``None``. Má dhiúltaíonn bailíochtóirí amháin nó níos mó don "
"phasfhocal, ardaíonn sé a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` "
"leis na teachtaireachtaí earráide go léir ó na bailíochtóirí."

msgid ""
"The ``user`` object is optional: if it's not provided, some validators may "
"not be able to perform any validation and will accept any password."
msgstr ""
"Tá an réad ``úsáideoir ``roghnach: mura gcuirtear ar fáil é, b'fhéidir nach "
"mbeidh roinnt bailíochtóirí in ann aon bhailíochtú a dhéanamh agus glacfaidh "
"siad le haon phasfhocal."

msgid ""
"Informs all validators that the password has been changed. This can be used "
"by validators such as one that prevents password reuse. This should be "
"called once the password has been successfully changed."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann gach bailíochtóir ar an eolas go bhfuil an pasfhocal athraithe. Is "
"féidir le bailíochtóirí mar cheann a chuireann cosc ar athúsáid pasfhocal é "
"seo a úsáid. Ba chóir é seo a ghlaoch nuair a athraítear an pasfhocal go "
"rathúil."

msgid ""
"For subclasses of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser`, the "
"password field will be marked as \"dirty\" when "
"calling :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser.set_password` "
"which triggers a call to ``password_changed()`` after the user is saved."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le fo-aicmí de:class: `~Django.Contrib.Auth.Models.AbstractBaseUser`, "
"marcálfar an réimse pasfhocal mar “salach” agus tú ag glao:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.abstractBaseUser.set_password` a spreagann glao "
"ar `password_modified () `tar éis an úsáideoir a shábháil."

msgid ""
"Returns a list of the help texts of all validators. These explain the "
"password requirements to the user."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé liosta de théacsanna cabhrach na mbailíochtóirí go léir ar ais. "
"Míníonn siad seo na riachtanais phasfhocal don úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"Returns an HTML string with all help texts in an ``<ul>``. This is helpful "
"when adding password validation to forms, as you can pass the output "
"directly to the ``help_text`` parameter of a form field."
msgstr ""
"Tugann teaghrán HTML ar ais le gach téacs cabhrach i <ul>```. Tá sé seo "
"cabhrach agus bailíochtú pasfhocal á chur le foirmeacha, mar is féidir leat "
"an t-aschur a chur go díreach chuig paraiméadar ``help_text`` réimse foirme."

msgid ""
"Returns a set of validator objects based on the ``validator_config`` "
"parameter. By default, all functions use the validators defined "
"in :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`, but by calling this function with an "
"alternate set of validators and then passing the result into the "
"``password_validators`` parameter of the other functions, your custom set of "
"validators will be used instead. This is useful when you have a typical set "
"of validators to use for most scenarios, but also have a special situation "
"that requires a custom set. If you always use the same set of validators, "
"there is no need to use this function, as the configuration "
"from :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` is used by default."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé tacar rudaí bailíochtaithe ar ais bunaithe ar an bparaiméadar "
"``validator_config``. De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáideann gach feidhm na "
"bailíochtóirí atá sainmhínithe in:setting: `AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`, ach "
"tríd an bhfeidhm seo a ghlaoch le tacar malartach bailíochtóirí agus ansin "
"an toradh a chur isteach i bparaiméadar ``password_validators ``na "
"feidhmeanna eile, úsáidfear do shraith saincheaptha bailíochtóirí ina ionad. "
"Tá sé seo úsáideach nuair a bhíonn tipiciúil tacar bailíochtóirí agat le "
"húsáid don chuid is mó de na cásanna, ach tá cás speisialta agat freisin a "
"éilíonn tacar saincheaptha. Má úsáideann tú an tacar bailíochtóirí céanna i "
"gcónaí, ní gá an fheidhm seo a úsáid, mar úsáidtear an chumraíocht "
"ó:setting: `AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"The structure of ``validator_config`` is identical to the structure "
"of :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`. The return value of this function "
"can be passed into the ``password_validators`` parameter of the functions "
"listed above."
msgstr ""
"Tá struchtúr ``validator_config`` comhionann leis an struchtúr de:setting: "
"`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`. Is féidir luach tuairisceáin na feidhme seo a "
"chur isteach i bparaiméadar ``password_validators ``de na feidhmeanna atá "
"liostaithe thuas."

msgid ""
"Note that where the password is passed to one of these functions, this "
"should always be the clear text password - not a hashed password."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, nuair a chuirtear an focal faire chuig ceann de na "
"feidhmeanna seo, ba cheart gurb é seo an pasfhocal téacs soiléir i gcónaí - "
"ní pasfhocal hashed."

msgid "Writing your own validator"
msgstr "Do bhailíochtóir féin a scríobh"

msgid ""
"If Django's built-in validators are not sufficient, you can write your own "
"password validators. Validators have a fairly small interface. They must "
"implement two methods:"
msgstr ""
"Mura leor bailíochtóirí ionsuite Django, is féidir leat do bhailíochtóirí "
"pasfhocal féin a scríobh. Tá comhéadan measartha beag ag bailíochtóirí. Ní "
"mór dóibh dhá mhodh a chur chun feidhme:"

msgid ""
"``validate(self, password, user=None)``: validate a password. Return "
"``None`` if the password is valid, or raise "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with an error message if "
"the password is not valid. You must be able to deal with ``user`` being "
"``None`` - if that means your validator can't run, return ``None`` for no "
"error."
msgstr ""
"``bailíochtú (féin, pasfhocal, úsáideoir = níl aon duine) ``: bailíochtú "
"pasfhocal. Cuir ar ais ``None`` má tá an pasfhocal bailí, nó ardaigh a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le teachtaireacht earráide mura "
"bhfuil an pasfhocal bailí. Caithfidh tú a bheith in ann déileáil le "
"```úsáideoir ```None`` - más ciallaíonn sé sin nach féidir le do "
"bhailíochtóir rith, filleadh ``None`` ar ais gan aon earráid."

msgid ""
"``get_help_text()``: provide a help text to explain the requirements to the "
"user."
msgstr ""
"``get_help_text () ``: téacs cabhrach a sholáthar chun na riachtanais a "
"mhíniú don úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"Any items in the ``OPTIONS`` in :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` for your "
"validator will be passed to the constructor. All constructor arguments "
"should have a default value."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear aon earraí sa `OPTIONS`` in:setting: `AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` do "
"bhailíochtaitheoir chuig an tógálaí. Ba chóir go mbeadh luach "
"réamhshocraithe ag gach argóint tógá"

msgid "Here's a basic example of a validator, with one optional setting::"
msgstr "Seo sampla bunúsach de bhailíochtóir, le socrú roghnach amháin:"

msgid ""
"You can also implement ``password_changed(password, user=None``), which will "
"be called after a successful password change. That can be used to prevent "
"password reuse, for example. However, if you decide to store a user's "
"previous passwords, you should never do so in clear text."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``password_changes (password, user=none``) a chur i bhfeidhm "
"freisin, a ghlaofar tar éis athrú pasfhocal rathúil. Is féidir é sin a úsáid "
"chun athúsáid pasfhocal a chosc, mar shampla. Mar sin féin, má shocraíonn tú "
"pasfhocail úsáideora roimhe seo a stóráil, níor cheart duit é sin a dhéanamh "
"riamh i dtéacs soiléir."

msgid "Django's cache framework"
msgstr "Creat taisce Django"

msgid ""
"A fundamental trade-off in dynamic websites is, well, they're dynamic. Each "
"time a user requests a page, the web server makes all sorts of calculations "
"-- from database queries to template rendering to business logic -- to "
"create the page that your site's visitor sees. This is a lot more expensive, "
"from a processing-overhead perspective, than your standard read-a-file-off-"
"the-filesystem server arrangement."
msgstr ""
"Is é trádáil bhunúsach i láithreáin ghréasáin dinimiciúla, go maith, tá siad "
"dinimiciúil. Gach uair a iarrann úsáideoir leathanach, déanann an freastalaí "
"gréasáin gach cineál ríomhanna - ó cheisteanna bunachar sonraí go rindreáil "
"teimpléad go loighic ghnó - chun an leathanach a fheiceann cuairteoir do "
"shuíomh a chruthú. Tá sé seo i bhfad níos costasaí, ó pheirspictíocht las-"
"phróiseála, ná do shocrú caighdeánach freastalaí freastalaí léamh comhad "
"lasmuigh den chóras comhaid."

msgid ""
"For most web applications, this overhead isn't a big deal. Most web "
"applications aren't ``washingtonpost.com`` or ``slashdot.org``; they're "
"small- to medium-sized sites with so-so traffic. But for medium- to high-"
"traffic sites, it's essential to cut as much overhead as possible."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le formhór na bhfeidhmchlár gréasáin, ní mór é an lasbhreas seo. Ní "
"`washingtonpost.com`` nó ``slashdot.org`` iad formhór na bhfeidhmchlár "
"gréasáin; is suíomhanna beaga go meánmhéide iad le trácht mar sin. Ach i "
"gcás suíomhanna meánmhéide agus ardthráchta, tá sé riachtanach an oiread "
"lasairde agus is féidir a ghearradh."

msgid "That's where caching comes in."
msgstr "Sin an áit a dtagann caching isteach."

msgid ""
"To cache something is to save the result of an expensive calculation so that "
"you don't have to perform the calculation next time. Here's some pseudocode "
"explaining how this would work for a dynamically generated web page:"
msgstr ""
"Is é rud éigin a thaisceadh ná toradh ríofa daor a shábháil ionas nach "
"mbeidh ort an ríomh a dhéanamh an chéad uair eile. Seo roinnt pseudocode a "
"mhíníonn conas a oibreodh sé seo le haghaidh leathanach gréasáin a ghintear "
"go dinimiciúil:"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a robust cache system that lets you save dynamic pages so "
"they don't have to be calculated for each request. For convenience, Django "
"offers different levels of cache granularity: You can cache the output of "
"specific views, you can cache only the pieces that are difficult to produce, "
"or you can cache your entire site."
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le córas taisce láidir a ligeann duit leathanaigh dhinimiciúla "
"a shábháil ionas nach gá iad a ríomh do gach iarratas. Ar mhaithe le "
"háisiúlacht, cuireann Django leibhéil éagsúla gráinneachta taisce ar fáil: "
"Is féidir leat aschur radhairc ar leith a thaisceadh, ní féidir leat ach na "
"píosaí atá deacair a tháirgeadh a thaisceadh, nó is féidir leat do shuíomh "
"iomlán a thaisceadh."

msgid ""
"Django also works well with \"downstream\" caches, such as `Squid <http://"
"www.squid-cache.org/>`_ and browser-based caches. These are the types of "
"caches that you don't directly control but to which you can provide hints "
"(via HTTP headers) about which parts of your site should be cached, and how."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn Django go maith freisin le taiscí “íossrutha”, mar shampla `Squid`< "
"http://www.squid-cache.org/> _ agus taiscí brabhsálaí-bhunaithe. Is iad seo "
"na cineálacha taiscí nach ndéanann tú rialú go díreach ach ar féidir leat "
"leideanna a sholáthar dóibh (trí cheanntásca HTTP) faoi na codanna de do "
"shuíomh ba chóir a stóráil, agus conas."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`Cache Framework design philosophy <cache-design-philosophy>` "
"explains a few of the design decisions of the framework."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an:ref: `Fealsúnacht dearaidh Cre <cache-design-philosophy>at Cache "
"`cúpla cinntí dearaidh an chreata."

msgid "Setting up the cache"
msgstr "An taisce a chur ar bun"

msgid ""
"The cache system requires a small amount of setup. Namely, you have to tell "
"it where your cached data should live -- whether in a database, on the "
"filesystem or directly in memory. This is an important decision that affects "
"your cache's performance; yes, some cache types are faster than others."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn an córas taisce méid beag socraithe. Eadhon, caithfidh tú a insint "
"dó cá háit ar chóir go gcónaíonn do shonraí taiscéadaithe - cibé acu i "
"mbunachar sonraí, ar an gcóras comhaid nó go díreach i gcuimhne. Is cinneadh "
"tábhachtach é seo a théann i bhfeidhm ar fheidhmíocht do taisce; sea, tá "
"roinnt cineálacha taisce níos gasta ná a chéile."

msgid ""
"Your cache preference goes in the :setting:`CACHES` setting in your settings "
"file. Here's an explanation of all available values for :setting:`CACHES`."
msgstr ""
"Téann do rogha taisce sa socrú:setting: `CACHES` i do chomhad socruithe. Seo "
"míniú ar na luachanna go léir atá ar fáil le haghaidh: socrú: `CACHES`."

msgid "Memcached"
msgstr "Memcached"

msgid ""
"Memcached__ is an entirely memory-based cache server, originally developed "
"to handle high loads at LiveJournal.com and subsequently open-sourced by "
"Danga Interactive. It is used by sites such as Facebook and Wikipedia to "
"reduce database access and dramatically increase site performance."
msgstr ""
"Is freastalaí taisce go hiomlán bunaithe ar chuimhne é Memcached__, a "
"forbraíodh ar dtús chun ualaí arda a láimhseáil ag LiveJournal.com agus "
"foinse oscailte ina dhiaidh sin ag Danga Interactive. Úsáideann suíomhanna "
"mar Facebook agus Wikipedia é chun rochtain ar bhunachar sonraí a laghdú "
"agus feidhmíocht an láithreáin a mhéadú go mór."

msgid ""
"Memcached runs as a daemon and is allotted a specified amount of RAM. All it "
"does is provide a fast interface for adding, retrieving and deleting data in "
"the cache. All data is stored directly in memory, so there's no overhead of "
"database or filesystem usage."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann Memcached mar démon agus leithdháiltear méid sonraithe RAM air. Níl "
"le déanamh aige ach comhéadan tapa a sholáthar chun sonraí sa taisce a chur "
"leis, a aisghabháil agus a scriosadh. Stóráiltear na sonraí go léir go "
"díreach i gcuimhne, mar sin níl aon lasbhunachar sonraí nó úsáid chórais "
"chomhad ann."

msgid ""
"After installing Memcached itself, you'll need to install a Memcached "
"binding. There are several Python Memcached bindings available; the two "
"supported by Django are :pypi:`pylibmc` and :pypi:`pymemcache`."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis duit Memcached féin a shuiteáil, beidh ort ceangailt Memcached a "
"shuiteáil. Tá roinnt ceangail Python Memcached ar fáil; is iad an dá cheann "
"a thacaíonn Django: pypi: `pylibmc` agus:pypi: `pymemcache`."

msgid "To use Memcached with Django:"
msgstr "Chun Memcached a úsáid le Django:"

msgid ""
"Set :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` to "
"``django.core.cache.backends.memcached.PyMemcacheCache`` or "
"``django.core.cache.backends.memcached.PyLibMCCache`` (depending on your "
"chosen memcached binding)"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh: Socrú: `BACKEND `go "
"``Django.core.cache.backends.memcached.pymemcachecache`<CACHES-BACKEND>` nó "
"``django.core.cache.backends.memcached.pylibmccache`` (ag brath ar an "
"gceangailt memcached roghnaithe agat)"

msgid ""
"Set :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>` to ``ip:port`` values, where "
"``ip`` is the IP address of the Memcached daemon and ``port`` is the port on "
"which Memcached is running, or to a ``unix:path`` value, where ``path`` is "
"the path to a Memcached Unix socket file."
msgstr ""
"SOC:SET:SETING: `LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>`go luachanna ``ip: port ``, áit "
"is é `ip`` seoladh IP an daemon Memcached agus ``port`` an calafort ar a "
"bhfuil Memcached ag rith, nó go luach ``unix:path``, áit is é ``path`` an "
"cosán chuig comhad soicéad Memcached Unix."

msgid ""
"In this example, Memcached is running on localhost (127.0.0.1) port 11211, "
"using the ``pymemcache`` binding::"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, tá Memcached ag rith ar chalafort localhost (127.0.0.1) "
"11211, ag baint úsáide as an cheangailteach ``pymemcache`:"

msgid ""
"In this example, Memcached is available through a local Unix socket "
"file :file:`/tmp/memcached.sock` using the ``pymemcache`` binding::"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, tá Memcached ar fáil trí chomhad soicéad áitiúil Unix: file: "
"`/tmp/memcached.sock` ag baint úsáide as an ceangailt ``pymemcache``:"

msgid ""
"One excellent feature of Memcached is its ability to share a cache over "
"multiple servers. This means you can run Memcached daemons on multiple "
"machines, and the program will treat the group of machines as a *single* "
"cache, without the need to duplicate cache values on each machine. To take "
"advantage of this feature, include all server addresses "
"in :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>`, either as a semicolon or comma "
"delimited string, or as a list."
msgstr ""
"Gné den scoth amháin de Memcached is ea a chumas taisce a roinnt thar "
"fhreastalaithe iolracha. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat daemons Memcached "
"a reáchtáil ar iliomad meaisíní, agus déileálfaidh an clár leis an ngrúpa "
"meaisíní mar taisce* aonair*, gan gá luachanna taisce a dhúbailt ar gach "
"meaisín. Ch <CACHES-LOCATION>un leas a bhaint as an ngné seo, cuir gach "
"seoladh freastalaí san áireamh in:socrú: `LOCATION `, mar shreang teoranta "
"leath-cholún nó camóg, nó mar liosta."

msgid ""
"In this example, the cache is shared over Memcached instances running on IP "
"address 172.19.26.240 and 172.19.26.242, both on port 11211::"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, roinntear an taisce thar chásanna Memcached atá ag rith ar "
"sheoladh IP 172.19.26.240 agus 172.19.26.242, araon ar chalafort 11211::"

msgid ""
"In the following example, the cache is shared over Memcached instances "
"running on the IP addresses 172.19.26.240 (port 11211), 172.19.26.242 (port "
"11212), and 172.19.26.244 (port 11213)::"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo a leanas, roinntear an taisce thar chásanna Memcached atá ag "
"rith ar na seoltaí IP 172.19.26.240 (calafort 11211), 172.19.26.242 "
"(calafort 11212), agus 172.19.26.244 (calafort 11213):"

msgid ""
"By default, the ``PyMemcacheCache`` backend sets the following options (you "
"can override them in your :setting:`OPTIONS <CACHES-OPTIONS>`)::"
msgstr ""
"<CACHES-OPTIONS>De réir réamhshocraithe, socraíonn an cúltaca "
"`PymemCacheCache`` na roghanna seo a leanas (is féidir leat iad a shárú i "
"d:setting: `OPTIONS `):"

msgid ""
"A final point about Memcached is that memory-based caching has a "
"disadvantage: because the cached data is stored in memory, the data will be "
"lost if your server crashes. Clearly, memory isn't intended for permanent "
"data storage, so don't rely on memory-based caching as your only data "
"storage. Without a doubt, *none* of the Django caching backends should be "
"used for permanent storage -- they're all intended to be solutions for "
"caching, not storage -- but we point this out here because memory-based "
"caching is particularly temporary."
msgstr ""
"Pointe deiridh faoi Memcached ná go bhfuil míbhuntáiste ag taiscáil cuimhne "
"bunaithe: toisc go stóráiltear na sonraí taisceáilte i gcuimhne, caillfear "
"na sonraí má thimpíonn do fhreastalaí. Is léir nach bhfuil cuimhne "
"beartaithe le haghaidh stórála sonraí buan, mar sin ná bí ag brath ar "
"chaching cuimhne mar an t-aon stóráil sonraí atá agat. Gan amhras, níor "
"cheart *aon cheann* de na cúltaca caching Django a úsáid le haghaidh stórála "
"buan - tá sé beartaithe go léir a bheith ina réitigh le haghaidh taiscéála, "
"ní stóráil - ach cuirimid é seo in iúl anseo toisc go bhfuil caching "
"bunaithe ar chuimhne go háirithe sealadach."

msgid "Redis"
msgstr "Redis"

msgid ""
"Redis__ is an in-memory database that can be used for caching. To begin "
"you'll need a Redis server running either locally or on a remote machine."
msgstr ""
"Is bunachar sonraí in-chuimhne é Redis__ is féidir a úsáid le haghaidh "
"taiscála. Chun tús a chur beidh freastalaí Redis ag teastáil uait ag rith go "
"háitiúil nó ar mheaisín iargúlta."

msgid ""
"After setting up the Redis server, you'll need to install Python bindings "
"for Redis. :pypi:`redis-py <redis>` is the binding supported natively by "
"Django. Installing the :pypi:`hiredis-py <hiredis>` package is also "
"recommended."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis duit an freastalaí Redis a bhunú, beidh ort ceangail Python a "
"shuiteáil do Redis. :pypi: Is é `redis-py <redis>`an ceangailt a thacaíonn "
"Django go dúchasach. <hiredis>Moltar an pacáiste: pypi: `hiredis-py `a "
"shuiteáil freisin."

msgid "To use Redis as your cache backend with Django:"
msgstr "Chun Redis a úsáid mar do chúltaca taisce le Django:"

msgid ""
"Set :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` to "
"``django.core.cache.backends.redis.RedisCache``."
msgstr ""
"<CACHES-BACKEND>Socraigh: socrú: `BACKEND `go "
"``Django.Core.Cache.Backends.Redis.RedisCache ``."

msgid ""
"Set :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>` to the URL pointing to your Redis "
"instance, using the appropriate scheme. See the ``redis-py`` docs for "
"`details on the available schemes <https://redis-py.readthedocs.io/en/stable/"
"connections.html#redis.connection.ConnectionPool.from_url>`_."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh: socrú: `SUÍOMH <CACHES-LOCATION>`chuig an URL ag díriú ar do "
"shampla Redis, ag baint úsáide as an scéim chuí. < https://redis-"
"py.readthedocs.io/en/stable/"
"connections.html#redis.connection.ConnectionPool.from_url>Féach na doiciméid "
"``redis-py`` le haghaidh `sonraí faoi na scéimeanna atá ar fáil `_."

msgid "For example, if Redis is running on localhost (127.0.0.1) port 6379::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá Redis ag rith ar chalafort localhost (127.0.0.1) 6379:"

msgid ""
"Often Redis servers are protected with authentication. In order to supply a "
"username and password, add them in the ``LOCATION`` along with the URL::"
msgstr ""
"Is minic a chosnaítear freastalaithe Redis le fíordheimhniú. D'fhonn ainm "
"úsáideora agus pasfhocal a sholáthar, cuir iad sa `SUÍOMH`` mar aon leis an "
"URL:"

msgid ""
"If you have multiple Redis servers set up in the replication mode, you can "
"specify the servers either as a semicolon or comma delimited string, or as a "
"list. While using multiple servers, write operations are performed on the "
"first server (leader). Read operations are performed on the other servers "
"(replicas) chosen at random::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá iolracha freastalaithe Redis curtha ar bun agat sa mhodh macasamhail, "
"is féidir leat na freastalaithe a shonrú mar shreang teoranta leath-cholún "
"nó camóg, nó mar liosta. Agus freastalaithe iolracha á úsáid agat, déantar "
"oibríochtaí scríofa ar an gcéad fhreastalaí (ceannaire) Déantar oibríochtaí "
"léite ar na freastalaithe eile (macasamhail) a roghnaítear go randamach:"

msgid "Database caching"
msgstr "Cacháil bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Django can store its cached data in your database. This works best if you've "
"got a fast, well-indexed database server."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le Django a chuid sonraí taiscéadaithe a stóráil i do bhunachar "
"sonraí. Oibríonn sé seo is fearr má tá freastalaí bunachar sonraí tapa, "
"innéacsaithe go maith agat."

msgid "To use a database table as your cache backend:"
msgstr "Chun tábla bunachar sonraí a úsáid mar do chúltaca taisce:"

msgid ""
"Set :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` to "
"``django.core.cache.backends.db.DatabaseCache``"
msgstr ""
"<CACHES-BACKEND>Socraigh: socrú: `BACKEND `go "
"``Django.core.cache.backends.db.databaseCache ``"

msgid ""
"Set :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>` to ``tablename``, the name of the "
"database table. This name can be whatever you want, as long as it's a valid "
"table name that's not already being used in your database."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh: socrú: `LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>`go ``tablename``, ainm an tábla "
"bunachar sonraí. Is féidir leis an ainm seo a bheith cibé rud is mian leat, "
"fad is ainm tábla bailí é nach bhfuil á úsáid cheana féin i do bhunachar "
"sonraí."

msgid "In this example, the cache table's name is ``my_cache_table``::"
msgstr "Sa sampla seo, is é `my_cache_table`` ainm an tábla taisce:"

msgid ""
"Unlike other cache backends, the database cache does not support automatic "
"culling of expired entries at the database level. Instead, expired cache "
"entries are culled each time ``add()``, ``set()``, or ``touch()`` is called."
msgstr ""
"Murab ionann agus cúltaca taisce eile, ní thacaíonn taisce an bhunachar "
"sonraí le cur isteach in éag go huathoibríoch ag leibhéal an bhunachar "
"sonraí. Ina áit sin, déantar iontrálacha taisce in éag a scriosadh gach uair "
"a thugtar ``add () ``, `set ()``, nó ``touch () ``."

msgid "Creating the cache table"
msgstr "An tábla taisce a chruthú"

msgid ""
"Before using the database cache, you must create the cache table with this "
"command:"
msgstr ""
"Sula n-úsáidtear taisce an bunachar sonraí, ní mór duit an tábla taisce a "
"chruthú leis an ordú seo:"

msgid ""
"This creates a table in your database that is in the proper format that "
"Django's database-cache system expects. The name of the table is taken "
"from :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>`."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé seo tábla i do bhunachar sonraí atá san fhormáid cheart a "
"bhfuil súil ag córas taisce bunachar sonraí Django. <CACHES-LOCATION>Tógtar "
"ainm an tábla ó:socrú: `SUÍOMH `."

msgid ""
"If you are using multiple database caches, :djadmin:`createcachetable` "
"creates one table for each cache."
msgstr ""
"Má tá iolracha bunachar sonraí á úsáid agat, cruthaíonn: djadmin: "
"`createcachetable` tábla amháin do gach taisce."

msgid ""
"If you are using multiple databases, :djadmin:`createcachetable` observes "
"the ``allow_migrate()`` method of your database routers (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá bunachar sonraí iolracha á úsáid agat, breathnaíonn: djadmin: "
"`createcachetable` modh `allow_migration () ``ar do ródairí bunachar sonraí "
"(féach thíos)."

msgid ""
"Like :djadmin:`migrate`, :djadmin:`createcachetable` won't touch an existing "
"table. It will only create missing tables."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla: Djadmin: `migrate`, :djadmin: ní dhéanfaidh `createcachetable` "
"teagmháil le tábla atá ann cheana. Ní chruthóidh sé ach táblaí ar iarraidh."

msgid ""
"To print the SQL that would be run, rather than run it, use "
"the :option:`createcachetable --dry-run` option."
msgstr ""
"Chun an SQL a reáchtálfaí a phriontáil, seachas é a reáchtáil, bain úsáid as "
"an roghna:option: `createcachetable --dry-run`."

msgid "Multiple databases"
msgstr "Bunachair sonraí iliom"

msgid ""
"If you use database caching with multiple databases, you'll also need to set "
"up routing instructions for your database cache table. For the purposes of "
"routing, the database cache table appears as a model named ``CacheEntry``, "
"in an application named ``django_cache``. This model won't appear in the "
"models cache, but the model details can be used for routing purposes."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú táscáil bunachar sonraí le bunachair sonraí iolracha, beidh "
"ort treoracha ródaithe a chur ar bun do thábla taisce bunachar sonraí "
"freisin. Chun críocha ródaithe, tá tábla taisce an bhunachar sonraí le "
"feiceáil mar mhúnla darb ainm ``cacheentry`, i bhfeidhmchlár darb ainm "
"``django_cache``. Ní bheidh an tsamhail seo le feiceáil i taisce na "
"samhlacha, ach is féidir sonraí an tsamhail a úsáid chun críocha ródaithe."

msgid ""
"For example, the following router would direct all cache read operations to "
"``cache_replica``, and all write operations to ``cache_primary``. The cache "
"table will only be synchronized onto ``cache_primary``::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, threoródh an ródaire seo a leanas gach oibríocht léite taisce "
"chuig ``cache_replica``, agus scríobhfadh gach oibríocht chuig "
"`cache_primary``. Ní dhéanfar an tábla taisce a shioncronú ach ar "
"`cache_primary``:"

msgid ""
"If you don't specify routing directions for the database cache model, the "
"cache backend will use the ``default`` database."
msgstr ""
"Mura sonraíonn tú treoracha ródaithe don tsamhail taisce bunachar sonraí, "
"úsáidfidh an cúltaca taisce an bunachar sonraí ``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"And if you don't use the database cache backend, you don't need to worry "
"about providing routing instructions for the database cache model."
msgstr ""
"Agus mura n-úsáideann tú cúltaca taisce an bhunachar sonraí, ní gá duit a "
"bheith buartha faoi threoracha ródaithe a sholáthar don tsamhail taisce "
"bunachar sonraí."

msgid "Filesystem caching"
msgstr "Caching chórais comhaid"

msgid ""
"The file-based backend serializes and stores each cache value as a separate "
"file. To use this backend set :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` to "
"``\"django.core.cache.backends.filebased.FileBasedCache\"`` "
"and :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>` to a suitable directory. For "
"example, to store cached data in ``/var/tmp/django_cache``, use this "
"setting::"
msgstr ""
"Déanann an cúltaca comhad-bhunaithe gach luach taisce a shraitheadh agus a "
"stóráil mar chomhad ar leithligh. <CACHES-LOCATION>Chun an tacar cúltaca seo "
"a úsáid: socrú: `BACKEND `go ``<CACHES-"
"BACKEND>\"django.core.cache.backends.fileBasedCache\"`` agus:setting: "
"`LOCATION` chuig eolaire oiriúnach. Mar shampla, chun sonraí taisceáilte a "
"stóráil i ``/var/tmp/django_cache``, bain úsáid as an socrú seo:"

msgid ""
"If you're on Windows, put the drive letter at the beginning of the path, "
"like this::"
msgstr "Má tá tú ar Windows, cuir an litir tiomána ag tús an chosáin, mar seo:"

msgid ""
"The directory path should be absolute -- that is, it should start at the "
"root of your filesystem. It doesn't matter whether you put a slash at the "
"end of the setting."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an cosán eolaire iomlán - is é sin, ba chóir go dtosódh "
"sé ag fréamh do chóras comhaid. Is cuma an gcuireann tú slash ag deireadh an "
"shocraithe."

msgid ""
"Make sure the directory pointed-to by this setting either exists and is "
"readable and writable, or that it can be created by the system user under "
"which your web server runs. Continuing the above example, if your server "
"runs as the user ``apache``, make sure the directory ``/var/tmp/"
"django_cache`` exists and is readable and writable by the user ``apache``, "
"or that it can be created by the user ``apache``."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go bhfuil an eolaire a luaitear ag an socrú seo ann agus go "
"bhfuil sé inléite agus inscríofa, nó gur féidir le húsáideoir an chórais "
"faoina ritheann do fhreastalaí gréasáin é a chruthú. Ag leanúint leis an "
"sampla thuas, má ritheann do fhreastalaí mar an úsáideoir ``apache``, déan "
"cinnte go bhfuil an eolaire ``/var/tmp/django_cache`` ann agus go bhfuil sé "
"inléite agus inscríofa ag an úsáideoir ``apache``, nó gur féidir leis an "
"úsáideoir ``apache`` é a chruthú."

msgid ""
"When the cache :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>` is contained "
"within :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT`, :setting:`STATIC_ROOT`, "
"or :setting:`STATICFILES_FINDERS`, sensitive data may be exposed."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn an cache:setting: `LOCATION `laistigh de: setting:` <CACHES-"
"LOCATION>MEDIA_ROOT`, :setting: `STATIC_ROOT`, nó: setting: "
"`STATICFILES_FINDERS`, féadfar sonraí íogaire a nochtadh."

msgid ""
"An attacker who gains access to the cache file can not only falsify HTML "
"content, which your site will trust, but also remotely execute arbitrary "
"code, as the data is serialized using :mod:`pickle`."
msgstr ""
"Ní amháin gur féidir le hionsaitheoir a fhaigheann rochtain ar an gcomhad "
"taisce ábhar HTML a fhalsú, a mbeidh muinín ag do shuíomh, ach cód treallach "
"a fhorghníomhú go cianda freisin, toisc go ndéantar na sonraí a shraitheadh "
"ag baint úsáide:mod: `pickle`."

msgid ""
"Filesystem caching may become slow when storing a large number of files. If "
"you run into this problem, consider using a different caching mechanism. You "
"can also subclass :source:`FileBasedCache <django/core/cache/backends/"
"filebased.py>` and improve the culling strategy."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cúisceáil chórais chomhad mall nuair a stóráiltear "
"líon mór comhaid. Má théann tú isteach sa fhadhb seo, smaoinigh ar "
"mheicníocht caching difriúil a úsáid. <django/core/cache/backends/"
"filebased.py>Is féidir leat fo-aicme freisin: source: `FileBasedCache` agus "
"an straitéis chailliúcháin a fheabhsú."

msgid "Local-memory caching"
msgstr "Cacháil cuimhne áitiúil"

msgid ""
"This is the default cache if another is not specified in your settings file. "
"If you want the speed advantages of in-memory caching but don't have the "
"capability of running Memcached, consider the local-memory cache backend. "
"This cache is per-process (see below) and thread-safe. To use it, "
"set :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` to "
"``\"django.core.cache.backends.locmem.LocMemCache\"``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an taisce réamhshocraithe mura sonraítear ceann eile i do chomhad "
"socruithe. Más mian leat na buntáistí luais a bhaineann le caching in-"
"chuimhne ach nach bhfuil an cumas agat Memcached a reáchtáil, smaoinigh ar "
"an gcúltaca taisce cuimhne áitiúil. Tá an taisce seo in aghaidh an phróisis "
"(féach thíos) agus sábháilte ó snáithe. <CACHES-BACKEND>Chun é a úsáid, "
"socraí:setting: `BACKEND `go "
"``\"django.core.cache.backends.locmem.locmemcache\"``. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"The cache :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>` is used to identify "
"individual memory stores. If you only have one ``locmem`` cache, you can "
"omit the :setting:`LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>`; however, if you have more "
"than one local memory cache, you will need to assign a name to at least one "
"of them in order to keep them separate."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an cache:setting: `LOCATION <CACHES-LOCATION>`chun siopaí cuimhne "
"aonair a aithint. Mura bhfuil ach taisce ``locmem`` amháin agat, is féidir "
"leat an:setting: `LOCATION `a fhágáil<CACHES-LOCATION>; áfach, má tá níos mó "
"ná taisce cuimhne áitiúil amháin agat, beidh ort ainm a shannadh do cheann "
"acu ar a laghad d'fhonn iad a choinneáil ar leithligh."

msgid "The cache uses a least-recently-used (LRU) culling strategy."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an taisce straitéis díothaithe is lú a úsáidtear le déanaí (LRU)."

msgid ""
"Note that each process will have its own private cache instance, which means "
"no cross-process caching is possible. This also means the local memory cache "
"isn't particularly memory-efficient, so it's probably not a good choice for "
"production environments. It's nice for development."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go mbeidh a shampla taisce príobháideach féin ag gach "
"próiseas, rud a chiallaíonn nach féidir aon chaching trasphróisis a "
"dhéanamh. Ciallaíonn sé seo freisin nach bhfuil an taisce cuimhne áitiúil go "
"háirithe éifeachtach ó chuimhne, mar sin is dócha nach rogha maith é do "
"thimpeallachtaí táirgeachta. Tá sé go deas le haghaidh forbartha."

msgid "Dummy caching (for development)"
msgstr "Caching dummy (le haghaidh forbartha)"

msgid ""
"Finally, Django comes with a \"dummy\" cache that doesn't actually cache -- "
"it just implements the cache interface without doing anything."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, tagann Django le taisce “dummy” nach ndéanann taisce i "
"ndáiríre - ní chuireann sé ach an comhéadan taisce i bhfeidhm gan aon rud a "
"dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"This is useful if you have a production site that uses heavy-duty caching in "
"various places but a development/test environment where you don't want to "
"cache and don't want to have to change your code to special-case the latter. "
"To activate dummy caching, set :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` like so::"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo úsáideach má tá suíomh táirgeachta agat a úsáideann taiscáil "
"tromshaothair in áiteanna éagsúla ach timpeallacht forbarta/tástála nach "
"dteastaíonn uait taisce a dhéanamh agus nach dteastaíonn uait do chód a "
"athrú go speisialta an dara ceann. <CACHES-BACKEND>Chun caching dummy a "
"ghníomhachtú, socraí:setting: `BACKEND `mar sin::"

msgid "Using a custom cache backend"
msgstr "Úsáid cúltaca taisce saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"While Django includes support for a number of cache backends out-of-the-box, "
"sometimes you might want to use a customized cache backend. To use an "
"external cache backend with Django, use the Python import path as "
"the :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` of the :setting:`CACHES` setting, "
"like so::"
msgstr ""
"Cé go gcuimsíonn Django tacaíocht do roinnt cúltaca taisce lasmuigh den "
"bhosca, uaireanta b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat cúltaca taisce saincheaptha a "
"úsáid. Chun cúltaca taisce seachtrach a úsáid le Django, bain úsáid as an "
"gcosán allmhairithe Python mar an:setting: `BACKEND `den socrú: "
"`CACHES<CACHES-BACKEND>`, mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"If you're building your own backend, you can use the standard cache backends "
"as reference implementations. You'll find the code in the :source:`django/"
"core/cache/backends/` directory of the Django source."
msgstr ""
"Má tá do chúlcheann féin á thógáil agat, is féidir leat na cúltaca "
"caighdeánacha taisce a úsáid mar chur i bhfeidhm tagartha. Gheobhaidh tú an "
"cód san eolaire: source: `django/core/cache/backends/` foinse Django."

msgid ""
"Note: Without a really compelling reason, such as a host that doesn't "
"support them, you should stick to the cache backends included with Django. "
"They've been well-tested and are well-documented."
msgstr ""
"Nóta: Gan cúis an-láidir, mar óstach nach dtacaíonn leo, ba chóir duit cloí "
"leis na cúltaca taisce atá san áireamh le Django. Rinneadh tástáil mhaith "
"orthu agus tá siad doiciméadaithe go maith."

msgid "Cache arguments"
msgstr "Argóintí taisce"

msgid ""
"Each cache backend can be given additional arguments to control caching "
"behavior. These arguments are provided as additional keys in "
"the :setting:`CACHES` setting. Valid arguments are as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir argóintí breise a thabhairt do gach cúltaca taisce chun iompar "
"taisce a rialú. Cuirtear na hargóintí seo ar fáil mar eochracha breise sa "
"socrú: socrú: `CACHES`. Is iad seo a leanas argóintí bailí:"

msgid ""
":setting:`TIMEOUT <CACHES-TIMEOUT>`: The default timeout, in seconds, to use "
"for the cache. This argument defaults to ``300`` seconds (5 minutes). You "
"can set ``TIMEOUT`` to ``None`` so that, by default, cache keys never "
"expire. A value of ``0`` causes keys to immediately expire (effectively "
"\"don't cache\")."
msgstr ""
":setting: `TIMEOUT <CACHES-TIMEOUT>`: An t-am réamhshocraithe, i soicindí, "
"le húsáid don taisce. Réamhshocraíonn an argóint seo go ``300`` soicind (5 "
"nóiméad). Is féidir leat ``TIMEOUT`` a shocrú go ``None`` ionas nach "
"rachaidh eochracha taisce in éag, de réir réamhshocraithe. Mar gheall ar "
"luach ``0`` is cúis le heochracha dul in éag láithreach (“ná taisceáil” go "
"héifeachtach)."

msgid ""
":setting:`OPTIONS <CACHES-OPTIONS>`: Any options that should be passed to "
"the cache backend. The list of valid options will vary with each backend, "
"and cache backends backed by a third-party library will pass their options "
"directly to the underlying cache library."
msgstr ""
":setting: `OPTIONS <CACHES-OPTIONS>`: Aon roghanna ba chóir a chur ar "
"aghaidh chuig an gcúltaca taisce. Athróidh liosta na roghanna bailí le gach "
"cúltaca, agus rachaidh cúltaca taisce le tacaíocht ó leabharlann tríú páirtí "
"a gcuid roghanna go díreach chuig an leabharlann taisce bunúsach."

msgid ""
"Cache backends that implement their own culling strategy (i.e., the "
"``locmem``, ``filesystem`` and ``database`` backends) will honor the "
"following options:"
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh cúltaca taisce a chuireann a straitéis díothaithe féin i bhfeidhm "
"(ie, na cúltaca ``locmem``, ``córas comhad ``agus ``bunachar sonraí``) onóir "
"na roghanna seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"``MAX_ENTRIES``: The maximum number of entries allowed in the cache before "
"old values are deleted. This argument defaults to ``300``."
msgstr ""
"``MAX_ENTRIES``: An líon uasta na n-iontrálacha a cheadaítear sa taisce sula "
"scriostar seanluachanna. Tá an argóint seo réamhshocraithe go ``300``."

msgid ""
"``CULL_FREQUENCY``: The fraction of entries that are culled when "
"``MAX_ENTRIES`` is reached. The actual ratio is ``1 / CULL_FREQUENCY``, so "
"set ``CULL_FREQUENCY`` to ``2`` to cull half the entries when "
"``MAX_ENTRIES`` is reached. This argument should be an integer and defaults "
"to ``3``."
msgstr ""
"``CULL_FREQUENCY``: An codán na n-iontrálacha a dhíothaítear nuair a "
"shroichtear ``MAX_ENTRIES``. Is é an cóimheas iarbhír ná ``1/"
"CULL_FREQUENCY``, mar sin socraigh ``CULL_FREQUENCY`` go ``2`` chun leath na "
"n-iontrálacha a scriosadh nuair a shroichtear ``MAX_ENTRIES ``. Ba chóir go "
"mbeadh an argóint seo ina shláimhir agus réamhshocraithe go ``3``."

msgid ""
"A value of ``0`` for ``CULL_FREQUENCY`` means that the entire cache will be "
"dumped when ``MAX_ENTRIES`` is reached. On some backends (``database`` in "
"particular) this makes culling *much* faster at the expense of more cache "
"misses."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn luach ``0`` do `CULL_FREQUENCY`` go ndéanfar an taisce iomlán a "
"dumpáil nuair a shroichfear ``MAX_ENTRIES``. Ar roinnt cúltaca (``bunachar "
"sonraí ``go háirithe) déanann sé seo go gcaithfeach* i bhfad níos gasta ar "
"chostas níos mó caitheamh taisce."

msgid ""
"The Memcached and Redis backends pass the contents of :setting:`OPTIONS "
"<CACHES-OPTIONS>` as keyword arguments to the client constructors, allowing "
"for more advanced control of client behavior. For example usage, see below."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann cúltaca Memcached agus Redis ábhar: socrú: `OPTIONS <CACHES-"
"OPTIONS>`mar argóintí eochairfhocal chuig tógálaí na gcliant, rud a "
"cheadaíonn rialú níos airde ar iompar cliant. Mar shampla úsáid, féach thíos."

msgid ""
":setting:`KEY_PREFIX <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>`: A string that will be "
"automatically included (prepended by default) to all cache keys used by the "
"Django server."
msgstr ""
":setting: `KEY_PREFIX <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>`: Sreang a chuirfear san áireamh "
"go huathoibríoch (réamhshocraithe de réir réamhshocraithe) go léir eochracha "
"taisce a úsáideann an freastalaí Django."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`cache documentation <cache_key_prefixing>` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:ref: `cáipéisíocht taiscéala <cache_key_prefixing>`le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
":setting:`VERSION <CACHES-VERSION>`: The default version number for cache "
"keys generated by the Django server."
msgstr ""
":setting: `VERSION <CACHES-VERSION>`: An uimhir leagan réamhshocraithe "
"d'eochracha taisce a ghineann an freastalaí Django."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`cache documentation <cache_versioning>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:ref: `cáipéisíocht taiscéala <cache_versioning>`le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
":setting:`KEY_FUNCTION <CACHES-KEY_FUNCTION>` A string containing a dotted "
"path to a function that defines how to compose a prefix, version and key "
"into a final cache key."
msgstr ""
":setting: `KEY_FUNCTION <CACHES-KEY_FUNCTION>`Sreang ina bhfuil cosán "
"poncach chuig feidhm a shainmhíníonn conas réimír, leagan agus eochair a "
"chumadh isteach i eochair taisce deiridh."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`cache documentation <cache_key_transformation>` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:ref: `cáipéisíocht taiscéala <cache_key_transformation>`le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"In this example, a filesystem backend is being configured with a timeout of "
"60 seconds, and a maximum capacity of 1000 items::"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, tá cúltaca córas comhaid á chumrú le haon ama 60 soicind, "
"agus cumas uasta 1000 mír:"

msgid ""
"Here's an example configuration for a ``pylibmc`` based backend that enables "
"the binary protocol, SASL authentication, and the ``ketama`` behavior mode::"
msgstr ""
"Seo cumraíocht shampla le haghaidh cúltaca bunaithe ar `pylibmc` a "
"chumasaíonn an prótacal dénártha, fíordheimhniú SASL, agus an modh "
"iompraíochta `ketama`:"

msgid ""
"Here's an example configuration for a ``pymemcache`` based backend that "
"enables client pooling (which may improve performance by keeping clients "
"connected), treats memcache/network errors as cache misses, and sets the "
"``TCP_NODELAY`` flag on the connection's socket::"
msgstr ""
"Seo cumraíocht shamplach le haghaidh cúltaca bunaithe ar `pymemcache` a "
"chuireann ar chumas comhdhlúthú cliant (a d'fhéadfadh feidhmíocht a fheabhsú "
"trí chliaint a choinneáil ceangailte), déileálann sé le hearráidí memcache/"
"líonra mar chailleann taisce, agus socraíonn an bratach ``TCP_NODELAY`` ar "
"soicéad an nasc:"

msgid ""
"Here's an example configuration for a ``redis`` based backend that selects "
"database ``10`` (by default Redis ships with 16 logical databases), and sets "
"a custom `connection pool class`_ (``redis.ConnectionPool`` is used by "
"default)::"
msgstr ""
"Seo cumraíocht shampla le haghaidh cúltaca bunaithe ar ``redis`` a "
"roghnaíonn bunachar sonraí ```10`` (de réir réamhshocraithe loingíonn Redis "
"le 16 bhunachar sonraí loighciúla), agus a leagann saincheaptha `rang linn "
"nasc`_ (``Redis.connectionPool`` úsáidtear de réir réamhshocraithe):"

msgid "The per-site cache"
msgstr "An taisce in aghaidh an láithreáin"

msgid ""
"Once the cache is set up, the simplest way to use caching is to cache your "
"entire site. You'll need to add "
"``'django.middleware.cache.UpdateCacheMiddleware'`` and "
"``'django.middleware.cache.FetchFromCacheMiddleware'`` to "
"your :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting, as in this example::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh an taisce curtha ar bun, is é an bealach is simplí chun "
"caching a úsáid ná do shuíomh iomlán a thaisceadh. Beidh ort "
"``django.middleware.cache.UpdateCacheMiddleware'` agus "
"``django.middleware.cache.fetchfromCacheMiddleware'` a chur le do shuíomh: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`, mar atá sa sampla seo::"

msgid ""
"No, that's not a typo: the \"update\" middleware must be first in the list, "
"and the \"fetch\" middleware must be last. The details are a bit obscure, "
"but see `Order of MIDDLEWARE`_ below if you'd like the full story."
msgstr ""
"Níl, ní clóscríobh é sin: caithfidh an middleware “nuashonrú” a bheith ar "
"dtús ar an liosta, agus caithfidh an middleware “faigh” a bheith deireanach. "
"Tá na sonraí beagán doiléir, ach féach `Ordú MIDDLEWARE`_ thíos más mian "
"leat an scéal iomlán."

msgid "Then, add the following required settings to your Django settings file:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cuir na socruithe riachtanacha seo a leanas le do chomhad socruithe "
"Django:"

msgid ""
":setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ALIAS` -- The cache alias to use for storage."
msgstr ""
":setting: `CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ALIAS` - An alias taisce le húsáid le haghaidh "
"stórála."

msgid ""
":setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS` -- The integer number of seconds each "
"page should be cached."
msgstr ""
":setting: `CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS` -- Ba chóir líon iomláir na soicind "
"gach leathanach a chosc."

msgid ""
":setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_KEY_PREFIX` -- If the cache is shared across "
"multiple sites using the same Django installation, set this to the name of "
"the site, or some other string that is unique to this Django instance, to "
"prevent key collisions. Use an empty string if you don't care."
msgstr ""
":setting: `CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_KEY_PREFIX` -- Má roinntear an taisce ar fud "
"suíomhanna iolracha ag baint úsáide as an suiteáil Django céanna, socraigh é "
"seo ar ainm an láithreáin, nó teaghrán éigin eile atá uathúil don sampla "
"Django seo, chun imbhuailtí eochair a chosc. Úsáid teaghrán folamh mura "
"bhfuil cúram ort."

msgid ""
"``FetchFromCacheMiddleware`` caches GET and HEAD responses with status 200, "
"where the request and response headers allow. Responses to requests for the "
"same URL with different query parameters are considered to be unique pages "
"and are cached separately. This middleware expects that a HEAD request is "
"answered with the same response headers as the corresponding GET request; in "
"which case it can return a cached GET response for HEAD request."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``Fetchfromcachemiddleware`` freagraí GET agus HEAD le stádas 200, "
"nuair a cheadaíonn na ceannteidil iarratais agus freagartha. Meastar gur "
"leathanaigh uathúla iad freagraí ar iarratais ar an URL céanna le "
"paraiméadair cheisteanna éagsúla agus cuirtear iad a chosc ar leithligh Tá "
"an middleware seo ag súil go bhfreagraítear iarratas HEAD leis na "
"ceannteidil freagartha céanna leis an iarratas GET comhfhreagrach; sa chás "
"sin féadfaidh sé freagra GET a chosaithe ar iarratas HEAD a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"Additionally, ``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` automatically sets a few headers in "
"each :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` which affect :ref:`downstream caches "
"<downstream-caches>`:"
msgstr ""
"<downstream-caches>Ina theannta sin, socraíonn ``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` "
"cúpla ceannteideal go huathoibríoch i ngach:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponse` a théann i bhfeidh:ref: `caches downstream `:"

msgid ""
"Sets the ``Expires`` header to the current date/time plus the "
"defined :setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS`."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an ceannteideal ``Expires`` go dtí an dáta/am reatha móide an "
"sainmhínithe:setting: `CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS`."

msgid ""
"Sets the ``Cache-Control`` header to give a max age for the page -- again, "
"from the :setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn sé an ceanntásc ``Cache-Control`` chun aoise uasta a thabhairt don "
"leathanach -- arís, ón socrú:setting: `CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS`."

msgid "See :doc:`/topics/http/middleware` for more on middleware."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `/topics/http/middleware` le haghaidh tuilleadh ar middleware."

msgid ""
"If a view sets its own cache expiry time (i.e. it has a ``max-age`` section "
"in its ``Cache-Control`` header) then the page will be cached until the "
"expiry time, rather than :setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS`. Using the "
"decorators in ``django.views.decorators.cache`` you can easily set a view's "
"expiry time (using the :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control` "
"decorator) or disable caching for a view (using "
"the :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.never_cache` decorator). See the "
"`using other headers`__ section for more on these decorators."
msgstr ""
"Má shocraíonn amharc a chuid ama éaga taisce féin (ie tá rannán ``max-aos`` "
"aige ina cheanntásc ``Cache-Control``) ansin déanfar an leathanach a stóráil "
"go dtí an t-am éaga, seach:setting: `CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS`. Ag baint "
"úsáide as na maisitheoirí i `django.views.decorators.cache`` is féidir leat "
"am éaga amharc a shocrú go héasca (ag baint úsáide as:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control` decorator) nó díchumasú a "
"chaching le haghaidh amharc (ag baint úsáide as an: func: "
"`~django.decorators.cache.neverator _cache`). Féach an chuid `ceannteidil "
"eile a úsáid `__ le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais faoi na maisitheoirí seo."

msgid ""
"If :setting:`USE_I18N` is set to ``True`` then the generated cache key will "
"include the name of the active :term:`language<language code>` -- see "
"also :ref:`how-django-discovers-language-preference`). This allows you to "
"easily cache multilingual sites without having to create the cache key "
"yourself."
msgstr ""
"<language code>Más rud é: Socrú: `USE_I18N` socraithe go ``True`` ansin "
"beidh ainm an ghníomhaí:term: `language `san eochair taisce a ghintear san "
"eochair taisce ginte -- féach freis:ref: `how django-discovers-language-"
"preference`). Ligeann sé seo duit suíomhanna ilteangacha a thaisceadh go "
"héasca gan an eochair taisce a chruthú tú féin."

msgid ""
"Cache keys also include the :ref:`current time zone <default-current-time-"
"zone>` when :setting:`USE_TZ` is set to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn eochracha taisce an: ref: `crios ama reatha `nuai:setting: `USE "
"<default-current-time-zone>_TZ` socraithe go ``True``."

msgid "The per-view cache"
msgstr "An taisce in aghaidh an amharc"

msgid ""
"A more granular way to use the caching framework is by caching the output of "
"individual views. ``django.views.decorators.cache`` defines a ``cache_page`` "
"decorator that will automatically cache the view's response for you::"
msgstr ""
"Bealach níos gráinneach chun an creat taiscéála a úsáid ná aschur tuairimí "
"aonair a chaitheamh. Sainmhíníonn ``django.views.decorators.cache`` "
"maisitheoir ``cache_page`` a thaisceoidh freagra an amharc duit go "
"huathoibríoch:"

msgid ""
"``cache_page`` takes a single argument: the cache timeout, in seconds. In "
"the above example, the result of the ``my_view()`` view will be cached for "
"15 minutes. (Note that we've written it as ``60 * 15`` for the purpose of "
"readability. ``60 * 15`` will be evaluated to ``900`` -- that is, 15 minutes "
"multiplied by 60 seconds per minute.)"
msgstr ""
"Tógann ``cache_page`` argóint amháin: an t-am taisce, i soicindí. Sa sampla "
"thuas, déanfar toradh an radharc ``my_view () `a stóráil ar feadh 15 "
"nóiméad. (Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil sé scríofa againn mar `60* 15`` chun "
"críche inléiteachta. Meastófar ``60* 15`` go `900`` - is é sin, 15 nóiméad "
"iolraithe le 60 soicind in aghaidh an nóiméid.)"

msgid ""
"The cache timeout set by ``cache_page`` takes precedence over the ``max-"
"age`` directive from the ``Cache-Control`` header."
msgstr ""
"Tá tosaíocht ag an am taisce atá leagtha síos ag `cache_page`` thar an "
"treoir ``max-aois ``ón gceannteideal ``Cache-Control``."

msgid ""
"The per-view cache, like the per-site cache, is keyed off of the URL. If "
"multiple URLs point at the same view, each URL will be cached separately. "
"Continuing the ``my_view`` example, if your URLconf looks like this::"
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an taisce in aghaidh an amharc, cosúil leis an taisce in aghaidh an "
"láithreáin, as an URL. Má thaispeánann URLanna iolracha ar an radharc "
"céanna, déanfar gach URL a stóráil ar leithligh. Ag leanúint leis an sampla "
"``my_view``, má tá cuma seo ar do URLConf:"

msgid ""
"then requests to ``/foo/1/`` and ``/foo/23/`` will be cached separately, as "
"you may expect. But once a particular URL (e.g., ``/foo/23/``) has been "
"requested, subsequent requests to that URL will use the cache."
msgstr ""
"ansin cuirfear iarratais ar ``/foo/1/`` agus ``/foo/23/`` a chosc ar "
"leithligh, mar a d'fhéadfá a bheith ag súil leis. Ach nuair a iarrtar URL "
"áirithe (m.sh., ``/foo/23/``), úsáidfidh iarratais ina dhiaidh sin chuig an "
"URL sin an taisce."

msgid ""
"``cache_page`` can also take an optional keyword argument, ``cache``, which "
"directs the decorator to use a specific cache (from your :setting:`CACHES` "
"setting) when caching view results. By default, the ``default`` cache will "
"be used, but you can specify any cache you want::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le ``cache_page`` argóint eochairfhocal roghnach a ghlacadh "
"freisin, `cache``, a threoraíonn don mhaisitheoir taisce ar leith a úsáid (ó "
"do shuíomh: `SETING: `CACHES`) agus torthaí amharc á chaitheamh agat. De "
"réir réamhshocraithe, úsáidfear an taisce ``default``, ach is féidir leat "
"aon taisce a theastaíonn uait a shonrú:"

msgid ""
"You can also override the cache prefix on a per-view basis. ``cache_page`` "
"takes an optional keyword argument, ``key_prefix``, which works in the same "
"way as the :setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_KEY_PREFIX` setting for the "
"middleware.  It can be used like this::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an réimír taisce a shárú freisin ar bhonn aghaidh amharc. "
"Glacann ``cache_page`` argóint eochairfhocal roghnach, ``key_prefix``, a "
"oibríonn ar an mbealach céanna leis an:setting: "
"`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_KEY_PREFIX` socrú don middleware. Is féidir é a úsáid mar "
"seo::"

msgid ""
"The ``key_prefix`` and ``cache`` arguments may be specified together. The "
"``key_prefix`` argument and the :setting:`KEY_PREFIX <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>` "
"specified under :setting:`CACHES` will be concatenated."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na hargóintí ``key_prefix`` agus ``cache`` a shonrú le chéile. "
"<CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>Déanfar an argóint ``key_prefix`` agus an:setting: "
"`KEY_PREFIX` a shonraítear fao:setting: `CACHES` a chomhcheangal."

msgid ""
"Additionally, ``cache_page`` automatically sets ``Cache-Control`` and "
"``Expires`` headers in the response which affect :ref:`downstream caches "
"<downstream-caches>`."
msgstr ""
"<downstream-caches>Ina theannta sin, socraíonn ``cache_page`` ceannteidil "
"``Cache-Control`` agus ``Expires`` go huathoibríoch sa fhreagra a théann i "
"bhfeidh:ref: `caches downstream `."

msgid "Specifying per-view cache in the URLconf"
msgstr "Taisce in aghaidh an amharc a shonrú sa URLConf"

msgid ""
"The examples in the previous section have hard-coded the fact that the view "
"is cached, because ``cache_page`` alters the ``my_view`` function in place. "
"This approach couples your view to the cache system, which is not ideal for "
"several reasons. For instance, you might want to reuse the view functions on "
"another, cache-less site, or you might want to distribute the views to "
"people who might want to use them without being cached. The solution to "
"these problems is to specify the per-view cache in the URLconf rather than "
"next to the view functions themselves."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé crua-chódaithe ag na samplaí sa chuid roimhe seo go bhfuil an dearcadh "
"a stóráil, toisc go n-athraíonn ``cache_page`` an fheidhm ``my_view`` atá i "
"bhfeidhm. Déanann an cur chuige seo do thuairim leis an gcóras taisce, nach "
"bhfuil oiriúnach ar chúiseanna éagsúla. Mar shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith "
"leat na feidhmeanna amharc a athúsáid ar shuíomh eile gan taisce, nó "
"b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat na tuairimí a dháileadh ar dhaoine a d'fhéadfadh a "
"bheith ag iarraidh iad a úsáid gan iad a chosc. Is é an réiteach ar na "
"fadhbanna seo ná an taisce in aghaidh an amharc a shonrú sa URLConf seachas "
"in aice leis na feidhmeanna amharc féin."

msgid ""
"You can do so by wrapping the view function with ``cache_page`` when you "
"refer to it in the URLconf. Here's the old URLconf from earlier::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat é sin a dhéanamh tríd an bhfeidhm amharc a fhilleadh le "
"`cache_page`` nuair a thagann tú tagairt dó sa URLConf. Seo an sean-URLConf "
"ó níos luaithe::"

msgid "Here's the same thing, with ``my_view`` wrapped in ``cache_page``::"
msgstr "Seo an rud céanna, le ``my_view`` fillte i ``cache_page``:"

msgid "Template fragment caching"
msgstr "Caching bhrúin teimpléad"

msgid ""
"If you're after even more control, you can also cache template fragments "
"using the ``cache`` template tag. To give your template access to this tag, "
"put ``{% load cache %}`` near the top of your template."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú tar éis níos mó smachta fós, is féidir leat blúirí teimpléad a "
"thaiscáil ag baint úsáide as an gclib teimpléad ``cache`. Chun rochtain a "
"thabhairt do do theimpléad ar an gclib seo, cuir ``{% load cache%}`` in aice "
"le barr do theimpléad."

msgid ""
"The ``{% cache %}`` template tag caches the contents of the block for a "
"given amount of time. It takes at least two arguments: the cache timeout, in "
"seconds, and the name to give the cache fragment. The fragment is cached "
"forever if timeout is ``None``. The name will be taken as is, do not use a "
"variable. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an chlib teimpléid ``{% cache%}`` ábhar an bhloc a chosc ar feadh "
"méid áirithe ama. Tógann sé dhá argóint ar a laghad: an t-am taisce, i "
"soicindí, agus an t-ainm chun an blúire taisce a thabhairt. Déantar an "
"blúire a stóráil go deo má tá an t-am amach ``None ``. Glacfar an t-ainm mar "
"atá, ná húsáid athróg. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Sometimes you might want to cache multiple copies of a fragment depending on "
"some dynamic data that appears inside the fragment. For example, you might "
"want a separate cached copy of the sidebar used in the previous example for "
"every user of your site. Do this by passing one or more additional "
"arguments, which may be variables with or without filters, to the ``{% cache "
"%}`` template tag to uniquely identify the cache fragment:"
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat cóipeanna iolracha de bhrúin a "
"thaisceadh ag brath ar roinnt sonraí dinimiciúla atá le feiceáil taobh Mar "
"shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat cóip taiscéadaithe ar leithligh den taobh "
"barra a úsáideadh sa sampla roimhe seo do gach úsáideoir de do shuíomh. Déan "
"é seo trí argóint bhreise amháin nó níos mó, a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ina "
"athróga le scagairí nó gan scagairí, a chur chuig an gclib teimpléid ``{% "
"cache%} `chun an blúir taisce a aithint go uathúil:"

msgid ""
"If :setting:`USE_I18N` is set to ``True`` the per-site middleware cache "
"will :ref:`respect the active language<i18n-cache-key>`. For the ``cache`` "
"template tag you could use one of the :ref:`translation-specific "
"variables<template-translation-vars>` available in templates to achieve the "
"same result:"
msgstr ""
"<i18n-cache-key>Má tá: SETTING: `USE_I18N` socraithe go ``True``, beidh "
"taisce meán-earraí in aghaidh an láithreáin: ref: `meas a thabhairt don "
"teanga ghníomhach`. <template-translation-vars>Maidir leis an gclib "
"teimpléad ``cache`` d'fhéadfá ceann de na hathróga:ref: `aistriúcháin-"
"shonracha `atá ar fáil i dteimpléid a úsáid chun an toradh céanna a bhaint "
"amach:"

msgid ""
"The cache timeout can be a template variable, as long as the template "
"variable resolves to an integer value. For example, if the template variable "
"``my_timeout`` is set to the value ``600``, then the following two examples "
"are equivalent:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an t-am taisce a bheith ina athróg teimpléad, chomh fada agus "
"a réitíonn an t-athróg teimpléad ar luach slámhshláir. Mar shampla, má tá an "
"t-athróg teimpléad ``my_timeout`` socraithe go luach ``600``, ansin tá an dá "
"shampla seo a leanas coibhéiseach:"

msgid ""
"This feature is useful in avoiding repetition in templates. You can set the "
"timeout in a variable, in one place, and reuse that value."
msgstr ""
"Tá an ghné seo úsáideach chun athdhéanamh i dteimpléid a sheachaint. Is "
"féidir leat an t-am a shocrú in athróg, in aon áit amháin, agus an luach sin "
"a athúsáid."

msgid ""
"By default, the cache tag will try to use the cache called "
"\"template_fragments\". If no such cache exists, it will fall back to using "
"the default cache. You may select an alternate cache backend to use with the "
"``using`` keyword argument, which must be the last argument to the tag."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, déanfaidh an clib taisce iarracht an taisce ar a "
"dtugtar “template_fragments” a úsáid. Mura bhfuil taisce den sórt sin ann, "
"tiocfaidh sé ar ais chun an taisce réamhshocraithe a úsáid. Féadfaidh tú "
"cúltaca taisce malartach a roghnú le húsáid leis an argóint eochairfhocal "
"``úsáid ``, nach mór gurb é an argóint deireanach don chlib."

msgid ""
"It is considered an error to specify a cache name that is not configured."
msgstr "Meastar gur earráid é ainm taisce nach bhfuil cumraithe a shonrú."

msgid ""
"If you want to obtain the cache key used for a cached fragment, you can use "
"``make_template_fragment_key``. ``fragment_name`` is the same as second "
"argument to the ``cache`` template tag; ``vary_on`` is a list of all "
"additional arguments passed to the tag. This function can be useful for "
"invalidating or overwriting a cached item, for example:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an eochair taisce a úsáidtear le haghaidh blúire taisceáilte a "
"fháil, is féidir leat ``make_template_fragment_key`` a úsáid. Tá "
"``fragment_name`` mar an gcéanna leis an dara argóint leis an gclib "
"teimpléad ``cache``; `vary_on`` liosta de na hargóintí breise go léir a "
"chuirtear chuig an gclib. Is féidir leis an bhfeidhm seo a bheith úsáideach "
"chun mír taisceáilte a neamhbhailí nó a fhorscríobh, mar shampla:"

msgid "The low-level cache API"
msgstr "An API taisce leibhéal íseal"

msgid ""
"Sometimes, caching an entire rendered page doesn't gain you very much and "
"is, in fact, inconvenient overkill."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta, ní ghnóthaíonn sé go mór duit a chaitheamh ar leathanach iomlán "
"rindreáilte agus bíonn sé, i ndáiríre, ró-dhochaoithiúil."

msgid ""
"Perhaps, for instance, your site includes a view whose results depend on "
"several expensive queries, the results of which change at different "
"intervals. In this case, it would not be ideal to use the full-page caching "
"that the per-site or per-view cache strategies offer, because you wouldn't "
"want to cache the entire result (since some of the data changes often), but "
"you'd still want to cache the results that rarely change."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir, mar shampla, tá radharc ar do shuíomh ag brath a thorthaí ar "
"roinnt ceisteanna daor, a n-athraíonn a dtorthaí ag eatraimh éagsúla. Sa "
"chás seo, ní bheadh sé oiriúnach an taisce leathanaigh lán-leathanaigh a "
"thairgeann na straitéisí taisce in aghaidh an láithreáin nó in aghaidh an "
"amharc a úsáid, toisc nach mbeadh tú ag iarraidh an toradh iomlán a "
"thaisceadh (ós rud é go n-athraíonn cuid de na sonraí go minic), ach ba "
"mhaith leat fós na torthaí a athraíonn."

msgid ""
"For cases like this, Django exposes a low-level cache API. You can use this "
"API to store objects in the cache with any level of granularity you like.  "
"You can cache any Python object that can be pickled safely: strings, "
"dictionaries, lists of model objects, and so forth. (Most common Python "
"objects can be pickled; refer to the Python documentation for more "
"information about pickling.)"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le cásanna mar seo, nochtann Django API taisce leibhéal íseal. Is "
"féidir leat an API seo a úsáid chun rudaí a stóráil sa taisce le haon "
"leibhéal gráinneachta is mian leat. Is féidir leat aon rud Python is féidir "
"a phiocadh go sábháilte a thaisceadh: teaghráin, foclóirí, liostaí rudaí "
"samhail, agus mar sin de. (Is féidir na rudaí Python is coitianta a "
"phiocáil; féach do dhoiciméadú Python le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoi "
"phiocáil.)"

msgid "Accessing the cache"
msgstr "Rochtain a fháil ar an taisce"

msgid ""
"You can access the caches configured in the :setting:`CACHES` setting "
"through a dict-like object: ``django.core.cache.caches``. Repeated requests "
"for the same alias in the same thread will return the same object."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar na táscáin atá cumraithe sa socrú:: "
"`CACHES` trí réad cosúil le dict: ``django.core.cache.caches``. Tabharfaidh "
"iarratais arís agus arís eile ar an alias céanna sa snáithe céanna ar ais an "
"réad céanna."

msgid ""
"If the named key does not exist, ``InvalidCacheBackendError`` will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an eochair ainmnithe ann, ardófar ``InvalidCacheBackendError``."

msgid ""
"To provide thread-safety, a different instance of the cache backend will be "
"returned for each thread."
msgstr ""
"Chun sábháilteacht snáithe a sholáthar, cuirfear sampla difriúil den "
"chúltaca taisce ar ais do gach snáithe."

msgid ""
"As a shortcut, the default cache is available as ``django.core.cache.cache``:"
msgstr ""
"Mar aicearra, tá an taisce réamhshocraithe ar fáil mar "
"``django.core.cache.cache``:"

msgid "This object is equivalent to ``caches['default']``."
msgstr "Tá an réad seo comhionann le ``caches ['réamhshocraithe'] ``."

msgid "Basic usage"
msgstr "Úsáid bunúsach"

msgid "The basic interface is:"
msgstr "Is é an comhéadan bunúsach:"

msgid ""
"``key`` should be a ``str``, and ``value`` can be any picklable Python "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh ``eochair`` ina `str``, agus is féidir ``luach`` a bheith "
"ina aon rud Python inpictilte."

msgid ""
"The ``timeout`` argument is optional and defaults to the ``timeout`` "
"argument of the appropriate backend in the :setting:`CACHES` setting "
"(explained above). It's the number of seconds the value should be stored in "
"the cache. Passing in ``None`` for ``timeout`` will cache the value forever. "
"A ``timeout`` of ``0`` won't cache the value."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint ``timeout`` roghnach agus réamhshocraíonn sé ar an argóint "
"``timeout`` den chúltaca cuí sa socrúit:setting: `CACHES` (mínithe thuas). "
"Is é líon na soicind ba chóir an luach a stóráil sa taisce. Ag dul isteach "
"``None`` le haghaidh ``timeout``, beidh an luach a thaisceadh go deo. Ní "
"dhéanfaidh ``timeout`` de ``0`` a thaisceadh an luach."

msgid ""
"If the object doesn't exist in the cache, ``cache.get()`` returns ``None``:"
msgstr "Mura bhfuil an réad ann sa taisce, filleann ``cache.get () ````None``:"

msgid ""
"If you need to determine whether the object exists in the cache and you have "
"stored a literal value ``None``, use a sentinel object as the default:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit a chinneadh an bhfuil an réad sa taisce agus go bhfuil luach "
"litriúil “None” stóráilte agat, bain úsáid as réad sentinel mar "
"réamhshocraithe:"

msgid ""
"``cache.get()`` can take a ``default`` argument. This specifies which value "
"to return if the object doesn't exist in the cache:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le ``cache.get () ``argóint ``default`` a ghlacadh. Sonraíonn sé "
"seo cén luach atá le filleadh mura bhfuil an réad ann sa taisce:"

msgid ""
"To add a key only if it doesn't already exist, use the ``add()`` method. It "
"takes the same parameters as ``set()``, but it will not attempt to update "
"the cache if the key specified is already present:"
msgstr ""
"Chun eochair a chur leis ach amháin mura bhfuil sé ann cheana féin, bain "
"úsáid as an modh ``add () ``. Tógann sé na paraiméadair chéanna le ``set () "
"``, ach ní dhéanfaidh sé iarracht an taisce a nuashonrú má tá an eochair a "
"shonraítear i láthair cheana féin:"

msgid ""
"If you need to know whether ``add()`` stored a value in the cache, you can "
"check the return value. It will return ``True`` if the value was stored, "
"``False`` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit fios a bheith agat an stóráil ``add () ``luach sa taisce, is "
"féidir leat an luach tuairisceáin a sheiceáil. Tabharfaidh sé ar ais "
"``True`` má stóráilíodh an luach, ``False`` ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"If you want to get a key's value or set a value if the key isn't in the "
"cache, there is the ``get_or_set()`` method. It takes the same parameters as "
"``get()`` but the default is set as the new cache value for that key, rather "
"than returned:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat luach eochair a fháil nó luach a shocrú mura bhfuil an eochair "
"sa taisce, tá an modh ``get_or_set () `ann. Tógann sé na paraiméadair "
"chéanna le ``get () ``ach socraítear an réamhshocrú mar an luach taisce nua "
"don eochair sin, seachas a thabhairt ar ais:"

msgid "You can also pass any callable as a *default* value:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat aon ghlaoch a chur ar aghaidh mar luach*réamhshocraithe*:"

msgid ""
"There's also a ``get_many()`` interface that only hits the cache once. "
"``get_many()`` returns a dictionary with all the keys you asked for that "
"actually exist in the cache (and haven't expired):"
msgstr ""
"Tá comhéadan ``get_many () ``ann freisin nach mbuaileann an taisce ach uair "
"amháin. Tugann ``get_many () ``foclóir ar ais leis na heochracha go léir a "
"d'iarr tú orthu atá ann i ndáiríre sa taisce (agus níor éag):"

msgid ""
"To set multiple values more efficiently, use ``set_many()`` to pass a "
"dictionary of key-value pairs:"
msgstr ""
"Chun luachanna iolracha a shocrú níos éifeachtaí, bain úsáid as ``set_many "
"() ``chun foclóir péirí eochairluacha a rith:"

msgid ""
"Like ``cache.set()``, ``set_many()`` takes an optional ``timeout`` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le ``cache.set () ``, glacann ``set_many ()`` paraiméadar roghnach "
"``timeout``."

msgid ""
"On supported backends (memcached), ``set_many()`` returns a list of keys "
"that failed to be inserted."
msgstr ""
"Ar chúltaca tacaithe (memcached), filleann ``set_many () ``liosta eochracha "
"ar theip orthu a chur isteach."

msgid ""
"You can delete keys explicitly with ``delete()`` to clear the cache for a "
"particular object:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat eochracha a scriosadh go sainráite le ``delete () ``chun an "
"taisce do réad áirithe a ghlanadh:"

msgid ""
"``delete()`` returns ``True`` if the key was successfully deleted, ``False`` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``delete () ``filleadh ``True`` má scriosadh an eochair go rathúil, "
"``False`` ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"If you want to clear a bunch of keys at once, ``delete_many()`` can take a "
"list of keys to be cleared:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat dornán eochracha a ghlanadh ag an am céanna, is féidir le "
"``delete_many () ``liosta eochracha atá le glanadh a ghlanadh:"

msgid ""
"Finally, if you want to delete all the keys in the cache, use "
"``cache.clear()``.  Be careful with this; ``clear()`` will remove "
"*everything* from the cache, not just the keys set by your application:"
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, más mian leat na heochracha go léir sa taisce a scriosadh, "
"bain úsáid as ``cache.clear () ``. Bí cúramach leis seo; bainfidh ``clear () "
"``*gach ruda* ón taisce, ní hamháin na heochracha atá leagtha síos ag "
"d'iarratas:"

msgid ""
"``cache.touch()`` sets a new expiration for a key. For example, to update a "
"key to expire 10 seconds from now:"
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn ``cache.touch () ``éag nua le haghaidh eochair. Mar shampla, chun "
"eochair a nuashonrú chun dul in éag 10 soicind as seo:"

msgid ""
"Like other methods, the ``timeout`` argument is optional and defaults to the "
"``TIMEOUT`` option of the appropriate backend in the :setting:`CACHES` "
"setting."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le modhanna eile, tá an argóint ``timeout`` roghnach agus "
"réamhshocraíonn sé ar an rogha ``TIMEOUT`` den chúltaca cuí sa "
"socrúit:setting: `CACHES`."

msgid ""
"``touch()`` returns ``True`` if the key was successfully touched, ``False`` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``touch () ```True`` má rinneadh teagmháil leis an eochair go "
"rathúil, ``False`` ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"You can also increment or decrement a key that already exists using the "
"``incr()`` or ``decr()`` methods, respectively. By default, the existing "
"cache value will be incremented or decremented by 1. Other increment/"
"decrement values can be specified by providing an argument to the increment/"
"decrement call. A ValueError will be raised if you attempt to increment or "
"decrement a nonexistent cache key:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat eochair atá ann cheana féin a mhéadú nó a laghdú ag baint "
"úsáide as na modhanna ``incr () ``nó `decr ()``, faoi seach. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, déanfar an luach taisce atá ann cheana a mhéadú nó a laghdú "
"faoi 1. Is féidir luachanna fáis/laghdaithe eile a shonrú trí argóint a "
"sholáthar don ghlao fáis/laghdaithe. Ardófar ValueError má dhéanann tú "
"iarracht eochair taisce nach bhfuil ann a mhéadú nó a laghdú:"

msgid ""
"``incr()``/``decr()`` methods are not guaranteed to be atomic. On those "
"backends that support atomic increment/decrement (most notably, the "
"memcached backend), increment and decrement operations will be atomic. "
"However, if the backend doesn't natively provide an increment/decrement "
"operation, it will be implemented using a two-step retrieve/update."
msgstr ""
"Ní ráthaítear go mbeidh modhanna ``incr () ```/`decr () ``adamhacha. Ar na "
"cúltacaí sin a thacaíonn le fhás/laghdú adamhach (go háirithe, an cúltaca "
"memcached), beidh oibríochtaí increimeádaithe agus laghdaithe adamhacha. Mar "
"sin féin, mura soláthraíonn an cúltaca oibríocht fhásai/laghdaithe go "
"dúchasach, cuirfear i bhfeidhm é ag baint úsáide as aisghabhálaí/nuashonrú "
"dhá chéim."

msgid ""
"You can close the connection to your cache with ``close()`` if implemented "
"by the cache backend."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an nasc le do taisce a dhúnadh le ``close () ``má chuireann "
"an cúltaca taisce i bhfeidhm."

msgid "For caches that don't implement ``close`` methods it is a no-op."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le tuairisceáin nach gcuireann modhanna ``dúnta ``i bhfeidhm is neamh-"
"op é."

msgid ""
"The async variants of base methods are prefixed with ``a``, e.g. "
"``cache.aadd()`` or ``cache.adelete_many()``. See `Asynchronous support`_ "
"for more details."
msgstr ""
"Tá na leaganacha async de mhodhanna bonn réamhshocraithe le ``a``, m.sh. "
"`cache.aadd () ``nó ``cache.adelete_many ()``. Féach `Tacaíocht "
"asincrónaithe`_ le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Cache key prefixing"
msgstr "Réamhshocrú eochair taisce"

msgid ""
"If you are sharing a cache instance between servers, or between your "
"production and development environments, it's possible for data cached by "
"one server to be used by another server. If the format of cached data is "
"different between servers, this can lead to some very hard to diagnose "
"problems."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sampla taisce á roinnt agat idir freastalaithe, nó idir do "
"thimpeallachtaí táirgeachta agus forbartha, is féidir go n-úsáidfidh "
"freastalaí eile sonraí a chuimsíonn freastalaí amháin. Má tá formáid na "
"sonraí taisceáilte difriúil idir freastalaithe, d'fhéadfadh fadhbanna an-"
"deacair a dhiagnóisiú a bheith mar thoradh air seo."

msgid ""
"To prevent this, Django provides the ability to prefix all cache keys used "
"by a server. When a particular cache key is saved or retrieved, Django will "
"automatically prefix the cache key with the value of "
"the :setting:`KEY_PREFIX <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>` cache setting."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a chosc, soláthraíonn Django an cumas na heochracha taisce go "
"léir a úsáideann freastalaí a réamhú <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>Nuair a shábháiltear "
"eochair taisce áirithe nó a aisghabháil, déanfaidh Django réamh-eochair an "
"taisce go huathoibríoch le luach an socrú taisce: socrú: `KEY_PREFIX`."

msgid ""
"By ensuring each Django instance has a different :setting:`KEY_PREFIX "
"<CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>`, you can ensure that there will be no collisions in "
"cache values."
msgstr ""
"Trí chinntiú go bhfuil difri:setting: `KEY_PREFIX <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>`ag "
"gach cás Django, is féidir leat a chinntiú nach mbeidh aon imbhuailtí i "
"luachanna taisce."

msgid "Cache versioning"
msgstr "Leagán taisce"

msgid ""
"When you change running code that uses cached values, you may need to purge "
"any existing cached values. The easiest way to do this is to flush the "
"entire cache, but this can lead to the loss of cache values that are still "
"valid and useful."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a athraíonn tú cód reatha a úsáideann luachanna taiscthe, b'fhéidir go "
"mbeidh ort aon luachanna taiscéadaithe atá ann cheana a ghlanadh. Is é an "
"bealach is éasca le seo a dhéanamh ná an taisce iomlán a shruthlú, ach "
"d'fhéadfadh sé seo go gcaillfear luachanna taisce atá fós bailí agus "
"úsáideach."

msgid ""
"Django provides a better way to target individual cache values. Django's "
"cache framework has a system-wide version identifier, specified using "
"the :setting:`VERSION <CACHES-VERSION>` cache setting. The value of this "
"setting is automatically combined with the cache prefix and the user-"
"provided cache key to obtain the final cache key."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django bealach níos fearr chun luachanna taisce aonair a "
"dhíriú. <CACHES-VERSION>Tá aitheantóir leagan ar fud an chórais ag creat "
"taisce Django, sonraithe ag baint úsáide as an socrú taisce: leagan: "
"`VERSION`. Déantar luach an socraithe seo a chomhcheangal go huathoibríoch "
"leis an réimír taisce agus leis an eochair taisce a sholáthraíonn an "
"úsáideoir chun an eochair taisce de"

msgid ""
"By default, any key request will automatically include the site default "
"cache key version. However, the primitive cache functions all include a "
"``version`` argument, so you can specify a particular cache key version to "
"set or get. For example:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, áireofar leagan eochair taisce réamhshocraithe an "
"láithreáin go huathoibríoch Mar sin féin, tá argóint ``leagan ``sa "
"fheidhmeanna taisce príomha uile, ionas gur féidir leat eochrleagan taisce "
"áirithe a shonrú le socrú nó a fháil. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"The version of a specific key can be incremented and decremented using the "
"``incr_version()`` and ``decr_version()`` methods. This enables specific "
"keys to be bumped to a new version, leaving other keys unaffected. "
"Continuing our previous example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leagan eochair shonrach a mhéadú agus a shocrú ag baint úsáide as "
"na modhanna ``incr_version () ``agus `decr_version ()``. Cuireann sé seo ar "
"chumas eochracha ar leith a chur chuig leagan nua, rud a fhágann gan "
"tionchar ar eochracha eile. Leanúint lenár sampla roimhe seo:"

msgid "Cache key transformation"
msgstr "Eochair claochlú taisce"

msgid ""
"As described in the previous two sections, the cache key provided by a user "
"is not used verbatim -- it is combined with the cache prefix and key version "
"to provide a final cache key. By default, the three parts are joined using "
"colons to produce a final string::"
msgstr ""
"Mar a thuairiscítear sa dá chuid roimhe seo, ní úsáidtear an eochair taisce "
"a sholáthraíonn úsáideoir focal focal - déantar é a chomhcheangal leis an "
"réimír taisce agus an leagan eochair chun eochair taisce deiridh a "
"sholáthar. De réir réamhshocraithe, ceanglaítear na trí chuid ag baint "
"úsáide as colons chun sreang deiridh a tháirgeadh:"

msgid ""
"If you want to combine the parts in different ways, or apply other "
"processing to the final key (e.g., taking a hash digest of the key parts), "
"you can provide a custom key function."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat na codanna a chur le chéile ar bhealaí éagsúla, nó próiseáil "
"eile a chur i bhfeidhm ar an eochair dheiridh (m.sh., díleá hash de na "
"príomhchodanna a thógáil), is féidir leat eochairfheidhm saincheaptha a "
"sholáthar."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`KEY_FUNCTION <CACHES-KEY_FUNCTION>` cache setting specifies a "
"dotted-path to a function matching the prototype of ``make_key()`` above. If "
"provided, this custom key function will be used instead of the default key "
"combining function."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn an socrú taisce: `KEY_FUNCTION <CACHES-KEY_FUNCTION>`cosán poncair "
"chuig feidhm a mheaitseann le fréamhshamhail ``make_key () ``thuas. Má "
"chuirtear ar fáil, úsáidfear an eochrfheidhm saincheaptha seo in ionad na "
"feidhme comhcheangailte eochair réamhshocrai"

msgid "Cache key warnings"
msgstr "Príomhrabhaidh taisce"

msgid ""
"Memcached, the most commonly-used production cache backend, does not allow "
"cache keys longer than 250 characters or containing whitespace or control "
"characters, and using such keys will cause an exception. To encourage cache-"
"portable code and minimize unpleasant surprises, the other built-in cache "
"backends issue a warning "
"(``django.core.cache.backends.base.CacheKeyWarning``) if a key is used that "
"would cause an error on memcached."
msgstr ""
"Ní cheadaíonn Memcached, an cúltaca taisce táirgeachta is coitianta a "
"úsáidtear, eochracha taisce níos faide ná 250 carachtar nó ina bhfuil spás "
"bán nó carachtair rialaithe, agus beidh eisceacht ina chúis le heochracha "
"den sórt sin a úsáid. Chun cód taisce iniompartha a spreagadh agus iontas "
"míthaitneamhach a íoslaghdú, eisíonn na cúltaca taisce ionsuite eile rabhadh "
"(``django.core.cache.backends.base.cachekeyWarning``) má úsáidtear eochair a "
"chuirfeadh earráid ar memcached."

msgid ""
"If you are using a production backend that can accept a wider range of keys "
"(a custom backend, or one of the non-memcached built-in backends), and want "
"to use this wider range without warnings, you can silence "
"``CacheKeyWarning`` with this code in the ``management`` module of one of "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá cúltaca táirgeachta á úsáid agat ar féidir leat glacadh le raon níos "
"leithne eochracha (cúltaca saincheaptha, nó ceann de na cúltaca neamh-"
"mheasta), agus gur mhaith leat an raon níos leithne seo a úsáid gan "
"rabhaidh, is féidir leat `CachekeyWarning`` a thostú leis an gcód seo sa "
"mhodúl `bainistí`` de cheann de do:"

msgid ""
"If you want to instead provide custom key validation logic for one of the "
"built-in backends, you can subclass it, override just the ``validate_key`` "
"method, and follow the instructions for `using a custom cache backend`_. For "
"instance, to do this for the ``locmem`` backend, put this code in a module::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat loighic bailíochtaithe eochair saincheaptha a sholáthar ina "
"ionad sin do cheann de na cúltaca ionsuite, is féidir leat é a fho-aicmiú, "
"díreach an modh `validate_key` a shárú, agus na treoracha chun `cúltaca "
"taisce saincheaptha a úsáid `_ a leanúint. Mar shampla, chun é seo a "
"dhéanamh don chúltaca ``locmem``, cuir an cód seo i modúl:"

msgid ""
"...and use the dotted Python path to this class in the :setting:`BACKEND "
"<CACHES-BACKEND>` portion of your :setting:`CACHES` setting."
msgstr ""
"... agus bain úsáid as an gcosán poncaigh Python chuig an rang seo sa chuid: "
"setting: `BACKEND `de do shuíomh:` <CACHES-BACKEND>CACHES`."

msgid ""
"Django has developing support for asynchronous cache backends, but does not "
"yet support asynchronous caching. It will be coming in a future release."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht ag forbairt ag Django do chúltaca taisce asincrónacha, ach ní "
"thacaíonn sé le caching asincrónach fós. Beidh sé ag teacht i scaoileadh "
"amach anseo."

msgid ""
"``django.core.cache.backends.base.BaseCache`` has async variants "
"of :ref:`all base methods <cache-basic-interface>`. By convention, the "
"asynchronous versions of all methods are prefixed with ``a``. By default, "
"the arguments for both variants are the same:"
msgstr ""
"<cache-basic-interface>Tá leaganacha async ag "
"``django.core.cache.backends.base.baseCache`` de:ref: `gach modh bonn `. De "
"réir choinbhinsiúin, tá na leaganacha asincrónacha de na modhanna go léir "
"réamhshocraithe le `a ``. De réir réamhshocraithe, tá na hargóintí don dá "
"leagan mar an gcéanna:"

msgid "Downstream caches"
msgstr "Caches downstream"

msgid ""
"So far, this document has focused on caching your *own* data. But another "
"type of caching is relevant to web development, too: caching performed by "
"\"downstream\" caches. These are systems that cache pages for users even "
"before the request reaches your website."
msgstr ""
"Go dtí seo, dhírigh an doiciméad seo ar do shonraí* díniú* a chaitheamh. Ach "
"tá cineál eile caighdeáin ábhartha d'fhorbairt gréasáin freisin: caistriú "
"arna ndéanamh ag taiscí “downstream”. Is córais iad seo a dhéanann taisce "
"leathanaigh d'úsáideoirí fiú sula sroicheann an t-iarratas do shuíomh "
"Gréasáin."

msgid "Here are a few examples of downstream caches:"
msgstr "Seo cúpla sampla de chaches iarshrutha:"

msgid ""
"When using HTTP, your :abbr:`ISP (Internet Service Provider)` may cache "
"certain pages, so if you requested a page from ``http://example.com/``, your "
"ISP would send you the page without having to access example.com directly. "
"The maintainers of example.com have no knowledge of this caching; the ISP "
"sits between example.com and your web browser, handling all of the caching "
"transparently. Such caching is not possible under HTTPS as it would "
"constitute a man-in-the-middle attack."
msgstr ""
"Agus HTTP á úsáid agat, féadfaidh do: abbr: `ISP (Soláthraí Seirbhíse "
"Idirlín) `leathanaigh áirithe a thaisceadh, mar sin má d'iarr tú leathanach "
"ó ``http://example.com/``, chuirfeadh do ISP an leathanach chugat gan "
"rochtain a fháil go díreach ar example.com. Níl aon eolas ag cothabhálaí "
"example.com ar an gcaistriú seo; suíonn an ISP idir example.com agus do "
"bhrabhsálaí gréasáin, ag láimhseáil an caistriú go léir go trédhearcach. Ní "
"féidir a chaiteáil den sórt sin indéanta faoi HTTPS toisc gur ionsaí fear sa "
"lár a bheadh ann."

msgid ""
"Your Django website may sit behind a *proxy cache*, such as Squid Web Proxy "
"Cache (http://www.squid-cache.org/), that caches pages for performance. In "
"this case, each request first would be handled by the proxy, and it would be "
"passed to your application only if needed."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh do shuíomh Gréasáin Django taobh thiar de*cache* "
"seachfhreastalaí*, mar shampla Squid Web Proxy Cache (http://www.squid-"
"cache.org/), a choscann leathanaigh le haghaidh feidhmíochta. Sa chás seo, "
"déanfadh an seachfhreastalaí gach iarratas a láimhseáil ar dtús, agus ní "
"chuirfeadh sé chuig d'iarratas ach amháin más gá."

msgid ""
"Your web browser caches pages, too. If a web page sends out the appropriate "
"headers, your browser will use the local cached copy for subsequent requests "
"to that page, without even contacting the web page again to see whether it "
"has changed."
msgstr ""
"Coscann do bhrabhsálaí gréasáin leathanaigh, freisin. Má sheolann leathanach "
"gréasáin na ceanntála cuí amach, úsáidfidh do bhrabhsálaí an chóip "
"thaisceáilte áitiúil le haghaidh iarratais ina dhiaidh sin chuig an "
"leathanach sin, gan teagmháil a dhéanamh leis an leathanach gréasáin arís "
"chun a fheiceáil an bhfuil athrú aige."

msgid ""
"Downstream caching is a nice efficiency boost, but there's a danger to it: "
"Many web pages' contents differ based on authentication and a host of other "
"variables, and cache systems that blindly save pages based purely on URLs "
"could expose incorrect or sensitive data to subsequent visitors to those "
"pages."
msgstr ""
"Is borradh deas éifeachtúlachta é an chaching anuas, ach tá contúirt ann dó: "
"Tá difríocht idir ábhar go leor leathanaigh ghréasáin bunaithe ar "
"fhíordheimhniú agus go leor athróg eile, agus d'fhéadfadh córais taisce a "
"shábháil leathanaigh atá bunaithe go dall ar URLanna sonraí míchearta nó "
"íogair a nochtadh do chuairteoirí ina dhiaidh sin ar na leathanaigh sin."

msgid ""
"For example, if you operate a web email system, then the contents of the "
"\"inbox\" page depend on which user is logged in. If an ISP blindly cached "
"your site, then the first user who logged in through that ISP would have "
"their user-specific inbox page cached for subsequent visitors to the site.  "
"That's not cool."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má oibríonn tú córas ríomhphoist gréasáin, ansin braitheann "
"ábhar an leathanaigh “bosca isteach” ar an úsáideoir atá logáilte isteach. "
"Má chuaigh ISP do shuíomh a chosc go dall, ansin bheadh a leathanach bosca "
"isteach úsáideora atá sonrach le húsáideoir a stóráilte isteach tríd an ISP "
"sin do chuairteoirí ina dhiaidh sin ar an suíomh. Níl sé sin fionnuar."

msgid ""
"Fortunately, HTTP provides a solution to this problem. A number of HTTP "
"headers exist to instruct downstream caches to differ their cache contents "
"depending on designated variables, and to tell caching mechanisms not to "
"cache particular pages. We'll look at some of these headers in the sections "
"that follow."
msgstr ""
"Ar ámharaí an tsaoil, soláthraíonn HTTP réiteach don fhadhb seo. Tá roinnt "
"ceanntásca HTTP ann chun treoir a thabhairt do chaches iarshrutha a n-ábhar "
"taisce a dhifriú ag brath ar athróga ainmnithe, agus chun meicníochtaí "
"taiscéála a insint gan leathanaigh áirithe a thaisceadh. Breathnóimid ar "
"chuid de na ceanntásca seo sna codanna a leanann."

msgid "Using ``Vary`` headers"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as ceanntásca ``Vary``"

msgid ""
"The ``Vary`` header defines which request headers a cache mechanism should "
"take into account when building its cache key. For example, if the contents "
"of a web page depend on a user's language preference, the page is said to "
"\"vary on language.\""
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an ceannteideal `Vary` cén ceannteideal iarratais ba chóir do "
"mheicníocht taisce a chur san áireamh agus a eochair taisce á thógáil. Mar "
"shampla, má bhraitheann ábhar leathanaigh ghréasáin ar rogha teanga "
"úsáideora, deirtear go n-athraíonn an leathanach ar an teanga."

msgid ""
"By default, Django's cache system creates its cache keys using the requested "
"fully-qualified URL -- e.g., ``\"https://www.example.com/stories/2005/?"
"order_by=author\"``. This means every request to that URL will use the same "
"cached version, regardless of user-agent differences such as cookies or "
"language preferences. However, if this page produces different content based "
"on some difference in request headers -- such as a cookie, or a language, or "
"a user-agent -- you'll need to use the ``Vary`` header to tell caching "
"mechanisms that the page output depends on those things."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, cruthaíonn córas taisce Django a heochracha taisce "
"ag baint úsáide as an URL láncháilithe a iarrtar - m.sh., ``” https://"
"www.example.com/stories/2005/?order_by=author “``. Ciallaíonn sé seo go n-"
"úsáidfidh gach iarratas ar an URL sin an leagan taisceáilte céanna, beag "
"beann ar dhifríochtaí gníomhaire úsáideora amhail fianáin nó roghanna "
"teanga. Mar sin féin, má tháirgeann an leathanach seo ábhar éagsúil bunaithe "
"ar dhifríocht éigin i gceanntásca iarratais - mar shampla fianán, nó teanga, "
"nó gníomhaire úsáideora - beidh ort an ceannteideal ``Vary`` a úsáid chun "
"meicníochtaí caching a insint go mbraitheann aschur an leathanaigh ar na "
"rudaí sin."

msgid ""
"To do this in Django, use the "
"convenient :func:`django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_headers` view "
"decorator, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a dhéanamh i Django, bain úsáid as an maisitheoir amharc "
"áisiú:func: `django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_headers`, mar sin:"

msgid ""
"In this case, a caching mechanism (such as Django's own cache middleware) "
"will cache a separate version of the page for each unique user-agent."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, déanfaidh meicníocht caching (mar shampla middleware taisce "
"Django féin) leagan ar leithligh den leathanach a thaisceadh do gach "
"gníomhaire úsáideora uathúil."

msgid ""
"The advantage to using the ``vary_on_headers`` decorator rather than "
"manually setting the ``Vary`` header (using something like "
"``response.headers['Vary'] = 'user-agent'``) is that the decorator *adds* to "
"the ``Vary`` header (which may already exist), rather than setting it from "
"scratch and potentially overriding anything that was already in there."
msgstr ""
"Is é an buntáiste a bhaineann leis an maisitheoir `vary_on_headers`` a úsáid "
"seachas an ceannteideal ``Vary`` a shocrú de láimh (ag baint úsáide as "
"`response.heads ['Vary'] = 'user-agent' ``) ná go gcuireann an maisitheoir "
"** leis an gceannteideal `Vary`` (a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ann cheana féin)."

msgid "You can pass multiple headers to ``vary_on_headers()``::"
msgstr "Is féidir leat ceanntásca iolracha a chur chuig ``vary_on_heads () ``:"

msgid ""
"This tells downstream caches to vary on *both*, which means each combination "
"of user-agent and cookie will get its own cache value. For example, a "
"request with the user-agent ``Mozilla`` and the cookie value ``foo=bar`` "
"will be considered different from a request with the user-agent ``Mozilla`` "
"and the cookie value ``foo=ham``."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé seo do chaisceanna iarshrutha go n-athróidh ar*an bheath*, rud a "
"chiallaíonn go bhfaighidh gach teaglaim de ghníomhaire úsáideora agus fianán "
"a luach taisce féin. Mar shampla, measfar iarratas leis an ngníomhaire "
"úsáideora ``Mozilla`` agus an luach fianáin ``foo=bar`` difriúil ó iarratas "
"leis an ngníomhaire úsáideora ``Mozilla`` agus an luach fianáin ``foo=ham``."

msgid ""
"Because varying on cookie is so common, there's "
"a :func:`django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_cookie` decorator. These two "
"views are equivalent::"
msgstr ""
"Toisc go bhfuil éagsúlacht ar fhianán chomh coitianta, tá a: func: "
"`django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_cookie` maisitheoir ann. Tá an dá "
"thuairim seo coibhéiseach:"

msgid ""
"The headers you pass to ``vary_on_headers`` are not case sensitive; ``\"User-"
"Agent\"`` is the same thing as ``\"user-agent\"``."
msgstr ""
"Níl na ceanntásca a chuireann tú chuig `vary_on_headers`` íogair do "
"chásanna; ``\"Gníomhaireacht úsáideora” ``an rud céanna le ``\"úsáideach-"
"gníomhaireaí\"`."

msgid ""
"You can also use a helper "
"function, :func:`django.utils.cache.patch_vary_headers`, directly. This "
"function sets, or adds to, the ``Vary header``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat feidhm chúntóra a úsáid freisin, :func: "
"`django.utils.cache.patch_vary_headers`, go díreach. Socraíonn an fheidhm "
"seo, nó cuireann sé leis an “Ceannteideal éagsúla”. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"``patch_vary_headers`` takes an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` instance "
"as its first argument and a list/tuple of case-insensitive header names as "
"its second argument."
msgstr ""
"Glacann ``patch_vary_headers`` an:class: `~django.http.http.httpResponse` "
"mar an chéad argóint agus liosta/tiúpla d'ainmneacha ceanntásc cás-neamh-"
"íogair mar an dara argóint."

msgid ""
"For more on Vary headers, see the :rfc:`official Vary spec "
"<9110#section-12.5.5>`."
msgstr ""
"<9110 #section -12.5.5>Le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais faoi cheanntásca Vary, "
"féach an:rfc: `official Vary spec`."

msgid "Controlling cache: Using other headers"
msgstr "Taisce a rialú: Ceannteidil eile a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Other problems with caching are the privacy of data and the question of "
"where data should be stored in a cascade of caches."
msgstr ""
"Is iad fadhbanna eile a bhaineann le caistriú ná príobháideacht sonraí agus "
"an cheist cá háit ar chóir sonraí a stóráil i gcaitheamh taiscí."

msgid ""
"A user usually faces two kinds of caches: their own browser cache (a private "
"cache) and their provider's cache (a public cache). A public cache is used "
"by multiple users and controlled by someone else. This poses problems with "
"sensitive data--you don't want, say, your bank account number stored in a "
"public cache. So web applications need a way to tell caches which data is "
"private and which is public."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth bíonn dhá chineál taisce ag úsáideoir: taisce a bhrabhsálaí féin "
"(taisce príobháideach) agus taisce a sholáthraí (taisce poiblí). Úsáideann "
"iolrúsáideoirí taisce poiblí agus tá sé á rialú ag duine eile. Cuireann sé "
"seo fadhbanna le sonraí íogair - níl tú ag iarraidh, abair, d'uimhir "
"chuntais bhainc a stóráiltear i taisce poiblí. Mar sin teastaíonn bealach ó "
"fheidhmchláir ghréasáin chun na sonraí atá príobháideach agus na sonraí atá "
"poiblí a insint"

msgid ""
"The solution is to indicate a page's cache should be \"private.\" To do this "
"in Django, use the :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control` view "
"decorator. Example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an réiteach ná a chur in iúl gur chóir go mbeadh taisce leathanaigh "
"“príobháideach.” Chun é seo a dhéanamh i Django, bain úsáid as an "
"maisitheoir amharc: :func: `~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control`. "
"Sampla::"

msgid ""
"This decorator takes care of sending out the appropriate HTTP header behind "
"the scenes."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an maisitheoir seo aire don cheannteideal HTTP cuí a sheoladh amach "
"taobh thiar de na radhairc."

msgid ""
"Note that the cache control settings \"private\" and \"public\" are mutually "
"exclusive. The decorator ensures that the \"public\" directive is removed if "
"\"private\" should be set (and vice versa). An example use of the two "
"directives would be a blog site that offers both private and public entries. "
"Public entries may be cached on any shared cache. The following code "
"uses :func:`~django.utils.cache.patch_cache_control`, the manual way to "
"modify the cache control header (it is internally called by "
"the :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control` decorator)::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil na socruithe rialaithe taisce “príobháideach” "
"agus “poiblí” go comhpháirteach. Cinntíonn an maisitheoir go mbaintear an "
"treoir “phoiblí” más chóir “príobháideach” a shocrú (agus a mhalairt). "
"Bheadh úsáid samplach den dá threoir ná suíomh blag a thairgeann iontrálacha "
"príobháideacha agus poiblí araon. Féadfar iontrálacha poiblí a stóráil ar "
"aon taisce roinnte. Úsáideann an cód seo a leanas: func: "
"`~django.utils.cache.patch_cache_control`, an bealach láimhe chun an "
"ceannteideal rialaithe taisce a mhodhnú (tugtar air go hinmheánach ag an "
"maisitheoir:: `~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control`):"

msgid ""
"You can control downstream caches in other ways as well (see :rfc:`9111` for "
"details on HTTP caching). For example, even if you don't use Django's server-"
"side cache framework, you can still tell clients to cache a view for a "
"certain amount of time with the :rfc:`max-age <9111#section-5.2.2.1>` "
"directive::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat taiscí iarshrutha a rialú ar bhealaí eile freisin (féach: "
