"-5.2.2.1>Mar shampla, fiú mura n-úsáideann tú creat taisce taobh freastalaí "
"Django, is féidir leat a rá fós do chliaint radharc a thaisceadh ar feadh "
"méid áirithe ama leis an treor:rfc: `max-age`::"

msgid ""
"(If you *do* use the caching middleware, it already sets the ``max-age`` "
"with the value of the :setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS` setting. In that "
"case, the custom ``max_age`` from "
"the :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control` decorator will take "
"precedence, and the header values will be merged correctly.)"
msgstr ""
"(Má úsáideann t* an middleware caching, socraíonn sé an `max-aois ``luach an "
"socruithe: `CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS` cheana féin. Sa chás sin, beidh "
"tosaíocht ag an maisitheoir saincheaptha ``max_age ``óna:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control`, agus cumasófar na luachanna "
"ceanntásc i gceart.)"

msgid ""
"Any valid ``Cache-Control`` response directive is valid in "
"``cache_control()``. Here are some more examples:"
msgstr ""
"Tá aon treoir bhailí freagartha ``Cache-Control`` bailí i ``cache_control () "
"``. Seo roinnt samplaí eile:"

msgid "``no_transform=True``"
msgstr "``no_transform=True``"

msgid "``must_revalidate=True``"
msgstr "``must_revalidate=True``"

msgid "``stale_while_revalidate=num_seconds``"
msgstr "``stale_while_revalidate=uimh_soicind``"

msgid "``no_cache=True``"
msgstr "``no_cache=True``"

msgid ""
"The full list of known directives can be found in the `IANA registry`_ (note "
"that not all of them apply to responses)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir liosta iomlán na dtreoracha ar eolas a fháil sa chlárlann IANA`_ "
"(tabhair faoi deara nach mbaineann gach ceann acu le freagraí)."

msgid ""
"If you want to use headers to disable caching "
"altogether, :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.never_cache` is a view "
"decorator that adds headers to ensure the response won't be cached by "
"browsers or other caches. Example::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat ceanntásca a úsáid chun cúisceáin a dhíchumasú ar fad, is "
"maisitheoir amharc é: :func: `~django.views.decorators.cache.never_cache` a "
"chuireann ceanntásc leis chun a chinntiú nach ndéanfaidh brabhsálaithe nó "
"caches eile an freagra a stóráil. Sampla::"

msgid "Order of ``MIDDLEWARE``"
msgstr "Ordú ``MIDDLEWARE``"

msgid ""
"If you use caching middleware, it's important to put each half in the right "
"place within the :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting. That's because the cache "
"middleware needs to know which headers by which to vary the cache storage. "
"Middleware always adds something to the ``Vary`` response header when it can."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú middleware caching, tá sé tábhachtach gach leath a chur san "
"áit cheart laistigh den socrú: setting: `MIDDLEWARE`. Sin toisc go "
"gcaithfidh an middleware taisce a bheith ar an eolas faoi na ceannteidil "
"trína ndéanfaidh an stóráil taisce a athrú. Cuireann Middleware rud éigin i "
"gcónaí leis an gceannteideal freagartha ``Vary` nuair is féidir leis."

msgid ""
"``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` runs during the response phase, where middleware "
"is run in reverse order, so an item at the top of the list runs *last* "
"during the response phase. Thus, you need to make sure that "
"``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` appears *before* any other middleware that might "
"add something to the ``Vary`` header. The following middleware modules do so:"
msgstr ""
"Ritheann ``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` le linn na céime freagartha, áit a "
"reáchtáiltear middleware in ord droim, mar sin ritheann mír ag barr an "
"liosta*deireana* le linn na céime freagartha. Mar sin, ní mór duit a "
"chinntiú go bhfeictear ``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` *roimh* aon mheán-earraí "
"eile a d'fhéadfadh rud éigin a chur leis an gceannteideal ``Vary``. Déanann "
"na modúil middleware seo a leanas amhlaidh:"

msgid "``SessionMiddleware`` adds ``Cookie``"
msgstr "Cuireann ``SessionMiddleware`` leis ``Cookie``"

msgid "``GZipMiddleware`` adds ``Accept-Encoding``"
msgstr "Cuireann ``GZipMiddleWare`` ``Accept-Encoding``"

msgid "``LocaleMiddleware`` adds ``Accept-Language``"
msgstr "Cuireann ``Localemiddleware`` leis ``Accept-Language``"

msgid ""
"``FetchFromCacheMiddleware``, on the other hand, runs during the request "
"phase, where middleware is applied first-to-last, so an item at the top of "
"the list runs *first* during the request phase. The "
"``FetchFromCacheMiddleware`` also needs to run after other middleware "
"updates the ``Vary`` header, so ``FetchFromCacheMiddleware`` must be *after* "
"any item that does so."
msgstr ""
"Ar an láimh eile, ritheann ``fetchfromcachemiddleware`` le linn na céime "
"iarratais, áit a gcuirtear meán-earraí i bhfeidhm den chéad uair go "
"deireanach, mar sin ritheann mír ag barr an liosta*an chéad* le linn na "
"céime iarratais. Caithfidh an ``FetchFromCacheMiddleware`` rith freisin tar "
"éis lár earraí eile an ceannteideal ``Vary`` a nuashonrú, mar sin caithfidh "
"``FetchfromCacheMiddleware`` a bheith aith* tar éis aon earra a dhéanann "
"amhlaidh."

msgid "System check framework"
msgstr "Creat seiceála an chórais"

msgid ""
"The system check framework is a set of static checks for validating Django "
"projects. It detects common problems and provides hints for how to fix them. "
"The framework is extensible so you can easily add your own checks."
msgstr ""
"Is sraith seiceálacha statacha é creat seiceála an chórais chun tionscadail "
"Django a bhailíochtú. Braithíonn sé fadhbanna coitianta agus soláthraíonn sé "
"leideanna maidir le conas iad a shocrú. Tá an creat inleathnaithe ionas gur "
"féidir leat do sheiceálacha féin a chur leis go héasca."

msgid ""
"Checks can be triggered explicitly via the :djadmin:`check` command. Checks "
"are triggered implicitly before most commands, "
"including :djadmin:`runserver` and :djadmin:`migrate`. For performance "
"reasons, checks are not run as part of the WSGI stack that is used in "
"deployment. If you need to run system checks on your deployment server, "
"trigger them explicitly using :djadmin:`check`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir seiceálacha a spreagadh go sainráite tríd an ordú:djadmin: "
"`check`. Cuirtear seiceálacha a spreagadh go hiontach roimh fhormhór na n-"
"orduithe, lena n-áirítear: djadmin: `runserver` agus:djadmin: `migrate`. Ar "
"chúiseanna feidhmíochta, ní reáchtáiltear seiceálacha mar chuid den chruach "
"WSGI a úsáidtear in imscaradh. Más gá duit seiceálacha córais a reáchtáil ar "
"do fhreastalaí imscartha, spreag iad go sainráite ag baint úsáide as: "
"djadmin: `check`."

msgid ""
"Serious errors will prevent Django commands (such as :djadmin:`runserver`) "
"from running at all. Minor problems are reported to the console. If you have "
"inspected the cause of a warning and are happy to ignore it, you can hide "
"specific warnings using the :setting:`SILENCED_SYSTEM_CHECKS` setting in "
"your project settings file."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh earráidí tromchúiseacha cosc ar orduithe Django (mar shampla: "
"djadmin: `runserver`) ó rith ar chor ar bith. Tuairiscítear mionfhadhbanna "
"don chonsól. Má rinne tú iniúchadh ar chúis rabhaidh agus má tá tú sásta "
"neamhaird a dhéanamh air, is féidir leat rabhaidh sonracha a cheilt ag baint "
"úsáide as an socrú: setting: `SILENCED_SYSTEM_CHECKS` i do chomhad socruithe "
"tionscadail."

msgid ""
"A full list of all checks that can be raised by Django can be found in "
"the :doc:`System check reference </ref/checks>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir liosta iomlán de na seiceálacha go léir is féidir le Django a ardú "
"a fháil in:doc: `Tagairt seiceála córas` </ref/checks>."

msgid "Writing your own checks"
msgstr "Do sheiceálacha féin a scríobh"

msgid ""
"The framework is flexible and allows you to write functions that perform any "
"other kind of check you may require. The following is an example stub check "
"function::"
msgstr ""
"Tá an creat solúbtha agus tugann sé deis duit feidhmeanna a scríobh a "
"dhéanann aon chineál eile seiceála a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ag teastáil uait. "
"Seo a leanas feidhm sheiceála stub sampla::"

msgid ""
"The check function *must* accept an ``app_configs`` argument; this argument "
"is the list of applications that should be inspected. If ``None``, the check "
"must be run on *all* installed apps in the project."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh an fheidhm seiceála* glacadh le hargóint ``app_configs``; is é an "
"argóint seo an liosta d'iarratais ar chóir a iniúchadh. Má tá ``None ``, ní "
"mór an seiceáil a reáchtáil ar* gach aipeanna suiteáilte sa tionscadal."

msgid ""
"The check will receive a ``databases`` keyword argument. This is a list of "
"database aliases whose connections may be used to inspect database level "
"configuration. If ``databases`` is ``None``, the check must not use any "
"database connections."
msgstr ""
"Gheobhaidh an seic argóint eochairfhocal ``bunachar sonraí ``. Is liosta é "
"seo d'ainmneacha bunachar sonraí ar féidir a naisc a úsáid chun cumraíocht "
"leibhéal bunachar sonraí a iniúchadh. Más é ```bunachar sonraí ``None``, ní "
"mór don seiceáil aon naisc bunachar sonraí a úsáid."

msgid "The ``**kwargs`` argument is required for future expansion."
msgstr "Tá an argóint `**kwargs ``ag teastáil le haghaidh leathnú amach anseo."

msgid "Messages"
msgstr "Teachtaireachtaí"

msgid ""
"The function must return a list of messages. If no problems are found as a "
"result of the check, the check function must return an empty list."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh an fheidhm liosta teachtaireachtaí a thabhairt ar ais. Mura "
"bhfaightear aon fhadhbanna mar thoradh ar an seiceáil, caithfidh an fheidhm "
"seiceála liosta folamh a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"The warnings and errors raised by the check method must be instances "
"of :class:`~django.core.checks.CheckMessage`. An instance "
"of :class:`~django.core.checks.CheckMessage` encapsulates a single "
"reportable error or warning. It also provides context and hints applicable "
"to the message, and a unique identifier that is used for filtering purposes."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh na rabhaidh agus na hearráidí arna ardú ag an modh seiceála a "
"bheith ina gcásanna de:class: `~django.core.checks.checkMessage`. Cuimsíonn "
"sampla de:class: `~Django.Core.Checks.CheckMessage` earráid nó rabhadh "
"amháin a thuairiscithe. Soláthraíonn sé comhthéacs agus leideanna is "
"infheidhme maidir leis an teachtaireacht, agus aitheantóir uathúil a "
"úsáidtear chun críocha scagtha."

msgid ""
"The concept is very similar to messages from the :doc:`message framework </"
"ref/contrib/messages>` or the :doc:`logging framework </topics/logging>`. "
"Messages are tagged with a ``level`` indicating the severity of the message."
msgstr ""
"Tá an coincheap an-chosúil le teachtaireachtaí óna:doc: `creat "
"teachtaireachtaí `nó la:doc: `creat logála `</ref/contrib/messages> </topics/"
"logging>. Tá 'leibhéal' clibeáilte ag teachtaireachtaí a léiríonn déine na "
"teachtaireachta."

msgid ""
"There are also shortcuts to make creating messages with common levels "
"easier. When using these classes you can omit the ``level`` argument because "
"it is implied by the class name."
msgstr ""
"Tá aicearraí ann freisin chun teachtaireachtaí a chruthú le leibhéil "
"choiteanna a dhéanamh níos éasca. Agus na ranganna seo á úsáid agat is "
"féidir leat an argóint ``leibhéil ``a fhágáil toisc go bhfuil ainm an ranga "
"intuigthe air."

msgid ":class:`Debug`"
msgstr ":class: `Dífhabhtú"

msgid ":class:`Info`"
msgstr ":class: `eolas `"

msgid ":class:`Warning`"
msgstr ":class: `Rabhadh `"

msgid ":class:`Error`"
msgstr ":class: `Earráid`"

msgid ":class:`Critical`"
msgstr ":class: `Criticial`"

