msgid "Built-in class-based generic views"
msgstr "Tuairimí cineálacha bunaithe ar rang ionsuite"

msgid ""
"Writing web applications can be monotonous, because we repeat certain "
"patterns again and again. Django tries to take away some of that monotony at "
"the model and template layers, but web developers also experience this "
"boredom at the view level."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le feidhmchláir gréasáin a scríobh a bheith aontónach, toisc go "
"ndéanaimid patrúin áirithe a athdhéanamh Déanann Django iarracht cuid den "
"aonfhoirmeacht sin a thógáil ar shiúl ag na sraitheanna samhail agus "
"teimpléad, ach bíonn forbróirí gréasáin ag an leamh seo ag an leibhéal "
"radhairc freisin."

msgid ""
"Django's *generic views* were developed to ease that pain. They take certain "
"common idioms and patterns found in view development and abstract them so "
"that you can quickly write common views of data without having to write too "
"much code."
msgstr ""
"Forbraíodh *tuairimí cineálacha* Django chun an pian sin a mhaolú. Tógann "
"siad nathanna agus patrúin choitianta áirithe a fhaightear i bhforbairt "
"amharc agus déanann siad teibí orthu ionas gur féidir leat tuairimí "
"coitianta ar shonraí a scríobh go tapa gan an iomarca cód a"

msgid ""
"We can recognize certain common tasks, like displaying a list of objects, "
"and write code that displays a list of *any* object. Then the model in "
"question can be passed as an extra argument to the URLconf."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir linn tascanna coitianta áirithe a aithint, cosúil le liosta rudaí "
"a thaispeáint, agus cód a scríobh a thaispeánann liosta de*aon réad*. Ansin "
"is féidir an tsamhail atá i gceist a chur ar aghaidh mar argóint bhreise "
"chuig an URLConf."

msgid "Django ships with generic views to do the following:"
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django le tuairimí cineálacha chun na nithe seo a leanas a dhéanamh:"

msgid ""
"Display list and detail pages for a single object. If we were creating an "
"application to manage conferences then a ``TalkListView`` and a "
"``RegisteredUserListView`` would be examples of list views. A single talk "
"page is an example of what we call a \"detail\" view."
msgstr ""
"Taispeáin liosta agus leathanaigh mionsonraithe le haghaidh réad amháin. Dá "
"mbeimid ag cruthú feidhmchlár chun comhdhálacha a bhainistiú ansin bheadh "
"`TalkListView` agus ``RegisteredUserListView`` ina samplaí de thuairimí "
"liosta. Is sampla é leathanach cainte amháin den rud a thugaimid ar radharc "
"“mionsonraí”."

msgid ""
"Present date-based objects in year/month/day archive pages, associated "
"detail, and \"latest\" pages."
msgstr ""
"Cuir rudaí dáta-bhunaithe i láthair i leathanaigh cartlainne blian/mí/lá, "
"mionsonraí gaolmhara, agus leathanaigh “is déanaí”."

msgid ""
"Allow users to create, update, and delete objects -- with or without "
"authorization."
msgstr ""
"Lig d'úsáideoirí rudaí a chruthú, a nuashonrú agus a scriosadh - le húdarú "
"nó gan údarú."

msgid ""
"Taken together, these views provide interfaces to perform the most common "
"tasks developers encounter."
msgstr ""
"Le chéile, soláthraíonn na tuairimí seo comhéadain chun na tascanna is "
"coitianta a thagann forbróirí a dhéanamh"

msgid "Extending generic views"
msgstr "Tuairimí cineálacha a le"

msgid ""
"There's no question that using generic views can speed up development "
"substantially. In most projects, however, there comes a moment when the "
"generic views no longer suffice. Indeed, the most common question asked by "
"new Django developers is how to make generic views handle a wider array of "
"situations."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon cheist ann gur féidir le tuairimí cineálacha a úsáid a bhrostú go "
"suntasach. I bhformhór na dtionscadail, áfach, tagann nóiméad nuair nach "
"leor na tuairimí cineálacha a thuilleadh. Go deimhin, is í an cheist is "
"coitianta a chuireann forbróirí nua Django ná conas tuairimí cineálacha a "
"láimhseáil le raon níos leithne cásanna."

msgid ""
"This is one of the reasons generic views were redesigned for the 1.3 release "
"- previously, they were view functions with a bewildering array of options; "
"now, rather than passing in a large amount of configuration in the URLconf, "
"the recommended way to extend generic views is to subclass them, and "
"override their attributes or methods."
msgstr ""
"Seo ceann de na cúiseanna a athdhearadh tuairimí cineálacha don scaoileadh "
"1.3 - roimhe seo, bhí feidhmeanna amharc acu le sraith roghanna mealltach; "
"anois, seachas cuid mhór cumraíochta a chur isteach sa URLConf, is é an "
"bealach molta chun tuairimí cineálacha a leathnú ná iad a fho-aicmiú, agus a "
"gcuid tréithe nó modhanna a shárú."

msgid ""
"That said, generic views will have a limit. If you find you're struggling to "
"implement your view as a subclass of a generic view, then you may find it "
"more effective to write just the code you need, using your own class-based "
"or functional views."
msgstr ""
"É sin ráite, beidh teorainn ag tuairimí cineálacha. Má aimsíonn tú go bhfuil "
"tú ag streachailt do dhearcadh a chur i bhfeidhm mar fho-aicme de radharc "
"cineálach, ansin b'fhéidir go mbeidh sé níos éifeachtaí duit ach an cód a "
"theastaíonn uait a scríobh, ag baint úsáide as do thuairimí rang-bhunaithe "
"nó feidhmiúla féin."

msgid ""
"More examples of generic views are available in some third party "
"applications, or you could write your own as needed."
msgstr ""
"Tá níos mó samplaí de thuairimí cineálacha ar fáil i roinnt feidhmchlár tríú "
"páirtí, nó d'fhéadfá do chuid féin a scríobh de réir mar is gá."

msgid "Generic views of objects"
msgstr "Tuairimí cineálacha ar rudaí"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.views.generic.base.TemplateView` certainly is useful, but "
"Django's generic views really shine when it comes to presenting views of "
"your database content. Because it's such a common task, Django comes with a "
"handful of built-in generic views to help generate list and detail views of "
"objects."
msgstr ""
":class: Is cinnte go bhfuil `~Django.Views.Generic.Base.TemplateView` "
"úsáideach, ach is cinnte go bhfuil tuairimí cineálacha Django ina ndáiríre "
"maidir le tuairimí d'ábhar bunachar sonraí a chur i láthair. Toisc gur tasc "
"chomh coitianta é, tagann Django le dornán tuairimí cineálacha ionsuite chun "
"cabhrú le tuairimí liosta agus mionsonraithe rudaí a ghiniúint."

msgid ""
"Let's start by looking at some examples of showing a list of objects or an "
"individual object."
msgstr ""
"Tosaímid trí fhéachaint ar roinnt samplaí de liosta rudaí nó réad aonair a "
"thaispeáint."

msgid "We'll be using these models::"
msgstr "Beidh muid ag baint úsáide as na samhlacha seo:"

msgid "Now we need to define a view::"
msgstr "Anois ní mór dúinn dearcadh a shainiú::"

msgid "Finally hook that view into your urls::"
msgstr "Ar deireadh, cuir an radharc sin isteach i do urls::"

msgid ""
"That's all the Python code we need to write. We still need to write a "
"template, however. We could explicitly tell the view which template to use "
"by adding a ``template_name`` attribute to the view, but in the absence of "
"an explicit template Django will infer one from the object's name. In this "
"case, the inferred template will be ``\"books/publisher_list.html\"`` -- the "
"\"books\" part comes from the name of the app that defines the model, while "
"the \"publisher\" bit is the lowercased version of the model's name."
msgstr ""
"Sin an cód Python go léir a chaithfimid a scríobh. Ní mór dúinn teimpléad a "
"scríobh fós, áfach. D'fhéadfaimis a insint go sainráite don radharc cén "
"teimpléad atá le húsáid trí thréith ``template_name`` a chur leis an "
"radharc, ach in éagmais teimpléad follasach tabharfaidh Django amach ceann ó "
"ainm an réada. Sa chás seo, is é ``” books/publisher_list.html “`` an "
"teimpléad intuartha - tagann an chuid “leabhair” ó ainm an aip a "
"shainmhíníonn an tsamhail, agus is é an giotán “foilsitheora” an leagan "
"íseal d'ainm an tsamhail."

msgid ""
"Thus, when (for example) the ``APP_DIRS`` option of a ``DjangoTemplates`` "
"backend is set to True in :setting:`TEMPLATES`, a template location could "
"be: /path/to/project/books/templates/books/publisher_list.html"
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, nuair a shocraítear (mar shampla) an rogha ``APP_DIRS`` de "
"chúltaca ``DjangoTemplates`` go Fíor in:setting: `TEMPLATES`, d'fhéadfadh "
"suíomh teimpléad a bheith: /path/to/project/books/templates/books/"
"publisher_list.html"

msgid ""
"This template will be rendered against a context containing a variable "
"called ``object_list`` that contains all the publisher objects. A template "
"might look like this:"
msgstr ""
"Déanfar an teimpléad seo a léiriú i gcoinne comhthéacs ina bhfuil athróg ar "
"a dtugtar `object_list`` ina bhfuil na rudaí foilsitheora go léir. "
"D'fhéadfadh cuma seo a bheith ar theimpléad:"

msgid ""
"That's really all there is to it. All the cool features of generic views "
"come from changing the attributes set on the generic view. The :doc:`generic "
"views reference</ref/class-based-views/index>` documents all the generic "
"views and their options in detail; the rest of this document will consider "
"some of the common ways you might customize and extend generic views."
msgstr ""
"Sin go léir atá ann i ndáiríre. Tagann gnéithe fionnuar uile na tuairimí "
"cineálacha ó na tréithe atá leagtha amach ar an radharc cineálach a athrú. "
"Déan:doc: tagairt tuairimí cineálacha '</ref/class-based-views/index> "
"doiciméadaíonn na tuairimí cineálacha go léir agus a roghanna go mion; "
"breithneoidh an chuid eile den doiciméad seo cuid de na bealaí coitianta a "
"d'fhéadfá tuairimí cineálacha a shaincheapadh agus a leathnú."

msgid "Making \"friendly\" template contexts"
msgstr "Comhthéacsanna teimpléid “cairdiúla”"

msgid ""
"You might have noticed that our sample publisher list template stores all "
"the publishers in a variable named ``object_list``. While this works just "
"fine, it isn't all that \"friendly\" to template authors: they have to "
"\"just know\" that they're dealing with publishers here."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur thug tú faoi deara go stórálann ár dteimpléad liosta "
"foilsitheoirí samplach na foilsitheoirí go léir in athróg darb ainm "
"`object_list``. Cé go n-oibríonn sé seo go breá, níl sé chomh “cairdiúil” "
"sin d'údair teimpléid: caithfidh siad “a fhios” a bheith acu go bhfuil siad "
"ag déileáil le foilsitheoirí anseo."

msgid ""
"Well, if you're dealing with a model object, this is already done for you. "
"When you are dealing with an object or queryset, Django is able to populate "
"the context using the lowercased version of the model class' name. This is "
"provided in addition to the default ``object_list`` entry, but contains "
"exactly the same data, i.e. ``publisher_list``."
msgstr ""
"Bhuel, má tá tú ag déileáil le réad samhail, déantar é seo duit cheana féin. "
"Nuair a bhíonn tú ag déileáil le réad nó tacar fiosrúcháin, tá Django in ann "
"an comhthéacs a líonadh ag baint úsáide as an leagan íseal d'ainm an ranga "
"samhail. Cuirtear é seo ar fáil i dteannta leis an iontráil réamhshocraithe "
"``object_list``, ach tá na sonraí céanna go díreach ann, ie "
"``publisher_list``."

msgid ""
"If this still isn't a good match, you can manually set the name of the "
"context variable. The ``context_object_name`` attribute on a generic view "
"specifies the context variable to use::"
msgstr ""
"Mura meaitseáil mhaith é seo fós, is féidir leat ainm an athróg comhthéacs a "
"shocrú de láimh. Sonraíonn an tréith ``context_object_name`` ar amharc "
"cineálach an t-athróg comhthéacs atá le húsáid:"

msgid ""
"Providing a useful ``context_object_name`` is always a good idea. Your "
"coworkers who design templates will thank you."
msgstr ""
"Is smaoineamh maith i gcónaí é ``context_object_name`` úsáideach a "
"sholáthar. Gabhfaidh do chomhoibrithe a dhearann teimpléid buíochas leat."

msgid "Adding extra context"
msgstr "Comhthéacs breise leis"

msgid ""
"Often you need to present some extra information beyond that provided by the "
"generic view. For example, think of showing a list of all the books on each "
"publisher detail page. The :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` "
"generic view provides the publisher to the context, but how do we get "
"additional information in that template?"
msgstr ""
"Go minic ní mór duit roinnt faisnéise breise a chur i láthair seachas an rud "
"a sholáthraíonn an dearcadh cineálach. Mar shampla, smaoinigh ar liosta de "
"na leabhair go léir a thaispeáint ar leathanach mionsonraí gach "
"foilsitheora. Soláthraíonn amharc cineálach: Class: "
"`~django.views.generic.detail.detailView` don fhoilsitheoir don chomhthéacs, "
"ach conas a gheobhaidh muid faisnéis bhreise sa teimpléad sin?"

msgid ""
"The answer is to subclass :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` "
"and provide your own implementation of the ``get_context_data`` method. The "
"default implementation adds the object being displayed to the template, but "
"you can override it to send more::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an freagra ar subclass:class: `~django.views.generic.detail.detailView` "
"agus cuir do chur i bhfeidhm féin ar an modh ``get_context_data ``a "
"sholáthar. Cuireann an cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe an réad atá á "
"thaispeáint leis an teimpléad, ach is féidir leat é a shárú chun níos mó a "
"sheoladh:"

msgid ""
"Generally, ``get_context_data`` will merge the context data of all parent "
"classes with those of the current class. To preserve this behavior in your "
"own classes where you want to alter the context, you should be sure to call "
"``get_context_data`` on the super class. When no two classes try to define "
"the same key, this will give the expected results. However if any class "
"attempts to override a key after parent classes have set it (after the call "
"to super), any children of that class will also need to explicitly set it "
"after super if they want to be sure to override all parents. If you're "
"having trouble, review the method resolution order of your view."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, cumasóidh ``get_context_data ``sonraí comhthéacs gach rang "
"tuismitheora le sonraí an ranga reatha. Chun an t-iompar seo a chaomhnú i do "
"ranganna féin inar mian leat an comhthéacs a athrú, ba cheart duit a bheith "
"cinnte glaoch ar ``get_context_data ``ar an sár-rang. Nuair nach ndéanann "
"dhá rang iarracht an eochair chéanna a shainiú, tabharfaidh sé seo na "
"torthaí a bhfuil súil leo. Mar sin féin má dhéanann aon rang iarracht "
"eochair a shárú tar éis do ranganna tuismitheoirí é a shocrú (tar éis an "
"glao ar an sár-scoth), beidh ar aon pháistí den rang sin é a shocrú go "
"sainráite i ndiaidh an super más mian leo a bheith cinnte go gcuirfidh siad "
"gach tuismitheoir a shárú. Má tá trioblóid agat, déan athbhreithniú ar ord "
"réitigh modh do dhearcadh."

msgid ""
"Another consideration is that the context data from class-based generic "
"views will override data provided by context processors; "
"see :meth:`~django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.get_context_data` "
"for an example."
msgstr ""
"Breithniú eile is ea go gcuirfidh na sonraí comhthéacs ó thuairimí "
"cineálacha aicmbunaithe ar shárú sonraí a sholáthraíonn próiseálaithe "
"comhthéacs; féach:meth: "
"`~django.views.generic.detail.singleObjectMixin.get_context_data` mar "
"shampla."

msgid "Viewing subsets of objects"
msgstr "Ag féachaint ar fhothacair rudaí"

msgid ""
"Now let's take a closer look at the ``model`` argument we've been using all "
"along. The ``model`` argument, which specifies the database model that the "
"view will operate upon, is available on all the generic views that operate "
"on a single object or a collection of objects. However, the ``model`` "
"argument is not the only way to specify the objects that the view will "
"operate upon -- you can also specify the list of objects using the "
"``queryset`` argument::"
msgstr ""
"Anois déanaimis breathnú níos dlúithe ar an argóint ``samhail ``a bhí á "
"úsáid againn ar fad. Tá an argóint ``samhail ``, a shonraíonn an tsamhail "
"bunachar sonraí ar a oibreoidh an dearcadh air, ar fáil ar na tuairimí "
"cineálacha go léir a oibríonn ar réad amháin nó ar bhailiúchán rudaí. Mar "
"sin féin, ní hé an argóint ``samhail ``an t-aon bhealach chun na rudaí a "
"oibreoidh an dearcadh orthu a shonrú - is féidir leat liosta na rudaí a "
"shonrú ag baint úsáide as an argóint ``Queryset``:"

msgid ""
"Specifying ``model = Publisher`` is shorthand for saying ``queryset = "
"Publisher.objects.all()``. However, by using ``queryset`` to define a "
"filtered list of objects you can be more specific about the objects that "
"will be visible in the view (see :doc:`/topics/db/queries` for more "
"information about :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` objects, and see "
"the :doc:`class-based views reference </ref/class-based-views/index>` for "
"the complete details)."
msgstr ""
"Is gearrthéacs é ``model = Foilsitheoir ``a shonrú chun ``queryset = "
"Publisher.Objects.all ()`` a rá. Mar sin féin, trí úsáid a bhaint as "
"``queryset`` chun liosta scagtha rudaí a shainiú is féidir leat a bheith "
"níos sainiúla faoi na rudaí a bheidh le feiceáil sa radharc (féach: Doc: `/"
"topics/db/queries` le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise fao:class: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset` rudaí, agus féach an tagair:doc: `rang-"
"bhunaithe tuairim` le haghaidh na </ref/class-based-views/index> sonraí "
"iomlána)."

msgid ""
"To pick an example, we might want to order a list of books by publication "
"date, with the most recent first::"
msgstr ""
"Chun sampla a roghnú, b'fhéidir gur mhaith linn liosta leabhair a ordú de "
"réir dáta foilsithe, agus an chéad cheann is déanaí:"

msgid ""
"That's a pretty minimal example, but it illustrates the idea nicely. You'll "
"usually want to do more than just reorder objects. If you want to present a "
"list of books by a particular publisher, you can use the same technique::"
msgstr ""
"Is sampla beag go leor é sin, ach léiríonn sé an smaoineamh go deas. De "
"ghnáth beidh tú ag iarraidh níos mó a dhéanamh ná rudaí a athordú amháin. "
"Más mian leat liosta leabhair ag foilsitheoir áirithe a chur i láthair, is "
"féidir leat an teicníc chéanna a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"Notice that along with a filtered ``queryset``, we're also using a custom "
"template name. If we didn't, the generic view would use the same template as "
"the \"vanilla\" object list, which might not be what we want."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuilimid ag úsáid ainm teimpléad saincheaptha in "
"éineacht le ``queryset ``scagtha. Mura ndéanfaimis, úsáidfeadh an dearcadh "
"cineálach an teimpléad céanna leis an liosta réada “vanilla”, rud b'fhéidir "
"nach é an rud a theastaíonn uainn."

msgid ""
"Also notice that this isn't a very elegant way of doing publisher-specific "
"books. If we want to add another publisher page, we'd need another handful "
"of lines in the URLconf, and more than a few publishers would get "
"unreasonable. We'll deal with this problem in the next section."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin nach bealach an-galánta é seo chun leabhair a "
"bhaineann go sonrach don fhoilsitheoir a dhéanamh. Más mian linn leathanach "
"foilsitheora eile a chur leis, bheadh dornán línte eile ag teastáil uainn sa "
"URLConf, agus bheadh níos mó ná cúpla foilsitheoir míréasúnach. "
"Déileálfaimid leis an bhfadhb seo sa chéad chuid eile."

msgid ""
"If you get a 404 when requesting ``/books/acme/``, check to ensure you "
"actually have a Publisher with the name 'ACME Publishing'.  Generic views "
"have an ``allow_empty`` parameter for this case.  See the :doc:`class-based-"
"views reference</ref/class-based-views/index>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Má fhaigheann tú 404 agus tú ag iarraidh ``/leabhairs/acme/``, seiceáil le "
"cinntiú go bhfuil Foilsitheoir agat leis an ainm 'Foilsitheoireacht ACME' i "
"ndáiríre. Tá paraiméadar ``allow_empty`` ag tuairimí cineálacha don chás "
"seo. Féach an:doc: `class-based-viewce` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí</ref/"
"class-based-views/index>."

msgid "Dynamic filtering"
msgstr "Scagadh dinimiciúil"

msgid ""
"Another common need is to filter down the objects given in a list page by "
"some key in the URL. Earlier we hard-coded the publisher's name in the "
"URLconf, but what if we wanted to write a view that displayed all the books "
"by some arbitrary publisher?"
msgstr ""
"Riachtanas coitianta eile is ea na rudaí a thugtar i leathanach liosta a "
"scagadh de réir eochair éigin sa URL. Níos luaithe rinneamar ainm an "
"fhoilsitheora go crua-chódaithe sa URLConf, ach cad dá mbeadh muid ag "
"iarraidh dearcadh a scríobh a thaispeánann na leabhair go léir ag "
"foilsitheoir treallach éigin?"

msgid ""
"Handily, the ``ListView`` has "
"a :meth:`~django.views.generic.list.MultipleObjectMixin.get_queryset` method "
"we can override. By default, it returns the value of the ``queryset`` "
"attribute, but we can use it to add more logic."
msgstr ""
"Go háirithe, tá a: meth: "
"`~django.views.generic.list.multipleObjectMixin.get_querySet` modh is féidir "
"linn a shárú. De réir réamhshocraithe, filleann sé luach an tréith "
"``queryset ``, ach is féidir linn é a úsáid chun níos mó loighic a chur leis."

msgid ""
"The key part to making this work is that when class-based views are called, "
"various useful things are stored on ``self``; as well as the request "
"(``self.request``) this includes the positional (``self.args``) and name-"
"based (``self.kwargs``) arguments captured according to the URLconf."
msgstr ""
"Is é an phríomhchuid chun an obair seo a dhéanamh ná go stóráiltear rudaí "
"úsáideacha éagsúla ar `féin` nuair a thugtar tuairimí rang-bhunaithe; chomh "
"maith leis an iarratas (`self.request``) san áireamh seo argóintí seasmhacha "
"(`self.args``) agus ainmbunaithe (`self.kwargs``) a ghabhadh de réir an "
"URLConf."

msgid "Here, we have a URLconf with a single captured group::"
msgstr "Anseo, tá URLConf againn le grúpa gabhadh amháin::"

msgid "Next, we'll write the ``PublisherBookListView`` view itself::"
msgstr "Ansin, scríobhfaimid an radharc ``PublisherBookListView ``féin:"

msgid ""
"Using ``get_queryset`` to add logic to the queryset selection is as "
"convenient as it is powerful. For instance, if we wanted, we could use "
"``self.request.user`` to filter using the current user, or other more "
"complex logic."
msgstr ""
"Tá úsáid a bhaint as ``get_queryset`` chun loighic a chur leis an roghnú "
"cueryset chomh áisiúil agus atá sé cumhachtach. Mar shampla, dá dteastaíonn "
"uainn, d'fhéadfaimis ``self.request.user`` a úsáid chun scagadh ag baint "
"úsáide as an úsáideoir reatha, nó loighic níos casta eile."

msgid ""
"We can also add the publisher into the context at the same time, so we can "
"use it in the template::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir linn an foilsitheoir a chur isteach sa chomhthéacs ag an am "
"céanna, ionas gur féidir linn é a úsáid sa teimpléad:"

msgid "Performing extra work"
msgstr "Obair bhreise a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"The last common pattern we'll look at involves doing some extra work before "
"or after calling the generic view."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá i gceist leis an bpatrún coitianta deireanach a bhreathnóimid "
"air roinnt oibre breise a dhéanamh roimh nó tar éis glaoch ar an dear"

msgid ""
"Imagine we had a ``last_accessed`` field on our ``Author`` model that we "
"were using to keep track of the last time anybody looked at that author::"
msgstr ""
"Samhlaigh go raibh réimse ``las_accessed`` againn ar ár samhail ``Author ``a "
"bhí á úsáid againn chun súil a choinneáil ar an uair dheireanach a d'fhéach "
"duine ar bith ar an údar sin:"

msgid ""
"The generic ``DetailView`` class wouldn't know anything about this field, "
"but once again we could write a custom view to keep that field updated."
msgstr ""
"Ní bheadh aon rud ar eolas ag an rang cineálach ``DetailView ``faoin réimse "
"seo, ach arís d'fhéadfaimis dearcadh saincheaptha a scríobh chun an réimse "
