msgid "Conditional View Processing"
msgstr "Próiseáil Amharc Coinníoll"

msgid ""
"HTTP clients can send a number of headers to tell the server about copies of "
"a resource that they have already seen. This is commonly used when "
"retrieving a web page (using an HTTP ``GET`` request) to avoid sending all "
"the data for something the client has already retrieved. However, the same "
"headers can be used for all HTTP methods (``POST``, ``PUT``, ``DELETE``, "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le cliaint HTTP roinnt ceanntásca a sheoladh chun insint don "
"fhreastalaí faoi chóipeanna d'acmhainn a chonaic siad cheana féin. Úsáidtear "
"é seo go coitianta agus leathanach gréasáin á aisghabháil (ag baint úsáide "
"as iarratas HTTP ``GET ``) chun na sonraí go léir a sheachaint le haghaidh "
"rud atá aisghabháilte an cliant cheana féin. Mar sin féin, is féidir na "
"ceanntásca céanna a úsáid le haghaidh gach modh HTTP (`POST ``, `PUT``, "
"`DELETE``, srl.)."

msgid ""
"For each page (response) that Django sends back from a view, it might "
"provide two HTTP headers: the ``ETag`` header and the ``Last-Modified`` "
"header. These headers are optional on HTTP responses. They can be set by "
"your view function, or you can rely on "
"the :class:`~django.middleware.http.ConditionalGetMiddleware` middleware to "
"set the ``ETag`` header."
msgstr ""
"I gcás gach leathanach (freagra) a sheolann Django ar ais ó radharc, "
"d'fhéadfadh sé dhá cheannteideal HTTP a sholáthar: an ceannteideal ``Etag`` "
"agus an ceannteideal ```Last-Modified``. Tá na ceanntásca seo roghnach ar "
"fhreagairtí HTTP. Is féidir iad a shocrú le d'fheidhm amharc, nó is féidir "
"leat brath ar an: class: `~django.middleware.http.ConditionalGetMiddleware` "
"middleware chun an ceannteideal ``Etag`` a shocrú."

msgid ""
"When the client next requests the same resource, it might send along a "
"header such as either :rfc:`If-Modified-Since <9110#section-13.1.3>` "
"or :rfc:`If-Unmodified-Since <9110#section-13.1.4>`, containing the date of "
"the last modification time it was sent, or either :rfc:`If-Match "
"<9110#section-13.1.1>` or :rfc:`If-None-Match <9110#section-13.1.2>`, "
"containing the last ``ETag`` it was sent. If the current version of the page "
"matches the ``ETag`` sent by the client, or if the resource has not been "
"modified, a 304 status code can be sent back, instead of a full response, "
"telling the client that nothing has changed.  Depending on the header, if "
"the page has been modified or does not match the ``ETag`` sent by the "
"client, a 412 status code (Precondition Failed) may be returned."
msgstr ""
"<9110 #section -13.1.1> <9110 #section -13.1.2>Nuair a iarrann an cliant an "
"acmhainn chéanna eile, féadfaidh sé ceannteideal a sheoladh ar nós: rfc: `If-"
"Modified-Since` nó: rfc: `If-<9110 #section -13.1.3> Unmodified-Since`, ina "
"bhfuil <9110 #section -13.1.4> dáta an t-am modhnaithe deireanach a seoladh "
"é, nó fiú:rfc: `If-Match` nó:rfc: `If-None-Match`, ina raibh an `Etag`` "
"deireanach seoladh. Má mheaitseálann an leagan reatha den leathanach leis an "
"`Etag ``a sheol an cliant, nó mura modhnaíodh an acmhainn, is féidir cód "
"stádais 304 a sheoladh ar ais, in ionad freagra iomlán, ag insint don "
"chliant nach bhfuil aon rud athraithe. Ag brath ar an gceanntásc, má tá an "
"leathanach modhnaithe nó mura bhfuil an leathanach comhoiriúnach leis an "
"`Etag`` a sheol an cliant, féadfar cód stádais 412 (Réamhchoinníoll Theip) a "
"thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"When you need more fine-grained control you may use per-view conditional "
"processing functions."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a theastaíonn rialú níos mionghráite uait féadfaidh tú feidhmeanna "
"próiseála coinníollach in aghaidh amharc a úsáid."

msgid "The ``condition`` decorator"
msgstr "An maisitheoir ``coinníoll``"

msgid ""
"Sometimes (in fact, quite often) you can create functions to rapidly compute "
"the :rfc:`ETag <9110#section-8.8.3>` value or the last-modified time for a "
"resource, **without** needing to do all the computations needed to construct "
"the full view. Django can then use these functions to provide an \"early "
"bailout\" option for the view processing. Telling the client that the "
"content has not been modified since the last request, perhaps."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta (i ndáiríre, go minic) is féidir leat feidhmeanna a chruthú chun "
"an luach: rfc: `EtaG` <9110 #section -8.8.3> nó an t-am deireanach "
"modhnaithe d'acmhainn a ríomh go tapa, **gan gá duit na ríomhanna go léir a "
"theastaíonn chun an radharc iomlán a thógáil. Is féidir le Django na "
"feidhmeanna seo a úsáid ansin chun rogha “fóirithint luath” a sholáthar don "
"phróiseáil amharc. Ag rá leis an gcliant nár modhnaíodh an t-ábhar ón "
"iarratas deireanach, b'fhéidir."

msgid ""
"These two functions are passed as parameters to the "
"``django.views.decorators.http.condition`` decorator. This decorator uses "
"the two functions (you only need to supply one, if you can't compute both "
"quantities easily and quickly) to work out if the headers in the HTTP "
"request match those on the resource. If they don't match, a new copy of the "
"resource must be computed and your normal view is called."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an dá fheidhm seo ar aghaidh mar pharaiméadair chuig an maisitheoir "
"``django.views.decorators.http.condition`. Úsáideann an maisitheoir seo an "
"dá fheidhm (ní gá duit ach ceann amháin a sholáthar, mura féidir leat an dá "
"chainníocht a ríomh go héasca agus go tapa) chun oibriú amach má "
"mheaitseálann na ceannteidil san iarratas HTTP iad siúd ar an acmhainn. Mura "
"n-oireann siad, caithfear cóip nua den acmhainn a ríomh agus glaoch ar do "
"ghnáthradharc."

msgid "The ``condition`` decorator's signature looks like this::"
msgstr "Tá cuma seo ar shíniú an maisitheora ``coinníoll``:"

msgid ""
"The two functions, to compute the ETag and the last modified time, will be "
"passed the incoming ``request`` object and the same parameters, in the same "
"order, as the view function they are helping to wrap. The function passed "
"``last_modified_func`` should return a standard datetime value specifying "
"the last time the resource was modified, or ``None`` if the resource doesn't "
"exist. The function passed to the ``etag`` decorator should return a string "
"representing the :rfc:`ETag <9110#section-8.8.3>` for the resource, or "
"``None`` if it doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear an dá fheidhm, chun an eTag agus an t-am modhnaithe deireanach a "
"ríomh, ar an réad ``iarraidh` atá ag teacht isteach agus na paraiméadair "
"chéanna, san ord céanna, mar an fheidhm amharc atá á gcabhrú leo a "
"fhilleadh. Ba chóir don fheidhm a rith ``last_modified_func`` luach "
"caighdeánach dáta-ama a thabhairt ar ais ag sonrú an uair dheireanach a "
"mhodhnaíodh an acmhainn, nó ``None`` mura bhfuil an acmhainn ann. <9110 "
"#section -8.8.3>Ba chóir don fheidhm a chuirtear chuig an maisitheoir "
"``etag`` sreang a thabhairt ar ais a léiríonn na:rfc: `Etag` don acmhainn, "
"nó ``None ``mura bhfuil sé ann."

msgid ""
"The decorator sets the ``ETag`` and ``Last-Modified`` headers on the "
"response if they are not already set by the view and if the request's method "
"is safe (``GET`` or ``HEAD``)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an maisitheoir na ceannteidil ``Etag`` agus ``Last-Modified`` ar "
"an bhfreagra mura bhfuil siad socraithe ag an dearcadh cheana féin agus má "
"tá modh an iarratais sábháilte (`GET`` nó `HEAD``)."

msgid ""
"Using this feature usefully is probably best explained with an example. "
"Suppose you have this pair of models, representing a small blog system::"
msgstr ""
"Is dócha gur fearr a mhíniú le sampla an ghné seo a úsáid go húsáideach. "
"Cuir i gcás go bhfuil an péire samhlacha seo agat, a léiríonn córas blag "
"beag:"

msgid ""
"If the front page, displaying the latest blog entries, only changes when you "
"add a new blog entry, you can compute the last modified time very quickly. "
"You need the latest ``published`` date for every entry associated with that "
"blog. One way to do this would be::"
msgstr ""
"Mura n-athraíonn an leathanach tosaigh, ag taispeáint na hiontrálacha blag "
"is déanaí, ach nuair a chuireann tú iontráil nua blag leis, is féidir leat "
"an t-am deireanach modhnaithe a ríomh go han-tapa. Teastaíonn an dáta "
"``foilsithe ``is déanaí uait do gach iontráil a bhaineann leis an bhlag sin. "
"Bealach amháin chun é seo a dhéanamh ná:"

msgid ""
"You can then use this function to provide early detection of an unchanged "
"page for your front page view::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an fheidhm seo a úsáid ansin chun leathanach gan athrú a "
"bhrath go luath do d'amharc leathanaigh tosaigh:"

msgid "Be careful with the order of decorators"
msgstr "Bí cúramach le hord na mhaisitheoirí"

msgid ""
"When ``condition()`` returns a conditional response, any decorators below it "
"will be skipped and won't apply to the response. Therefore, any decorators "
"that need to apply to both the regular view response and a conditional "
"response must be above ``condition()``. In "
"particular, :func:`~django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_cookie`, :func:`~django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_headers`, "
"and :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control` should come first "
"because :rfc:`RFC 9110 <9110#section-15.4.5>` requires that the headers they "
"set be present on 304 responses."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a fhilleann ``coinníoll () `freagra coinníollach, scipeánfar aon "
"mhaisitheoirí faoin bhfois agus ní bheidh feidhm acu leis an bhfreagra. Dá "
"bhrí sin, caithfidh aon mhaisitheoirí a gcaithfidh iarratas a dhéanamh ar an "
"bhfreagra radharc rialta agus ar fhreagra coinníollach a bheith os cionn "
"``coinníoll () ``. <9110 #section -15.4.5>Go háirithe, ba chóir go "
"dtiocfadh :func: `~django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_cookie`, :func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.vary.vary_on_headers`, agus:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_control` toisc: `110RFC 'éilíonn sé go "
"mbeidh na ceanntásca a leagann siad i láthair ar 304 freagra."

msgid "Shortcuts for only computing one value"
msgstr "Aicearraí chun luach amháin a ríomh"

msgid ""
"As a general rule, if you can provide functions to compute *both* the ETag "
"and the last modified time, you should do so. You don't know which headers "
"any given HTTP client will send you, so be prepared to handle both. However, "
"sometimes only one value is easy to compute and Django provides decorators "
"that handle only ETag or only last-modified computations."
msgstr ""
"Mar riail ghinearálta, más féidir leat feidhmeanna a sholáthar chun * an "
"eTag agus an t-am deireanach modhnaithe a ríomh, ba cheart duit é sin a "
"dhéanamh. Níl a fhios agat cé na ceanntásca a sheolfaidh aon chliant HTTP ar "
"leith chugat, mar sin bí réidh chun an dá rud a láimhseáil. Mar sin féin, "
"uaireanta ní furasta ach luach amháin a ríomh agus soláthraíonn Django "
"maisiúcháin nach ndéanann ach eTag nó ríomhanna modhnaithe deiridh amháin."

msgid ""
"The ``django.views.decorators.http.etag`` and "
"``django.views.decorators.http.last_modified`` decorators are passed the "
"same type of functions as the ``condition`` decorator. Their signatures are::"
msgstr ""
"Rinne na maisitheoirí ``django.views.decorators.http.etag`` agus "
"``django.views.decorators.http.last_modified`` an cineál céanna feidhmeanna "
"leis an maisitheoir ``condition`. Is iad seo a gcuid sínithe:"

msgid ""
"We could write the earlier example, which only uses a last-modified "
"function, using one of these decorators::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfaimis an sampla níos luaithe a scríobh, nach n-úsáideann ach feidhm "
"modhnaithe deireanach, ag baint úsáide as ceann de na maisitheoirí seo:"

msgid "...or::"
msgstr "... nó::"

msgid "Use ``condition`` when testing both conditions"
msgstr "Úsáid ``coinníoll`` agus an dá choinníoll á thástáil"

msgid ""
"It might look nicer to some people to try and chain the ``etag`` and "
"``last_modified`` decorators if you want to test both preconditions. "
"However, this would lead to incorrect behavior."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cuma níos deise ag daoine áirithe triail a bhaint as "
"na maisitheoirí ``etag`` agus `last_modified` a shlánú más mian leat an dá "
"réamhchoinníoll a thástáil. Mar sin féin, bheadh iompar mícheart mar thoradh "
"air seo."

msgid ""
"The first decorator doesn't know anything about the second and might answer "
"that the response is not modified even if the second decorators would "
"determine otherwise. The ``condition`` decorator uses both callback "
"functions simultaneously to work out the right action to take."
msgstr ""
"Níl a fhios ag an gcéad maisitheoir aon rud faoin dara ceann agus "
"d'fhéadfadh sé freagra a thabhairt nach ndéantar an freagra a mhodhnú fiú má "
"chinnfeadh an dara maisitheoirí a mhalairt. Úsáideann an maisitheoir "
"``coinníoll`` an dá fheidhm aisghlaonna ag an am céanna chun an gníomh ceart "
"atá le déanamh a oibriú amach."

msgid "Using the decorators with other HTTP methods"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as na maisitheoirí le modhanna HTTP eile"

msgid ""
"The ``condition`` decorator is useful for more than only ``GET`` and "
"``HEAD`` requests (``HEAD`` requests are the same as ``GET`` in this "
"situation). It can also be used to provide checking for ``POST``, ``PUT`` "
"and ``DELETE`` requests. In these situations, the idea isn't to return a "
"\"not modified\" response, but to tell the client that the resource they are "
"trying to change has been altered in the meantime."
msgstr ""
"Tá an maisitheoir ``coinníoll`` úsáideach le haghaidh níos mó ná iarratais "
"``GET`` agus `HEAD`` amháin (tá iarratais ``HEAD`` mar an gcéanna le ``GET`` "
"sa chás seo). Is féidir é a úsáid freisin chun seiceáil a sholáthar "
"d'iarratais ``POST ``, `PUT`` agus ``DELETE``. Sna cásanna seo, ní é an "
"smaoineamh freagra “neamh-mhodhnaithe” a thabhairt ar ais, ach a rá don "
"chliant gur athraíodh an acmhainn atá siad ag iarraidh a athrú idir an dá "
"linn."

msgid ""
"For example, consider the following exchange between the client and server:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, smaoinigh ar an malartú seo a leanas idir an cliant agus an "
"freastalaí:"

msgid "Client requests ``/foo/``."
msgstr "Iarratann cliant ``/foo/``."

msgid "Server responds with some content with an ETag of ``\"abcd1234\"``."
msgstr "Freagraíonn freastalaí le ábhar áirithe le ETag de ``\"abcd1234\"`."

msgid ""
"Client sends an HTTP ``PUT`` request to ``/foo/`` to update the resource. It "
"also sends an ``If-Match: \"abcd1234\"`` header to specify the version it is "
"trying to update."
msgstr ""
"Seolann cliant iarratas HTTP ``PUT`` chuig ``/foo/`` chun an acmhainn a "
"nuashonrú. Seolann sé ceanntásc ``If-Match: “abcd1234\" ``freisin chun an "
"leagan atá á iarraidh a nuashonrú a shonrú."

msgid ""
"Server checks to see if the resource has changed, by computing the ETag the "
"same way it does for a ``GET`` request (using the same function). If the "
"resource *has* changed, it will return a 412 status code, meaning "
"\"precondition failed\"."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann freastalaí chun a fháil amach an bhfuil an acmhainn athraithe, "
"tríd an eTag a ríomh ar an mbealach céanna a dhéanann sé d'iarratas ``GET "
"``(ag baint úsáide as an bhfeidhm chéanna). Má athraíodh an acmhainne**, "
"cuirfidh sé cód stádais 412 ar ais, rud a chiallaíonn “theip ar "
"réamhchoinníoll”."

msgid ""
"Client sends a ``GET`` request to ``/foo/``, after receiving a 412 response, "
"to retrieve an updated version of the content before updating it."
msgstr ""
"Seolann an cliant iarratas ``GET ``chuig `/foo/``, tar éis freagra 412 a "
"fháil, leagan nuashonraithe den ábhar a aisghabháil sula ndéantar é a "
"nuashonrú."

msgid ""
"The important thing this example shows is that the same functions can be "
"used to compute the ETag and last modification values in all situations. In "
"fact, you **should** use the same functions, so that the same values are "
"returned every time."
msgstr ""
"Is é an rud tábhachtach a thaispeánann an sampla seo ná gur féidir na "
"feidhmeanna céanna a úsáid chun luachanna eTag agus modhnú deireanacha a "
"ríomh i ngach cás. Déanta na fírinne, ba cheart duit** na feidhmeanna céanna "
"a úsáid, ionas go gcuirfear na luachanna céanna ar ais gach uair."

msgid "Validator headers with non-safe request methods"
msgstr "Ceanntásca bailíochtaithe le modhanna iarratais neamhshábhá"

msgid ""
"The ``condition`` decorator only sets validator headers (``ETag`` and ``Last-"
"Modified``) for safe HTTP methods, i.e. ``GET`` and ``HEAD``. If you wish to "
"return them in other cases, set them in your view. "
"See :rfc:`9110#section-9.3.4` to learn about the distinction between setting "
"a validator header in response to requests made with ``PUT`` versus ``POST``."
msgstr ""
"Ní shocraíonn an maisitheoir ``coinníoll`` ach ceannteidil bailíochtaithe "
"(``Etag`` agus ``Last-Modified``) le haghaidh modhanna HTTP sábháilte, ie "
"``GET`` agus ``HEAD``. Más mian leat iad a thabhairt ar ais i gcásanna eile, "
"socraigh iad i do thuairim. Féach: RFC: `9110 #section -9.3.4` chun foghlaim "
"faoin idirdhealú idir ceanntásc bailíochtaithe a shocrú mar fhreagra ar "
"iarratais a rinneadh le `PUT`` i gcoinne ``POST ``."

msgid "Comparison with middleware conditional processing"
msgstr "Comparáid le próiseáil choinníollach middleware"

msgid ""
"Django provides conditional ``GET`` handling "
"via :class:`django.middleware.http.ConditionalGetMiddleware`. While being "
"suitable for many situations, the middleware has limitations for advanced "
"usage:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django láimhseáil coinníollach ``GET`` via: class: "
"`django.middleware.http.conditionalGetMiddleware`. Cé go bhfuil sé oiriúnach "
"do go leor cásanna, tá teorainneacha ag an middleware maidir le hardúsáid:"

msgid "It's applied globally to all views in your project."
msgstr "Cuirtear i bhfeidhm go domhanda ar gach tuairim i do thionscadal."

msgid ""
"It doesn't save you from generating the response, which may be expensive."
msgstr ""
"Ní shábhálann sé tú ón bhfreagra a ghiniúint, rud a d'fhéadfadh a bheith "
"daor."

msgid "It's only appropriate for HTTP ``GET`` requests."
msgstr "Níl sé oiriúnach ach le haghaidh iarratais HTTP ``GET``."

msgid ""
"You should choose the most appropriate tool for your particular problem "
"here. If you have a way to compute ETags and modification times quickly and "
"if some view takes a while to generate the content, you should consider "
"using the ``condition`` decorator described in this document. If everything "
"already runs fairly quickly, stick to using the middleware and the amount of "
"network traffic sent back to the clients will still be reduced if the view "
"hasn't changed."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit an uirlis is oiriúnaí a roghnú do d'fhadhb ar leith anseo. Má "
"tá bealach agat chun eTags agus amanna modhnaithe a ríomh go tapa agus má "
"thógann dearcadh éigin tamall an t-ábhar a ghiniúint, ba cheart duit "
"smaoineamh ar an maisitheoir ``coinníoll`` a thuairiscítear sa doiciméad seo "
"a úsáid. Má ritheann gach rud go gasta cheana féin, cloí leis an meán-earraí "
"a úsáid agus laghdófar méid tráchta líonra a sheoltar ar ais chuig na "
"cliaint fós mura bhfuil an dearcadh athraithe."

msgid "Aggregation"
msgstr "Comhiomlánú"

msgid ""
"The topic guide on :doc:`Django's database-abstraction API </topics/db/"
"queries>` described the way that you can use Django queries that create, "
"retrieve, update and delete individual objects. However, sometimes you will "
"need to retrieve values that are derived by summarizing or *aggregating* a "
"collection of objects. This topic guide describes the ways that aggregate "
"values can be generated and returned using Django queries."
msgstr ""
"Chuir an treoir ábhair ar:doc: `API teastarbhaithe bunachar sonraí Django` "
"síos ar an mbealach is féidir leat ceisteanna Django a úsáid a chruthaíonn, "
"a aisghabhann, a nuashon</topics/db/queries> rú agus a scriosann rudaí "
"aonair. Mar sin féin, uaireanta beidh ort luachanna a dhíorthaítear a "
"aisghabháil trí bhailiúchán rudaí a achoimriú nó *a chomhthóiriú*. Déanann "
"an treoir ábhair seo cur síos ar na bealaí is féidir luachanna comhiomlána a "
"ghiniúint agus a thabhairt ar ais ag baint"

msgid ""
"Throughout this guide, we'll refer to the following models. These models are "
"used to track the inventory for a series of online bookstores:"
msgstr ""
"Le linn na treoir seo, déanfaimid tagairt do na samhlacha seo a leanas. "
"Úsáidtear na samhlacha seo chun an fardal do shraith siopaí leabhar ar líne "
"a rianú:"

msgid "Cheat sheet"
msgstr "Bileog cheat"

msgid ""
"In a hurry? Here's how to do common aggregate queries, assuming the models "
"above:"
msgstr ""
"Ar deifir? Seo conas ceisteanna comhiomlán coitianta a dhéanamh, ag glacadh "
"leis na samhlacha thuas:"

msgid "Generating aggregates over a ``QuerySet``"
msgstr "Comhiomlánacha a ghiniúint thar ``QuerySet``"

msgid ""
"Django provides two ways to generate aggregates. The first way is to "
"generate summary values over an entire ``QuerySet``. For example, say you "
"wanted to calculate the average price of all books available for sale. "
"Django's query syntax provides a means for describing the set of all books:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django dhá bhealach chun comhiomlán a ghiniúint. Is é an chéad "
"bhealach ná luachanna achoimre a ghiniúint thar ``QuerySet ``iomlán. Mar "
"shampla, abair gur mhaith leat meánphraghas na leabhar go léir atá ar fáil "
"le díol a ríomh. Soláthraíonn comhréir fiosrúcháin Django bealach chun cur "
"síos a dhéanamh ar shraith na leabhar go léir:"

msgid ""
"What we need is a way to calculate summary values over the objects that "
"belong to this ``QuerySet``. This is done by appending an ``aggregate()`` "
"clause onto the ``QuerySet``:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an rud a theastaíonn uainn ná bealach chun luachanna achoimre a ríomh "
"thar na rudaí a bhaineann leis an ``QuerySet` seo. Déantar é seo trí chlásal "
"``comhiomlán () ``a chur leis an ``QuerySet``:"

msgid ""
"The ``all()`` is redundant in this example, so this could be simplified to:"
msgstr ""
"Tá an ``all () ``iomarcach sa sampla seo, mar sin d'fhéadfaí é seo a "
"shimpliú go:"

msgid ""
"The argument to the ``aggregate()`` clause describes the aggregate value "
"that we want to compute - in this case, the average of the ``price`` field "
"on the ``Book`` model. A list of the aggregate functions that are available "
"can be found in the :ref:`QuerySet reference <aggregation-functions>`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an argóint leis an gclásal ``comhiomlán () ``cur síos ar an luach "
"comhiomlán a theastaíonn uainn a ríomh - sa chás seo, meán an réimse "
"``praghas`` ar an tsamhail ``Leabhar``. <aggregation-functions>Is féidir "
"liosta de na feidhmeanna comhiomlána atá ar fáil a fháil in:ref: `QuerySet "
"tagairt `."

msgid ""
"``aggregate()`` is a terminal clause for a ``QuerySet`` that, when invoked, "
"returns a dictionary of name-value pairs. The name is an identifier for the "
"aggregate value; the value is the computed aggregate. The name is "
"automatically generated from the name of the field and the aggregate "
"function. If you want to manually specify a name for the aggregate value, "
"you can do so by providing that name when you specify the aggregate clause:"
msgstr ""
"Is clásal teirminéil é ``comhiomlán () ``do `QuerySet`` a thugann foclóir de "
"phéirí ainmluacha ar ais, nuair a ghairmtear é. Is aitheantóir é an t-ainm "
"don luach comhiomlán; is é an luach an comhiomlán ríomhaithe. Gintear an t-"
"ainm go huathoibríoch ó ainm an réimse agus ón bhfeidhm chomhiomlán. Más "
"mian leat ainm a shonrú de láimh don luach comhiomlán, is féidir leat é sin "
"a dhéanamh tríd an ainm sin a sholáthar nuair a shonraíonn tú an clásal "
"comhiomlán:"

msgid ""
"If you want to generate more than one aggregate, you add another argument to "
"the ``aggregate()`` clause. So, if we also wanted to know the maximum and "
"minimum price of all books, we would issue the query:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat níos mó ná comhiomlán amháin a ghiniúint, cuireann tú argóint "
"eile leis an gclásal ``comhiomlán () ``. Mar sin, dá mbeimis ag iarraidh "
"uasphraghas agus íosta na leabhar go léir a fháil amach, eisíomar an cheist:"

msgid "Generating aggregates for each item in a ``QuerySet``"
msgstr "Comhiomlánacha a ghiniúint do gach mír i ``QuerySet``"

msgid ""
"The second way to generate summary values is to generate an independent "
"summary for each object in a :class:`.QuerySet`. For example, if you are "
"retrieving a list of books, you may want to know how many authors "
"contributed to each book. Each Book has a many-to-many relationship with the "
"Author; we want to summarize this relationship for each book in the "
"``QuerySet``."
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara bealach chun luachanna achoimre a ghiniúint ná achoimre "
"neamhspleách a ghiniúint do gach réad in a:class: `.QuerySet`. Mar shampla, "
"má tá liosta leabhair á aisghabháil agat, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat a fháil "
"amach cé mhéad údar a chuir le gach leabhar. Tá caidreamh go leor ag gach "
"Leabhar leis an Údar; ba mhaith linn achoimre a dhéanamh ar an gcaidreamh "
"seo do gach leabhar sa ``QuerySet``."

msgid ""
"Per-object summaries can be generated using the :meth:`~.QuerySet.annotate` "
"clause. When an ``annotate()`` clause is specified, each object in the "
"``QuerySet`` will be annotated with the specified values."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir achoimrí in aghaidh an rud a ghiniúint ag baint úsáide as an "
"gclásal: meth: `~.queryset.annotate`. Nuair a shonraítear clásal ``annotate "
"() ``, déanfar anótáil ar gach réad sa ``QuerySet` leis na luachanna "
"sonraithe."

msgid ""
"The syntax for these annotations is identical to that used for "
"the :meth:`~.QuerySet.aggregate` clause. Each argument to ``annotate()`` "
"describes an aggregate that is to be calculated. For example, to annotate "
"books with the number of authors:"
msgstr ""
"Tá comhréir na n-anótaí seo comhionann leis an gclásal: meth: "
"`~.queryset.aggregate`. Déanann gach argóint le ``annotate () ``cur síos ar "
"chomhiomlán atá le ríomh. Mar shampla, chun leabhair a anótáil le líon na n-"
"údar:"

msgid ""
"As with ``aggregate()``, the name for the annotation is automatically "
"derived from the name of the aggregate function and the name of the field "
"being aggregated. You can override this default name by providing an alias "
"when you specify the annotation:"
msgstr ""
"Mar is amhlaidh le ``comhiomlán () ``, díorthaítear an t-ainm don anótáil go "
"huathoibríoch ó ainm na feidhme comhiomlán agus ainm an réimse atá á "
"chomhiomlánú. Is féidir leat an t-ainm réamhshocraithe seo a shárú trí ainm "
"a sholáthar nuair a shonraíonn tú an t-anótáil:"

msgid ""
"Unlike ``aggregate()``, ``annotate()`` is *not* a terminal clause. The "
"output of the ``annotate()`` clause is a ``QuerySet``; this ``QuerySet`` can "
"be modified using any other ``QuerySet`` operation, including ``filter()``, "
"``order_by()``, or even additional calls to ``annotate()``."
msgstr ""
"Murab ionann agus ``comhiomlán () ``, `annotate ()`` is clásal teirminéil "
"*ní*. Is é ``QuerySet`` aschur an chlásal ``annotate () ``; is féidir an "
"`QuerySet`` seo a mhodhnú ag baint úsáide as aon oibríocht ``QuerySet`` "
"eile, lena n-áirítear ``filter ()``, `ord_by () ``, nó fiú glaonna breise "
"chuig ``annotate ()``."

msgid "Combining multiple aggregations"
msgstr "Comhiomlánú iolracha a chur"

msgid ""
"Combining multiple aggregations with ``annotate()`` will :ticket:`yield the "
"wrong results <10060>` because joins are used instead of subqueries:"
msgstr ""
"<10060>Comhiomlánú iolracha a chomhcheangal le ``annotate () ``beidh: "
"ticket: `na torthaí míchearta mar úsáidtear comhpháirteanna in ionad fo-"
"cheisteanna:"

msgid ""
"For most aggregates, there is no way to avoid this problem, however, "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.Count` aggregate has a ``distinct`` parameter "
"that may help:"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le formhór na gcomhiomlánaithe, níl aon bhealach ann chun an fhadhb "
"seo a sheachaint, áfach, tá paraiméadar ``difriúil ``ag comhiomlán:class: "
"`~django.db.models.count` a d'fhéadfadh cabhrú le:"

msgid "If in doubt, inspect the SQL query!"
msgstr "Má tá amhras ort, déan iniúchadh ar an gceist SQL!"

msgid ""
"In order to understand what happens in your query, consider inspecting the "
"``query`` property of your ``QuerySet``."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn tuiscint a fháil ar cad a tharlaíonn i d'fhiosrúchán, smaoinigh ar "
"mhaoin ``fiosraithe`` de do `QuerySet` a iniúchadh."

msgid "Joins and aggregates"
msgstr "Comhcheangail agus comhiomlánaithe"

msgid ""
"So far, we have dealt with aggregates over fields that belong to the model "
"being queried. However, sometimes the value you want to aggregate will "
"belong to a model that is related to the model you are querying."
msgstr ""
"Go dtí seo, déileálamar le comhiomlánaithe thar réimsí a bhaineann leis an "
"tsamhail atá á cheistiú. Mar sin féin, uaireanta bainfidh an luach a "
"theastaíonn uait a chomhiomlánú le samhail a bhaineann leis an tsamhail atá "
"á fhiosrú agat."

msgid ""
"When specifying the field to be aggregated in an aggregate function, Django "
"will allow you to use the same :ref:`double underscore notation <field-"
"lookups-intro>` that is used when referring to related fields in filters. "
"Django will then handle any table joins that are required to retrieve and "
"aggregate the related value."
msgstr ""
"Agus an réimse atá le comhiomlánú a shonrú i bhfeidhm chomhiomlán, ligfidh "
"Django duit an chéanna a úsáid: ref: `notáil béim dúbailte <field-lookups-"
"intro>`a úsáidtear agus tú ag tagairt do réimsí gaolmhara i scagairí. "
"Déanfaidh Django ansin láimhseáil le haon chomhcheangail tábla atá ag "
"teastáil chun an luach gaolmhar a aisghabháil"

msgid ""
"For example, to find the price range of books offered in each store, you "
"could use the annotation:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun raon praghsanna na leabhar a thairgtear i ngach siopa a "
"fháil, d'fhéadfá an anótáil a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"This tells Django to retrieve the ``Store`` model, join (through the many-to-"
"many relationship) with the ``Book`` model, and aggregate on the price field "
"of the book model to produce a minimum and maximum value."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé seo do Django an tsamhail ``Store`` a aisghabháil, páirt a "
"ghlacadh (tríd an gcaidreamh go leor) leis an tsamhail ``Leabhar ``, agus "
"comhiomlánú ar réimse praghsanna an tsamhail leabhar chun luach íosta agus "
"uasta a tháirgeadh."

msgid ""
"The same rules apply to the ``aggregate()`` clause. If you wanted to know "
"the lowest and highest price of any book that is available for sale in any "
"of the stores, you could use the aggregate:"
msgstr ""
"Tá feidhm ag na rialacha céanna maidir leis an gclásal ``comhiomlán () ``. "
"Dá dteastaíonn uait an praghas is ísle agus is airde d'aon leabhar atá ar "
"fáil le díol in aon cheann de na siopaí a fháil, d'fhéadfá an comhiomlán a "
"úsáid:"

msgid ""
"Join chains can be as deep as you require. For example, to extract the age "
"of the youngest author of any book available for sale, you could issue the "
"query:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le slabhraí a bheith chomh domhain agus is gá duit. Mar shampla, "
"chun aois an údair is óige d'aon leabhar atá ar fáil le díol a bhaint, "
"d'fhéadfá an cheist a eisiúint:"

msgid "Following relationships backwards"
msgstr "Ag leanúint caidrimh ar ais"

msgid ""
"In a way similar to :ref:`lookups-that-span-relationships`, aggregations and "
"annotations on fields of models or models that are related to the one you "
"are querying can include traversing \"reverse\" relationships. The lowercase "
"name of related models and double-underscores are used here too."
msgstr ""
"Ar bhealach cosúil le:ref: `lookups-that-span-reachships`, is féidir le "
"comhiomlánú agus anótaí ar réimsí samhlacha nó samhlacha a bhaineann leis an "
"gceann atá á fhiosrú agat caidrimh “droim” a bheith san áireamh. Úsáidtear "
"ainm beaga samhlacha gaolmhara agus béim dhúbailte anseo freisin."

msgid ""
"For example, we can ask for all publishers, annotated with their respective "
"total book stock counters (note how we use ``'book'`` to specify the "
"``Publisher`` -> ``Book`` reverse foreign key hop):"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, is féidir linn iarraidh ar gach foilsitheoir, a bhfuil anótáil "
"acu lena gcuntair stoc leabhar iomlána faoi seach (tabhair faoi deara conas "
"a úsáidimid ```leabhar`` chun an ``Foilsitheoir ``-> `Leabhar`` eochair "
"eachtrach droim a shonrú):"

msgid ""
"(Every ``Publisher`` in the resulting ``QuerySet`` will have an extra "
"attribute called ``book__count``.)"
msgstr ""
"(Beidh tréith bhreise ar a dtugtar ``book__count`` ag gach `Foilsitheoir "
"``sa `QuerySet`` mar thoradh air.)"

msgid ""
"We can also ask for the oldest book of any of those managed by every "
"publisher:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir linn an leabhar is sine a iarraidh freisin d'aon cheann de na cinn "
"atá á mbainistiú ag gach foilsitheoir:"

msgid ""
"(The resulting dictionary will have a key called ``'oldest_pubdate'``. If no "
"such alias were specified, it would be the rather long "
"``'book__pubdate__min'``.)"
msgstr ""
"(Beidh eochair ar a dtugtar ``'oldest_pubdate'`` ag an bhfoclóir mar thoradh "
"air. Mura ndéanfaí aon ainm den sórt sin a shonrú, bheadh sé an "
"``book__pubdate__min'`` sách fada.)"

msgid ""
"This doesn't apply just to foreign keys. It also works with many-to-many "
"relations. For example, we can ask for every author, annotated with the "
"total number of pages considering all the books the author has (co-)authored "
"(note how we use ``'book'`` to specify the ``Author`` -> ``Book`` reverse "
"many-to-many hop):"
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann sé seo ach le heochracha eachtracha. Oibríonn sé freisin le "
"caidreamh go leor. Mar shampla, is féidir linn gach údar a iarraidh, "
"anótáilte le líon iomlán na leathanaigh ag smaoineamh ar na leabhair go léir "
"atá (co-) údar an t-údar (tabhair faoi deara conas a úsáidimid ```leabhar`` "
"chun an ``Údar`` -> `Leabhar`` a shonrú go leor hop):"

msgid ""
"(Every ``Author`` in the resulting ``QuerySet`` will have an extra attribute "
"called ``total_pages``. If no such alias were specified, it would be the "
"rather long ``book__pages__sum``.)"
msgstr ""
"(Beidh tréith bhreise ar a dtugtar ``total_pages`` ag gach ``Údar`` sa "
"`QuerySet`` mar thoradh air. Mura ndéanfaí aon ainm den sórt sin a shonrú, "
"bheadh sé an `book__pages__sum ``sách fada.)"

msgid ""
"Or ask for the average rating of all the books written by author(s) we have "
"on file:"
msgstr ""
"Nó iarr meánrátáil na leabhar go léir atá scríofa ag údar (í) atá againn ar "
"chomhad:"

msgid ""
"(The resulting dictionary will have a key called ``'average_rating'``. If no "
"such alias were specified, it would be the rather long "
"``'book__rating__avg'``.)"
msgstr ""
"(Beidh eochair ar a dtugtar ``'average_rating'`` ag an bhfoclóir mar thoradh "
"air. Mura ndéanfaí aon ainm den sórt sin a shonrú, bheadh sé an "
"``book__rating__avg'`` sách fada.)"

msgid "Aggregations and other ``QuerySet`` clauses"
msgstr "Comhiomlánú agus clásail eile ``QuerySet`"

msgid "``filter()`` and ``exclude()``"
msgstr "``scagaire () ``agus ``eisiamh ()``"

msgid ""
"Aggregates can also participate in filters. Any ``filter()`` (or "
"``exclude()``) applied to normal model fields will have the effect of "
"constraining the objects that are considered for aggregation."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le comhiomlán páirt a ghlacadh i scagairí Beidh éifeacht ag aon "
"``scagaire () ``(nó ``eisiamh ()``) a chuirtear i bhfeidhm ar ghnáthréimsí "
"samhlacha srian ar na rudaí a mheastar lena chomhiomlánú."

msgid ""
"When used with an ``annotate()`` clause, a filter has the effect of "
"constraining the objects for which an annotation is calculated. For example, "
"you can generate an annotated list of all books that have a title starting "
"with \"Django\" using the query:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear é le clásal ``annotate () `, tá éifeacht ag scagaire srian "
"ar na rudaí a ríomhtar anótáil dóibh. Mar shampla, is féidir leat liosta "
"anótaithe a ghiniúint de na leabhair go léir a bhfuil teideal acu ag tosú le "
"“Django” ag baint úsáide as an bhfiosrú:"

msgid ""
"When used with an ``aggregate()`` clause, a filter has the effect of "
"constraining the objects over which the aggregate is calculated. For "
"example, you can generate the average price of all books with a title that "
"starts with \"Django\" using the query:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear é le clásal ``comhiomlán () ``, tá éifeacht ag scagaire "
"srian ar na rudaí a ríomhtar an comhiomlán orthu. Mar shampla, is féidir "
"leat meánphraghas gach leabhar a ghiniúint le teideal a thosaíonn le "
"“Django” ag baint úsáide as an gceist:"

msgid "Filtering on annotations"
msgstr "Scagadh ar anótaí"

msgid ""
"Annotated values can also be filtered. The alias for the annotation can be "
"used in ``filter()`` and ``exclude()`` clauses in the same way as any other "
"model field."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir luachanna anótaithe a scagadh freisin. Is féidir an t-ailias don "
"anótáil a úsáid i gclásail ``scagaire () ``agus ``eisiamh ()`` ar an "
"mbealach céanna le haon réimse samhail eile."

msgid ""
"For example, to generate a list of books that have more than one author, you "
"can issue the query:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun liosta leabhair a ghiniúint a bhfuil níos mó ná údar "
"amháin acu, is féidir leat an cheist a eisiúint:"

msgid ""
"This query generates an annotated result set, and then generates a filter "
"based upon that annotation."
msgstr ""
"Gineann an cheist seo tacar torthaí anótaithe, agus ansin gineann sé "
"scagaire bunaithe ar an anótáil sin."

msgid ""
"If you need two annotations with two separate filters you can use the "
"``filter`` argument with any aggregate. For example, to generate a list of "
"authors with a count of highly rated books:"
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn dhá anótáil uait le dhá scagaire ar leithligh is féidir leat "
"an argóint ``scagair`` a úsáid le haon chomhiomlán. Mar shampla, chun liosta "
"údair a ghiniúint le líon leabhair ardrátáilte:"

msgid ""
"Each ``Author`` in the result set will have the ``num_books`` and "
"``highly_rated_books`` attributes. See also :ref:`conditional-aggregation`."
msgstr ""
"Beidh na tréithe ``num_books`` agus ``highly_rated_books`` ag gach ``Údar`` "
"sa tacar torthaí. Féach freis:ref: `comhiomlánú coinníollach`."

msgid "Choosing between ``filter`` and ``QuerySet.filter()``"
msgstr "Roghnú idir ``filter`` agus ``QuerySet.Filter () ``"

msgid ""
"Avoid using the ``filter`` argument with a single annotation or aggregation. "
"It's more efficient to use ``QuerySet.filter()`` to exclude rows. The "
"aggregation ``filter`` argument is only useful when using two or more "
"aggregations over the same relations with different conditionals."
msgstr ""
"Seachain an argóint ``scagair`` a úsáid le anótáil nó comhiomlánú amháin. Tá "
"sé níos éifeachtaí ``QuerySet.filter () ``a úsáid chun sraitheanna a "
"eisiamh. Níl an argóint comhiomlánaithe ``scagair`` úsáideach ach amháin "
"nuair a úsáidtear dhá chomhiomlánú nó níos mó thar an gcaidreamh céanna le "
"coinníollacha éagsúla."

msgid "Order of ``annotate()`` and ``filter()`` clauses"
msgstr "Ordú clásail ``anótáit () ``agus ``scagaire ()``"

msgid ""
"When developing a complex query that involves both ``annotate()`` and "
"``filter()`` clauses, pay particular attention to the order in which the "
"clauses are applied to the ``QuerySet``."
msgstr ""
"Agus ceist casta á fhorbairt ina mbaineann clásail ``annotate () ``agus "
"`scagaire ()`` araon, tabhair aird ar leith ar an ord ina gcuirtear na "
"clásail i bhfeidhm ar an ``QuerySet``."

msgid ""
"When an ``annotate()`` clause is applied to a query, the annotation is "
"computed over the state of the query up to the point where the annotation is "
"requested. The practical implication of this is that ``filter()`` and "
"``annotate()`` are not commutative operations."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuirtear clásal ``annotate () ``i bhfeidhm ar cheist, ríomhtar an t-"
"anótáil thar staid na fiosrúcháin suas go dtí an pointe ina n-iarrtar an t-"
"anótáil. Is é an tionchar praiticiúil a bhaineann leis seo nach oibríochtaí "
"comutaitheacha iad ``filter () ``agus ``annotate ()``."

msgid "Given:"
msgstr "A thugtar:"

msgid "Publisher A has two books with ratings 4 and 5."
msgstr "Tá dhá leabhar ag Foilsitheoir A le rátálacha 4 agus 5."

msgid "Publisher B has two books with ratings 1 and 4."
msgstr "Tá dhá leabhar ag Foilsitheoir B le rátálacha 1 agus 4."

msgid "Publisher C has one book with rating 1."
msgstr "Tá leabhar amháin ag Foilsitheoir C le rátáil 1."

msgid "Here's an example with the ``Count`` aggregate:"
msgstr "Seo sampla leis an comhiomlán ``Count``:"

msgid ""
"Both queries return a list of publishers that have at least one book with a "
"rating exceeding 3.0, hence publisher C is excluded."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an dá cheist liosta foilsitheoirí a bhfuil leabhar amháin ar a laghad "
"acu le rátáil níos mó ná 3.0, dá bhrí sin tá foilsitheoir C eisiata."

msgid ""
"In the first query, the annotation precedes the filter, so the filter has no "
"effect on the annotation. ``distinct=True`` is required to avoid "
"a :ref:`query bug <combining-multiple-aggregations>`."
msgstr ""
"Sa chéad cheist, bíonn an anótáil roimh an scagaire, mar sin níl aon "
"éifeacht ag an scagaire ar an anótáil. <combining-multiple-"
"aggregations>Teastaíonn ``Distinct=True`` chun a:ref: `fabht ceiste`` a "
"sheachaint."

msgid ""
"The second query counts the number of books that have a rating exceeding 3.0 "
"for each publisher. The filter precedes the annotation, so the filter "
"constrains the objects considered when calculating the annotation."
msgstr ""
"Áireamh sa dara ceist líon na leabhar a bhfuil rátáil níos mó ná 3.0 acu do "
"gach foilsitheoir. Tá an scagaire roimh an anótáil, mar sin cuireann an "
"scagaire srian ar na rudaí a mheastar agus an anótáil á ríomh."

msgid "Here's another example with the ``Avg`` aggregate:"
msgstr "Seo sampla eile leis an comhiomlán ``Avg``:"

msgid ""
"The first query asks for the average rating of all a publisher's books for "
"publisher's that have at least one book with a rating exceeding 3.0. The "
"second query asks for the average of a publisher's book's ratings for only "
"those ratings exceeding 3.0."
msgstr ""
"Iarrann an chéad cheist meán-rátáil leabhair uile foilsitheora do "
"fhoilsitheoirí a bhfuil leabhar amháin ar a laghad acu le rátáil níos mó ná "
"3.0. Iarrann an dara ceist meán rátálacha leabhar foilsitheora le haghaidh "
"na rátálacha sin níos mó ná 3.0 amháin."

msgid ""
"It's difficult to intuit how the ORM will translate complex querysets into "
"SQL queries so when in doubt, inspect the SQL with ``str(queryset.query)`` "
"and write plenty of tests."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé deacair a chur in iúl conas a aistríonn an ORM ceisteanna casta go "
"ceisteanna SQL mar sin nuair a bhíonn amhras ort, iniúchadh ar an SQL le "
"`str (queryset.query) ``agus scríobh neart tástálacha."

msgid "``order_by()``"
msgstr "``ord_by () ``"

msgid ""
"Annotations can be used as a basis for ordering. When you define an "
"``order_by()`` clause, the aggregates you provide can reference any alias "
"defined as part of an ``annotate()`` clause in the query."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anótaí a úsáid mar bhunús le haghaidh ordú. Nuair a shainmhíníonn "
"tú clásal ``order_by () `, is féidir leis na comhiomláin a sholáthraíonn tú "
"tagairt a dhéanamh d'aon ainm a shainmhínítear mar chuid de chlásal "
"``annotate ()` sa cheist."

msgid ""
"For example, to order a ``QuerySet`` of books by the number of authors that "
"have contributed to the book, you could use the following query:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun “QuerySet” de leabhair a ordú de réir líon na n-údar a "
"chuir leis an leabhar, d'fhéadfá an cheist seo a leanas a úsáid:"

msgid "``values()``"
msgstr "``luachanna () ``"

msgid ""
"Ordinarily, annotations are generated on a per-object basis - an annotated "
"``QuerySet`` will return one result for each object in the original "
"``QuerySet``. However, when a ``values()`` clause is used to constrain the "
"columns that are returned in the result set, the method for evaluating "
"annotations is slightly different. Instead of returning an annotated result "
"for each result in the original ``QuerySet``, the original results are "
"grouped according to the unique combinations of the fields specified in the "
"``values()`` clause. An annotation is then provided for each unique group; "
"the annotation is computed over all members of the group."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, gintear anótaí ar bhonn in aghaidh an réada - tabharfaidh "
"``QuerySet` anótáilte toradh amháin ar ais do gach réad sa ``QuerySet` "
"bunaidh. Mar sin féin, nuair a úsáidtear clásal ``luachanna () ``chun srian "
"a chur ar na colúin a chuirtear ar ais sa tacar torthaí, tá an modh chun "
"anótaí a mheas beagán difriúil. In ionad toradh anótaithe a thabhairt ar ais "
"do gach toradh sa “QuerySet” bunaidh, déantar na torthaí bunaidh a ghrúpáil "
"de réir na gcomhcheangail uathúla de na réimsí a shonraítear sa chlásal "
"``luachanna () ``. Cuirtear anótáil ar fáil ansin do gach grúpa uathúil; "
"ríomhtar an t-anótáil thar gach ball den ghrúpa."

msgid ""
"For example, consider an author query that attempts to find out the average "
"rating of books written by each author:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, smaoinigh ar cheist údair a dhéanann iarracht meánrátáil "
"leabhar a scríobh gach údar a fháil amach:"

msgid ""
"This will return one result for each author in the database, annotated with "
"their average book rating."
msgstr ""
"Tabharfaidh sé seo toradh amháin ar ais do gach údar sa bhunachar sonraí, "
"anótáilte lena meánrátáil leabhar."

msgid ""
"However, the result will be slightly different if you use a ``values()`` "
"clause:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, beidh an toradh beagán difriúil má úsáideann tú clásal "
"``luachanna () ``:"

msgid ""
"In this example, the authors will be grouped by name, so you will only get "
"an annotated result for each *unique* author name. This means if you have "
"two authors with the same name, their results will be merged into a single "
"result in the output of the query; the average will be computed as the "
"average over the books written by both authors."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, déanfar na húdair a ghrúpáil de réir ainm, mar sin ní "
"gheobhaidh tú ach toradh anótaithe do gach ainm údair uath* uath*. "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo má tá beirt údar agat leis an ainm céanna, déanfar a "
"dtorthaí a chumasc i dtoradh amháin in aschur na fiosrúcháin; ríomhfar an "
"meán mar an meán thar na leabhair a scríobh an dá údar."

msgid "Order of ``annotate()`` and ``values()`` clauses"
msgstr "Ordú clásail ``anótáit () ``agus `luachanna ()``"

msgid ""
"As with the ``filter()`` clause, the order in which ``annotate()`` and "
"``values()`` clauses are applied to a query is significant. If the "
"``values()`` clause precedes the ``annotate()``, the annotation will be "
"computed using the grouping described by the ``values()`` clause."
msgstr ""
"Mar is amhlaidh leis an gclásal ``scagaire () ``, tá an t-ord ina gcuirtear "
"clásail ``annotate ()`` agus `luachanna () `i bhfeidhm ar cheist suntasach. "
"Má théann an clásal ``luachanna () ``roimh an `annotate ()``, ríomhfar an t-"
"anótáil ag baint úsáide as an ngrúpáil a thuairiscítear leis an gclásal "
"``luachanna () ``."

msgid ""
"However, if the ``annotate()`` clause precedes the ``values()`` clause, the "
"annotations will be generated over the entire query set. In this case, the "
"``values()`` clause only constrains the fields that are generated on output."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má théann an clásal ``annotate () ``roimh an gclásal "
"``luachanna ()``, ginfear na nótaí thar an tacar fiosrúcháin iomlán. Sa chás "
"seo, ní chuireann an clásal `luachanna () ``srian ach ar na réimsí a "
"ghintear ar aschur."

msgid ""
"For example, if we reverse the order of the ``values()`` and ``annotate()`` "
"clause from our previous example:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má aisiompaímid ord na clásal ``luachanna () ``agus ``annotate "
"()`` ónár sampla roimhe seo:"

msgid ""
"This will now yield one unique result for each author; however, only the "
"author's name and the ``average_rating`` annotation will be returned in the "
"output data."
msgstr ""
"Tabharfaidh sé seo toradh uathúil amháin anois do gach údar; áfach, ní "
"thabharfar ach ainm an údair agus an anótáil `meán_rating`` ar ais sna "
"sonraí aschuir."

msgid ""
"You should also note that ``average_rating`` has been explicitly included in "
"the list of values to be returned. This is required because of the ordering "
"of the ``values()`` and ``annotate()`` clause."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit a thabhairt faoi deara freisin go bhfuil ``meán_rating`` san "
"áireamh go sainráite sa liosta luachanna atá le tabhairt ar ais. Tá sé seo "
"ag teastáil mar gheall ar ordú na clásal ``luachanna () ``agus ``annotate "
"()``."

msgid ""
"If the ``values()`` clause precedes the ``annotate()`` clause, any "
"annotations will be automatically added to the result set. However, if the "
"``values()`` clause is applied after the ``annotate()`` clause, you need to "
"explicitly include the aggregate column."
msgstr ""
"Má théann an clásal ``luachanna () ``roimh an gclásal ``annotate ()``, "
"cuirfear aon anótaí go huathoibríoch leis an tacar torthaí. Mar sin féin, má "
"chuirtear an clásal `luachanna () ``i bhfeidhm tar éis an chlásal ``annotate "
"()``, ní mór duit an colún comhiomlán a chur san áireamh go sainráite."

msgid "Interaction with ``order_by()``"
msgstr "Idirghníomhaíocht le ``order_by () ``"

msgid ""
"Fields that are mentioned in the ``order_by()`` part of a queryset are used "
"when selecting the output data, even if they are not otherwise specified in "
"the ``values()`` call. These extra fields are used to group \"like\" results "
"together and they can make otherwise identical result rows appear to be "
"separate. This shows up, particularly, when counting things."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear réimsí a luaitear sa chuid ``order_by () ``de tacar fiosrúcháin "
"agus na sonraí aschuir á roghnú, fiú mura sonraítear iad a shlí eile sa "
"ghlao ``values ()``. Úsáidtear na réimsí breise seo chun torthaí “cosúil "
"leis” a ghrúpáil le chéile agus is féidir leo a dhéanamh go bhfuil "
"sraitheanna torthaí comhionanna ar leithligh Taispeánann sé seo, go "
"háirithe, agus rudaí á chomhaireamh."

msgid "By way of example, suppose you have a model like this::"
msgstr "Mar shampla, cuir i gcás go bhfuil samhail mar seo agat:"

msgid ""
"If you want to count how many times each distinct ``data`` value appears in "
"an ordered queryset, you might try this::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat a chomhaireamh cé mhéad uair atá gach luach `sonraí ``ar leith "
"le feiceáil i tacar ceisteanna ordaithe, b'fhéidir go dtriail a bhaint as "
"seo:"

msgid ""
"...which will group the ``Item`` objects by their common ``data`` values and "
"then count the number of ``id`` values in each group. Except that it won't "
"quite work. The ordering by ``name`` will also play a part in the grouping, "
"so this query will group by distinct ``(data, name)`` pairs, which isn't "
"what you want. Instead, you should construct this queryset::"
msgstr ""
"... a ghrúpáidh na rudaí ``Mír ``de réir a luachanna coitianta ``sonra`` "
"agus ansin líon na luachanna ``id`` a chomhaireamh i ngach grúpa. Ach amháin "
"nach n-oibreoidh sé go leor. Beidh páirt ag an ordú trí ``ainm ``sa ghrúpáil "
"freisin, mar sin déanfar an ceist seo a ghrúpáil de réir péirí`` (sonraí, "
"ainm) ``ar leithligh, nach é an rud atá uait. Ina áit sin, ba cheart duit an "
"tacar fiosrúcháin seo a thógáil::"

msgid ""
"...clearing any ordering in the query. You could also order by, say, "
"``data`` without any harmful effects, since that is already playing a role "
"in the query."
msgstr ""
"... aon ordú sa cheist a ghlanadh. D'fhéadfá ordú freisin trí, abair, "
"`sonraí ``gan aon éifeachtaí díobhálacha, ós rud é go bhfuil ról ag imirt "
"sin cheana féin sa cheist."

msgid ""
"This behavior is the same as that noted in the queryset documentation "
"for :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.distinct` and the general rule "
"is the same: normally you won't want extra columns playing a part in the "
"result, so clear out the ordering, or at least make sure it's restricted "
"only to those fields you also select in a ``values()`` call."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-iompar seo mar an gcéanna leis an gcáipéisíocht Queryset dag:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.Distinct` agus tá an riail ghinearálta mar "
"an gcéanna: de ghnáth ní theastaíonn uait colúin bhreise a imirt sa toradh, "
"mar sin soiléir an t-ordú, nó ar a laghad cinnte go bhfuil sé srianta do na "
"réimsí sin a roghnaíonn tú freisin i nglao ``values () `."

msgid ""
"You might reasonably ask why Django doesn't remove the extraneous columns "
"for you. The main reason is consistency with ``distinct()`` and other "
"places: Django **never** removes ordering constraints that you have "
"specified (and we can't change those other methods' behavior, as that would "
"violate our :doc:`/misc/api-stability` policy)."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir go bhfiafraíonn tú go réasúnta cén fáth nach mbaineann Django na "
"colúin seachtracha duit. Is é an chúis is mó ná comhsheasmhacht le "
"``difriúil () ``agus áiteanna eile: Baineann Django **riam** srianta "
"ordaithe atá sonraithe agat (agus ní féidir linn iompar na modhanna eile sin "
"a athrú, mar sháródh sé sin ár mbeartas: doc: `/misc/api-stability`)."

msgid "Aggregating annotations"
msgstr "Anótaí a chomhiomlánú"

msgid ""
"You can also generate an aggregate on the result of an annotation. When you "
"define an ``aggregate()`` clause, the aggregates you provide can reference "
"any alias defined as part of an ``annotate()`` clause in the query."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat comhiomlán a ghiniúint freisin ar thoradh anótála. Nuair a "
"shainmhíníonn tú clásal ``comhiomlán () ``, is féidir leis na comhiomláin a "
"sholáthraíonn tú tagairt a thabhairt d'aon ainm a shainmhínítear mar chuid "
"de chlásal ``annotate () `sa cheist."

msgid ""
"For example, if you wanted to calculate the average number of authors per "
"book you first annotate the set of books with the author count, then "
"aggregate that author count, referencing the annotation field:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, más mian leat meánlíon na n-údar in aghaidh an leabhair a ríomh "
"déanann tú anótáil ar dtús an tacar leabhar le comhaireamh na n-údair, ansin "
"comhiomlánú an údair sin, ag tagairt don réimse anótála:"

msgid "Aggregating on empty querysets or groups"
msgstr "Comhiomlánú ar cheisteanna nó grúpaí folamh"

msgid ""
"When an aggregation is applied to an empty queryset or grouping, the result "
"defaults to its :ref:`default <aggregate-default>` parameter, typically "
"``None``. This behavior occurs because aggregate functions return ``NULL`` "
"when the executed query returns no rows."
msgstr ""
