"sraithe, déanfar na srianta seo a sheiceáil ag deireadh an idirbheart. "
"D'fhéadfadh earráid ualaigh a bheith mar thoradh ar aon chaidrimh ar fud "
"daingneáin mura dtacaíonn cumraíocht an bhunachar sonraí le seiceáil srianta "
"iarchurtha (féach do na doiciméid `MySQL`_ mar shampla)."

msgid "How fixtures are saved to the database"
msgstr "Conas a shábháil daingneáin sa bhunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"When fixture files are processed, the data is saved to the database as is. "
"Model defined :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` methods are not called, "
"and any :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_save` "
"or :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_save` signals will be called with "
"``raw=True`` since the instance only contains attributes that are local to "
"the model. You may, for example, want to disable handlers that access "
"related fields that aren't present during fixture loading and would "
"otherwise raise an exception::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a phróiseáiltear comhaid daingneáin, sábhálfar na sonraí chuig an "
"mbunachar sonraí mar atá. Samhail sainmhínithe: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.save` ní ghlaofar modhanna, agus glaofar aon "
"chomharthaí: `~django.db.models.signals.pre_save` nó:data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_save` le ``raw=true`` ós rud é nach bhfuil "
"ach tréithe áitiúil don tsamhail múnla. B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat, mar "
"shampla, láimhseálaithe a dhíchumasú a dhéanann rochtain ar réimsí gaolmhara "
"nach bhfuil i láthair le linn luchtú daingneáin agus a ardódh eisceacht ar "
"shlí eile"

msgid "You could also write a decorator to encapsulate this logic::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfá maisitheoir a scríobh freisin chun an loighic seo a chumhdú::"

msgid ""
"Just be aware that this logic will disable the signals whenever fixtures are "
"deserialized, not just during :djadmin:`loaddata`."
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas go ndéanfaidh an loighic seo na comharthaí a dhíchumasú aon "
"uair a dhíshealtar daingneáin, ní hamháin le linn: djadmin: `loaddata`."

msgid "Compressed fixtures"
msgstr "Daingneáin chomhbh"

msgid ""
"Fixtures may be compressed in ``zip``, ``gz``, ``bz2``, ``lzma``, or ``xz`` "
"format. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Féadfar daingneáin a chomhbhrúite i bhformáid ``zip``, `gz``, `bz2``, `lz``, "
"nó ``xz``. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"would look for any of ``mydata.json``, ``mydata.json.zip``, "
"``mydata.json.gz``, ``mydata.json.bz2``, ``mydata.json.lzma``, or "
"``mydata.json.xz``. The first file contained within a compressed archive is "
"used."
msgstr ""
"lorg aon cheann de `mydata.json``, `mydata.json.zip``, `mydata.json.gz``, "
"`mydata.json.gz``, `mydata.json.xz``, `mydata.json.lz``, nó "
"``mydata.json.xz``. Úsáidtear an chéad chomhad atá laistigh de chartlann "
"comhbhrúite."

msgid ""
"Note that if two fixtures with the same name but different fixture type are "
"discovered (for example, if ``mydata.json`` and ``mydata.xml.gz`` were found "
"in the same fixture directory), fixture installation will be aborted, and "
"any data installed in the call to :djadmin:`loaddata` will be removed from "
"the database."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara má aimsítear dhá daingneán leis an ainm céanna ach cineál "
"daingneáin difriúil (mar shampla, má aimsíodh ``mydata.json`` agus "
"`mydata.xml.gz`` san eolaire daingneáin chéanna), cuirfear deireadh leis an "
"suiteáil daingneáin, agus bainfear aon sonraí suiteáilte sa ghlao "
"chu:djadmin: `loaddata` ón mbunachar sonraí."

msgid "MySQL with MyISAM and fixtures"
msgstr "MySQL le MyISAM agus daingneáin"

msgid ""
"The MyISAM storage engine of MySQL doesn't support transactions or "
"constraints, so if you use MyISAM, you won't get validation of fixture data, "
"or a rollback if multiple transaction files are found."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn inneall stórála MyISAM MySQL le hidirbhearta nó srianta, mar "
"sin má úsáideann tú MyISAM, ní gheobhaidh tú bailíochtú sonraí daingneáin, "
"ná rolladh siar má aimsítear comhad idirbheart iolracha."

msgid "Database-specific fixtures"
msgstr "Daingneáin sonrach le bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"If you're in a multi-database setup, you might have fixture data that you "
"want to load onto one database, but not onto another. In this situation, you "
"can add a database identifier into the names of your fixtures."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú i socrú ilbhunachar sonraí, b'fhéidir go mbeadh sonraí daingneáin "
"agat ar mhaith leat a luchtú ar bhunachar sonraí amháin, ach ní ar bhunachar "
"sonraí eile. Sa chás seo, is féidir leat aitheantóir bunachar sonraí a chur "
"isteach in ainmneacha do daingneáin."

msgid ""
"For example, if your :setting:`DATABASES` setting has a ``users`` database "
"defined, name the fixture ``mydata.users.json`` or ``mydata.users.json.gz`` "
"and the fixture will only be loaded when you specify you want to load data "
"into the ``users`` database."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá bunachar sonraí ``users`` sainithe ag do shuíomh: "
"`DATABASES`, ainmnigh an daingneán ``mydata.users.json`` nó "
"``mydata.users.json.gz`` agus ní luchtálfar an daingneán ach nuair a "
"shonraíonn tú gur mhaith leat sonraí a luchtú isteach sa bhunachar sonraí "
"``users``."

msgid "Models and databases"
msgstr "Samhlacha agus bunachair sonraí"

msgid ""
"A model is the single, definitive source of information about your data. It "
"contains the essential fields and behaviors of the data you're storing. "
"Generally, each model maps to a single database table."
msgstr ""
"Is é samhail an fhoinse aonair, cinntitheach faisnéise faoi do shonraí. Tá "
"réimsí agus iompraíochtaí riachtanacha ann na sonraí atá á stóráil agat. Go "
"ginearálta, déanann gach samhail mapáil chuig tábla bunachar sonraí amháin."

msgid "Database instrumentation"
msgstr "Ionstraimíocht bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"To help you understand and control the queries issued by your code, Django "
"provides a hook for installing wrapper functions around the execution of "
"database queries. For example, wrappers can count queries, measure query "
"duration, log queries, or even prevent query execution (e.g. to make sure "
"that no queries are issued while rendering a template with prefetched data)."
msgstr ""
"Chun cabhrú leat na ceisteanna a eisíonn do chód a thuiscint agus a rialú, "
"soláthraíonn Django crúca chun feidhmeanna fillte a shuiteáil timpeall ar "
"fhiosruithe bunachar sonraí a fhorghní Mar shampla, is féidir le fillteoirí "
"ceisteanna a chomhaireamh, fad na fiosrúcháin a thomhas, ceisteanna logála, "
"nó fiú cosc a chur ar fhorghníomhú ceisteanna (m.sh. chun a chinntiú nach n-"
"eisítear aon cheisteanna agus teimpléad á rindreáil le sonraí réamhf"

msgid ""
"The wrappers are modeled after :doc:`middleware </topics/http/middleware>` "
"-- they are callables which take another callable as one of their arguments. "
"They call that callable to invoke the (possibly wrapped) database query, and "
"they can do what they want around that call. They are, however, created and "
"installed by user code, and so don't need a separate factory like middleware "
"do."
msgstr ""
"Déantar na fillteáin a mhúnlú tar éis: doc: `middleware` - is glaonna iad a "
"ghlac</topics/http/middleware> ann glaoch eile mar cheann dá n-argóintí. "
"Glaonn siad ar an glaoch sin chun an cheist bunachar sonraí (fillte "
"b'fhéidir) a ghairm, agus is féidir leo an méid a theastaíonn uathu a "
"dhéanamh timpeall an ghlao sin. Cruthaítear agus suiteáiltear iad, áfach, le "
"cód úsáideora, agus mar sin ní theastaíonn monarcha ar leithligh uathu mar a "
"dhéanann middleware."

msgid ""
"Installing a wrapper is done in a context manager -- so the wrappers are "
"temporary and specific to some flow in your code."
msgstr ""
"Déantar fillteán a shuiteáil i mbainisteoir comhthéacs - mar sin tá na "
"fillteáin sealadach agus go sonrach le sreabhadh éigin i do chód."

msgid ""
"As mentioned above, an example of a wrapper is a query execution blocker. It "
"could look like this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar a luadh thuas, is sampla de fhillteán ná blocaire forghníomhaithe "
"fiosrúcháin. D'fhéadfadh cuma seo a bheith air::"

msgid ""
"And it would be used in a view to block queries from the template like so::"
msgstr "Agus úsáidfí é d'fhonn ceisteanna ón teimpléad a bhac mar sin:"

msgid "The parameters sent to the wrappers are:"
msgstr "Is iad na paraiméadair a sheoltar chuig na fillteáin ná:"

msgid ""
"``execute`` -- a callable, which should be invoked with the rest of the "
"parameters in order to execute the query."
msgstr ""
"``fhorghníomhach` - glaoch, ar chóir a ghairm leis an gcuid eile de na "
"paraiméadair d'fhonn an cheist a fhorghníomhú."

msgid "``sql`` -- a ``str``, the SQL query to be sent to the database."
msgstr ""
"``sql`` - `str``, an ceist SQL atá le seoladh chuig an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"``params`` -- a list/tuple of parameter values for the SQL command, or a "
"list/tuple of lists/tuples if the wrapped call is ``executemany()``."
msgstr ""
"``params`` - liosta/tiúpla de luachanna paraiméadar don ordú SQL, nó liosta/"
"tiúpla de liosta/tuples más é `executemany () ``an glao fillte."

msgid ""
"``many`` -- a ``bool`` indicating whether the ultimately invoked call is "
"``execute()`` or ``executemany()`` (and whether ``params`` is expected to be "
"a sequence of values, or a sequence of sequences of values)."
msgstr ""
"```many ``- `bool`` a thugann le fios an bhfuil `executar ()`` nó "
"`executemany () ``an glao a ghairmtear sa deireadh ()`` (agus cibé an "
"bhfuiltear ag súil go mbeidh `params`` ina seicheamh luachanna, nó seicheamh "
"seicheamh luachanna)."

msgid ""
"``context`` -- a dictionary with further data about the context of "
"invocation. This includes the connection and cursor."
msgstr ""
"``context`` -- foclóir le sonraí breise faoi chomhthéacs an t-ionghairm. "
"Áirítear leis seo an nasc agus an cúrsóir."

msgid ""
"Using the parameters, a slightly more complex version of the blocker could "
"include the connection name in the error message::"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as na paraiméadair, d'fhéadfadh leagan beagán níos casta den "
"bhlocóir ainm an nasc sa teachtaireacht earráide a áireamh:"

msgid "For a more complete example, a query logger could look like this::"
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sampla níos iomláine, d'fhéadfadh cuma seo a bheith ar logálaí "
"ceisteanna::"

msgid ""
"To use this, you would create a logger object and install it as a wrapper::"
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a úsáid, chruthófá réad logger agus é a shuiteáil mar fhilleadh:"

msgid "``connection.execute_wrapper()``"
msgstr "``nascach.execute_wrapper () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns a context manager which, when entered, installs a wrapper around "
"database query executions, and when exited, removes the wrapper. The wrapper "
"is installed on the thread-local connection object."
msgstr ""
"Filleann bainisteoir comhthéacs ar ais a shuiteálann, nuair a chuirtear "
"isteach é, timpeall forghníomhaithe fiosrúcháin bunachar sonraí, agus nuair "
"a bhíonn sé amach, baineann sé an fillteán Tá an fillteán suiteáilte ar an "
"réad nasc snáithe áitiúil."

msgid ""
"``wrapper`` is a callable taking five arguments.  It is called for every "
"query execution in the scope of the context manager, with arguments "
"``execute``, ``sql``, ``params``, ``many``, and ``context`` as described "
"above. It's expected to call ``execute(sql, params, many, context)`` and "
"return the return value of that call."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``wrapper`` is féidir glaoch a ghlacadh cúig argóint. Iarrtar ar gach "
"forghníomhú ceisteanna i raon feidhme an bhainisteora comhthéacs, le "
"hargóintí ``forghníomhaítear ``, `sql``, `params``, ``go leor``, agus "
"``context`` mar a thuairiscítear thuas. Táthar ag súil go gcuirfidh sé "
"glaoch ar ``executar (sql, params, go leor, comhthéacs) ``agus luach "
"tuairisceáin an ghlao sin a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid "Managers"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí"

msgid ""
"A ``Manager`` is the interface through which database query operations are "
"provided to Django models. At least one ``Manager`` exists for every model "
"in a Django application."
msgstr ""
"Is é “Bainisteoir” an comhéadan trína gcuirtear oibríochtaí fiosrúcháin "
"bunachar sonraí ar fáil do mhúnlaí Django. Tá ``Bainisteoir ``amháin ar a "
"laghad ann do gach samhail i bhfeidhmchlár Django."

msgid ""
"The way ``Manager`` classes work is documented in :doc:`/topics/db/queries`; "
"this document specifically touches on model options that customize "
"``Manager`` behavior."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an bealach a oibríonn ranganna ``Bainiste`` doiciméadaithe in:doc: `/"
"topics/db/queries`; baineann an doiciméad seo go sonrach le roghanna "
"samhlacha a shaincheapann iompar ``Bainiste``."

msgid "Manager names"
msgstr "Ainmneacha bainisteora"

msgid ""
"By default, Django adds a ``Manager`` with the name ``objects`` to every "
"Django model class. However, if you want to use ``objects`` as a field name, "
"or if you want to use a name other than ``objects`` for the ``Manager``, you "
"can rename it on a per-model basis. To rename the ``Manager`` for a given "
"class, define a class attribute of type ``models.Manager()`` on that model. "
"For example::"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, cuireann Django ``Bainiste`` leis an ainm ``ruda`` "
"le gach rang samhail Django. Mar sin féin, más mian leat ``ruda`` a úsáid "
"mar ainm réimse, nó más mian leat ainm seachas ``ruda`` a úsáid don "
"`Bainiste``, is féidir leat é a athainmniú ar bhonn in aghaidh an mhúnla. "
"Chun an ``Bainiste`` a athainmniú do rang ar leith, sainmhínigh tréith aicme "
"de chineál ``Models.manager () ``ar an tsamhail sin. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Using this example model, ``Person.objects`` will generate an "
"``AttributeError`` exception, but ``Person.people.all()`` will provide a "
"list of all ``Person`` objects."
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as an tsamhail samplach seo, ginfidh ``Person.Objects`` "
"eisceacht ``AttributeError``, ach soláthróidh ``Person.People.all () "
"``liosta de na rudaí ``Person`` go léir."

msgid "Custom managers"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"You can use a custom ``Manager`` in a particular model by extending the base "
"``Manager`` class and instantiating your custom ``Manager`` in your model."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``Bainisteoir ``saincheaptha a úsáid i samhail áirithe tríd "
"an rang bonn ``Bainiste`` a leathnú agus do `Bainisteoir`` saincheaptha a "
"chur i do mhúnla."

msgid ""
"There are two reasons you might want to customize a ``Manager``: to add "
"extra ``Manager`` methods, and/or to modify the initial ``QuerySet`` the "
"``Manager`` returns."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá chúis ann b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat ``Bainiste`` a shaincheapadh: "
"modhanna ``Bainiste`` breise a chur leis, agus/nó an `QuerySet`` tosaigh "
"``Bainiste`` a mhodhnú."

msgid "Adding extra manager methods"
msgstr "Modhanna bainisteora breise a chur leis"

msgid ""
"Adding extra ``Manager`` methods is the preferred way to add \"table-level\" "
"functionality to your models. (For \"row-level\" functionality -- i.e., "
"functions that act on a single instance of a model object -- use :ref:`Model "
"methods <model-methods>`, not custom ``Manager`` methods.)"
msgstr ""
"Is é modhanna breise ``Bainiste`` a chur leis an mbealach is fearr chun "
"feidhmiúlacht “leibhéal tábla” a chur le do mhúnlaí. (Maidir le "
"feidhmiúlacht “leibhéal sraithe” - ie, feidhmeanna a ghníomhaíonn ar shampla "
"amháin de réad samhail - bain úsáid as: ref: `Modhanna samhlacha `, <model-"
"methods>ní modhanna saincheaptha ``Bainiste``.)"

msgid "For example, this custom ``Manager`` adds a method ``with_counts()``::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, cuireann an ``Bainisteoir ``saincheaptha seo modh ``with_counts "
"()``:"

msgid ""
"With this example, you'd use ``OpinionPoll.objects.with_counts()`` to get a "
"``QuerySet`` of ``OpinionPoll`` objects with the extra ``num_responses`` "
"attribute attached."
msgstr ""
"Leis an sampla seo, úsáidfeá ``OpinionPoll.Objects.with_Counts () ``chun "
"`QuerySet` de rudaí ``OpinionPoll`` a fháil leis an tréith breise "
"``num_responses`` ceangailte."

msgid ""
"A custom ``Manager`` method can return anything you want. It doesn't have to "
"return a ``QuerySet``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le modh saincheaptha ``Bainiste`` aon rud a theastaíonn uait a "
"thabhairt ar ais. Ní gá dó ``QuerySet ``a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"Another thing to note is that ``Manager`` methods can access ``self.model`` "
"to get the model class to which they're attached."
msgstr ""
"Rud eile le tabhairt faoi deara ná gur féidir le modhanna ``Bainiste`` "
"rochtain a fháil ar ``self.model ``chun an rang samhail lena bhfuil siad "
"ceangailte a fháil."

msgid "Modifying a manager's initial ``QuerySet``"
msgstr "“QuerySet” tosaigh bainisteora a mhodhnú"

msgid ""
"A ``Manager``’s base ``QuerySet`` returns all objects in the system. For "
"example, using this model::"
msgstr ""
"Tugann bonn ``Bainiste`` `QuerySet`` gach rud sa chóras ar ais. Mar shampla, "
"ag baint úsáide as an tsamhail seo:"

msgid ""
"...the statement ``Book.objects.all()`` will return all books in the "
"database."
msgstr ""
"... cuirfidh an ráiteas ``Book.Objects.all () ``gach leabhar sa bhunachar "
"sonraí ar ais."

msgid ""
"You can override a ``Manager``’s base ``QuerySet`` by overriding the "
"``Manager.get_queryset()`` method. ``get_queryset()`` should return a "
"``QuerySet`` with the properties you require."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat bonn ```Manager`` `QuerySet`` a shárú tríd an modh "
"`Manager.get_querySet () ``a shárú. Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh ``get_queryset () "
"``QuerySet`` a thabhairt ar ais leis na hairíonna a theastaíonn uait."

msgid ""
"For example, the following model has *two* ``Manager``\\s -- one that "
"returns all objects, and one that returns only the books by Roald Dahl::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, tá *dha* ``Bainisteoir ``\\ s sa tsamhail seo a leanas - ceann "
"a thugann gach rud ar ais, agus ceann nach dtugann ach na leabhair le Roald "
"Dahl ar ais:"

msgid ""
"With this sample model, ``Book.objects.all()`` will return all books in the "
"database, but ``Book.dahl_objects.all()`` will only return the ones written "
"by Roald Dahl."
msgstr ""
"Leis an tsamhail samplach seo, ní thabharfaidh `Book.Objects.all () ``gach "
"leabhar sa bhunachar sonraí ar ais, ach ní thabharfaidh "
"`Book.dahl_objects.all ()`` ach na cinn a scríobh Roald Dahl ar ais."

msgid ""
"Because ``get_queryset()`` returns a ``QuerySet`` object, you can use "
"``filter()``, ``exclude()`` and all the other ``QuerySet`` methods on it. So "
"these statements are all legal::"
msgstr ""
"Toisc go bhfilleann ``get_queryset () ``réad ``QuerySet``, is féidir leat "
"``filter () ``,``, () ``a úsáid agus na modhanna ``QuerySet`` eile air. Mar "
"sin tá na ráitis seo go léir dlíthiúil:"

msgid ""
"This example also pointed out another interesting technique: using multiple "
"managers on the same model. You can attach as many ``Manager()`` instances "
"to a model as you'd like. This is a non-repetitive way to define common "
"\"filters\" for your models."
msgstr ""
"Chuir an sampla seo in iúl teicníc spéisiúil eile freisin: bainisteoirí "
"iolracha a úsáid ar an tsamhail chéanna. Is féidir leat an oiread cásanna "
"``Bainisteoir () ``a cheangal le samhail agus is mian leat. Is bealach neamh-"
"athchleachtach é seo chun “scagairí” coitianta do do mhúnlaí a shainiú."

msgid ""
"This example allows you to request ``Person.authors.all()``, "
"``Person.editors.all()``, and ``Person.people.all()``, yielding predictable "
"results."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an sampla seo duit ``Person.Authors.all () ``, `Person.Editors.all "
"()``, agus ``Person.People.all () ``a iarraidh, ag tabhairt torthaí "
"intuartha."

msgid "Default managers"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí réamhshoc"

msgid ""
"If you use custom ``Manager`` objects, take note that the first ``Manager`` "
"Django encounters (in the order in which they're defined in the model) has a "
"special status. Django interprets the first ``Manager`` defined in a class "
"as the \"default\" ``Manager``, and several parts of Django "
"(including :djadmin:`dumpdata`) will use that ``Manager`` exclusively for "
"that model. As a result, it's a good idea to be careful in your choice of "
"default manager in order to avoid a situation where overriding "
"``get_queryset()`` results in an inability to retrieve objects you'd like to "
"work with."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú rudaí saincheaptha ``Bainiste``, tabhair faoi deara go "
"bhfuil stádas speisialta ag an gcéad ``Bainisteoir ``Django (san ord ina "
"sainmhínítear iad sa tsamhail). Léirmhíníonn Django an chéad ``Bainiste`` a "
"shainmhínítear i rang mar an “réamhshocraithe” ``Bainiste``, agus úsáidfidh "
"roinnt codanna de Django (lena n-áirítear: djadmin: `dumpdata`) an "
"`Bainisteoir ``sin go heisiach don tsamhail sin. Mar thoradh air sin, is "
"smaoineamh maith é a bheith cúramach i do rogha bainisteora réamhshocraithe "
"d'fhonn cás a sheachaint ina mbíonn neamhábaltacht rudaí ar mhaith leat "
"oibriú leo mar thoradh ar 'get_queryset ()' a shárú."

msgid ""
"You can specify a custom default manager "
"using :attr:`Meta.default_manager_name "
"<django.db.models.Options.default_manager_name>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.default_manager_name>Is féidir leat bainisteoir "
"réamhshocraithe saincheaptha a shonrú ag baint úsáidea:attr: "
"`meta.default_manager_name `."

msgid ""
"If you're writing some code that must handle an unknown model, for example, "
"in a third-party app that implements a generic view, use this manager "
"(or :attr:`~Model._base_manager`) rather than assuming the model has an "
"``objects`` manager."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cód éigin á scríobh agat a chaithfidh samhail anaithnid a láimhseáil, "
"mar shampla, in aip tríú páirtí a chuireann dearcadh cineálach i bhfeidhm, "
"bain úsáid as an mbainisteoir seo (nó: attr: `~Model. _base_manager`) "
"seachas glacadh leis go bhfuil bainisteoir ``ruda`` ag an tsamhail."

msgid "Base managers"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí bonn"

msgid "Using managers for related object access"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí a úsáid le haghaidh rochtana gaolmhara"

msgid ""
"By default, Django uses an instance of the ``Model._base_manager`` manager "
"class when accessing related objects (e.g. ``choice.question``), not the "
"``_default_manager`` on the related object. This is because Django needs to "
"be able to retrieve the related object, even if it would otherwise be "
"filtered out (and hence be inaccessible) by the default manager."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the normal base manager class (:class:`django.db.models.Manager`) isn't "
"appropriate for your circumstances, you can tell Django which class to use "
"by setting :attr:`Meta.base_manager_name "
"<django.db.models.Options.base_manager_name>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.base_manager_name>Mura bhfuil an gnáthrang "
"bainisteora bonn (:class: `Django.db.Models.Manager`) oiriúnach do do "
"chúinsí, is féidir leat a rá le Django cén rang atá le húsáid trí "
"shocting:attr: `Meta.base_Manager_name `."

msgid ""
"Base managers aren't used when querying on related models, or "
"when :ref:`accessing a one-to-many or many-to-many relationship <backwards-"
"related-objects>`. For example, if the ``Question`` model :ref:`from the "
"tutorial <creating-models>` had a ``deleted`` field and a base manager that "
"filters out instances with ``deleted=True``, a queryset like "
"``Choice.objects.filter(question__name__startswith='What')`` would include "
"choices related to deleted questions."
msgstr ""
"<backwards-related-objects>Ní úsáidtear bainisteoirí bonn agus iad ag fiosrú "
"ar mhúnlaí gaolmhara, nó nuair: ref: `rochtain a fháil ar chaidreamh duine "
"le go leor nó go leor '. Mar shampla, má bhí <creating-models>réimse "
"``scriostha ``agus bainisteoir bonn ag an tsamhail ``Cheiste`:ref: `ón rang "
"teagaisc`` agus bainisteoir bonn a scagann amach cásanna le "
"``deleted=true``, chuimsíodh roghanna a bhaineann le ceisteanna scriosta mar "
"``choice.objects.filter (question__name__startswith='What') `."

msgid "Don't filter away any results in this type of manager subclass"
msgstr "Ná scagadh aon torthaí sa chineál seo fo-aicme bainisteora"

msgid ""
"This manager is used to access objects that are related to from some other "
"model. In those situations, Django has to be able to see all the objects for "
"the model it is fetching, so that *anything* which is referred to can be "
"retrieved."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an bainisteoir seo chun rochtain a fháil ar rudaí a bhaineann leo "
"ó mhúnla éigin eile. Sna cásanna sin, caithfidh Django a bheith in ann na "
"rudaí go léir don tsamhail atá á fháil aige a fheiceáil, ionas gur féidir "
"*aon ruda* a dtagraítear dó a aisghabháil."

msgid ""
"Therefore, you should not override ``get_queryset()`` to filter out any "
"rows. If you do so, Django will return incomplete results."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, níor cheart duit ``get_queryset () ``a shárú chun aon "
"sraitheanna a scagadh amach. Má dhéanann tú amhlaidh, cuirfidh Django "
"torthaí neamhiomlán ar ais."

msgid "Calling custom ``QuerySet`` methods from the manager"
msgstr "Ag glaoch ar mhodhanna saincheaptha ``QuerySet` ón mbainisteoir"

msgid ""
"While most methods from the standard ``QuerySet`` are accessible directly "
"from the ``Manager``, this is only the case for the extra methods defined on "
