"leat bailiúchán rudaí teibí a bheith agat, níl sé ciall a bheith ag "
"bainistiú iad. Má tá feidhmiúlacht agat a bhaineann leis an tsamhail teibí, "
"ba cheart duit an fheidhmiúlacht sin a chur i “modh statach” nó i “modh "
"ranga” ar an tsamhail teibí."

msgid "Implementation concerns"
msgstr "Imeachtaí cur chun feidhme"

msgid ""
"Whatever features you add to your custom ``Manager``, it must be possible to "
"make a shallow copy of a ``Manager`` instance; i.e., the following code must "
"work:"
msgstr ""
"Cibé gnéithe a chuireann tú le do “Bainisteoir” saincheaptha, caithfidh sé a "
"bheith indéanta cóip éadrom a dhéanamh de shampla ``Bainiste``; ie, "
"caithfidh an cód seo a leanas oibriú:"

msgid ""
"Django makes shallow copies of manager objects during certain queries; if "
"your Manager cannot be copied, those queries will fail."
msgstr ""
"Déanann Django cóipeanna éadmhara de rudaí bainisteora le linn fiosruithe "
"áirithe; mura féidir do Bhainisteoir a chóipeáil, teipeann ar"

msgid ""
"This won't be an issue for most custom managers. If you are just adding "
"simple methods to your ``Manager``, it is unlikely that you will "
"inadvertently make instances of your ``Manager`` uncopyable. However, if "
"you're overriding ``__getattr__`` or some other private method of your "
"``Manager`` object that controls object state, you should ensure that you "
"don't affect the ability of your ``Manager`` to be copied."
msgstr ""
"Ní cheist é seo don chuid is mó de na bainisteoirí saincheaptha. Mura bhfuil "
"tú ach modhanna simplí ag cur le do ``Bainiste``, ní dócha go ndéanfaidh tú "
"cásanna de do `Bainisteoir ``gan chóipeáil gan aon ghnó. Mar sin féin, má tá "
"tú ag dul i bhfeidhm ar ``__getattr__`` nó modh príobháideach éigin eile de "
"do réad ```Bainiste`` a rialaíonn staid réada, ba cheart duit a chinntiú "
"nach ndéanann tú difear do chumas do ``Bainisteoir ``a chóipeáil."

msgid "Models"
msgstr "Samhla"

msgid "The basics:"
msgstr "Na buneilimintí:"

msgid ""
"Each model is a Python class that subclasses :class:`django.db.models.Model`."
msgstr ""
"Is aicme Python é gach samhail a fho-aicmi:class: `Django.db.Models.Model`."

msgid "Each attribute of the model represents a database field."
msgstr "Léiríonn gach tréith den tsamhail réimse bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"With all of this, Django gives you an automatically-generated database-"
"access API; see :doc:`/topics/db/queries`."
msgstr ""
"Leis seo go léir, tugann Django API rochtana bunachar sonraí a ghintear go "
"huathoibríoch duit; féach: doc: `/topics/db/queries`."

msgid "Quick example"
msgstr "Sampla tapa"

msgid ""
"This example model defines a ``Person``, which has a ``first_name`` and "
"``last_name``::"
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an tsamhail sampla seo ``Person``, a bhfuil ``chéad_ainm`` agus "
"``ainm_deiride`` aige:"

msgid ""
"``first_name`` and ``last_name`` are fields_ of the model. Each field is "
"specified as a class attribute, and each attribute maps to a database column."
msgstr ""
"Is réimsí den tsamhail iad ``chéad_ainm`` agus ``ainm_deiridh ``. Sonraítear "
"gach réimse mar thréith aicme, agus léarscálann gach tréith chuig colún "
"bunachar sonraí."

msgid "The above ``Person`` model would create a database table like this:"
msgstr "Chruthódh an tsamhail “Duine” thuas tábla bunachar sonraí mar seo:"

msgid "Some technical notes:"
msgstr "Roinnt nótaí teicniúla:"

msgid ""
"The name of the table, ``myapp_person``, is automatically derived from some "
"model metadata but can be overridden. See :ref:`table-names` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Díorthaítear ainm an tábla, `myapp_person``, go huathoibríoch ó roinnt "
"meiteashonraí samhail ach is féidir é a shárú. Féach: Ref: `table-names` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"An ``id`` field is added automatically, but this behavior can be overridden. "
"See :ref:`automatic-primary-key-fields`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear réimse `id ``leis go huathoibríoch, ach is féidir an t-iompar seo a "
"shárú. Féach: tagairt: `uathoibrí-phríomh-eochair-réimsí `."

msgid ""
"The ``CREATE TABLE`` SQL in this example is formatted using PostgreSQL "
"syntax, but it's worth noting Django uses SQL tailored to the database "
"backend specified in your :doc:`settings file </topics/settings>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá an SQL `CREATE TABLE`` sa sampla seo formáidithe ag baint úsáide as "
"comhréiteach PostgreSQL, ach is fiú a thabhairt faoi deara go n-úsáideann "
"Django SQL atá curtha in oiriúint don chúlcheann bunachar sonraí a "
"shonraítear i do: doc: `comhad </topics/settings> socruithe `."

msgid "Using models"
msgstr "Múnlaí a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Once you have defined your models, you need to tell Django you're going to "
"*use* those models. Do this by editing your settings file and changing "
"the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting to add the name of the module that "
"contains your ``models.py``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh do mhúnlaí sainmhínithe agat, ní mór duit a rá le Django go "
"bhfuil tú chun * úsáid* na samhlacha sin. Déan é seo trí do chomhad "
"socruithe a chur in eagar agus an socrú:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` a athrú "
"chun ainm an mhodúil ina bhfuil do `models.py`` a chur leis."

msgid ""
"For example, if the models for your application live in the module "
"``myapp.models`` (the package structure that is created for an application "
"by the :djadmin:`manage.py startapp <startapp>` "
"script), :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` should read, in part::"
msgstr ""
"<startapp>Mar shampla, má tá na samhlacha d'iarratais ina gcónaí sa mhodúl "
"``myapp.models`` (struchtúr an phacáiste a chruthaítear d'iarratas leis an "
"scripte:djadmin: `manage.py startapp `), ba chóir :setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` "
"léamh, go páirteach::"

msgid ""
"When you add new apps to :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, be sure to "
"run :djadmin:`manage.py migrate <migrate>`, optionally making migrations for "
"them first with :djadmin:`manage.py makemigrations <makemigrations>`."
msgstr ""
"<migrate><makemigrations>Nuair a chuireann tú aipeanna nua chuig: setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`, bí cinnte rith: djadmin: `manage.py migration `, ag "
"déanamh imirce dóibh go roghnach le: djadmin: `manage.py makemigrations`."

msgid "Fields"
msgstr "Réimsí"

msgid ""
"The most important part of a model -- and the only required part of a model "
"-- is the list of database fields it defines. Fields are specified by class "
"attributes. Be careful not to choose field names that conflict with "
"the :doc:`models API </ref/models/instances>` like ``clean``, ``save``, or "
"``delete``."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chuid is tábhachtaí de mhúnla - agus an t-aon chuid riachtanach de "
"mhúnla - liosta na réimsí bunachar sonraí a shainmhíníonn sé. Sonraítear "
"réimsí de réir tréithe ranga. Bí cúramach gan ainmneacha réimse a roghnú atá "
"ag teacht ar choinníoll leis na:doc: `models API` cosúil le ``glan ``, "
"`shábháil`` </ref/models/instances>, nó ``scrios``."

msgid "Example::"
msgstr "Sampla::"

msgid "Field types"
msgstr "Cineálacha réimse"

msgid ""
"Each field in your model should be an instance of the "
"appropriate :class:`~django.db.models.Field` class. Django uses the field "
"class types to determine a few things:"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh gach réimse i do mhúnla mar shampla den rang "
"oiriúna:class: `~Django.db.Models.Field`. Úsáideann Django na cineálacha "
"ranga allamuigh chun cúpla rud a chinneadh:"

msgid ""
"The column type, which tells the database what kind of data to store (e.g. "
"``INTEGER``, ``VARCHAR``, ``TEXT``)."
msgstr ""
"An cineál colún, a insíonn don bhunachar sonraí cén cineál sonraí atá le "
"stóráil (m.sh. ``INTEGER``, `VARCHAR``, `TEXT``)."

msgid ""
"The default HTML :doc:`widget </ref/forms/widgets>` to use when rendering a "
"form field (e.g. ``<input type=\"text\">``, ``<select>``)."
msgstr ""
"</ref/forms/widgets> <input type=\"text\"><select>An réamhshocraithe "
"HTML:doc: `giuirléid` le húsáid agus réimse foirme á rindreáil (m.sh. ``,`` "
"`,` ``)."

msgid ""
"The minimal validation requirements, used in Django's admin and in "
"automatically-generated forms."
msgstr ""
"Na ceanglais bailíochtaithe íosta, a úsáidtear i riarachán Django agus i "
"bhfoirmeacha a ghintear go huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"Django ships with dozens of built-in field types; you can find the complete "
"list in the :ref:`model field reference <model-field-types>`. You can easily "
"write your own fields if Django's built-in ones don't do the trick; "
"see :doc:`/howto/custom-model-fields`."
msgstr ""
"<model-field-types>Loingíonn Django le mórán cineálacha réimse ionsuite; is "
"féidir leat an liosta iomlán a fháil in:ref: `tagairt réimse samhail `. Is "
"féidir leat do réimsí féin a scríobh go héasca mura ndéanann cinn ionsuite "
"Django an cleas; féach: doc: `/howto/custom-model-fields`."

msgid "Field options"
msgstr "Roghanna réimse"

msgid ""
"Each field takes a certain set of field-specific arguments (documented in "
"the :ref:`model field reference <model-field-types>`). For "
"example, :class:`~django.db.models.CharField` (and its subclasses) require "
"a :attr:`~django.db.models.CharField.max_length` argument which specifies "
"the size of the ``VARCHAR`` database field used to store the data."
msgstr ""
"<model-field-types>Glacann gach réimse sraith áirithe d'argóintí "
"réimsiúnacha (doiciméadaithe in:ref: `tagairt réimse samhail `). Mar "
"shampla, éilíonn :class: `~django.db.models.charfield` (agus a fho-aicmí) "
"a:attr: `~django.db.models.charfield.max_Length` argóint a shonraíonn méid "
"an réimse bunachar sonraí ``VARCHAR`` a úsáidtear chun na sonraí a stóráil."

msgid ""
"There's also a set of common arguments available to all field types. All are "
"optional. They're fully explained in the :ref:`reference <common-model-field-"
"options>`, but here's a quick summary of the most often-used ones:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sraith argóintí coitianta ar fáil do gach cineál réimse freisin. Tá gach "
"ceann roghnach. Mínítear iad go hiomlán in:ref: `tagairt <common-model-field-"
"options>`, ach seo achoimre tapa ar na cinn is minice a úsáidtear:"

msgid ":attr:`~Field.null`"
msgstr ":attr: `~field.null`"

msgid ""
"If ``True``, Django will store empty values as ``NULL`` in the database. "
"Default is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``True``, stóráilfidh Django luachanna folmha mar ``NULL`` sa "
"bhunachar sonraí. Is é “False” réamhshocraithe."

msgid ":attr:`~Field.blank`"
msgstr ":attr: `~Field.blank`"

msgid "If ``True``, the field is allowed to be blank. Default is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá “Fíor”, ceadaítear don réimse a bheith bán. Is é “False” "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Note that this is different than :attr:`~Field.null`. :attr:`~Field.null` is "
"purely database-related, whereas :attr:`~Field.blank` is validation-related. "
"If a field has :attr:`blank=True <Field.blank>`, form validation will allow "
"entry of an empty value. If a field has :attr:`blank=False <Field.blank>`, "
"the field will be required."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil sé seo difriúil ná: attr: `~Field.null`. :attr: "
"`~Field.null` a bhaineann le bunachar sonraí amháin, áit a bhaineann le "
"bailíochtú: attr: `~Field.blank`. Má tá réimse ag: attr: `Blank=true "
"<Field.blank>`, ceadóidh bailíochtú foirm luach folamh a iontráil. Má tá "
"réimse ag: attr: `Blank=false <Field.blank>`, beidh an réimse ag teastáil."

msgid ":attr:`~Field.choices`"
msgstr ":attr: `~Field.Choices`"

msgid ""
"A :term:`sequence` of 2-value tuples, a :term:`mapping`, "
"an :ref:`enumeration type <field-choices-enum-types>`, or a callable (that "
"expects no arguments and returns any of the previous formats), to use as "
"choices for this field. If this is given, the default form widget will be a "
"select box instead of the standard text field and will limit choices to the "
"choices given."
msgstr ""
"A: Téarma: `seicheamh` de thúpaí 2-luach, a: term: `maping`, an:ref: `cineál "
"áireamha`, nó inghlaonta (nach bhfuil súil ag aon argóintí agus a thugann "
"<field-choices-enum-types>aon cheann de na formáidí roimhe seo ar ais), le "
"húsáid mar roghanna don réimse seo. Má thugtar é seo, is bosca roghnaithe é "
"an giuirléid fhoirme réamhshocraithe in ionad an réimse téacs caighdeánach "
"agus teorannfaidh sé roghanna leis na roghanna a thugtar."

