msgstr "Cruthaítear imirce nua gach uair a athraíonn ord na “roghanna”."

msgid ""
"The first element in each tuple is the value that will be stored in the "
"database. The second element is displayed by the field's form widget."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad ghné i ngach tuple an luach a stóráilfear sa bhunachar sonraí. "
"Taispeántar an dara gné ag giuirléid fhoirme an réimse."

msgid ""
"Given a model instance, the display value for a field with ``choices`` can "
"be accessed using the :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.get_FOO_display` "
"method. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar shampla samhail, is féidir rochtain a fháil ar an luach "
"taispeána do réimse le ``roghnaí`` ag baint úsáide as an modh: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.get_foo_display`. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"You can also use enumeration classes to define ``choices`` in a concise way::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ranganna áireamh a úsáid freisin chun “roghanna” a shainiú ar "
"bhealach gonta:"

msgid ""
"Further examples are available in the :ref:`model field reference <field-"
"choices>`."
msgstr ""
"<field-choices>Tá samplaí breise ar fáil in:ref: `tagairt réimse samhail `."

msgid ":attr:`~Field.default`"
msgstr ":attr: `~field.default`"

msgid ""
"The default value for the field. This can be a value or a callable object. "
"If callable it will be called every time a new object is created."
msgstr ""
"An luach réamhshocraithe don réimse. Is féidir leis seo a bheith ina luach "
"nó ina réad inghlaonta. Má tá sé inghlaoch, glaofar air gach uair a "
"chruthaítear réad nua."

msgid ":attr:`~Field.db_default`"
msgstr ":attr: `~field.db_default`"

msgid ""
"The database-computed default value for the field. This can be a literal "
"value or a database function."
msgstr ""
"An luach réamhshocraithe ríofa bunachar sonraí don réimse. Is féidir leis "
"seo a bheith ina luach litriúil nó ina fheidhm bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"If both ``db_default`` and :attr:`Field.default` are set, ``default`` will "
"take precedence when creating instances in Python code. ``db_default`` will "
"still be set at the database level and will be used when inserting rows "
"outside of the ORM or when adding a new field in a migration."
msgstr ""
"Má tá `db_default`` agus:attr: `Field.default` araon socraithe, tabharfaidh "
"``default`` tosaíocht agus cásanna á chruthú i gcód Python. Socrófar "
"``db_default`` fós ag leibhéal an bhunachar sonraí agus úsáidfear é agus "
"sraitheanna á chur isteach lasmuigh den ORM nó nuair a chuirtear réimse nua "
"i imirce."

msgid ":attr:`~Field.help_text`"
msgstr ":attr: `~field.help_text`"

msgid ""
"Extra \"help\" text to be displayed with the form widget. It's useful for "
"documentation even if your field isn't used on a form."
msgstr ""
"Téacs breise “cabhrach” le taispeáint leis an ngiuirléid fhoirme. Tá sé "
"úsáideach le haghaidh doiciméadú fiú mura n-úsáidtear do réimse ar fhoirm."

msgid ":attr:`~Field.primary_key`"
msgstr ":attr: `~Field.primary_key`"

msgid "If ``True``, this field is the primary key for the model."
msgstr "Má tá ``True``, is é an réimse seo an príomh-eochair don tsamhail."

msgid ""
"If you don't specify :attr:`primary_key=True <Field.primary_key>` for any "
"fields in your model, Django will automatically add a field to hold the "
"primary key, so you don't need to set :attr:`primary_key=True "
"<Field.primary_key>` on any of your fields unless you want to override the "
"default primary-key behavior. For more, see :ref:`automatic-primary-key-"
"fields`."
msgstr ""

