"Tá sé go hiomlán ceart go leor samhail a cheangal le ceann amháin ó aip "
"eile. Chun seo a dhéanamh, iompórtáil an tsamhail ghaolmhar ag barr an "
"chomhaid ina bhfuil do mhúnla sainmhínithe. Ansin, déan tagairt don rang "
"samhail eile cibé áit is gá. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use a lazy reference to the related model, specified "
"as a string in the format ``\"app_label.ModelName\"``. This does not require "
"the related model to be imported. For example::"
msgstr ""

msgid "See :ref:`lazy relationships <lazy-relationships>` for more details."
msgstr ""

msgid "Field name restrictions"
msgstr "Srianta ainm réimse"

msgid "Django places some restrictions on model field names:"
msgstr "Cuireann Django roinnt srianta ar ainmneacha réimse samhail:"

msgid ""
"A field name cannot be a Python reserved word, because that would result in "
"a Python syntax error. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir ainm réimse a bheith ina fhocal áirithe Python, toisc go mbeadh "
"earráid comhréireachta Python mar thoradh air sin. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"A field name cannot contain more than one underscore in a row, due to the "
"way Django's query lookup syntax works. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir níos mó ná béim amháin i ndiaidh a chéile i ainm réimse, mar "
"gheall ar an mbealach a oibríonn comhréir cuardaigh ceisteanna Django. Mar "
"shampla::"

msgid "A field name cannot end with an underscore, for similar reasons."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir le hainm réimse deireadh a chur le béim, ar chúiseanna comhchosúla."

msgid ""
"A field name cannot be ``check``, as this would override the check "
"framework's ``Model.check()`` method."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These limitations can be worked around, though, because your field name "
"doesn't necessarily have to match your database column name. See "
"the :attr:`~Field.db_column` option."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na teorainneacha seo a oibriú timpeall, áfach, toisc nach gá go "
"gcaithfidh d'ainm réimse d'ainm colún bunachar sonraí a mheaitseáil. Féach "
"an roghna:attr: `~Field.db_Column`."

msgid ""
"SQL reserved words, such as ``join``, ``where`` or ``select``, *are* allowed "
"as model field names, because Django escapes all database table names and "
"column names in every underlying SQL query. It uses the quoting syntax of "
"your particular database engine."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear focail fhorchoimeádta SQL, mar shampla ``join`, ``, ```nó "
"``roghnaigh``, ** mar ainmneacha réimse samhail, toisc go n-éalaíonn Django "
"gach ainm tábla bunachar sonraí agus ainmneacha colún i ngach ceist "
"bhunúsach SQL. Úsáideann sé comhréir luachana d'inneall bunachar sonraí "
"áirithe."

msgid "Custom field types"
msgstr "cineálacha réimse saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"If one of the existing model fields cannot be used to fit your purposes, or "
"if you wish to take advantage of some less common database column types, you "
"can create your own field class. Full coverage of creating your own fields "
"is provided in :doc:`/howto/custom-model-fields`."
msgstr ""
"Mura féidir ceann de na réimsí samhlacha atá ann cheana a úsáid chun do "
"chuspóirí a fheistiú, nó más mian leat leas a bhaint as roinnt cineálacha "
"colún bunachar sonraí nach bhfuil chomh coitianta, is féidir leat do rang "
"réimse féin a chruthú. Cuirtear clúdach iomlán ar do réimsí féin a chruthú "
"ar fáil in:doc: `/howto/custom-model-fields`."

msgid "``Meta`` options"
msgstr "Roghanna ``Meta``"

msgid "Give your model metadata by using an inner ``class Meta``, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair meiteashonraí do mhúnla trí ``aicme Meta`` istigh a úsáid, mar sin:"

msgid ""
"Model metadata is \"anything that's not a field\", such as ordering options "
"(:attr:`~Options.ordering`), database table name "
"(:attr:`~Options.db_table`), or human-readable singular and plural names "
"(:attr:`~Options.verbose_name` and :attr:`~Options.verbose_name_plural`). "
"None are required, and adding ``class Meta`` to a model is completely "
"optional."
msgstr ""
"Is é meiteashonraí samhail “aon rud nach réimse”, mar shampla roghanna "
"ordaithe (:attr: `~Options.Ordering`), ainm tábla bunachar sonraí (:attr: "
"`~Options.db_table`), nó ainmneacha uaineacha agus iolra inléite don duine "
"(:attr: `~Options.verbose_name_plural`). Níl aon cheann de dhíth, agus tá sé "
"go hiomlán roghnach ``aicme Meta ``a chur le samhail."

msgid ""
"A complete list of all possible ``Meta`` options can be found in "
"the :doc:`model option reference </ref/models/options>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir liosta iomlán de na roghanna `Meta`` féideartha go léir a fháil "
"in:doc: `tagairt rogha samhail`. </ref/models/options>"

msgid "Model attributes"
msgstr "Tréithe samhail"

msgid "``objects``"
msgstr "```ruda``"

msgid ""
"The most important attribute of a model is "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.Manager`. It's the interface through which "
"database query operations are provided to Django models and is used "
"to :ref:`retrieve the instances <retrieving-objects>` from the database. If "
"no custom ``Manager`` is defined, the default name "
"is :attr:`~django.db.models.Model.objects`. Managers are only accessible via "
"model classes, not the model instances."
msgstr ""
"Is é an tréith is tábhachtaí de mhúnla ná: aicme: "
"`~django.db.models.manager`. Is é an comhéadan trína gcuirtear oibríochtaí "
"fiosrúcháin bunachar sonraí ar fáil do mhúnlaí Django agus úsáidtear é chun: "
"ref: `na cásanna a aisghabháil ón mbunachar son <retrieving-objects>raí. "
"Mura sainmhínítear ``Bainiste`` saincheaptha, is é an t-ainm "
"réamhshocraithe:attr: `~Django.db.Models.Model.Objects`. Ní féidir "
"bainisteoirí inrochtana ach trí ranganna samhail, ní na cásanna samhail."

msgid "Model methods"
msgstr "Modhanna múnla"

msgid ""
"Define custom methods on a model to add custom \"row-level\" functionality "
"to your objects. Whereas :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` methods are "
"intended to do \"table-wide\" things, model methods should act on a "
"particular model instance."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínigh modhanna saincheaptha ar mhúnla chun feidhmiúlacht saincheaptha "
"“leibhéal sraithe” a chur le do chuid rudaí. Cá bhfuil: Class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Manager` i gceist le modhanna rudaí “ar fud an tábla” a "
"dhéanamh, ba cheart do mhodhanna samhail gníomhú ar shampla samhail áirithe."

msgid ""
"This is a valuable technique for keeping business logic in one place -- the "
"model."
msgstr ""
"Is teicníc luachmhar é seo chun loighic ghnó a choinneáil in aon áit amháin "
"- an tsamhail."

