msgstr "Is é an modh deireanach sa sampla seo a: téarma: `maoin `."

msgid ""
"The :doc:`model instance reference </ref/models/instances>` has a complete "
"list of :ref:`methods automatically given to each model <model-instance-"
"methods>`. You can override most of these -- see `overriding predefined "
"model methods`_, below -- but there are a couple that you'll almost always "
"want to define:"
msgstr ""
"</ref/models/instances> <model-instance-methods>Tá liosta iomlán de:ref: "
"`modhanna a thugtar go huathoibríoch do gach samhail `sa tagairt samhail: "
"Doc: `samhail tagair`. Is féidir leat an chuid is mó díobh seo a shárú - "
"féach `modhanna samhail réamhshainithe a shárú `_, thíos - ach tá lánúin ann "
"a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a shainiú beagnach i gcónaí:"

msgid ":meth:`~Model.__str__`"
msgstr ": meth: `~ Múnla. __str__`"

msgid ""
"A Python \"magic method\" that returns a string representation of any "
"object. This is what Python and Django will use whenever a model instance "
"needs to be coerced and displayed as a plain string. Most notably, this "
"happens when you display an object in an interactive console or in the admin."
msgstr ""
"“Modh draíochta” Python a thugann léiriú teaghrán ar aon rud ar ais. Seo a "
"úsáidfidh Python agus Django aon uair is gá samhail samhail a iallú agus a "
"thaispeáint mar shreang simplí. Go háirithe, tarlaíonn sé seo nuair a "
"thaispeánann tú réad i gconsól idirghníomhach nó sa riarachán."

msgid ""
"You'll always want to define this method; the default isn't very helpful at "
"all."
msgstr ""
"Beidh tú ag iarraidh an modh seo a shainiú i gcónaí; ní bhíonn an "
"réamhshocrú an-chabhrach ar chor ar"

