"It's important to remember to call the superclass method -- that's that "
"``super().save(**kwargs)`` business -- to ensure that the object still gets "
"saved into the database. If you forget to call the superclass method, the "
"default behavior won't happen and the database won't get touched."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach cuimhneamh ar an modh sáraicme a ghlaoch - sin an gnó sin "
"``super () .save (** kwargs) `- chun a chinntiú go sábhálfar an réad sa "
"bhunachar sonraí fós. Má dhéanann tú dearmad glaoch ar an modh sáraicme, ní "
"tharlóidh an t-iompar réamhshocraithe agus ní dhéanfar teagmháil leis an "
"mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"It's also important that you pass through the arguments that can be passed "
"to the model method -- that's what the ``**kwargs`` bit does. Django will, "
"from time to time, extend the capabilities of built-in model methods, adding "
"new keyword arguments. If you use ``**kwargs`` in your method definitions, "
"you are guaranteed that your code will automatically support those arguments "
"when they are added."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach freisin go dtéann tú tríd na hargóintí is féidir a chur ar "
"aghaidh chuig an modh samhail - sin an rud a dhéanann an giotán `**kwargs "
"``. Leathnóidh Django, ó am go ham, cumais modhanna samhail ionsuite, ag cur "
"argóintí eochairfhocal nua leis. Má úsáideann tú ``**kwargs ``i do "
"shainmhínithe ar mhodh, ráthaítear duit go dtacóidh do chód leis na "
"hargóintí sin go huathoibríoch nuair a chuirtear iad leis."

msgid ""
"If you wish to update a field value in the :meth:`~Model.save` method, you "
"may also want to have this field added to the ``update_fields`` keyword "
"argument. This will ensure the field is saved when ``update_fields`` is "
"specified. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat luach réimse a nuashonrú sa modh:meth: `~Model.save`, "
"b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an réimse seo a chur leis an argóint eochairfhocal "
"``update_fields``. Cinnteoidh sé seo go sábhálfar an réimse nuair a "
"shonraítear ``update_fields``. Mar shampla::"

msgid "See :ref:`ref-models-update-fields` for more details."
msgstr "Féach: ref: `ref-models-update-fields` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Overridden model methods are not called on bulk operations"
msgstr "Ní ghlaítear ar mhodhanna samhlacha athsháraithe ar mhór-oibríochtaí"

msgid ""
"Note that the :meth:`~Model.delete()` method for an object is not "
"necessarily called when :ref:`deleting objects in bulk using a QuerySet "
"<topics-db-queries-delete>` or as a result of a :attr:`cascading delete "
"<django.db.models.ForeignKey.on_delete>`. To ensure customized delete logic "
"gets executed, you can use :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_delete` and/"
"or :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_delete` signals."
msgstr ""
"<topics-db-queries-delete><django.db.models.ForeignKey.on_delete>Tabhair "
"faoi deara nach gá go dtugtar ar an modh:meth: `~model.delete () `le "
"haghaidh réad nuai:ref: `rudaí a scriosadh ar an mórchóir ag baint úsáide as "
"QuerySet` nó mar thoradh ar a:attr: `scriosadh cascading `. Chun a chinntiú "
"go bhforghníomhaítear loighic scriosta saincheaptha, is féidir leat "
"comharthaí: `~django.db.models.signals.pre_delete` agus/nó: data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_delete` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, there isn't a workaround "
"when :meth:`creating<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>` "
"or :meth:`updating<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update>` objects in bulk, "
"since none "
"of :meth:`~Model.save()`, :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_save`, "
"and :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_save` are called."
msgstr ""
"Ar an drochuair, níl réiteach ann nuain:meth: `ag cruthú `nó: meth: `nu "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>ashonrú` ruda "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update>í ar an mórchóir, ós rud é nach "
"dtugtar aon cheann de:meth: `~model.save () `, :data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_save`, agus:data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_save`."

msgid "Executing custom SQL"
msgstr "SQL saincheaptha a fheidhmiú"

msgid ""
"Another common pattern is writing custom SQL statements in model methods and "
"module-level methods. For more details on using raw SQL, see the "
"documentation on :doc:`using raw SQL</topics/db/sql>`."
msgstr ""
"Patrún coitianta eile is ea ráitis SQL saincheaptha a scríobh i modhanna "
"samhail agus modhanna leibhéal modúl. Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí maidir le "
"SQL amh a úsáid, féach an doiciméadú ar:doc: `using</topics/db/sql> raw SQL`."

msgid "Model inheritance"
msgstr "Oidhreacht múnla"

msgid ""
"Model inheritance in Django works almost identically to the way normal class "
"inheritance works in Python, but the basics at the beginning of the page "
"should still be followed. That means the base class should "
"subclass :class:`django.db.models.Model`."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn oidhreacht mhúnla i Django beagnach cosúil leis an mbealach a "
"oibríonn gnáthoidhreacht aicme i Python, ach ba cheart na buneilimintí ag "
"tús an leathanaigh a leanúint fós. Ciallaíonn sé sin gur chóir don rang bonn "
"fo-aicme: class: `Django.db.Models.Model`."

msgid ""
"The only decision you have to make is whether you want the parent models to "
"be models in their own right (with their own database tables), or if the "
"parents are just holders of common information that will only be visible "
"through the child models."
msgstr ""
"Is é an t-aon chinneadh a chaithfidh tú a dhéanamh ná an dteastaíonn uait go "
"mbeadh na samhlacha tuismitheoirí ina samhlacha ina gceart féin (lena "
"dtáblaí bunachar sonraí féin), nó mura bhfuil na tuismitheoirí ach "
"sealbhóirí faisnéise coiteann nach mbeidh le feiceáil ach trí na samhlacha "
"leanaí."

msgid "There are three styles of inheritance that are possible in Django."
msgstr "Tá trí stíl oidhreachta ann atá indéanta i Django."

msgid ""
"Often, you will just want to use the parent class to hold information that "
"you don't want to have to type out for each child model. This class isn't "
"going to ever be used in isolation, so :ref:`abstract-base-classes` are what "
"you're after."
msgstr ""
"Go minic, ní bheidh tú ag iarraidh ach an rang tuismitheoirí a úsáid chun "
"faisnéis a shealbhú nach dteastaíonn uait a chlóscríobh do gach samhail "
"linbh. Ní úsáidfear an rang seo ina n-aonar riamh, mar sin: ref: Is iad "
"`abstract-base-classes` an rud atá ina dhiaidh leat."

msgid ""
"If you're subclassing an existing model (perhaps something from another "
"application entirely) and want each model to have its own database "
"table, :ref:`multi-table-inheritance` is the way to go."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag fo-aicmiú samhail atá ann cheana (rud éigin ó fheidhmchlár eile "
"go hiomlán b'fhéidir) agus má theastaíonn uait go mbeadh a tábla bunachar "
"sonraí féin ag gach samhail, :ref: is é `il-tábla-oidhreacht `an bealach le "
"dul."

msgid ""
"Finally, if you only want to modify the Python-level behavior of a model, "
"without changing the models fields in any way, you can use :ref:`proxy-"
"models`."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, mura dteastaíonn uait ach iompar samhail ar leibhéal Python "
"a mhodhnú, gan réimsí na samhlacha a athrú ar bhealach ar bith, is féidir "
"leat:ref: `proxy-models` a úsáid."

msgid "Abstract base classes"
msgstr "Aicmí bonn teibí"

msgid ""
"Abstract base classes are useful when you want to put some common "
"information into a number of other models. You write your base class and put "
"``abstract=True`` in the :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` class. This model will "
"then not be used to create any database table. Instead, when it is used as a "
"base class for other models, its fields will be added to those of the child "
"class."
msgstr ""
"Tá ranganna bonn teibí úsáideach nuair is mian leat roinnt faisnéise "
"coitianta a chur i roinnt samhlacha eile. <meta-options>Scríobhann tú do "
"rang bonn agus cuireann tú ``abstract=True`` sa rang:ref: `Meta `. Ní "
"úsáidfear an tsamhail seo ansin chun aon tábla bunachar sonraí a chruthú. "
"Ina áit sin, nuair a úsáidtear é mar bhunrang do mhúnlaí eile, cuirfear a "
"réimsí le réimsí ranga an linbh."

msgid "An example::"
msgstr "Sampla::"

msgid ""
"The ``Student`` model will have three fields: ``name``, ``age`` and "
"``home_group``. The ``CommonInfo`` model cannot be used as a normal Django "
"model, since it is an abstract base class. It does not generate a database "
"table or have a manager, and cannot be instantiated or saved directly."
msgstr ""
"Beidh trí réimse ag an tsamhail ``Mac Léinn ``: `ainm``, `aois ``agus "
"``grúpa_baile``. Ní féidir an tsamhail `CommonInfo ``a úsáid mar "
"ghnáthmhúnla Django, ós rud é gur aicme bonn teibí é. Ní ghineann sé tábla "
"bunachar sonraí ná ní bhfuil bainisteoir aige, agus ní féidir é a "
"thionscnamh nó a shábháil go díreach."

msgid ""
"Fields inherited from abstract base classes can be overridden with another "
"field or value, or be removed with ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir réimsí oidhreachta ó ranganna bonn teibí a shárú le réimse nó "
"luach eile, nó iad a bhaint le ``None``."

msgid ""
"For many uses, this type of model inheritance will be exactly what you want. "
"It provides a way to factor out common information at the Python level, "
"while still only creating one database table per child model at the database "
"level."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le go leor úsáidí, beidh an cineál seo oidhreachta samhail go díreach "
"mar a theastaíonn uait. Soláthraíonn sé bealach chun faisnéis choiteann a "
"bhaint amach ag leibhéal Python, agus ní chruthaíonn sé ach tábla bunachar "
"sonraí amháin in aghaidh an tsamhail linbh ag leibhéal an bhunachar sonraí."

msgid "``Meta`` inheritance"
msgstr "Oidhreacht ``Meta``"

msgid ""
"When an abstract base class is created, Django makes any :ref:`Meta <meta-"
"options>` inner class you declared in the base class available as an "
"attribute. If a child class does not declare its own :ref:`Meta <meta-"
"options>` class, it will inherit the parent's :ref:`Meta <meta-options>`. If "
"the child wants to extend the parent's :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` class, it "
"can subclass it. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chruthaítear rang bonn teib <meta-options>í, déanann Django aon "
"aicme istigh: ref: `Meta `a dhearbhaigh tú sa rang bonn atá ar fáil mar "
"thréith. <meta-options>Mura dhearbhóidh rang linbh a rang féin:ref: `Meta "
"<meta-options>`, beidh sé oidhreacht ar an tuismitheoirí:ref: `Meta`. Más "
"mian leis an leanbh rang an tuismitheora: ref: `Meta <meta-options>`a "
"leathnú, is féidir leis é a fho-aicmiú. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Django does make one adjustment to the :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` class of "
"an abstract base class: before installing the :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` "
"attribute, it sets ``abstract=False``. This means that children of abstract "
"base classes don't automatically become abstract classes themselves. To make "
"an abstract base class that inherits from another abstract base class, you "
"need to explicitly set ``abstract=True`` on the child."
msgstr ""
"<meta-options>Déanann Django coigeartú amháin ar <meta-options>aicme: ref: "
"`Meta `de bhonn teibí: sula ndéantar an tréith: ref: `Meta` a shuiteáil, "
"leagann sé ``abstract = false ``. Ciallaíonn sé seo nach n-éiríonn leanaí "
"bunranganna teibí ina ranganna teibí go huathoibríoch iad féin. Chun rang "
"bonn teibí a dhéanamh a thagann oidhreacht ó rang bonn teibí eile, ní mór "
"duit ``abstract=True`` a shocrú go sainráite ar an leanbh."

msgid ""
"Some attributes won't make sense to include in the :ref:`Meta <meta-"
"options>` class of an abstract base class. For example, including "
"``db_table`` would mean that all the child classes (the ones that don't "
"specify their own :ref:`Meta <meta-options>`) would use the same database "
"table, which is almost certainly not what you want."
msgstr ""
"Ní bheidh ciall ar roinnt tréithe a chur san áireamh san aicme:ref: `Meta "
"<meta-options>`de rang bonn teibí. Mar shampla, lena n-áirítear ``db_table`` "
"chiallódh go n- <meta-options>úsáidfeadh na ranganna uile leanaí (na cinn "
"nach sonraíonn a gcuid féin: ref: `Meta `) an tábla bunachar sonraí céanna, "
"rud beagnach cinnte nach bhfuil an rud a theastaíonn uait."

msgid ""
"Due to the way Python inheritance works, if a child class inherits from "
"multiple abstract base classes, only the :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` options "
"from the first listed class will be inherited by default. To "
"inherit :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` options from multiple abstract base "
"classes, you must explicitly declare the :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` "
"inheritance. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an mbealach a oibríonn oidhreacht Python, má fhaigheann rang "
"linbh oidhreacht ó iliomad bunaicmí teibí, ní bhe <meta-options>idh ach na "
"roghanna: ref: `Meta `ón gcéad rang liostaithe oidhreacht de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. <meta-options>Chun roghanna oidhreacht:ref: `Meta <meta-"
"options>`ó iliomad bunaicmí teibí, ní mór duit an oidhreacht: ref: `Meta` a "
"dhearbhú go sainráite. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Be careful with ``related_name`` and ``related_query_name``"
msgstr "Bí cúramach le ``ainm_gaolmhar ``agus ``ainm_ceisteanna gaolaitheach``"

msgid ""
"If you are using :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` "
"or :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_query_name` on a "
"``ForeignKey`` or ``ManyToManyField``, you must always specify a *unique* "
"reverse name and query name for the field. This would normally cause a "
"problem in abstract base classes, since the fields on this class are "
"included into each of the child classes, with exactly the same values for "
"the attributes (including :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` "
"and :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_query_name`) each time."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag baint úsáide:attr: `~django.db.models.foreignkey.related_name` "
"nó:attr: `~django.db.models.foreignkey.related_query_name` ar `ForeignKey`` "
"nó ``ManyTomanyField``, ní mór duit ainm aisiom*unique* a shonrú don réimse "
"i gcónaí. De ghnáth bheadh fadhb ann i ranganna bonn teibí, ós rud é go "
"gcuirtear na réimsí ar an rang seo san áireamh i ngach ceann de na ranganna "
"leanaí, leis na luachanna céanna do na tréithe (lena n-áirítear: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.~db.models.~django.related_query_name`) gach uair."

msgid ""
"To work around this problem, when you are "
"using :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` "
"or :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_query_name` in an abstract "
"base class (only), part of the value should contain ``'%(app_label)s'`` and "
"``'%(class)s'``."
msgstr ""
"Chun oibriú timpeall ar an bhfadhb seo, nuair a bhíonn tú ag baint "
"úsáide:attr: `~django.db.models.foreignkey.related_name` nó:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignkey.related_query_name` i rang bonn teibí "
"(amháin), ba chóir go mbeadh ``% (app_label)`` agus ``% (rang) s'``."

msgid ""
"``'%(class)s'`` is replaced by the lowercased name of the child class that "
"the field is used in."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear ainm íseal an aicme linbh ina n-úsáidtear an réimse in ionad `'% "
"(class) s'``."

msgid ""
"``'%(app_label)s'`` is replaced by the lowercased name of the app the child "
"class is contained within. Each installed application name must be unique "
"and the model class names within each app must also be unique, therefore the "
"resulting name will end up being different."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear ainm íseal an aip atá an rang linbh ann in ionad `'% (app_label) "
"s'``. Caithfidh gach ainm feidhmchláir suiteáilte a bheith uathúil agus "
"caithfidh ainmneacha aicme samhail laistigh de gach aip a bheith uathúil "
"freisin, mar sin beidh an t-ainm mar thoradh air sin difriúil."

msgid "For example, given an app ``common/models.py``::"
msgstr "Mar shampla, ag tabhairt faoi aip `common/models.py``:"

msgid "Along with another app ``rare/models.py``::"
msgstr "In éineacht le aip eile ``rare/models.py``:"

msgid ""
"The reverse name of the ``common.ChildA.m2m`` field will be "
"``common_childa_related`` and the reverse query name will be "
"``common_childas``. The reverse name of the ``common.ChildB.m2m`` field will "
"be ``common_childb_related`` and the reverse query name will be "
"``common_childbs``. Finally, the reverse name of the ``rare.ChildB.m2m`` "
"field will be ``rare_childb_related`` and the reverse query name will be "
"``rare_childbs``. It's up to you how you use the ``'%(class)s'`` and ``'%"
"(app_label)s'`` portion to construct your related name or related query name "
"but if you forget to use it, Django will raise errors when you perform "
"system checks (or run :djadmin:`migrate`)."
msgstr ""
"Is é `common_childa_related`` ainm droim an réimse ``common.childa.m2m`` "
"agus `common_childas`` is é `common_childas`` an t-ainm fiosrúcháin droim. "
"Is é `common_childb_related`` ainm droim an réimse ``common.childb.m2m`` "
"agus is é `common_childbs`` an t-ainm fiosrúcháin droim. Faoi dheireadh, is "
"é ``rare_childb_related`` ainm droim an réimse ``rare.childb.m2m`` agus is é "
"`rare_childbs`` an t-ainm fiosrúcháin droim. Is fútsa atá sé conas a "
"úsáideann tú an chuid ``'% (class) s'`` agus ```% (app_label) s'` chun "
"d'ainm gaolmhar nó d'ainm ceisteanna gaolmhar a thógáil ach má dhéanann tú "
"dearmad é a úsáid, ardóidh Django earráidí nuair a dhéanann tú seiceálacha "
"córais (nó run:djadmin: `migrate`)."

msgid ""
"If you don't specify a :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` "
"attribute for a field in an abstract base class, the default reverse name "
"will be the name of the child class followed by ``'_set'``, just as it "
"normally would be if you'd declared the field directly on the child class. "
"For example, in the above code, if "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` attribute was omitted, "
"the reverse name for the ``m2m`` field would be ``childa_set`` in the "
"``ChildA`` case and ``childb_set`` for the ``ChildB`` field."
msgstr ""
"Mura sonraíonn tú a: attr: `~django.db.models.foreignkey.related_name` "
"tréith do réimse i rang bonn teibí, is é an t-ainm cúil réamhshocraithe ainm "
"ranga an linbh ina dhiaidh sin ``'_set'``, díreach mar a bheadh sé de ghnáth "
"dá dhearbhaigh tú an réimse go díreach ar an rang linbh. Mar shampla, sa "
"chód thuas, má fhágfaí tréith an:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignkey.related_name`, an t-ainm droim don réimse "
"``m2m`` ná `childa_set`` sa chás ``Childa`` agus ``childb_set`` don réimse "
"``Childb``."

msgid "Multi-table inheritance"
msgstr "Oidhreacht il-tábla"

msgid ""
"The second type of model inheritance supported by Django is when each model "
"in the hierarchy is a model all by itself. Each model corresponds to its own "
"database table and can be queried and created individually. The inheritance "
"relationship introduces links between the child model and each of its "
"parents (via an automatically-"
"created :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField`). For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara cineál oidhreachta samhail a thacaíonn Django ná nuair a bhíonn "
"gach samhail san ordlathas ina samhail leis féin. Freagraíonn gach samhail "
"dá tábla bunachar sonraí féin agus is féidir é a fhiosrú agus a chruthú ina "
"n-aonar. Tugann an caidreamh oidhreachta naisc isteach idir samhail an linbh "
"agus gach ceann dá thuismitheoirí (trí:class: "
"`~django.db.models.onetoonefield`) a chruthaítear go huathoibríoch. Mar "
"shampla::"

msgid ""
"All of the fields of ``Place`` will also be available in ``Restaurant``, "
"although the data will reside in a different database table. So these are "
"both possible:"
msgstr ""
"Beidh na réimsí go léir de ``Áite`` ar fáil i ``Bialain`` freisin, cé go "
"mbeidh na sonraí ina gcónaí i dtábla bunachar sonraí difriúil. Mar sin is "
"féidir iad seo a dhéanamh:"

msgid ""
"If you have a ``Place`` that is also a ``Restaurant``, you can get from the "
"``Place`` object to the ``Restaurant`` object by using the lowercase version "
"of the model name:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``Áite`` agat atá ina ``Bialain`` freisin, is féidir leat teacht ón "
"réad ``Áite`` go dtí an réad ``Bialainne`` tríd an leagan beaga den ainm "
"samhail a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"However, if ``p`` in the above example was *not* a ``Restaurant`` (it had "
"been created directly as a ``Place`` object or was the parent of some other "
"class), referring to ``p.restaurant`` would raise a "
"``Restaurant.DoesNotExist`` exception."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, mura raibh `p`` sa sampla thuas*ní* ina `Bialann ``(cruthaíodh "
"é go díreach mar réad ``Plac`` nó gur tuismitheoir aicme éigin eile é), "
"d'ardódh tagairt do `p.restaurant`` eisceacht ``Restaurant.doesNotExist``."

msgid ""
"The automatically-created :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` on "
"``Restaurant`` that links it to ``Place`` looks like this::"
msgstr ""
"Breathnaítear go huathoibríoch: class: `~django.db.models.onetoonefield` ar "
"``Restaurant`` a nascann é le ``Plac`` mar seo:"

msgid ""
"You can override that field by declaring your "
"own :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` with :attr:`parent_link=True "
"<django.db.models.OneToOneField.parent_link>` on ``Restaurant``."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.OneToOneField.parent_link>Is féidir leat an réimse sin a "
"shárú trí do chuid féin a dhearbhú:: `~django.db.models.onetoonefield` le: "
"attr: `Parent_link=True `ar ``Restaurant``."

msgid "``Meta`` and multi-table inheritance"
msgstr "``Meta`` agus oidhreacht il-tábla"

msgid ""
"In the multi-table inheritance situation, it doesn't make sense for a child "
"class to inherit from its parent's :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` class. All "
"the :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` options have already been applied to the "
"parent class and applying them again would normally only lead to "
"contradictory behavior (this is in contrast with the abstract base class "
"case, where the base class doesn't exist in its own right)."
msgstr ""
"<meta-options>Sa staid oidhreachta iltábla, níl sé ciall do rang linbh "
"oidhreacht a thabhairt dá thuismitheoirí:ref: `Meta `. Cuireadh na <meta-"
"options>roghanna uile: ref: `Meta `i bhfeidhm cheana féin ar an rang "
"tuismitheoirí agus de ghnáth ní bheadh iompar contrártha mar thoradh orthu a "
"chur i bhfeidhm arís (tá sé seo i gcodarsnacht leis an gcás bunaicme teibí, "
"i gcás nach bhfuil an bunaicme ann féin)."

msgid ""
"So a child model does not have access to its parent's :ref:`Meta <meta-"
"options>` class. However, there are a few limited cases where the child "
"inherits behavior from the parent: if the child does not specify "
"an :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.ordering` attribute or "
"a :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.get_latest_by` attribute, it will inherit "
"these from its parent."
msgstr ""
"<meta-options>Mar sin níl rochtain ag samhail leanbh ar rang a "
"thuismitheoir:ref: `Meta `. Mar sin féin, tá cúpla cás teoranta ann ina n-"
"oidhreann an leanbh iompar ón tuismitheoir: mura sonraíonn an leanbh tréith: "
"`~django.db.models.options.ordering` nó a:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.get_latest_by` tréith, oidhreoidh sé iad seo óna "
"thuismitheoir."

msgid ""
"If the parent has an ordering and you don't want the child to have any "
"natural ordering, you can explicitly disable it::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá ordú ag an tuismitheoir agus mura dteastaíonn uait go mbeadh aon ordú "
"nádúrtha ag an leanbh, is féidir leat é a dhíchumasú go sainráite:"

msgid "Inheritance and reverse relations"
msgstr "Caidreamh oidhreachta agus droim ar ais"

msgid ""
"Because multi-table inheritance uses an "
"implicit :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` to link the child and the "
"parent, it's possible to move from the parent down to the child, as in the "
"above example. However, this uses up the name that is the "
"default :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` value "
"for :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` relations.  If you are "
"putting those types of relations on a subclass of the parent model, you "
"**must** specify the :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` "
"attribute on each such field. If you forget, Django will raise a validation "
"error."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go n-úsáideann oidhreacht il-tábla implit:class: "
"`~django.db.models.onetoonefield` chun an leanbh agus an tuismitheoir a "
"nascadh, is féidir bogadh ón tuismitheoir síos go dtí an leanbh, mar atá sa "
"sampla thuas. Mar sin féin, úsáideann sé seo an t-ainm atá an luach "
"réamhshocraithe:attr: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey.Related_Name` le "
"haghaidh caidrimh: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey` agus:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.manyToManyField`. Má tá na cineálacha caidrimh sin á chur "
"agat ar fho-aicme den tsamhail tuismitheora, ní mór duit** an tréith: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey.related_name` a shonrú ar gach réimse den sórt "
"sin. Má dhéanann tú dearmad, ardóidh Django earráid bailíochtaithe."

msgid ""
"For example, using the above ``Place`` class again, let's create another "
"subclass with a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, ag baint úsáide as an rang ``Place`` thuas arís, cruthaímid fo-"
"aicme eile le a:class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField`:"

msgid "This results in the error:"
msgstr "Mar thoradh air seo tá an earráid:"

msgid ""
"Adding ``related_name`` to the ``customers`` field as follows would resolve "
"the error: ``models.ManyToManyField(Place, related_name='provider')``."
msgstr ""
"Ag cur ``related_name`` leis an réimse ``custaiméirí ``mar seo a leanas "
"réitfeadh an earráid: ``Models.manyTomanyField (Place, "
"related_name='provider')``."

msgid "Specifying the parent link field"
msgstr "An réimse nasc tuismitheoireachta"

msgid ""
"As mentioned, Django will automatically create "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` linking your child class back to "
"any non-abstract parent models. If you want to control the name of the "
"attribute linking back to the parent, you can create your "
"own :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` and set :attr:`parent_link=True "
"<django.db.models.OneToOneField.parent_link>` to indicate that your field is "
"the link back to the parent class."
msgstr ""
"Mar a luadh, cruthóidh Django a:class: `~django.db.models.onetoonefield` go "
"huathoibríoch a nascann rang do pháiste ar ais le haon samhlacha "
"tuismitheoirí neamh-teibí. <django.db.models.OneToOneField.parent_link>Más "
"mian leat ainm na tréithe a nascann ar ais leis an tuismitheoir a rialú, is "
"féidir leat do chuid féin a chruthú: class: "
"`~django.db.models.onetoonefield` agus set:attr: `Parent_link=True `chun a "
"léiriú gurb é do réimse an nasc ar ais chuig an rang tuismitheora."

msgid ""
"When using :ref:`multi-table inheritance <multi-table-inheritance>`, a new "
"database table is created for each subclass of a model. This is usually the "
"desired behavior, since the subclass needs a place to store any additional "
"data fields that are not present on the base class. Sometimes, however, you "
"only want to change the Python behavior of a model -- perhaps to change the "
"default manager, or add a new method."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear: ref: `oidhreacht il-tábla <multi-table-inheritance>`, "
"cruthaítear tábla bunachar sonraí nua do gach fo-aicme de mhúnla. Is é seo "
"de ghnáth an t-iompar atá ag teastáil, ós rud é go dteastaíonn áit ón bhfo-"
"rang chun aon réimsí sonraí breise nach bhfuil i láthair ar an rang bonn a "
"stóráil. Uaireanta, áfach, ní theastaíonn uait ach iompar Python samhail a "
"athrú - b'fhéidir an bainisteoir réamhshocraithe a athrú, nó modh nua a chur "
"leis."

msgid ""
"This is what proxy model inheritance is for: creating a *proxy* for the "
"original model. You can create, delete and update instances of the proxy "
"model and all the data will be saved as if you were using the original (non-"
"proxied) model. The difference is that you can change things like the "
"default model ordering or the default manager in the proxy, without having "
"to alter the original."
msgstr ""
"Seo a bhfuil oidhreacht samhail seachfhreastalaí ann: * proxy* a chruthú don "
"tsamhail bhunaidh. Is féidir leat cásanna den tsamhail seachfhreastalaí a "
"chruthú, a scriosadh agus a nuashonrú agus sábhálfar na sonraí go léir "
"amhail is dá mbeadh an tsamhail bhunaidh (neamh-sheachadaithe) á úsáid agat. "
"Is í an difríocht ná gur féidir leat rudaí mar ordú an tsamhail "
"réamhshocraithe nó an bainisteoir réamhshocraithe sa seachfhreastalaí a "
"athrú, gan an bunaidh a athrú."

msgid ""
"Proxy models are declared like normal models. You tell Django that it's a "
"proxy model by setting the :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.proxy` attribute "
"of the ``Meta`` class to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Fógraítear samhlacha seachfhreastalaí cosúil le gn Deir tú le Django gur "
"samhail seachfhreastalaí é trí:attr: `~django.db.models.options.proxy` "
"tréith an aicme ``Meta`` a shocrú go ``True``."

msgid ""
"For example, suppose you want to add a method to the ``Person`` model. You "
"can do it like this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, cuir i gcás gur mhaith leat modh a chur leis an tsamhail "
"``Person`. Is féidir leat é a dhéanamh mar seo::"

msgid ""
"The ``MyPerson`` class operates on the same database table as its parent "
"``Person`` class. In particular, any new instances of ``Person`` will also "
"be accessible through ``MyPerson``, and vice-versa:"
msgstr ""
"Feidhmíonn an rang `MyPerson`` ar an tábla bunachar sonraí céanna leis an "
"rang ``Person`` a thuismitheoir. Go háirithe, beidh aon chásanna nua de "
"``Person`` inrochtana freisin trí ``My Person``, agus a mhalairt:"

msgid ""
"You could also use a proxy model to define a different default ordering on a "
"model. You might not always want to order the ``Person`` model, but "
"regularly order by the ``last_name`` attribute when you use the proxy::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfá samhail seachfhreastalaí a úsáid freisin chun ordú réamhshocraithe "
"difriúil ar mhúnla a shainiú. B'fhéidir nach mbeadh tú ag iarraidh an "
"tsamhail ``Person` a ordú i gcónaí, ach ordú go rialta de réir an tréith "
"``last_name`` nuair a úsáideann tú an seachfhreastalaí:"

msgid ""
"Now normal ``Person`` queries will be unordered and ``OrderedPerson`` "
"queries will be ordered by ``last_name``."
msgstr ""
"Anois ní bheidh gnáth-cheisteanna ``Person` neamh-ordaithe agus ordófar "
"ceisteanna ``OrderedPerson`` ag ``last_name``."

msgid ""
"Proxy models inherit ``Meta`` attributes :ref:`in the same way as regular "
"models <meta-and-multi-table-inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"<meta-and-multi-table-inheritance>Oifreann samhlacha seachfhreastalaí "
"tréithe ``Meta``: ref: `ar an mbealach céanna le samhlacha rialta `."

msgid "``QuerySet``\\s still return the model that was requested"
msgstr "Tugann ``QuerySet`` fós an tsamhail a iarradh ar ais"

msgid ""
"There is no way to have Django return, say, a ``MyPerson`` object whenever "
"you query for ``Person`` objects. A queryset for ``Person`` objects will "
"return those types of objects. The whole point of proxy objects is that code "
"relying on the original ``Person`` will use those and your own code can use "
"the extensions you included (that no other code is relying on anyway). It is "
"not a way to replace the ``Person`` (or any other) model everywhere with "
"something of your own creation."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon bhealach ann chun réad ``MyPerson` a thabhairt ar Django a thabhairt "
"ar ais, abair, aon uair a fhiosraíonn tú ar rudaí ``Person`. Tabharfaidh "
"tacar fiosrúcháin do rudaí ``Person` ar ais na cineálacha rudaí sin. Is é "
"pointe iomlán na rudaí seachfhreastalaí ná go n-úsáidfidh cód ag brath ar an "
"``Person` bunaidh iad siúd agus is féidir le do chód féin na síntí a chuir "
"tú san áireamh a úsáid (nach bhfuil aon chód eile ag brath air ar aon nós). "
"Ní bealach é chun rud éigin de do chruthú féin a chur in ionad an tsamhail "
"``Person` (nó aon rud eile) i ngach áit."

msgid "Base class restrictions"
msgstr "Srianta aicme bonn"

msgid ""
"A proxy model must inherit from exactly one non-abstract model class. You "
"can't inherit from multiple non-abstract models as the proxy model doesn't "
"provide any connection between the rows in the different database tables. A "
"proxy model can inherit from any number of abstract model classes, providing "
"they do *not* define any model fields. A proxy model may also inherit from "
"any number of proxy models that share a common non-abstract parent class."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh samhail seachfhreastalaí oidhreacht ó rang samhail neamh-teibí "
"amháin go díreach Ní féidir leat oidhreacht a dhéanamh ó iolracha samhlacha "
"neamh-teibí toisc nach soláthraíonn an tsamhail seachfhreastalaí aon nasc "
"idir na sraitheanna sna táblaí bunachar sonraí Is féidir le samhail "
"seachfhreastalaí oidhreacht ó aon líon ranganna samhail teibí, ar an "
"gcoinníoll nach sainmhíníonn siad aon réimsí samhlacha. Féadfaidh samhail "
"seachfhreastalaí oidhreacht freisin ó aon líon samhlacha seachfhreastalaí a "
"roinneann rang tuismitheoirí coiteann neamh"

msgid "Proxy model managers"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí samhail seachf"

msgid ""
"If you don't specify any model managers on a proxy model, it inherits the "
"managers from its model parents. If you define a manager on the proxy model, "
"it will become the default, although any managers defined on the parent "
"classes will still be available."
msgstr ""
"Mura sonraíonn tú aon bhainisteoirí samhlacha ar mhúnla seachfhreastalaí, "
"faigheann sé na bainisteoirí oidhreachta óna thuismitheoirí samhlacha. Má "
"shainmhíníonn tú bainisteoir ar an tsamhail seachfhreastalaí, beidh sé mar "
"réamhshocrú, cé go mbeidh aon bhainisteoirí a shainmhínítear ar na "
"tuismitheoirí ranganna ar fáil fós."

msgid ""
"Continuing our example from above, you could change the default manager used "
"when you query the ``Person`` model like this::"
msgstr ""
"Ag leanúint lenár sampla ó thuas, d'fhéadfá an bainisteoir réamhshocraithe a "
"úsáidtear a athrú nuair a fhiosraíonn tú an tsamhail ``Person` mar seo:"

msgid ""
"If you wanted to add a new manager to the Proxy, without replacing the "
"existing default, you can use the techniques described in the :ref:`custom "
"manager <custom-managers-and-inheritance>` documentation: create a base "
"class containing the new managers and inherit that after the primary base "
"class::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat bainisteoir nua a chur leis an Seachfhreastalaí, gan an "
"réamhshocrú atá ann cheana a athsholáthar, is féidir leat na te <custom-"
"managers-and-inheritance>icnící a thuairiscítear sa dhoiciméadúiséireacht: "
"`bainisteoir saincheapaithe' a úsáid: bunaicme a chruthú ina bhfuil na "
"bainisteoirí nua agus é sin a oidhreacht tar éis an bunaicme:"

msgid ""
"You probably won't need to do this very often, but, when you do, it's "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Is dócha nach mbeidh ort é seo a dhéanamh go minic, ach, nuair a dhéanann "
"tú, is féidir é a dhéanamh."

msgid "Differences between proxy inheritance and unmanaged models"
msgstr "Difríochtaí idir oidhreacht seachfhreastalaí agus samhlacha ne"

msgid ""
"Proxy model inheritance might look fairly similar to creating an unmanaged "
"model, using the :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.managed` attribute on a "
"model's ``Meta`` class."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cuma an-chosúil ar oidhreacht samhail seachfhreastalaí "
"le samhail neamh-bhainistithe a chruthú, ag baint úsáide as tréith: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.managed` ar aicme ``Meta`` samhail."

msgid ""
"With careful setting of :attr:`Meta.db_table "
"<django.db.models.Options.db_table>` you could create an unmanaged model "
"that shadows an existing model and adds Python methods to it. However, that "
"would be very repetitive and fragile as you need to keep both copies "
"synchronized if you make any changes."
msgstr ""
"Le socrú cúramach de: attr: `Meta.db_table "
"<django.db.models.Options.db_table>`d'fhéadfá samhail neamh-bhainistithe a "
"chruthú a dhéanann scáth ar mhúnla atá ann cheana agus a chuireann modhanna "
"Python leis. Mar sin féin, bheadh sé sin an-athchleachtach agus leochaileach "
"mar ní mór duit an dá chóip a choinneáil sioncronaithe má dhéanann tú aon "
"athruithe."

msgid ""
"On the other hand, proxy models are intended to behave exactly like the "
"model they are proxying for. They are always in sync with the parent model "
"since they directly inherit its fields and managers."
msgstr ""
"Ar an láimh eile, tá sé i gceist le samhlacha seachfhreastalaí iompar "
"díreach cosúil leis an tsamhail atá siad ag seachfhreastalaí dó. Bíonn siad "
"i gcónaí i gcomhréir leis an tsamhail tuismitheora ós rud é go ndéanann siad "
"a réimsí agus a bhainisteoirí"

msgid "The general rules are:"
msgstr "Is iad na rialacha ginearálta:"

msgid ""
"If you are mirroring an existing model or database table and don't want all "
"the original database table columns, use ``Meta.managed=False``. That option "
"is normally useful for modeling database views and tables not under the "
"control of Django."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag scáthú samhail nó tábla bunachar sonraí atá ann cheana agus mura "
"dteastaíonn na colúin bunaidh tábla bunachar sonraí uile uait, bain úsáid as "
"`Meta.Managed=False``. De ghnáth bíonn an rogha sin úsáideach chun tuairimí "
"bunachar sonraí agus táblaí nach bhfuil faoi smacht Django a shamhaltú."

msgid ""
"If you are wanting to change the Python-only behavior of a model, but keep "
"all the same fields as in the original, use ``Meta.proxy=True``. This sets "
"things up so that the proxy model is an exact copy of the storage structure "
"of the original model when data is saved."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat iompar samhail Python amháin a athrú, ach na réimsí céanna go "
"léir a choinneáil mar atá sa bhunaidh, bain úsáid as `Meta.proxy=True``. "
"Socraíonn sé seo rudaí suas ionas gur cóip cruinn é an tsamhail "
"seachfhreastalaí de struchtúr stórála an tsamhail bhunaidh nuair a "
"shábháiltear sonraí"

msgid "Multiple inheritance"
msgstr "Oidhreacht iolrach"

msgid ""
"Just as with Python's subclassing, it's possible for a Django model to "
"inherit from multiple parent models. Keep in mind that normal Python name "
"resolution rules apply. The first base class that a particular name "
"(e.g. :ref:`Meta <meta-options>`) appears in will be the one that is used; "
"for example, this means that if multiple parents contain a :ref:`Meta <meta-"
"options>` class, only the first one is going to be used, and all others will "
"be ignored."
msgstr ""
"Díreach mar atá le fo-aicmiú Python, is féidir go mhúnla Django oidhreacht ó "
"mhúnlaí ilthuismitheoirí. Coinnigh i gcuimhne go bhfuil feidhm ag "
"gnáthrialacha réitigh ainm Python. Is é an ché <meta-options>ad rang bonn a "
"bhfuil ainm áirithe (e.g.:ref: `Meta `) le feiceáil ann an ceann a úsá <meta-"
"options>idtear; mar shampla, ciallaíonn sé seo má tá aicme a:ref: `Meta` i "
"iliomad tuismitheoirí, ní bheidh ach an chéad cheann le húsáid, agus déanfar "
"neamhaird ar gach duine eile."

msgid ""
"Generally, you won't need to inherit from multiple parents. The main use-"
"case where this is useful is for \"mix-in\" classes: adding a particular "
"extra field or method to every class that inherits the mix-in. Try to keep "
"your inheritance hierarchies as simple and straightforward as possible so "
"that you won't have to struggle to work out where a particular piece of "
"information is coming from."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, ní bheidh ort oidhreacht a dhéanamh ó iliomad tuismitheoirí. "
"Is é an príomhchás úsáide ina bhfuil sé seo úsáideach ná do ranganna "
"“measctha isteach”: réimse nó modh breise ar leith a chur le gach rang a "
"thugann an meascán in oidhreacht. Déan iarracht d'ordlathais oidhreachta a "
"choinneáil chomh simplí agus chomh simplí agus is féidir ionas nach mbeidh "
"ort streachailt a dhéanamh chun oibriú amach cá as a bhfuil píosa faisnéise "
"áirithe ag teacht."

msgid ""
"Note that inheriting from multiple models that have a common ``id`` primary "
"key field will raise an error. To properly use multiple inheritance, you can "
"use an explicit :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` in the base models::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go n-ardóidh earráid ag oidhreacht ó iolracha samhlacha a "
"bhfuil príomhréimse coitianta “id” acu. Chun oidhreacht iolrach a úsáid i "
"gceart, is féidir leat explicit:class: `~django.db.models.autofield` a úsáid "
"sna bunmhúnlaí::"

msgid ""
"Or use a common ancestor to hold the :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField`. "
"This requires using an explicit :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` "
"from each parent model to the common ancestor to avoid a clash between the "
"fields that are automatically generated and inherited by the child::"
msgstr ""
"Nó bain úsáid as sinsear coiteann chun an: class: "
"`~django.db.models.autofield` a shealbhú. Éilíonn sé seo úsáid a bhaint as "
"explicit:class: `~django.db.models.onetoonefield` ó gach samhail "
"tuismitheora go dtí an sinsear coiteann chun coimhlint idir na réimsí a "
"ghineann agus a oidhreann an leanbh go huathoibríoch a sheachaint::"

msgid "Field name \"hiding\" is not permitted"
msgstr "Ní cheadaítear ainm réimse “i bhfolach”"

msgid ""
"In normal Python class inheritance, it is permissible for a child class to "
"override any attribute from the parent class. In Django, this isn't usually "
"permitted for model fields. If a non-abstract model base class has a field "
"called ``author``, you can't create another model field or define an "
"attribute called ``author`` in any class that inherits from that base class."
msgstr ""
"I ngnáthoidhreacht aicme Python, ceadaítear do rang linbh aon tréith ón rang "
"tuismitheora a shárú. I Django, ní cheadaítear é seo de ghnáth do réimsí "
"samhlacha. Má tá réimse ar a dtugtar ``údar`` ag rang bun-mhúnla neamh-"
"teibí, ní féidir leat réimse samhail eile a chruthú nó tréith ar a dtugtar "
"``údar`` a shainiú in aon aicme a fhaigheann oidhreacht ón rang bonn sin."

msgid ""
"This restriction doesn't apply to model fields inherited from an abstract "
"model. Such fields may be overridden with another field or value, or be "
"removed by setting ``field_name = None``."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann an srian seo le réimsí samhlacha a oidhreacht ó mhúnla teibí. "
"Féadfar réimsí den sórt sin a shárú le réimse nó luach eile, nó iad a bhaint "
"trí “field_name = None” a shocrú."

msgid ""
"Model managers are inherited from abstract base classes. Overriding an "
"inherited field which is referenced by an "
"inherited :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` may cause subtle bugs. "
"See :ref:`custom managers and model inheritance <custom-managers-and-"
"inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá bainisteoirí samhlacha oidhreachta ó ranganna bonn teibí. D'fhéadfadh "
"fabhtanna caolchúiseacha a bheith ina chúis le réimse oidhreachta dá "
"dtagraíonn oidhreacht:class: `~Django.db.Models.Manager` a shárú. <custom-"
"managers-and-inheritance>Féach: tagairt: `bainisteoirí saincheaptha agus "
"oidhreacht mhúnla `."

msgid ""
"Some fields define extra attributes on the model, e.g. "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` defines an extra attribute with "
"``_id`` appended to the field name, as well as ``related_name`` and "
"``related_query_name`` on the foreign model."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn roinnt réimsí tréithe breise ar an tsamhail, m.sh. a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey` sainmhíníonn tréith breise le ``_id`` curtha "
"leis an ainm réimse, chomh maith le ``related_name`` agus "
"`related_query_name`` ar an tsamhail eachtrach."

msgid ""
"These extra attributes cannot be overridden unless the field that defines it "
"is changed or removed so that it no longer defines the extra attribute."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir na tréithe breise seo a athrú mura n-athraítear nó baintear an "
"réimse a shainmhíníonn é ionas nach sainmhíníonn sé an tréith breise a "
"thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"Overriding fields in a parent model leads to difficulties in areas such as "
"initializing new instances (specifying which field is being initialized in "
"``Model.__init__``) and serialization. These are features which normal "
"Python class inheritance doesn't have to deal with in quite the same way, so "
"the difference between Django model inheritance and Python class inheritance "
"isn't arbitrary."
msgstr ""
"Bíonn deacrachtaí i réimsí ar nós cásanna nua a thionscnamh (ag sonrú cén "
"réimse atá á thionscnamh i `Samhail. __init__``) agus sraitheadh. Is gnéithe "
"iad seo nach gá le gnáthoidhreacht aicme Python déileáil leo ar an mbealach "
"céanna, mar sin níl an difríocht idir oidhreacht mhúnla Django agus "
"oidhreacht aicme Python treallach."

msgid ""
"This restriction only applies to attributes which "
"are :class:`~django.db.models.Field` instances. Normal Python attributes can "
"be overridden if you wish. It also only applies to the name of the attribute "
"as Python sees it: if you are manually specifying the database column name, "
"you can have the same column name appearing in both a child and an ancestor "
"model for multi-table inheritance (they are columns in two different "
"database tables)."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann an srian seo ach le tréithe arba:class: "
"`~django.db.models.field` cásanna. Is féidir gnáthtréithe Python a shárú más "
"mian leat. Ní bhaineann sé ach le hainm na tréithe mar a fheiceann Python é: "
"má tá ainm an cholún bunachar sonraí á shonrú agat de láimh, is féidir leat "
"an t-ainm colún céanna a bheith le feiceáil i samhail leanbh agus sinsear le "
"haghaidh oidhreachta il-tábla (is colúin iad i dhá thábla bunachar sonraí "
"éagsúla)."

msgid ""
"Django will raise a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.FieldError` if you "
"override any model field in any ancestor model."
msgstr ""
"Ardóidh Django a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.fielderror` má sháraigh tú "
"aon réimse samhail in aon mhúnla sinsear."

msgid ""
"Note that because of the way fields are resolved during class definition, "
"model fields inherited from multiple abstract parent models are resolved in "
"a strict depth-first order. This contrasts with standard Python MRO, which "
"is resolved breadth-first in cases of diamond shaped inheritance. This "
"difference only affects complex model hierarchies, which (as per the advice "
"above) you should try to avoid."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, mar gheall ar an mbealach a réitítear réimsí le linn "
"sainmhínithe ranga, réitear réimsí samhail a oidhreacht ó iliomad samhlacha "
"teibí tuismitheoirí i ord doimhneach- Tá sé seo i gcodarsnacht le Python MRO "
"caighdeánach, a réitear ar leithead ar dtús i gcásanna oidhreachta cruth "
"diamaint. Ní théann an difríocht seo ach ar ordlathais chasta samhlacha, ar "
"cheart duit iarracht a dhéanamh (de réir na comhairle thuas) a sheachaint."

msgid "Organizing models in a package"
msgstr "Múnlaí a eagrú i bpacáiste"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`manage.py startapp <startapp>` command creates an application "
"structure that includes a ``models.py`` file. If you have many models, "
"organizing them in separate files may be useful."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn an t-ordú: DjaDmin: `manage.py startapp` struchtúr feidhmchláir a "
"chuimsíonn comhad ``<startapp>models.py`. Má tá go leor samhlacha agat, "
"d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith úsáideach iad a eagrú i gcomhaid ar leithligh."

msgid ""
"To do so, create a ``models`` package. Remove ``models.py`` and create a "
"``myapp/models/`` directory with an ``__init__.py`` file and the files to "
"store your models. You must import the models in the ``__init__.py`` file."
msgstr ""
"Chun é sin a dhéanamh, cruthaigh pacáiste ``samhlacha ``. Bain ``models.py`` "
"agus cruthaigh eolaire ``myapp/models/`` le comhad ``__init__.py`` agus na "
"comhaid chun do mhúnlaí a stóráil. Ní mór duit na samhlacha a iompórtáil sa "
"chomhad ``__init__.py``."

msgid ""
"For example, if you had ``organic.py`` and ``synthetic.py`` in the "
"``models`` directory:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má bhí ``organic.py`` agus ``synthetic.py`` agat san eolaire "
"``models``:"

msgid "``myapp/models/__init__.py``"
msgstr "``myapp/samhlacha/__init__.py``"

msgid ""
"Explicitly importing each model rather than using ``from .models import *`` "
"has the advantages of not cluttering the namespace, making code more "
"readable, and keeping code analysis tools useful."
msgstr ""
"Tá na buntáistí ag iompórtáil gach samhail go sainráite seachas "
"``from .models allmhairiúcháin *`` a úsáid ná gan an spás ainmneacha a "
"ghabháil, an cód a dhéanamh níos inléite, agus uirlisí anailíse cód a "
"choinneáil úsáideach."

msgid ":doc:`The Models Reference </ref/models/index>`"
msgstr ":doc: `Tagairt na Mhúnlaí` </ref/models/index>"

msgid ""
"Covers all the model related APIs including model fields, related objects, "
"and ``QuerySet``."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn sé na APIs go léir a bhaineann le samhail lena n-áirítear réimsí "
"samhail, rudaí gaolmhara, agus ``QuerySet ``."

msgid ""
"This topic guide describes Django's support for interacting with multiple "
"databases. Most of the rest of Django's documentation assumes you are "
"interacting with a single database. If you want to interact with multiple "
"databases, you'll need to take some additional steps."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an treoir ábhair seo cur síos ar thacaíocht Django chun idirghníomhú "
"le bunachair Glacann an chuid is mó den chuid eile de dhoiciméadú Django go "
"bhfuil tú ag idirghníomhú le bunachar sonraí amháin. Más mian leat "
"idirghníomhú le bunachair sonraí iolracha, beidh ort roinnt céimeanna breise "
"a ghlacadh."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`testing-multi-db` for information about testing with multiple "
"databases."
msgstr ""
"Féach: ref: `testing-multi-db` le haghaidh faisnéise faoi thástáil le "
"bunachair sonraí iolracha."

msgid "Defining your databases"
msgstr "Sainmhíniú do bhunachar"

msgid ""
"The first step to using more than one database with Django is to tell Django "
"about the database servers you'll be using. This is done using "
"the :setting:`DATABASES` setting. This setting maps database aliases, which "
"are a way to refer to a specific database throughout Django, to a dictionary "
"of settings for that specific connection. The settings in the inner "
"dictionaries are described fully in the :setting:`DATABASES` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad chéim chun níos mó ná bunachar sonraí amháin a úsáid le Django "
"ná insint do Django faoi na freastalaithe bunachar sonraí a bheidh á úsáid "
"agat. Déantar é seo ag baint úsáide as an socrú:setting: `DATABASES`. "
"Déanann an socrú seo mapáil ainmneacha bunachar sonraí, ar bealach iad chun "
"tagairt a dhéanamh do bhunachar sonraí ar leith ar fud Django, chuig foclóir "
"socruithe don nasc sonrach sin. Déantar cur síos iomlán ar na socruithe sna "
"foclóirí istigh sa doiciméadach:setting: `DATABASES`."

msgid ""
"Databases can have any alias you choose. However, the alias ``default`` has "
"special significance. Django uses the database with the alias of ``default`` "
"when no other database has been selected."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le bunachair sonraí aon ainm a roghnaíonn tú a bheith Mar sin "
"féin, tá tábhacht speisialta ag an alias ``default``. Úsáideann Django an "
"bunachar sonraí leis an alias de ``default`` nuair nach roghnaíodh aon "
"bhunachar sonraí eile."

msgid ""
"The following is an example ``settings.py`` snippet defining two databases "
"-- a default PostgreSQL database and a MySQL database called ``users``::"
msgstr ""
"Seo a leanas sampla ``settings.py`` snippet a shainmhíníonn dhá bhunachar "
"sonraí - bunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe PostgreSQL agus bunachar sonraí "
"MySQL ar a dtugtar ``users``:"

msgid ""
"If the concept of a ``default`` database doesn't make sense in the context "
"of your project, you need to be careful to always specify the database that "
"you want to use. Django requires that a ``default`` database entry be "
"defined, but the parameters dictionary can be left blank if it will not be "
"used. To do this, you must set up :setting:`DATABASE_ROUTERS` for all of "
"your apps' models, including those in any contrib and third-party apps "
"you're using, so that no queries are routed to the default database. The "
"following is an example ``settings.py`` snippet defining two non-default "
"databases, with the ``default`` entry intentionally left empty::"
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil ciall ag coincheap bunachar sonraí `réamhshocraithe`` i "
"gcomhthéacs do thionscadail, ní mór duit a bheith cúramach an bunachar "
"sonraí a theastaíonn uait a úsáid a shonrú i gcónaí. Éilíonn Django go "
"ndéanfar iontráil bunachar sonraí ``default` a shainiú, ach is féidir "
"foclóir na paraiméadair a fhágáil bán mura n-úsáidfear é. Chun seo a "
"dhéanamh, ní mór duit:setting: `DATABASE_ROUTERS` a chur ar bun do mhúnlaí "
"uile d'aipeanna, lena n-áirítear iad siúd in aon aipeanna contrib agus tríú "
"páirtí atá á úsáid agat, ionas nach ndéanfar aon cheisteanna a atreorú chuig "
"an mbunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe. Seo a leanas sampla ``settings.py`` "
"snippet a shainmhíníonn dhá bhunachar sonraí neamh-réamhshocraithe, agus an "
"iontráil ``default`` fágtha folamh d'aon ghnó:"

msgid ""
"If you attempt to access a database that you haven't defined in "
"your :setting:`DATABASES` setting, Django will raise a "
"``django.utils.connection.ConnectionDoesNotExist`` exception."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéanann tú iarracht rochtain a fháil ar bhunachar sonraí nach bhfuil "
"sainmhínithe agat i do shuíomh: `DATABASES`, ardóidh Django eisceacht "
"``Django.Utils.CONNECTION.CONNECTIONDOESNOTEXIST ``."

msgid "Synchronizing your databases"
msgstr "Sioncrónú do bhunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`migrate` management command operates on one database at a "
"time. By default, it operates on the ``default`` database, but by providing "
"the :option:`--database <migrate --database>` option, you can tell it to "
"synchronize a different database. So, to synchronize all models onto all "
"databases in the first example above, you would need to call:"
msgstr ""
"Feidhmíonn an t-ordú bainistíochta: DJADmin: `imirce` ar bhunachar sonraí "
"amháin ag an am. De réir réamhshocraithe, oibríonn sé ar an mbunachar sonraí "
"``réamhshocraithe``, ach tríd an rogha: `--database `a sholáthar, is féidir "
"leat a rá dó bunachar sonraí difriúil a <migrate --database>shioncronú. Mar "
"sin, chun gach samhail a shioncronú ar gach bunachar sonraí sa chéad shampla "
"thuas, bheadh ort glaoch ar:"

msgid ""
"If you don't want every application to be synchronized onto a particular "
"database, you can define a :ref:`database router<topics-db-multi-db-"
"routing>` that implements a policy constraining the availability of "
"particular models."
msgstr ""
"Mura dteastaíonn uait go ndéanfaí gach feidhmchlár a shioncronú le bunachar "
"sonraí áirithe, is féidir leat a: ref: `ródaire bunachar sonraí <topics-db-"
"multi-db-routing>`a shainiú a chuireann beartas i bhfeidhm ag cur srian ar "
"infhaighteacht samhlacha áirithe."

msgid ""
"If, as in the second example above, you've left the ``default`` database "
"empty, you must provide a database name each time you "
"run :djadmin:`migrate`. Omitting the database name would raise an error. For "
"the second example:"
msgstr ""
"Má d'fhág tú, mar atá sa dara sampla thuas, an bunachar sonraí ``default`` "
"folamh, ní mór duit ainm bunachar sonraí a sholáthar gach uair a rith tú: "
"djadmin: `migrate`. Trí ainm an bhunachar sonraí a fhágáil, d'ardódh "
"earráid. Maidir leis an dara sampla:"

msgid "Using other management commands"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta eile a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Most other ``django-admin`` commands that interact with the database operate "
"in the same way as :djadmin:`migrate` -- they only ever operate on one "
"database at a time, using ``--database`` to control the database used."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn an chuid is mó d'orduithe ``django-admin ``eile a idirghníomhaíonn "
"leis an mbunachar sonraí ar an mbealach céanna le: djadmin: `migrate` - ní "
"oibríonn siad riamh ar bhunachar sonraí amháin ag an am, ag baint úsáide as "
"``- bunachar sonraí`` chun an bunachar sonraí a úsáidtear a rialú."

msgid ""
"An exception to this rule is the :djadmin:`makemigrations` command. It "
"validates the migration history in the databases to catch problems with the "
"existing migration files (which could be caused by editing them) before "
"creating new migrations. By default, it checks only the ``default`` "
"database, but it consults the :meth:`allow_migrate` method of :ref:`routers "
"<topics-db-multi-db-routing>` if any are installed."
msgstr ""
"Eisceacht ón riail seo is ea an t-ordú:djadmin: `makemigrations`. Bailíonn "
"sé stair na himirce sna bunachair sonraí chun fadhbanna a ghabháil leis na "
"comhaid imirce atá ann cheana féin (a d'fhéadfadh a bheith mar thoradh orthu "
"a chur in eagar) sula gcruthaítear imirce nua. <topics-db-multi-db-"
"routing>De réir réamhshocraithe, ní sheiceálann sé ach an bunachar sonraí "
"``default`, ach déanann sé dul i gcomhairle leis an modh:meth: "
"`allow_migrate` de:ref: `ródair` má tá aon cheann suiteáilte."

msgid "Automatic database routing"
msgstr "Ródú uathoibríoch bunachar"

msgid ""
"The easiest way to use multiple databases is to set up a database routing "
"scheme. The default routing scheme ensures that objects remain 'sticky' to "
"their original database (i.e., an object retrieved from the ``foo`` database "
"will be saved on the same database). The default routing scheme ensures that "
"if a database isn't specified, all queries fall back to the ``default`` "
"database."
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach is éasca le bunachair sonraí iolracha a úsáid ná scéim "
"ródaithe bunachar sonraí a bhunú. Cinntíonn an scéim ródaithe "
"réamhshocraithe go bhfanann rudaí 'greamaitheach' lena mbunachar sonraí "
"bunaidh (ie, sábhálfar réad a aisghabhadh ón mbunachar sonraí `foo' ar an "
"mbunachar sonraí céanna). Cinntíonn an scéim ródaithe réamhshocraithe mura "
"sonraítear bunachar sonraí, go dtagann gach ceist ar ais chuig an mbunachar "
"sonraí `réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"You don't have to do anything to activate the default routing scheme -- it "
"is provided 'out of the box' on every Django project. However, if you want "
"to implement more interesting database allocation behaviors, you can define "
"and install your own database routers."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá duit aon rud a dhéanamh chun an scéim ródaithe réamhshocraithe a "
"ghníomhachtú - cuirtear ar fáil í 'amach as an mbosca' ar gach tionscadal "
"Django. Mar sin féin, más mian leat iompraíochtaí leithdháileadh bunachar "
"sonraí níos spéisiúla a chur i bhfeidhm, is féidir leat do ródairí bunachar "
"sonraí féin a shainiú agus"

msgid "Database routers"
msgstr "Ródaithe bunachar sonraí"

msgid "A database Router is a class that provides up to four methods:"
msgstr ""
"Is rang é Ródaire bunachar sonraí a sholáthraíonn suas le ceithre mhodh:"

msgid ""
"Suggest the database that should be used for read operations for objects of "
"type ``model``."
msgstr ""
"Moltar an bunachar sonraí ba chóir a úsáid le haghaidh oibríochtaí "
"léitheoireachta le haghaidh rudaí de chineál ``samhail`."

msgid ""
"If a database operation is able to provide any additional information that "
"might assist in selecting a database, it will be provided in the ``hints`` "
"dictionary. Details on valid hints are provided :ref:`below <topics-db-multi-"
"db-hints>`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá oibríocht bunachar sonraí in ann aon fhaisnéis bhreise a sholáthar a "
"d'fhéadfadh cabhrú le bunachar sonraí a roghnú, cuirfear ar fáil sa "
"bhfoclóir ``leideanna ``. <topics-db-multi-db-hints>Cuirtear sonraí ar "
"leideanna bailí ar fáil: ref: `thíos `."

msgid "Returns ``None`` if there is no suggestion."
msgstr "Tugann sé ar ais ``None`` mura bhfuil aon mholadh ann."

msgid ""
"Suggest the database that should be used for writes of objects of type Model."
msgstr ""
"Moltar an bunachar sonraí ba chóir a úsáid le haghaidh scríobh rudaí de "
"chineál Samhail."

msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if a relation between ``obj1`` and ``obj2`` should be "
"allowed, ``False`` if the relation should be prevented, or ``None`` if the "
"router has no opinion. This is purely a validation operation, used by "
"foreign key and many to many operations to determine if a relation should be "
"allowed between two objects."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair ar ais ``True`` má chóir gaol idir ``obj1`` agus `obj2`` a cheadú, "
"``Fal`` má chóir an gaol a chosc, nó ``None`` mura bhfuil aon tuairim ag an "
"ródaire. Is oibríocht bailíochtaithe amháin é seo, a úsáidtear ag eochair "
"eachtrach agus go leor oibríochtaí chun a chinneadh an cheart caidreamh a "
"cheadú idir dhá réad."

msgid ""
"If no router has an opinion (i.e. all routers return ``None``), only "
"relations within the same database are allowed."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tuairim ag aon ródaire (ie filleann gach ródaire ``None ``), ní "
"cheadaítear ach caidreamh laistigh den bhunachar sonraí céanna."

msgid ""
"Determine if the migration operation is allowed to run on the database with "
"alias ``db``. Return ``True`` if the operation should run, ``False`` if it "
"shouldn't run, or ``None`` if the router has no opinion."
msgstr ""
"Faigh amach an gceadaítear don oibríocht imirce a reáchtáil ar an mbunachar "
"sonraí le alias ``db``. Fill ar ais ``True`` más chóir go rithfeadh an "
"oibríocht, ``False`` mura chóir dó rith, nó ``None`` mura bhfuil aon tuairim "
"ag an ródaire."

msgid ""
"The ``app_label`` positional argument is the label of the application being "
"migrated."
msgstr ""
"Is é an argóint seasaimh `app_label`` lipéad an fheidhmchláir atá á imirce."

msgid ""
"``model_name`` is set by most migration operations to the value of "
"``model._meta.model_name`` (the lowercased version of the model "
"``__name__``) of the model being migrated. Its value is ``None`` for "
"the :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` "
"and :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operations unless they "
"provide it using hints."
msgstr ""
"Socraítear ``model_name`` ag an gcuid is mó d'oibríochtaí imirce go luach "
"``samhail. _meta.model_name`` (an leagan íseal den tsamhail ``__name__``) "
"den tsamhail atá á imirce. Is é a luach ``None`` d'oibríochtaí: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` agus:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` mura soláthraíonn siad é ag baint "
"úsáide as leideanna."

msgid ""
"``hints`` are used by certain operations to communicate additional "
"information to the router."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann oibríochtaí áirithe ``leideanna ``chun faisnéis bhreise a chur in "
"iúl don ródaire."

msgid ""
"When ``model_name`` is set, ``hints`` normally contains the model class "
"under the key ``'model'``. Note that it may be a :ref:`historical model "
"<historical-models>`, and thus not have any custom attributes, methods, or "
"managers. You should only rely on ``_meta``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shocraítear ``model_name``, is gnách go mbíonn ``hints`` an rang "
"samhail faoin eochair ```samhail``. Tabhair faoi deara go bhféadfadh sé a: "
"ref: `samhail stairiúil <historical-models>`, agus dá bhrí sin nach bhfuil "
"aon tréithe, modhanna nó bainisteoirí saincheaptha aige. Níor chóir duit "
"brath ach ar ``_meta``."

msgid ""
"This method can also be used to determine the availability of a model on a "
"given database."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an modh seo a úsáid freisin chun infhaighteacht samhail ar "
"bhunachar sonraí ar leith a chinneadh."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`makemigrations` always creates migrations for model changes, but "
"if ``allow_migrate()`` returns ``False``, any migration operations for the "
"``model_name`` will be silently skipped when running :djadmin:`migrate` on "
"the ``db``. Changing the behavior of ``allow_migrate()`` for models that "
"already have migrations may result in broken foreign keys, extra tables, or "
"missing tables. When :djadmin:`makemigrations` verifies the migration "
"history, it skips databases where no app is allowed to migrate."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Cruthaíonn `makemigrations` imirce i gcónaí le haghaidh athruithe "
"samhail, ach má fhilleann ``allow_migration () ```False``, scipeánfar aon "
"oibríochtaí imirce don `model_name`` go ciúin agus iad ag rith: djadmin: "
"`migrate` ar an `db``. D'fhéadfadh eochracha eachtracha briste, táblaí "
"breise, nó táblaí in easnamh mar thoradh ar iompar `allow_migration () ``a "
"athrú do mhúnlaí a bhfuil imirce acu cheana féin. Nuair a fhíoraíonn "
"DjaDmin: `makemigrations` stair an imirce, scipeann sé bunachair sonraí nach "
"gceadaítear aon aip imirce."

msgid ""
"A router doesn't have to provide *all* these methods -- it may omit one or "
"more of them. If one of the methods is omitted, Django will skip that router "
"when performing the relevant check."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá do ródaire na modhanna seo uach* a sholáthar - féadfaidh sé ceann "
"amháin nó níos mó acu a fhágáil. Má fhágtar ceann de na modhanna, "
"scipeánfaidh Django an ródaire sin agus an seiceáil ábhartha á ndéanamh agat."

msgid "Hints"
msgstr "Leideanna"

msgid ""
"The hints received by the database router can be used to decide which "
"database should receive a given request."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na leideanna a fhaigheann an ródaire bunachar sonraí a úsáid chun "
"cinneadh a dhéanamh cén bunachar sonraí ba chóir iarratas ar leith a fháil."

msgid ""
"At present, the only hint that will be provided is ``instance``, an object "
"instance that is related to the read or write operation that is underway. "
"This might be the instance that is being saved, or it might be an instance "
"that is being added in a many-to-many relation. In some cases, no instance "
"hint will be provided at all. The router checks for the existence of an "
"instance hint, and determine if that hint should be used to alter routing "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Faoi láthair, is é an t-aon leid a chuirfear ar fáil ná `instance`, sampla "
"réada a bhaineann leis an oibríocht léitheoireachta nó scríbhneoireachta atá "
"ar siúl. D'fhéadfadh gurb é seo an cás atá á shábháil, nó d'fhéadfadh sé a "
"bheith ina sampla atá á chur leis i ngaol go leor. I roinnt cásanna, ní "
"chuirfear aon leid ar fáil ar chor ar bith. Seiceálann an ródaire go bhfuil "
"leid shampla ann, agus cinneann sé an cheart an leid sin a úsáid chun iompar "
"ródúcháin a athrú."

msgid "Using routers"
msgstr "Úsáid ródairí"

msgid ""
"Database routers are installed using the :setting:`DATABASE_ROUTERS` "
"setting. This setting defines a list of class names, each specifying a "
"router that should be used by the base router (``django.db.router``)."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáiltear ródairí bunachar sonraí ag baint úsáide as an socrú: setting: "
"`DATABASE_ROUTERS`. Sainmhíníonn an socrú seo liosta d'ainmneacha ranga, "
"gach ceann acu ag sonrú ródaire ar chóir an bunródaire a úsáid "
"(``django.db.router``)."

msgid ""
"The base router is used by Django's database operations to allocate database "
"usage. Whenever a query needs to know which database to use, it calls the "
"base router, providing a model and a hint (if available). The base router "
"tries each router class in turn until one returns a database suggestion. If "
"no routers return a suggestion, the base router tries the "
"current :attr:`instance._state.db <django.db.models.Model._state>` of the "
"hint instance. If no hint instance was provided, "
"or :attr:`instance._state.db <django.db.models.Model._state>` is ``None``, "
"the base router will allocate the ``default`` database."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann oibríochtaí bunachar sonraí Django an ródaire bunachar sonraí chun "
"úsáid bunachar sonraí a leithdháileadh. Aon uair a chaithfidh fiosrúchán a "
"fháil amach cén bunachar sonraí atá le húsáid, glaonn sé ar an ródaire bonn, "
"ag soláthar samhail agus leid (má tá sé ar fáil). Déanann an bunródaire "
"iarracht gach rang ródaire ina dhiaidh sin go dtí go bhfilleann duine moladh "
"bunachar sonraí. Mura dtugann aon ródairí moladh ar ais, déanann an ródaire "
"bonn iarracht an reatha: attr: `instance. _state.db "
"<django.db.models.Model._state>`den chás leideanna. Mura soláthraíodh aon "
"sampla leideanna, nó:attr: `instance. Is é _state.db "
"<django.db.models.Model._state>```None ``, leithdháileoidh an bunródaire an "
"bunachar sonraí ``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid "An example"
msgstr "Sampla"

msgid "Example purposes only!"
msgstr "Cuspóirí samplacha amháin!"

msgid ""
"This example is intended as a demonstration of how the router infrastructure "
"can be used to alter database usage. It intentionally ignores some complex "
"issues in order to demonstrate how routers are used."
msgstr ""
"Tá an sampla seo beartaithe mar léiriú ar an gcaoi is féidir bonneagar an "
"ródaire a úsáid chun úsáid bunachar sonraí a athrú. Déanann sé neamhaird de "
"ghnó roinnt saincheisteanna casta d'fhonn a léiriú conas a úsáidtear ródair"

msgid ""
"This example won't work if any of the models in ``myapp`` contain "
"relationships to models outside of the ``other`` database. :ref:`Cross-"
"database relationships <no_cross_database_relations>` introduce referential "
"integrity problems that Django can't currently handle."
msgstr ""
"Ní oibreoidh an sampla seo má tá caidreamh le samhlacha lasmuigh den "
"bhunachar sonraí ```eile ``ag aon cheann de na samhlacha i `myapp``. :ref: "
"Tugann `caidrimh tras-bhunachar sonraí "
"<no_cross_database_relations>`fadhbanna sláine tagartha isteach nach féidir "
"le Django a láimhseáil faoi láthair."

msgid ""
"The primary/replica (referred to as master/slave by some databases) "
"configuration described is also flawed -- it doesn't provide any solution "
"for handling replication lag (i.e., query inconsistencies introduced because "
"of the time taken for a write to propagate to the replicas). It also doesn't "
"consider the interaction of transactions with the database utilization "
"strategy."
msgstr ""
"Tá an chumraíocht bunús/macasamhail (dá ngairtear máistir/sclábhaí ag roinnt "
"bunachair sonraí) a thuairiscítear lochtach freisin - ní sholáthraíonn sé "
"aon réiteach chun moill macasamhail a láimhseáil (ie, neamhréireachtaí "
"fiosrúcháin a tugadh isteach mar gheall ar an am a thógtar le scríobh chun "
"iomadú chuig na macasamhail). Ní mheasann sé freisin idirghníomhaíocht "
"idirbhearta leis an straitéis úsáide bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"So - what does this mean in practice? Let's consider another sample "
"configuration. This one will have several databases: one for the ``auth`` "
"application, and all other apps using a primary/replica setup with two read "
"replicas. Here are the settings specifying these databases::"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin - cad a chiallaíonn sé seo i gcleachtas? Déanaimis smaoineamh ar "
"chumraíocht samplach eile. Beidh roinnt bunachar sonraí ag an gceann seo: "
"ceann don fheidhmchlár ``auth`, agus gach aip eile ag baint úsáide as socrú "
"bunscoil/macasamhail le dhá mhacasamhail léite. Seo na socruithe a "
"shonraíonn na bunachair sonraí seo:"

msgid ""
"Now we'll need to handle routing. First we want a router that knows to send "
"queries for the ``auth`` and ``contenttypes`` apps to ``auth_db`` (``auth`` "
"models are linked to ``ContentType``, so they must be stored in the same "
"database)::"
msgstr ""
"Anois beidh orainn ródú a láimhseáil. Ar dtús ba mhaith linn ródaire a "
"bhfuil a fhios aige ceisteanna a sheoladh do na feidhmchláir `auth`` agus "
"`contenttypes`` chuig `auth_db`` (tá samhlacha `auth`` nasctha le "
"`contentType``, mar sin caithfear iad a stóráil sa bhunachar sonraí céanna):"

msgid ""
"And we also want a router that sends all other apps to the primary/replica "
"configuration, and randomly chooses a replica to read from::"
msgstr ""
"Agus theastaíonn ródaire uainn freisin a sheolann gach aip eile chuig an "
"gcumraíocht bunscoil/macasamhail, agus a roghnaíonn macasamhail go randamach "
"le léamh as:"

msgid ""
"Finally, in the settings file, we add the following (substituting "
"``path.to.`` with the actual Python path to the module(s) where the routers "
"are defined)::"
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, sa chomhad socruithe, cuirimid an méid seo a leanas leis (ag "
"cur `path.to.`` in ionad an cosán Python iarbhír chuig an modúl (í) ina "
"bhfuil na ródairí sainmhínithe):"

msgid ""
"The order in which routers are processed is significant. Routers will be "
"queried in the order they are listed in the :setting:`DATABASE_ROUTERS` "
"setting. In this example, the ``AuthRouter`` is processed before the "
"``PrimaryReplicaRouter``, and as a result, decisions concerning the models "
"in ``auth`` are processed before any other decision is made. If "
"the :setting:`DATABASE_ROUTERS` setting listed the two routers in the other "
"order, ``PrimaryReplicaRouter.allow_migrate()`` would be processed first. "
"The catch-all nature of the PrimaryReplicaRouter implementation would mean "
"that all models would be available on all databases."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-ord ina ndéantar ródairí a phróiseáil suntasach. Cuirfear ceist ar "
"ródairí san ord atá siad liostaithe sa socrú: SETTING: `DATABASE_ROUTERS`. "
"Sa sampla seo, déantar an `Authrough ``a phróiseáil roimh an "
"``PrimaryRepliCarouter``, agus mar thoradh air sin, déantar cinntí a "
"bhaineann leis na samhlacha in `auth` a phróiseáil sula ndéantar aon "
"chinneadh eile. Má liostaíodh an socrú:setting: `DATABASE_ROUTERS` an dá "
"ródaire san ord eile, bheadh `primaryReplicaRouter.ALLOW_MIGRATE () ``a "
"phróiseáil ar dtús. Ciallaíonn nádúr uile an chur i bhfeidhm "
"PrimaryReplicaOuter go mbeadh na samhlacha go léir ar fáil ar gach bunachar "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"With this setup installed, and all databases migrated as "
"per :ref:`synchronizing_multiple_databases`, lets run some Django code:"
msgstr ""
"Leis an socrú seo suiteáilte, agus na bunachair sonraí go léir a imirceadh "
"mar: ref: `synchronizing_multiple_databases`, ligeann sé roinnt cód Django a "
"reáchtáil:"

msgid ""
"This example defined a router to handle interaction with models from the "
"``auth`` app, and other routers to handle interaction with all other apps. "
"If you left your ``default`` database empty and don't want to define a catch-"
"all database router to handle all apps not otherwise specified, your routers "
"must handle the names of all apps in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` before you "
"migrate. See :ref:`contrib_app_multiple_databases` for information about "
"contrib apps that must be together in one database."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínigh an sampla seo ródaire chun idirghníomhaíocht a láimhseáil le "
"samhlacha ón aip `auth`, agus ródairí eile chun idirghníomhú le gach aip "
"eile a láimhseáil. Má d'fhág tú do bhunachar sonraí ``default`` folamh agus "
"mura dteastaíonn uait ródaire bunachar sonraí catch-all a shainiú chun gach "
"aip nach sonraítear ar mhalairt a láimhseáil, ní mór do ródairí ainmneacha "
"gach aip a láimhseáil in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` sula ndéanann tú imirce. "
"Féach:ref: `contrib_app_multiple_databases` le haghaidh faisnéise faoi apps "
"contrib nach mór a bheith le chéile i mbunachar sonraí amháin."

msgid "Manually selecting a database"
msgstr "Bunachar sonraí a roghnú de láimh"

msgid ""
"Django also provides an API that allows you to maintain complete control "
"over database usage in your code. A manually specified database allocation "
"will take priority over a database allocated by a router."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django API freisin a ligeann duit smacht iomlán a choinneáil ar "
"úsáid bunachar sonraí i do chód. Glacfaidh leithdháileadh bunachar sonraí "
"sonraithe de láimh tosaíocht ar bhunachar sonraí a leithdháiltear"

msgid "Manually selecting a database for a ``QuerySet``"
msgstr "Bunachar sonraí a roghnú de láimh le haghaidh ``QuerySet``"

msgid ""
"You can select the database for a ``QuerySet`` at any point in the "
"``QuerySet`` \"chain.\" Call ``using()`` on the ``QuerySet`` to get another "
"``QuerySet`` that uses the specified database."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an bunachar sonraí do `QuerySet`` a roghnú ag pointe ar bith "
"sa slabhra ``QuerySet``. Glaoigh ar ``using () ``ar an `QuerySet`` chun "
"``QuerySet`` eile a fháil a úsáideann an bunachar sonraí sonraithe."

msgid ""
"``using()`` takes a single argument: the alias of the database on which you "
"want to run the query. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tógann ``using () ``argóint amháin: ainm an bhunachar sonraí ar mhaith leat "
"an cheist a reáchtáil. Mar shampla:"

msgid "Selecting a database for ``save()``"
msgstr "Bunachar sonraí a roghnú le haghaidh ``save () ``"

msgid ""
"Use the ``using`` keyword to ``Model.save()`` to specify to which database "
"the data should be saved."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an eochairfhocal ``using`` le `Model.save () ``chun a shonrú ar cén "
"bunachar sonraí ba chóir na sonraí a shábháil."

msgid ""
"For example, to save an object to the ``legacy_users`` database, you'd use "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun réad a shábháil chuig an mbunachar sonraí `legacy_users`, "
"d'úsáideann tú seo:"

msgid ""
"If you don't specify ``using``, the ``save()`` method will save into the "
"default database allocated by the routers."
msgstr ""
"Mura sonraíonn tú ``úsáid ``, sábhálfaidh an modh ``save ()`` isteach sa "
"bhunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe arna leithdháileadh ag na ródairí."

msgid "Moving an object from one database to another"
msgstr "Ag bogadh réad ó bhunachar sonraí amháin go ceann eile"

msgid ""
"If you've saved an instance to one database, it might be tempting to use "
"``save(using=...)`` as a way to migrate the instance to a new database. "
"However, if you don't take appropriate steps, this could have some "
"unexpected consequences."
msgstr ""
"Má shábháil tú sampla chuig bunachar sonraí amháin, b'fhéidir go mbeadh sé "
"mealltach ``save (using =...) ``a úsáid mar bhealach chun an sampla a "
"aistriú chuig bunachar sonraí nua. Mar sin féin, mura nglacann tú céimeanna "
"iomchuí, d'fhéadfadh roinnt iarmhairtí gan choinne a bheith aige seo."

msgid "Consider the following example:"
msgstr "Smaoinigh ar an sampla seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"In statement 1, a new ``Person`` object is saved to the ``first`` database. "
"At this time, ``p`` doesn't have a primary key, so Django issues an SQL "
"``INSERT`` statement. This creates a primary key, and Django assigns that "
"primary key to ``p``."
msgstr ""
"I ráiteas 1, sábhálfar réad nua ```Person`` chuig an mbunachar sonraí "
"``chéad``. Ag an am seo, níl eochair phríomhúil ag `p``, mar sin eisíonn "
"Django ráiteas ``INSERT`` SQL. Cruthaíonn sé seo eochair phríomhúil, agus "
"sannann Django an príomh-eochair sin do `p``."

msgid ""
"When the save occurs in statement 2, ``p`` already has a primary key value, "
"and Django will attempt to use that primary key on the new database. If the "
"primary key value isn't in use in the ``second`` database, then you won't "
"have any problems -- the object will be copied to the new database."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a tharlaíonn an sábháil i ráiteas 2, tá príomhluach ag `p`` cheana "
"féin, agus déanfaidh Django iarracht an eochair phríomhúil sin a úsáid ar an "
"mbunachar sonraí nua. Mura bhfuil an príomhluach in úsáid sa bhunachar "
"sonraí ``dara ``, ansin ní bheidh aon fhadhbanna agat - cóipeálfar an réad "
"chuig an mbunachar sonraí nua."

msgid ""
"However, if the primary key of ``p`` is already in use on the ``second`` "
"database, the existing object in the ``second`` database will be overridden "
"when ``p`` is saved."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má tá príomh-eochair `p`` in úsáid cheana féin ar an mbunachar "
"sonraí ``dara ``, cuirfear an réad atá ann cheana sa bhunachar sonraí "
"``soicin` nuair a shábháiltear `p``."

msgid ""
"You can avoid this in two ways. First, you can clear the primary key of the "
"instance. If an object has no primary key, Django will treat it as a new "
"object, avoiding any loss of data on the ``second`` database:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat é seo a sheachaint ar dhá bhealach. Ar dtús, is féidir leat "
"eochair phríomhúil an cháis a ghlanadh. Mura bhfuil aon phríomh-eochair ag "
"réad, déileálfaidh Django leis mar réad nua, ag seachaint aon chaillteanas "
"sonraí ar an mbunachar sonraí ``dara ``:"

msgid ""
"The second option is to use the ``force_insert`` option to ``save()`` to "
"ensure that Django does an SQL ``INSERT``:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara rogha ná an rogha ``force_insert`` a úsáid chun ``save () "
"``chun a chinntiú go ndéanann Django SQL ``INSERT``:"

msgid ""
"This will ensure that the person named ``Fred`` will have the same primary "
"key on both databases. If that primary key is already in use when you try to "
"save onto the ``second`` database, an error will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Cinnteoidh sé seo go mbeidh an príomh-eochair chéanna ag an duine darb ainm "
"``Fred` ar an dá bhunachar sonraí. Má tá an príomh-eochair sin in úsáid "
"cheana féin nuair a dhéanann tú iarracht sábháil ar an mbunachar sonraí "
"``dara ``, ardófar earráid."

msgid "Selecting a database to delete from"
msgstr "Bunachar sonraí a roghnú le scriosadh as"

msgid ""
"By default, a call to delete an existing object will be executed on the same "
"database that was used to retrieve the object in the first place:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, cuirfear glao chun réad atá ann cheana a scriosadh "
"ar an mbunachar sonraí céanna a úsáideadh chun an réad a aisghabháil sa "
"chéad áit:"

msgid ""
"To specify the database from which a model will be deleted, pass a ``using`` "
"keyword argument to the ``Model.delete()`` method. This argument works just "
"like the ``using`` keyword argument to ``save()``."
msgstr ""
"Chun an bunachar sonraí as a scriosfar samhail a shonrú, cuir argóint "
"eochairfhocal ``úsáid ``chuig an modh ``Model.delete ()``. Oibríonn an "
"argóint seo díreach cosúil leis an argóint eochairfhocal ```úsáid ``chun "
"`save ()``."

msgid ""
"For example, if you're migrating a user from the ``legacy_users`` database "
"to the ``new_users`` database, you might use these commands:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá tú ag aistriú úsáideora ón mbunachar sonraí "
"`legacy_users` chuig an mbunachar sonraí ``new_users`, d'fhéadfá na "
"horduithe seo a úsáid:"

msgid "Using managers with multiple databases"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí a úsáid le bunachair sonraí il"

msgid ""
"Use the ``db_manager()`` method on managers to give managers access to a non-"
"default database."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an modh `db_manager () `ar bhainisteoirí chun rochtain a thabhairt do "
"bhainisteoirí ar bhunachar sonraí neamh-réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"For example, say you have a custom manager method that touches the database "
"-- ``User.objects.create_user()``. Because ``create_user()`` is a manager "
"method, not a ``QuerySet`` method, you can't do "
"``User.objects.using('new_users').create_user()``. (The ``create_user()`` "
"method is only available on ``User.objects``, the manager, not on "
"``QuerySet`` objects derived from the manager.) The solution is to use "
"``db_manager()``, like this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, abair go bhfuil modh bainisteora saincheaptha agat a théann i "
"dteagmháil leis an mbunachar sonraí - ``User.Objects.create_user () ``. "
"Toisc gur modh bainisteora é `create_user () ``, ní modh ``QuerySet``, ní "
"féidir leat ``User.Objects.using ('new_users') .create_user ()`` a dhéanamh. "
"(Níl an modh `create_user () `ar fáil ach ar ``User.Objects``, an "
"bainisteoir, ní ar rudaí ``QuerySet` a dhíorthaítear ón mbainisteoir.) Is é "
"an réiteach ná ``db_manager () ``a úsáid, mar seo:"

msgid ""
"``db_manager()`` returns a copy of the manager bound to the database you "
"specify."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``db_manager () ``cóip den bhainisteoir atá ceangailte leis an "
"mbunachar sonraí a shonraíonn tú."

msgid "Using ``get_queryset()`` with multiple databases"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as ``get_queryset () ``le bunachair sonraí iolracha"

msgid ""
"If you're overriding ``get_queryset()`` on your manager, be sure to either "
"call the method on the parent (using ``super()``) or do the appropriate "
"handling of the ``_db`` attribute on the manager (a string containing the "
"name of the database to use)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag cur ``get_queryset () ``ar do bhainisteoir, déan cinnte glaoch "
"ar an modh ar an tuismitheoir (ag baint úsáide as ``super ()``) nó déan "
"láimhseáil chuí an tréith ``_db`` ar an mbainisteoir (sreang ina bhfuil ainm "
"an bhunachar sonraí le húsáid)."

msgid ""
"For example, if you want to return a custom ``QuerySet`` class from the "
"``get_queryset`` method, you could do this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, más mian leat rang saincheaptha ``QuerySet`` a thabhairt ar ais "
"ón modh ``get_queryset``, d'fhéadfá seo a dhéanamh:"

msgid "Exposing multiple databases in Django's admin interface"
msgstr "Bunachair sonraí iolracha a nochtadh i gcomhéadan riaracháin D"

msgid ""
"Django's admin doesn't have any explicit support for multiple databases. If "
"you want to provide an admin interface for a model on a database other than "
"that specified by your router chain, you'll need to write "
"custom :class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` classes that will direct "
"the admin to use a specific database for content."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon tacaíocht shoiléir ag riarachán Django do iliomad bunachair sonraí. "
"Más mian leat comhéadan riaracháin a sholáthar do mhúnla ar bhunachar sonraí "
"seachas an ceann a shonraíonn do slabhra ródaire, beidh ort ranganna "
"saincheap:class: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin` a scríobh a threoróidh "
"an riarachán bunachar sonraí sonrach a úsáid le haghaidh ábhar."

msgid ""
"``ModelAdmin`` objects have the following methods that require customization "
"for multiple-database support::"
msgstr ""
"Tá na modhanna seo a leanas ag rudaí `ModelAdmin` a éilíonn saincheaptha le "
"haghaidh tacaíochta ilbhunachar sonraí:"

msgid ""
"The implementation provided here implements a multi-database strategy where "
"all objects of a given type are stored on a specific database (e.g., all "
"``User`` objects are in the ``other`` database). If your usage of multiple "
"databases is more complex, your ``ModelAdmin`` will need to reflect that "
"strategy."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an cur i bhfeidhm a chuirtear ar fáil anseo straitéis ilbhunachar "
"sonraí i bhfeidhm ina ndéantar gach rud de chineál ar leith a stóráil ar "
"bhunachar sonraí ar leith (m.sh., tá gach rud ``Úsáideora ``sa bhunachar "
"sonraí ``eile``). Má tá do úsáid a bhaineann le bunachair sonraí iolracha "
"níos casta, beidh ar do `ModelAdmin`` an straitéis sin a léiriú."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin` objects can be handled in a "
"similar fashion. They require three customized methods::"
msgstr ""
":class: Is féidir rudaí `~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin` a "
"láimhseáil ar bhealach den chineál céanna. Teastaíonn trí mhodh saincheaptha "
"uathu:"

msgid ""
"Once you've written your model admin definitions, they can be registered "
"with any ``Admin`` instance::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh do shainmhínithe riaracháin samhail scríofa agat, is féidir "
"iad a chlárú le haon shampla ``Riarachán``:"

msgid ""
"This example sets up two admin sites. On the first site, the ``Author`` and "
"``Publisher`` objects are exposed; ``Publisher`` objects have a tabular "
"inline showing books published by that publisher. The second site exposes "
"just publishers, without the inlines."
msgstr ""
"Bunaíonn an sampla seo dhá shuíomh riaracháin. Ar an gcéad láithreán, "
"nochtar na rudaí ``Údar`` agus `Foilsitheoir``; tá inlíne táblaí ag rudaí "
"``Foilsitheora ``a thaispeánann leabhair arna fhoilsiú ag an bhfoilsitheoir "
"sin. Nochtann an dara suíomh ach foilsitheoirí, gan na línte."

msgid "Using raw cursors with multiple databases"
msgstr "Cúrsaí amh a úsáid le bunachair sonraí iolracha"

msgid ""
"If you are using more than one database you can use "
"``django.db.connections`` to obtain the connection (and cursor) for a "
"specific database. ``django.db.connections`` is a dictionary-like object "
"that allows you to retrieve a specific connection using its alias::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá níos mó ná bunachar sonraí amháin á úsáid agat is féidir leat "
"``django.db.connections`` a úsáid chun an nasc (agus an cúrsóir) a fháil le "
"haghaidh bunachar sonraí ar leith. Is réad cosúil le foclóir é "
"``django.db.connections`` a ligeann duit nasc ar leith a aisghabháil ag "
"baint úsáide as a ainm:"

msgid "Limitations of multiple databases"
msgstr "Teorainneacha ar bhunachar sonraí"

msgid "Cross-database relations"
msgstr "Caidreamh trasbhunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Django doesn't currently provide any support for foreign key or many-to-many "
"relationships spanning multiple databases. If you have used a router to "
"partition models to different databases, any foreign key and many-to-many "
"relationships defined by those models must be internal to a single database."
msgstr ""
"Faoi láthair ní sholáthraíonn Django aon tacaíocht d'eochair eachtracha nó "
"caidrimh go leor a chuimsíonn bunachair sonraí iolracha. Má d'úsáid tú "
"ródaire chun samhlacha a dheighilt chuig bunachair sonraí éagsúla, caithfidh "
"aon eochair eachtrach agus caidrimh go leor a shainmhíníonn na samhlacha sin "
"a bheith inmheánach le bunachar sonraí amháin."

msgid ""
"This is because of referential integrity. In order to maintain a "
"relationship between two objects, Django needs to know that the primary key "
"of the related object is valid. If the primary key is stored on a separate "
"database, it's not possible to easily evaluate the validity of a primary key."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo mar gheall ar shláine tagartha. D'fhonn caidreamh idir dhá réad a "
"choinneáil, ní mór go mbeadh a fhios ag Django go bhfuil príomh-eochair an "
"réada gaolmhara bailí. Má stóráiltear an príomh-eochair ar bhunachar sonraí "
"ar leithligh, ní féidir bailíocht eochair phríomhúil a mheas go héasca."

msgid ""
"If you're using Postgres, SQLite, Oracle, or MySQL with InnoDB, this is "
"enforced at the database integrity level -- database level key constraints "
"prevent the creation of relations that can't be validated."
msgstr ""
"Má tá Postgres, SQLite, Oracle, nó MySQL á úsáid agat le InnoDB, cuirtear é "
"seo i bhfeidhm ag leibhéal sláine an bhunachar sonraí - cosc ar "
"phríomhshrianta ar leibhéal bunachar sonraí caidrimh nach féidir a "
"bhailíochtú a chruthú."

msgid ""
"However, if you're using MySQL with MyISAM tables, there is no enforced "
"referential integrity; as a result, you may be able to 'fake' cross database "
"foreign keys. However, this configuration is not officially supported by "
"Django."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má tá MySQL á úsáid agat le táblaí MyISAM, níl aon sláine "
"tagartha forfheidhmithe ann; mar thoradh air sin, b'fhéidir go mbeidh tú in "
"ann eochracha eachtracha trasbhunachar sonraí 'bréige' a dhéanamh. Mar sin "
"féin, ní thacaíonn Django leis an gcumraíocht seo go hoifigiúil."

msgid "Behavior of contrib apps"
msgstr "Iompar aipeanna contrib"

msgid ""
"Several contrib apps include models, and some apps depend on others. Since "
"cross-database relationships are impossible, this creates some restrictions "
"on how you can split these models across databases:"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn roinnt aipeanna contrib samhlacha, agus braitheann roinnt aipeanna "
"ar dhaoine eile. Ós rud é go bhfuil caidrimh tras-bhunachar sonraí "
"dodhéanta, cruthaíonn sé seo roinnt srianta ar an gcaoi ar féidir leat na "
"samhlacha seo"

msgid ""
"each one of ``contenttypes.ContentType``, ``sessions.Session`` and "
"``sites.Site`` can be stored in any database, given a suitable router."
msgstr ""
"is féidir gach ceann de `ContentTypes.ContentType``, `Sessions.Session`` "
"agus ``Sites.Site`` a stóráil in aon bhunachar sonraí, mar gheall ar ródaire "
"oiriúnach."

msgid ""
"``auth`` models — ``User``, ``Group`` and ``Permission`` — are linked "
"together and linked to ``ContentType``, so they must be stored in the same "
"database as ``ContentType``."
msgstr ""
"Tá samhlacha ``auth`` - ``Úsáideor``, `Grúpa`` agus ``Cead`` - nasctha le "
"chéile agus nasctha le ``ContentType``, mar sin ní mór iad a stóráil sa "
"bhunachar sonraí céanna le `ContentType``."

msgid ""
"``admin`` depends on ``auth``, so its models must be in the same database as "
"``auth``."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann ``admin ``ar `auth``, mar sin caithfidh a mhúnlaí a bheith sa "
"bhunachar sonraí céanna le ``auth``."

msgid ""
"``flatpages`` and ``redirects`` depend on ``sites``, so their models must be "
"in the same database as ``sites``."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann ``flatpages`` agus ``atreoruithe ``ar `suíomhanna``, mar sin "
"caithfidh a gcuid samhlacha a bheith sa bhunachar sonraí céanna le "
"``suíomhanna ``."

msgid ""
"In addition, some objects are automatically created just "
"after :djadmin:`migrate` creates a table to hold them in a database:"
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, cruthaítear roinnt rudaí go huathoibríoch díreach tar éis: "
"cruthaíonn `migrate` tábla chun iad a choinneáil i mbunachar sonraí:"

msgid "a default ``Site``,"
msgstr "réamhshocraithe ``Suíomh ``,"

msgid ""
"a ``ContentType`` for each model (including those not stored in that "
"database),"
msgstr ""
"“cineál ábhair” do gach samhail (lena n-áirítear iad siúd nach stóráiltear "
"sa bhunachar sonraí sin),"

msgid ""
"the ``Permission``\\s for each model (including those not stored in that "
"database)."
msgstr ""
"na `Ceadúna`` do gach samhail (lena n-áirítear iad siúd nach stóráiltear sa "
"bhunachar sonraí sin)."

msgid ""
"For common setups with multiple databases, it isn't useful to have these "
"objects in more than one database. Common setups include primary/replica and "
"connecting to external databases. Therefore, it's recommended to write "
"a :ref:`database router<topics-db-multi-db-routing>` that allows "
"synchronizing these three models to only one database. Use the same approach "
"for contrib and third-party apps that don't need their tables in multiple "
"databases."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le socruithe coitianta le bunachair sonraí iolracha, níl sé úsáideach "
"na rudaí seo a bheith i níos mó ná bunachar sonraí amháin. I measc na "
"socruithe coitianta tá bunúsche/macasamhail agus nascadh le bunachair sonraí "
"Dá bhrí sin, moltar a scríobh a:ref: `ródaire bunachar sonraí <topics-db-"
"multi-db-routing>`a cheadaíonn na trí mhúnla seo a shioncrónú le bunachar "
"sonraí amháin. Úsáid an cur chuige céanna le haghaidh aipeanna contrib agus "
"tríú páirtí nach dteastaíonn a dtáblaí uathu i iliomad bunachar"

msgid ""
"If you're synchronizing content types to more than one database, be aware "
"that their primary keys may not match across databases. This may result in "
"data corruption or data loss."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cineálacha ábhair á shioncronú agat le níos mó ná bunachar sonraí "
"amháin, bí ar an eolas go bhféadfadh nach n-oireann a bpríomh-eochracha "
"trasna bunachair sonraí D'fhéadfadh éilliú sonraí nó caillteanas sonraí mar "
"thoradh air seo."

msgid "Database access optimization"
msgstr "Optamú ar rochtain bunachar"

msgid ""
"Django's database layer provides various ways to help developers get the "
"most out of their databases. This document gathers together links to the "
"relevant documentation, and adds various tips, organized under a number of "
"headings that outline the steps to take when attempting to optimize your "
"database usage."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn ciseal bunachar sonraí Django bealaí éagsúla chun cabhrú le "
"forbróirí an leas is fearr a bhaint as a mbunachar Bailíonn an doiciméad seo "
"naisc leis an doiciméad ábhartha le chéile, agus cuireann sé leideanna "
"éagsúla leis, eagraithe faoi roinnt ceannteidil a thugann cur síos ar na "
"céimeanna atá le glacadh agus tú ag iarraidh úsáid do bhunachar sonraí a"

msgid "Profile first"
msgstr "Próifíl ar dtús"

msgid ""
"As general programming practice, this goes without saying. Find "
"out :ref:`what queries you are doing and what they are costing you <faq-see-"
"raw-sql-queries>`. Use :meth:`.QuerySet.explain` to understand how specific "
"``QuerySet``\\s are executed by your database. You may also want to use an "
"external project like :pypi:`django-debug-toolbar`, or a tool that monitors "
"your database directly."
msgstr ""
"Mar chleachtas cláraithe ginearálta, téann sé seo gan rá. <faq-see-raw-sql-"
"queries>Faigh amach: ref: `cad iad na ceisteanna atá á dhéanamh agat agus "
"cad a chosnaíonn siad duit `. Úsáid: Meth: `.querySet.explain` chun tuiscint "
"a fháil ar cé chomh sonrach a fhorghníomhaíonn do bhunachar sonraí "
"``QuerySet``\\ s. B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat tionscadal seachtrach a úsáid "
"freisin cosúil:pypi: `django-debug-toolbar`, nó uirlis a dhéanann "
"monatóireacht díreach ar do bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Remember that you may be optimizing for speed or memory or both, depending "
"on your requirements. Sometimes optimizing for one will be detrimental to "
"the other, but sometimes they will help each other. Also, work that is done "
"by the database process might not have the same cost (to you) as the same "
"amount of work done in your Python process. It is up to you to decide what "
"your priorities are, where the balance must lie, and profile all of these as "
"required since this will depend on your application and server."
msgstr ""
"Cuimhnigh go bhféadfadh tú a bheith ag barrfheabhsú le haghaidh luas nó "
"cuimhne nó araon, ag brath ar do riachtanais Uaireanta beidh barrfheabhsú do "
"cheann amháin díobhálach don cheann eile, ach uaireanta cabhróidh siad lena "
"chéile. Chomh maith leis sin, b'fhéidir nach mbeadh an costas céanna "
"(duitse) ag an obair a dhéanann an próiseas bunachar sonraí leis an méid "
"céanna oibre a dhéantar i do phróiseas Python. Is fútsa atá sé cinneadh a "
"dhéanamh cad iad do thosaíochtaí, cá gcaithfidh an t-iarmhéid a bheith, agus "
"iad seo go léir a phróifíliú de réir mar is gá ós rud é go mbeidh sé seo ag "
"brath ar d'iarratas agus ar d'fhre"

msgid ""
"With everything that follows, remember to profile after every change to "
"ensure that the change is a benefit, and a big enough benefit given the "
"decrease in readability of your code. **All** of the suggestions below come "
"with the caveat that in your circumstances the general principle might not "
"apply, or might even be reversed."
msgstr ""
"Le gach rud a leanann, cuimhnigh próifíl a dhéanamh tar éis gach athraithe "
"chun a chinntiú gur sochar é an t-athrú, agus sochar mór go leor i "
"bhfianaise an laghdú ar inléiteacht do chód. ** Tagann gach ceann de na "
"moltaí thíos leis an rabhadh go bhféadfadh an prionsabal ginearálta a bheith "
"i bhfeidhm i do chúinsí, nó go bhféadfadh sé a aisiompú fiú."

msgid "Use standard DB optimization techniques"
msgstr "Bain úsáid as teicnící caighdeánacha"

msgid "...including:"
msgstr "... lena n-áirítear:"

msgid ""
"Indexes_. This is a number one priority, *after* you have determined from "
"profiling what indexes should be added. Use :attr:`Meta.indexes "
"<django.db.models.Options.indexes>` or :attr:`Field.db_index "
"<django.db.models.Field.db_index>` to add these from Django. Consider adding "
"indexes to fields that you frequently query "
"using :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.filter()`, :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.exclude()`, :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.order_by()`, "
"etc. as indexes may help to speed up lookups. Note that determining the best "
"indexes is a complex database-dependent topic that will depend on your "
"particular application. The overhead of maintaining an index may outweigh "
"any gains in query speed."
msgstr ""
"Innéacsai_. Is tosaíocht uimhir a haon é seo, * ina dhiaithe* tá cinneadh "
"agat ó phróifíliú cad iad na hinnéacsanna ba chóir a chur leis. "
"<django.db.models.Field.db_index>Úsáid: attr: `Meta.Indexes "
"<django.db.models.Options.indexes>`nó: attr: `Field.db_index` chun iad seo a "
"chur leis ó Django. Smaoinigh ar innéacsanna a chur le réimsí a fhiosraíonn "
"tú go minic ag baint úsáide:meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.filter "
"() `, :meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.Excluded ()`, :meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.order_by () `, srl. d'fhéadfadh innéacsanna "
"cabhrú le cuardach a bhrostú. Tabhair faoi deara gur ábhar casta atá ag "
"brath ar bhunachar sonraí é na hinnéacsanna is fearr a chinneadh a bheidh ag "
"brath ar d'iarratas ar leith. Féadfaidh lasaird a bhaineann le hinnéacs a "
"chothabháil níos mó ná aon ghnóthachain i luas ceisteanna."

msgid "Appropriate use of field types."
msgstr "Úsáid chuí de chineálacha réimse."

msgid ""
"We will assume you have done the things listed above. The rest of this "
"document focuses on how to use Django in such a way that you are not doing "
"unnecessary work. This document also does not address other optimization "
"techniques that apply to all expensive operations, such as :doc:`general "
"purpose caching </topics/cache>`."
msgstr ""
"Glacfaimid leis go ndearna tú na rudaí atá liostaithe thuas. Díríonn an "
"chuid eile den doiciméad seo ar conas Django a úsáid sa chaoi nach bhfuil tú "
"ag déanamh obair gan ghá. Ní thugann an doiciméad seo aghaidh freisin ar "
"theicnící optamaithe eile a bhaineann le gach oibríocht daor, mar "
"shampla:doc: `taiscáil cuspóir ginear</topics/cache> álta`."

msgid "Understand ``QuerySet``\\s"
msgstr "Tuiscint a fháil ar ``QuerySet``\\ s"

msgid ""
"Understanding :doc:`QuerySets </ref/models/querysets>` is vital to getting "
"good performance with simple code. In particular:"
msgstr ""
"Tuiscint: doc: Tá `QuerySets` </ref/models/querysets> ríthábhachtach chun "
"feidhmíocht mhaith a fháil le cód simplí. Go háirithe:"

msgid "Understand ``QuerySet`` evaluation"
msgstr "Meastóireacht ``QuerySet ``a thuiscint"

msgid "To avoid performance problems, it is important to understand:"
msgstr "Chun fadhbanna feidhmíochta a sheachaint, tá sé tábhachtach tuiscint:"

msgid "that :ref:`QuerySets are lazy <querysets-are-lazy>`."
msgstr "<querysets-are-lazy>that:ref: `Tá ceisteanna leisciúil `."

msgid "when :ref:`they are evaluated <when-querysets-are-evaluated>`."
msgstr "<when-querysets-are-evaluated>when: ref: `déantar iad a mheas `."

msgid "how :ref:`the data is held in memory <caching-and-querysets>`."
msgstr "<caching-and-querysets>cona:ref: `coinnítear na sonraí i gcuimhne `."

msgid "Understand cached attributes"
msgstr "Tréithe taiscéadta a thuiscint"

msgid ""
"As well as caching of the whole ``QuerySet``, there is caching of the result "
"of attributes on ORM objects. In general, attributes that are not callable "
"will be cached. For example, assuming the :ref:`example blog models "
"<queryset-model-example>`:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le caistriú an ``QuerySet ``iomlán, tá toradh tréithe ar rudaí "
"ORM a chaitheamh a chaitheamh. Go ginearálta, déanfar tréithe nach féidir "
"glaoch a stóráil. <queryset-model-example>Mar shampla, ag glacadh leis "
"na:ref: `samplaí blag samplacha `:"

msgid "But in general, callable attributes cause DB lookups every time:"
msgstr ""
"Ach go ginearálta, is cúis le tréithe inghlaonta cuardach DB gach uair:"

msgid ""
"Be careful when reading template code - the template system does not allow "
"use of parentheses, but will call callables automatically, hiding the above "
"distinction."
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach agus tú ag léamh cód teimpléid - ní cheadaíonn an córas "
"teimpléid lúibíní a úsáid, ach glaoifidh sé glaonna go huathoibríoch, ag "
"folach an t-idirdhealú thuas."

msgid ""
"Be careful with your own custom properties - it is up to you to implement "
"caching when required, for example using "
"the :class:`~django.utils.functional.cached_property` decorator."
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach le d'airíonna saincheaptha féin - is fútsa atá sé caching a chur "
"i bhfeidhm nuair is gá, mar shampla ag baint úsáide as an maisitheoir: "
"class: `~django.utils.functional.cached_property`."

msgid "Use the ``with`` template tag"
msgstr "Úsáid an chlib teimpléad ``with`"

msgid ""
"To make use of the caching behavior of ``QuerySet``, you may need to use "
"the :ttag:`with` template tag."
msgstr ""
"Chun úsáid a bhaint as iompar caching ``QuerySet ``, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort "
"an chlib teimpléad:ttag: `with` a úsáid."

msgid "Use ``iterator()``"
msgstr "Úsáid ``iterator () ``"

msgid ""
"When you have a lot of objects, the caching behavior of the ``QuerySet`` can "
"cause a large amount of memory to be used. In this "
"case, :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.iterator()` may help."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn a lán rudaí agat, is féidir le hiompar caching an ``QuerySet "
"``a bheith ina chúis le cuimhne mór a úsáid. Sa chás seo, d'fhéadfadh :meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.iterator () `cabhrú."

msgid "Use ``explain()``"
msgstr "Úsáid ``mhínigh () ``"

msgid ""
":meth:`.QuerySet.explain` gives you detailed information about how the "
"database executes a query, including indexes and joins that are used. These "
"details may help you find queries that could be rewritten more efficiently, "
"or identify indexes that could be added to improve performance."
msgstr ""
":meth: Tugann `.querySet.explain` faisnéis mhionsonraithe duit faoin gcaoi a "
"bhfeidhmíonn an bunachar sonraí ceist, lena n-áirítear innéacsanna agus "
"comhpháirteanna a úsáidtear. D'fhéadfadh na sonraí seo cabhrú leat "
"ceisteanna a fháil a d'fhéadfaí a athscríobh níos éifeachtaí a fháil, nó "
"innéacsanna a d'fhéadfaí a chur leis chun feidhmíocht a fheabhsú a"

msgid "Do database work in the database rather than in Python"
msgstr "An oibríonn bunachar sonraí sa bhunachar sonraí seachas i Python"

msgid "For instance:"
msgstr "Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"At the most basic level, use :ref:`filter and exclude <queryset-api>` to do "
"filtering in the database."
msgstr ""
"Ag an leibhéal is bunúsaí, bain úsáid as: ref: `scagadh agus eisiamh "
"<queryset-api>`chun scagadh a dhéanamh sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Use :class:`F expressions <django.db.models.F>` to filter based on other "
"fields within the same model."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: aicme: abairtí `F <django.db.models.F>`chun scagadh bunaithe ar "
"réimsí eile laistigh den tsamhail chéanna."

msgid ""
"Use :doc:`annotate to do aggregation in the database </topics/db/"
"aggregation>`."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid:doc: `anótáil chun comhiomlánú a dhéanamh sa bhunachar sonraithe' </"
"topics/db/aggregation>."

msgid "If these aren't enough to generate the SQL you need:"
msgstr "Mura leor iad seo chun an SQL a theastaíonn uait a ghiniúint:"

msgid "Use ``RawSQL``"
msgstr "Úsáid ``Rawsql``"

msgid ""
"A less portable but more powerful method is "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.RawSQL` expression, which allows "
"some SQL to be explicitly added to the query. If that still isn't powerful "
"enough:"
msgstr ""
"Modh nach bhfuil chomh iniompartha ach níos cumhachtaí ná an léir:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Expressions.RawSql`, a ligeann roinnt SQL a chur go "
"sainráite leis an bhfiosrúchán. Mura bhfuil sé sin cumhachtach go leor fós:"

msgid "Use raw SQL"
msgstr "Úsáid SQL amh"

msgid ""
"Write your own :doc:`custom SQL to retrieve data or populate models </topics/"
"db/sql>`. Use ``django.db.connection.queries`` to find out what Django is "
"writing for you and start from there."
msgstr ""
"Scríobh do chuid féin: doc: `SQL saincheaptha chun sonraí a aisghabháil nó "
"samhlacha a dhaonrú '</topics/db/sql>. Úsáid "
"``django.db.connection.queries`` chun a fháil amach cad atá ag scríobh "
"Django duit agus tosú as sin."

msgid "Retrieve individual objects using a unique, indexed column"
msgstr "Aisghabháil rudaí aonair ag úsáid colún uathúil, innéacsaithe"

msgid ""
"There are two reasons to use a column "
"with :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.unique` "
"or :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_index` when "
"using :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.get` to retrieve individual "
"objects. First, the query will be quicker because of the underlying database "
"index. Also, the query could run much slower if multiple objects match the "
"lookup; having a unique constraint on the column guarantees this will never "
"happen."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá chúis ann le colún a úsáid le:attr: `~django.db.models.field.unique` "
"nó:attr: `~django.db.models.field.db_index` agus tú ag úsáid: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.get` chun rudaí aonair a aisghabháil. Ar dtús, "
