msgid ""
"Same goes for underscores. Both percentage signs and underscores are handled "
"for you transparently."
msgstr ""
"Baineann an rud céanna le béim. Déantar comharthaí céatadáin agus béim a "
"láimhseáil duit go trédhearcach."

msgid "Caching and ``QuerySet``\\s"
msgstr "Caching agus ``QuerySet``\\ s"

msgid ""
"Each :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` contains a cache to minimize "
"database access. Understanding how it works will allow you to write the most "
"efficient code."
msgstr ""
"Tá taisce ag gach ceann: Class: `~django.db.models.query.querySet` chun "
"rochtain ar bhunachar sonraí a íoslaghdú. Ligfidh tuiscint ar an gcaoi a n-"
"oibríonn sé duit an cód is éifeachtaí a scríobh."

msgid ""
"In a newly created :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet`, the cache is "
"empty. The first time a :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` is "
"evaluated -- and, hence, a database query happens -- Django saves the query "
"results in the :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet`’s cache and returns "
"the results that have been explicitly requested (e.g., the next element, if "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` is being iterated over). "
"Subsequent evaluations of the :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` "
"reuse the cached results."
msgstr ""
"I: class: `~django.db.models.query.queryset` nua-chruthaithe, tá an taisce "
"folamh. An chéad uair a dhéantar a: class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset` a mheas -- agus, dá bhrí sin, tarlaíonn "
"ceist bunachar sonraí -- Sábhálann Django torthaí na fiosrúcháin i "
"taisce:class: `~django.db.models.queryset` agus filleann sé na torthaí a "
"iarradh go sainráite (m.sh., an chéad eilimint eile, más air:class: "
"`~django..DB.Models.Query.QuerySet` á athrá). Déanann meastóireachtaí ina "
"dhiaidh sin ar an: aicme: `~django.db.models.query.queryset` athúsáid na "
"torthaí taisceáilte."

msgid ""
"Keep this caching behavior in mind, because it may bite you if you don't use "
"your :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet`\\s correctly. For example, "
"the following will create two :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet`\\s, "
"evaluate them, and throw them away:"
msgstr ""
"Coinnigh an t-iompar taiscéála seo i gcuimhne, toisc go bhféadfadh sé greim "
"ort mura n-úsáideann tú do: class: `~django.db.models.query.queryset`\\ s i "
"gceart. Mar shampla, cruthóidh an méid seo a leanas dhá cheant:class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset`\\ s, iad a mheas, agus caith amach iad:"

msgid ""
"That means the same database query will be executed twice, effectively "
"doubling your database load. Also, there's a possibility the two lists may "
"not include the same database records, because an ``Entry`` may have been "
"added or deleted in the split second between the two requests."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé sin go ndéanfar an ceist bunachar sonraí céanna a fhorghníomhú "
"faoi dhó, ag dúbailt go héifeachtach Chomh maith leis sin, tá an "
"fhéidearthacht nach gcuimsíonn an dá liosta na taifid bunachar sonraí "
"céanna, toisc go bhféadfadh “Iontráil” a chur leis nó a scriosadh sa dara "
"scoilt idir an dá iarratas."

msgid ""
"To avoid this problem, save the :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` "
"and reuse it:"
msgstr ""
"Chun an fhadhb seo a sheachaint, sábháil an:class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset` agus athúsáid é:"

msgid "When ``QuerySet``\\s are not cached"
msgstr "Nuair nach ndéantar ``QuerySet``\\\\ s a chosc"

msgid ""
"Querysets do not always cache their results.  When evaluating only *part* of "
"the queryset, the cache is checked, but if it is not populated then the "
"items returned by the subsequent query are not cached. Specifically, this "
"means that :ref:`limiting the queryset <limiting-querysets>` using an array "
"slice or an index will not populate the cache."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanann Querysets a gcuid torthaí a taisce i gcónaí. Nuair a dhéantar "
"meastóireacht amháin* den tacar fiosrúcháin amháin, déantar an taisce a "
"sheiceáil, ach mura bhfuil sé daonra ansin ní chuirtear na míreanna ar ais "
"ag an gceist ina dhiaidh sin a chosc. Go sonrach, ciallaíonn sé seo nach "
"ndéanfaidh: ref: `teorannú an tacar fiosrúcháin <limiting-querysets>`ag "
"baint úsáide as slisnacht eagar nó innéacs an taisce a líonadh."

msgid ""
"For example, repeatedly getting a certain index in a queryset object will "
"query the database each time:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, déanfaidh innéacs áirithe a fháil arís agus arís agus arís eile "
"i réad socraithe ceisteanna an bunachar sonraí gach uair:"

msgid ""
"However, if the entire queryset has already been evaluated, the cache will "
"be checked instead:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má rinneadh an tacar fiosrúcháin iomlán a mheas cheana féin, "
"seiceálfar an taisce ina ionad sin:"

msgid ""
"Here are some examples of other actions that will result in the entire "
"queryset being evaluated and therefore populate the cache:"
msgstr ""
"Seo roinnt samplaí de ghníomhartha eile a mbeidh meastóireacht ar an tacar "
"fiosrúcháin iomlán mar thoradh air agus dá bhrí sin an taisce a líonadh:"

msgid ""
"Simply printing the queryset will not populate the cache. This is because "
"the call to ``__repr__()`` only returns a slice of the entire queryset."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanfaidh an taisce an taisce a phriontáil ach an tacar fiosrúcháin a "
"phriontáil. Tá sé seo toisc nach bhfilleann an glao chuig ``__repr__ () "
"``ach slisnacht den tacar fiosrúcháin iomlán."

msgid "Asynchronous queries"
msgstr "Fiosrúcháin asincrónach"

msgid ""
"If you are writing asynchronous views or code, you cannot use the ORM for "
"queries in quite the way we have described above, as you cannot call "
"*blocking* synchronous code from asynchronous code - it will block up the "
"event loop (or, more likely, Django will notice and raise a "
"``SynchronousOnlyOperation`` to stop that from happening)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tuairimí nó cód asincrónacha á scríobh agat, ní féidir leat an ORM a "
"úsáid le haghaidh fiosrúcháin ar an mbealach atá cur síos againn thuas, mar "
"ní féidir leat cód sioncrónas* a ghlaoch ó chód asincrónach - cuirfidh sé "
"bac ar an lúb imeachta (nó, is dóichí, tabharfaidh Django faoi deara agus "
"ardóidh sé “SynchronousOnlyOperation” chun é sin a stopadh ó tharlóidh)."

msgid ""
"Fortunately, you can do many queries using Django's asynchronous query APIs. "
"Every method that might block - such as ``get()`` or ``delete()`` - has an "
"asynchronous variant (``aget()`` or ``adelete()``), and when you iterate "
"over results, you can use asynchronous iteration (``async for``) instead."
msgstr ""
"Ar ámharaí an tsaoil, is féidir leat go leor ceisteanna a dhéanamh ag baint "
"úsáide as APIs ceist asincrónach Django. Tá leagan asincrónach ag gach modh "
"a d'fhéadfadh bac a chur - mar shampla ``get () ``nó ``delete ()`` - ``nó "
"``adelete ()``), agus nuair a athraitheann tú thar thorthaí, is féidir leat "
"athrú asincrónach (`async for``) a úsáid ina ionad."

msgid "Query iteration"
msgstr "Athraitheadh ceisteanna"

msgid ""
"The default way of iterating over a query - with ``for`` - will result in a "
"blocking database query behind the scenes as Django loads the results at "
"iteration time. To fix this, you can swap to ``async for``::"
msgstr ""
"Beidh ceist bunachar sonraí blocála taobh thiar de na radhairc mar thoradh "
"ar an mbealach réamhshocraithe chun athrá thar cheist - le `for`` - - mar "
"thoradh ar an mbealach réamhshocraithe agus Django á luchtú ag am athraithe. "
"Chun é seo a shocrú, is féidir leat a mhalartú go ``async for``:"

msgid ""
"Be aware that you also can't do other things that might iterate over the "
"queryset, such as wrapping ``list()`` around it to force its evaluation (you "
"can use ``async for`` in a comprehension, if you want it)."
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas nach féidir leat rudaí eile a dhéanamh a d'fhéadfadh athrú "
"thar an tacar ceisteanna, mar shampla ``liosta () ``a fhilleadh timpeall air "
"chun a mheastóireacht a chur i bhfeidhm (is féidir leat ``async for`` a "
"úsáid i dtuiscint, más mian leat é)."

msgid ""
"Because ``QuerySet`` methods like ``filter()`` and ``exclude()`` do not "
"actually run the query - they set up the queryset to run when it's iterated "
"over - you can use those freely in asynchronous code. For a guide to which "
"methods can keep being used like this, and which have asynchronous versions, "
"read the next section."
msgstr ""
"Toisc nach ritheann modhanna ``QuerySet ``mar `filter ()`` agus ``eisiamh () "
"``an ceist i ndáiríre - bhunaíonn siad an tacar ceisteanna le rith nuair a "
"dhéantar é a athrá - is féidir leat iad sin a úsáid go saor i gcód "
"asincrónach. Le haghaidh treoir maidir le cé na modhanna is féidir a "
"choinneáil a úsáid mar seo, agus a bhfuil leaganacha asincrónacha acu, léigh "
"an chéad chuid eile."

msgid "``QuerySet`` and manager methods"
msgstr "``QuerySet ``agus modhanna bainisteora"

msgid ""
"Some methods on managers and querysets - like ``get()`` and ``first()`` - "
"force execution of the queryset and are blocking. Some, like ``filter()`` "
"and ``exclude()``, don't force execution and so are safe to run from "
"asynchronous code. But how are you supposed to tell the difference?"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann roinnt modhanna ar bhainisteoirí agus ceisteanna ceisteanna - "
"cosúil le ``get () ``agus ``first ()`` - forghníomhú an tacar ceisteanna "
"agus tá siad ag blocáil. Ní chuireann cuid acu, cosúil le `filter () ``agus "
"``eisiamh ()``, forghníomhú i bhfeidhm agus mar sin tá siad sábháilte a rith "
"ó chód asincrónach. Ach conas a cheaptar duit an difríocht a insint?"

msgid ""
"While you could poke around and see if there is an ``a``-prefixed version of "
"the method (for example, we have ``aget()`` but not ``afilter()``), there is "
"a more logical way - look up what kind of method it is in the :doc:`QuerySet "
"reference </ref/models/querysets>`."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhféadfá dul timpeall agus a fheiceáil an bhfuil leagan "
"réamhshocraithe ``a`` ann (mar shampla, tá ``aget () ``againn ach ní "
"``afilter ()``), tá bealach níos loighciúla ann - féach suas cén cineál modh "
"atá ann in:doc: `QuerySet tagair`. </ref/models/querysets>"

msgid ""
"In there, you'll find the methods on QuerySets grouped into two sections:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, gheobhaidh tú na modhanna ar QuerySets atá grúpáilte ina dhá chuid:"

msgid ""
"*Methods that return new querysets*: These are the non-blocking ones, and "
"don't have asynchronous versions. You're free to use these in any situation, "
"though read the notes on ``defer()`` and ``only()`` before you use them."
msgstr ""
"* Modhanna a thabharann fiosrúcháin nua*: Is iad seo na cinn neamh-bhlocála, "
"agus níl leaganacha asincrónacha acu. Tá saor ort iad seo a úsáid in aon "
"chás, cé léigh na nótaí ar ``defer () ``agus ``only ()`` sula n-úsáideann tú "
"iad."

msgid ""
"*Methods that do not return querysets*: These are the blocking ones, and "
"have asynchronous versions - the asynchronous name for each is noted in its "
"documentation, though our standard pattern is to add an ``a`` prefix."
msgstr ""
"* Modhanna nach gcuireann fiosrúcháin ar ais *: Is iad seo na cinn blocála, "
"agus tá leaganacha asincrónacha acu - tugtar an t-ainm asincrónach do gach "
"ceann acu faoi deara ina dhoiciméadú, cé gur é ár bpatrún caighdeánach "
"réimír `a ``a chur leis."

msgid ""
"Using this distinction, you can work out when you need to use asynchronous "
"versions, and when you don't. For example, here's a valid asynchronous "
"query::"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as an idirdhealú seo, is féidir leat oibriú amach nuair is "
"gá duit leaganacha asincrónacha a úsáid, agus nuair nach ndéanann tú. Mar "
"shampla, seo ceist asincrónach bailí:"

msgid ""
"``filter()`` returns a queryset, and so it's fine to keep chaining it inside "
"an asynchronous environment, whereas ``first()`` evaluates and returns a "
"model instance - thus, we change to ``afirst()``, and use ``await`` at the "
"front of the whole expression in order to call it in an asynchronous-"
"friendly way."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``filter () ``tacar fiosrúcháin, agus mar sin tá sé go breá é a "
"choinneáil taobh istigh de thimpeallacht asincrónach, ach déanann ``first "
"()`` measúnú agus filleann sé samhail - dá bhrí sin, athraímid go ``first () "
"``, agus úsáidimid ```ag teacht tosaigh an abairt iomlán chun é a ghlaoch ar "
"bhealach asincrónach."

msgid ""
"If you forget to put the ``await`` part in, you may see errors like "
"*\"coroutine object has no attribute x\"* or *\"<coroutine …>\"* strings in "
"place of your model instances. If you ever see these, you are missing an "
"``await`` somewhere to turn that coroutine into a real value."
msgstr ""
"<coroutine ... >Má dhéanann tú dearmad an chuid ```ag fanacht ``a chur "
"isteach, b'fhéidir go bhfeicfidh tú earráidí cosúil* “níl aon tréith x” * nó "
"*\"* teaghráin ag réad coroutine in ionad do chásanna samhail. Má fheiceann "
"tú iad seo riamh, tá “ag fanacht” in easnamh áit éigin chun an coroutine sin "
"a iompú ina luach fíor."

msgid "Transactions"
msgstr "Idirbhearta"

msgid ""
"Transactions are **not** currently supported with asynchronous queries and "
"updates. You will find that trying to use one raises "
"``SynchronousOnlyOperation``."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear le hidirbhearta faoi láthair le ceisteanna agus nuashonruithe "
"asincrónacha. Gheobhaidh tú amach go n-ardaíonn iarracht ceann amháin a "
"úsáid ``SynchronousOnlyOperation``."

msgid ""
"If you wish to use a transaction, we suggest you write your ORM code inside "
"a separate, synchronous function and then call that using ``sync_to_async`` "
"- see :doc:`/topics/async` for more."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat idirbheart a úsáid, molaimid duit do chód ORM a scríobh istigh "
"de fheidhm shioncronach ar leithligh agus ansin glaoch air sin ag úsáid "
"`sync_to_async`` - féach: doc: `/topics/async` le haghaidh tuilleadh."

msgid "Querying ``JSONField``"
msgstr "Ag fiosrú ``Jsonfield``"

msgid ""
"Lookups implementation is different in :class:`~django.db.models.JSONField`, "
"mainly due to the existence of key transformations. To demonstrate, we will "
"use the following example model::"
msgstr ""
"Tá cur i bhfeidhm Lookups difriúil in:class: `~django.db.models.jsonField`, "
"go príomha mar gheall ar phríomhchlaochruithe a bheith ann. Chun a "
"thaispeáint, úsáidfimid an tsamhail sampla seo a leanas:"

msgid "Storing and querying for ``None``"
msgstr "Stóráil agus fiosrú ar ``None``"

msgid ""
"As with other fields, storing ``None`` as the field's value will store it as "
"SQL ``NULL``. While not recommended, it is possible to store JSON scalar "
"``null`` instead of SQL ``NULL`` by using :class:`Value(None, JSONField()) "
"<django.db.models.Value>`."
msgstr ""
"Mar is amhlaidh le réimsí eile, stóráilfear ``None`` mar luach an réimse é "
"mar SQL ``NULL``. <django.db.models.Value>Cé nach mholtar, is féidir scalar "
"JSON a stóráil ``null`` in ionad SQL ``NULL`` trí:class: `Value (None, "
"JSONField ()) `a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Whichever of the values is stored, when retrieved from the database, the "
"Python representation of the JSON scalar ``null`` is the same as SQL "
"``NULL``, i.e. ``None``. Therefore, it can be hard to distinguish between "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Cibé ceann de na luachanna a stóráiltear, nuair a aisghabtar ón mbunachar "
"sonraí, tá léiriú Python ar an scalar JSON ``null`` mar an gcéanna le SQL "
"``NULL``, ie ``None ``. Dá bhrí sin, is féidir go mbeadh sé deacair "
"idirdhealú eatarthu."

msgid ""
"This only applies to ``None`` as the top-level value of the field. If "
"``None`` is inside a :py:class:`list` or :py:class:`dict`, it will always be "
"interpreted as JSON ``null``."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann sé seo ach le ``None`` mar luach barrleibhéil an réimse. Má tá "
"``None`` taobh istigh de a:py:class: `list` nó: py:class: `dict`, "
"léirmhínítear é i gcónaí mar JSON ``null``."

msgid ""
"When querying, ``None`` value will always be interpreted as JSON ``null``. "
"To query for SQL ``NULL``, use :lookup:`isnull`:"
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag fiosrú, léirmhínítear luach ``None ``i gcónaí mar JSON ``null``. "
"Chun fiosrú a dhéanamh ar SQL ``NULL``, bain úsáid:lookup: `isnull`:"

msgid ""
"Unless you are sure you wish to work with SQL ``NULL`` values, consider "
"setting ``null=False`` and providing a suitable default for empty values, "
"such as ``default=dict``."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú cinnte gur mhaith leat oibriú le luachanna SQL ``NULL``, "
"smaoinigh ar `Null=False`` a shocrú agus réamhshocrú oiriúnach a sholáthar "
"do luachanna folmha, mar shampla ``default=dict``."

msgid ""
"Storing JSON scalar ``null`` does not violate :attr:`null=False "
"<django.db.models.Field.null>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Field.null>Ní sháraíonn scálar JSON ``null`` a stóráil: "
"attr: `Null = false `."

msgid "Key, index, and path transforms"
msgstr "Athraíonn eochair, innéacs agus cosán"

msgid ""
"To query based on a given dictionary key, use that key as the lookup name:"
msgstr ""
"Chun ceist a dhéanamh bunaithe ar eochair foclóra ar leith, bain úsáid as an "
"eochair sin mar ainm an chuardaigh:"

msgid "Multiple keys can be chained together to form a path lookup:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir eochracha iolracha a shlánú le chéile chun cuardach cosáin a "
"fhoirmiú:"

msgid ""
"If the key is an integer, it will be interpreted as an index transform in an "
"array:"
msgstr ""
"Más slámhshláir é an eochair, léirmhínítear é mar athrú innéacs i sraith:"

msgid ""
"If the key you wish to query by clashes with the name of another lookup, use "
"the :lookup:`contains <jsonfield.contains>` lookup instead."
msgstr ""
"<jsonfield.contains>Má tá an eochair is mian leat a cheistiú trí chomhraic "
"le hainm cuardaigh eile, bain úsáid as an cuardach: `lookup: `include `ina "
"ionad."

msgid "To query for missing keys, use the ``isnull`` lookup:"
msgstr ""
"Chun ceist a dhéanamh ar eochracha atá in easnamh, bain úsáid as an lorg "
"``isnull``:"

msgid ""
"The lookup examples given above implicitly use the :lookup:`exact` lookup. "
"Key, index, and path transforms can also be chained "
