"socraigh an luach nua mar an samhail nua ar mhaith leat a chur in iúl dó. "
"Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"The ``update()`` method is applied instantly and returns the number of rows "
"matched by the query (which may not be equal to the number of rows updated "
"if some rows already have the new value). The only restriction on "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` being updated is that it can "
"only access one database table: the model's main table. You can filter based "
"on related fields, but you can only update columns in the model's main "
"table. Example:"
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an modh `update () ``i bhfeidhm láithreach agus filleann sé líon na "
"sraitheanna a mheaitseálann an cheist (nach bhféadfadh a bheith comhionann "
"le líon na sraitheanna a nuashonraítear má tá an luach nua ag roinnt "
"sraitheanna cheana féin). Is é an t-aon srian ar an:class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset` atá á nuashonrú ná nach féidir leis "
"rochtain a fháil ach tábla bunachar sonraí amháin: príomh-tábla an tsamhail. "
"Is féidir leat scagadh bunaithe ar réimsí gaolmhara, ach ní féidir leat "
"colúin a nuashonrú ach i bpríomh-thábla an tsamhail. Sampla:"

msgid ""
"Be aware that the ``update()`` method is converted directly to an SQL "
"statement. It is a bulk operation for direct updates. It doesn't run "
"any :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` methods on your models, or emit the "
"``pre_save`` or ``post_save`` signals (which are a consequence of "
"calling :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save`), or honor "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.DateField.auto_now` field option. If you want "
"to save every item in a :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` and make "
"sure that the :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` method is called on each "
"instance, you don't need any special function to handle that. Loop over them "
"and call :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save`::"
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas go ndéantar an modh ``update () ``a thiontú go díreach go "
"ráiteas SQL. Is mór-oibríocht í le haghaidh nuashonruithe díreacha. Ní "
"ritheann sé modhanna ar bit:meth: `~django.db.models.model.save` ar do "
"mhúnlaí, nó astaíonn sé na comharthaí ``pre_save`` nó ``post_save`` (atá mar "
"thoradh ar ghlao:meth: `~Django.db.Models.Model.save`), nó onóir dó:attr: "
"`~django.db.db.Rogha réimse models.datefield.auto_now`. Más mian leat gach "
"mír a shábháil in a:class: `~django.db.models.query.queryset` agus a "
"chinntiú go ndéantar an modh:meth: `~django.db.models.model.save` ar gach "
"cás, ní gá duit aon fheidhm speisialta chun é sin a láimhseáil. Lúb orthu "
"agus glaoigh ar: meth: `~django.db.models.model.save`::"

msgid ""
"Calls to update can also use :class:`F expressions <django.db.models.F>` to "
"update one field based on the value of another field in the model. This is "
"especially useful for incrementing counters based upon their current value. "
"For example, to increment the pingback count for every entry in the blog:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le glaonna chun nuashonrú a úsáid freisin: aicme: abairtí `F "
"<django.db.models.F>`chun réimse amháin a nuashonrú bunaithe ar luach réimse "
"eile sa tsamhail. Tá sé seo úsáideach go háirithe chun cuntair a mhéadú "
"bunaithe ar a luach reatha. Mar shampla, chun an comhaireamh pingback a "
"mhéadú do gach iontráil sa bhlag:"

msgid ""
"However, unlike ``F()`` objects in filter and exclude clauses, you can't "
"introduce joins when you use ``F()`` objects in an update -- you can only "
"reference fields local to the model being updated. If you attempt to "
"introduce a join with an ``F()`` object, a ``FieldError`` will be raised:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, murab ionann agus rudaí `F () ``i gclásail scagaire agus "
"eisiamh, ní féidir leat comhpháirteanna a thabhairt isteach nuair a "
"úsáideann tú rudaí ``F ()`` i nuashonrú - ní féidir leat tagairt a dhéanamh "
"ach réimsí áitiúla don tsamhail atá á nuashonrú. Má dhéanann tú iarracht "
"teagmháil a thabhairt isteach le réad ``F () ``, ardófar ``Fielderror``:"

msgid "Related objects"
msgstr "Rudaí gaolmhara"

msgid ""
"When you define a relationship in a model (i.e., "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`, :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField`, "
"or :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`), instances of that model will "
"have a convenient API to access the related object(s)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shainmhíníonn tú caidreamh i samhail (ie: a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey`, :class: `~django.db.models.onetoonefield`, "
"nó:class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField`), beidh API áisiúil ag cásanna "
"den tsamhail sin chun rochtain a fháil ar an réad (í) gaolmhar."

msgid ""
"Using the models at the top of this page, for example, an ``Entry`` object "
"``e`` can get its associated ``Blog`` object by accessing the ``blog`` "
"attribute: ``e.blog``."
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as na samhlacha ag barr an leathanaigh seo, mar shampla, is "
"féidir le réad ```Entry`` a réad gaolmhar ``Blog`` a fháil trí rochtain a "
"fháil ar an tréith ``blog ``: `e.blog``."

msgid ""
"(Behind the scenes, this functionality is implemented by "
"Python :doc:`descriptors <python:howto/descriptor>`. This shouldn't really "
"matter to you, but we point it out here for the curious.)"
msgstr ""
"<python:howto/descriptor>( Taobh thiar de na radhairc, cuireann Python: Doc: "
"`tuairiscí 'i bhfeidhm an fheidhmiúlacht seo. Níor chóir go bhfuil sé seo "
"tábhachtach duit i ndáiríre, ach cuirimid in iúl é anseo do dhaoine "
"aisteach.)"

msgid ""
"Django also creates API accessors for the \"other\" side of the relationship "
"-- the link from the related model to the model that defines the "
"relationship. For example, a ``Blog`` object ``b`` has access to a list of "
"all related ``Entry`` objects via the ``entry_set`` attribute: "
"``b.entry_set.all()``."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn Django rochtainí API freisin don taobh “eile” den chaidreamh - an "
"nasc ón tsamhail ghaolmhar leis an tsamhail a shainmhíníonn an caidreamh. "
"Mar shampla, tá rochtain ag réad ``Blog`` ``b`` ar liosta de na rudaí "
"gaolmhara ``Entry`` tríd an tréith ``entry_set``: `b.entry_set.all () ``."

msgid ""
"All examples in this section use the sample ``Blog``, ``Author`` and "
"``Entry`` models defined at the top of this page."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann gach sampla sa chuid seo na samhlacha samplacha ``Blog``, `Údar`` "
"agus ``Iontrála`` atá sainmhínithe ag barr an leathanaigh seo."

msgid "One-to-many relationships"
msgstr "Caidrimh duine le go leor"

msgid "Forward"
msgstr "Ar aghaidh"

msgid ""
"If a model has a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`, instances of that "
"model will have access to the related (foreign) object via an attribute of "
"the model."
msgstr ""
"Má tá a: class: `~django.db.models.foreignKey` ag samhail, beidh rochtain ag "
"cásanna den tsamhail sin ar an réad gaolmhar (eachtrach) trí thréith den "
"tsamhail."

msgid ""
"You can get and set via a foreign-key attribute. As you may expect, changes "
"to the foreign key aren't saved to the database until you "
"call :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save`. Example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat a fháil agus a shocrú trí thréith eochair eachtrach. Mar a "
"d'fhéadfá a bheith ag súil leis, ní shábháiltear athruithe ar an eochair "
"eachtrach sa bhunachar sonraí go dtí go nglaonn tú ar: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.save`. Sampla:"

msgid ""
"If a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` field has ``null=True`` set "
"(i.e., it allows ``NULL`` values), you can assign ``None`` to remove the "
"relation. Example:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá a: class: `~django.db.models.foreignKey` sraith ``Null=True`` réimse "
"(ie, ceadaíonn sé luachanna ``NULL``), is féidir leat ``None`` a shannadh "
"chun an gaol a bhaint. Sampla:"

msgid ""
"Forward access to one-to-many relationships is cached the first time the "
"related object is accessed. Subsequent accesses to the foreign key on the "
"same object instance are cached. Example:"
msgstr ""
"Déantar rochtain ar aghaidh ar chaidrimh duine le go leor a stóráil an chéad "
"uair a rochtaítear ar an réad gaolmhar. Déantar rochtainí ina dhiaidh sin ar "
"an eochair eachtrach ar an gcás réad céanna a stóráil. Sampla:"

msgid ""
"Note that "
"the :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` "
"method recursively prepopulates the cache of all one-to-many relationships "
"ahead of time. Example:"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go ndéanann an modh:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related`:class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset` taisce gach caidreamh duine le go leor "
"roimh am go réamh-athshlánach. Sampla:"

msgid "Following relationships \"backward\""
msgstr "Ag leanúint caidrimh “siar”"

msgid ""
"If a model has a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`, instances of the "
"foreign-key model will have access to a :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` "
"that returns all instances of the first model. By default, "
"this :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` is named ``FOO_set``, where ``FOO`` "
"is the source model name, lowercased. "
"This :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` returns ``QuerySet`` instances, "
"which can be filtered and manipulated as described in the \"Retrieving "
"objects\" section above."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can override the ``FOO_set`` name by setting "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` parameter in "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` definition. For example, if the "
"``Entry`` model was altered to ``blog = ForeignKey(Blog, "
"on_delete=models.CASCADE, related_name='entries')``, the above example code "
"would look like this:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an t-ainm `foo_set`` a shárú tríd an sainmhíniú:attr: "
"`~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey.Related_Name` a shocrú sa sainmhíniú: class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey`. Mar shampla, má athraíodh an tsamhail "
"``Entry ``go `blog = ForeignKey (Blog, on_delete=Models.Cascade, "
"related_name='entries')``, bheadh cuma seo ar an gcód sampla thuas:"

msgid "Using a custom reverse manager"
msgstr "Bainisteoir droim saincheaptha a úsáid"

msgid ""
"By default the :class:`~django.db.models.fields.related.RelatedManager` used "
"for reverse relations is a subclass of the :ref:`default manager <manager-"
"names>` for that model. If you would like to specify a different manager for "
"a given query you can use the following syntax::"
msgstr ""
"<manager-names>De réir réamhshocraithe an: class: "
"`~django.db.Models.Fields.Related.RelatedManager` a úsáidtear le haghaidh "
"caidrimh droim ina fho-aicme den :ref: `bainisteoir réamhshocraithe `don "
"tsamhail sin. Más mian leat bainisteoir difriúil a shonrú le haghaidh ceist "
"ar leith is féidir leat an comhréir seo a leanas a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"If ``EntryManager`` performed default filtering in its ``get_queryset()`` "
"method, that filtering would apply to the ``all()`` call."
msgstr ""
"Má rinne ``EntryManager`` scagadh réamhshocraithe ina mhodh ``get_queryset "
"() ``, bheadh feidhm ag an scagadh sin leis an nglao ``all ()``."

msgid ""
"Specifying a custom reverse manager also enables you to call its custom "
"methods::"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann bainisteoir droim saincheaptha a shonrú ar chumas tú a mhodhanna "
"saincheaptha a ghlaoch freisin:"

msgid "Interaction with prefetching"
msgstr "Idirghníomhaíocht le réamhghabháil"

msgid ""
"When calling :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related` with "
"a reverse relation, the default manager will be used. If you want to "
"prefetch related objects using a custom reverse manager, "
"use :class:`Prefetch() <django.db.models.Prefetch>`. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag glaoch: meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.prefetch_related` "
"le gaol droim, úsáidfear an bainisteoir réamhshocraithe. "
"<django.db.models.Prefetch>Más mian leat rudaí gaolmhara a réamh-fháil ag "
"baint úsáide as bainisteoir droim saincheaptha, bain úsáid as: class: "
"`Prefetch () `. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Additional methods to handle related objects"
msgstr "Modhanna breise chun rudaí gaolmhara a láim"

msgid ""
"In addition to the :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` methods defined "
"in \"Retrieving objects\" above, "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` "
"has additional methods used to handle the set of related objects. A synopsis "
"of each is below, and complete details can be found in the :doc:`related "
"objects reference </ref/models/relations>`."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na modhanna: :class: `~django.db.models.query.querySet` atá "
"sainmhínithe i “Aisghabháil rudaí” thuas, tá modhanna breise ag an:class: "
"`~django.db.models.manager` chun an tacar rudaí gaolmhara a láimhseáil. Tá "
"achoimre ar gach ceann thíos, agus is féidir sonraí iomlána a fháil in:doc: "
"`tagairt rudaí gaolmhara '</ref/models/relations>."

msgid "``add(obj1, obj2, ...)``"
msgstr "``add (obj1, obj2, ... ) ``"

msgid "Adds the specified model objects to the related object set."
msgstr "Cuireann sé na rudaí samhail sonraithe leis an tacar réad gaolmhar."

msgid "``create(**kwargs)``"
msgstr "``cruthaigh (**kwargs) ``"

msgid ""
"Creates a new object, saves it and puts it in the related object set. "
"Returns the newly created object."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé réad nua, sábhálann sé agus cuireann sé sa tacar réad gaolmhar "
"é. Tugann sé an réad nua-chruthaithe ar ais."

msgid "``remove(obj1, obj2, ...)``"
msgstr "``bhaint (obj1, obj2, ... ) ``"

msgid "Removes the specified model objects from the related object set."
msgstr "Baineann na rudaí samhail sonraithe as an tacar réad gaolmhar."

msgid "``clear()``"
msgstr "``soiléir () ``"

msgid "Removes all objects from the related object set."
msgstr "Baineann gach rud as an tacar réad gaolmhar."

msgid "``set(objs)``"
msgstr "``set (objs) ``"

msgid "Replace the set of related objects."
msgstr "Cuir an tacar rudaí gaolmhara in ionad."

msgid ""
"To assign the members of a related set, use the ``set()`` method with an "
"iterable of object instances. For example, if ``e1`` and ``e2`` are "
"``Entry`` instances::"
msgstr ""
"Chun baill tacar gaolmhar a shannadh, bain úsáid as an modh ``set () ``le "
"cásanna réad inathraithe. Mar shampla, más cásanna ```Iontrála`` iad `e1`` "
"agus ``e2``:"

msgid ""
"If the ``clear()`` method is available, any preexisting objects will be "
"removed from the ``entry_set`` before all objects in the iterable (in this "
"case, a list) are added to the set. If the ``clear()`` method is *not* "
"available, all objects in the iterable will be added without removing any "
"existing elements."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an modh ``clear () ``ar fáil, bainfear aon rudaí atá ann cheana ón "
"`entry_set`` sula gcuirfear gach rud san athraitheach (sa chás seo, liosta) "
"leis an tacar. Má tá an modh ``clear () ``*níl* ar fáil, cuirfear gach rud "
"san athraitheach leis gan aon eilimintí atá ann cheana a bhaint."

msgid ""
"Each \"reverse\" operation described in this section has an immediate effect "
"on the database. Every addition, creation and deletion is immediately and "
"automatically saved to the database."
msgstr ""
"Tá éifeacht láithreach ag gach oibríocht “droim” a thuairiscítear sa chuid "
"seo ar an mbunachar sonraí. Sábháiltear gach breise, cruthú agus scriosadh "
"láithreach agus go huathoibríoch sa bhunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Both ends of a many-to-many relationship get automatic API access to the "
"other end. The API works similar to a \"backward\" one-to-many relationship, "
"above."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann an dá fhoirceann de chaidreamh go leor rochtain uathoibríoch API "
"ar an gceann eile. Oibríonn an API cosúil le caidreamh duine le go leor “ar "
"chúl”, thuas."

msgid ""
"One difference is in the attribute naming: The model that defines "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` uses the attribute name of "
"that field itself, whereas the \"reverse\" model uses the lowercased model "
"name of the original model, plus ``'_set'`` (just like reverse one-to-many "
"relationships)."
msgstr ""
"Tá difríocht amháin san ainmniú tréithe: Úsáideann an tsamhail a "
"shainmhíníonn an:class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField` ainm tréithe an "
"réimse sin féin, ach úsáideann an tsamhail “droim” ainm samhail íseal an "
"tsamhail bhunaidh, móide ``'_set'` (díreach cosúil le caidrimh aon-go leor)."

msgid "An example makes this easier to understand::"
msgstr "Déanann sampla é seo níos éasca a thuiscint:"

msgid ""
"Like :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`, :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` "
"can specify :attr:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField.related_name`. In the "
"above example, if the :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` in "
"``Entry`` had specified ``related_name='entries'``, then each ``Author`` "
"instance would have an ``entries`` attribute instead of ``entry_set``."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey`, :class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField` is féidir le sonraithe:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField.Related_Nam`. Sa sampla thuas, má "
"shonraíodh an:class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField` i `Entry`` "
"``related_name='entries'`, ansin bheadh tréith ``entries`` ag gach "
"``Author`` tréith ``entries`` in ionad `entry_set``."

msgid ""
"Another difference from one-to-many relationships is that in addition to "
"model instances,  the ``add()``, ``set()``, and ``remove()`` methods on many-"
"to-many relationships accept primary key values. For example, if ``e1`` and "
"``e2`` are ``Entry`` instances, then these ``set()`` calls work identically::"
msgstr ""
"Difríocht eile ó chaidrimh duine le go leor ná go nglacann na modhanna ``add "
"() ``, `set ()``, agus ``remove () ``ar chaidrimh go leor príomhluachanna, i "
"dteannta le cásanna samhail. Mar shampla, más cásanna ``Entry`` iad ``e1`` "
"agus ``e2``, ansin oibríonn na glaonna ``set () ``seo go comhionann:"

msgid ""
"One-to-one relationships are very similar to many-to-one relationships. If "
"you define a :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` on your model, "
"instances of that model will have access to the related object via an "
"attribute of the model."
msgstr ""
"Tá caidrimh duine le duine an-chosúil le caidrimh go leor. Má shainmhíníonn "
"tú a:class: `~django.db.models.onetoonefield` ar do mhúnla, beidh rochtain "
"ag cásanna den tsamhail sin ar an réad gaolmhar trí thréith den tsamhail."

msgid ""
"The difference comes in \"reverse\" queries. The related model in a one-to-"
"one relationship also has access to a :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` "
"object, but that :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` represents a single "
"object, rather than a collection of objects::"
msgstr ""
"Tagann an difríocht i gceisteanna “droim”. Tá rochtain ag an tsamhail "
"ghaolmhar i gcaidreamh duine le duine freisin ar réad a:class: "
"`~django.db.Models.Manager`, ach is ionann: class: "
"`~django.db.Models.Manager` réad amháin, seachas bailiúchán rudaí:"

msgid ""
"If no object has been assigned to this relationship, Django will raise a "
"``DoesNotExist`` exception."
msgstr ""
"Mura sannadh aon réad don chaidreamh seo, ardóidh Django eisceacht "
"`DoesNotExist`."

msgid ""
"Instances can be assigned to the reverse relationship in the same way as you "
"would assign the forward relationship::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir cásanna a shannadh don chaidreamh droim ar an mbealach céanna agus "
"a shannófá an réamhchaidreamh:"

msgid "How are the backward relationships possible?"
msgstr "Conas is féidir na caidrimh chúl indéanta?"

msgid ""
"Other object-relational mappers require you to define relationships on both "
"sides. The Django developers believe this is a violation of the DRY (Don't "
"Repeat Yourself) principle, so Django only requires you to define the "
"relationship on one end."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn mapaitheoirí réad-ghaolmhara eile ort caidrimh a shainiú ar an dá "
"thaobh. Creideann forbróirí Django gur sárú é seo ar phrionsabal DRY (Ná "
"Déan Athdhéanamh Féin), mar sin ní éilíonn Django ach ort an caidreamh a "
"shainiú ar cheann amháin."

msgid ""
"But how is this possible, given that a model class doesn't know which other "
"model classes are related to it until those other model classes are loaded?"
msgstr ""
"Ach conas is féidir é seo a dhéanamh, ós rud é nach bhfuil a fhios ag rang "
"samhail cé na ranganna samhail eile a bhaineann leis go dtí go luchtaítear "
"na ranganna samhail eile sin?"

msgid ""
"The answer lies in the :data:`app registry <django.apps.apps>`. When Django "
"starts, it imports each application listed in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, and "
"then the ``models`` module inside each application. Whenever a new model "
"class is created, Django adds backward-relationships to any related models. "
"If the related models haven't been imported yet, Django keeps tracks of the "
"relationships and adds them when the related models eventually are imported."
msgstr ""
"<django.apps.apps>Tá an freagra sa chlárlann: data: `app `. Nuair a "
"thosaíonn Django, allmhairíonn sé gach feidhmchlár atá liostaithe "
"in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, agus ansin an modúl ``samhlacha ``taobh istigh "
"de gach feidhmchlár. Aon uair a chruthaítear rang samhail nua, cuireann "
"Django caidrimh siar le haon mhúnlaí gaolmhara. Mura n-allmhairíodh na "
"samhlacha gaolmhara fós, coinníonn Django rianta de na caidrimh agus "
"cuireann sé leo nuair a allmhairítear na samhlacha gaolmhara sa deireadh."

msgid ""
"For this reason, it's particularly important that all the models you're "
"using be defined in applications listed in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. "
"Otherwise, backwards relations may not work properly."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcúis seo, tá sé tábhachtach go bhfuil na samhlacha go léir atá á "
"úsáid agat a shainiú in iarratais atá liostaithe in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`. Seachas sin, b'fhéidir nach n-oibreoidh caidreamh cúil i "
"gceart."

msgid "Queries over related objects"
msgstr "Fiosruithe ar rudaí gaolm"

msgid ""
"Queries involving related objects follow the same rules as queries involving "
"normal value fields. When specifying the value for a query to match, you may "
"use either an object instance itself, or the primary key value for the "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Leanann ceisteanna a bhaineann le rudaí gaolmhara na rialacha céanna le "
"ceisteanna a bhaineann le réimsí Nuair a shonraítear an luach le haghaidh "
"ceisteanna a mheaitseáil, féadfaidh tú sampla réada féin, nó an príomhluach "
"don réad a úsáid."

msgid ""
"For example, if you have a Blog object ``b`` with ``id=5``, the following "
"three queries would be identical::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá réad Blag ``b`` agat le `id=5``, bheadh na trí cheist seo "
"a leanas comhionann:"

msgid "Falling back to raw SQL"
msgstr "Ag titim ar ais go SQL amh"

msgid ""
"If you find yourself needing to write an SQL query that is too complex for "
"Django's database-mapper to handle, you can fall back on writing SQL by "
"hand. Django has a couple of options for writing raw SQL queries; see :doc:`/"
"topics/db/sql`."
msgstr ""
"Má bhíonn gá duit fiosrúchán SQL a scríobh atá ró-chasta chun mapálaí "
"bunachar sonraí Django a láimhseáil, is féidir leat titim siar ar SQL a "
"scríobh de láimh. Tá cúpla rogha ag Django chun ceisteanna SQL amh a "
"scríobh; féach: doc: `/topics/db/sql`."

msgid ""
"Finally, it's important to note that the Django database layer is merely an "
"interface to your database. You can access your database via other tools, "
"programming languages or database frameworks; there's nothing Django-"
"specific about your database."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, tá sé tábhachtach a thabhairt faoi deara nach bhfuil ciseal "
"bunachar sonraí Django ach comhéadan le do bhunachar sonraí. Is féidir leat "
"rochtain a fháil ar do bhunachar sonraí trí uirlisí eile, teangacha cláir nó "
"creataí bunachar sonraí; níl aon rud Django-sonrach faoi do bhunachar sonraí."

msgid "Search"
msgstr "Cuardach"

msgid ""
"A common task for web applications is to search some data in the database "
"with user input. In a simple case, this could be filtering a list of objects "
"by a category. A more complex use case might require searching with "
"weighting, categorization, highlighting, multiple languages, and so on. This "
"document explains some of the possible use cases and the tools you can use."
msgstr ""
"Tasc coitianta d'fheidhmchláir gréasáin is ea roinnt sonraí sa bhunachar "
"sonraí a chuardach le hionchur úsáideora. I gcás simplí, d'fhéadfadh sé seo "
"a bheith ag scagadh liosta rudaí de réir catagóire. D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh gá "
"le cás úsáide níos casta cuardach le meáchain, catagóiriú, aibhsiú, "
"teangacha éagsúla, agus mar sin de. Míníonn an doiciméad seo cuid de na "
"cásanna úsáide féideartha agus na huirlisí is féidir leat a úsáid."

msgid "We'll refer to the same models used in :doc:`/topics/db/queries`."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaimid tagairt do na samhlacha céanna a úsáidtear in:doc: `/topics/db/"
"queries`."

msgid "Use Cases"
msgstr "Úsáid Cásanna"

msgid "Standard textual queries"
msgstr "Ceisteanna téacsúla caighdeán"

msgid ""
"Text-based fields have a selection of matching operations. For example, you "
"may wish to allow lookup up an author like so:"
msgstr ""
"Tá rogha oibríochtaí meaitseála ag réimsí téacs-bhunaithe. Mar shampla, "
"b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat údar a chuardach mar sin a cheadú:"

msgid ""
"This is a very fragile solution as it requires the user to know an exact "
"substring of the author's name. A better approach could be a case-"
"insensitive match (:lookup:`icontains`), but this is only marginally better."
msgstr ""
"Is réiteach an-leochaileach é seo mar éilíonn sé ar an úsáideoir fotheagán "
"cruinn d'ainm an údair a fháil amach. D'fhéadfadh cur chuige níos fearr a "
"bheith ina mheaitseáil cás-neamh-íogair (:lookup: `icontains`), ach níl sé "
"seo ach beagán níos fearr."

msgid "A database's more advanced comparison functions"
msgstr "Feidhmeanna comparáide níos airde bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"If you're using PostgreSQL, Django provides :doc:`a selection of database "
"specific tools </ref/contrib/postgres/search>` to allow you to leverage more "
"complex querying options. Other databases have different selections of "
"tools, possibly via plugins or user-defined functions. Django doesn't "
"include any support for them at this time. We'll use some examples from "
"PostgreSQL to demonstrate the kind of functionality databases may have."
msgstr ""
"Má tá PostgreSQL á úsáid agat, soláthraíonn Django: doc: `rogha uirlisí "
"sonracha bunachar sonraí' chun ligean duit roghanna fiosrúcháin níos casta a "
"gh</ref/contrib/postgres/search> iaráil. Tá roghanna éagsúla uirlisí ag "
"bunachair sonraí eile, b'fhéidir trí bhreiseáin nó feidhmeanna sainmhínithe "
"Ní chuimsíonn Django aon tacaíocht dóibh ag an am seo. Úsáidfimid roinnt "
"samplaí ó PostgreSQL chun an cineál feidhmiúlachta a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ag "
"bunachair sonraí a thaispeáint."

msgid "Searching in other databases"
msgstr "Cuardach i mbunachair sonraí eile"

msgid ""
"All of the searching tools provided by :mod:`django.contrib.postgres` are "
"constructed entirely on public APIs such as :doc:`custom lookups </ref/"
"models/lookups>` and :doc:`database functions </ref/models/database-"
"functions>`. Depending on your database, you should be able to construct "
"queries to allow similar APIs. If there are specific things which cannot be "
"achieved this way, please open a ticket."
msgstr ""
"Tá na huirlisí cuardaigh go léir a sholáthraí:mod: `django.contrib.postgres` "
"tógtha go hiomlán ar APIs poiblí mar: doc: `saincheaptha lookups` agus:doc: "
"`feidhmeanna bunachar sonraí</ref/models/lookups> </ref/models/database-"
"functions> `. Ag brath ar do bhunachar sonraí, ba cheart go mbeadh tú in ann "
"ceisteanna a thógáil chun APIs comhchosúla Má tá rudaí ar leith ann nach "
"féidir a bhaint amach ar an mbealach seo, oscail ticéad le do thoil."

msgid ""
"In the above example, we determined that a case insensitive lookup would be "
"more useful. When dealing with non-English names, a further improvement is "
"to use :lookup:`unaccented comparison <unaccent>`:"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, chinneamar go mbeadh cuardach neamhíogair cás níos "
"úsáideach. <unaccent>Agus tú ag déileáil le hainmneacha neamh-Bhéarla, is é "
"feabhas breise le húsáid:lookup: `comparáid unacented `:"

msgid ""
"This shows another issue, where we are matching against a different spelling "
"of the name. In this case we have an asymmetry though - a search for "
"``Helen`` will pick up ``Helena`` or ``Hélène``, but not the reverse. "
"Another option would be to use a :lookup:`trigram_similar` comparison, which "
"compares sequences of letters."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann sé seo saincheist eile, áit a bhfuilimid ag meaitseáil i gcoinne "
"litriú difriúil an ainm. Sa chás seo tá neamhshiméadracht againn áfach - "
"piocfaidh cuardach ar ``Helen`` suas ``Helena`` nó ``Hélène``, ach ní an "
"cúil. Rogha eile ba ea comparáid a: lookup: `trigram_similar` a úsáid, a "
"dhéanann comparáid idir seicheamh litreacha."

msgid ""
"Now we have a different problem - the longer name of \"Helena Bonham "
"Carter\" doesn't show up as it is much longer. Trigram searches consider all "
"combinations of three letters, and compares how many appear in both search "
"and source strings. For the longer name, there are more combinations that "
"don't appear in the source string, so it is no longer considered a close "
"match."
msgstr ""
"Anois tá fadhb dhifriúil againn - ní thaispeánann ainm níos faide “Helena "
"Bonham Carter” mar tá sé i bhfad níos faide. Measann cuardaigh Trigram gach "
"teaglaim de thrí litir, agus déanann siad comparáid idir cé mhéad atá le "
"feiceáil i dteaghráin cuardaigh agus foinse Maidir leis an ainm níos faide, "
"tá níos mó teaglaim ann nach bhfuil le feiceáil sa sreang foinse, mar sin ní "
"mheastar gur dlúthmheaitseáil é a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The correct choice of comparison functions here depends on your particular "
"data set, for example the language(s) used and the type of text being "
"searched. All of the examples we've seen are on short strings where the user "
"is likely to enter something close (by varying definitions) to the source "
"data."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann an rogha ceart feidhmeanna comparáide anseo ar do shraith sonraí, "
"mar shampla an teanga/na teanga/na teangacha a úsáidtear agus an cineál "
"téacs atá á chuardach. Tá na samplaí go léir a chonaic muid ar teaghráin "
"ghearra inar dócha go gcuirfidh an t-úsáideoir rud éigin gar (trí "
"shainmhínithe éagsúla) do na sonraí foinse."

msgid "Document-based search"
msgstr "Cuardach doiciméadarbhun"

msgid ""
"Standard database operations stop being a useful approach when you start "
"considering large blocks of text. Whereas the examples above can be thought "
"of as operations on a string of characters, full text search looks at the "
"actual words. Depending on the system used, it's likely to use some of the "
"following ideas:"
msgstr ""
"Stopann oibríochtaí caighdeánacha bunachar sonraí ina chur chuige úsáideach "
"nuair a thosaíonn tú ag smaoineamh ar bh Cé gur féidir smaoineamh ar na "
"samplaí thuas mar oibríochtaí ar shreang carachtair, féachann cuardach téacs "
"iomlán ar na focail iarbhír. Ag brath ar an gcóras a úsáidtear, is dócha go "
"n-úsáidfidh sé cuid de na smaointe seo a leanas:"

msgid "Ignoring \"stop words\" such as \"a\", \"the\", \"and\"."
msgstr "Neamhaird a dhéanamh ar “focail stad” mar “a”, “an”, “agus”."

msgid "Stemming words, so that \"pony\" and \"ponies\" are considered similar."
msgstr ""
"Focail a spreagadh, ionas go meastar go bhfuil “pánach” agus “pánaigh” "
"cosúil leo."

msgid ""
"Weighting words based on different criteria such as how frequently they "
"appear in the text, or the importance of the fields, such as the title or "
"keywords, that they appear in."
msgstr ""
"Focail mheáchain bunaithe ar chritéir éagsúla amhail cé chomh minic a bhíonn "
"siad le feiceáil sa téacs, nó tábhacht na réimsí, amhail an teideal nó an "
"eochairfhocail, a bhfuil siad le feiceáil iontu."

msgid ""
"There are many alternatives for using searching software, some of the most "
"prominent are Elastic_ and Solr_. These are full document-based search "
"solutions. To use them with data from Django models, you'll need a layer "
"which translates your data into a textual document, including back-"
"references to the database ids. When a search using the engine returns a "
"certain document, you can then look it up in the database. There are a "
"variety of third-party libraries which are designed to help with this "
"process."
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor roghanna eile ann maidir le bogearraí cuardaigh a úsáid, is iad "
"Elastic_ agus Solr_ cuid de na cinn is suntasaí. Is réitigh chuardaigh "
"iomlána bunaithe ar dhoiciméid iad seo Chun iad a úsáid le sonraí ó mhúnlaí "
"Django, beidh ciseal ag teastáil uait a aistríonn do chuid sonraí go "
"doiciméad téacsúil, lena n-áirítear cúltagairtí do idí bunachar sonraí. "
"Nuair a chuireann cuardach ag baint úsáide as an inneall doiciméad áirithe "
"ar ais, is féidir leat é a lorg suas sa bhunachar sonraí ansin. Tá "
"éagsúlacht leabharlanna tríú páirtí ann atá deartha chun cabhrú leis an "
"bpróiseas seo."

msgid "PostgreSQL support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL has its own full text search implementation built-in. While not "
"as powerful as some other search engines, it has the advantage of being "
"inside your database and so can easily be combined with other relational "
"queries such as categorization."
msgstr ""
"Tá a chur i bhfeidhm cuardaigh téacs iomlán féin ionsuite ag PostgreSQL. Cé "
"nach bhfuil sé chomh cumhachtach le roinnt innill chuardaigh eile, tá an "
"buntáiste aige a bheith taobh istigh de do bhunachar sonraí agus mar sin is "
"féidir é a chomhcheangal go héasca le ceisteanna gaolmhara eile mar "
"chatagóiriú."

msgid ""
"The :mod:`django.contrib.postgres` module provides some helpers to make "
"these queries. For example, a query might select all the blog entries which "
"mention \"cheese\":"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an modúl:MOD: `django.contrib.postgres` roinnt cúntóirí chun na "
"ceisteanna seo a dhéanamh. Mar shampla, d'fhéadfadh ceist na hiontrálacha "
"blag go léir a luann “cáis” a roghnú:"

msgid "You can also filter on a combination of fields and on related models:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat scagadh freisin ar mheascán de réimsí agus ar mhúnlaí "
"gaolmhara:"

msgid ""
"See the ``contrib.postgres`` :doc:`/ref/contrib/postgres/search` document "
"for complete details."
msgstr ""
"Féach an doiciméad ``contrib.postgres``:doc: `/ref/contrib/postgres/search` "
"le haghaidh sonraí iomlána."

msgid "Performing raw SQL queries"
msgstr "Fiosrúcháin SQL amh a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"Django gives you two ways of performing raw SQL queries: you can "
"use :meth:`Manager.raw()` to `perform raw queries and return model "
"instances`__, or you can avoid the model layer entirely and `execute custom "
"SQL directly`__."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django dhá bhealach duit chun ceisteanna SQL amh a dhéanamh: is "
"féidir leat: meth: `Manager.raw () `a úsáid chun `fiosruithe amh a dhéanamh "
"agus instancí samhail a thabhairt ar ais `__, nó is féidir leat an ciseal "
"samhail a sheachaint go hiomlán agus `SQL saincheaptha a fhorghníomhú go "
"díreach `__."

msgid "Explore the ORM before using raw SQL!"
msgstr "Déan iniúchadh ar an ORM sula n-úsáideann tú SQL amh!"

msgid ""
"The Django ORM provides many tools to express queries without writing raw "
"SQL. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an Django ORM go leor uirlisí chun ceisteanna a chur in iúl gan "
"SQL amh a scríobh. Mar shampla:"

msgid "The :doc:`QuerySet API </ref/models/querysets>` is extensive."
msgstr "Tá an: doc: `QuerySet API` fairsing </ref/models/querysets>."

msgid ""
"You can :meth:`annotate <.QuerySet.annotate>` and :doc:`aggregate </topics/"
"db/aggregation>` using many built-in :doc:`database functions </ref/models/"
"database-functions>`. Beyond those, you can create :doc:`custom query "
"expressions </ref/models/expressions/>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat: meth: `annotate <.queryset.annotate>` agus:doc: `aggregate` "
"ag baint úsáide as go leor feidhmean</topics/db/aggregation> </ref/models/"
"database-functions> na bunachar sonraí ionsuite: doc: `bunachar sonraí`. "
"Taobh amuigh de na cinn, is féidir leat: doc: `abairtí ceisteanna "
"saincheapaithe' </ref/models/expressions/> a chruthú."

msgid ""
"Before using raw SQL, explore :doc:`the ORM </topics/db/index>`. Ask on one "
"of :doc:`the support channels </faq/help>` to see if the ORM supports your "
"use case."
msgstr ""
"Sula n-úsáidtear SQL amh, déan iniúchadh: doc: `an ORM` </topics/db/index>. "
"Fiafraigh ar cheann de:doc: `na cainéil tacaíochta 'chun a fheiceáil an "
"dtaca</faq/help> íonn an ORM le do chás úsáide."

msgid ""
"You should be very careful whenever you write raw SQL. Every time you use "
"it, you should properly escape any parameters that the user can control by "
"using ``params`` in order to protect against SQL injection attacks. Please "
"read more about :ref:`SQL injection protection <sql-injection-protection>`."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit a bheith an-chúramach aon uair a scríobhann tú SQL amh. Gach "
"uair a úsáideann tú é, ba cheart duit éalú i gceart aon pharaiméadair is "
"féidir leis an úsáideoir a rialú trí `params' a úsáid d'fhonn cosaint a "
"dhéanamh ar ionsaithe insteallta SQL. <sql-injection-protection>Léigh "
"tuilleadh fao:ref: `Cosaint insteallta SQL `."

msgid "Performing raw queries"
msgstr "Fiosrúcháin amh a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"The ``raw()`` manager method can be used to perform raw SQL queries that "
"return model instances:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an modh bainisteora ``raw () `a úsáid chun ceisteanna SQL amh a "
"dhéanamh a thugann cásanna samhail ar ais:"

msgid ""
"This method takes a raw SQL query, executes it, and returns a "
"``django.db.models.query.RawQuerySet`` instance. This ``RawQuerySet`` "
"instance can be iterated over like a "
"normal :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` to provide object instances."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an modh seo fiosrúchán SQL amh, cuireann sé i bhfeidhm é, agus "
"filleann sé sampla ``Django.db.Models.Query.RawQuerySet ``ar ais. Is féidir "
"an sampla ``RawQuerySet`` seo a athrú cosúil le gnáth:class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.querySet` chun cásanna réada a sholáthar."

msgid ""
"This is best illustrated with an example. Suppose you have the following "
"model::"
msgstr ""
"Is fearr é seo a léiriú le sampla. Cuir i gcás go bhfuil an tsamhail seo a "
"leanas agat::"

msgid "You could then execute custom SQL like so:"
msgstr "Ansin d'fhéadfá SQL saincheaptha a fhorghníomhú mar sin:"

msgid ""
"This example isn't very exciting -- it's exactly the same as running "
"``Person.objects.all()``. However, ``raw()`` has a bunch of other options "
"that make it very powerful."
msgstr ""
"Níl an sampla seo an-spreagúil - tá sé díreach mar an gcéanna le rith "
"``Person.Objects.all () ``. Mar sin féin, tá dornán roghanna eile ag ``raw "
"() ``a fhágann go bhfuil sé an-chumhachtach."

msgid "Model table names"
msgstr "Ainmneacha tábla múnla"

msgid "Where did the name of the ``Person`` table come from in that example?"
msgstr "Cá as a tháinig ainm an tábla ``Person` sa sampla sin?"

msgid ""
"By default, Django figures out a database table name by joining the model's "
"\"app label\" -- the name you used in ``manage.py startapp`` -- to the "
"model's class name, with an underscore between them. In the example we've "
"assumed that the ``Person`` model lives in an app named ``myapp``, so its "
"table would be ``myapp_person``."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, déanann Django ainm tábla bunachar sonraí amach trí "
"“lipéad aip” an tsamhail a cheangal - an t-ainm a d'úsáid tú i `manage.py "
"startapp`` - le hainm ranga an tsamhail, le béim eatarthu. Sa sampla ghlac "
"muid leis go gcónaíonn an tsamhail ``Person` i aip darb ainm ``myapp``, mar "
"sin bheadh a tábla ``myapp_person``."

msgid ""
"For more details check out the documentation for "
"the :attr:`~Options.db_table` option, which also lets you manually set the "
"database table name."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí féach ar an doiciméadú don rogha: attr: "
"`~Options.db_table`, a ligeann duit ainm an tábla bunachar sonraí a shocrú "
"de láimh freisin."

msgid ""
"No checking is done on the SQL statement that is passed in to ``.raw()``. "
"Django expects that the statement will return a set of rows from the "
"database, but does nothing to enforce that. If the query does not return "
"rows, a (possibly cryptic) error will result."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar aon seiceáil ar an ráiteas SQL a chuirtear isteach chuig ``.raw "
"() ``. Tá Django ag súil go dtabharfaidh an ráiteas sraith sraitheanna ar "
"ais ón mbunachar sonraí, ach ní dhéanann sé aon rud chun é sin a "
"fhorfheidhmiú. Mura bhfilleann an cheist sraitheanna ar ais, beidh earráid "
"(b'fhéidir criptic) mar thoradh air."

msgid ""
"If you are performing queries on MySQL, note that MySQL's silent type "
"coercion may cause unexpected results when mixing types. If you query on a "
"string type column, but with an integer value, MySQL will coerce the types "
"of all values in the table to an integer before performing the comparison. "
"For example, if your table contains the values ``'abc'``, ``'def'`` and you "
"query for ``WHERE mycolumn=0``, both rows will match. To prevent this, "
"perform the correct typecasting before using the value in a query."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag déanamh ceisteanna ar MySQL, tabhair faoi deara go bhféadfadh "
"foréigean cineál ciúin MySQL a bheith ina chúis le torthaí gan choinne agus "
"cineál Má fhiosraíonn tú ar cholún cineál sreangán, ach le luach sláimhir, "
"cuirfidh MySQL na cineálacha na luachanna go léir sa tábla a chur i gcomhar "
"sula ndéanann tú an comparáid. Mar shampla, má tá na luachanna ``'abc'``, "
"`def'``` i do thábla agus má fhiosraíonn tú ar ``WHERE mycolumn=0``, "
"meaitneoidh an dá shraith. Chun é seo a chosc, déan an clóscáil cheart sula "
"n-úsáidtear an luach i bhfiosrúchán."

msgid "Mapping query fields to model fields"
msgstr "Réimsí fiosrúcháin a mapáil go réimsí"

msgid ""
"``raw()`` automatically maps fields in the query to fields on the model."
msgstr ""
"Léarscáil ``raw () ``réimsí san fhiosrúchán go réimsí ar an tsamhail go "
"huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"The order of fields in your query doesn't matter. In other words, both of "
"the following queries work identically:"
msgstr ""
"Ní cuma ord na réimsí i d'fhiosrúchán. Is é sin le rá, oibríonn an dá cheist "
"seo a leanas go comhionann:"

msgid ""
"Matching is done by name. This means that you can use SQL's ``AS`` clauses "
"to map fields in the query to model fields. So if you had some other table "
"that had ``Person`` data in it, you could easily map it into ``Person`` "
"instances:"
msgstr ""
"Déantar meaitseáil de réir ainm. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat clásail "
"``AS ``SQL a úsáid chun réimsí a mhapáil sna réimsí fiosrúcháin go réimsí "
"samhlacha. Mar sin dá mbeadh tábla éigin eile agat ina raibh sonraí "
