msgstr "Déanfaidh sé seo glaoch air:"

msgid "Tablespaces"
msgstr "Spásanna tábla"

msgid ""
"A common paradigm for optimizing performance in database systems is the use "
"of `tablespaces`_ to organize disk layout."
msgstr ""
"Paraidím choitianta chun feidhmíocht a bharrfheabhsú i gcórais bunachar "
"sonraí is ea `tablespaces`_ a úsáid chun leagan amach diosca a eagrú."

msgid ""
"Django does not create the tablespaces for you. Please refer to your "
"database engine's documentation for details on creating and managing "
"tablespaces."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaíonn Django na spásanna tábla duit. Féach do thoil do dhoiciméadú "
"inneall bunachar sonraí le haghaidh sonraí maidir le spásanna tábla a "
"chruthú agus a bhainistiú."

msgid "Declaring tablespaces for tables"
msgstr "Spásanna tábla a dhearbhú le haghaidh táblaí"

msgid ""
"A tablespace can be specified for the table generated by a model by "
"supplying the :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.db_tablespace` option inside "
"the model's ``class Meta``. This option also affects tables automatically "
"created for :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`\\ s in the model."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir spás tábla a shonrú don tábla a ghineann samhail tríd an rogha "
"``aicme Meta``: attr: `~django.db.models.options.db_TableSpace` a sholáthar. "
"Bíonn tionchar ag an rogha seo freisin ar tháblaí a cruthaíodh go "
"huathoibríoch le haghaidh: class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField`\\ s sa "
"tsamhail."

msgid ""
"You can use the :setting:`DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` setting to specify a default "
"value for :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.db_tablespace`. This is useful "
"for setting a tablespace for the built-in Django apps and other applications "
"whose code you cannot control."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an socrú:setting: `DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` a úsáid chun luach "
"réamhshocraithe a shonrú le haghaidh: attr: "
"`~DJANGO.DB.Models.Options.DB_TableSpace`. Tá sé seo úsáideach chun spás "
"tábla a shocrú do na feidhmchláir ionsuite Django agus feidhmchláir eile "
"nach féidir leat a gcód a rialú."

msgid "Declaring tablespaces for indexes"
msgstr "Spásanna tábla a dhearbhú le haghaidh innéacsanna"

msgid ""
"You can pass the :attr:`~django.db.models.Index.db_tablespace` option to an "
"``Index`` constructor to specify the name of a tablespace to use for the "
"index. For single field indexes, you can pass "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_tablespace` option to a ``Field`` "
"constructor to specify an alternate tablespace for the field's column index. "
"If the column doesn't have an index, the option is ignored."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an roghna:attr: `~django.db.models.index.db_TableSpace` a "
"chur chuig tógálaí ``Index ``chun ainm spás tábla a shonrú le húsáid don "
"innéacs. Maidir le hinnéacsanna réimse aonair, is féidir leat rogha: :attr: "
"`~django.db.models.field.db_TableSpace` a chur chuig tógálaí ``Field`` chun "
"spás tábla malartach a shonrú d'innéacs colún an réimse. Mura bhfuil innéacs "
"ag an gcolún, déantar neamhaird ar an rogha."

msgid ""
"You can use the :setting:`DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` setting to specify a "
"default value for :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_tablespace`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an socrú:setting: `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` a úsáid chun "
"luach réamhshocraithe a shonrú le haghaidh: attr: "
"`~DJANGO.DB.Models.FIELD.DB_TableSpace`."

msgid ""
"If :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_tablespace` isn't specified and you "
"didn't set :setting:`DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE`, the index is created in the "
"same tablespace as the tables."
msgstr ""
"Má tá: Attr: `~django.db.models.field.DB_TableSpace` sonraithe agus níor "
"shocraigh tú: SETTING: `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE`, cruthaítear an t-innéacs "
"sa spás tábla céanna leis na táblaí."

msgid ""
"In this example, the tables generated by the ``TablespaceExample`` model "
"(i.e. the model table and the many-to-many table) would be stored in the "
"``tables`` tablespace. The index for the name field and the indexes on the "
"many-to-many table would be stored in the ``indexes`` tablespace. The "
"``data`` field would also generate an index, but no tablespace for it is "
"specified, so it would be stored in the model tablespace ``tables`` by "
"default. The index for the ``shortcut`` field would be stored in the "
"``other_indexes`` tablespace."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, déanfaí na táblaí a ghineann an tsamhail "
"``TableSpaceExample`` (ie an tábla samhail agus an tábla go leor) a stóráil "
"sa spás tábla ``tábla``. Déanfaí an t-innéacs don réimse ainm agus na "
"hinnéacsanna ar an tábla go leor a stóráil sa spás tábla ``indexes``. "
"Ghinfeadh an réimse `sonra`` innéacs freisin, ach ní shonraítear aon spás "
"tábla dó, mar sin stóráilfí é sa spás tábla samhail ``táblaí ``de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Stórálfaí an t-innéacs don réimse ``gearrcut`` sa spás "
"tábla ``other_indexes``."

msgid "Database support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL and Oracle support tablespaces. SQLite, MariaDB and MySQL don't."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn PostgreSQL agus Oracle le spásanna tábla. Ní dhéanann SQLite, "
"MariaDB agus MySQL."

msgid ""
"When you use a backend that lacks support for tablespaces, Django ignores "
"all tablespace-related options."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáideann tú cúltaca nach bhfuil tacaíocht ann do spásanna tábla, "
"déanann Django neamhaird ar gach rogha a bhaineann le spás tábla."

msgid "Database transactions"
msgstr "Idirbheart bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Django gives you a few ways to control how database transactions are managed."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django cúpla bealach duit chun a rialú conas a bhainistítear "
"idirbhearta bunachar sonraí."

msgid "Managing database transactions"
msgstr "Bainistiú idirbheart bunachar"

msgid "Django's default transaction behavior"
msgstr "Iompar idirbheart réamhshocraithe Django"

msgid ""
"Django's default behavior is to run in autocommit mode. Each query is "
"immediately committed to the database, unless a transaction is "
"active. :ref:`See below for details <autocommit-details>`."
msgstr ""
"Is é iompar réamhshocraithe Django rith i mód autocommit. Tá gach ceist "
"tiomanta láithreach don bhunachar sonraí, mura bhfuil idirbheart gníomhach. "
"<autocommit-details>:ref: `Féach thíos le haghaidh sonraí `."

msgid ""
"Django uses transactions or savepoints automatically to guarantee the "
"integrity of ORM operations that require multiple queries, "
"especially :ref:`delete() <topics-db-queries-delete>` and :ref:`update() "
"<topics-db-queries-update>` queries."
msgstr ""
"<topics-db-queries-update>Úsáideann Django idirbhearta nó pointí sábhála go "
"huathoibríoch chun sláine oibríochtaí ORM a ráthú a dteastaíonn ceisteanna "
"iolracha uathu, go háirithe:ref: `delete () <topics-db-queries-delete>`agus: "
"ref: `update ()` ceisteanna."

msgid ""
"Django's :class:`~django.test.TestCase` class also wraps each test in a "
"transaction for performance reasons."
msgstr ""
"Django's:class: `~django.test.testcase` a fhilleann rang gach tástáil in "
"idirbheart ar chúiseanna feidhmíochta freisin."

msgid "Tying transactions to HTTP requests"
msgstr "Idirbhearta a cheangal le hiarratais HTTP"

msgid ""
"A common way to handle transactions on the web is to wrap each request in a "
"transaction. Set :setting:`ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>` to "
"``True`` in the configuration of each database for which you want to enable "
"this behavior."
msgstr ""
"Bealach coitianta chun idirbhearta a láimhseáil ar an ngréasán is ea gach "
"iarratas a fhilleadh in idirbheart. Socraigh: Socrú: `ATOMIC_REQUESTS` go "
"``<DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>True`` i gcumraíocht gach bunachar sonraí ar "
"mhaith leat an t-iompar seo a chumasú dó."

msgid ""
"It works like this. Before calling a view function, Django starts a "
"transaction. If the response is produced without problems, Django commits "
"the transaction. If the view produces an exception, Django rolls back the "
"transaction."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn sé mar seo. Sula nglaonn sé ar fheidhm amharc, tosaíonn Django "
"idirbheart. Má tháirgtear an freagra gan fadhbanna, déanann Django an t-"
"idirbheart a dhéanamh. Má tháirgeann an dearcadh eisceacht, rollann Django "
"an t-idirbheart ar ais."

msgid ""
"You may perform subtransactions using savepoints in your view code, "
"typically with the :func:`atomic` context manager. However, at the end of "
"the view, either all or none of the changes will be committed."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tú fo-idirbhearta a dhéanamh ag baint úsáide as pointí sábhála i "
"do chód amharc, de ghnáth leis an mbainisteoir comhthéacs: func: `atomic`. "
"Mar sin féin, ag deireadh an dearcadh, déanfar na hathruithe go léir nó aon "
"cheann de na hathruithe a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"While the simplicity of this transaction model is appealing, it also makes "
"it inefficient when traffic increases. Opening a transaction for every view "
"has some overhead. The impact on performance depends on the query patterns "
"of your application and on how well your database handles locking."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil simplíocht an tsamhail idirbheart seo tarraingteach, fágann sé "
"go bhfuil sé neamhéifeachtach freisin nuair a mhéadaíonn trácht. Tá roinnt "
"lasbhaird ag oscailt idirbheart do gach radharc. Braitheann an tionchar ar "
"fheidhmíocht ar phatrúin cheisteanna d'iarratais agus ar cé chomh maith agus "
"a láimhseálann do bhunachar sonraí"

msgid "Per-request transactions and streaming responses"
msgstr "Idirbhearta agus freagraí sruthú de réir iarrat"

msgid ""
"When a view returns a :class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse`, reading "
"the contents of the response will often execute code to generate the "
"content. Since the view has already returned, such code runs outside of the "
"transaction."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a fhilleann amharc a:class: `~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse`, is "
"minic a fhorghníomhaítear ábhar an fhreagra cód chun an t-ábhar a ghiniúint. "
"Ós rud é go bhfuil an dearcadh ar ais cheana féin, ritheann an cód sin "
"lasmuigh den idirbheart."

msgid ""
"Generally speaking, it isn't advisable to write to the database while "
"generating a streaming response, since there's no sensible way to handle "
"errors after starting to send the response."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, ní mholtar scríobh chuig an mbunachar sonraí agus freagra "
"sruthú á ghiniúint, ós rud é nach bhfuil aon bhealach ciallmhar ann chun "
"earráidí a láimhseáil tar éis tosú ag seoladh an fhreagra."

msgid ""
"In practice, this feature wraps every view function in the :func:`atomic` "
"decorator described below."
msgstr ""
"Go praiticiúil, fillteann an ghné seo gach feidhm amharc sa maisitheoir: "
"func: `atomic` a thuairiscítear thíos."

msgid ""
"Note that only the execution of your view is enclosed in the transactions. "
"Middleware runs outside of the transaction, and so does the rendering of "
"template responses."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil ach forghníomhú do dhearcadh faoi iúl sna "
"hidirbhearta. Ritheann Middleware lasmuigh den idirbheart, agus mar sin "
"déanann rindreáil freagraí teimpléid."

msgid ""
"When :setting:`ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>` is enabled, it's "
"still possible to prevent views from running in a transaction."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn: SETTING: `ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-"
"ATOMIC_REQUESTS>`cumasaithe, is féidir fós tuairimí a chosc ó rith in "
"idirbheart."

msgid ""
"This decorator will negate the effect of :setting:`ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-"
"ATOMIC_REQUESTS>` for a given view::"
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>Déanfaidh an maisitheoir seo diúltú ar éifeacht "
"de:setting: `ATOMIC_REQUESTS `le haghaidh radharc ar leith::"

msgid "It only works if it's applied to the view itself."
msgstr "Ní oibríonn sé ach má chuirtear i bhfeidhm é ar an radharc féin."

msgid "Controlling transactions explicitly"
msgstr "Idirbheart a rialú go sainrá"

msgid "Django provides a single API to control database transactions."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django API amháin chun idirbhearta bunachar sonraí a rialú."

msgid ""
"Atomicity is the defining property of database transactions. ``atomic`` "
"allows us to create a block of code within which the atomicity on the "
"database is guaranteed. If the block of code is successfully completed, the "
"changes are committed to the database. If there is an exception, the changes "
"are rolled back."
msgstr ""
"Is é atomicity maoin sainmhínithe idirbhearta bunachar sonraí. Ligeann "
"``atomic` dúinn bloc cód a chruthú ina ndéantar an t-atomacht ar an "
"mbunachar sonraí a ráthú. Má chuirtear an bloc cód i gcrích go rathúil, tá "
"na hathruithe tiomanta don bhunachar sonraí. Má tá eisceacht ann, déantar na "
"hathruithe a rolladh ar ais."

msgid ""
"``atomic`` blocks can be nested. In this case, when an inner block completes "
"successfully, its effects can still be rolled back if an exception is raised "
"in the outer block at a later point."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir bloic ``atomic` a neadú. Sa chás seo, nuair a chríochnaíonn bloc "
"istigh go rathúil, is féidir a éifeachtaí a rolladh ar ais fós má ardaítear "
"eisceacht sa bhloc seachtrach ag pointe níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"It is sometimes useful to ensure an ``atomic`` block is always the outermost "
"``atomic`` block, ensuring that any database changes are committed when the "
"block is exited without errors. This is known as durability and can be "
"achieved by setting ``durable=True``. If the ``atomic`` block is nested "
"within another it raises a ``RuntimeError``."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta bíonn sé úsáideach a chinntiú gurb é bloc ``atomic` an bloc "
"`atomic` is seachtrach i gcónaí, ag cinntiú go ndéantar aon athruithe "
"bunachar sonraí nuair a bhíonn an bloc amach gan earráidí. Tugtar "
"marthanacht air seo agus is féidir é a bhaint amach trí “durable=True” a "
"shocrú. Má tá an bloc ``atomic` neadaithe laistigh de bhealach eile ardaíonn "
"sé ``Runtimeerror``."

msgid "``atomic`` is usable both as a :py:term:`decorator`::"
msgstr "Is féidir ``atomic`` inúsáidte araon mar a:py:term: `decorator`::"

msgid "and as a :py:term:`context manager`::"
msgstr "agus mar a: py:term: `bainisteoir comhthéacsaí`::"

msgid ""
"Wrapping ``atomic`` in a try/except block allows for natural handling of "
"integrity errors::"
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn timfhilleadh ``atomic`` i mbloc trialachta/seachas amháin go "
"ndéanfar earráidí sláine a láimhseáil nádúrtha:"

msgid ""
"In this example, even if ``generate_relationships()`` causes a database "
"error by breaking an integrity constraint, you can execute queries in "
"``add_children()``, and the changes from ``create_parent()`` are still there "
"and bound to the same transaction. Note that any operations attempted in "
"``generate_relationships()`` will already have been rolled back safely when "
"``handle_exception()`` is called, so the exception handler can also operate "
"on the database if necessary."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, fiú má tá earráid bunachar sonraí ina chúis le "
"`generate_relations () ``trí shrianadh sláine a bhriseadh, is féidir leat "
"ceisteanna a fhorghníomhú i `add_children ()``, agus tá na hathruithe ó "
"``create_parent () ``fós ann agus ceangailte leis an idirbheart céanna. "
"Tabhair faoi deara go mbeidh aon oibríochtaí a dhéanfar iarracht i "
"`generate_relations () ``rolladh ar ais go sábháilte cheana féin nuair a "
"thugtar ``handle_exception ()``, ionas gur féidir leis an láimhseálaí "
"eisceachta oibriú ar an mbunachar sonraí más gá."

msgid "Avoid catching exceptions inside ``atomic``!"
msgstr "Seachain eisceachtaí a ghabháil taobh istigh de `atomic`!"

msgid ""
"When exiting an ``atomic`` block, Django looks at whether it's exited "
"normally or with an exception to determine whether to commit or roll back. "
"If you catch and handle exceptions inside an ``atomic`` block, you may hide "
"from Django the fact that a problem has happened. This can result in "
"unexpected behavior."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag imeacht as bloc ``atomic`, féachann Django ar an bhfuil sé ag "
"imeacht de ghnáth nó le heisceacht chun a chinneadh an ndéanfaidh sé "
"tiomantas nó rolladh siar. Má ghlacann tú agus má láimhseálann tú "
"eisceachtaí taobh istigh de bhloc `atomic`, féadfaidh tú a cheilt ó Django "
"go bhfuil fadhb tharla. D'fhéadfadh iompar gan choinne a bheith mar thoradh "
"air seo."

msgid ""
"This is mostly a concern for :exc:`~django.db.DatabaseError` and its "
"subclasses such as :exc:`~django.db.IntegrityError`. After such an error, "
"the transaction is broken and Django will perform a rollback at the end of "
"the ``atomic`` block. If you attempt to run database queries before the "
"rollback happens, Django will raise "
"a :class:`~django.db.transaction.TransactionManagementError`. You may also "
"encounter this behavior when an ORM-related signal handler raises an "
"exception."
msgstr ""
"Is imní é seo den chuid is mó le haghaidh: exc: `~django.db.databaseError` "
"agus a fho-aicmí mar: exc: `~django.db.integrityError`. Tar éis earráid den "
"sórt sin, bristear an t-idirbheart agus déanfaidh Django rolladh ar ais ag "
"deireadh an bhloc `atomic`. Má dhéanann tú iarracht ceisteanna bunachar "
"sonraí a reáchtáil sula dtarlaíonn an rolladh ar ais, ardóidh Django "
"a:class: `~django.db.transaction.transactionManagementError`. D'fhéadfá "
"teacht ar an iompar seo freisin nuair a ardaíonn láimhseálaí comhartha a "
"bhaineann le ORM eisceacht."

msgid ""
"The correct way to catch database errors is around an ``atomic`` block as "
"shown above. If necessary, add an extra ``atomic`` block for this purpose. "
"This pattern has another advantage: it delimits explicitly which operations "
"will be rolled back if an exception occurs."
msgstr ""
"Tá an bealach ceart chun earráidí bunachar sonraí a ghabháil timpeall ar "
"bhloc ``atomic` mar a thaispeántar thuas. Más gá, cuir bloc breise ``atomic` "
"leis chun na críche seo. Tá buntáiste eile ag an bpatrún seo: déanann sé "
"teorannú go sainráite cé na hoibríochtaí a rollófar ar ais má tharlaíonn "
"eisceacht."

msgid ""
"If you catch exceptions raised by raw SQL queries, Django's behavior is "
"unspecified and database-dependent."
msgstr ""
"Má ghlacann tú eisceachtaí arna ardú ag ceisteanna amh SQL, tá iompar Django "
"neamhshonraithe agus ag brath ar bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"You may need to manually revert app state when rolling back a transaction."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort stát an aip a chur ar ais de láimh agus idirbheart á "
"rolladh ar ais."

msgid ""
"The values of a model's fields won't be reverted when a transaction rollback "
"happens. This could lead to an inconsistent model state unless you manually "
"restore the original field values."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirfear luachanna réimsí samhail ar ais nuair a tharlaíonn aistriú "
"idirbheart. D'fhéadfadh stát samhail neamhchomhsheasmhach a bheith mar "
"thoradh air seo mura gcuireann tú na luachanna réimse bunaidh ar ais"

msgid ""
"For example, given ``MyModel`` with an ``active`` field, this snippet "
"ensures that the ``if obj.active`` check at the end uses the correct value "
"if updating ``active`` to ``True`` fails in the transaction::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, mar gheall ar ``MyModel`` le réimse ``gníomha``, cinntíonn an "
"snippet seo go n-úsáideann an seiceáil `if obj.active`` ag an deireadh an "
"luach ceart má theipeann nuashonrú ``gníomha`` go `True`` san idirbheart:"

msgid ""
"This also applies to any other mechanism that may hold app state, such as "
"caching or global variables. For example, if the code proactively updates "
"data in the cache after saving an object, it's recommended to "
"use :ref:`transaction.on_commit() <performing-actions-after-commit>` "
"instead, to defer cache alterations until the transaction is actually "
"committed."
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé seo freisin le haon mheicníocht eile a d'fhéadfadh stát aip a "
"shealbhú, mar shampla caching nó athróga domhanda. Mar shampla, má "
"nuashonraíonn an cód sonraí sa taisce go réamhghníomhach tar éis réad a "
"shábháil, moltar úsáid:ref: `transaction.on_commit () <performing-actions-"
"after-commit>`ina ionad sin, chun athruithe taisce a chur siar go dtí go "
"ndéanfar an t-idirbheart i ndáiríre."

msgid ""
"In order to guarantee atomicity, ``atomic`` disables some APIs. Attempting "
"to commit, roll back, or change the autocommit state of the database "
"connection within an ``atomic`` block will raise an exception."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn atomacht a ráthú, déanann ``atomic` roinnt APIs a dhíchumasú. "
"Ardóidh iarracht staid uathchomhcheangail an nasc bunachar sonraí a "
"thiomantas, a rolladh siar nó a athrú laistigh de bhloc `atomic`, ardóidh "
"eisceacht."

msgid ""
"``atomic`` takes a ``using`` argument which should be the name of a "
"database. If this argument isn't provided, Django uses the ``\"default\"`` "
"database."
msgstr ""
"Glacann ``atomic` argóint ``úsáid`` ar chóir gurb é ainm bunachar sonraí. "
"Mura gcuirtear an argóint seo ar fáil, úsáideann Django an bunachar sonraí "
"``\"réamhshocraithe”."

msgid "Under the hood, Django's transaction management code:"
msgstr "Faoin gcochall, cód bainistíochta idirbheart Django:"

msgid "opens a transaction when entering the outermost ``atomic`` block;"
msgstr ""
"osclaíonn sé idirbheart agus tú ag dul isteach sa bhloc “atomach” is "
"seachtrach;"

msgid "creates a savepoint when entering an inner ``atomic`` block;"
msgstr ""
"cruthaíonn sé pointe sábhála agus tú ag dul isteach i mbloc ``atomic` istigh;"

msgid "releases or rolls back to the savepoint when exiting an inner block;"
msgstr ""
"scaoileann nó rollaíonn sé ar ais chuig an bpointe sábhála agus tú ag "
"imeacht as bloc istigh;"

msgid "commits or rolls back the transaction when exiting the outermost block."
msgstr ""
"geallann nó rollann siar an idirbheart agus é ag imeacht an bhloc is "
"seachtrach."

msgid ""
"You can disable the creation of savepoints for inner blocks by setting the "
"``savepoint`` argument to ``False``. If an exception occurs, Django will "
"perform the rollback when exiting the first parent block with a savepoint if "
"there is one, and the outermost block otherwise. Atomicity is still "
"guaranteed by the outer transaction. This option should only be used if the "
"overhead of savepoints is noticeable. It has the drawback of breaking the "
"error handling described above."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cruthú pointí sábhála do bhloic istigh a dhíchumasú tríd an "
"argóint ``savepoint`` a shocrú go ``False``. Má tharlaíonn eisceacht, "
"déanfaidh Django an rolladh siar agus é ag imeacht an chéad bhloc "
"tuismitheora le pointe sábhála má tá ceann ann, agus an bloc is seachtrach a "
"shlí eile. Tá atomacht fós ráthaithe ag an idirbheart seachtrach. Níor "
"cheart an rogha seo a úsáid ach amháin má tá laochaird na bpointí sábhála le "
"feiceáil. Tá an mhíbhuntáiste aige an láimhseáil earráide a thuairiscítear "
"thuas"

msgid ""
"You may use ``atomic`` when autocommit is turned off. It will only use "
"savepoints, even for the outermost block."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tú ``atomic` a úsáid nuair a mhúchtar autocommit. Ní úsáidfidh sé "
"ach pointí sábhála, fiú don bhloc is seachtrach."

msgid "Performance considerations"
msgstr "Creithniúcháin"

msgid ""
"Open transactions have a performance cost for your database server. To "
"minimize this overhead, keep your transactions as short as possible. This is "
"especially important if you're using :func:`atomic` in long-running "
"processes, outside of Django's request / response cycle."
msgstr ""
"Tá costas feidhmíochta ag idirbhearta oscailte do do fhreastalaí bunachar "
"Chun an lascaire seo a íoslaghdú, coinnigh d'idirbhearta chomh gearr agus is "
"féidir Tá sé seo tábhachtach go háirithe má tá tú ag úsáid: func: `atomic` i "
"bpróisis fhada, lasmuigh de thimthriall iarrata/freagartha Django."

msgid "Autocommit"
msgstr "Uathchomhaontú"

msgid "Why Django uses autocommit"
msgstr "Cén fáth a n-úsáideann Django autocommit"

msgid ""
"In the SQL standards, each SQL query starts a transaction, unless one is "
"already active. Such transactions must then be explicitly committed or "
"rolled back."
msgstr ""
"Sna caighdeáin SQL, tosaíonn gach ceist SQL idirbheart, mura bhfuil ceann "
"gníomhach cheana féin. Caithfear idirbhearta den sórt sin a dhéanamh go "
"sainráite nó a rolladh ar ais."

msgid ""
"This isn't always convenient for application developers. To alleviate this "
"problem, most databases provide an autocommit mode. When autocommit is "
"turned on and no transaction is active, each SQL query gets wrapped in its "
"own transaction. In other words, not only does each such query start a "
"transaction, but the transaction also gets automatically committed or rolled "
"back, depending on whether the query succeeded."
msgstr ""
"Níl sé seo áisiúil i gcónaí d'fhorbróirí feidhmchlár. Chun an fhadhb seo a "
"mhaolú, soláthraíonn an chuid is mó de na bunachair sonraí modh Nuair a "
"dhéantar autocommit a chasadh air agus nach bhfuil aon idirbheart gníomhach, "
"filtear gach ceist SQL ina idirbheart féin. Is é sin le rá, ní amháin go "
"dtosaíonn gach ceist den sórt sin idirbheart, ach déantar an t-idirbheart "
"tiomanta nó a rolladh ar ais go huathoibríoch freisin, ag brath ar éirigh "
"leis an bhfiosrú."

msgid ""
":pep:`249`, the Python Database API Specification v2.0, requires autocommit "
"to be initially turned off. Django overrides this default and turns "
"autocommit on."
msgstr ""
":pep: `249`, Éilíonn Sonraíocht API Bunachar Sonraí Python v2.0, go mhúchfaí "
"autocommit ar dtús. Sáraíonn Django an réamhshocrú seo agus casann sé "
"autocommit air."

msgid ""
"To avoid this, you can :ref:`deactivate the transaction management "
"<deactivate-transaction-management>`, but it isn't recommended."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a sheachaint, is féidir leat: ref: `bainistíocht an idirbheart a "
"dhíghníomhachtú <deactivate-transaction-management>`, ach ní mholtar é."

msgid "Deactivating transaction management"
msgstr "Bainistíocht idirbheart a dhígh"

msgid ""
"You can totally disable Django's transaction management for a given database "
"by setting :setting:`AUTOCOMMIT <DATABASE-AUTOCOMMIT>` to ``False`` in its "
"configuration. If you do this, Django won't enable autocommit, and won't "
"perform any commits. You'll get the regular behavior of the underlying "
"database library."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat bainistíocht idirbheart Django a dhíchumasú go hiomlán do "
"bhunachar sonraí ar leith trí shocrú: “AUTOCOMMIT” go `False <DATABASE-"
"AUTOCOMMIT>`ina chumraíocht. Má dhéanann tú é seo, ní chumasóidh Django "
"autocommit, agus ní dhéanfaidh sé aon gealltanais. Gheobhaidh tú iompar "
"rialta leabharlann bunachar sonraí bunúsach."

msgid ""
"This requires you to commit explicitly every transaction, even those started "
"by Django or by third-party libraries. Thus, this is best used in situations "
"where you want to run your own transaction-controlling middleware or do "
"something really strange."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn sé seo ort gach idirbheart a dhéanamh go sainráite, fiú iad siúd a "
"thosaigh Django nó ag leabharlanna tríú páirtí. Dá bhrí sin, is fearr é seo "
"a úsáid i gcásanna inar mian leat do mheánearraí rialaithe idirbhearta féin "
"a reáchtáil nó rud éigin an-aisteach a dhéanamh."

msgid "Performing actions after commit"
msgstr "Gníomhartha a dhéanamh tar éis tiom"

msgid ""
"Sometimes you need to perform an action related to the current database "
"transaction, but only if the transaction successfully commits. Examples "
"might include a background task, an email notification, or a cache "
"invalidation."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta ní mór duit gníomh a dhéanamh a bhaineann leis an idirbheart "
"reatha bunachar sonraí, ach amháin má dhéanann an t-idirbheart go rathúil. "
"D'fhéadfadh tasc cúlra, fógra ríomhphoist, nó neamhbhailíú taisce a bheith "
"san áireamh samplaí."

msgid ""
":func:`on_commit` allows you to register callbacks that will be executed "
"after the open transaction is successfully committed:"
msgstr ""
":func: Ligeann `on_commit` duit aisghlaonna a chlárú a fhorghníomhfar tar "
"éis don idirbheart oscailte a dhéanamh go rathúil:"

msgid "Pass a function, or any callable, to :func:`on_commit`::"
msgstr "Rith feidhm, nó aon ghlaoch, chuig:func: `on_commit`::"

msgid ""
"Callbacks will not be passed any arguments, but you can bind them "
"with :func:`functools.partial`::"
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirfear aon argóintí ar ais, ach is féidir leat iad a cheangal le:func: "
"`functools.partial`::"

msgid ""
"Callbacks are called after the open transaction is successfully committed. "
"If the transaction is instead rolled back (typically when an unhandled "
"exception is raised in an :func:`atomic` block), the callback will be "
"discarded, and never called."
msgstr ""
"Glaofar ar ais tar éis don idirbheart oscailte a dhéanamh go rathúil. Má "
"dhéantar an t-idirbheart a rolladh ar ais ina ionad sin (de ghnáth nuair a "
"ardaítear eisceacht neamh-láimhseáilte i bhloc:func: `atomic`), caithfear an "
"glaoch ar ais, agus ní ghlaofar air riamh."

msgid ""
"If you call ``on_commit()`` while there isn't an open transaction, the "
"callback will be executed immediately."
msgstr ""
"Má ghlaonn tú ar ``on_commit () ``cé nach bhfuil idirbheart oscailte ann, "
"déanfar an glaoch ar ais a fhorghníomhú láithreach."

msgid ""
"It's sometimes useful to register callbacks that can fail. Passing "
"``robust=True`` allows the next callbacks to be executed even if the current "
"one throws an exception. All errors derived from Python's ``Exception`` "
"class are caught and logged to the ``django.db.backends.base`` logger."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta bíonn sé úsáideach aisghlaonna a chlárú a d'fhéadfadh teipeadh "
"orthu. Trí ``robust=True`` is féidir leis na chéad ghlaonna eile a "
"fhorghníomhú fiú má chaitheann an ceann reatha eisceacht. Gafa agus "
"logáiltear gach earráid a dhíorthaítear ó rang ``Exception` Python agus "
"logáiltear chuig an logger ``django.db.backends.base``."

msgid ""
"You can use :meth:`.TestCase.captureOnCommitCallbacks` to test callbacks "
"registered with :func:`on_commit`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat: meth: `.testcase.captureonCommitCallbacks` a úsáid chun "
"glaonna a chláraithe le: func: `on_commit` a thástáil."

msgid "Savepoints"
msgstr "Sábháilteachta"

msgid ""
"Savepoints (i.e. nested :func:`atomic` blocks) are handled correctly. That "
"is, an :func:`on_commit` callable registered after a savepoint (in a "
"nested :func:`atomic` block) will be called after the outer transaction is "
"committed, but not if a rollback to that savepoint or any previous savepoint "
"occurred during the transaction::"
msgstr ""
"Láimhseáiltear pointí sábhála (ie neasted:func: bloic `atomic`) i gceart. Is "
"é sin, glaofar ar:func: `on_commit` inghlaonta tar éis sábhála (i mbloc "
"neastad:func: `atomic`) tar éis an t-idirbheart seachtrach a dhéanamh, ach "
"ní má tharla rolladh ar ais chuig an bpointe sábhála sin nó aon phointe "
"sábhála roimhe seo le linn an idirbheart::"

msgid ""
"On the other hand, when a savepoint is rolled back (due to an exception "
"being raised), the inner callable will not be called::"
msgstr ""
"Ar an láimh eile, nuair a dhéantar pointe sábhála a rolladh ar ais (mar "
"gheall ar eisceacht a ardaítear), ní ghlaofar ar an glaoch istigh:"

msgid "Order of execution"
msgstr "Ordú forghníomhaithe"

msgid ""
"On-commit functions for a given transaction are executed in the order they "
"were registered."
msgstr ""
"Déantar feidhmeanna ar thiomantas d'idirbheart ar leith a fhorghníomhú san "
"ord a cláraíodh iad."

msgid "Exception handling"
msgstr "Láimhseáil eisce"

msgid ""
"If one on-commit function registered with ``robust=False`` within a given "
"transaction raises an uncaught exception, no later registered functions in "
"that same transaction will run. This is the same behavior as if you'd "
"executed the functions sequentially yourself without :func:`on_commit`."
msgstr ""
"Má ardaíonn feidhm ar thiomantas amháin atá cláraithe le ``robust=false "
"``laistigh d'idirbheart ar leith eisceacht gan ghabháil, ní rithfidh aon "
"fheidhmeanna cláraithe níos déanaí san idirbheart céanna sin. Is é seo an t-"
"iompar céanna agus dá gcuirfeá na feidhmeanna a fhorghníomhú go seicheamhach "
"tú féin gan: func: `on_commit`."

msgid "Timing of execution"
msgstr "Uainiú forghníomhú"

msgid ""
"Your callbacks are executed *after* a successful commit, so a failure in a "
"callback will not cause the transaction to roll back. They are executed "
"conditionally upon the success of the transaction, but they are not *part* "
"of the transaction. For the intended use cases (mail notifications, "
"background tasks, etc.), this should be fine. If it's not (if your follow-up "
"action is so critical that its failure should mean the failure of the "
"transaction itself), then you don't want to use the :func:`on_commit` hook. "
"Instead, you may want `two-phase commit`_ such as the :ref:`psycopg Two-"
"Phase Commit protocol support <psycopg:two-phase-commit>` and "
"the :pep:`optional Two-Phase Commit Extensions in the Python DB-API "
"specification <249#optional-two-phase-commit-extensions>`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear do ghlaonna a fhorghníomhacht* tar éis tiomantas rathúil, mar sin "
"ní chuirfidh teip ar ais glaonna faoi deara go dtiocfaidh an t-idirbheart ar "
"ais. Déantar iad a fhorghníomhú go coinníollach ar rath leis an idirbheart, "
"ach níl* cuid* den idirbheart iad. Maidir leis na cásanna úsáide atá "
"beartaithe (fógraí ríomhphoist, tascanna cúlra, srl.), Ba chóir go mbeadh sé "
"seo go breá. Mura bhfuil sé (má tá do ghníomh leantach chomh ríthábhachtach "
"gur chóir go gciallódh a theip go dteipfeadh an idirbheart féin), ansin níl "
"tú ag iarraidh an crúca:func: `on_commit` a úsáid. <249 #optional -two-phase-"
"commit-extensions>Ina áit sin, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat `coimite dhá chéim' "
"_ mar thacaíocht prótacal Tiomanta Dhá Chéim psycopg <psycopg:two-phase-"
"commit>`agus an:pep: `Síntí Tiomanta Dhá Chéim roghnach sa sonraíocht Python "
"DB-API '."

msgid ""
"Callbacks are not run until autocommit is restored on the connection "
"following the commit (because otherwise any queries done in a callback would "
"open an implicit transaction, preventing the connection from going back into "
"autocommit mode)."
msgstr ""
"Ní reáchtáiltear aisghlaonna go dtí go ndéantar autocommit a athchóiriú ar "
"an nasc tar éis an tiomanta (mar shlí eile d'osclódh aon cheisteanna a "
"dhéantar i aisghlao idirbheart intuigthe, ag cosc ar an nasc dul ar ais "
"isteach i mód autocommit)."

msgid ""
"When in autocommit mode and outside of an :func:`atomic` block, the function "
"will run immediately, not on commit."
msgstr ""
"Nuair atá i mód autocommit agus lasmuigh de bhloc:func: `atomic`, rithfidh "
"an fheidhm láithreach, ní ar thiomantas."

msgid ""
"On-commit functions only work with :ref:`autocommit mode <managing-"
"autocommit>` and the :func:`atomic` (or :setting:`ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-"
"ATOMIC_REQUESTS>`) transaction API. Calling :func:`on_commit` when "
"autocommit is disabled and you are not within an atomic block will result in "
"an error."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>Ní oibríonn feidhmeanna ar chomhcheangal ach le: "
"ref: `modh autocommit `agus <managing-autocommit>la:func: `atomic` (nó: "
"setting: `ATOMIC_REQUESTS`) API idirbheart. Glaoi:func: `on_commit` nuair a "
"dhéantar autocommit míchumasaithe agus nach bhfuil tú laistigh de bhloc "
"adamhach beidh earráid mar thoradh air."

msgid "Use in tests"
msgstr "Úsáid i dtástálacha"

msgid ""
"Django's :class:`~django.test.TestCase` class wraps each test in a "
"transaction and rolls back that transaction after each test, in order to "
"provide test isolation. This means that no transaction is ever actually "
"committed, thus your :func:`on_commit` callbacks will never be run."
msgstr ""
"Django's:class: `~django.test.testcase` fillteann rang gach tástáil in "
"idirbheart agus rollaíonn sé an t-idirbheart sin ar ais tar éis gach "
"tástála, d'fhonn aonrú tástála a sholáthar. Ciallaíonn sé seo nach ndéantar "
"aon idirbheart riamh i ndáiríre, mar sin ní reáchtálfar d'aisghlaonna: func: "
"`on_commit` riamh."

msgid ""
"You can overcome this limitation by "
"using :meth:`.TestCase.captureOnCommitCallbacks`. This captures "
"your :func:`on_commit` callbacks in a list, allowing you to make assertions "
"on them, or emulate the transaction committing by calling them."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an teorannú seo a shárú trí:meth: "
"`.testcase.captureonCommitCallbacks` a úsáid. Gabhann sé seo d'aisghlaonna: "
"func: `on_commit` i liosta, rud a ligeann duit dearbhú a dhéanamh orthu, nó "
"aithris a dhéanamh ar an idirbheart a dhéantar trí ghlaoch orthu."

msgid ""
"Another way to overcome the limitation is to "
"use :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` instead "
"of :class:`~django.test.TestCase`. This will mean your transactions are "
"committed, and the callbacks will run. "
"However :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` flushes the database "
"between tests, which is significantly slower "
"than :class:`~django.test.TestCase`\\'s isolation."
msgstr ""
"Bealach eile chun an teorannú a shárú ná úsáid: class: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase` in ionad:class: `~django.test.testcase`. "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo go bhfuil d'idirbhearta tiomanta, agus rithfidh na "
"haisghlaonna. Mar sin féin: Sruthlaíonn Class: "
"`~Django.Test.TransactionTestCase` an bunachar sonraí idir tástálacha, atá i "
"bhfad níos moille ná: aicme: `~django.test.testcase` aonrú."

msgid "Why no rollback hook?"
msgstr "Cén fáth nach bhfuil crúca rollta ar ais?"

msgid ""
"A rollback hook is harder to implement robustly than a commit hook, since a "
"variety of things can cause an implicit rollback."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé níos deacra crúca rollta a chur i bhfeidhm go láidir ná crúca "
"tiomanta, ós rud é gur féidir le rudaí éagsúla a bheith ina chúis le rolladh "
"intuigthe."

msgid ""
"For instance, if your database connection is dropped because your process "
"was killed without a chance to shut down gracefully, your rollback hook will "
"never run."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má thiteann do nasc bunachar sonraí toisc go maraíodh do "
"phróiseas gan deis dúnadh go grásta, ní rithfidh do chrúca rollta riamh."

msgid ""
"But there is a solution: instead of doing something during the atomic block "
"(transaction) and then undoing it if the transaction fails, "
"use :func:`on_commit` to delay doing it in the first place until after the "
"transaction succeeds. It's a lot easier to undo something you never did in "
"the first place!"
msgstr ""
"Ach tá réiteach ann: in ionad rud éigin a dhéanamh le linn an bhloc adamhach "
"(idirbheart) agus ansin é a dhíchur má theipeann ar an idirbheart, bain "
"úsáid as: func: `on_commit` chun moill a dhéanamh ar é sa chéad áit go dtí "
"tar éis éireoidh leis an idirbheart. Tá sé i bhfad níos éasca rud a rinne tú "
"riamh a chealú sa chéad áit!"

msgid "Low-level APIs"
msgstr "APIs ar leibhéal íseal"

msgid ""
"Always prefer :func:`atomic` if possible at all. It accounts for the "
"idiosyncrasies of each database and prevents invalid operations."
msgstr ""
"Is fearr i gcónaí:func: `atomic` más féidir ar chor ar bith. Déanann sé "
"cuntas ar shainiúlachtaí gach bunachar sonraí agus cuireann sé cosc ar "
"oibríochtaí neamhbhailí."

msgid ""
"The low level APIs are only useful if you're implementing your own "
"transaction management."
msgstr ""
"Níl na APIs ar leibhéal íseal úsáideach ach má tá do bhainistíocht "
"idirbheart féin á chur i bhfeidhm agat."

msgid ""
"Django provides an API in the :mod:`django.db.transaction` module to manage "
"the autocommit state of each database connection."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django API sa mhodúl:mod: `django.db.transaction` chun staid "
"autocommit gach nasc bunachar sonraí a bhainistiú."

msgid ""
"These functions take a ``using`` argument which should be the name of a "
"database. If it isn't provided, Django uses the ``\"default\"`` database."
msgstr ""
"Glacann na feidhmeanna seo argóint ``úsáid ``ar chóir gurb é ainm bunachar "
"sonraí. Mura gcuirtear é ar fáil, úsáideann Django an bunachar sonraí "
"``\"réamhshocraithe”."

msgid ""
"Autocommit is initially turned on. If you turn it off, it's your "
"responsibility to restore it."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear Autocommit air ar dtús. Má chasann tú as é, tá sé de fhreagracht "
"ort é a chur ar ais."

msgid ""
"Once you turn autocommit off, you get the default behavior of your database "
"adapter, and Django won't help you. Although that behavior is specified "
"in :pep:`249`, implementations of adapters aren't always consistent with one "
"another. Review the documentation of the adapter you're using carefully."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chasann tú autocommit as, gheobhaidh tú iompar réamhshocraithe "
"d'oiriúnaitheoir bunachar sonraí, agus ní chabhróidh Django leat. Cé go "
"sonraítear an t-iompar sin in:pep: `249`, ní bhíonn cur i bhfeidhm "
"oiriúnaitheoirí comhsheasmhach lena chéile i gcónaí. Déan athbhreithniú "
"cúramach ar dhoiciméadú an chuibheora atá á úsáid agat"

msgid ""
"You must ensure that no transaction is active, usually by issuing "
"a :func:`commit` or a :func:`rollback`, before turning autocommit back on."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór duit a chinntiú nach bhfuil aon idirbheart gníomhach, de ghnáth trí "
"a: func: `commit` nó a:func: `rollback` a eisiúint, sula ndéanann tú "
"autocommit ar ais."

msgid ""
"Django will refuse to turn autocommit off when an :func:`atomic` block is "
"active, because that would break atomicity."
msgstr ""
"Diúltóidh Django autocommit a mhúchadh nuair a bheidh bloc: func: `atomic` "
"gníomhach, toisc go mbriseadh sé sin atomacht."

msgid ""
"A transaction is an atomic set of database queries. Even if your program "
"crashes, the database guarantees that either all the changes will be "
"applied, or none of them."
msgstr ""
"Is tacar adamhach de cheisteanna bunachar sonraí é idirbheart. Fiú má "
"tharlaíonn do chlár, ráthaíonn an bunachar sonraí go gcuirfear na hathruithe "
"go léir i bhfeidhm, nó aon cheann acu."

msgid ""
"Django doesn't provide an API to start a transaction. The expected way to "
"start a transaction is to disable autocommit with :func:`set_autocommit`."
msgstr ""
"Ní sholáthraíonn Django API chun idirbheart a thosú. Is é an bealach a "
"bhfuiltear ag súil leis chun idirbheart a thosú ná autocommit a dhíchumasú "
"le:func: `set_autocommit `."

msgid ""
"Once you're in a transaction, you can choose either to apply the changes "
"you've performed until this point with :func:`commit`, or to cancel them "
"with :func:`rollback`. These functions are defined "
"in :mod:`django.db.transaction`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh tú in idirbheart, is féidir leat na hathruithe a rinne tú a "
"chur i bhfeidhm go dtí an pointe seo le:func: `commit`, nó iad a chealú "
"le:func: `rollback`. Sainmhínítear na feidhmeanna seo in:mod: "
"`django.db.transaction`."

msgid ""
"Django will refuse to commit or to rollback when an :func:`atomic` block is "
"active, because that would break atomicity."
msgstr ""
"Diúltóidh Django tiomantas nó rolladh siar nuair a bheidh bloc: func: "
"`atomic` gníomhach, toisc go mbriseadh sé sin atomacht."

msgid ""
"A savepoint is a marker within a transaction that enables you to roll back "
"part of a transaction, rather than the full transaction. Savepoints are "
"available with the SQLite, PostgreSQL, Oracle, and MySQL (when using the "
"InnoDB storage engine) backends. Other backends provide the savepoint "
"functions, but they're empty operations -- they don't actually do anything."
msgstr ""
"Is marcóir laistigh d'idirbheart é pointe sábhála a chuireann ar do chumas "
"cuid d'idirbheart a rolladh siar, seachas an t-idirbheart iomlán. Tá "
"Savepoints ar fáil leis na cúltaca SQLite, PostgreSQL, Oracle, agus MySQL "
"(agus an t-inneall stórála InnoDB á úsáid agat). Soláthraíonn cúltaca eile "
"na feidhmeanna sábhála, ach is oibríochtaí folamh iad - ní dhéanann siad aon "
"rud i ndáiríre."

msgid ""
"Savepoints aren't especially useful if you are using autocommit, the default "
"behavior of Django. However, once you open a transaction "
"with :func:`atomic`, you build up a series of database operations awaiting a "
"commit or rollback. If you issue a rollback, the entire transaction is "
"rolled back. Savepoints provide the ability to perform a fine-grained "
"rollback, rather than the full rollback that would be performed by "
"``transaction.rollback()``."
msgstr ""
"Níl pointí sábhála úsáideach go háirithe má tá tú ag úsáid autocommit, "
"iompar réamhshocraithe Django. Mar sin féin, nuair a osclaíonn tú idirbheart "
"le:func: `atomic`, tógann tú sraith oibríochtaí bunachar sonraí ag fanacht "
"le tiomantas nó rolladh siar. Má eisíonn tú rolladh ar ais, déantar an t-"
"idirbheart iomlán a rolladh ar ais. Soláthraíonn Savepoints an cumas rolladh "
"mionghráinneach a dhéanamh, seachas an rolladh iomlán a dhéanfadh "
"``transaction.rollback () ``."

msgid ""
"When the :func:`atomic` decorator is nested, it creates a savepoint to allow "
"partial commit or rollback. You're strongly encouraged to use :func:`atomic` "
"rather than the functions described below, but they're still part of the "
"public API, and there's no plan to deprecate them."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a dhéantar an maisitheoir:func: `atomic` neadaithe, cruthaíonn sé "
"pointe sábhála chun tiomantas páirteach nó rolladh siar a cheadú. Spreagtar "
"go láidir duit: func: `atomic` a úsáid seachas na feidhmeanna a "
"thuairiscítear thíos, ach tá siad fós mar chuid den API poiblí, agus níl aon "
"phlean ann chun iad a dhíchur."

msgid ""
"Each of these functions takes a ``using`` argument which should be the name "
"of a database for which the behavior applies.  If no ``using`` argument is "
"provided then the ``\"default\"`` database is used."
msgstr ""
"Glacann gach ceann de na feidhmeanna seo argóint ``úsáid`` ar chóir gurb é "
"ainm bunachar sonraí lena mbaineann an t-iompar. Mura gcuirtear aon argóint "
"``úsáid`` ar fáil ansin úsáidtear an bunachar sonraí ``\"réamhshocraithe”."

msgid ""
"Savepoints are controlled by three functions in :mod:`django.db.transaction`:"
msgstr ""
"Tá pointí sábhála á rialú ag trí fheidhm in:mod: `django.db.transaction`:"

msgid ""
"Creates a new savepoint. This marks a point in the transaction that is known "
"to be in a \"good\" state. Returns the savepoint ID (``sid``)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé pointe sábhála nua. Marcann sé seo pointe san idirbheart ar "
"eol go bhfuil i stát “maith”. Tugann an t-aitheantas sábhála ar ais (`sid``)."

msgid ""
"Releases savepoint ``sid``. The changes performed since the savepoint was "
"created become part of the transaction."
msgstr ""
"Scaoileann sé savepoint ``sid``. Tá na hathruithe a rinneadh ó cruthaíodh an "
"pointe sábhála mar chuid den idirbheart."

msgid "Rolls back the transaction to savepoint ``sid``."
msgstr "Rollaíonn sé an t-idirbheart ar ais chun sábháil ``sid``."

msgid ""
"These functions do nothing if savepoints aren't supported or if the database "
"is in autocommit mode."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanann na feidhmeanna seo aon rud mura dtacaítear le pointí sábhála nó "
"má tá an bunachar sonraí i mód uathchomhcheangail."

msgid "In addition, there's a utility function:"
msgstr "Ina theannta sin, tá feidhm fóntais ann:"

msgid "Resets the counter used to generate unique savepoint IDs."
msgstr ""
"Athshocraíonn sé an cuntar a úsáidtear chun IDanna uathúla sábhála a "
"ghiniúint."

msgid "The following example demonstrates the use of savepoints::"
msgstr "Taispeánann an sampla seo a leanas úsáid pointí sábhála:"

msgid ""
"Savepoints may be used to recover from a database error by performing a "
"partial rollback. If you're doing this inside an :func:`atomic` block, the "
"entire block will still be rolled back, because it doesn't know you've "
"handled the situation at a lower level! To prevent this, you can control the "
"rollback behavior with the following functions."
msgstr ""
"Féadfar pointí sábhála a úsáid chun aisghabháil ó earráid bunachar sonraí "
"trí aistriú páirteach a dhéanamh. Má tá tú ag déanamh seo taobh istigh de "
"bhloc:func: `atomic`, déanfar an bloc iomlán a rolladh ar ais fós, toisc "
"nach bhfuil a fhios aige gur láimhseáil tú an cás ag leibhéal níos ísle! "
"Chun é seo a chosc, is féidir leat an t-iompar rollta a rialú leis na "
"feidhmeanna seo a leanas."

msgid ""
"Setting the rollback flag to ``True`` forces a rollback when exiting the "
"innermost atomic block. This may be useful to trigger a rollback without "
"raising an exception."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an bhratach rollta ar ais go ``True``, cuirtear isteach ar ais agus "
"tú ag imeacht an bhloc adamhach is taobh istigh. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith "
"úsáideach chun rolladh a spreagadh gan eisceacht a ardú."

msgid ""
"Setting it to ``False`` prevents such a rollback. Before doing that, make "
"sure you've rolled back the transaction to a known-good savepoint within the "
"current atomic block! Otherwise you're breaking atomicity and data "
"corruption may occur."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann é a shocrú go ``False`` cosc ar rolladh den sórt sin. Sula ndéanann "
"tú é sin, déan cinnte go bhfuil an t-idirbheart a rolladh ar ais go pointe "
"sábhála maith ar eolas laistigh den bhloc adamhach reatha! Seachas sin tá tú "
"ag briseadh atomacht agus d'fhéadfadh éilliú sonraí tarlú."

msgid "Database-specific notes"
msgstr "Nótaí sonracha bunachar sonraí"

msgid "Savepoints in SQLite"
msgstr "Sábháilteachta i SQLite"

msgid ""
"While SQLite supports savepoints, a flaw in the design of the :mod:`sqlite3` "
"module makes them hardly usable."
msgstr ""
"Cé go dtacaíonn SQLite le pointí sábhála, ní fhágann locht i ndearadh an "
"mhodúil: mod: `sqlite3` is ar éigean iad inúsáidte."

msgid ""
"When autocommit is enabled, savepoints don't make sense. When it's "
"disabled, :mod:`sqlite3` commits implicitly before savepoint statements. (In "
"fact, it commits before any statement other than ``SELECT``, ``INSERT``, "
"``UPDATE``, ``DELETE`` and ``REPLACE``.) This bug has two consequences:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a dhéantar autocommit cumasaithe, ní bhíonn ciall ag pointí sábhála. "
"Nuair a bhíonn sé díchumasaithe, tiomhann :mod: `sqlite3` go hinneach roimh "
"ráitis savepoint. (Go deimhin, déanann sé tiomantas roimh aon ráiteas "
"seachas ``SELECT``, `INSERT``, `UPDATE``, `DELETE`` agus ``REPLACE``.) Tá "
"dhá iarmhairtí ag an fabht seo:"

msgid ""
"The low level APIs for savepoints are only usable inside a transaction i.e. "
"inside an :func:`atomic` block."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir na APIs leibhéal íseal le haghaidh pointí sábhála inúsáidte ach "
"taobh istigh d'idirbheart i.e. taobh istigh de bhloc:func: `atomic`."

msgid "It's impossible to use :func:`atomic` when autocommit is turned off."
msgstr "Tá sé dodhéanta: func: `atomic` a úsáid nuair a mhúchtar autocommit."

msgid "Transactions in MySQL"
msgstr "Idirbhearta i MySQL"

msgid ""
"If you're using MySQL, your tables may or may not support transactions; it "
"depends on your MySQL version and the table types you're using. (By \"table "
"types,\" we mean something like \"InnoDB\" or \"MyISAM\".) MySQL transaction "
"peculiarities are outside the scope of this article, but the MySQL site has "
"`information on MySQL transactions`_."
msgstr ""
"Má tá MySQL á úsáid agat, d'fhéadfadh nó nach dtacaíonn do tháblaí le "
"hidirbhearta; braitheann sé ar do leagan MySQL agus ar na cineálacha tábla "
"atá á úsáid agat. (Le “cineálacha tábla,” ciallaímid rud éigin cosúil le "
"“InnoDB” nó “MyISAM”.) Tá tréithe idirbheart MySQL lasmuigh de raon feidhme "
"an ailt seo, ach tá `faisnéis faoi idirbhearta MySQL `_ ag an suíomh MySQL."

msgid ""
"If your MySQL setup does *not* support transactions, then Django will always "
"function in autocommit mode: statements will be executed and committed as "
"soon as they're called. If your MySQL setup *does* support transactions, "
"Django will handle transactions as explained in this document."
msgstr ""
"Mura dtacaíonn do shocrú MySQL* le hidirbhearta, ansin feidhmeoidh Django i "
"gcónaí i mód autocommit: déanfar ráitis a fhorghníomhú agus a thiomnamh a "
"luaithe a ghlaofar orthu. Má thacaíonn do shocrú MySQL* le hidirbhearta, "
"láimhseálfaidh Django idirbhearta mar a mhínítear sa doiciméad seo."

msgid "Handling exceptions within PostgreSQL transactions"
msgstr "Láimhseáil eisceachtaí laistigh d'idirbhearta PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"This section is relevant only if you're implementing your own transaction "
"management. This problem cannot occur in Django's default mode "
"and :func:`atomic` handles it automatically."
msgstr ""
"Níl an chuid seo ábhartha ach amháin má tá do bhainistíocht idirbheart féin "
"á chur i bhfeidhm agat. Ní féidir leis an bhfadhb seo tarlú i mód "
"réamhshocraithe Django agus láimhseálann: func: `atomic` é go huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"Inside a transaction, when a call to a PostgreSQL cursor raises an exception "
"(typically ``IntegrityError``), all subsequent SQL in the same transaction "
"will fail with the error \"current transaction is aborted, queries ignored "
"until end of transaction block\". While the basic use of ``save()`` is "
"unlikely to raise an exception in PostgreSQL, there are more advanced usage "
"patterns which might, such as saving objects with unique fields, saving "
"using the ``force_insert``/``force_update`` flag, or invoking custom SQL."
msgstr ""
"Taobh istigh d'idirbheart, nuair a ardaíonn glao chuig cúrsóir PostgreSQL "
"eisceacht (de ghnáth ``IntegrityError``), teipeann ar gach SQL ina dhiaidh "
"sin san idirbheart céanna leis an earráid “cuirtear an t-idirbheart reatha, "
"neamhaird ar cheisteanna go dtí deireadh an bhloc idirbheart”. Cé nach dócha "
"go n-ardóidh úsáid bhunúsach ``save () ``eisceacht i PostgreSQL, tá patrúin "
"úsáide níos airde ann a d'fhéadfadh, mar shampla rudaí a shábháil le réimsí "
"uathúla, sábháil ag baint úsáide as an bhratach ```force_insert``/"
"``force_updat``, nó SQL saincheaptha a ghairm."

msgid "There are several ways to recover from this sort of error."
msgstr "Tá bealaí éagsúla ann chun aisghabháil ón gcineál seo earráide."

msgid "Transaction rollback"
msgstr "Aisghabháil idirbheart"

msgid "The first option is to roll back the entire transaction. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad rogha an t-idirbheart iomlán a rolladh ar ais. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Calling ``transaction.rollback()`` rolls back the entire transaction. Any "
"uncommitted database operations will be lost. In this example, the changes "
"made by ``a.save()`` would be lost, even though that operation raised no "
"error itself."
msgstr ""
"Ag glaoch ar ``transaction.rollback () ``rollann an t-idirbheart iomlán ar "
"ais. Caillfear aon oibríochtaí bunachar sonraí neamhthiomanta. Sa sampla "
"seo, caillfeadh na hathruithe a rinne `a.save () ``, cé nach n-ardaigh an "
"oibríocht sin aon earráid féin."

msgid "Savepoint rollback"
msgstr "Aisghabháil Savepoint"

msgid ""
"You can use :ref:`savepoints <topics-db-transactions-savepoints>` to control "
"the extent of a rollback. Before performing a database operation that could "
"fail, you can set or update the savepoint; that way, if the operation fails, "
"you can roll back the single offending operation, rather than the entire "
"transaction. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat:ref: `savepoints <topics-db-transactions-savepoints>`a úsáid "
"chun méid rollta a rialú. Sula ndéanann tú oibríocht bunachar sonraí a "
"d'fhéadfadh teipeadh air, is féidir leat an pointe sábhála a shocrú nó a "
"nuashonrú; ar an mbealach sin, má theipeann ar an oibríocht, is féidir leat "
"an oibríocht ciontaithe aonair a rolladh ar ais, seachas an t-idirbheart "
"iomlán. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"In this example, ``a.save()`` will not be undone in the case where "
"``b.save()`` raises an exception."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, ní dhéantar ``a.save () ``ar ais sa chás ina ndéanann "
"``b.save ()`` eisceacht."

msgid "Sending email"
msgstr "Seoladh ríomhphoist"

msgid ""
"Although Python provides a mail sending interface via the :mod:`smtplib` "
"module, Django provides a couple of light wrappers over it. These wrappers "
"are provided to make sending email extra quick, to help test email sending "
"during development, and to provide support for platforms that can't use SMTP."
msgstr ""
"Cé go soláthraíonn Python comhéadan seolta ríomhphoist tríd an modúl: mod: "
"`smtplib`, soláthraíonn Django cúpla fillteán éadrom air. Cuirtear na "
"fillteáin seo ar fáil chun ríomhphost a sheoladh go tapa, chun cabhrú le "
"seoladh ríomhphoist a thástáil le linn na forbartha, agus chun tacaíocht a "
"sholáthar d'ardáin nach féidir leo SMTP a úsáid."

msgid "The code lives in the ``django.core.mail`` module."
msgstr "Tá an cód ina gcónaí sa mhodúl ``django.core.mail``."

msgid "Quick examples"
msgstr "Samplaí gasta"

msgid ""
"Use :func:`send_mail` for straightforward email sending. For example, to "
"send a plain text message::"
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: func: `send_mail` le haghaidh seoladh ríomhphoist simplí. Mar "
"shampla, chun teachtaireacht téacs simplí a sheoladh:"

msgid ""
"When additional email sending functionality is needed, "
"use :class:`EmailMessage` or :class:`EmailMultiAlternatives`. For example, "
"to send a multipart email that includes both HTML and plain text versions "
"with a specific template and custom headers, you can use the following "
"approach::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn feidhmiúlacht bhreise seolta ríomhphoist ag teastáil, bain "
"úsáid as: class: `EmailMessage` nó:class: `EmailMultiAlternatives`. Mar "
"shampla, chun ríomhphost ilpháirteach a sheoladh a chuimsíonn leaganacha "
"HTML agus téacs simplí le teimpléad ar leith agus ceanntásca saincheaptha, "
"is féidir leat an cur chuige seo a leanas a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"Mail is sent using the SMTP host and port specified in "
"the :setting:`EMAIL_HOST` and :setting:`EMAIL_PORT` settings. "
"The :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_USER` and :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD` settings, "
"if set, are used to authenticate to the SMTP server, and "
"the :setting:`EMAIL_USE_TLS` and :setting:`EMAIL_USE_SSL` settings control "
"whether a secure connection is used."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar ríomhphost ag baint úsáide as an óstach SMTP agus an calafort a "
"shonraítear sna socruithe:: `EMAIL_HOST` agus:setting: `EMAIL_PORT`. "
"Úsáidtear socruithe an:SETTING: `EMAIL_HOST_USER` agus:setting: "
"`EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD`, má tá sé socraithe, chun fíordheimhniú chuig an "
"bhfreastalaí SMTP, agus rialaíonn an:setting: `EMAIL_USE_TLS` agus:setting: "
"`EMAIL_USE_SSL` an bhfuil nasc slán."

msgid ""
"The character set of email sent with ``django.core.mail`` will be set to the "
"value of your :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` setting."
msgstr ""
"Socrófar an tacar carachtair ríomhphoist a sheoltar le ``django.core.mail`` "
"ar luach do shuíomh: `DEFAULT_CHARSET`."

msgid "``send_mail()``"
msgstr "``seol_mail () ``"

msgid ""
"In most cases, you can send email using ``django.core.mail.send_mail()``."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna, is féidir leat ríomhphost a sheoladh ag baint "
"úsáide as ``django.core.mail.send_mail () ``."

msgid ""
"The ``subject``, ``message``, ``from_email`` and ``recipient_list`` "
"parameters are required."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn na paraiméadair ``ábhar ``, `teachtaire``, `from_email`` agus "
"``liosta_faighteannaithe``."

msgid "``subject``: A string."
msgstr "``ábhar ``: Sreang."

msgid "``message``: A string."
msgstr "``teachtaireacht ``: Sreang."

msgid ""
"``from_email``: A string. If ``None``, Django will use the value of "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` setting."
msgstr ""
"``from_email``: teaghrán. Má tá ``None``, úsáidfidh Django luach an "
"socruithe:: `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL`."

msgid ""
"``recipient_list``: A list of strings, each an email address. Each member of "
"``recipient_list`` will see the other recipients in the \"To:\" field of the "
"email message."
msgstr ""
"``recipient_list``: Liosta teaghráin, seoladh ríomhphoist gach ceann acu. "
"Feicfidh gach ball de ``recipient_list`` na faighteoirí eile sa réimse "
"“Chun:” den teachtaireacht ríomhphoist."

msgid ""
"``fail_silently``: A boolean. When it's ``False``, ``send_mail()`` will "
"raise an :exc:`smtplib.SMTPException` if an error occurs. See "
"the :mod:`smtplib` docs for a list of possible exceptions, all of which are "
"subclasses of :exc:`~smtplib.SMTPException`."
msgstr ""
"``fail_silently``: Boolean. Nuair a bhíonn sé `False``, ardóidh ``send_mail "
"() ``an:exc: `smtplib.smtpException` má tharlaíonn earráid. Féach na docs: "
"mod: `smtplib` le haghaidh liosta de na heisceachtaí féideartha, agus is fo-"
"aicmí iad uile ceann de: exc: `~smtplib.smtpException`."

msgid ""
"``auth_user``: The optional username to use to authenticate to the SMTP "
"server. If this isn't provided, Django will use the value of "
"the :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_USER` setting."
msgstr ""
"``auth_user``: An t-ainm úsáideora roghnach le húsáid chun fíordheimhniú "
"chuig an bhfreastalaí SMTP. Mura gcuirtear é seo ar fáil, úsáidfidh Django "
"luach an socruithe: setting: `EMAIL_HOST_USER`."

msgid ""
"``auth_password``: The optional password to use to authenticate to the SMTP "
"server. If this isn't provided, Django will use the value of "
"the :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD` setting."
msgstr ""
"``auth_password``: An pasfhocal roghnach le húsáid chun fíordheimhniú chuig "
"an bhfreastalaí SMTP. Mura gcuirtear é seo ar fáil, úsáidfidh Django luach "
"an socruithe:: `EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD`."

msgid ""
"``connection``: The optional email backend to use to send the mail. If "
"unspecified, an instance of the default backend will be used. See the "
"documentation on :ref:`Email backends <topic-email-backends>` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"``nasc``: An cúltaca roghnach ríomhphoist le húsáid chun an post a sheoladh. "
"Mura bhfuil sé sonraithe, úsáidfear sampla den chúltaca réamhshocraithe. "
"Féach an doiciméadú ar:ref: `Ríomhphost backends <topic-email-backends>`le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"``html_message``: If ``html_message`` is provided, the resulting email will "
"be a :mimetype:`multipart/alternative` email with ``message`` as "
"the :mimetype:`text/plain` content type and ``html_message`` as "
"the :mimetype:`text/html` content type."
msgstr ""
"``html_message``: Má chuirtear `html_message`` ar fáil, beidh an ríomhphost "
"mar thoradh air:: mimetype: `multipart/alternative `r-phost le "
"``teachtaire`` mar an cineál ábhair: mimetype: `text/plain` agus "
"``html_message`` mar an:mimetype: `text/html` cineál ábhair."

msgid ""
"The return value will be the number of successfully delivered messages "
"(which can be ``0`` or ``1`` since it can only send one message)."
msgstr ""
"Is é an luach tuairisceáin líon na dteachtaireachtaí a sheachadadh go "
"rathúil (ar féidir iad a bheith ``0`` nó ``1`` ós rud é nach féidir leis ach "
"teachtaireacht amháin a sheoladh)."

msgid "``send_mass_mail()``"
msgstr "``seol_mass_mail () ``"

msgid ""
"``django.core.mail.send_mass_mail()`` is intended to handle mass emailing."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé beartaithe ag ``django.core.mail.send_mass_mail () ``ollseoladh "
"ríomhphoist a láimhseáil."

msgid "``datatuple`` is a tuple in which each element is in this format::"
msgstr "Is é `datatuple`` tuple ina bhfuil gach eilimint sa fhormáid seo:"

msgid ""
"``fail_silently``, ``auth_user`` and ``auth_password`` have the same "
"functions as in :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each separate element of ``datatuple`` results in a separate email message. "
"As in :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail`, recipients in the same "
"``recipient_list`` will all see the other addresses in the email messages' "
"\"To:\" field."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For example, the following code would send two different messages to two "
"different sets of recipients; however, only one connection to the mail "
"server would be opened::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chuirfeadh an cód seo a leanas dhá theachtaireacht éagsúla "
"chuig dhá shraith éagsúla faighteoirí; áfach, ní osclófaí ach nasc amháin "
"leis an bhfreastalaí ríomhphoist:"

msgid "The return value will be the number of successfully delivered messages."
msgstr ""
"Is é an luach tuairisceáin líon na dteachtaireachtaí a sheachadadh go "
"rathúil."

msgid "``send_mass_mail()`` vs. ``send_mail()``"
msgstr "``send_mass_mail () ``vs ``send_mail ()``"

msgid ""
"The main difference between :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mass_mail` "
"and :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` is "
"that :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` opens a connection to the mail "
"server each time it's executed, "
"while :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mass_mail` uses a single connection for "
"all of its messages. This makes :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mass_mail` "
"slightly more efficient."
msgstr ""

msgid "``mail_admins()``"
msgstr "``mail_admins () ``"

msgid ""
"``django.core.mail.mail_admins()`` is a shortcut for sending an email to the "
"site admins, as defined in the :setting:`ADMINS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Is aicearra é ``django.core.mail.mail_admins () ``chun ríomhphost a sheoladh "
"chuig riarthóirí an láithreáin, mar a shainmhínítear sa socrú: `ADMINS`."

msgid ""
"``mail_admins()`` prefixes the subject with the value of "
"the :setting:`EMAIL_SUBJECT_PREFIX` setting, which is ``\"[Django] \"`` by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraíonn ``mail_admins () ``an t-ábhar le luach an socrú: "
"`EMAIL_SUBJECT_PREFIX`, arb é`` \"[Django] “``de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"The \"From:\" header of the email will be the value of "
"the :setting:`SERVER_EMAIL` setting."
msgstr ""
"Is é ceannteideal “Ó:” an ríomhphoist luach an socruithe: setting: "
"`SERVER_EMAIL`."

msgid "This method exists for convenience and readability."
msgstr "Tá an modh seo ann le haghaidh áisiúlachta agus inléiteachta."

msgid ""
"If ``html_message`` is provided, the resulting email will be "
"a :mimetype:`multipart/alternative` email with ``message`` as "
"the :mimetype:`text/plain` content type and ``html_message`` as "
"the :mimetype:`text/html` content type."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear `html_message`` ar fáil, beidh an ríomhphost mar thoradh air:: "
"mimetype: `multipart/alternative `r-phost le `teachtaire`` mar an:mimetype: "
"`text/plain` cineál ábhair agus `html_message`` mar an cineál ábhair: "
"mimetype: `text/html`."

msgid "``mail_managers()``"
msgstr "``bainisteoirí poist () ``"

msgid ""
"``django.core.mail.mail_managers()`` is just like ``mail_admins()``, except "
"it sends an email to the site managers, as defined in "
"the :setting:`MANAGERS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.core.mail.mail_managers () ``díreach cosúil le ``mail_admins "
"()``, ach amháin go seolann sé ríomhphost chuig bainisteoirí an láithreáin, "
"mar a shainmhínítear sa socrú: `MANAGERS`."

msgid "Examples"
msgstr "Samplaí"

msgid ""
"This sends a single email to john@example.com and jane@example.com, with "
"them both appearing in the \"To:\"::"
msgstr ""
"Seolann sé ríomhphost amháin chuig john@example.com agus jane@example.com, "
"agus tá an bheirt acu le feiceáil sa “Chun:”:"

msgid ""
"This sends a message to john@example.com and jane@example.com, with them "
"both receiving a separate email::"
msgstr ""
"Seolann sé seo teachtaireacht chuig john@example.com agus jane@example.com, "
"agus faigheann an bheirt acu ríomhphost ar leithligh:"

msgid "Preventing header injection"
msgstr "Instealladh ceannteidil"

msgid ""
"`Header injection`_ is a security exploit in which an attacker inserts extra "
"email headers to control the \"To:\" and \"From:\" in email messages that "
"your scripts generate."
msgstr ""
"Is saothrú slándála é `instealladh ceannteannair`_ ina gcuireann "
"ionsaitheoir ceannteidil ríomhphoist breise isteach chun an “Chun:” agus "
"“Ó:” a rialú i dteachtaireachtaí ríomhphoist a ghineann do scripteanna."

msgid ""
"The Django email functions outlined above all protect against header "
"injection by forbidding newlines in header values. If any ``subject``, "
"``from_email`` or ``recipient_list`` contains a newline (in either Unix, "
"Windows or Mac style), the email function "
"(e.g. :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail`) will raise "
"``django.core.mail.BadHeaderError`` (a subclass of ``ValueError``) and, "
"hence, will not send the email. It's your responsibility to validate all "
"data before passing it to the email functions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a ``message`` contains headers at the start of the string, the headers "
"will be printed as the first bit of the email message."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ceanntásca i “teachtaireacht” ag tús an teaghrán, clófar na ceanntásca "
"mar an chéad ghiotán den teachtaireacht ríomhphoist."

msgid ""
"Here's an example view that takes a ``subject``, ``message`` and "
"``from_email`` from the request's POST data, sends that to admin@example.com "
"and redirects to \"/contact/thanks/\" when it's done::"
msgstr ""
"Seo dearcadh samplach a thógann ``ábhar ``, `teachtaireacht`` agus "
"``from_email`` ó shonraí POST an iarratais, seolann sé sin chuig "
"admin@example.com agus a atreoraíonn sé chuig “/contact/thanks/” nuair a "
"bheidh sé déanta:"

msgid "The ``EmailMessage`` class"
msgstr "An rang ``EmailMessage``"

msgid ""
"Django's :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` "
"and :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mass_mail` functions are actually thin "
"wrappers that make use of the :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` class."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Not all features of the :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` class are "
"available through the :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` and related "
"wrapper functions. If you wish to use advanced features, such as BCC'ed "
"recipients, file attachments, or multi-part email, you'll need to "
"create :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` instances directly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is a design feature. :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` and related "
"functions were originally the only interface Django provided. However, the "
"list of parameters they accepted was slowly growing over time. It made sense "
"to move to a more object-oriented design for email messages and retain the "
"original functions only for backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` is responsible for creating the "
"email message itself. The :ref:`email backend <topic-email-backends>` is "
"then responsible for sending the email."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.mail.emailMessage` atá freagrach as an teachtaireacht "
"ríomhphoist féin a chruthú. Ansin tá an:ref: `backend ríomhphoist <topic-"
"email-backends>`freagrach as an ríomhphost a sheoladh."

msgid ""
"For convenience, :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` provides a "
"``send()`` method for sending a single email. If you need to send multiple "
"messages, the email backend API :ref:`provides an alternative <topics-"
"sending-multiple-emails>`."
msgstr ""
"Ar mhaithe le áisiúlacht, soláthraíonn :class: "
"`~django.core.mail.emailMessage` modh ``send () ``chun ríomhphost amháin a "
"sheoladh. <topics-sending-multiple-emails>Más gá duit teachtaireachtaí "
"iolracha a sheoladh, soláthraíonn an cúltaca ríomhphoist API: ref: `rogha "
"eile `."

msgid "``EmailMessage`` Objects"
msgstr "``Ríomhphost teachtaire`` Cuspóirí"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` class is initialized with the "
"following parameters (in the given order, if positional arguments are used). "
"All parameters are optional and can be set at any time prior to calling the "
"``send()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an rang:class: `~django.core.mail.emailMessage` a thionscnamh leis "
"na paraiméadair seo a leanas (san ord tugtha, má úsáidtear argóintí "
"seasaimh). Tá na paraiméadair go léir roghnach agus is féidir iad a shocrú "
"ag am ar bith sula nglactar ar an modh ``send () `."

msgid "``subject``: The subject line of the email."
msgstr "``ábhar ``: Líne ábhair an ríomhphoist."

msgid "``body``: The body text. This should be a plain text message."
msgstr ""
"``corp ``: An téacs comhlachta. Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo ná teachtaireacht "
"téacs simplí."

msgid ""
"``from_email``: The sender's address. Both ``fred@example.com`` and "
"``\"Fred\" <fred@example.com>`` forms are legal. If omitted, "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` setting is used."
msgstr ""
"``from_email``: Seoladh an tseoltóra. < fred@example.com >Tá an dá fhoirm "
"``fred@example.com`` agus ``\"Fred ``dlíthiúil. Má fhágtar amach, úsáidtear "
"an socrú:setting: `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL`."

msgid "``to``: A list or tuple of recipient addresses."
msgstr "````: Liosta nó feadán de sheoltaí faighteora."

msgid ""
"``bcc``: A list or tuple of addresses used in the \"Bcc\" header when "
"sending the email."
msgstr ""
"``bcc``: Liosta nó tuple seoltaí a úsáidtear sa cheanntásc “Bcc” agus an "
"ríomhphost á sheoladh."

msgid ""
"``connection``: An :ref:`email backend <topic-email-backends>` instance. Use "
"this parameter if you are sending the ``EmailMessage`` via ``send()`` and "
"you want to use the same connection for multiple messages. If omitted, a new "
"connection is created when ``send()`` is called. This parameter is ignored "
"when using :ref:`send_messages() <topics-sending-multiple-emails>`."
msgstr ""
"<topic-email-backends>``nasc``: an:ref: `cúltaca ríomhphost` sampla. Úsáid "
"an paraiméadar seo má tá an ``emailMessage`` á sheoladh agat trí ``send () "
"``agus gur mhaith leat an nasc céanna a úsáid le haghaidh teachtaireachtaí "
"iolracha. Má fhágtar amach, cruthaítear nasc nua nuair a thugtar ``send () "
"``. <topics-sending-multiple-emails>Déantar neamhaird ar an bparaiméadar seo "
"nuair a úsáidtear: ref: `send_messages () `."

msgid ""
"``attachments``: A list of attachments to put on the message. These can be "
"instances of :class:`~email.mime.base.MIMEBase` "
"or :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailAttachment`, or a tuple with attributes "
"``(filename, content, mimetype)``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Support for :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailAttachment` items of "
"``attachments`` was added."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``headers``: A dictionary of extra headers to put on the message. The keys "
"are the header name, values are the header values. It's up to the caller to "
"ensure header names and values are in the correct format for an email "
"message. The corresponding attribute is ``extra_headers``."
msgstr ""
"``headers``: Foclóir ceanntásca breise le cur ar an teachtaireacht. Is iad "
"na heochracha ainm an ceanntásc, is iad luachanna na luachanna ceanntásc. Is "
"faoin nglaoiteoir atá sé a chinntiú go bhfuil ainmneacha agus luachanna "
"ceanntásc san fhormáid cheart do theachtaireacht ríomhphoist. Is é an tréith "
"chomhfhreagrach ná ``extra_headers``."

msgid ""
"``cc``: A list or tuple of recipient addresses used in the \"Cc\" header "
"when sending the email."
msgstr ""
"``cc``: Liosta nó cúpla de sheoltaí faighteora a úsáidtear sa cheanntásc "
"“Cc” agus an ríomhphost á sheoladh."

msgid ""
"``reply_to``: A list or tuple of recipient addresses used in the \"Reply-"
"To\" header when sending the email."
msgstr ""
"``reply_to``: Liosta nó cúpla de sheoltaí faighteora a úsáidtear sa "
"cheanntásc “Reply-To” agus an ríomhphost á sheoladh."

msgid "The class has the following methods:"
msgstr "Tá na modhanna seo a leanas ag an rang:"

msgid ""
"``send(fail_silently=False)`` sends the message. If a connection was "
"specified when the email was constructed, that connection will be used. "
"Otherwise, an instance of the default backend will be instantiated and used. "
"If the keyword argument ``fail_silently`` is ``True``, exceptions raised "
"while sending the message will be quashed. An empty list of recipients will "
"not raise an exception. It will return ``1`` if the message was sent "
"successfully, otherwise ``0``."
msgstr ""
"Seolann ``send (fail_silently=False) ``an teachtaireacht. Má shonraíodh nasc "
"nuair a tógadh an ríomhphost, úsáidfear an nasc sin. Seachas sin, déanfar "
"sampla den chúltaca réamhshocraithe a thabhairt isteach agus a úsáid. Más é "
"``True`` an argóint eochairfhocal ``fail_silently``, cuirfear deireadh leis "
"na heisceachtaí a ardaítear agus an teachtaireacht á sheoladh. Ní ardóidh "
"liosta folamh de na bhfaighteoirí eisceacht. Tabharfaidh sé ar ais ``1`` má "
"sheoladh an teachtaireacht go rathúil, ar shlí eile ``0``."

msgid ""
"``message()`` constructs a ``django.core.mail.SafeMIMEText`` object (a "
"subclass of Python's :class:`~email.mime.text.MIMEText` class) or a "
"``django.core.mail.SafeMIMEMultipart`` object holding the message to be "
"sent. If you ever need to extend the :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` "
"class, you'll probably want to override this method to put the content you "
"want into the MIME object."
msgstr ""
"Tógann ``message () ``réad ``Django.Core.Mail.SafeMeText`` (fo-aicme de "
"Python's:Class: `~email.mime.text.mimeText` aicme) nó réad "
"``Django.Core.Mail.SafeMeMultiPart`` ina bhfuil an teachtaireacht le "
"seoladh. Más gá duit riamh an rang:class: `~django.core.mail.emailMessage` a "
"leathnú, is dócha go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh an modh seo a shárú chun an t-"
"ábhar a theastaíonn uait a chur isteach sa réad MIME."

msgid ""
"``recipients()`` returns a list of all the recipients of the message, "
"whether they're recorded in the ``to``, ``cc`` or ``bcc`` attributes. This "
"is another method you might need to override when subclassing, because the "
"SMTP server needs to be told the full list of recipients when the message is "
"sent. If you add another way to specify recipients in your class, they need "
"to be returned from this method as well."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``faighteoirí () ``liosta de fhaighteoirí uile na teachtaireachta, "
"cibé acu a thaifeadtar sna tréithe ````, `cc`` nó `bcc``. Is modh eile é seo "
"b'fhéidir go gcaithfidh tú a shárú agus tú ag fo-aicmiú, toisc go gcaithfear "
"liosta iomlán na bhfaighteoirí a insint don fhreastalaí SMTP nuair a "
"sheoltar an teachtaireacht. Má chuireann tú bealach eile chun faighteoirí a "
"shonrú i do rang, ní mór iad a thabhairt ar ais ón modh seo freisin."

msgid ""
"``attach()`` creates a new file attachment and adds it to the message. There "
"are two ways to call ``attach()``:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn ``attachment () ``ceangaltán nua comhad agus cuireann sé leis an "
"teachtaireacht é. Tá dhá bhealach ann chun glaoch ar ``attachment ()``:"

msgid ""
"You can pass it a single argument that is "
"a :class:`~email.mime.base.MIMEBase` instance. This will be inserted "
"directly into the resulting message."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat argóint amháin a chur air argóint arb é a: class: "
"`~email.mime.base.mimeBase` sampla. Cuirfear é seo isteach go díreach sa "
"teachtaireacht mar thoradh air."

msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can pass ``attach()`` three arguments: ``filename``, "
"``content`` and ``mimetype``. ``filename`` is the name of the file "
"attachment as it will appear in the email, ``content`` is the data that will "
"be contained inside the attachment and ``mimetype`` is the optional MIME "
"type for the attachment. If you omit ``mimetype``, the MIME content type "
"will be guessed from the filename of the attachment."
msgstr ""
"De rogha air sin, is féidir leat trí argóint ``attachment () ``a rith: "
"``ainm comhaid``, `content`` agus ``mimetype``. Is é ``ainm comhad ``ainm an "
"cheangaltán comhad mar a bheidh sé le feiceáil sa ríomhphost,`` ábhar ``na "
"sonraí a bheidh taobh istigh den cheangaltán agus is é `mimetype`` an cineál "
"MIME roghnach don cheangaltán. Má fhágann tú `mimetype``, déanfar an cineál "
"ábhair MIME a thuairim ó ainm comhaid an cheangaltáin."

msgid ""
"If you specify a ``mimetype`` of :mimetype:`message/rfc822`, it will also "
"accept :class:`django.core.mail.EmailMessage` "
"and :py:class:`email.message.Message`."
msgstr ""
"Má shonraíonn tú `mimetype`` o:mimetype: `teachtaireach/rfc822`, glacfaidh "
"sé freisin le: class: `django.core.mail.emailMessage` agus:py:class: "
"`email.message.message`."

msgid ""
"For a ``mimetype`` starting with :mimetype:`text/`, content is expected to "
"be a string. Binary data will be decoded using UTF-8, and if that fails, the "
"MIME type will be changed to :mimetype:`application/octet-stream` and the "
"data will be attached unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le `mimetype`` ag tosú le:mimetype: `text/`, táthar ag súil go mbeidh "
"an t-ábhar ina shreang. Déanfar sonraí dénártha a dhíchódú ag baint úsáide "
"as UTF-8, agus má theipeann air sin, athrófar an cineál MIME go: mimetype: "
"`application/octet-stream` agus cuirfear na sonraí ceangailte gan athrú."

msgid ""
"In addition, :mimetype:`message/rfc822` attachments will no longer be base64-"
"encoded in violation of :rfc:`2046#section-5.2.1`, which can cause issues "
"with displaying the attachments in `Evolution`__ and `Thunderbird`__."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, ní bheidh ceangaltáin:: mimetype: `teachtairea/rfc822` "
"base64-ionchódaithe a thuilleadh i sárú ar:rfc: `2046 #section -5.2.1`, rud "
"a d'fhéadfadh fadhbanna a bheith ina chúis le na ceangaltáin a thaispeáint "
"in `Evolution`__ agus `Thunderbird`__."

msgid ""
"``attach_file()`` creates a new attachment using a file from your "
"filesystem. Call it with the path of the file to attach and, optionally, the "
"MIME type to use for the attachment. If the MIME type is omitted, it will be "
"guessed from the filename. You can use it like this::"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn ``attach_file () ``ceangaltán nua ag baint úsáide as comhad ó do "
"chóras comhaid. Glaoigh air le cosán an chomhaid le ceangal agus, go "
"roghnach, an cineál MIME le húsáid don cheangaltán. Má fhágtar an cineál "
"MIME amach, déanfar é a thuairim ón ainm comhaid. Is féidir leat é a úsáid "
"mar seo::"

msgid ""
"For MIME types starting with :mimetype:`text/`, binary data is handled as in "
"``attach()``."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le cineálacha MIME ag tosú le:mimetype: `text/`, láimhseáiltear "
"sonraí dénártha mar atá i ``attachment ()``."

