msgid "Defining a custom email backend"
msgstr "Cúlcheann ríomhphoist saincheaptha a shainiú"

msgid ""
"If you need to change how emails are sent you can write your own email "
"backend. The :setting:`EMAIL_BACKEND` setting in your settings file is then "
"the Python import path for your backend class."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit conas a sheoltar ríomhphoist a athrú is féidir leat do chúltaca "
"ríomhphoist féin a scríobh. Is é an socrú: SETTING: `EMAIL_BACKEND` i do "
"chomhad socruithe ansin an cosán allmhairithe Python do do rang cúltaca."

msgid ""
"Custom email backends should subclass ``BaseEmailBackend`` that is located "
"in the ``django.core.mail.backends.base`` module. A custom email backend "
"must implement the ``send_messages(email_messages)`` method. This method "
"receives a list of :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` instances and "
"returns the number of successfully delivered messages. If your backend has "
"any concept of a persistent session or connection, you should also implement "
"the ``open()`` and ``close()`` methods. Refer to ``smtp.EmailBackend`` for a "
"reference implementation."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh cúltaca ríomhphoist saincheaptha fo-aicme "
"``BaseMailBackend`` atá suite sa mhodúl ``django.core.mail.backends.base``. "
"Caithfidh cúltaca ríomhphoist saincheaptha an modh ``send_messages "
"(email_messages) ``a chur i bhfeidhm. Faigheann an modh seo liosta de:class: "
"`~django.core.mail.emailMessage` cásanna agus filleann sé líon na "
"dteachtaireachtaí a sheachadadh go rathúil. Má tá aon choincheap maidir le "
"seisiún nó nasc leanúnach ag do chúlcheann, ba cheart duit na modhanna `open "
"() `agus ``close ()` a chur i bhfeidhm freisin. Féach ``SMTP.EmailBackend`` "
"le haghaidh cur i bhfeidhm tagartha."

msgid "Sending multiple emails"
msgstr "Seoladh ríomhphoist iliom"

msgid ""
"Establishing and closing an SMTP connection (or any other network "
"connection, for that matter) is an expensive process. If you have a lot of "
"emails to send, it makes sense to reuse an SMTP connection, rather than "
"creating and destroying a connection every time you want to send an email."
msgstr ""
"Is próiseas costasach é nasc SMTP a bhunú agus a dhúnadh (nó aon nasc líonra "
"eile, ar an ábhar sin). Má tá a lán ríomhphoist agat le seoladh, bíonn sé "
"ciallmhar nasc SMTP a athúsáid, seachas nasc a chruthú agus a scriosadh gach "
"uair is mian leat ríomhphost a sheoladh."

msgid "There are two ways you tell an email backend to reuse a connection."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá bhealach ann a insíonn tú do chúltaca ríomhphoist nasc a athúsáid."

msgid ""
"Firstly, you can use the ``send_messages()`` method on a connection. This "
"takes a list of :class:`EmailMessage` (or subclass) instances, and sends "
"them all using that single connection. As a consequence, "
"any :class:`connection <EmailMessage>` set on an individual message is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, is féidir leat an modh `send_messages () ``a úsáid ar nasc. Tógann "
"sé seo liosta de:class: `EmailMessage` (nó fo-aicme) cásanna, agus seolann "
"sé iad go léir ag baint úsáide as an nasc aonair sin. Mar thoradh air sin, "
"déantar neamhaird ar haon:class: `nasc <EmailMessage>`atá socraithe ar "
"theachtaireacht aonair."

msgid ""
"For example, if you have a function called ``get_notification_email()`` that "
"returns a list of :class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` objects "
"representing some periodic email you wish to send out, you could send these "
"emails using a single call to send_messages::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá feidhm agat ar a dtugtar ``get_notification_email () ``a "
"thugann liosta de:class: `~django.core.mail.emailmessage` rudaí a léiríonn "
"roinnt ríomhphoist tréimhsiúil is mian leat a sheoladh amach, d'fhéadfá na "
"ríomhphoist seo a sheoladh ag úsáid glao amháin chuig send_messages::"

msgid ""
"In this example, the call to ``send_messages()`` opens a connection on the "
"backend, sends the list of messages, and then closes the connection again."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, osclaíonn an glao chuig `send_messages () ``nasc ar an "
"gcúltaca, seolann sé liosta na dteachtaireachtaí, agus ansin dúnann sé an "
"nasc arís."

msgid ""
"The second approach is to use the ``open()`` and ``close()`` methods on the "
"email backend to manually control the connection. ``send_messages()`` will "
"not manually open or close the connection if it is already open, so if you "
"manually open the connection, you can control when it is closed. For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara cur chuige ná na modhanna ``open () ``agus ``close ()`` a úsáid "
"ar an gcúltaca ríomhphoist chun an nasc a rialú de láimh. Ní osclóidh nó ní "
"dhúnfaidh ``send_messages () ``an nasc de láimh má tá sé oscailte cheana "
"féin, mar sin má osclaíonn tú an nasc de láimh, is féidir leat rialú a "
"dhéanamh nuair a dhúntar é. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Configuring email for development"
msgstr "Ríomhphost a chumrú le haghaidh forbartha"

msgid ""
"There are times when you do not want Django to send emails at all. For "
"example, while developing a website, you probably don't want to send out "
"thousands of emails -- but you may want to validate that emails will be sent "
"to the right people under the right conditions, and that those emails will "
"contain the correct content."
msgstr ""
"Tá amanna ann nuair nach dteastaíonn uait Django ríomhphoist a sheoladh ar "
"chor ar bith. Mar shampla, agus tú ag forbairt láithreán gréasáin, is dócha "
"nach dteastaíonn uait na mílte ríomhphost a sheoladh amach - ach b'fhéidir "
"gur mhaith leat a bhailíochtú go seolfar ríomhphoist chuig na daoine cearta "
"faoi na coinníollacha cearta, agus go mbeidh an t-ábhar ceart sna "
"ríomhphoist sin."

msgid ""
"The easiest way to configure email for local development is to use "
"the :ref:`console <topic-email-console-backend>` email backend. This backend "
"redirects all email to ``stdout``, allowing you to inspect the content of "
"mail."
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach is éasca chun ríomhphost a chumrú d'fhorbairt áitiúil ná "
"cúltaca ríomhphoist: ref: `console <topic-email-console-backend>`a úsáid. "
"Atreoraíonn an cúltaca seo gach ríomhphost chuig `stdout``, rud a ligeann "
"duit ábhar an phoist a iniúchadh."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`file <topic-email-file-backend>` email backend can also be useful "
"during development -- this backend dumps the contents of every SMTP "
"connection to a file that can be inspected at your leisure."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le cúltaca rí <topic-email-file-backend>omhphoist: Ref: `comhad `a "
"bheith úsáideach le linn na forbartha freisin - tugann an cúltaca seo ábhar "
"gach nasc SMTP le comhad is féidir a iniúchadh ag do chuid fóillíochta."

msgid ""
"Another approach is to use a \"dumb\" SMTP server that receives the emails "
"locally and displays them to the terminal, but does not actually send "
"anything. The :pypi:`aiosmtpd` package provides a way to accomplish this:"
msgstr ""
"Cur chuige eile is ea freastalaí SMTP “buma” a úsáid a fhaigheann na "
"ríomhphoist go háitiúil agus a thaispeánann iad chuig an teirminéal, ach "
"nach seolann aon rud i ndáiríre. Soláthraíonn an pacáiste: pypi: `aiosmtpd` "
"bealach chun é seo a chur i gcrích:"

msgid ""
"This command will start a minimal SMTP server listening on port 8025 of "
"localhost. This server prints to standard output all email headers and the "
"email body. You then only need to set the :setting:`EMAIL_HOST` "
"and :setting:`EMAIL_PORT` accordingly. For a more detailed discussion of "
"SMTP server options, see the documentation of the `aiosmtpd`_ module."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh an t-ordú seo tús le freastalaí SMTP íosta ag éisteacht ar "
"chalafort 8025 de localhost. Priontáil an freastalaí seo chuig aschur "
"caighdeánach gach ceanntáil ríomhphoist agus an corp Ní gá duit ansin ach "
"an: setting: `EMAIL_HOST` agus:setting: `EMAIL_PORT` a shocrú dá réir. Le "
"haghaidh plé níos mionsonraithe ar roghanna freastalaí SMTP, féach "
"doiciméadú an mhodúil `aiosmtpd`_."

msgid ""
"For information about unit-testing the sending of emails in your "
"application, see the :ref:`topics-testing-email` section of the testing "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh faisnéise maidir le haonad-tástáil ríomhphoist a sheoladh i "
"d'iarratas, féach an ranna:ref: `topics-testing-email` den doiciméad tástála."

msgid "External packages"
msgstr "Pacáistí seachtr"

msgid ""
"Django ships with a variety of extra, optional tools that solve common "
"problems (``contrib.*``). For easier maintenance and to trim the size of the "
"codebase, a few of those applications have been moved out to separate "
"projects."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django le réimse uirlisí roghnacha breise a réitíonn fadhbanna "
"coitianta (``contrib.*``). Le haghaidh cothabháil níos éasca agus méid an "
"chóid a ghearradh, aistríodh cúpla ceann de na feidhmchláir sin amach chuig "
"tionscadail ar leithligh."

msgid "Localflavor"
msgstr "Áitiúil Flavor"

msgid ""
"``django-localflavor`` is a collection of utilities for particular countries "
"and cultures."
msgstr ""
"Is bailiúchán fóntais do thíortha agus cultúir áirithe é `django-"
"localflavor``."

msgid "`GitHub <https://github.com/django/django-localflavor>`__"
msgstr "< https://github.com/django/django-localflavor>`Github`__"

msgid "`Documentation <https://django-localflavor.readthedocs.io/>`__"
msgstr "`Doiciméadach`__ < https://django-localflavor.readthedocs.io/>"

msgid ":pypi:`PyPI <django-localflavor>`"
msgstr "<django-localflavor>:pypi: `Pypi`"

msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Tuairimí"

msgid ""
"``django-contrib-comments`` can be used to attach comments to any model, so "
"you can use it for comments on blog entries, photos, book chapters, or "
"anything else. Most users will be better served with a custom solution, or a "
"hosted product like Disqus."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ``django-contrib-comments`` a úsáid chun tráchtanna a cheangal le "
"haon mhúnla, ionas gur féidir leat é a úsáid le haghaidh tuairimí ar "
"iontrálacha blag, grianghraif, caibidlí leabhar, nó aon rud eile. "
"Freastalfar níos fearr ar fhormhór na n-úsáideoirí le réiteach saincheaptha, "
"nó táirge óstáilte mar Disqus."

msgid "`GitHub <https://github.com/django/django-contrib-comments>`__"
msgstr "< https://github.com/django/django-contrib-comments>`Github`__"

msgid "`Documentation <https://django-contrib-comments.readthedocs.io/>`__"
msgstr "`Doiciméadach`__ < https://django-contrib-comments.readthedocs.io/>"

msgid ":pypi:`PyPI <django-contrib-comments>`"
msgstr "<django-contrib-comments>:pypi: `Pypi`"

msgid "Formtools"
msgstr "Formtools"

msgid ""
"``django-formtools`` is a collection of assorted utilities to work with "
"forms."
msgstr ""
"Is bailiúchán fóntais éagsúla é `django-formtools`` chun oibriú le "
"foirmeacha."

msgid "`GitHub <https://github.com/jazzband/django-formtools/>`__"
msgstr "`Github`__ < https://github.com/jazzband/django-formtools/>"

msgid "`Documentation <https://django-formtools.readthedocs.io/>`__"
msgstr "`Doiciméadach`__ < https://django-formtools.readthedocs.io/>"

msgid ":pypi:`PyPI <django-formtools>`"
msgstr "<django-formtools>:pypi: `Pypi`"

msgid "Managing files"
msgstr "Comhaid a bhainistiú"

msgid ""
"This document describes Django's file access APIs for files such as those "
"uploaded by a user. The lower level APIs are general enough that you could "
"use them for other purposes. If you want to handle \"static files\" (JS, "
"CSS, etc.), see :doc:`/howto/static-files/index`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an doiciméad seo cur síos ar APIs rochtana comhaid Django do "
"chomhaid mar iad siúd a uaslódálann úsáideoir Tá na APIs leibhéal níos ísle "
"ginearálta go leor gur féidir leat iad a úsáid chun críocha eile. Más mian "
"leat “comhaid statacha” a láimhseáil (JS, CSS, srl.), Féach: doc: `/howto/"
"static-files/index `."

msgid ""
"By default, Django stores files locally, using the :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` "
"and :setting:`MEDIA_URL` settings. The examples below assume that you're "
"using these defaults."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, stóráilíonn Django comhaid go háitiúil, ag baint "
"úsáide as socruithe:: `MEDIA_ROOT` agus:setting: `MEDIA_URL`. Glacann na "
"samplaí thíos leis go bhfuil na réamhshocruithe seo á úsáid agat."

msgid ""
"However, Django provides ways to write custom `file storage systems`_ that "
"allow you to completely customize where and how Django stores files. The "
"second half of this document describes how these storage systems work."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, soláthraíonn Django bealaí chun `córais stórála comhad `_ "
"saincheaptha a scríobh a ligeann duit cá háit agus conas a stórálann Django "
"comhaid a shaincheapadh go hiomlán. Déanann an dara leath den doiciméad seo "
"cur síos ar conas a oibríonn na córais stórála"

msgid "Using files in models"
msgstr "Comhaid a úsáid i samhlacha"

msgid ""
"When you use a :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` "
"or :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField`, Django provides a set of APIs you "
"can use to deal with that file."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáideann tú a:class: `~django.db.models.filefield` nó:class: "
"`~django.db.models.imagefield`, soláthraíonn Django sraith APIs is féidir "
"leat a úsáid chun déileáil leis an gcomhad sin."

msgid ""
"Consider the following model, using an :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` "
"to store a photo::"
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh ar an tsamhail seo a leanas, ag baint úsáide as an:class: "
"`~django.db.models.imagefield` chun grianghraf a stóráil::"

msgid ""
"Any ``Car`` instance will have a ``photo`` attribute that you can use to get "
"at the details of the attached photo:"
msgstr ""
"Beidh tréith ``grianghraf ``ag aon shampla ``Car`` is féidir leat a úsáid "
"chun sonraí an ghrianghraf ceangailte a fháil:"

msgid ""
"This object -- ``car.photo`` in the example -- is a ``File`` object, which "
"means it has all the methods and attributes described below."
msgstr ""
"Is réad “Comhad” é an réad seo - ``car.photo`` sa sampla -- réad ``Comhad "
"``, rud a chiallaíonn go bhfuil na modhanna agus na tréithe go léir a "
"thuairiscítear thíos aige."

msgid ""
"The file is saved as part of saving the model in the database, so the actual "
"file name used on disk cannot be relied on until after the model has been "
"saved."
msgstr ""
"Sábháiltear an comhad mar chuid den tsamhail a shábháil sa bhunachar sonraí, "
"mar sin ní féidir brath ar an ainm comhaid iarbhír a úsáidtear ar dhiosca go "
"dtí go ndéanfar an tsamhail a shábháil."

msgid ""
"For example, you can change the file name by setting the "
"file's :attr:`~django.core.files.File.name` to a path relative to the file "
"storage's location (:setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` if you are using the "
"default :class:`~django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage`):"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, is féidir leat ainm an chomhaid a athrú tríd an comhad a shocrú "
"'s:attr: `~django.core.files.name` go cosán i gcoibhneas le suíomh stórála "
"an chomhaid (:setting: `MEDIA_ROOT` má tá an réamhshocraithe:class: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.fileSystemStorage`):"

msgid ""
"To save an existing file on disk to a :class:`~django.db.models.FileField`:"
msgstr ""
"Chun comhad atá ann cheana a shábháil ar dhiosca chuig a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.FileField`:"

msgid ""
"While :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` non-image data attributes, such "
"as ``height``, ``width``, and ``size`` are available on the instance, the "
"underlying image data cannot be used without reopening the image. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil tréithe sonraí neamh-íomhá: Class: "
"`~django.db.models.imagefield` ar fáil ar an gcás, mar shampla ``airde ``, "
"`leithead``, agus ``size`` `` `` `` `fiú, ní féidir na sonraí íomhá "
"bunúsacha a úsáid gan an íomhá a athoscailt. Mar shampla:"

msgid "The ``File`` object"
msgstr "An réad ``Comhad ``"

msgid ""
"Internally, Django uses a :class:`django.core.files.File` instance any time "
"it needs to represent a file."
msgstr ""
"Go hinmheánach, úsáideann Django sampla a:class: `Django.core.files.file` "
"aon uair a theastaíonn uaidh comhad a léiriú."

msgid ""
"Most of the time you'll use a ``File`` that Django's given you (i.e. a file "
"attached to a model as above, or perhaps an uploaded file)."
msgstr ""
"An chuid is mó den am úsáidfidh tú ``Comhad ``a thug Django duit (ie comhad "
"atá ceangailte le samhail mar thuas, nó comhad uaslódáilte b'fhéidir)."

msgid ""
"If you need to construct a ``File`` yourself, the easiest way is to create "
"one using a Python built-in ``file`` object:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit ``Comhad ``a thógáil duit féin, is é an bealach is éasca ceann a "
"chruthú ag baint úsáide as réad `comhad`` ionsuite Python:"

msgid ""
"Now you can use any of the documented attributes and methods of "
"the :class:`~django.core.files.File` class."
msgstr ""
"Anois is féidir leat aon cheann de na tréithe agus na modhanna "
"doiciméadaithe den aicme:class: `~django.core.files.file` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Be aware that files created in this way are not automatically closed. The "
"following approach may be used to close files automatically:"
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas nach ndúntar comhaid a cruthaíodh ar an mbealach seo go "
"huathoibr Is féidir an cur chuige seo a leanas a úsáid chun comhaid a "
"dhúnadh go huathoibr"

msgid ""
"Closing files is especially important when accessing file fields in a loop "
"over a large number of objects. If files are not manually closed after "
"accessing them, the risk of running out of file descriptors may arise. This "
"may lead to the following error:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach go háirithe comhaid a dhúnadh agus tú ag teacht ar réimsí "
"comhaid i lúb thar líon mór rudaí. Mura ndúntar comhaid de láimh tar éis "
"rochtain a fháil orthu, d'fhéadfadh an riosca go n-éireoidh amach as "
"tuairiscí comhaid. D'fhéadfadh an earráid seo a leanas a bheith mar thoradh "
"air seo:"

msgid "File storage"
msgstr "Stóráil comhad"

msgid ""
"Behind the scenes, Django delegates decisions about how and where to store "
"files to a file storage system. This is the object that actually understands "
"things like file systems, opening and reading files, etc."
msgstr ""
"Taobh thiar de na radhairc, déanann Django cinntí faoi conas agus cá háit a "
"stóráil comhaid chuig córas stórála comhaid. Is é seo an réad a thuigeann "
"rudaí cosúil le córais chomhaid, comhad a oscailt agus a léamh, srl."

msgid ""
"Django's default file storage is "
"``'``:class:`django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage`\\ ``'``. If you "
"don't explicitly provide a storage system in the ``default`` key of "
"the :setting:`STORAGES` setting, this is the one that will be used."
msgstr ""
"Is é stóráil comhaid réamhshocraithe Django `````:class: "
"`django.core.files.storage.filesystemStorage`\\ ````. Mura soláthraíonn tú "
"córas stórála go sainráite san eochair ``réamhshocraithe`` den "
"socrú:setting: `STORAGES`, is é seo an ceann a úsáidfear."

msgid ""
"See below for details of the built-in default file storage system, and "
"see :doc:`/howto/custom-file-storage` for information on writing your own "
"file storage system."
msgstr ""
"Féach thíos le haghaidh sonraí faoin gcóras stórála comhaid réamhshocraithe "
"ionsuite, agus féach: doc: `/howto/custom-file-storage` le haghaidh "
"faisnéise maidir le do chóras stórála comhaid féin a scríobh."

msgid "Storage objects"
msgstr "Rudaí stórála"

msgid ""
"Though most of the time you'll want to use a ``File`` object (which "
"delegates to the proper storage for that file), you can use file storage "
"systems directly. You can create an instance of some custom file storage "
"class, or -- often more useful -- you can use the global default storage "
"system:"
msgstr ""
"Cé go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh réad ``Comhad ``a úsáid an chuid is mó den am (a "
"thosclaíonn chuig an stóráil cheart don chomhad sin), is féidir leat córais "
"stórála comhaid a úsáid go díreach. Is féidir leat sampla de rang stórála "
"comhaid saincheaptha a chruthú, nó - is minic níos úsáideach - is féidir "
"leat an córas stórála réamhshocraithe domhanda a úsáid:"

msgid "See :doc:`/ref/files/storage` for the file storage API."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/ref/files/storage` don API stórála comhaid."

msgid "The built-in filesystem storage class"
msgstr "An rang stórála córas comhaid ionsuite"

msgid ""
"Django ships with a :class:`django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage` "
"class which implements basic local filesystem file storage."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django le aicme a:class: "
"`django.core.files.storage.filesystemStorage` a chuireann stóráil bhunúsach "
"comhaid chórais comhaid áitiúil i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"For example, the following code will store uploaded files under ``/media/"
"photos`` regardless of what your :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` setting is::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, stóráilfidh an cód seo a leanas comhaid uaslódáilte faoi ``/"
"meáin/grianghraif ``is cuma cad é do shuíomh: `MEDIA_ROOT`::"

msgid ""
":doc:`Custom storage systems </howto/custom-file-storage>` work the same "
"way: you can pass them in as the ``storage`` argument to "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.FileField`."
msgstr ""
":doc: Oibríonn `córais stórála saincheaptaí` ar an mbe</howto/custom-file-"
"storage> alach céanna: is féidir leat iad a chur isteach mar an argóint "
"``stóráil ``chuig a:class: `~django.db.models.filefield`."

msgid "Using a callable"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as inghlaoch"

msgid ""
"You can use a callable as the :attr:`~django.db.models.FileField.storage` "
"parameter for :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` "
"or :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField`. This allows you to modify the used "
"storage at runtime, selecting different storages for different environments, "
"for example."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat glaoch a úsáid mar an paraiméadar: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.filefield.storage` le haghaidh: class: "
"`~django.db.models.filefield` nó:class: `~django.db.models.imagefield`. "
"Ligeann sé seo duit an stóráil a úsáidtear a mhodhnú ag rith, ag roghnú "
"stórásanna éagsúla do thimpeallachtaí éagsúla, mar shampla."

msgid ""
"Your callable will be evaluated when your models classes are loaded, and "
"must return an instance of :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage`."
msgstr ""
"Déanfar do ghlaoch a mheas nuair a luchtar do ranganna samhlacha, agus ní "
"mór duit sampla de:class: `~django.core.files.storage.storage` a thabhairt "
"ar ais."

msgid ""
"In order to set a storage defined in the :setting:`STORAGES` setting you can "
"use :data:`~django.core.files.storage.storages`::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn stóráil a shainmhínítear sa socrú: socrú: `STORAGES` is féidir leat "
"úsáid:data: `~django.core.files.storage.storages`::"

msgid ""
"Because the callable is evaluated when your models classes are loaded, if "
"you need to override the :setting:`STORAGES` setting in tests, you should "
"use a ``LazyObject`` subclass instead::"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ``LazyObject`` delays the evaluation of the storage until it's actually "
"needed, allowing :func:`~django.test.override_settings` to take effect::"
msgstr ""

msgid "Formsets"
msgstr "Foirmeacha"

msgid ""
"A formset is a layer of abstraction to work with multiple forms on the same "
"page. It can be best compared to a data grid. Let's say you have the "
"following form:"
msgstr ""
"Is sraith teastartha é foirmshraith chun oibriú le foirmeacha iolracha ar an "
"leathanach céanna. Is féidir é a bheith is fearr i gcomparáid le greille "
"sonraí. Abair go bhfuil an fhoirm seo a leanas agat:"

msgid ""
"You might want to allow the user to create several articles at once. To "
"create a formset out of an ``ArticleForm`` you would do:"
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat ligean don úsáideoir roinnt alt a chruthú ag an am "
"céanna. Chun foirm a chruthú as ``Airteagal Form`` déanfaí an méid seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid ""
"You now have created a formset class named ``ArticleFormSet``. Instantiating "
"the formset gives you the ability to iterate over the forms in the formset "
"and display them as you would with a regular form:"
msgstr ""
"Tá rang formset cruthaithe agat anois darb ainm ``ArticleFormSet``. Tugann "
"an tacar foirmeacha a thaispeáint tugtar an cumas duit athrá a dhéanamh thar "
"na foirmeacha sa tacar foirme agus iad a thaispeáint mar a dhéanfá le foirm "
"rialta:"

msgid ""
"As you can see it only displayed one empty form. The number of empty forms "
"that is displayed is controlled by the ``extra`` parameter. By "
"default, :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory` defines one extra "
"form; the following example will create a formset class to display two blank "
"forms:"
msgstr ""
"Mar a fheiceann tú ní thaispeánann sé ach foirm folamh amháin. Tá líon na "
"bhfoirmeacha folamh a thaispeántar á rialú ag an bparaiméadar ``breise``. De "
"réir réamhshocraithe, :func: "
"`~django.forms.formsets.formsets.formset_factory` sainmhíníonn foirm bhreise "
"amháin; cruthóidh an sampla seo a leanas rang formset chun dhá fhoirm bán a "
"thaispeáint:"

msgid ""
"Formsets can be iterated and indexed, accessing forms in the order they were "
"created. You can reorder the forms by overriding the "
"default :py:meth:`iteration <object.__iter__>` and :py:meth:`indexing "
"<object.__getitem__>` behavior if needed."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir foirmeacha a athrá agus a innéacsú, ag rochtain a fháil ar "
"fhoirmeacha san ord a cruthaíodh iad. "
"<object.__iter__><object.__getitem__>Is féidir leat na foirmeacha a athordú "
"trí iompar réamhshocraithe: py:meth: `iteration `agus:py:meth: "
"`innéacsaíocht` a shárú más gá."

msgid "Using initial data with a formset"
msgstr "Sonraí tosaigh a úsáid le tacar foirme"

msgid ""
"Initial data is what drives the main usability of a formset. As shown above "
"you can define the number of extra forms. What this means is that you are "
"telling the formset how many additional forms to show in addition to the "
"number of forms it generates from the initial data. Let's take a look at an "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Is iad na sonraí tosaigh an rud a spreagann príomh-inúsáidteacht "
"foirmshraith. Mar a thaispeántar thuas is féidir leat líon na bhfoirmeacha "
"breise a shainiú. Is é an rud a chiallaíonn sé seo ná go bhfuil tú ag insint "
"don fhoirm cé mhéad foirm bhreise atá le taispeáint i dteannta leis an líon "
"foirmeacha a ghineann sé ó na sonraí tosaigh. Breathnaímid ar shampla:"

msgid ""
"There are now a total of three forms showing above. One for the initial data "
"that was passed in and two extra forms. Also note that we are passing in a "
"list of dictionaries as the initial data."
msgstr ""
"Tá trí fhoirm san iomlán anois ag taispeáint thuas. Ceann amháin do na "
"sonraí tosaigh a cuireadh isteach agus dhá fhoirm bhreise. Tabhair faoi "
"deara freisin go bhfuilimid ag dul isteach i liosta foclóirí mar na sonraí "
"tosaigh."

msgid ""
"If you use an ``initial`` for displaying a formset, you should pass the same "
"``initial`` when processing that formset's submission so that the formset "
"can detect which forms were changed by the user. For example, you might have "
"something like: ``ArticleFormSet(request.POST, initial=[...])``."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú ``tosaithe`` chun tacar foirme a thaispeáint, ba cheart duit "
"an ``tosaitheach`` céanna a rith agus tú ag próiseáil aighneacht foirmeacha "
"sin ionas gur féidir leis an tacar foirme a bhrath cé na foirmeacha a "
"d'athraigh an t-úsáideoir. Mar shampla, b'fhéidir go mbeadh rud éigin cosúil "
"le: ``ArticleFormSet (request.post, initial= [...])``."

msgid ""
":ref:`Creating formsets from models with model formsets <model-formsets>`."
msgstr ""
"<model-formsets>:ref: `Foirmeacha a chruthú ó mhúnlaí le foirmeacha samhail "
"`."

msgid "Limiting the maximum number of forms"
msgstr "An líon uasta na bhfoirmeacha a theorannú"

msgid ""
"The ``max_num`` parameter to :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory` "
"gives you the ability to limit the number of forms the formset will display:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann an paraiméadar ``max_num`` to:func: "
"`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory` an cumas duit líon na bhfoirmeacha "
"a thaispeánfaidh an formset a theorannú:"

msgid ""
"If the value of ``max_num`` is greater than the number of existing items in "
"the initial data, up to ``extra`` additional blank forms will be added to "
"the formset, so long as the total number of forms does not exceed "
"``max_num``. For example, if ``extra=2`` and ``max_num=2`` and the formset "
"is initialized with one ``initial`` item, a form for the initial item and "
"one blank form will be displayed."
msgstr ""
"Má tá luach ``max_num`` níos mó ná líon na míreanna atá ann cheana sna "
"sonraí tosaigh, cuirfear foirmeacha bán breise suas le ``extra`` leis an "
"tacar foirmeacha, fad nach mbeidh líon iomlán na bhfoirmeacha níos mó ná "
"``max_num``. Mar shampla, má tá ``extra=2`` agus ``max_num=2`` agus má "
"thosaítear an foirmshraith le mír ``initial`` amháin, taispeánfar foirm don "
"mhír tosaigh agus foirm bán amháin."

msgid ""
"If the number of items in the initial data exceeds ``max_num``, all initial "
"data forms will be displayed regardless of the value of ``max_num`` and no "
"extra forms will be displayed. For example, if ``extra=3`` and ``max_num=1`` "
"and the formset is initialized with two initial items, two forms with the "
"initial data will be displayed."
msgstr ""
"Má sháraíonn líon na míreanna sna sonraí tosaigh ``max_num``, taispeánfar "
"gach foirm sonraí tosaigh beag beann ar luach ``max_num`` agus ní "
"thaispeánfar aon fhoirmeacha breise. Mar shampla, má tá ``extra=3`` agus "
"``max_num=1`` agus má dhá mhír tosaigh an foirmeach a thosú, taispeánfar dhá "
"fhoirm leis na sonraí tosaigh."

msgid ""
"A ``max_num`` value of ``None`` (the default) puts a high limit on the "
"number of forms displayed (1000). In practice this is equivalent to no limit."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann luach ``max_num`` de ``None`` (an réamhshocrú) teorainn ard ar líon "
"na bhfoirmeacha a thaispeántar (1000). Go praiticiúil tá sé seo coibhéiseach "
"le haon teorainn."

msgid ""
"By default, ``max_num`` only affects how many forms are displayed and does "
"not affect validation.  If ``validate_max=True`` is passed to "
"the :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, then ``max_num`` will "
"affect validation.  See :ref:`validate_max`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ní théann `max_num`` i bhfeidhm ach ar an méid "
"foirm a thaispeántar agus ní dhéanann sé difear do bhailíochtú. Má chuirtear "
"``validate_max=true`` chuig an:func: "
"`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, ansin beidh tionchar ag "
"``max_num`` ar bhailíochtú. Féach:ref: `validate_max`."

msgid "Limiting the maximum number of instantiated forms"
msgstr "Uaslíon na bhfoirmeacha ionchasacha a theorannú"

msgid ""
"The ``absolute_max`` parameter to :func:`.formset_factory` allows limiting "
"the number of forms that can be instantiated when supplying ``POST`` data. "
"This protects against memory exhaustion attacks using forged ``POST`` "
"requests:"
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an paraiméadar ``absolute_max`` to:func: `.formset_factory` líon "
"na bhfoirmeacha is féidir a dhéanamh a theorannú nuair a sholáthraítear "
"sonraí `POST ``. Cosnaíonn sé seo i gcoinne ionsaithe ídithe cuimhne ag "
"úsáid iarratais brionnaithe ``POST ``"

msgid ""
"When ``absolute_max`` is ``None``, it defaults to ``max_num + 1000``. (If "
"``max_num`` is ``None``, it defaults to ``2000``)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair is é ``absolute_max`` ``None ``, réamhshocraithe é go ``max_num + "
"1000``. (Má tá ```max_num`` ``None ``, réamhshocraithe é go ``2000``)."

msgid ""
"If ``absolute_max`` is less than ``max_num``, a ``ValueError`` will be "
"raised."
msgstr "Má tá ``absolute_max`` níos lú ná ``max_num``, ardófar ``Error lua``."

msgid "Formset validation"
msgstr "Bailíochtú Formset"

msgid ""
"Validation with a formset is almost identical to a regular ``Form``. There "
"is an ``is_valid`` method on the formset to provide a convenient way to "
"validate all forms in the formset:"
msgstr ""
"Tá bailíochtú le tacar foirme beagnach comhionann le ``Foirm ``rialta. Tá "
"modh ``is_valid`` ar an tacar foirmeacha chun bealach áisiúil a sholáthar "
"chun gach foirm sa tacar foirme a bhailíochtú:"

msgid ""
"We passed in no data to the formset which is resulting in a valid form. The "
"formset is smart enough to ignore extra forms that were not changed. If we "
"provide an invalid article:"
msgstr ""
"Níor chuireamar aon sonraí isteach chuig an tacar foirme a bhfuil foirm "
"bhailí mar thoradh air. Tá an tacar foirmeacha cliste go leor chun neamhaird "
"a dhéanamh ar fhoirmeacha breise nár athraíodh. Má sholáthraímid alt "
"neamhbhailí:"

msgid ""
"As we can see, ``formset.errors`` is a list whose entries correspond to the "
"forms in the formset. Validation was performed for each of the two forms, "
"and the expected error message appears for the second item."
msgstr ""
"Mar a fheicimid, is liosta é ``formset.errors`` a fhreagraíonn a n-"
"iontrálacha do na foirmeacha sa tacar foirmeacha. Rinneadh bailíochtú do "
"gach ceann den dá fhoirm, agus tá an teachtaireacht earráide ag súil leis le "
"feiceáil don dara mír."

msgid ""
"Just like when using a normal ``Form``, each field in a formset's forms may "
"include HTML attributes such as ``maxlength`` for browser validation. "
"However, form fields of formsets won't include the ``required`` attribute as "
"that validation may be incorrect when adding and deleting forms."
msgstr ""
"Díreach cosúil le gnáth-`Foirm ``á n-úsáid, d'fhéadfadh tréithe HTML mar "
"``maxlength`` a bheith san áireamh i ngach réimse i bhfoirmeacha foirmeacha "
"le haghaidh bailíochtaithe brabhsálaí. Mar sin féin, ní chuimsíonn réimsí "
"foirmeacha foirmeacha an tréith ``riachtan`` mar d'fhéadfadh an bailíochtú "
"sin a bheith mícheart agus foirmeacha á gcur leis agus á scriosadh."

msgid ""
"To check how many errors there are in the formset, we can use the "
"``total_error_count`` method:"
msgstr ""
"Chun a sheiceáil cé mhéad earráid atá sa fhoirmset, is féidir linn an modh "
"`total_error_count`` a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"We can also check if form data differs from the initial data (i.e. the form "
"was sent without any data):"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir linn a sheiceáil freisin an bhfuil sonraí foirme difriúil ó na "
"sonraí tosaigh (ie seoladh an fhoirm gan aon sonraí):"

msgid "Understanding the ``ManagementForm``"
msgstr "An “Foirm Bainistíochta” a thuiscint"

msgid ""
"You may have noticed the additional data (``form-TOTAL_FORMS``, ``form-"
"INITIAL_FORMS``) that was required in the formset's data above. This data is "
"required for the ``ManagementForm``. This form is used by the formset to "
"manage the collection of forms contained in the formset. If you don't "
"provide this management data, the formset will be invalid:"
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur thug tú faoi deara na sonraí breise (``Form-Total_Forms``, "
"`Form-Initial_Forms``) a bhí ag teastáil i sonraí an fhoirmscair thuas. Tá "
"na sonraí seo ag teastáil don ``Foirm Bainistíochta ``. Úsáideann an tacar "
"foirmeacha seo chun bailiúchán na bhfoirmeacha atá sa tacar foirme a "
"bhainistiú. Mura gcuireann tú na sonraí bainistíochta seo ar fáil, beidh an "
"tacar foirme neamhbhailí:"

msgid ""
"It is used to keep track of how many form instances are being displayed. If "
"you are adding new forms via JavaScript, you should increment the count "
"fields in this form as well. On the other hand, if you are using JavaScript "
"to allow deletion of existing objects, then you need to ensure the ones "
"being removed are properly marked for deletion by including ``form-#-"
"DELETE`` in the ``POST`` data. It is expected that all forms are present in "
"the ``POST`` data regardless."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear é chun súil a choinneáil ar cé mhéad cásanna foirme atá á "
"thaispeáint. Má tá foirmeacha nua á chur agat trí JavaScript, ba cheart duit "
"na réimsí comhaireamh san fhoirm seo a mhéadú freisin. Ar an láimh eile, má "
"tá JavaScript á úsáid agat chun rudaí atá ann cheana a scriosadh, ansin ní "
"mór duit a chinntiú go ndéantar na cinn atá á mbaintear marcáilte i gceart "
"lena scriosadh trí ``Form-#-delete`` a chur san áireamh sna sonraí `POST ``. "
"Táthar ag súil go mbeidh gach foirm i láthair sna sonraí `POST ``beag beann."

msgid ""
"The management form is available as an attribute of the formset itself. When "
"rendering a formset in a template, you can include all the management data "
"by rendering ``{{ my_formset.management_form }}`` (substituting the name of "
"your formset as appropriate)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fhoirm bhainistíochta ar fáil mar thréith den tacar foirme féin. Agus "
"tacar foirme á rindreáil i dteimpléad, is féidir leat na sonraí "
"bainistíochta go léir a chur san áireamh trí "
"``{{my_formset.management_form}} `a rindreáil (ainm do thacar foirme a chur "
"in ionad mar is cuí)."

msgid ""
"As well as the ``form-TOTAL_FORMS`` and ``form-INITIAL_FORMS`` fields shown "
"in the examples here, the management form also includes ``form-"
"MIN_NUM_FORMS`` and ``form-MAX_NUM_FORMS`` fields. They are output with the "
"rest of the management form, but only for the convenience of client-side "
"code. These fields are not required and so are not shown in the example "
"``POST`` data."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na réimsí ``Form-Total_Forms`` agus ``Form-Initial_Forms`` "
"a thaispeántar sna samplaí anseo, cuimsíonn an fhoirm bhainistíochta réimsí "
"``Form-Min_Num_Forms`` agus ``Form-Max_Num_Forms ``freisin. Tá siad aschur "
"leis an gcuid eile den fhoirm bhainistíochta, ach amháin ar mhaithe le "
"háisiúlacht cód taobh an chliaint. Níl na réimsí seo ag teastáil agus mar "
"sin ní thaispeántar iad sa shampla sonraí ``POST ``."

msgid "``total_form_count`` and ``initial_form_count``"
msgstr "``comhaireann_foirme_iomlán`` agus ``comhaireann_foirme_tosaithe``"

msgid ""
"``BaseFormSet`` has a couple of methods that are closely related to the "
"``ManagementForm``, ``total_form_count`` and ``initial_form_count``."
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla modh ag ``BaseFormSet`` a bhfuil dlúthbhaint acu leis an "
"``ManagementForm``, `total_form_count`` agus ``initial_form_count``."

msgid ""
"``total_form_count`` returns the total number of forms in this formset. "
"``initial_form_count`` returns the number of forms in the formset that were "
"pre-filled, and is also used to determine how many forms are required. You "
"will probably never need to override either of these methods, so please be "
"sure you understand what they do before doing so."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``total_form_count`` líon iomlán na bhfoirmeacha sa tacar foirme seo "
"ar ais. Tugann ``initial_form_count`` líon na bhfoirmeacha sa tacar foirme a "
"rinneadh réamh-líonadh, agus úsáidtear é freisin chun a chinneadh cé mhéad "
"foirm atá ag teastáil. Is dócha nach mbeidh ort riamh ceachtar de na "
"modhanna seo a shárú, mar sin bí cinnte le do thoil go dtuigeann tú cad a "
"dhéanann siad sula ndéanann siad é sin."

msgid "``empty_form``"
msgstr "``foirme_folam``"

msgid ""
"``BaseFormSet`` provides an additional attribute ``empty_form`` which "
"returns a form instance with a prefix of ``__prefix__`` for easier use in "
"dynamic forms with JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn ``BaseFormSet`` tréith bhreise ``empty_form`` a thugann sampla "
"foirme le réimír ``__prefix__`` le húsáid níos éasca i bhfoirmeacha "
"dinimiciúla le JavaScript."

msgid "``error_messages``"
msgstr "``teachtaireachtaí earráid``"

msgid ""
"The ``error_messages`` argument lets you override the default messages that "
"the formset will raise. Pass in a dictionary with keys matching the error "
"messages you want to override. Error message keys include "
"``'too_few_forms'``, ``'too_many_forms'``, and "
"``'missing_management_form'``. The ``'too_few_forms'`` and "
"``'too_many_forms'`` error messages may contain ``%(num)d``, which will be "
"replaced with ``min_num`` and ``max_num``, respectively."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an argóint ``error_messages`` duit na teachtaireachtaí "
"réamhshocraithe a ardóidh an foirmset a shárú. Pas isteach i bhfoclóir le "
"heochracha a mheaitseálann leis na teachtaireachtaí earráide is mian leat a "
"shárú. I measc na heochracha teachtaireachta earráide tá "
"```too_few_forms'``, ``too_many_forms'``, agus "
"```missing_management_form'``. D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh ``% (num) d`` sna "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide ```too_few_forms'`` agus ```too_many_forms'``, "
"agus ``max_num``, ina gcuirfear `min_num`` agus ``max_num`` in ionad "
"``min_num`` faoi seach."

msgid ""
"For example, here is the default error message when the management form is "
"missing:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, seo an teachtaireacht earráide réamhshocraithe nuair a bhíonn "
"an fhoirm bhainistíochta in easnamh:"

msgid "And here is a custom error message:"
msgstr "Agus seo teachtaireacht earráide saincheaptha:"

msgid "Custom formset validation"
msgstr "Bailíochtú foirm saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"A formset has a ``clean`` method similar to the one on a ``Form`` class. "
"This is where you define your own validation that works at the formset level:"
msgstr ""
"Tá modh ``glan ``ag tacar foirme cosúil leis an gceann ar rang ``Foirme``. "
"Seo an áit a shainmhíníonn tú do bhailíochtú féin a oibríonn ag an leibhéal "
"foirmset:"

msgid ""
"The formset ``clean`` method is called after all the ``Form.clean`` methods "
"have been called. The errors will be found using the ``non_form_errors()`` "
"method on the formset."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ar an modh ``clean ``foirmeacha tar éis na modhanna ``Form.clean`` go "
"léir a ghlaoch. Faighfear na hearráidí ag baint úsáide as an modh "
"``non_form_errors () ``ar an tacar foirme."

msgid ""
"Non-form errors will be rendered with an additional class of ``nonform`` to "
"help distinguish them from form-specific errors. For example, "
"``{{ formset.non_form_errors }}`` would look like:"
msgstr ""
"Déanfar earráidí neamh-fhoirme a thabhairt le aicme breise de "
"``neamhfhoirme`` chun cabhrú leo a idirdhealú ó earráidí foirm-shonracha. "
"Mar shampla, bheadh cuma ``{{formset.non_form_errors}} `:"

msgid "Validating the number of forms in a formset"
msgstr "Líon na bhfoirmeacha i dtacar foirmeacha a bhailíochtú"

msgid ""
"Django provides a couple ways to validate the minimum or maximum number of "
"submitted forms. Applications which need more customizable validation of the "
"number of forms should use custom formset validation."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django cúpla bealach chun líon íosta nó uasta na bhfoirmeacha "
"curtha isteach a bhailíochtú. Ba cheart d'iarratais a dteastaíonn bailíochtú "
"níos inúsáidte uathu ar líon na bhfoirmeacha bailíochtú saincheaptha"

msgid "``validate_max``"
msgstr "``bailite_max``"

msgid ""
"If ``validate_max=True`` is passed "
"to :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, validation will also "
"check that the number of forms in the data set, minus those marked for "
"deletion, is less than or equal to ``max_num``."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear ``validate_max=True`` chuig: :func: "
"`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, seiceálfaidh bailíochtú freisin go "
"bhfuil líon na bhfoirmeacha sa tacar sonraí, lúide iad siúd atá marcáilte le "
"scriosadh, níos lú ná ``max_`num` nó cothrom le `max_`num`."

msgid ""
"``validate_max=True`` validates against ``max_num`` strictly even if "
"``max_num`` was exceeded because the amount of initial data supplied was "
"excessive."
msgstr ""
"``validate_max=Bailíonn True`` i gcoinne ``max_num`` go docht fiú má "
"sháraíodh ``max_num`` toisc go raibh méid na sonraí tosaigh a sholáthraíodh "
"iomarcach."

msgid ""
"The error message can be customized by passing the ``'too_many_forms'`` "
"message to the :ref:`formsets-error-messages` argument."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an teachtaireacht earráide a shaincheapadh tríd an teachtaireacht "
"```too_many_forms'` a chur chuig an argóint:ref: `formsets-error-messages`."

msgid ""
"Regardless of ``validate_max``, if the number of forms in a data set exceeds "
"``absolute_max``, then the form will fail to validate as if ``validate_max`` "
"were set, and additionally only the first ``absolute_max`` forms will be "
"validated. The remainder will be truncated entirely. This is to protect "
"against memory exhaustion attacks using forged POST requests. "
"See :ref:`formsets-absolute-max`."
msgstr ""
"Beag beann ar ``validate_max``, má sháraíonn líon na bhfoirmeacha i tacar "
"sonraí ``absolute_max``, ansin teipeann ar an bhfoirm a bhailíochtú amhail "
"is dá gcuirfí `validate_max`` socraithe, agus ina theannta sin ní bheidh ach "
"na chéad fhoirmeacha `absolute_max`` bailíochtaithe. Déanfar an chuid eile a "
"ghearradh go hiomlán. Déanann sé seo chun cosaint a dhéanamh ar ionsaithe "
"ídithe cuimhne ag baint úsáide as iarrat Féach: tagairt: `formsets-absolute-"
"max`."

msgid "``validate_min``"
msgstr "``bailate_min``"

msgid ""
"If ``validate_min=True`` is passed "
"to :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, validation will also "
"check that the number of forms in the data set, minus those marked for "
"deletion, is greater than or equal to ``min_num``."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear ``validate_min=True`` chuig: :func: "
"`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, seiceálfaidh bailíochtú freisin go "
"bhfuil líon na bhfoirmeacha sa tacar sonraí, lúide iad siúd atá marcáilte le "
"scriosadh, níos mó ná ``min_`num` nó cothrom le `min_`num`."

msgid ""
"The error message can be customized by passing the ``'too_few_forms'`` "
"message to the :ref:`formsets-error-messages` argument."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an teachtaireacht earráide a shaincheapadh tríd an teachtaireacht "
"```too_few_forms'` a chur chuig argóint:ref: `formsets-error-messages`."

msgid ""
"Regardless of ``validate_min``, if a formset contains no data, then ``extra "
"+ min_num`` empty forms will be displayed."
msgstr ""
"Beag beann ar ``validate_min``, mura bhfuil aon sonraí i bhfoirmshraith, "
"taispeánfar foirmeacha folamh ``extra + min_num``."

msgid "Dealing with ordering and deletion of forms"
msgstr "Déileáil le foirmeacha a ordú agus a scriosadh"

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory` provides two optional "
"parameters ``can_order`` and ``can_delete`` to help with ordering of forms "
"in formsets and deletion of forms from a formset."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an: Func: `~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory` dhá "
"pharaiméadar roghnach ``can_order`` agus ``can_delete`` chun cabhrú le "
"foirmeacha a ordú i bhfoirmeacha agus foirmeacha a scriosadh ó fhoirmshraith."

msgid "``can_order``"
msgstr "``Is féidir _ordú ``"

msgid "Default: ``False``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Fréag``"

msgid "Lets you create a formset with the ability to order:"
msgstr "Ligeann duit tacar foirme a chruthú leis an gcumas a ordú:"

msgid ""
"This adds an additional field to each form. This new field is named "
"``ORDER`` and is an ``forms.IntegerField``. For the forms that came from the "
"initial data it automatically assigned them a numeric value. Let's look at "
"what will happen when the user changes these values:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé seo réimse breise le gach foirm. Ainmnítear ``ORDER`` ar an "
"réimse nua seo agus is ``Forms.IntegerField`` é. Maidir leis na foirmeacha a "
"tháinig ó na sonraí tosaigh sé luach uimhriúil dóibh go huathoibríoch. "
"Breathnaímid ar cad a tharlóidh nuair a athraíonn an t-úsáideoir na "
"luachanna seo:"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet` also provides "
"an :attr:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.ordering_widget` attribute "
"and :meth:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.get_ordering_widget` method "
"that control the widget used "
"with :attr:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.can_order`."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.forms.formsets.baseFormSet` soláthraíonn tréith freisin: "
"attr: `~django.forms.formsets.baseFormSet.Ordering_Widget` agus:meth: "
"`~django.formsets.baseFormset.get_Ordering_Widget` modh a rialaíonn an "
"giuirléid a úsáidtear la:attr: `~django.forms.formset.get_ordering_widget` "
"FormSets.BaseFormSet.Can_Order `."

msgid "``ordering_widget``"
msgstr "``ording_widget``"

msgid "Default: :class:`~django.forms.NumberInput`"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: :class: `~django.forms.numberInput`"

msgid ""
"Set ``ordering_widget`` to specify the widget class to be used with "
"``can_order``:"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ``ordering_widget`` chun an rang giuirléid atá le húsáid le "
"``can_order`` a shonrú:"

msgid "``get_ordering_widget``"
msgstr "``faigh_ording_widget``"

msgid ""
"Override ``get_ordering_widget()`` if you need to provide a widget instance "
"for use with ``can_order``:"
msgstr ""
"Athraigh ``get_ordering_widget () ``más gá duit sampla giuirléid a sholáthar "
"le húsáid le ``can_order``:"

msgid "``can_delete``"
msgstr "```is féidir _scriosa``"

msgid ""
"Lets you create a formset with the ability to select forms for deletion:"
msgstr ""
"Ligeann duit tacar foirme a chruthú leis an gcumas foirmeacha a roghnú le "
"scriosadh:"

msgid ""
"Similar to ``can_order`` this adds a new field to each form named ``DELETE`` "
"and is a ``forms.BooleanField``. When data comes through marking any of the "
"delete fields you can access them with ``deleted_forms``:"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le ``can_order`` cuireann sé seo réimse nua le gach foirm darb ainm "
"``DELETE`` agus is ``Forms.BooleanField`` é. Nuair a thagann sonraí trí aon "
"cheann de na réimsí scriosta a mharcáil is féidir leat rochtain a fháil "
"orthu le `deleted_forms``:"

msgid ""
"If you are using "
"a :class:`ModelFormSet<django.forms.models.BaseModelFormSet>`, model "
"instances for deleted forms will be deleted when you call ``formset.save()``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá a: class: `ModelFormSet <django.forms.models.BaseModelFormSet>`á úsáid "
"agat, scriosfar cásanna samhail d'fhoirmeacha scriosta nuair a ghlaonn tú ar "
"``formset.save () ``."

msgid ""
"If you call ``formset.save(commit=False)``, objects will not be deleted "
"automatically.  You'll need to call ``delete()`` on each of "
"the :attr:`formset.deleted_objects "
"<django.forms.models.BaseModelFormSet.deleted_objects>` to actually delete "
"them:"
msgstr ""
"Má ghlaonn tú ar ``formset.save (Commit=false) ``, ní scriosfar rudaí go "
"huathoibríoch. <django.forms.models.BaseModelFormSet.deleted_objects>Beidh "
"ort glaoch ar `delete () ``ar gach ceann de na:attr: "
"`formset.deleted_objects `chun iad a scriosadh i ndáiríre:"

msgid ""
"On the other hand, if you are using a plain ``FormSet``, it's up to you to "
"handle ``formset.deleted_forms``, perhaps in your formset's ``save()`` "
"method, as there's no general notion of what it means to delete a form."
msgstr ""
"Ar an láimh eile, má tá simplí ``formSet ``á úsáid agat, is fútsa atá sé "
"`formset.deleted_forms`` a láimhseáil, b'fhéidir i modh `save ()`` do "
"fhoirmset, mar níl aon smaoineamh ginearálta ann faoi cad a chiallaíonn sé "
"foirm a scriosadh."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet` also provides "
"a :attr:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.deletion_widget` attribute "
"and :meth:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.get_deletion_widget` method "
"that control the widget used "
"with :attr:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.can_delete`."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.forms.formsets.baseFormSet` soláthraíonn tréith freisin "
"a:attr: `~django.forms.formsets.baseformset.deletion_widget` modh agus:meth: "
"`~django.formsets.baseformset.get_deletion_widget` modh a rialaíonn an "
"giuirléid a úsáidtear le:attr: `~django.formset.get_deletion_widget` "
"s.formsets.baseformset.can_delete`."

msgid "``deletion_widget``"
msgstr "``scrios_widget``"

msgid "Default: :class:`~django.forms.CheckboxInput`"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: :class: `~django.forms.checkboxInput`"

msgid ""
"Set ``deletion_widget`` to specify the widget class to be used with "
"``can_delete``:"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ``deletion_widget`` chun an rang giuirléid atá le húsáid le "
"``can_delete`` a shonrú:"

msgid "``get_deletion_widget``"
msgstr "``faigh_scrios_widget``"

msgid ""
"Override ``get_deletion_widget()`` if you need to provide a widget instance "
"for use with ``can_delete``:"
msgstr ""
"Athraigh ``get_deletion_widget () ``más gá duit sampla giuirléid a sholáthar "
"le húsáid le ``can_delete``:"

msgid "``can_delete_extra``"
msgstr "```is féidir _scrios_breise``"

msgid "Default: ``True``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Fíor`"

msgid ""
"While setting ``can_delete=True``, specifying ``can_delete_extra=False`` "
"will remove the option to delete extra forms."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag socrú ``can_delete=True``, bainfear an rogha chun foirmeacha "
"breise a scriosadh ``can_delete_extra=false`` a shonrú."

msgid "Adding additional fields to a formset"
msgstr "Réimsí breise a chur le tacar foirmeacha"

msgid ""
"If you need to add additional fields to the formset this can be easily "
"accomplished. The formset base class provides an ``add_fields`` method. You "
"can override this method to add your own fields or even redefine the default "
"fields/attributes of the order and deletion fields:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit réimsí breise a chur leis an tacar foirme is féidir é seo a chur "
"i gcrích go héasca. Soláthraíonn an bunaicme foirmset modh ``add_fields``. "
"Is féidir leat an modh seo a shárú chun do réimsí féin a chur leis nó fiú "
"réimsí réamhshocraithe/tréithe na réimsí ordaithe agus scriostha a "
"athshainiú:"

msgid "Passing custom parameters to formset forms"
msgstr "Ag dul paraiméadair saincheaptha chuig foirmeacha"

msgid ""
"Sometimes your form class takes custom parameters, like ``MyArticleForm``. "
"You can pass this parameter when instantiating the formset:"
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta glacann do rang foirme paraiméadair saincheaptha, cosúil le "
"``MyArticleForm ``. Is féidir leat an paraiméadar seo a rith agus an tacar "
"foirmeacha á gcur isteach agat:"

msgid ""
"The ``form_kwargs`` may also depend on the specific form instance. The "
"formset base class provides a ``get_form_kwargs`` method. The method takes a "
"single argument - the index of the form in the formset. The index is "
"``None`` for the :ref:`empty_form`:"
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh an ``form_kwargs`` ag brath ar an gcás foirme shonrach freisin. "
"Soláthraíonn an bunaicme formset modh ``get_form_kwargs``. Tógann an modh "
"argóint amháin - innéacs na foirme sa tacar foirme. Is é ``None`` an t-"
"innéacs fao:ref: `empty_form`:"

msgid "Customizing a formset's prefix"
msgstr "Réimír foirmshraith a shaincheapadh"

msgid ""
"In the rendered HTML, formsets include a prefix on each field's name. By "
"default, the prefix is ``'form'``, but it can be customized using the "
"formset's ``prefix`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Sa HTML rindreáilte, cuimsíonn foirmeacha réimír ar ainm gach réimse. De "
"réir réamhshocraithe, is é ``foirm`` an réimír, ach is féidir é a "
"shaincheapadh ag baint úsáide as argóint ``prefix`` an fhoirmshraith."

msgid "For example, in the default case, you might see:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, sa chás réamhshocraithe, b'fhéidir go bhfeicfidh tú:"

msgid "But with ``ArticleFormset(prefix='article')`` that becomes:"
msgstr "Ach le ``ArticleFormSet (prefix='article') ``éiríonn sé sin:"

msgid ""
"This is useful if you want to :ref:`use more than one formset in a view "
"<multiple-formsets-in-view>`."
msgstr ""
"<multiple-formsets-in-view>Tá sé seo úsáideach más mian leat: ref: `úsáid "
"níos mó ná tacar foirme amháin i radharc `."

msgid "Using a formset in views and templates"
msgstr "Foirmshraith a úsáid i radhairc agus teimpléid"

msgid ""
"Formsets have the following attributes and methods associated with rendering:"
msgstr ""
"Tá na tréithe agus na modhanna seo a leanas ag foirmeacha a bhaineann le "
"rindreáil:"

msgid ""
"Specifies the :doc:`renderer </ref/forms/renderers>` to use for the formset. "
"Defaults to the renderer specified by the :setting:`FORM_RENDERER` setting."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an: doc: `renderer` </ref/forms/renderers> le húsáid don "
"fhoirmshraith. Réamhshocraithe don rindeoir a shonraítear leis an socrú: "
"setting: `FORM_RENDER`."

msgid ""
"The name of the template rendered if the formset is cast into a string, e.g. "
"via ``print(formset)`` or in a template via ``{{ formset }}``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an teimpléid a rinneadh má theilgtear an tacar foirme isteach i sreang, "
"m.sh. trí ``print (formset) ``nó i dteimpléad trí`` {{formset}} ``."

msgid ""
"By default, a property returning the value of the "
"renderer's :attr:`~django.forms.renderers.BaseRenderer.formset_template_name`. "
"You may set it as a string template name in order to override that for a "
"particular formset class."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, maoin ag filleadh luach an renderer's:attr: "
"`~django.forms.renderers.baserenderer.formset_template_name`. Féadfaidh tú é "
"a shocrú mar ainm teimpléad teaghrán d'fhonn é sin a shárú d'aicme "
"foirmeacha áirithe."

msgid ""
"This template will be used to render the formset's management form, and then "
"each form in the formset as per the template defined by the "
"form's :attr:`~django.forms.Form.template_name`."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfear an teimpléad seo chun foirm bhainistíochta an fhoirmeacha a "
"léiriú, agus ansin gach foirm sa tacar foirme de réir an teimpléid atá "
"sainmhínithe ag an bhfoirm 's:attr: `~django.forms.form.template_name`."

msgid ""
"The name of the template used when calling :meth:`.as_div`. By default this "
"is ``\"django/forms/formsets/div.html\"``. This template renders the "
"formset's management form and then each form in the formset as per the "
"form's :meth:`~django.forms.Form.as_div` method."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an teimpléid a úsáidtear agus tú ag glaoch: meth: `.as_div`. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe is é seo ``” django/forms/formsets/div.html “``. Déanann an "
"teimpléad seo foirm bhainistíochta an fhoirm agus ansin gach foirm sa tacar "
"foirme de réir an mhodh foirme's:meth: `~django.forms.form.as_div`."

msgid ""
"The name of the template used when calling :meth:`.as_p`. By default this is "
"``\"django/forms/formsets/p.html\"``. This template renders the formset's "
"management form and then each form in the formset as per the "
"form's :meth:`~django.forms.Form.as_p` method."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an teimpléid a úsáidtear agus tú ag glaoch: meth: `.as_p`. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe is é seo ``” django/forms/formsets/p.html “``. Déanann an "
"teimpléad seo foirm bhainistíochta an fhoirm agus ansin gach foirm sa tacar "
"foirme de réir an mhodh foirme's:meth: `~django.forms.form.as_p`."

msgid ""
"The name of the template used when calling :meth:`.as_table`. By default "
"this is ``\"django/forms/formsets/table.html\"``. This template renders the "
"formset's management form and then each form in the formset as per the "
"form's :meth:`~django.forms.Form.as_table` method."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an teimpléid a úsáidtear agus tú ag glaoch: meth: `.as_table`. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe is é seo ``” django/forms/formsets/table.html “``. Déanann "
"an teimpléad seo foirm bhainistíochta an fhoirm agus ansin gach foirm sa "
"tacar foirme de réir an mhodh foirme's:meth: `~django.forms.form.as_table`."

msgid ""
"The name of the template used when calling :meth:`.as_ul`. By default this "
"is ``\"django/forms/formsets/ul.html\"``. This template renders the "
"formset's management form and then each form in the formset as per the "
"form's :meth:`~django.forms.Form.as_ul` method."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an teimpléid a úsáidtear agus tú ag glaoch: meth: `.as_ul`. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe is é seo ``” django/forms/formsets/ul.html “``. Déanann an "
"teimpléad seo foirm bhainistíochta an fhoirm agus ansin gach foirm sa tacar "
"foirme de réir an mhodh foirme's:meth: `~django.forms.form.as_ul`."

msgid "Returns the context for rendering a formset in a template."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an comhthéacs ar ais chun tacar foirme a rindreáil i dteimpléad."

msgid "The available context is:"
msgstr "Is é an comhthéacs atá ar fáil:"

msgid "``formset`` : The instance of the formset."
msgstr "``formset``: An sampla den fhoirmset."

msgid ""
"The render method is called by ``__str__`` as well as "
"the :meth:`.as_div`, :meth:`.as_p`, :meth:`.as_ul`, and :meth:`.as_table` "
"methods. All arguments are optional and will default to:"
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ``__str__`` ar an modh rindreála chomh maith leis na modhanna: meth: "
"`.as_div`, :meth: `.as_p`, :meth: `.as_ul`, agus:meth: `.as_table`. Tá na "
"hargóintí go léir roghnach agus beidh siad réamhshocraithe:"

msgid "``template_name``: :attr:`.template_name`"
msgstr "``ainmne_teimpléad``: :attr: `.template_ainm`"

msgid "``context``: Value returned by :meth:`.get_context`"
msgstr "``context``: Luach ar ais ag: meth: `.get_context`"

msgid "``renderer``: Value returned by :attr:`.renderer`"
msgstr "``renderer``: Luach ar ais ar:attr: `.renderer`"

msgid "Renders the formset with the :attr:`.template_name_div` template."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé an tacar foirme leis an teimpléad:attr: `.template_name_div."

msgid "Renders the formset with the :attr:`.template_name_p` template."
msgstr "Déanann sé an tacar foirme leis an teimpléad:attr: `.template_name_p`."

msgid "Renders the formset with the :attr:`.template_name_table` template."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé an tacar foirme leis an teimpléad:attr: `.template_name_table`."

msgid "Renders the formset with the :attr:`.template_name_ul` template."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé an tacar foirme leis an teimpléad:attr: `.template_name_ul`."

msgid ""
"Using a formset inside a view is not very different from using a regular "
"``Form`` class. The only thing you will want to be aware of is making sure "
"to use the management form inside the template. Let's look at a sample view::"
msgstr ""
"Níl sé an-difriúil le tacar foirme a úsáid taobh istigh de radharc ó rang "
"rialta ``Foirme`` a úsáid. Is é an t-aon rud a theastaíonn uait a bheith ar "
"an eolas faoi ná a chinntiú go n-úsáidtear an fhoirm bhainistíochta taobh "
"istigh den teimpléad. Breathnaímid ar radharc samplach::"

msgid "The ``manage_articles.html`` template might look like this:"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh cuma seo a bheith ar an teimpléad `manage_articles.html``:"

msgid ""
"However there's a slight shortcut for the above by letting the formset "
"itself deal with the management form:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin tá aicearra beag ann don méid thuas trí ligean don fhoirmscar "
"féin déileáil leis an bhfoirm bhainistíochta:"

msgid ""
"The above ends up calling the :meth:`BaseFormSet.render` method on the "
"formset class. This renders the formset using the template specified by "
"the :attr:`~BaseFormSet.template_name` attribute. Similar to forms, by "
"default the formset will be rendered ``as_div``, with other helper methods "
"of ``as_p``, ``as_ul``, and ``as_table`` being available. The rendering of "
"the formset can be customized by specifying the ``template_name`` attribute, "
"or more generally by :ref:`overriding the default template <overriding-built-"
"in-formset-templates>`."
msgstr ""
"Críochnaíonn an méid thuas ag glaoch ar an modh: meth: `BaseFormSet.render` "
"ar an rang formset. Déanann sé seo an tacar foirme ag baint úsáide as an "
"teimpléad a shonraítear leis an tréith: attr: `~BaseFormSet.Template_Name`. "
"Cosúil le foirmeacha, de réir réamhshocraithe déanfar an tacar foirme "
"``as_div``, agus modhanna cúntóra eile ``as_p``, `as_ul``, agus ``as_table`` "
"ar fáil. <overriding-built-in-formset-templates>Is féidir rindreáil an "
"fhoirmshraith a shaincheapadh tríd an tréith ``template_name`` a shonrú, nó "
"níos ginearálta trí:ref: `an teimpléad réamhshocraithe a shárú `."

msgid "Manually rendered ``can_delete`` and ``can_order``"
msgstr "Rinneadh de láimh ``can_delete`` agus ``can_order``"

msgid ""
"If you manually render fields in the template, you can render ``can_delete`` "
"parameter with ``{{ form.DELETE }}``:"
msgstr ""
"Má rindeann tú réimsí de láimh sa teimpléad, is féidir leat paraiméadar "
"``can_delete`` a rinneadh le ``{{form.Delete}}``:"

msgid ""
"Similarly, if the formset has the ability to order (``can_order=True``), it "
"is possible to render it with ``{{ form.ORDER }}``."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, má tá sé de chumas ag an bhfoirm ordú "
"(``can_order=true``), is féidir é a rinneadh le ``{{form.order}}``."

msgid "Using more than one formset in a view"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as níos mó ná tacar foirme amháin i radharc"

msgid ""
"You are able to use more than one formset in a view if you like. Formsets "
"borrow much of its behavior from forms. With that said you are able to use "
"``prefix`` to prefix formset form field names with a given value to allow "
"more than one formset to be sent to a view without name clashing. Let's take "
"a look at how this might be accomplished::"
msgstr ""
"Tá tú in ann níos mó ná tacar foirme amháin a úsáid i radharc más mian leat. "
"Tá foirmeacha ar iasacht cuid mhaith dá iompar ó fhoirmeacha. Agus é sin "
"ráite tá tú in ann ``prefix`` a úsáid chun ainmneacha réimse foirmeacha "
"foirmeacha a bhfuil luach ar leith acu chun ligean níos mó ná tacar foirme "
"amháin a sheoladh chuig amharc gan ainmneacha a chomhrac. Breathnaímid ar an "
"gcaoi a bhféadfaí é seo a chur i gcrích:"

msgid ""
"You would then render the formsets as normal. It is important to point out "
"that you need to pass ``prefix`` on both the POST and non-POST cases so that "
"it is rendered and processed correctly."
msgstr ""
"Ansin déanfá na foirmeacha a rinneadh mar is gnách. Tá sé tábhachtach a chur "
"in iúl gur gá duit ``prefix` a rith ar na cásanna POST agus neamh-POST araon "
"ionas go ndéanfar é a léiriú agus a phróiseáil i gceart."

msgid ""
"Each formset's :ref:`prefix <formset-prefix>` replaces the default ``form`` "
"prefix that's added to each field's ``name`` and ``id`` HTML attributes."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann gach formset's:ref: `réimír `in ionad an réimír réamh <formset-"
"prefix>shocraithe ``foirm ``a chuirtear le tréithe HTML ``ainm`` agus `id`` "
"gach réimse."

msgid "Working with forms"
msgstr "Ag obair le foirmeacha"

msgid "About this document"
msgstr "Maidir leis an doiciméad seo"

msgid ""
"This document provides an introduction to the basics of web forms and how "
"they are handled in Django. For a more detailed look at specific areas of "
"the forms API, see :doc:`/ref/forms/api`, :doc:`/ref/forms/fields`, "
"and :doc:`/ref/forms/validation`."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an doiciméad seo réamhrá ar buneilimintí na bhfoirmeacha "
"gréasáin agus conas a láimhseálfar iad i Django Chun breathnú níos "
"mionsonraithe ar réimsí sonracha de API na bhfoirmeacha, féach:doc: `/ref/"
"forms/api`, :doc: `/ref/forms/fields`, agus:doc: `/ref/forms/validation`."

msgid ""
"Unless you're planning to build websites and applications that do nothing "
"but publish content, and don't accept input from your visitors, you're going "
"to need to understand and use forms."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú ag pleanáil láithreáin ghréasáin agus feidhmchláir a thógáil "
"nach ndéanann aon rud ach ábhar a fhoilsiú, agus nach nglacann sé le "
"hionchur ó do chuairteoirí, beidh ort foirmeacha a thuiscint agus a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Django provides a range of tools and libraries to help you build forms to "
"accept input from site visitors, and then process and respond to the input."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django raon uirlisí agus leabharlanna chun cabhrú leat "
"foirmeacha a thógáil chun glacadh le hionchur ó chuairteoirí an láithreáin, "
"agus ansin an t-ionchur a phróiseáil agus"

msgid "HTML forms"
msgstr "Foirmeacha HTML"

msgid ""
"In HTML, a form is a collection of elements inside ``<form>...</form>`` that "
"allow a visitor to do things like enter text, select options, manipulate "
"objects or controls, and so on, and then send that information back to the "
"server."
msgstr ""
"<form>I HTML, is bailiúchán eilimintí é foirm taobh istigh de ``...</form> "
"``a ligeann do chuairteoir rudaí a dhéanamh mar téacs a iontráil, roghanna a "
"roghnú, rudaí nó rialuithe a ionramháil, agus mar sin de, agus ansin an "
"fhaisnéis sin a sheoladh ar ais chuig an bhfreastalaí."

msgid ""
"Some of these form interface elements - text input or checkboxes - are built "
"into HTML itself. Others are much more complex; an interface that pops up a "
"date picker or allows you to move a slider or manipulate controls will "
"typically use JavaScript and CSS as well as HTML form ``<input>`` elements "
"to achieve these effects."
msgstr ""
"Tá cuid de na heilimintí comhéadain foirme seo - ionchur téacs nó boscaí "
"seiceála - tógtha isteach i HTML féin. Tá daoine eile i bhfad níos casta; de "
"ghnáth úsáidfidh comhéadan a chuireann roghnóir dáta suas nó a ligeann duit "
"sleamhnán a bhogadh nó rialuithe a ionramháil JavaScript agus CSS chomh "
"maith le heilimintí foirme HTML <input>```chun na héifeachtaí seo a bhaint "
"amach."

msgid "As well as its ``<input>`` elements, a form must specify two things:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith lena eilimintí <input>```, ní mór do fhoirm dhá rud a shonrú:"

msgid ""
"*where*: the URL to which the data corresponding to the user's input should "
"be returned"
msgstr ""
"*áite*: an URL ar chóir na sonraí a fhreagraíonn d'ionchur an úsáideora a "
"thabhairt ar ais"

msgid "*how*: the HTTP method the data should be returned by"
msgstr "* cona*: an modh HTTP ba chóir na sonraí a thabhairt ar ais"

msgid ""
"As an example, the login form for the Django admin contains several "
"``<input>`` elements: one of ``type=\"text\"`` for the username, one of "
"``type=\"password\"`` for the password, and one of ``type=\"submit\"`` for "
"the \"Log in\" button. It also contains some hidden text fields that the "
"user doesn't see, which Django uses to determine what to do next."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, tá roinnt eilimintí ```sa fhoirm logála isteach do riarachán "
"Django<input>: ceann de ``type=\"text\"`` don ainm úsáideora, ceann de "
"``type=\"password\"`` don phasfhocal, agus ceann de ``type=\"submit\"`` don "
"chnaipe “Logáil isteach”. Tá roinnt réimsí téacs i bhfolach ann freisin nach "
"bhfeiceann an t-úsáideoir, a úsáideann Django chun a chinneadh cad atá le "
"déanamh ina dhiaidh sin."

msgid ""
"It also tells the browser that the form data should be sent to the URL "
"specified in the ``<form>``’s ``action`` attribute - ``/admin/`` - and that "
"it should be sent using the HTTP mechanism specified by the ``method`` "
"attribute - ``post``."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé leis an mbrabhsálaí freisin gur chóir na sonraí foirme a sheoladh "
"chuig an URL a sh <form>onraítear sa tréith ```` ```` ```` ```` - `/admin/`` "
"- agus gur chóir iad a sheoladh ag baint úsáide as an meicníocht HTTP a "
"shonraítear leis an tréith ``modh`` - `post ``."

msgid ""
"When the ``<input type=\"submit\" value=\"Log in\">`` element is triggered, "
"the data is returned to ``/admin/``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a spreagtar an eilim <input type=\"submit\" value=\"Log in\">int ```, "
"cuirtear na sonraí ar ais chuig ``/admin/``."

msgid "``GET`` and ``POST``"
msgstr "``GET`` agus ``POST ``"

msgid ""
"``GET`` and ``POST`` are the only HTTP methods to use when dealing with "
"forms."
msgstr ""
"Is iad ``GET`` agus `POST ``na modhanna HTTP amháin atá le húsáid agus tú ag "
"déileáil le foirmeacha."

msgid ""
"Django's login form is returned using the ``POST`` method, in which the "
"browser bundles up the form data, encodes it for transmission, sends it to "
"the server, and then receives back its response."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear foirm logála isteach Django ar ais ag baint úsáide as an modh `POST "
"``, ina ndéanann an brabhsálaí sonraí na bhfoirme suas, iad a ionchódú lena "
"tharchur, seolann sé chuig an bhfreastalaí, agus ansin faigheann sé a "
"fhreagra ar ais."

msgid ""
"``GET``, by contrast, bundles the submitted data into a string, and uses "
"this to compose a URL. The URL contains the address where the data must be "
"sent, as well as the data keys and values. You can see this in action if you "
"do a search in the Django documentation, which will produce a URL of the "
"form ``https://docs.djangoproject.com/search/?q=forms&release=1``."
msgstr ""
"I gcodarsnacht leis sin, cuireann `GET`` na sonraí curtha isteach i sreang, "
"agus úsáideann sé seo chun URL a chumadh. Tá an seoladh san URL ina "
"gcaithfear na sonraí a sheoladh, chomh maith leis na heochracha agus na "
"luachanna sonraí. Is féidir leat é seo a fheiceáil i ngníomh má dhéanann tú "
"cuardach sa dhoiciméadú Django, a tháirgfidh URL den fhoirm ``https://"
"docs.djangoproject.com/search/?q=forms&release=1``."

msgid "``GET`` and ``POST`` are typically used for different purposes."
msgstr "Is gnách go n-úsáidtear `GET`` agus `POST ``chun críocha éagsúla."

msgid ""
"Any request that could be used to change the state of the system - for "
"example, a request that makes changes in the database - should use ``POST``. "
"``GET`` should be used only for requests that do not affect the state of the "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir d'aon iarratas a d'fhéadfaí a úsáid chun staid an chórais a athrú - "
"mar shampla, iarratas a dhéanann athruithe sa bhunachar sonraí - `POST ``a "
"úsáid. Níor chóir `GET ``a úsáid ach amháin le haghaidh iarratais nach "
"ndéanann difear do staid an chórais."

msgid ""
"``GET`` would also be unsuitable for a password form, because the password "
"would appear in the URL, and thus, also in browser history and server logs, "
"all in plain text. Neither would it be suitable for large quantities of "
"data, or for binary data, such as an image. A web application that uses "
"``GET`` requests for admin forms is a security risk: it can be easy for an "
"attacker to mimic a form's request to gain access to sensitive parts of the "
"system. ``POST``, coupled with other protections like Django's :doc:`CSRF "
"protection </ref/csrf/>` offers more control over access."
msgstr ""
"Bheadh `GET ``mí-oiriúnach freisin d'fhoirm pasfhocal, toisc go mbeadh an "
"pasfhocal le feiceáil sa URL, agus dá bhrí sin, i stair an bhrabhsálaí agus "
"i logaí freastalaí, go léir i dtéacs simplí. Ní bheadh sé oiriúnach do "
"chainníochtaí móra sonraí, nó do shonraí dénártha, mar shampla íomhá. Is "
"riosca slándála é feidhmchlár gréasáin a úsáideann iarratais `GET ``ar "
"fhoirmeacha riaracháin: is féidir go mbeadh sé éasca d'ionsaitheoir aithris "
"a dhéanamh ar iarratas foirme chun rochtain a fháil ar chodanna íogaire den "
"chóras. Tugann ``POST ``, in éineacht le cosaintí eile cosúil le Django: "
"Doc: `Cosaint CSRF `níos mó smachta ar rochtain </ref/csrf/>."

msgid ""
"On the other hand, ``GET`` is suitable for things like a web search form, "
"because the URLs that represent a ``GET`` request can easily be bookmarked, "
"shared, or resubmitted."
msgstr ""
"Ar an láimh eile, tá `GET`` oiriúnach do rudaí cosúil le foirm chuardaigh "
"gréasáin, toisc gur féidir na URLanna a léiríonn iarratas ``GET`` a "
"leabharmharcáil, a roinnt nó a athchur isteach go héasca."

msgid "Django's role in forms"
msgstr "Ról Django i bhfoirmeacha"

msgid ""
"Handling forms is a complex business. Consider Django's admin, where "
"numerous items of data of several different types may need to be prepared "
"for display in a form, rendered as HTML, edited using a convenient "
"interface, returned to the server, validated and cleaned up, and then saved "
"or passed on for further processing."
msgstr ""
"Is gnó casta é foirmeacha láimhseála. Smaoinigh ar riarachán Django, áit a "
"bhféadfadh go mbeadh gá go leor míreanna sonraí de roinnt cineálacha éagsúla "
"a ullmhú le taispeáint i bhfoirm, a léiriú mar HTML, a chur in eagar ag "
"baint úsáide as comhéadan áisiúil, filleadh ar ais chuig an bhfreastalaí, a "
"bhailíochtú agus a ghlanadh, agus ansin a shábháil nó"

msgid ""
"Django's form functionality can simplify and automate vast portions of this "
"work, and can also do it more securely than most programmers would be able "
"to do in code they wrote themselves."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le feidhmiúlacht fhoirme Django codanna móra den obair seo a "
"shimpliú agus a uathoibriú, agus féadann sé é a dhéanamh níos sábháilte "
"freisin ná mar a bheadh mórchuid na ríomhchláraitheoirí in ann a dhéanamh sa "
"chód a sc"

msgid "Django handles three distinct parts of the work involved in forms:"
msgstr ""
"Láimhseálann Django trí chuid ar leith den obair a bhaineann le foirmeacha:"

msgid "preparing and restructuring data to make it ready for rendering"
msgstr ""
"sonraí a ullmhú agus a athstruchtúrú chun iad a dhéanamh réidh le rindreáil"

msgid "creating HTML forms for the data"
msgstr "foirmeacha HTML a chruthú do na sonraí"

msgid "receiving and processing submitted forms and data from the client"
msgstr ""
"foirmeacha agus sonraí curtha isteach ón gcliant a fháil agus a phróiseáil"

msgid ""
"It is *possible* to write code that does all of this manually, but Django "
"can take care of it all for you."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir aithe* cód a scríobh a dhéanann é seo go léir de láimh, ach is "
"féidir le Django aire a thabhairt dó go léir duit."

msgid "Forms in Django"
msgstr "Foirmeacha i Django"

msgid ""
"We've described HTML forms briefly, but an HTML ``<form>`` is just one part "
"of the machinery required."
msgstr ""
"Tá cur síos déanta againn ar fhoirmeacha HTML go hachomair, ach níl HTML "
"<form>```` ach cuid amháin den innealra a theastaíonn."

msgid ""
"In the context of a web application, 'form' might refer to that HTML "
"``<form>``, or to the Django :class:`Form` that produces it, or to the "
"structured data returned when it is submitted, or to the end-to-end working "
"collection of these parts."
msgstr ""
"I gcomhthéacs iarratais gréasáin, d'fhéadfadh 'foirm' tagairt a dhéanamh don "
"HTML sin ```<form>, nó don Django:Class: `Foirm` a tháirgeann í, nó do na "
"sonraí struchtúrtha ar ais nuair a chuirtear isteach í, nó don bhailiúchán "
"oibre deireadh go deireadh na gcodanna seo."

msgid "The Django :class:`Form` class"
msgstr "An rang Django: Class: `Form`"

msgid ""
"At the heart of this system of components is Django's :class:`Form` class. "
"In much the same way that a Django model describes the logical structure of "
"an object, its behavior, and the way its parts are represented to us, "
"a :class:`Form` class describes a form and determines how it works and "
"appears."
msgstr ""
"I gcroílár an chórais comhpháirteanna seo tá rang Django's:Class: `Form`. Ar "
"an mbealach céanna a dhéanann samhail Django cur síos ar struchtúr "
"loighciúil réada, a iompar, agus an bealach a léirítear a chodanna dúinn, a: "
"aicme: `Foirm` cur síos ar fhoirm agus socraíonn sé conas a oibríonn sé agus "
"a fheictear."

msgid ""
"In a similar way that a model class's fields map to database fields, a form "
"class's fields map to HTML form ``<input>`` elements. (A :class:`ModelForm` "
"maps a model class's fields to HTML form ``<input>`` elements via "
"a :class:`Form`; this is what the Django admin is based upon.)"
msgstr ""
"Ar bhealach cosúil le réimsí rang samhail a léarscáil go réimsí bunachar "
"sonraí, léarscáil réimsí ranga foirme chuig eilimintí foirm HTML <input>```. "
"(A: Aicme: Mapáil `ModelForm `réimsí ranga samhail chuig eilimintí foirm "
"HTML ``` `<input>trí a: class: `Form`; seo a bhfuil riarachán Django "
"bunaithe air.)"

msgid ""
"A form's fields are themselves classes; they manage form data and perform "
"validation when a form is submitted. A :class:`DateField` and "
"a :class:`FileField` handle very different kinds of data and have to do "
"different things with it."
msgstr ""
"Is ranganna iad réimsí foirme iad féin; bainistíonn siad sonraí foirme agus "
"déanann siad bailíochtú nuair a chuirtear foirm isteach. A: Aicme: "
"Láimhseálann `DateField` agus a:class: `FileField` cineálacha an-éagsúla "
"sonraí agus caithfidh siad rudaí éagsúla a dhéanamh leis."

msgid ""
"A form field is represented to a user in the browser as an HTML \"widget\" - "
"a piece of user interface machinery. Each field type has an appropriate "
"default :doc:`Widget class </ref/forms/widgets/>`, but these can be "
"overridden as required."
msgstr ""
"Léirítear réimse foirme d'úsáideoir sa bhrabhsálaí mar “giuirléid” HTML - "
"píosa innealra comhéadan úsáideora. Tá réamhshocrú cuí ag gach cineál "
"réimse: doc: `Aicme giuirléid`, ach is féidir iad seo a shárú </ref/forms/"
"widgets/> de réir mar is gá."

msgid "Instantiating, processing, and rendering forms"
msgstr "Foirmeacha a thionscnamh, a phróiseáil agus a rindreáil"

msgid "When rendering an object in Django, we generally:"
msgstr "Agus réad á rindreáil i Django, is ginearálta déanaimid:"

msgid "get hold of it in the view (fetch it from the database, for example)"
msgstr "faigh greim air sa radharc (faigh ón mbunachar sonraí é, mar shampla)"

msgid "pass it to the template context"
msgstr "cuir chuig comhthéacs an teimpléid é"

msgid "expand it to HTML markup using template variables"
msgstr "é a leathnú go marcáil HTML ag úsáid athróga teimpléad"

msgid ""
"Rendering a form in a template involves nearly the same work as rendering "
"any other kind of object, but there are some key differences."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá i gceist le foirm a rindreáil i dteimpléad beagnach an obair "
"chéanna le haon chineál réad eile a rindreáil, ach tá roinnt "
"príomhdhifríochtaí ann."

msgid ""
"In the case of a model instance that contained no data, it would rarely if "
"ever be useful to do anything with it in a template. On the other hand, it "
"makes perfect sense to render an unpopulated form - that's what we do when "
"we want the user to populate it."
msgstr ""
"I gcás samhail samhail nach raibh aon sonraí ann, is annamh a bheadh sé "
"úsáideach riamh aon rud a dhéanamh leis i dteimpléad. Ar an láimh eile, "
"bíonn ciall foirfe foirm neamhdhaonra a thabhairt - sin an rud a dhéanaimid "
"nuair is mian linn go ndéanfadh an t-úsáideoir é a dhaonrú."

msgid ""
"So when we handle a model instance in a view, we typically retrieve it from "
"the database. When we're dealing with a form we typically instantiate it in "
"the view."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin nuair a láimhseálann muid samhail samhail i radharc, is gnách go "
"mbímid é a aisghabháil ón mbunachar sonraí. Nuair a bhíonn muid ag déileáil "
"le foirm de ghnáth déanaimid í sa radharc."

msgid ""
"When we instantiate a form, we can opt to leave it empty or prepopulate it, "
"for example with:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a dhéanaimid foirm a chruthú, is féidir linn a roghnú í a fhágáil "
"folamh nó í a réamhdhíonrú, mar shampla le:"

msgid ""
"data from a saved model instance (as in the case of admin forms for editing)"
msgstr ""
"sonraí ó shampla samhail shábháilte (mar atá i gcás foirmeacha riaracháin le "
"haghaidh eagarthóireachta)"

msgid "data that we have collated from other sources"
msgstr "sonraí atá curtha le chéile againn ó fhoinsí eile"

msgid "data received from a previous HTML form submission"
msgstr "sonraí a fuarthas ó aighneacht foirm HTML roimhe seo"

msgid ""
"The last of these cases is the most interesting, because it's what makes it "
"possible for users not just to read a website, but to send information back "
"to it too."
msgstr ""
"Is é an ceann deireanach de na cásanna seo an ceann is suimiúla, toisc gurb "
"é an rud a fhágann gur féidir d'úsáideoirí ní amháin láithreán gréasáin a "
"léamh, ach faisnéis a sheoladh ar ais chuige freisin."

msgid "Building a form"
msgstr "Foirm a thógáil"

msgid "The work that needs to be done"
msgstr "An obair is gá a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"Suppose you want to create a simple form on your website, in order to obtain "
"the user's name. You'd need something like this in your template:"
msgstr ""
"Cuir i gcás gur mhaith leat foirm shimplí a chruthú ar do shuíomh Gréasáin, "
"d'fhonn ainm an úsáideora a fháil. Bheadh rud éigin mar seo ag teastáil uait "
"i do theimpléad:"

msgid ""
"This tells the browser to return the form data to the URL ``/your-name/``, "
"using the ``POST`` method. It will display a text field, labeled \"Your name:"
"\", and a button marked \"OK\". If the template context contains a "
"``current_name`` variable, that will be used to pre-fill the ``your_name`` "
"field."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé seo don bhrabhsálaí sonraí na bhfoirme a thabhairt ar ais chuig "
"an URL ``/your-ainm/``, ag baint úsáide as an modh ``POST ``. Taispeánfaidh "
"sé réimse téacs, lipéadaithe “Do ainm:”, agus cnaipe marcáilte “OK”. Má tá "
"athróg ``current_name`` sa chomhthéacs teimpléid, úsáidfear é sin chun an "
"réimse ``your_name`` réamh-líonadh."

msgid ""
"You'll need a view that renders the template containing the HTML form, and "
"that can supply the ``current_name`` field as appropriate."
msgstr ""
"Beidh amharc ag teastáil uait a léiríonn an teimpléad ina bhfuil an fhoirm "
"HTML, agus is féidir leis an réimse ``current_name`` a sholáthar de réir mar "
"is cuí."

msgid ""
"When the form is submitted, the ``POST`` request which is sent to the server "
"will contain the form data."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuirtear an fhoirm isteach, beidh sonraí na foirme san iarratas "
"``POST ``a sheoltar chuig an bhfreastalaí."

msgid ""
"Now you'll also need a view corresponding to that ``/your-name/`` URL which "
"will find the appropriate key/value pairs in the request, and then process "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Anois beidh radharc ag teastáil uait freisin a fhreagraíonn don URL ``/"
"d'ainm/`` sin a gheobhaidh na péirí eochair/luacha cuí san iarratas, agus "
"ansin iad a phróiseáil."

msgid ""
"This is a very simple form. In practice, a form might contain dozens or "
"hundreds of fields, many of which might need to be prepopulated, and we "
"might expect the user to work through the edit-submit cycle several times "
"before concluding the operation."
msgstr ""
"Is foirm an-simplí é seo. Go praiticiúil, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh mórán nó na "
"céadta réimsí i bhfoirm, a d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh go leor acu a réamhdhaonrú, "
"agus b'fhéidir go bhfuilimid ag súil go n-oibreoidh an t-úsáideoir tríd an "
"timthriall eagarthóireach-chur isteach arís agus arís eile"

msgid ""
"We might require some validation to occur in the browser, even before the "
"form is submitted; we might want to use much more complex fields, that allow "
"the user to do things like pick dates from a calendar and so on."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir go mbeidh roinnt bailíochtaithe ag teastáil uainn sa bhrabhsálaí, "
"fiú sula gcuirtear an fhoirm isteach; b'fhéidir gur mhaith linn réimsí i "
"bhfad níos casta a úsáid, a ligeann don úsáideoir rudaí a dhéanamh cosúil le "
"dátaí a roghnú ó fhéilire agus mar sin de."

msgid ""
"At this point it's much easier to get Django to do most of this work for us."
msgstr ""
"Ag an bpointe seo tá sé i bhfad níos éasca Django a fháil chun an chuid is "
"mó den obair seo a dhéanamh dúinn."

msgid "Building a form in Django"
msgstr "Foirm a thógáil i Django"

msgid "The :class:`Form` class"
msgstr "An rang: aicme: `Foirm`"

msgid ""
"We already know what we want our HTML form to look like. Our starting point "
"for it in Django is this:"
msgstr ""
"Tá a fhios againn cheana féin cén chuma atá againn ar ár bhfoirm HTML. Is é "
"seo an pointe tosaigh atá againn dó i Django:"

msgid ""
"This defines a :class:`Form` class with a single field (``your_name``). "
"We've applied a human-friendly label to the field, which will appear in the "
"``<label>`` when it's rendered (although in this case, "
"the :attr:`~Field.label` we specified is actually the same one that would be "
"generated automatically if we had omitted it)."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn sé seo a: aicme: `Foirm` aicme le réimse amháin "
"(``your_name``). Chuireamar lipéad atá cairdiúil don duine i bhfeidhm ar an "
"réimse, a bheidh le feiceáil sa <label>```nuair a rinneofar é (cé sa chás "
"seo, is é an:attr: `~field.label` a shonraíomar an ceann céanna i ndáiríre a "
"ghinteofaí go huathoibríoch dá bhfágfaimis é)."

msgid ""
"The field's maximum allowable length is defined "
"by :attr:`~CharField.max_length`. This does two things. It puts a "
"``maxlength=\"100\"`` on the HTML ``<input>`` (so the browser should prevent "
"the user from entering more than that number of characters in the first "
"place). It also means that when Django receives the form back from the "
"browser, it will validate the length of the data."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear uasfhad incheadaithe an réimse ag: attr: "
"`~charfield.max_Length`. Déanann sé seo dhá rud. Cuireann sé ``maxlength "
"=\"100\"`` ar an HTML ``<input>`` (mar sin ba chóir don bhrabhsálaí cosc ar "
"an úsáideoir níos mó ná an líon sin carachtair a iontráil sa chéad áit). "
"Ciallaíonn sé freisin nuair a fhaigheann Django an fhoirm ar ais ón "
"mbrabhsálaí, go ndéanfaidh sé fad na sonraí a bhailíochtú."

msgid ""
"A :class:`Form` instance has an :meth:`~Form.is_valid()` method, which runs "
"validation routines for all its fields. When this method is called, if all "
"fields contain valid data, it will:"
msgstr ""
"A: Class: Tá modh: meth: `~form.is_valid () `ag sampla `Form`, a ritheann "
"gnáthaimh bailíochtaithe dá réimsí go léir. Nuair a thugtar ar an modh seo, "
"má tá sonraí bailí i ngach réimse, beidh sé:"

msgid "return ``True``"
msgstr "tuairisceán ``True``"

msgid "place the form's data in its :attr:`~Form.cleaned_data` attribute."
msgstr "cuir sonraí na foirme ina tréith: attr: `~form.Cleaned_Data`."

msgid "The whole form, when rendered for the first time, will look like:"
msgstr ""
"Beidh cuma ar an bhfoirm iomlán, nuair a rindreáiltear den chéad uair, mar "
"seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Note that it **does not** include the ``<form>`` tags, or a submit button. "
"We'll have to provide those ourselves in the template."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach n-áirítear ion** na clibeanna ``<form>``, nó cnaipe "
"cuir isteach. Beidh orainn iad siúd féin a sholáthar sa teimpléad."

msgid "The view"
msgstr "An radharc"

msgid ""
"Form data sent back to a Django website is processed by a view, generally "
"the same view which published the form. This allows us to reuse some of the "
"same logic."
msgstr ""
"Déantar sonraí foirme a sheoltar ar ais chuig suíomh Gréasáin Django a "
"phróiseáil le dearcadh, de ghnáth an dearcadh céanna a d'fhoilsigh an fhoirm "
"Ligeann sé seo dúinn cuid den loighic chéanna a athúsáid."

msgid ""
"To handle the form we need to instantiate it in the view for the URL where "
"we want it to be published:"
msgstr ""
"Chun an fhoirm a láimhseáil ní mór dúinn í a chur isteach sa radharc don URL "
"áit ar mhaith linn go bhfoilsíodh í:"

msgid ""
"If we arrive at this view with a ``GET`` request, it will create an empty "
"form instance and place it in the template context to be rendered. This is "
"what we can expect to happen the first time we visit the URL."
msgstr ""
"Má thagann muid ar an radharc seo le hiarratas ``GET ``, cruthóidh sé sampla "
"foirme folamh agus cuirfidh sé i gcomhthéacs an teimpléid atá le léiriú. Seo "
"an rud is féidir linn a bheith ag súil go dtarlóidh an chéad uair a "
"thugaimid cuairt ar an URL."

msgid ""
"If the form is submitted using a ``POST`` request, the view will once again "
"create a form instance and populate it with data from the request: ``form = "
"NameForm(request.POST)`` This is called \"binding data to the form\" (it is "
"now a *bound* form)."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear an fhoirm isteach ag baint úsáide as iarratas ``POST ``, "
"cruthóidh an dearcadh sampla foirme arís agus líonfaidh sé le sonraí ón "
"iarratas: ``form = AinmForm (request.post)`` Tugtar “sonraí ceangailteach "
"leis an bhfoirm” air seo (foirme*teorann* í anois)."

msgid ""
"We call the form's ``is_valid()`` method; if it's not ``True``, we go back "
"to the template with the form. This time the form is no longer empty "
"(*unbound*) so the HTML form will be populated with the data previously "
"submitted, where it can be edited and corrected as required."
msgstr ""
"Glaoimid modh ``is_valid () ``ar an bhfoirm; mura bhfuil sé ``True``, téimid "
"ar ais chuig an teimpléad leis an bhfoirm. An uair seo níl an fhoirm folamh "
"a thuilleadh (*untheor*) mar sin déanfar na sonraí a cuireadh isteach roimhe "
"seo sa fhoirm HTML, áit ar féidir í a chur in eagar agus a cheartú de réir "
"mar is gá."

msgid ""
"If ``is_valid()`` is ``True``, we'll now be able to find all the validated "
"form data in its ``cleaned_data`` attribute. We can use this data to update "
"the database or do other processing before sending an HTTP redirect to the "
"browser telling it where to go next."
msgstr ""
"Más é ``is_valid () ```True``, beidh muid in ann anois na sonraí foirme "
"bailíochtaithe go léir a fháil ina tréith ``cleaned_data``. Is féidir linn "
"na sonraí seo a úsáid chun an bunachar sonraí a nuashonrú nó próiseáil eile "
"a dhéanamh sula seolfaimid atreorú HTTP chuig an mbrabhsálaí ag insint dó cá "
"háit a rachaidh"

msgid "The template"
msgstr "An teimpléad"

msgid "We don't need to do much in our ``name.html`` template:"
msgstr "Ní gá dúinn mórán a dhéanamh inár dteimpléad ``name.html``:"

msgid ""
"All the form's fields and their attributes will be unpacked into HTML markup "
"from that ``{{ form }}`` by Django's template language."
msgstr ""
"Déanfar réimsí uile na foirme agus a dtréithe a dhíphacáil isteach i marcáil "
"HTML ón ``{{form}}`` sin ag teanga teimpléad Django."

msgid "Forms and Cross Site Request Forgery protection"
msgstr "Foirmeacha agus Iarratas ar Trasláithreán Cosaint ar Fhol"

msgid ""
"Django ships with an easy-to-use :doc:`protection against Cross Site Request "
"Forgeries </ref/csrf>`. When submitting a form via ``POST`` with CSRF "
"protection enabled you must use the :ttag:`csrf_token` template tag as in "
"the preceding example. However, since CSRF protection is not directly tied "
"to forms in templates, this tag is omitted from the following examples in "
"this document."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django le cosaint éasca le húsáid:doc: `cosaint i gcoinne "
"Forgeasaithe Iarratais Tras-Láithreach' </ref/csrf>. Nuair a chuirtear foirm "
"isteach trí `POST ``le cosaint CSRF cumasaithe ní mór duit an chlib "
"teimpléad:ttag: `csrf_token` a úsáid mar atá sa sampla roimhe seo. Mar sin "
"féin, ós rud é nach bhfuil cosaint CSRF ceangailte go díreach le foirmeacha "
"i dteimpléid, fágtar an chlib seo as na samplaí seo a leanas sa doiciméad "
"seo."

msgid "HTML5 input types and browser validation"
msgstr "Cineálacha ionchuir HTML5 agus bailíochtú brabh"

msgid ""
"If your form includes a :class:`~django.forms.URLField`, "
"an :class:`~django.forms.EmailField` or any integer field type, Django will "
"use the ``url``, ``email`` and ``number`` HTML5 input types. By default, "
"browsers may apply their own validation on these fields, which may be "
"stricter than Django's validation. If you would like to disable this "
"behavior, set the ``novalidate`` attribute on the ``form`` tag, or specify a "
"different widget on the field, like :class:`TextInput`."
msgstr ""
"Má chuimsíonn d'fhoirm a:class: `~django.forms.URLField`, an:class: "
"`~django.forms.emailField` nó aon chineál réimse sláireach, úsáidfidh Django "
"na cineálacha ionchuir ``url ``, `email`` agus ``Number`` HTML5. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, féadfaidh brabhsálaithe a bhailíochtú féin a chur i "
"bhfeidhm ar na réimsí seo, a d'fhéadfadh a bheith níos déine ná bailíochtú "
"Django. Más mian leat an t-iompar seo a dhíchumasú, socraigh an tréith "
"``novalidate`` ar an gclib ``foirm ``, nó sonraigh giuirléid dhifriúil ar an "
"réimse, cosúil:class: `textInput`."

msgid ""
"We now have a working web form, described by a Django :class:`Form`, "
"processed by a view, and rendered as an HTML ``<form>``."
msgstr ""
"<form>Tá foirm gréasáin oibre againn anois, a thuairiscítear ag Django: "
"Class: `Form`, a phróiseáiltear ag radharc, agus a rindreáiltear mar HTML "
"```."

msgid ""
"That's all you need to get started, but the forms framework puts a lot more "
"at your fingertips. Once you understand the basics of the process described "
"above, you should be prepared to understand other features of the forms "
"system and ready to learn a bit more about the underlying machinery."
msgstr ""
"Sin gach rud a theastaíonn uait chun tosú, ach cuireann creat na "
"bhfoirmeacha i bhfad níos mó ar do mhéar. Nuair a thuigeann tú buneilimintí "
"an phróisis a thuairiscítear thuas, ba chóir duit a bheith réidh chun "
"gnéithe eile den chóras foirmeacha a thuiscint agus réidh chun beagán níos "
"mó a fhoghlaim faoin innealra bunúsach."

msgid "More about Django :class:`Form` classes"
msgstr "Tuilleadh faoi ranganna Django:Class: `Form`"

msgid ""
"All form classes are created as subclasses of "
"either :class:`django.forms.Form` or :class:`django.forms.ModelForm`. You "
"can think of ``ModelForm`` as a subclass of ``Form``. ``Form`` and "
"``ModelForm`` actually inherit common functionality from a (private) "
"``BaseForm`` class, but this implementation detail is rarely important."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaítear gach rang foirme mar fho-aicmí de: aicme: `django.forms.form` "
"nó:class: `Django.Forms.ModelForm`. Is féidir leat smaoineamh ar "
"``ModelForm`` mar fho-aicme de ``Form``. Tá feidhmiúlacht choiteann ag "
"``Foirm ``agus `ModelForm`` i ndáiríre ó rang ``BaseForm ``(príobháideach), "
"ach is annamh a bhíonn an mionsonraí cur chun feidhme seo tábhachtach."

msgid "Models and Forms"
msgstr "Múnlaí agus Foirmeacha"

msgid ""
"In fact if your form is going to be used to directly add or edit a Django "
"model, a :doc:`ModelForm </topics/forms/modelforms>` can save you a great "
"deal of time, effort, and code, because it will build a form, along with the "
"appropriate fields and their attributes, from a ``Model`` class."
msgstr ""
"Déanta na fírinne má úsáidfear d'fhoirm chun samhail Django a chur leis nó a "
"chur in eagar go díreach, is féidir le a:doc: `ModelForm` go leor ama, "
"iarrachta agus cód a shábháil duit, toisc go dtógfaidh sé foirm, mar aon "
"leis na réimsí cuí </topics/forms/modelforms> agus a gcuid tréithe, ó rang "
"``Samhail ``."

msgid "Bound and unbound form instances"
msgstr "Cásanna foirmeacha ceangailte agus gan cheangal"

msgid ""
"The distinction between :ref:`ref-forms-api-bound-unbound` is important:"
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-idirdhealú idir: ref: `ref-forms-api-bound-unbord` tábhachtach:"

msgid ""
"An unbound form has no data associated with it. When rendered to the user, "
"it will be empty or will contain default values."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon sonraí a bhaineann le foirm neamhcheangailte leis. Nuair a dhéanfar "
"é don úsáideoir, beidh sé folamh nó beidh luachanna réamhshocraithe ann."

msgid ""
"A bound form has submitted data, and hence can be used to tell if that data "
"is valid. If an invalid bound form is rendered, it can include inline error "
"messages telling the user what data to correct."
msgstr ""
"Tá sonraí curtha isteach ag foirm cheangailte, agus dá bhrí sin is féidir í "
"a úsáid chun a rá an bhfuil na sonraí sin bailí. Má dhéantar foirm "
"cheangailte neamhbhailí a léiriú, féadfaidh teachtaireachtaí earráide inlíne "
"a áireamh ann ag insint don úsáideoir na sonraí"

msgid ""
"The form's :attr:`~Form.is_bound` attribute will tell you whether a form has "
"data bound to it or not."
msgstr ""
"Inseoidh an tréith foirm 's:attr: `~form.is_bound` duit an bhfuil sonraí "
"ceangailte ag foirm nó nach bhfuil."

msgid "More on fields"
msgstr "Tuilleadh ar réimsí"

msgid ""
"Consider a more useful form than our minimal example above, which we could "
"use to implement \"contact me\" functionality on a personal website:"
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh ar fhoirm níos úsáideach ná ár sampla íosta thuas, a d'fhéadfaimis "
"a úsáid chun feidhmiúlacht “déan teagmháil liom” a chur i bhfeidhm ar "
"shuíomh Gréasáin pearsanta:"

msgid ""
"Our earlier form used a single field, ``your_name``, a :class:`CharField`. "
"In this case, our form has four fields: ``subject``, ``message``, ``sender`` "
"and ``cc_myself``. :class:`CharField`, :class:`EmailField` "
"and :class:`BooleanField` are just three of the available field types; a "
"full list can be found in :doc:`/ref/forms/fields`."
msgstr ""
"D'úsáid ár bhfoirm níos luaithe réimse amháin, ``your_name``, a: class: "
"`Charfield`. Sa chás seo, tá ceithre réimse ag ár bhfoirm: ``ábhar ``, "
"`teachtaireacht``, `seoltóir ``agus ``cc_myself``. :class: "
"`Charfield`, :class: `emailField` agus:class: `BooleanField` ach trí cinn de "
"na cineálacha réimse atá ar fáil; is féidir liosta iomlán a fháil in:doc: `/"
"ref/forms/fields`."

msgid "Widgets"
msgstr "Giuirléidí"

msgid ""
"Each form field has a corresponding :doc:`Widget class </ref/forms/widgets/"
">`, which in turn corresponds to an HTML form widget such as ``<input "
"type=\"text\">``."
msgstr ""
"</ref/forms/widgets/> <input type=\"text\">Tá comhfhreagrach ag gach réimse "
"foirme: doc: `Class giuirléid`, a fhreagraíonn do ghuirléid fhoirme HTML mar "
"````."

msgid ""
"In most cases, the field will have a sensible default widget. For example, "
"by default, a :class:`CharField` will have a :class:`TextInput` widget, that "
"produces an ``<input type=\"text\">`` in the HTML. If you needed "
"``<textarea>`` instead, you'd specify the appropriate widget when defining "
"your form field, as we have done for the ``message`` field."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna, beidh giuirléid réamhshocraithe ciallmhar sa réimse "
"<input type=\"text\">Mar shampla, de réir réamhshocraithe, beidh a: class: "
"`textInput` giuirléid ag a: class: `Charfield`, a tháirgeann ```` sa HTML. "
"Más gá duit ``<textarea>`` ina ionad sin, shonrófá an giuirléid chuí agus do "
"réimse foirme á shainiú agat, mar a rinneamar don réimse ``teachtaireacht ``."

msgid "Field data"
msgstr "Sonraí réimse"

msgid ""
"Whatever the data submitted with a form, once it has been successfully "
"validated by calling ``is_valid()`` (and ``is_valid()`` has returned "
"``True``), the validated form data will be in the ``form.cleaned_data`` "
"dictionary. This data will have been nicely converted into Python types for "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Cibé na sonraí a chuirtear isteach le foirm, nuair a bheidh siad "
"bailíochtaithe go rathúil trí ghlaoch ar ``is_valid () `(agus ``is_valid ()` "
"tar éis ``True`` ar ais), beidh sonraí na bhfoirme bailíochtaithe sa "
"fhoclóir ``form.cleaned_data``. Déanfar na sonraí seo a thiontú go deas i "
"gcineálacha Python duit."

msgid ""
"You can still access the unvalidated data directly from ``request.POST`` at "
"this point, but the validated data is better."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar na sonraí neamhbhailíochtaithe go díreach "
"ó ``Request.post`` ag an bpointe seo, ach tá na sonraí bailíochtaithe níos "
"fearr."

msgid ""
"In the contact form example above, ``cc_myself`` will be a boolean value. "
"Likewise, fields such as :class:`IntegerField` and :class:`FloatField` "
"convert values to a Python ``int`` and ``float`` respectively."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla foirme teagmhála thuas, is luach boolean é `cc_myself``. Mar an "
"gcéanna, déanann réimsí mar: class: `IntegerField` agus:class: `FloatField` "
"luachanna a thiontú go Python `int`` agus ``float`` faoi seach."

msgid ""
"Here's how the form data could be processed in the view that handles this "
"form:"
msgstr ""
"Seo conas a d'fhéadfaí na sonraí foirme a phróiseáil sa dearcadh a "
"láimhseálann an fhoirm seo:"

msgid "For more on sending email from Django, see :doc:`/topics/email`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faoi ríomhphost a sheoladh ó Django, féach: doc: `/"
"topics/email`."

msgid ""
"Some field types need some extra handling. For example, files that are "
"uploaded using a form need to be handled differently (they can be retrieved "
"from ``request.FILES``, rather than ``request.POST``). For details of how to "
"handle file uploads with your form, see :ref:`binding-uploaded-files`."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn roinnt láimhseála breise ó roinnt cineálacha Mar shampla, ní mór "
"comhaid a uaslódáiltear ag baint úsáide as foirm a láimhseáil ar bhealach "
"difriúil (is féidir iad a aisghabháil ó ``Request.Files``, seachas "
"``request.post``). Le haghaidh sonraí maidir le conas uaslódálacha comhad a "
"láimhseáil le d'fhoirm, féach:ref: `binding-uploaded-files`."

msgid "Working with form templates"
msgstr "Ag obair le teimpléid fhoir"

msgid ""
"All you need to do to get your form into a template is to place the form "
"instance into the template context. So if your form is called ``form`` in "
"the context, ``{{ form }}`` will render its ``<label>`` and ``<input>`` "
"elements appropriately."
msgstr ""
"Níl le déanamh agat chun d'fhoirm a chur i dteimpléad ná an tsampla foirme a "
"chur i gcomhthéacs an teimpléid. <label><input>Mar sin má thugtar ``foirm "
"``sa chomhthéacs ar d'fhoirm, déanfaidh`` {{form}} ``a eilimintí`` ``agus`` "
"```a ghnéithe go cuí."

msgid "Additional form template furniture"
msgstr "Troscán teimpléad foirm bh"

msgid ""
"Don't forget that a form's output does *not* include the surrounding "
"``<form>`` tags, or the form's ``submit`` control. You will have to provide "
"these yourself."
msgstr ""
"Ná déan dearmad go gcuimsíonn aschur foirme*ní* na clibeanna "
"``máguaird<form>, nó rialú ```aighneacht' na foirme. Beidh ort iad seo a "
"sholáthar duit féin."

msgid "Reusable form templates"
msgstr "Teimpléid foirme in-ath"

msgid ""
"The HTML output when rendering a form is itself generated via a template. "
"You can control this by creating an appropriate template file and setting a "
"custom :setting:`FORM_RENDERER` to use "
"that :attr:`~django.forms.renderers.BaseRenderer.form_template_name` site-"
"wide. You can also customize per-form by overriding the "
"form's :attr:`~django.forms.Form.template_name` attribute to render the form "
"using the custom template, or by passing the template name directly "
"to :meth:`.Form.render`."
msgstr ""
"Gintear an t-aschur HTML agus foirm á rindreáil air féin trí theimpléad. Is "
"féidir leat é seo a rialú trí chomhad teimpléad iomchuí a chruthú agus "
"saincheap:setting: `FORM_RENDER` a shocrú chun sean:attr: "
"`~django.forms.renderers.baserenderer.form_template_name` a úsáid ar fud an "
"láithreáin. Is féidir leat foirm a shaincheapadh freisin tríd an tréith "
"foirm 's:attr: `~django.forms.form.template_name` a shárú chun an fhoirm a "
"léiriú ag baint úsáide as an teimpléad saincheaptha, nó trí ainm an "
"teimpléid a chur go díreach chuig:meth: `.form.render`."

msgid ""
"The example below will result in ``{{ form }}`` being rendered as the output "
"of the ``form_snippet.html`` template."
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar an sampla thíos beidh ``{{form}}`` a rinneadh mar aschur an "
"teimpléad ``form_snippet.html``."

msgid "In your templates:"
msgstr "I do theimpléid:"

msgid "Then you can configure the :setting:`FORM_RENDERER` setting:"
msgstr "Ansin is féidir leat an socrú: setting: `FORM_RENDER` a chumrú:"

msgid "``settings.py``"
msgstr "``settings.py``"

msgid "… or for a single form::"
msgstr "... nó le haghaidh foirm amháin:"

msgid ""
"… or for a single render of a form instance, passing in the template name to "
"the :meth:`.Form.render`. Here's an example of this being used in a view::"
msgstr ""
"... nó le haghaidh rindreáil aonair de shampla foirme, ag cur isteach ainm "
"an teimpléid chuig an:meth: `.form.render`. Seo sampla de seo a úsáidtear i "
"radharc:"

msgid "See :ref:`ref-forms-api-outputting-html` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Féach:ref: `ref-forms-api-outputting-html` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Reusable field group templates"
msgstr "Teimpléid grúpa allamuigh"

msgid ""
"Each field is available as an attribute of the form, using "
