"`~django.db.models.filefield`:"

msgid "Uploading multiple files"
msgstr "Comhad iolracha a uaslódáil"

msgid ""
"If you want to upload multiple files using one form field, create a subclass "
"of the field's widget and set its ``allow_multiple_selected`` class "
"attribute to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat comhad iolracha a uaslódáil ag baint úsáide as réimse foirme "
"amháin, cruthaigh fo-aicme de ghuirléid an réimse agus socraigh a tréith "
"aicme `allow_multiple_selected` go ``True``."

msgid ""
"In order for such files to be all validated by your form (and have the value "
"of the field include them all), you will also have to subclass "
"``FileField``. See below for an example."
msgstr ""
"Ionas go mbeidh comhaid den sórt sin go léir a bhailíochtú ag d'fhoirm (agus "
"go mbeidh luach an réimse iad go léir san áireamh), beidh ort fo-aicme "
"“FileField” a dhéanamh freisin. Féach thíos le haghaidh sampla."

msgid "Multiple file field"
msgstr "Réimse comhad iolrach"

msgid ""
"Django is likely to have a proper multiple file field support at some point "
"in the future."
msgstr ""
"Is dócha go mbeidh tacaíocht cheart réimse comhad iolrach ag Django ag "
"pointe éigin sa todhchaí."

msgid ""
"Then override the ``form_valid()`` method of "
"your :class:`~django.views.generic.edit.FormView` subclass to handle "
"multiple file uploads:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin athraigh an modh ``form_valid () ``de d':class: "
"`~django.views.generic.edit.formView` chun uaslódálacha comhad iolracha a "
"láimhseáil:"

msgid ""
"This will allow you to handle multiple files at the form level only. Be "
"aware that you cannot use it to put multiple files on a single model "
"instance (in a single field), for example, even if the custom widget is used "
"with a form field related to a model ``FileField``."
msgstr ""
"Ligfidh sé seo duit comhad iolracha a láimhseáil ag leibhéal na foirme "
"amháin. Bí ar an eolas nach féidir leat é a úsáid chun comhad iolracha a "
"chur ar shampla samhail amháin (i réimse amháin), mar shampla, fiú má "
"úsáidtear an giuirléid saincheaptha le réimse foirme a bhaineann le samhail "
"``FileField`."

msgid "Upload Handlers"
msgstr "Uaslódáil Handlers"

msgid ""
"When a user uploads a file, Django passes off the file data to an *upload "
"handler* -- a small class that handles file data as it gets uploaded. Upload "
"handlers are initially defined in the :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_HANDLERS` "
"setting, which defaults to::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a uaslódálann úsáideoir comhad, cuireann Django sonraí na gcomhad "
"chuig*láimhseálaí uaslódálaí* - rang beag a láimhseálann sonraí comhaid de "
"réir mar a uaslódáltar iad. Sainmhínítear láimhseálaithe uaslódála ar dtús "
"sa socrú:setting: `FILE_UPLOAD_HANDLERS`, a réamhshocraíonn:"

msgid ""
"Together :class:`MemoryFileUploadHandler` "
"and :class:`TemporaryFileUploadHandler` provide Django's default file upload "
"behavior of reading small files into memory and large ones onto disk."
msgstr ""
"Le chéile: Class: `MemoryFileUploadHandler` agus: class: "
"`TemporaryFileUploadHandler` soláthraíonn iompar uaslódála comhaid "
"réamhshocraithe Django maidir le comhaid bheaga a léamh isteach i gcuimhne "
"agus cinn mhóra ar an diosca."

msgid ""
"You can write custom handlers that customize how Django handles files. You "
"could, for example, use custom handlers to enforce user-level quotas, "
"compress data on the fly, render progress bars, and even send data to "
"another storage location directly without storing it locally. "
"See :ref:`custom_upload_handlers` for details on how you can customize or "
"completely replace upload behavior."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat láimhseálaithe saincheaptha a scríobh a shaincheapann an "
"chaoi a láimhseálann D'fhéadfá, mar shampla, láimhseálaithe saincheaptha a "
"úsáid chun cuótaí ar leibhéal an úsáideora a fhorfheidhmiú, sonraí a "
"chomhbhrú ar an eitilt, barraí dul chun cinn a léiriú, agus fiú sonraí a "
"sheoladh chuig áit stórála eile go díreach gan Féach: ref: "
"`custom_upload_handlers` le haghaidh sonraí maidir le conas is féidir leat "
"iompar uaslódála a shaincheapadh nó a athsholáthar go hiomlán."

msgid "Where uploaded data is stored"
msgstr "Nuair a stóráiltear sonraí uaslódá"

msgid "Before you save uploaded files, the data needs to be stored somewhere."
msgstr ""
"Sula sábhálann tú comhaid uaslódáilte, ní mór na sonraí a stóráil áit éigin."

msgid ""
"By default, if an uploaded file is smaller than 2.5 megabytes, Django will "
"hold the entire contents of the upload in memory. This means that saving the "
"file involves only a read from memory and a write to disk and thus is very "
"fast."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, má tá comhad uaslódáilte níos lú ná 2.5 meigabyte, "
"coinneoidh Django ábhar iomlán an uaslódála i gcuimhne. Ciallaíonn sé seo "
"nach mbíonn ach léamh ón gcuimhne agus scríobh chuig diosca i gceist leis an "
"gcomhad a shábháil agus dá bhrí sin tá sé an-tapa."

msgid ""
"However, if an uploaded file is too large, Django will write the uploaded "
"file to a temporary file stored in your system's temporary directory. On a "
"Unix-like platform this means you can expect Django to generate a file "
"called something like ``/tmp/tmpzfp6I6.upload``. If an upload is large "
"enough, you can watch this file grow in size as Django streams the data onto "
"disk."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má tá comhad uaslódáilte ró-mhór, scríobhfaidh Django an "
"comhad uaslódáilte chuig comhad sealadach atá stóráilte in eolaire sealadach "
"do chórais. Ar ardán cosúil le Unix ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat a "
"bheith ag súil go nginfidh Django comhad ar a dtugtar rud éigin cosúil le ``/"
"tmpzfp6i6.upload``. Má tá uaslódáil mór go leor, is féidir leat féachaint ar "
"an gcomhad seo ag fás i méid de réir mar a shruthlaíonn Django na sonraí ar "
"an diosca."

msgid ""
"These specifics -- 2.5 megabytes; ``/tmp``; etc. -- are \"reasonable "
"defaults\" which can be customized as described in the next section."
msgstr ""
"Is “réamhshocruithe réasúnacha” iad na sonraíochtaí seo - 2.5 meigabyte; ``/"
"tmp``; srl. - is féidir iad a shaincheapadh mar a thuairiscítear sa chéad "
"chuid eile."

msgid "Changing upload handler behavior"
msgstr "Iompar láimhseála uaslódála"

msgid ""
"There are a few settings which control Django's file upload behavior. "
"See :ref:`File Upload Settings <file-upload-settings>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla socrú ann a rialaíonn iompar uaslódála comhad Django. Féach: Ref: "
"`Socruithe Uaslódála Comhad <file-upload-settings>`le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Modifying upload handlers on the fly"
msgstr "Láimhseálóirí uaslódála a mhodhnú"

msgid ""
"Sometimes particular views require different upload behavior. In these "
"cases, you can override upload handlers on a per-request basis by modifying "
"``request.upload_handlers``. By default, this list will contain the upload "
"handlers given by :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_HANDLERS`, but you can modify the "
"list as you would any other list."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta teastaíonn iompar uaslódála éagsúla Sna cásanna seo, is féidir "
"leat láimhseálaithe uaslódála a shárú ar bhonn in aghaidh iarratais trí "
"``request.upload_handlers` a mhodhnú. De réir réamhshocraithe, beidh na "
"láimhseálaithe uaslódála a thugtar ar:setting: `FILE_UPLOAD_HANDLERS` sa "
"liosta seo, ach is féidir leat an liosta a mhodhnú mar a dhéanfá aon liosta "
"eile."

msgid ""
"For instance, suppose you've written a ``ProgressBarUploadHandler`` that "
"provides feedback on upload progress to some sort of AJAX widget. You'd add "
"this handler to your upload handlers like this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, cuir i gcás go bhfuil “ProgressbarUploadHandler” scríofa agat a "
"sholáthraíonn aiseolas ar dhul chun cinn a uaslódáil chuig cineál éigin "
"giuirléid AJAX. Chuirfeá an láimhseálaí seo le do láimhseálaithe uaslódála "
"mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Using ``list.insert()``, as shown above, ensures that the progress bar "
"handler is placed at the beginning of the list. Since upload handlers are "
"executed in order, this placement guarantees that the progress bar handler "
"runs before the default handlers, allowing it to track progress across the "
"entire upload."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to replace the upload handlers completely, you can assign a new "
"list::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat na láimhseálaithe uaslódála a chur in ionad go hiomlán, is "
"féidir leat liosta nua a shannadh:"

msgid ""
"You can only modify upload handlers *before* accessing ``request.POST`` or "
"``request.FILES`` -- it doesn't make sense to change upload handlers after "
"upload handling has already started. If you try to modify "
"``request.upload_handlers`` after reading from ``request.POST`` or "
"``request.FILES`` Django will throw an error."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir leat láimhseálaithe uaslódála a mhodhnú ach roimh* roimh rochtain "
"a fháil ar ``Request.Post`` nó ``Request.Files`` - níl ciall láimhseálaithe "
"uaslódála a athrú tar éis do láimhseáil uaslódála tosú cheana féin. Má "
"dhéanann tú iarracht ``request.upload_handlers`` a mhodhnú tar éis léamh ó "
"``Request.post`` nó ``Request.Files`` caithfidh Django earráid."

msgid ""
"Thus, you should always modify uploading handlers as early in your view as "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, ba cheart duit láimhseálaithe uaslódála a mhodhnú chomh luath i "
"do thuairim agus is féidir."

msgid ""
"Also, ``request.POST`` is accessed "
"by :class:`~django.middleware.csrf.CsrfViewMiddleware` which is enabled by "
"default. This means you will need to "
"use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` on your view to allow "
"you to change the upload handlers.  You will then need to "
"use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` on the function that "
"actually processes the request.  Note that this means that the handlers may "
"start receiving the file upload before the CSRF checks have been done. "
"Example code::"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin, tá rochtain ag `request.post`` ag: class: "
"`~django.middleware.csrf.csrfViewMiddleware` atá cumasaithe de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Ciallaíonn sé seo go mbeidh ort: func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exemt` a úsáid ar do thuairim chun "
"ligean duit na láimhseálaithe uaslódála a athrú. Ansin beidh ort: func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` a úsáid ar an bhfeidhm a "
"phróiseálann an iarratas i ndáiríre. Tabhair faoi deara go gciallaíonn sé "
"seo go bhféadfadh na láimhseálaithe tosú ag fáil an uaslódáil comhad sula "
"ndéantar na seiceálacha CSRF. Cód sampla::"

msgid ""
"If you are using a class-based view, you will need to "
"use :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` on "
"its :meth:`~django.views.generic.base.View.dispatch` method "
"and :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` on the method that "
"actually processes the request. Example code::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá radharc bunaithe ar rang á úsáid agat, beidh ort: func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` a úsáid ara:meth: "
"`~django.views.generic.base.view.dispch` modh agus:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` ar an modh próiseálann an "
"iarratas i ndáiríre. Cód sampla::"

msgid "Generic views"
msgstr "Tuairimí cineálacha"

msgid "See :doc:`/ref/class-based-views/index`."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/ref/rang-bhunaithe tuairim/innéacs `."

msgid "Handling HTTP requests"
msgstr "Láimhseáil iarratais HTTP"

msgid "Information on handling HTTP requests in Django:"
msgstr "Eolas maidir le hiarrataí HTTP a láimhseáil i Django:"

msgid "Middleware"
msgstr "Meán-earraí"

msgid ""
"Middleware is a framework of hooks into Django's request/response "
"processing. It's a light, low-level \"plugin\" system for globally altering "
"Django's input or output."
msgstr ""
"Is creat crúcaí é Middleware i bpróiseáil iarrata/freagartha Django. Is "
"córas “breiseán” éadrom, ar leibhéal íseal é chun ionchur nó aschur Django a "
"athrú go domhanda."

msgid ""
"Each middleware component is responsible for doing some specific function. "
"For example, Django includes a middleware "
"component, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`, "
"that associates users with requests using sessions."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach comhpháirt middleware freagrach as feidhm ar leith a dhéanamh. Mar "
"shampla, cuimsíonn Django comhpháirt middleware, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`, a "
"chomhcheanglaíonn úsáideoirí le hiarratais ag baint úsáide as seisiúin."

msgid ""
"This document explains how middleware works, how you activate middleware, "
"and how to write your own middleware. Django ships with some built-in "
"middleware you can use right out of the box. They're documented in "
"the :doc:`built-in middleware reference </ref/middleware>`."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo conas a oibríonn middleware, conas a "
"ghníomhachaíonn tú middleware, agus conas do mheánware féin a scríobh. "
"Loingíonn Django le roinnt earraí lárnacha ionsuite is féidir leat a úsáid "
"díreach as an mbosca. Tá siad doiciméadaithe san: doc: `tagairt middleware "
"ionsuite '</ref/middleware>."

msgid "Writing your own middleware"
msgstr "Do mheán-earraí féin a scríobh"

msgid ""
"A middleware factory is a callable that takes a ``get_response`` callable "
"and returns a middleware. A middleware is a callable that takes a request "
"and returns a response, just like a view."
msgstr ""
"Is é monarcha earraí meánghlaoithe a thógann glaoch ``get_response`` agus a "
"thugann middleware ar ais. Is féidir glaoch é middleware a ghlacann iarratas "
"agus a thugann freagra ar ais, díreach cosúil le radharc."

msgid "A middleware can be written as a function that looks like this::"
msgstr "Is féidir middleware a scríobh mar fheidhm a bhfuil cuma seo air:"

msgid ""
"Or it can be written as a class whose instances are callable, like this::"
msgstr ""
"Nó is féidir é a scríobh mar rang a bhfuil a gcásanna inghlaonta, mar seo:"

msgid ""
"The ``get_response`` callable provided by Django might be the actual view "
"(if this is the last listed middleware) or it might be the next middleware "
"in the chain. The current middleware doesn't need to know or care what "
"exactly it is, just that it represents whatever comes next."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh gurb é an glaoch ``get_response`` a sholáthraíonn Django an "
"dearcadh iarbhír (más é seo an middleware liostaithe deireanach) nó "
"d'fhéadfadh gurb é an chéad lár-earraí eile sa slabhra é. Ní gá don mheán-"
"earraí reatha a bheith ar an eolas nó aire a thabhairt cad é go díreach é, "
"ach go léiríonn sé cibé rud a thagann ina dhiaidh sin."

msgid ""
"The above is a slight simplification -- the ``get_response`` callable for "
"the last middleware in the chain won't be the actual view but rather a "
"wrapper method from the handler which takes care of applying :ref:`view "
"middleware <view-middleware>`, calling the view with appropriate URL "
"arguments, and applying :ref:`template-response <template-response-"
"middleware>` and :ref:`exception <exception-middleware>` middleware."
msgstr ""
"<template-response-middleware><exception-middleware>Is simplíocht bheag é an "
"méid thuas - ní é an `get_response`` a ghlaoch don mheán deireanach sa "
"slabhra an dearcadh iarbhír ach modh fillte ón láimhseálaí a thugann aire "
"d'iarrat:ref: `view middleware `, ag glaoch an dearcadh le hargóintí URL "
"cuí, agus iarrth:ref: `teimplé-response` agus:ref: `eisceacht <view-"
"middleware>`middleware."

msgid ""
"Middleware can either support only synchronous Python (the default), only "
"asynchronous Python, or both. See :ref:`async-middleware` for details of how "
"to advertise what you support, and know what kind of request you are getting."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir le Middleware tacú le Python sioncronach amháin (an "
"réamhshocraithe), ach Python asincrónach, nó an dá cheann. Féach: ref: "
"`async-middleware` le haghaidh sonraí faoin méid a thacaíonn tú a fhógairt, "
"agus a fhios agat cén cineál iarratais atá á fháil agat."

msgid "Middleware can live anywhere on your Python path."
msgstr "Is féidir le middleware maireachtáil áit ar bith ar do chonair Python."

msgid "``__init__(get_response)``"
msgstr "``__init__ (faigh_response) ``"

msgid ""
"Middleware factories must accept a ``get_response`` argument. You can also "
"initialize some global state for the middleware. Keep in mind a couple of "
"caveats:"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh monarchana middleware glacadh le hargóint ``get_response``. Is "
"féidir leat stát dhomhanda éigin a thionscnamh don middleware freisin. "
"Coinnigh i gcuimhne cúpla rabhadh:"

msgid ""
"Django initializes your middleware with only the ``get_response`` argument, "
"so you can't define ``__init__()`` as requiring any other arguments."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django tús le do middleware gan ach an argóint ``get_response``, "
"mar sin ní féidir leat ``__init__ () ``a shainiú mar a theastaíonn aon "
"argóintí eile."

msgid ""
"Unlike the ``__call__()`` method which is called once per request, "
"``__init__()`` is called only *once*, when the web server starts."
msgstr ""
"Murab ionann agus an modh ``__call__ () ``ar a dtugtar uair amháin in "
"aghaidh an iarratais, ní thugtar ``__init__ ()`` ach *uaire*, nuair a "
"thosaíonn an freastalaí gréasáin."

msgid "Marking middleware as unused"
msgstr "Meán-earraí a mharcáil mar neamhúsá"

msgid ""
"It's sometimes useful to determine at startup time whether a piece of "
"middleware should be used. In these cases, your middleware's ``__init__()`` "
"method may raise :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.MiddlewareNotUsed`. Django "
"will then remove that middleware from the middleware process and log a debug "
"message to the :ref:`django-request-logger` logger when :setting:`DEBUG` is "
"``True``."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta bíonn sé úsáideach a chinneadh ag am tosaithe an gcaithfear píosa "
"meán-earraí a úsáid. Sna cásanna seo, féadfaidh modh ``__init__ () ``do "
"middleware a ardó:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.middlewareNotUsed`. Ansin "
"bainfidh Django an middleware sin ón bpróiseas middleware agus logálfaidh "
"teachtaireacht dífhabhtaithe chuig an logger: ref: `django-request-logger` "
"nuai:setting: `DEBUG` ``True``."

msgid "Activating middleware"
msgstr "Middleware a ghníomhachtú"

msgid ""
"To activate a middleware component, add it to the :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` list "
"in your Django settings."
msgstr ""
"Chun comhpháirt middleware a ghníomhachtú, cuir é leis an liosta:setting: "
"`MIDDLEWARE` i do shocruithe Django."

msgid ""
"In :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`, each middleware component is represented by a "
"string: the full Python path to the middleware factory's class or function "
"name. For example, here's the default value created by :djadmin:`django-"
"admin startproject <startproject>`::"
msgstr ""
"In: SETTING: `MIDDLEWARE`, léiríonn teaghrán gach comhpháirt middleware: an "
"cosán iomlán Python chuig ainm ranga nó feidhm an mhonarcha middleware. "
"<startproject>Mar shampla, seo an luach réamhshocraithe a chruthaí:djadmin: "
"`django-admin startproject `:"

msgid ""
"A Django installation doesn't require any middleware — :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` "
"can be empty, if you'd like — but it's strongly suggested that you at least "
"use :class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware`."
msgstr ""
"Ní theastaíonn aon middleware ó shuiteáil Django -: setting: Is féidir le "
"`MIDDLEWARE` a bheith folamh, más mian leat - ach moltar go láidir go n-"
"úsáideann tú: class: `~django.middleware.common.commonMiddleware` ar a "
"laghad."

msgid ""
"The order in :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` matters because a middleware can depend "
"on other middleware. For "
"instance, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware` "
"stores the authenticated user in the session; therefore, it must run "
"after :class:`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware`. "
"See :ref:`middleware-ordering` for some common hints about ordering of "
"Django middleware classes."
msgstr ""
"Tá tábhacht ag an ordú in:setting: `MIDDLEWARE` toisc gur féidir le "
"middleware a bheith ag brath ar mheán-earraí eile. Mar shampla, "
"stóráilíonn :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleWare` an t-úsáideoir "
"fíordheimhnithe sa seisiún; dá bhrí sin, ní mór dó rith tar éis: :class: "
"`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.sessionMiddleware`. Féach: ref: "
"`middleware-ording` le haghaidh roinnt leideanna coitianta maidir le "
"ranganna meán-earraí Django a ordú."

msgid "Middleware order and layering"
msgstr "Ordú agus sraitheadh lár-earraí"

msgid ""
"During the request phase, before calling the view, Django applies middleware "
"in the order it's defined in :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`, top-down."
msgstr ""
"Le linn na céime iarratais, sula nglaonn sé ar an radharc, cuireann Django "
"middleware i bhfeidhm san ord a shainmhínítear é in:setting: `MIDDLEWARE`, "
"barr anuas."

msgid ""
"You can think of it like an onion: each middleware class is a \"layer\" that "
"wraps the view, which is in the core of the onion. If the request passes "
"through all the layers of the onion (each one calls ``get_response`` to pass "
"the request in to the next layer), all the way to the view at the core, the "
"response will then pass through every layer (in reverse order) on the way "
"back out."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat smaoineamh air mar oinniún: is “ciseal” é gach rang "
"middleware a fhilleann an radharc, atá i gcroílár an oinniúin. Má théann an "
"t-iarratas trí na sraitheanna uile den oinniún (glaonn gach ceann ar "
"``get_response`` chun an t-iarratas a chur isteach chuig an gcéad chiseal "
"eile), an bealach ar fad go dtí an radharc ag croílár, rachaidh an freagra "
"ansin trí gach sraith (in ord droim) ar an mbealach ar ais amach."

msgid ""
"If one of the layers decides to short-circuit and return a response without "
"ever calling its ``get_response``, none of the layers of the onion inside "
"that layer (including the view) will see the request or the response. The "
"response will only return through the same layers that the request passed in "
"through."
msgstr ""
"Má chinneann ceann de na sraitheanna gearrchiorcad a dhéanamh agus freagra a "
"thabhairt ar ais gan a `get_response`` a ghlaoch riamh, ní fheicfidh aon "
"cheann de na sraitheanna den oinniún taobh istigh den chiseal sin (lena n-"
"áirítear an radharc) an iarraidh ná an freagra. Ní thabharfaidh an freagra "
"ar ais ach tríd na sraitheanna céanna a chuir an t-iarratas isteach tríd."

msgid "Other middleware hooks"
msgstr "Crúcaí meán-earraí eile"

msgid ""
"Besides the basic request/response middleware pattern described earlier, you "
"can add three other special methods to class-based middleware:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis an bpatrún lár-earraí iarrata/freagartha bunúsach a "
"thuairiscítear níos luaithe, is féidir leat trí mhodh speisialta eile a chur "
"le middleware rang-bhunaithe:"

msgid "``process_view()``"
msgstr "``próise_amharc () ``"

msgid ""
"``request`` is an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object. ``view_func`` is "
"the Python function that Django is about to use. (It's the actual function "
"object, not the name of the function as a string.) ``view_args`` is a list "
"of positional arguments that will be passed to the view, and ``view_kwargs`` "
"is a dictionary of keyword arguments that will be passed to the view. "
"Neither ``view_args`` nor ``view_kwargs`` include the first view argument "
"(``request``)."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``request`` ná: aicme: `~django.http.httpRequest` réad. Is é "
"``view_func`` an fheidhm Python atá ar tí Django a úsáid. (Is é an réad "
"feidhme iarbhír é, ní ainm na feidhme mar shreang.) Is liosta d'argóintí "
"seasaimh é ``view_args`` a chuirfear ar aghaidh chuig an dearcadh, agus is "
"foclóir argóintí eochairfhocal é ``view_kwargs`` a chuirfear chuig an "
"dearcadh. Ní chuimsíonn ``view_args`` ná `view_kwargs`` an argóint chéad "
"amharc (``request``)."

msgid "``process_view()`` is called just before Django calls the view."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ar ``process_view () ``díreach sula nglaonn Django ar an radharc."

msgid ""
"It should return either ``None`` or an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` "
"object. If it returns ``None``, Django will continue processing this "
"request, executing any other ``process_view()`` middleware and, then, the "
"appropriate view. If it returns an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` "
"object, Django won't bother calling the appropriate view; it'll apply "
"response middleware to that :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` and return "
"the result."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir dó réad ``None`` nó an:class: `~django.http.httpResponse` a "
"thabhairt ar ais. Má fhilleann sé ``None ``, leanfaidh Django ar aghaidh ag "
"próiseáil an iarratais seo, ag forghníomhú aon mheánware ``process_view ()`` "
"eile agus, ansin, an dearcadh cuí. Má fhilleann sé ruda:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponse` réad, ní chuirfidh Django isteach ar an radharc "
"cuí a ghlaoch; cuirfidh sé middleware freagartha i bhfeidhm ar ain:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponse` agus cuirfidh sé an toradh ar ais."

msgid ""
"Accessing :attr:`request.POST <django.http.HttpRequest.POST>` inside "
"middleware before the view runs or in ``process_view()`` will prevent any "
"view running after the middleware from being able to :ref:`modify the upload "
"handlers for the request <modifying_upload_handlers_on_the_fly>`, and should "
"normally be avoided."
msgstr ""
"<modifying_upload_handlers_on_the_fly>Accessing:attr: `Request.post "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.POST>`taobh istigh de mheán-earraí sula ritheann an "
"radharc nó i ``process_view () ``cosc ar aon radharc atá ag rith tar éis an "
"middleware a bheith in ann: ref: `na láimhseálaithe uaslódála don iarraidh a "
"mhodhnú, agus ba chóir é a sheachaint de ghnáth."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.middleware.csrf.CsrfViewMiddleware` class can be "
"considered an exception, as it provides "
"the :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` "
"and :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` decorators which "
"allow views to explicitly control at what point the CSRF validation should "
"occur."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an rang:Class: `~django.middleware.csrf.csrfviewMiddleware` a "
"mheas ina eisceacht, toisc go soláthraíonn sé na:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_exempt` agus:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.csrf.csrf_protect` a cheadaíonn tuairimí go "
"sainráite rialú ag cén pointe ba chóir go dtarlódh bailíochtú CSRF."

msgid "``process_exception()``"
msgstr "``próise_eisceacht () ``"

msgid ""
"``request`` is an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object. ``exception`` is "
"an ``Exception`` object raised by the view function."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``request`` ná: aicme: `~django.http.httpRequest` réad. Is réad "
"````Eisceacht' é ``eisceacht' a ardaíonn an fheidhm amharc."

msgid ""
"Django calls ``process_exception()`` when a view raises an exception. "
"``process_exception()`` should return either ``None`` or "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` object. If it returns "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` object, the template response and "
"response middleware will be applied and the resulting response returned to "
"the browser. Otherwise, :ref:`default exception handling <error-views>` "
"kicks in."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn Django ar ``process_exception () ``nuair a ardaíonn dearcadh "
"eisceacht. Ba chóir go bhfaighidh ``process_exception () ``réad ``None`` nó "
"ruda:class: `~django.http.httpResponse` a thabhairt ar ais. Má fhilleann sé "
"ruda:class: `~django.http.httpResponse` réad, cuirfear an freagra teimpléid "
"agus an lámhleabhair freagartha i bhfeidhm agus cuirfear an freagra mar "
"thoradh air sin ar ais chuig an mbrabhsálaí. Seachas sin, tosaíonn :ref: "
"`láimhseáil eisceachta réamhshocrai <error-views>the `isteach."

msgid ""
"Again, middleware are run in reverse order during the response phase, which "
"includes ``process_exception``. If an exception middleware returns a "
"response, the ``process_exception`` methods of the middleware classes above "
"that middleware won't be called at all."
msgstr ""
"Arís, reáchtáiltear middleware in ord droim le linn na céime freagartha, "
"lena n-áirítear ``process_exception`. Má thugann meán-earraí eisceachta "
"freagra ar ais, ní ghlaofar ar chor ar chor ar bith ar na modhanna "
"`process_exception` de na ranganna middleware thuas an middleware sin."

msgid "``process_template_response()``"
msgstr "``próise_teimpléad_fhreagra () ``"

msgid ""
"``request`` is an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object. ``response`` is "
"the :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` object (or "
"equivalent) returned by a Django view or by a middleware."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``request`` ná: aicme: `~django.http.httpRequest` réad. Is é `freagra "
"``an réad: :class: `~django.template.response.templateResponse` réad (nó "
"coibhéis) a chuirtear ar ais ag radharc Django nó ag middleware."

msgid ""
"``process_template_response()`` is called just after the view has finished "
"executing, if the response instance has a ``render()`` method, indicating "
"that it is a :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` or "
"equivalent."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ``process_template_response () ``díreach tar éis don amharc a bheith "
"críochnaithe a chur i bhfeidhm, má tá modh `render ()`` ag an gcás "
"freagartha, ag léiriú gurb é a:class: "
"`~django.template.response.templateResponse` nó coibhéiseach."

msgid ""
"It must return a response object that implements a ``render`` method. It "
"could alter the given ``response`` by changing ``response.template_name`` "
"and ``response.context_data``, or it could create and return a brand-"
"new :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` or equivalent."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh sé réad freagartha a thabhairt ar ais a chuireann modh `render`` i "
"bhfeidhm. D'fhéadfadh sé an ``freagra`` a athrú trí "
"`response.template_name`` agus `response.context_data`` a athrú, nó "
"d'fhéadfadh sé branda nua:class: "
"`~django.template.response.templateResponse` nó coibhéis a chruthú agus a "
"thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"You don't need to explicitly render responses -- responses will be "
"automatically rendered once all template response middleware has been called."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá duit freagraí a thabhairt go sainráite - déanfar freagraí a thabhairt "
"go huathoibríoch nuair a bheidh meán-earraí freagartha teimpléid uile glaoch."

msgid ""
"Middleware are run in reverse order during the response phase, which "
"includes ``process_template_response()``."
msgstr ""
"Reáchtáiltear middleware in ord droim le linn na céime freagartha, lena n-"
"áirítear ``process_template_response () ``."

msgid "Dealing with streaming responses"
msgstr "Déileáil le freagraí sruthú"

msgid ""
"Unlike :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`, :class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse` "
"does not have a ``content`` attribute. As a result, middleware can no longer "
"assume that all responses will have a ``content`` attribute. If they need "
"access to the content, they must test for streaming responses and adjust "
"their behavior accordingly::"
msgstr ""
"Unlike:class: `~django.http.httpResponse`, :class: `~django.http.níl tréith "
"``content`` ag `~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse`. Mar thoradh air sin, ní "
"féidir le middleware glacadh leis a thuilleadh go mbeidh tréith ``ábhar ``ag "
"gach freagra. Má theastaíonn rochtain uathu ar an ábhar, ní mór dóibh "
"freagraí sruthú a thástáil agus a n-iompar a choigeartú dá réir:"

msgid ""
"``streaming_content`` should be assumed to be too large to hold in memory. "
"Response middleware may wrap it in a new generator, but must not consume it. "
"Wrapping is typically implemented as follows::"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir glacadh leis go bhfuil `streaming_content`` ró-mhór le coinneáil i "
"gcuimhne. Féadfaidh meán-earraí freagartha é a fhilleadh i ngineadóir nua, "
"ach níor cheart dó é a ithe. Is iondúil go gcuirtear timfhilleadh i bhfeidhm "
"mar seo"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse` allows both synchronous and "
"asynchronous iterators. The wrapping function must match. "
"Check :attr:`StreamingHttpResponse.is_async "
"<django.http.StreamingHttpResponse.is_async>` if your middleware needs to "
"support both types of iterator."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse` ceadaíonn athraitheoirí "
"sioncrónach agus asincrónach araon. Caithfidh an fheidhm timfhillte "
"meaitseáil <django.http.StreamingHttpResponse.is_async>Seiceáil: attr: "
"`StreamInghttPresponse.is_async `más gá do mheán-earraí tacú leis an dá "
"chineál athraitheora."

msgid ""
"Django automatically converts exceptions raised by the view or by middleware "
"into an appropriate HTTP response with an error status code. :ref:`Certain "
"exceptions <error-views>` are converted to 4xx status codes, while an "
"unknown exception is converted to a 500 status code."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn Django eisceachtaí arna ardú ag an radharc nó ag middleware go "
"huathoibríoch ina fhreagairt HTTP cuí le cód stádais earráide. :ref: Déantar "
"`eisceachtaí áirithe <error-views>`a thiontú go cóid stádais 4xx, agus "
"déantar eisceacht anaithnid a thiontú go cód stádais 500."

msgid ""
"This conversion takes place before and after each middleware (you can think "
"of it as the thin film in between each layer of the onion), so that every "
"middleware can always rely on getting some kind of HTTP response back from "
"calling its ``get_response`` callable. Middleware don't need to worry about "
"wrapping their call to ``get_response`` in a ``try/except`` and handling an "
"exception that might have been raised by a later middleware or the view. "
"Even if the very next middleware in the chain raises "
"an :class:`~django.http.Http404` exception, for example, your middleware "
"won't see that exception; instead it will get "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` object with "
"a :attr:`~django.http.HttpResponse.status_code` of 404."
msgstr ""
"Tarlaíonn an tiontú seo roimh agus tar éis gach middleware (is féidir leat "
"smaoineamh air mar an scannán tanaí idir gach sraith den oinniún), ionas gur "
"féidir le gach middleware brath i gcónaí ar chineál éigin freagra HTTP a "
"fháil ar ais ó a `get_response`` glaoch inghlaonta. Ní gá go mbeadh buartha "
"a bheith buartha faoi a nglao chuig `get_response`` a fhilleadh i `triacht/"
"except`` agus eisceacht a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ardaithe ag middleware nó an "
"dearcadh níos déanaí a láimhseáil. Fiú má ardaíonn an chéad earraí eile sa "
"slabhra eisceacht: Class: `~django.http.http404`, mar shampla, ní fheicfidh "
"do mheán-earraí an eisceacht sin; ina ionad sin gheobhaidh sé réad: "
"`~django.http.http.httpResponse` le a:attr: `~django.http.http.http.code` de "
"404."

msgid ""
"You can set :setting:`DEBUG_PROPAGATE_EXCEPTIONS` to ``True`` to skip this "
"conversion and propagate exceptions upward."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat socrú:setting: `DEBUG_PROPAGATE_EXCEPTIONS` go ``True`` chun "
"an tiontú seo a scipeáil agus eisceachtaí a iomadú aníos."

msgid ""
"Middleware can support any combination of synchronous and asynchronous "
"requests. Django will adapt requests to fit the middleware's requirements if "
"it cannot support both, but at a performance penalty."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le Middleware tacú le haon teaglaim d'iarratais sioncrónach agus "
"asincrónach. Cuirfidh Django iarratais in oiriúint chun freastal ar "
"riachtanais an middleware mura féidir leis tacú leis an dá cheann, ach ag "
"pionós feidhmíochta."

msgid ""
"By default, Django assumes that your middleware is capable of handling only "
"synchronous requests. To change these assumptions, set the following "
"attributes on your middleware factory function or class:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, glacann Django leis nach bhfuil do middleware in "
"ann ach iarratais sioncrónacha a láimhseáil. Chun na toimhdeanna seo a "
"athrú, socraigh na tréithe seo a leanas ar do fheidhm nó rang monarchan "
"middleware:"

msgid ""
"``sync_capable`` is a boolean indicating if the middleware can handle "
"synchronous requests. Defaults to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Is boolean é ``sync_capable`` a thugann le fios an féidir leis an meán-"
"earraí iarratais sioncrónach a láimhseáil. Réamhshocraithe go ``True``."

msgid ""
"``async_capable`` is a boolean indicating if the middleware can handle "
"asynchronous requests. Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Is boolean é `async_capable`` a thugann le fios an féidir leis an meán-"
"earraí iarratais asincrónacha a láimhseáil. Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid ""
"If your middleware has both ``sync_capable = True`` and ``async_capable = "
"True``, then Django will pass it the request without converting it. In this "
"case, you can work out if your middleware will receive async requests by "
"checking if the ``get_response`` object you are passed is a coroutine "
"function, using ``asgiref.sync.iscoroutinefunction``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``sync_enable = True`` agus ``async_enable = True`` araon ag do "
"middleware, ansin rachaidh Django an t-iarratas air gan é a thiontú. Sa chás "
"seo, is féidir leat oibriú amach an bhfaighidh do mheán-earraí iarratais "
"async trí sheiceáil an bhfuil feidhm coroutine an réad ``get_response`` a "
"chuirtear ar rith ort, ag baint úsáide as "
"``asgiref.sync.iscoroutinefunction``."

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.decorators`` module "
"contains :func:`~django.utils.decorators.sync_only_middleware`, :func:`~django.utils.decorators.async_only_middleware`, "
"and :func:`~django.utils.decorators.sync_and_async_middleware` decorators "
"that allow you to apply these flags to middleware factory functions."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modúl ``django.utils.decorators ``: func: "
"`~django.utils.decorators.sync_only_middleware`, :func: "
"`~django.utils.decorators.async_only_middleware`, agus:func: "
"`~django.utils.decorators.sync_and_async_middleware' `maisitheoirí a ligeann "
"duit na bratacha seo a chur i bhfeidhm ar fheidhmeanna monarchan meánearraí."

msgid ""
"The returned callable must match the sync or async nature of the "
"``get_response`` method. If you have an asynchronous ``get_response``, you "
"must return a coroutine function (``async def``)."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh an t-inghlaoch a fhilleadh a mheaitseáil le nádúr sioncrónaithe nó "
"async an mhodha ``get_response``. Má tá `get_response`` asincrónach agat, ní "
"mór duit feidhm coroutine a thabhairt ar ais (``async def``)."

msgid ""
"``process_view``, ``process_template_response`` and ``process_exception`` "
"methods, if they are provided, should also be adapted to match the sync/"
"async mode. However, Django will individually adapt them as required if you "
"do not, at an additional performance penalty."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir modhanna ``process_view``, `process_template_response`` agus "
"``process_exception``, má chuirtear ar fáil iad, a oiriúnú freisin chun an "
"modh sionc/async a mheaitseáil. Mar sin féin, déanfaidh Django iad a oiriúnú "
"ina n-aonar de réir mar is gá mura ndéanann tú, ag pionós feidhmíochta "
"breise."

msgid ""
"Here's an example of how to create a middleware function that supports both::"
msgstr ""
"Seo sampla de conas feidhm middleware a chruthú a thacaíonn leis an dá "
"cheann:"

msgid ""
"If you declare a hybrid middleware that supports both synchronous and "
"asynchronous calls, the kind of call you get may not match the underlying "
"view. Django will optimize the middleware call stack to have as few sync/"
"async transitions as possible."
msgstr ""
"Má dhearbhíonn tú meán-earraí hibrideach a thacaíonn le glaonna sioncrónacha "
"agus asincrónacha araon, b'fhéidir nach n-oireann an cineál glaonna a "
"gheobhaidh tú leis an radharc bunúsach. Déanfaidh Django an staca glaonna "
"middleware a bharrfheabhsú chun an oiread aistrithe sionc/async agus is "
"féidir a bheith aige."

msgid ""
"Thus, even if you are wrapping an async view, you may be called in sync mode "
"if there is other, synchronous middleware between you and the view."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, fiú má tá radharc async á fhilleadh agat, féadfar glaoch ort i "
"mód sioncrónaithe má tá meán-earraí sioncrónach eile idir tú féin agus an "
"radharc."

msgid ""
"When using an asynchronous class-based middleware, you must ensure that "
"instances are correctly marked as coroutine functions::"
msgstr ""
"Agus meán-earraí aicme asincrónach á úsáid agat, ní mór duit a chinntiú go "
"ndéantar cásanna a mharcáil i gceart mar fheidhmeanna coroutine:"

msgid "Upgrading pre-Django 1.10-style middleware"
msgstr "Meán-earraí i stíl réamh-Django 1.10 a uasghrádú"

msgid ""
"Django provides ``django.utils.deprecation.MiddlewareMixin`` to ease "
"creating middleware classes that are compatible with "
"both :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` and the old ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, and support "
"synchronous and asynchronous requests. All middleware classes included with "
"Django are compatible with both settings."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django ``Django.Utils.DEPRECATION.MIDDLEWAREMIXIN`` chun "
"ranganna middleware a chruthú atá comhoiriúnach leis an mbeach:setting: "
"`MIDDLEWARE` agus an sean-``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES` a éascú, agus tacú le "
"hiarratais sioncrónach agus asincrónach. Tá gach rang middleware atá san "
"áireamh le Django comhoiriúnach leis an dá shocrú."

msgid ""
"The mixin provides an ``__init__()`` method that requires a ``get_response`` "
"argument and stores it in ``self.get_response``."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an mixin modh ``__init__ () ``a éilíonn argóint "
"``get_response`` agus a stóráilíonn sé i ``self.get_response``."

msgid "The ``__call__()`` method:"
msgstr "An modh ``__call__ () ``:"

msgid "Calls ``self.process_request(request)`` (if defined)."
msgstr "Glaonna ```self.process_request (request) ``(má shainmhínítear)."

msgid ""
"Calls ``self.get_response(request)`` to get the response from later "
"middleware and the view."
msgstr ""
"Glaonna ar ``self.get_response (request) ``chun an freagra a fháil ó mheán-"
"earraí níos déanaí agus an radharc."

msgid "Calls ``self.process_response(request, response)`` (if defined)."
msgstr ""
"Glaonna ```self.process_response (iarratas, freagra) ``(má shainmhínítear)."

msgid "Returns the response."
msgstr "Tugann an freagra ar ais."

msgid ""
"If used with ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, the ``__call__()`` method will never be "
"used; Django calls ``process_request()`` and ``process_response()`` directly."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáidtear é le `MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, ní úsáidfear an modh ``__call__ () "
"``riamh; glaonn Django ``process_request ()`` agus ``process_response () "
"``go díreach."

msgid ""
"In most cases, inheriting from this mixin will be sufficient to make an old-"
"style middleware compatible with the new system with sufficient backwards-"
"compatibility. The new short-circuiting semantics will be harmless or even "
"beneficial to the existing middleware. In a few cases, a middleware class "
"may need some changes to adjust to the new semantics."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna, is leor oidhreacht ón meascán seo chun meán-earraí "
"sean-stíl a dhéanamh comhoiriúnach leis an gcóras nua le comhoiriúnacht "
"leordhóthanach cúl. Beidh an séimeantaic gearrchiorcaid nua neamhdhíobhálach "
"nó fiú tairbheach don mheán-earraí atá ann cheana. I gcúpla cás, b'fhéidir "
"go mbeadh roinnt athruithe ag teastáil ó rang middleware chun dul in "
"oiriúint don shéimeantaic nua."

msgid ""
"These are the behavioral differences between using :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` and "
"``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``:"
msgstr ""
"Seo iad na difríochtaí iompraíochta idir úsáid: setting: `MIDDLEWARE` agus "
"`MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``:"

msgid ""
"Under ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, every middleware will always have its "
"``process_response`` method called, even if an earlier middleware short-"
"circuited by returning a response from its ``process_request`` method. "
"Under :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`, middleware behaves more like an onion: the "
"layers that a response goes through on the way out are the same layers that "
"saw the request on the way in. If a middleware short-circuits, only that "
"middleware and the ones before it in :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` will see the "
"response."
msgstr ""
"Faoi ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, beidh a mhodh `process_response`` ag gach "
"middleware i gcónaí, fiú má ghearrchiorcáladh meán-earraí níos luaithe trí "
"fhreagra a thabhairt ar ais óna mhodh ``process_request``. Faoi: Socrú: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`, iompraíonn middleware níos cosúil le oinniún: is iad na "
"sraitheanna a théann freagra tríd ar an mbealach amach na sraitheanna céanna "
"a chonaic an t-iarratas ar an mbealach isteach. Má tá gearrchiorcaid lár-"
"earraí ann, ní fheicfidh an freagra ach an middleware sin agus na cinn roimh "
"i:setting: `MIDDLEWARE`."

msgid ""
"Under ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, ``process_exception`` is applied to exceptions "
"raised from a middleware ``process_request`` method. "
"Under :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`, ``process_exception`` applies only to "
"exceptions raised from the view (or from the ``render`` method of "
"a :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse`). Exceptions raised "
"from a middleware are converted to the appropriate HTTP response and then "
"passed to the next middleware."
msgstr ""
"Faoi ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, cuirtear `process_exception`` i bhfeidhm ar "
"eisceachtaí a ardaítear ó mhodh `process_request`` middleware. Fao:SETTING: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`, ní bhaineann ``process_exception`` ach le heisceachtaí a "
"ardaíodh ón radharc (nó ón modh ``render`` de a:class: "
"`~django.template.response.templateResponse`). Déantar eisceachtaí a "
"ardaítear ó mheán-earraí a thiontú go dtí an freagra HTTP cuí agus ansin "
"cuirtear ar aghaidh chuig an chéad mheán-earraí eile."

msgid ""
"Under ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, if a ``process_response`` method raises an "
"exception, the ``process_response`` methods of all earlier middleware are "
"skipped and a ``500 Internal Server Error`` HTTP response is always returned "
"(even if the exception raised was e.g. an :class:`~django.http.Http404`). "
"Under :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`, an exception raised from a middleware will "
"immediately be converted to the appropriate HTTP response, and then the next "
"middleware in line will see that response. Middleware are never skipped due "
"to a middleware raising an exception."
msgstr ""
"Faoi `MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``, má ardaíonn modh ``process_response`` eisceacht, "
"scipeántar modhanna ``process_response`` gach middleware roimhe seo agus "
"cuirtear freagra HTTP ``500 Inmheánach Freastala`` ar ais i gcónaí (fiú má "
"bhí an eisceacht m.sh:class: `~django.http.http404`). Fao:SETTING: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`, tionófar eisceacht a ardaíodh ó mheán-earraí láithreach go dtí "
"an freagra HTTP cuí, agus ansin feicfidh an chéad mheán-earraí eile atá i "
"líne an freagra sin. Ní scipeántar Middleware riamh mar gheall ar mheán-"
"earraí a ardaíonn eisceacht."

msgid "How to use sessions"
msgstr "Conas seisiúin a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Django provides full support for anonymous sessions. The session framework "
"lets you store and retrieve arbitrary data on a per-site-visitor basis. It "
"stores data on the server side and abstracts the sending and receiving of "
"cookies. Cookies contain a session ID -- not the data itself (unless you're "
"using the :ref:`cookie based backend<cookie-session-backend>`)."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django tacaíocht iomlán do sheisiúin gan ainm. Ligeann creat an "
"seisiúin duit sonraí treallach a stóráil agus a aisghabháil ar bhonn "
"cuairteora in aghaidh an láithre Stórálann sé sonraí ar thaobh an "
"fhreastalaí agus déanann sé achoimrí ar sheoladh agus a fháil fianáin. "
"<cookie-session-backend>Tá aitheantas seisiúin i bhfianáin - ní na sonraí "
"féin (mura bhfuil tú ag úsáid an:ref: `backend bhunaithe ar fianáin `)."

msgid "Enabling sessions"
msgstr "Seisiúin chumasaithe"

msgid ""
"Sessions are implemented via a piece of :doc:`middleware </ref/middleware>`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear seisiúin i bhfeidhm trí phíosa de:doc: `middleware` </ref/"
"middleware>."

msgid "To enable session functionality, do the following:"
msgstr "Chun feidhmiúlacht seisiúin a chumasú, déan an méid seo"

msgid ""
"Edit the :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting and make sure it contains "
"``'django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware'``. The default "
"``settings.py`` created by ``django-admin startproject`` has "
"``SessionMiddleware`` activated."
msgstr ""
"Cuir an socrú:setting: `MIDDLEWARE` in eagar agus déan cinnte go bhfuil "
"``Django.contrib.sessions.middleware.sessionMiddleware'` ann. Tá "
"`SessionMiddleware`` gníomhachtaithe ag ``django-admin startproject`` "
"réamhshocraithe ``settings.py``."

msgid ""
"If you don't want to use sessions, you might as well remove the "
"``SessionMiddleware`` line from :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` and "
"``'django.contrib.sessions'`` from your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. It'll "
"save you a small bit of overhead."
msgstr ""
"Mura dteastaíonn uait seisiúin a úsáid, b'fhéidir go bhfaighidh tú an líne "
"``SessionMiddleware`` ó:setting: `MIDDLEWARE` agus "
"```django.contrib.sessions' ``ó d':setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`. Sábhálfaidh sé "
"beagán laochairde duit."

msgid "Configuring the session engine"
msgstr "Inneall an seisiúin a chumrú"

msgid ""
"By default, Django stores sessions in your database (using the model "
"``django.contrib.sessions.models.Session``). Though this is convenient, in "
"some setups it's faster to store session data elsewhere, so Django can be "
"configured to store session data on your filesystem or in your cache."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, stórálann Django seisiúin i do bhunachar sonraí (ag "
"baint úsáide as an tsamhail ``Django.Contrib.Sessions.Models.Session ``). Cé "
"go bhfuil sé seo áisiúil, i roinnt socruithe tá sé níos tapúla sonraí "
"seisiúin a stóráil in áiteanna eile, mar sin is féidir Django a chumrú chun "
"sonraí seisiúin a stóráil ar do chóras comhaid nó i do taisce."

msgid "Using database-backed sessions"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as seisiúin tacaithe"

msgid ""
"If you want to use a database-backed session, you need to add "
"``'django.contrib.sessions'`` to your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat seisiún tacaíochta le bunachar sonraí a úsáid, ní mór duit "
"``django.contrib.sessions'` a chur le do shuíomh: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"Once you have configured your installation, run ``manage.py migrate`` to "
"install the single database table that stores session data."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh do shuiteáil cumraithe agat, reáchtáil ``manage.py migrate`` "
"chun an tábla bunachar sonraí aonair a stóráil sonraí seisiúin a shuiteáil."

msgid "Using cached sessions"
msgstr "Seisiúin taisceáilte a úsáid"

msgid ""
"For better performance, you may want to use a cache-based session backend."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh feidhmíochta níos fearr, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat cúltaca "
"seisiúin bunaithe ar taisce a úsáid."

msgid ""
"To store session data using Django's cache system, you'll first need to make "
"sure you've configured your cache; see the :doc:`cache documentation </"
"topics/cache>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Chun sonraí seisiúin a stóráil ag baint úsáide as córas taisce Django, beidh "
"ort a chinntiú go bhfuil do taisce cumraithe agat ar dtús; féach an:doc: "
"`cáipéisíocht taisceach` le haghaidh sonraí </topics/cache>."

msgid ""
"You should only use cache-based sessions if you're using the Memcached or "
"Redis cache backend. The local-memory cache backend doesn't retain data long "
"enough to be a good choice, and it'll be faster to use file or database "
"sessions directly instead of sending everything through the file or database "
"cache backends. Additionally, the local-memory cache backend is NOT multi-"
"process safe, therefore probably not a good choice for production "
"environments."
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir duit seisiúin cach-bhunaithe a úsáid ach má tá cúltaca taisce "
"Memcached nó Redis á úsáid agat. Ní choinníonn an cúltaca taisce cuimhne "
"áitiúil sonraí fada go leor le bheith ina rogha maith, agus beidh sé níos "
"tapúla seisiúin comhad nó bunachar sonraí a úsáid go díreach in ionad gach "
"rud a sheoladh tríd an gcúltaca taisce comhaid nó bunachar sonraí. Ina "
"theannta sin, NÍL cúltaca taisce cuimhne áitiúil sábháilte ilphróisis, dá "
"bhrí sin is dócha nach rogha maith é do thimpeallachtaí táirgeachta."

msgid ""
"If you have multiple caches defined in :setting:`CACHES`, Django will use "
"the default cache. To use another cache, set :setting:`SESSION_CACHE_ALIAS` "
"to the name of that cache."
msgstr ""
"Má tá iliomad taisce sainithe agat in:setting: `CACHES`, úsáidfidh Django an "
"taisce réamhshocraithe. Chun taisce eile a úsáid, socraí:setting: "
"`SESSION_CACHE_ALIAS` ar ainm an taisce sin."

msgid ""
"Once your cache is configured, you have to choose between a database-backed "
"cache or a non-persistent cache."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh do taisce cumraithe, caithfidh tú a roghnú idir taisce "
"tacaíochta bunachar sonraí nó taisce neamh-leanúnach."

msgid ""
"The cached database backend (``cached_db``) uses a write-through cache -- "
"session writes are applied to both the database and cache, in that order. If "
"writing to the cache fails, the exception is handled and logged via "
"the :ref:`sessions logger <django-contrib-sessions-logger>`, to avoid "
"failing an otherwise successful write operation."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann cúltaca an bhunachar sonraí taisceáilte (`cached_db``) taisce "
"scríbhneoireachta - cuirtear scríbhneoireachtaí seisiúin i bhfeidhm ar an "
"mbunachar sonraí agus taisce araon, san ord sin. Má theipeann ar scríobh "
"chuig an taisce, déantar an eisceacht a láimhseáil agus a logáil trí:ref: "
"`session logger <django-contrib-sessions-logger>`, chun a sheachaint ar "
"oibríocht scríbhneoireachta rathúil ar shlí eile."

msgid "Handling and logging of exceptions when writing to the cache was added."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh eisceachtaí a láimhseáil agus a logáil agus iad ag scríobh chuig an "
"taisce."

msgid ""
"Session reads use the cache, or the database if the data has been evicted "
"from the cache. To use this backend, set :setting:`SESSION_ENGINE` to "
"``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.cached_db\"``, and follow the "
"configuration instructions for the `using database-backed sessions`_."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann léitheanna seisiúin an taisce, nó an bunachar sonraí má "
"dhíothraíodh na sonraí ón taisce. Chun an cúltaca seo a úsáid, "
"socraí:setting: `SESSION_ENGINE` go "
"``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.cached_db\"``, agus lean na treoracha "
"cumraíochta do `úsáid seisiúin tacaíochta bunachar sonraí`_."

msgid ""
"The cache backend (``cache``) stores session data only in your cache. This "
"is faster because it avoids database persistence, but you will have to "
"consider what happens when cache data is evicted. Eviction can occur if the "
"cache fills up or the cache server is restarted, and it will mean session "
"data is lost, including logging out users. To use this backend, "
"set :setting:`SESSION_ENGINE` to "
"``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.cache\"``."
msgstr ""
"Ní stórálann an cúltaca taisce (``cache``) sonraí seisiúin amháin i do "
"taisce. Tá sé seo níos gasta toisc go seachnaíonn sé marthanacht bunachar "
"sonraí, ach beidh ort machnamh a dhéanamh ar cad a tharlaíonn nuair a "
"dhéantar sonraí taisce a dhíbirt. Is féidir le díothú tarlú má líonann an "
"taisce nó má athosaítear an freastalaí taisce, agus ciallaíonn sé go "
"gcailltear sonraí seisiúin, lena n-áirítear úsáideoirí logáil amach. Chun an "
"cúltaca seo a úsáid, socraí:setting: `SESSION_ENGINE` go "
"``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.cache\"``."

msgid ""
"The cache backend can be made persistent by using a persistent cache, such "
"as Redis with appropriate configuration. But unless your cache is definitely "
"configured for sufficient persistence, opt for the cached database backend. "
"This avoids edge cases caused by unreliable data storage in production."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an cúltaca taisce a dhéanamh leanúnach trí taisce leanúnach a "
"úsáid, mar shampla Redis le cumraíocht chuí. Ach mura bhfuil do taisce "
"cumraithe cinnte le haghaidh marthanacht leordhóthanach, roghnaigh cúltaca "
"an bhunachar sonraí taisceáilte. Seachnaíonn sé seo cásanna imeall de bharr "
"stóráil sonraí neamhiontaofa sa táirge"

msgid "Using file-based sessions"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as seisiúin comhad"

msgid ""
"To use file-based sessions, set the :setting:`SESSION_ENGINE` setting to "
"``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.file\"``."
msgstr ""
"Chun seisiúin comhadbhunaithe a úsáid, socraigh an socrú:setting: "
"`SESSION_ENGINE` go ``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.file\"``."

msgid ""
"You might also want to set the :setting:`SESSION_FILE_PATH` setting (which "
"defaults to output from ``tempfile.gettempdir()``, most likely ``/tmp``) to "
"control where Django stores session files. Be sure to check that your web "
"server has permissions to read and write to this location."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an socrú: setting: `SESSION_FILE_PATH` a shocrú (a "
"réamhshocraíonn aschur ó `tempfile.gettempdir () ``, is dóichí ``/tmp``) "
"chun rialú a dhéanamh ar an áit a stórálann Django comhaid seisiúin. Bí "
"cinnte a sheiceáil go bhfuil ceadanna ag do fhreastalaí gréasáin chun léamh "
"agus scríobh chuig an áit seo."

msgid "Using cookie-based sessions"
msgstr "Seisiúin bunaithe ar fhianán a úsáid"

msgid ""
"To use cookies-based sessions, set the :setting:`SESSION_ENGINE` setting to "
"``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.signed_cookies\"``. The session data "
"will be stored using Django's tools for :doc:`cryptographic signing </topics/"
"signing>` and the :setting:`SECRET_KEY` setting."
msgstr ""
"Chun seisiúin bunaithe ar fhianáin a úsáid, socraigh an socrú:setting: "
"`SESSION_ENGINE` go ``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.signed_cookies\"``. "
"Stórálfar sonraí na seisiúin ag baint úsáide as uirlisí Django le haghaidh: "
"doc: `síniú cripteagrafach' agus an socrú:: `SECRET_KEY`. </topics/signing>"

msgid ""
"It's recommended to leave the :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` setting on "
"``True`` to prevent access to the stored data from JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Moltar an socrú:setting: `SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` a fhágáil ar `True`` chun "
"rochtain ar na sonraí stóráilte ó JavaScript a chosc."

msgid "**The session data is signed but not encrypted**"
msgstr "** Sínítear sonraí na seisiúin ach níl siad criptithe"

msgid ""
"When using the cookies backend the session data can be read by the client."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn cúltaca na fianáin á n-úsáid agat is féidir leis an gcliant "
"sonraí na seisiúin a léamh."

msgid ""
"A MAC (Message Authentication Code) is used to protect the data against "
"changes by the client, so that the session data will be invalidated when "
"being tampered with. The same invalidation happens if the client storing the "
"cookie (e.g. your user's browser) can't store all of the session cookie and "
"drops data. Even though Django compresses the data, it's still entirely "
"possible to exceed the :rfc:`common limit of 4096 bytes <2965#section-5.3>` "
"per cookie."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear MAC (Cód Fíordheimhnithe Teachtaireachta) chun na sonraí a "
"chosaint ar athruithe a dhéanann an chliant, ionas go ndéanfar sonraí na "
"seisiúin neamhbhailí agus iad ag cur isteach orthu. Tarlaíonn an neamhbhailí "
"céanna mura féidir leis an gcliant atá ag stóráil an fianán (m.sh. "
"brabhsálaí d'úsáideora) an fianán seisiúin go léir a stóráil agus scaoileann "
"<2965 #section -5.3>Cé go gcomhbhrúiteann Django na sonraí, is féidir go "
"hiomlán fós an: rfc: `teorainn choiteann de 4096 baite' in aghaidh an "
"fhianáin a shárú."

msgid "**No freshness guarantee**"
msgstr "** Gan aon ráthaíocht úire**"

msgid ""
"Note also that while the MAC can guarantee the authenticity of the data "
"(that it was generated by your site, and not someone else), and the "
"integrity of the data (that it is all there and correct), it cannot "
"guarantee freshness i.e. that you are being sent back the last thing you "
"sent to the client. This means that for some uses of session data, the "
"cookie backend might open you up to `replay attacks`_. Unlike other session "
"backends which keep a server-side record of each session and invalidate it "
"when a user logs out, cookie-based sessions are not invalidated when a user "
"logs out. Thus if an attacker steals a user's cookie, they can use that "
"cookie to login as that user even if the user logs out. Cookies will only be "
"detected as 'stale' if they are older than "
